window.WORD_NINJA_IMPORTED = {"basic":[["able","/ˈeɪbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “able”.","able [ˈeɪbl] -K5 adj. 能；[经管] 有能力的；能干的 n. (Able)人名；(伊朗)阿布勒；(英)埃布尔 (中高 385/295)","欧陆词典释义：able [ˈeɪbl] -K5 adj. 能；[经管] 有能力的；能干的 n. (Able)人名；(伊朗)阿布勒；(英)埃布尔 (中高 385/295)","The older child should be able to prepare a simple meal...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"to have the skill, intelligence, opportunity, etc. needed to do something","example":"You must be able to speak French for this job."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"intelligent; good at something","example":"A viral illness left her barely able to walk."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"I didn't feel able to disagree with him."}]],["about","/əˈbaʊt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “about”.","about [əˈbaʊt] -K5 prep. 关于；大约 n. 大致；粗枝大叶；不拘小节的人 adj. 在附近的；四处走动的；在起作用的 adv. 大约；周围；到处 n. (About)人名；(法)阿布 (中高 46/63)","欧陆词典释义：about [əˈbaʊt] -K5 prep. 关于；大约 n. 大致；粗枝大叶；不拘小节的人 adj. 在附近的；四处走动的；在起作用的 adv. 大约；周围；到处 n. (About)人名；(法)阿布 (中高 46/63)","She came in for a coffee, and told me about her friend Shona...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"a little more or less than; a little before or after","example":"It costs about $10."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"nearly; very close to","example":"They waited (for) about an hour."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"in many directions; here and there","example":"He arrived (at) about ten."}]],["above","/əˈbʌv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “above”.","above [əˈbʌv] -K4 prep. 超过；在……上面；在……之上 n. 上文 adj. 上文的 adv. 在上面；在上文 (中高 893/733)","欧陆词典释义：above [əˈbʌv] -K4 prep. 超过；在……上面；在……之上 n. 上文 adj. 上文的 adv. 在上面；在上文 (中高 893/733)","He lifted his hands above his head...",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"at or to a higher place or position than something/somebody","example":"The water came above our knees."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"more than something; greater in number, level or age than somebody/something","example":"We were flying above the clouds."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"of greater importance or of higher quality than somebody/something","example":"the people in the apartment above mine"}]],["accept","/əkˈsept/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accept”.","accept [əkˈsept] -K5 vi. 承认；同意；承兑 vt. 接受；承认；承担；承兑；容纳 时态: accepted, accepting, accepts (中高研四 766/488)","欧陆词典释义：accept [əkˈsept] -K5 vi. 承认；同意；承兑 vt. 接受；承认；承担；承兑；容纳 时态: accepted, accepting, accepts (中高研四 766/488)","Eventually Sam persuaded her to accept an offer of marriage...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take willingly something that is offered; to say ‘yes’ to an offer, invitation, etc.","example":"He asked me to marry him and I accepted."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to receive something as suitable or good enough","example":"Please accept our sincere apologies."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to agree to or approve of something","example":"It was pouring with rain so I accepted his offer of a lift."}]],["action","/ˈækʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “action”.","action [ˈækʃn] -K5 n. 行动；活动；功能；战斗；情节 n. (Action)人名；(英)埃克申 (中高研四六托雅 502/340)","欧陆词典释义：action [ˈækʃn] -K5 n. 行动；活动；功能；战斗；情节 n. (Action)人名；(英)埃克申 (中高研四六托雅 502/340)","The government is taking emergency action to deal with a housing crisis...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of doing something in order to make something happen or to deal with a situation","example":"The time has come for action if these beautiful animals are to survive."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a thing that somebody does","example":"Firefighters took action"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a legal process to stop a person or company from doing something, or to make them pay for a mistake, etc.","example":"What is the best course of action"}]],["active","/ˈæktɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “active”.","active [ˈæktɪv] -K4 n. 主动语态；积极分子 adj. 积极的；活跃的；主动的；有效的；现役的 (中高研四托 1444/1316)","欧陆词典释义：active [ˈæktɪv] -K4 n. 主动语态；积极分子 adj. 积极的；活跃的；主动的；有效的；现役的 (中高研四托 1444/1316)","Having an active youngster about the house can be quite wearing.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"always busy doing things, especially physical activities","example":"Although he's nearly 80, he is still very active."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"involved in something; making a determined effort and not leaving something to happen by itself","example":"Before our modern age, people had a more physical and active lifestyle."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"doing something regularly; functioning","example":"They were both politically active."}]],["afternoon","/ˌɑ:ftəˈnu:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “afternoon”.","afternoon [ˌɑ:ftəˈnu:n] -K4 n. 午后，下午 (中高 1191/1118)","欧陆词典释义：afternoon [ˌɑ:ftəˈnu:n] -K4 n. 午后，下午 (中高 1191/1118)","He's arriving in the afternoon ...",""],["air","/eə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “air”.","air [eə(r)] -K5 n. 空气，大气；天空；样子；曲调 vt. 使通风，晾干；夸耀 vi. 通风 时态: aired, airing, airs (中高托雅 370/527)","欧陆词典释义：air [eə(r)] -K5 n. 空气，大气；天空；样子；曲调 vt. 使通风，晾干；夸耀 vi. 通风 时态: aired, airing, airs (中高托雅 370/527)","Draughts help to circulate air ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the mixture of gases that surrounds the earth and that we breathe","example":"air pollution"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the space above the ground or that is around things","example":"Let's go out for some fresh air"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the space above the earth where planes fly","example":"I need to put some air in my tyres."}]],["animal","/ˈænɪml/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “animal”.","animal [ˈænɪml] -K4 n. 动物 动物的 (中高雅 728/652)","欧陆词典释义：animal [ˈænɪml] -K4 n. 动物 动物的 (中高雅 728/652)","He was attacked by wild animal s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a creature that is not a bird, a fish, a reptile","example":"the animals and birds of South America"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"any living thing that is not a plant or a human","example":"a small furry animal"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"any living creature, including humans","example":"Fish oils are less saturated than animal fats."}]],["answer","/ˈɑ:nsə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “answer”.","answer [ˈɑ:nsə(r)] -K5 n. 回答；答案；答辩 vt. 回答；符合 vi. 回答；符合 时态: answered, answering, answers (中高 767/808)","欧陆词典释义：answer [ˈɑ:nsə(r)] -K5 n. 回答；答案；答辩 vt. 回答；符合 vi. 回答；符合 时态: answered, answering, answers (中高 767/808)","I knew Ben was lying when he answer ed me...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that you say, write or do to react to a question or situation","example":"I rang the bell, but there was no answer."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"something that you write or say in reply to a question in a test, an exam, an exercise, etc.; the correct reply to a question in a test, etc.","example":"a question and answer session"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a solution to a problem","example":"I can't easily give an answer"}]],["apple","/ˈæpl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “apple”.","apple [ˈæpl] -K3 n. 苹果，苹果树，苹果似的东西；[美俚]炸弹，手榴弹，（棒球的）球；[美俚]人，家伙。 (中高 2695/2446)","欧陆词典释义：apple [ˈæpl] -K3 n. 苹果，苹果树，苹果似的东西；[美俚]炸弹，手榴弹，（棒球的）球；[美俚]人，家伙。 (中高 2695/2446)","I want an apple .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a round fruit with shiny red or green skin and firm white flesh","example":"Peel and core the apples."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"an apple pie"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a child usually behaves in a similar way to his or her parent(s)","example":"apple sauce"}]],["arrive","/əˈraɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “arrive”.","arrive [əˈraɪv] -K4 vi. 到达；成功；达成；出生 n. (Arrive)人名；(法)阿里夫 时态: arrived, arriving, arrives (中高 810/708)","欧陆词典释义：arrive [əˈraɪv] -K4 vi. 到达；成功；达成；出生 n. (Arrive)人名；(法)阿里夫 时态: arrived, arriving, arrives (中高 810/708)","Fresh groups of guests arrive d...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to get to a place, especially at the end of a journey","example":"I'll wait until they arrive."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be brought to somebody","example":"I was pleased to hear you arrived home safely."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to happen or to come, especially when you have been waiting for it","example":"to arrive early/late"}]],["baby","/ˈbeɪbi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “baby”.","baby [ˈbeɪbi] -K4 n. 婴儿，婴孩；孩子气的人 adj. 婴儿的；幼小的 vt. 纵容，娇纵；把……当婴儿般对待 n. (Baby)人名；(法、葡)巴比；(英)巴比，芭比(女名)；(俄)巴贝 时态: babied, babying, babies (中高 588/869)","欧陆词典释义：baby [ˈbeɪbi] -K4 n. 婴儿，婴孩；孩子气的人 adj. 婴儿的；幼小的 vt. 纵容，娇纵；把……当婴儿般对待 n. (Baby)人名；(法、葡)巴比；(英)巴比，芭比(女名)；(俄)巴贝 时态: babied, babying, babies (中高 588/869)","She used to take care of me when I was a baby ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a very young child or animal","example":"The baby's crying!"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the youngest member of a family or group","example":"a newborn baby"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person who behaves like a young child and is easily upset","example":"My sister's expecting a baby"}]],["back","/bæk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “back”.","back [bæk] -K5 n. 后面；背部；靠背；足球等的后卫；书报等的末尾 adj. 后面的；过去的；拖欠的 vt. 支持；后退；背书；下赌注 adv. 以前；向后地；来回地；上溯；回来；回原处 vi. 后退；背靠；倒退 n. (Back)人名；(西、英、德、法、瑞典、捷)巴克 时态: backed, backing, backs (中高雅 108/105)","欧陆词典释义：back [bæk] -K5 n. 后面；背部；靠背；足球等的后卫；书报等的末尾 adj. 后面的；过去的；拖欠的 vt. 支持；后退；背书；下赌注 adv. 以前；向后地；来回地；上溯；回来；回原处 vi. 后退；背靠；倒退 n. (Back)人名；(西、英、德、法、瑞典、捷)巴克 时态: backed, backing, backs (中高雅 108/105)","The photographers drew back to let us view the body...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the part of the human body that is on the opposite side to the chest, between the neck and the tops of the legs; the part of an animal’s body that corresponds","example":"Do you sleep on your back or your front?"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the row of bones in the middle of the back","example":"He stood with his back to the door."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"the part or area of something that is furthest from the front","example":"They had their hands tied behind their backs."}]],["bad","/bæd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bad”.","bad [bæd] -K5 n. 坏事；坏人 adj. 坏的；严重的；劣质的 adv. 很，非常；坏地；邪恶地 n. (Bad)人名；(罗)巴德 级别: worse, worst (中高 282/349)","欧陆词典释义：bad [bæd] -K5 n. 坏事；坏人 adj. 坏的；严重的；劣质的 adv. 很，非常；坏地；邪恶地 n. (Bad)人名；(罗)巴德 级别: worse, worst (中高 282/349)","The bad weather conditions prevented the plane from landing...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"unpleasant; full of problems","example":"bad news/weather/dreams/habits"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"of poor quality; below an acceptable standard","example":"I'm having a really bad day."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"not able to do something well or in an acceptable way","example":"It was the worst experience of her life."}]],["beautiful","/ˈbju:tɪfl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “beautiful”.","beautiful [ˈbju:tɪfl] -K4 adj. 美丽的 出色地 出色的 迷人的 迷人地 (中高雅 992/1161)","欧陆词典释义：beautiful [ˈbju:tɪfl] -K4 adj. 美丽的 出色地 出色的 迷人的 迷人地 (中高雅 992/1161)","She was a very beautiful woman...",""],["become","/bɪˈkʌm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “become”.","become [bɪˈkʌm] -K5 vt. 适合；相称 vi. 成为；变得；变成 时态: became, become, becoming, becomes (中高雅 139/122)","欧陆词典释义：become [bɪˈkʌm] -K5 vt. 适合；相称 vi. 成为；变得；变成 时态: became, become, becoming, becomes (中高雅 139/122)","I first became interested in Islam while I was doing my nursing training...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to start to be something","example":"It was becoming more and more difficult to live on his salary."},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to be suitable for somebody","example":"It soon became apparent that no one was going to come."},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to look attractive on somebody","example":"She was becoming confused."}]],["before","/bɪˈfɔ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “before”.","before [bɪˈfɔ:(r)] -K5 prep. 在…之前，先于 conj. 在…以前；在…之前 adv. 以前；在前 (中高 219/198)","欧陆词典释义：before [bɪˈfɔ:(r)] -K5 prep. 在…之前，先于 conj. 在…以前；在…之前 adv. 以前；在前 (中高 219/198)","Annie was born a few weeks before Christmas...",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"earlier than somebody/something","example":"before lunch"},{"pos":"conjunction","definition":"used to say that somebody/something is in a position in front of somebody/something","example":"the day before yesterday"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used to say that somebody/something is ahead of somebody/something in an order or arrangement","example":"The year before last he won a gold medal, and the year before that he won a silver."}]],["begin","/bɪˈgɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “begin”.","begin [bɪˈgɪn] -K5 vi. 开始；首先 vt. 开始 n. (Begin)人名；(以、德)贝京；(英)贝让 时态: began, begun, beginning, begins (中高 164/193)","欧陆词典释义：begin [bɪˈgɪn] -K5 vi. 开始；首先 vt. 开始 n. (Begin)人名；(以、德)贝京；(英)贝让 时态: began, begun, beginning, begins (中高 164/193)","He stood up and began to move around the room...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to start doing something; to do the first part of something","example":"Shall I begin?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to start to happen or exist, especially from a particular time","example":"Let's begin at page 9."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be something first, before becoming something else","example":"She began by thanking us all for coming."}]],["best","/best/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “best”.","best [best] n. 最好的人，最好的事物；最佳状态 adj. 最好的 vt. 打败，胜过 adv. 最好地 n. (Best)人名；(英、西、德、葡、法)贝斯特 时态: bested, besting, bests 原型: best 是 good 的最高级 (雅 309/1212)","欧陆词典释义：best [best] n. 最好的人，最好的事物；最佳状态 adj. 最好的 vt. 打败，胜过 adv. 最好地 n. (Best)人名；(英、西、德、葡、法)贝斯特 时态: bested, besting, bests 原型: best 是 good 的最高级 (雅 309/1212)","If you want further information the best thing to do is have a word with the driver as you get on the bus...",""],["better","/ˈbetə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “better”.","better [ˈbetə(r)] -K5 n. 长辈；较好者；打赌的人（等于bettor） adj. 较好的 vt. 改善；胜过 adv. 更好的；更多的；较大程度地 vi. 变得较好 n. (Better)人名；(西、瑞典、德)贝特尔 时态: bettered, bettering, betters 原型: better 是 good 的比较级 (高雅 452/704)","欧陆词典释义：better [ˈbetə(r)] -K5 n. 长辈；较好者；打赌的人（等于bettor） adj. 较好的 vt. 改善；胜过 adv. 更好的；更多的；较大程度地 vi. 变得较好 n. (Better)人名；(西、瑞典、德)贝特尔 时态: bettered, bettering, betters 原型: better 是 good 的比较级 (高雅 452/704)","I like your interpretation better than the one I was taught...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"of a higher standard or less poor quality; not as bad as something else","example":"We're hoping for better weather tomorrow."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"more able or skilled","example":"Her work is getting better and better"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"more suitable or appropriate","example":"He is in a much better mood than usual."}]],["big","/bɪg/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “big”.","big [bɪg] -K5 adj. 大的；重要的；量大的 adv. 大量地；顺利；夸大地 n. (Big)人名；(土)比格 级别: bigger, biggest (中高 162/260)","欧陆词典释义：big [bɪg] -K5 adj. 大的；重要的；量大的 adv. 大量地；顺利；夸大地 n. (Big)人名；(土)比格 级别: bigger, biggest (中高 162/260)","Australia's a big country...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"large in size, degree, amount, etc.","example":"a big man/house/increase"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"older","example":"This shirt isn't big enough."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"important; serious","example":"It's the world's biggest computer company."}]],["bird","/bɜ:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bird”.","bird [bɜ:d] -K4 n. 鸟；家伙；羽毛球 vt. 向…喝倒彩；起哄 vi. 猎鸟；观察研究野鸟 n. (Bird)人名；(英、西)伯德 时态: birded, birding, birds (中高 1122/1072)","欧陆词典释义：bird [bɜ:d] -K4 n. 鸟；家伙；羽毛球 vt. 向…喝倒彩；起哄 vi. 猎鸟；观察研究野鸟 n. (Bird)人名；(英、西)伯德 时态: birded, birding, birds (中高 1122/1072)","They warned him that next time he'd find himself doing bird .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a creature that is covered with feathers and has two wings and two legs. Most birds can fly.","example":"a bird’s nest with two eggs in it"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a way of referring to a young woman","example":"a species of bird"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person of a particular type, especially somebody who is strange or unusual in some way","example":"The area has a wealth of bird life."}]],["black","/blæk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “black”.","black [blæk] -K5 n. 黑色；黑人；黑颜料 adj. 黑色的；黑人的；邪恶的 vt. 使变黑；把鞋油等涂在…上；把（眼眶）打成青肿 vi. 变黑 n. (Black)人名；(英、西)布莱克；(德、葡、捷)布拉克 时态: blacked, blacking, blacks 级别: blacker, blackest (中高雅 253/426)","欧陆词典释义：black [blæk] -K5 n. 黑色；黑人；黑颜料 adj. 黑色的；黑人的；邪恶的 vt. 使变黑；把鞋油等涂在…上；把（眼眶）打成青肿 vi. 变黑 n. (Black)人名；(英、西)布莱克；(德、葡、捷)布拉克 时态: blacked, blacking, blacks 级别: blacker, blackest (中高雅 253/426)","She was wearing a black coat with a white collar...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having the very darkest colour, like coal or the sky at night","example":"a shiny black car"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"without light; completely dark","example":"black storm clouds"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"belonging to a race of people who have dark skin; connected with black people","example":"a black night"}]],["blue","/blu:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “blue”.","blue [blu:] -K5 adj. 蓝色的；沮丧的，忧郁的；下流的 n. 蓝色；[复数]（美国海、陆、空三军穿的）蓝色制服；蓝颜料；[the blue(s)][用作单数或复数]布鲁斯（歌曲）（一种伤感的美国黑人民歌 vi. 变成蓝色，呈蓝色 vt. 把…染成蓝色；使成蓝色；给…用上蓝剂；用上蓝剂于 n. （英、西、意）布卢（人名） 时态: blued, bluing, blues (高宝 842/1083)","欧陆词典释义：blue [blu:] -K5 adj. 蓝色的；沮丧的，忧郁的；下流的 n. 蓝色；[复数]（美国海、陆、空三军穿的）蓝色制服；蓝颜料；[the blue(s)][用作单数或复数]布鲁斯（歌曲）（一种伤感的美国黑人民歌 vi. 变成蓝色，呈蓝色 vt. 把…染成蓝色；使成蓝色；给…用上蓝剂；用上蓝剂于 n. （英、西、意）布卢（人名） 时态: blued, bluing, blues (高宝 842/1083)","There were swallows in the cloudless blue sky...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having the colour of a clear sky or the sea/ocean on a clear day","example":"piercing blue eyes"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"looking slightly blue in colour because the person is cold or cannot breathe easily","example":"a blue shirt"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"sad","example":"a navy blue jumper"}]],["body","/ˈbɒdi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “body”.","body [ˈbɒdi] -K5 n. 身体；主体；大量；团体；主要部分 vt. 赋以形体 n. (Body)人名；(英、法、罗)博迪 时态: bodied, bodying, bodies (中 313/274)","欧陆词典释义：body [ˈbɒdi] -K5 n. 身体；主体；大量；团体；主要部分 vt. 赋以形体 n. (Body)人名；(英、法、罗)博迪 时态: bodied, bodying, bodies (中 313/274)","The largest organ in the body is the liver.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the whole physical structure of a human or an animal","example":"a human/female/male/naked body"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the main part of a body not including the head, or not including the head, arms and legs","example":"parts of the body"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the body of a dead person or animal","example":"His whole body was trembling."}]],["book","/bʊk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “book”.","book [bʊk] -K5 n. 书籍；卷；帐簿；名册；工作簿 vt. 预订；登记 n. (Book)人名；(中)卜(广东话·威妥玛)；(朝)北；(英)布克；(瑞典)博克 时态: booked, booking, books (中高雅 241/235)","欧陆词典释义：book [bʊk] -K5 n. 书籍；卷；帐簿；名册；工作簿 vt. 预订；登记 n. (Book)人名；(中)卜(广东话·威妥玛)；(朝)北；(英)布克；(瑞典)博克 时态: booked, booking, books (中高雅 241/235)","His eighth book came out earlier this year and was an instant best-seller...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a set of printed pages that are fastened inside a cover so that you can turn them and read them","example":"a pile of books"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a written work published in printed or electronic form","example":"hardback/paperback books"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a set of sheets of paper that are fastened together inside a cover and used for writing in","example":"a book by Stephen King"}]],["boy","/bɔɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “boy”.","boy [bɔɪ] -K5 n. 男孩；男人 n. (Boy)人名；(英、德、西、意、刚(金)、印尼、瑞典)博伊；(法)布瓦 (中高 382/462)","欧陆词典释义：boy [bɔɪ] -K5 n. 男孩；男人 n. (Boy)人名；(英、德、西、意、刚(金)、印尼、瑞典)博伊；(法)布瓦 (中高 382/462)","I knew him when he was a little boy ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a male child or a young male person","example":"a little/small/young boy"},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"a young son","example":"I used to play here as a boy."},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"a boy or young man who does a particular job","example":"The older boys at school used to tease him."}]],["bread","/bred/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bread”.","bread [bred] -K3 n. 面包；生计 vt. 在…上洒面包屑 时态: breaded, breading, breads (中高 2113/2292)","欧陆词典释义：bread [bred] -K3 n. 面包；生计 vt. 在…上洒面包屑 时态: breaded, breading, breads (中高 2113/2292)","a loaf of bread ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a type of food made from flour, water and usually yeast","example":"a loaf/slice/piece of bread"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"money","example":"white/brown/wholemeal bread"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"He had to live on bread and water for two weeks."}]],["bring","/brɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bring”.","bring [brɪŋ] -K5 vt. 带来；促使；引起；使某人处于某种情况或境地 n. (Bring)人名；(英、瑞典)布林 时态: brought, bringing, brings (中高雅 215/195)","欧陆词典释义：bring [brɪŋ] -K5 vt. 带来；促使；引起；使某人处于某种情况或境地 n. (Bring)人名；(英、瑞典)布林 时态: brought, bringing, brings (中高雅 215/195)","Remember to bring an apron or an old shirt to protect your clothes...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to come to a place with somebody/something","example":"Don't forget to bring your books with you."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to provide somebody/something with something","example":"She brought her boyfriend to the party."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to cause something","example":"Bring a present for Helen."}]],["brother","/ˈbrʌðə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “brother”.","brother [ˈbrʌðə(r)] -K5 n. 兄弟；同事；战友 int. 我的老兄！ n. (Brother)人名；(英)布拉泽 (中高 614/827)","欧陆词典释义：brother [ˈbrʌðə(r)] -K5 n. 兄弟；同事；战友 int. 我的老兄！ n. (Brother)人名；(英)布拉泽 (中高 614/827)","Oh, so you're Peter's younger brother ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a boy or man who has the same mother and father as another person","example":"We're brothers."},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"used for talking to or talking about other male members of an organization or other men who have the same ideas, purpose, etc. as yourself","example":"He's my brother."},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"a male member of a religious group, especially a monk","example":"an older/younger brother"}]],["build","/bɪld/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “build”.","build [bɪld] -K5 n. 构造；体形；体格 vi. 建筑；建造 vt. 建立；建筑 时态: built, building, builds (中高 408/415)","欧陆词典释义：build [bɪld] -K5 n. 构造；体形；体格 vi. 建筑；建造 vt. 建立；建筑 时态: built, building, builds (中高 408/415)","Developers are now proposing to build a hotel on the site...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something, especially a building, by putting parts together","example":"They have permission to build 200 new houses."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to create or develop something","example":"Robins build nests almost anywhere."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to become gradually stronger","example":"They're going to build on the site of the old power station."}]],["buy","/baɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “buy”.","buy [baɪ] -K5 n. 购买，买卖；所购的物品 vi. 买，采购 vt. 购买；获得；贿赂 n. (Buy)人名；(法)比伊 时态: bought, buying, buys (中高 397/351)","欧陆词典释义：buy [baɪ] -K5 n. 购买，买卖；所购的物品 vi. 买，采购 vt. 购买；获得；贿赂 n. (Buy)人名；(法)比伊 时态: bought, buying, buys (中高 397/351)","He could not afford to buy a house...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to obtain something by paying money for it","example":"Where did you buy that dress?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be enough to pay for something","example":"If you're thinking of getting a new car, now is a good time to buy."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to persuade somebody to do something dishonest in return for money","example":"I bought it from a friend for £10."}]],["call","/kɔ:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “call”.","call [kɔ:l] -K5 n. 电话；呼叫；要求；访问 vi. 呼叫；拜访；叫牌 vt. 呼叫；称呼；召集 n. (Call)人名；(瑞典、罗)卡尔；(英)考尔 时态: called, calling, calls (中高雅 122/161)","欧陆词典释义：call [kɔ:l] -K5 n. 电话；呼叫；要求；访问 vi. 呼叫；拜访；叫牌 vt. 呼叫；称呼；召集 n. (Call)人名；(瑞典、罗)卡尔；(英)考尔 时态: called, calling, calls (中高雅 122/161)","I always wanted to call the dog Mufty for some reason...",""],["car","/kɑ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “car”.","car [kɑ:(r)] -K5 n. 汽车；车厢 n. (Car)人名；(土)贾尔；(法、西)卡尔；(塞)察尔 (中高 289/247)","欧陆词典释义：car [kɑ:(r)] -K5 n. 汽车；车厢 n. (Car)人名；(土)贾尔；(法、西)卡尔；(塞)察尔 (中高 289/247)","He had left his tickets in his car ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a road vehicle with an engine and four wheels that can carry a small number of passengers","example":"Paula got into the car and drove off."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a separate section of a train","example":"‘How did you come?’ ‘ By car"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a coach/ car","example":"Are you going in the car"}]],["carry","/ˈkæri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “carry”.","carry [ˈkæri] -K5 n. 运载；[计] 进位；射程 vi. 能达到；被携带；被搬运 vt. 拿，扛；携带；支持；搬运 n. (Carry)人名；(英)卡里 时态: carried, carrying, carries (中高雅 487/283)","欧陆词典释义：carry [ˈkæri] -K5 n. 运载；[计] 进位；射程 vi. 能达到；被携带；被搬运 vt. 拿，扛；携带；支持；搬运 n. (Carry)人名；(英)卡里 时态: carried, carrying, carries (中高雅 487/283)","He was carry ing a briefcase...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to support the weight of somebody/something and take them or it from place to place; to take somebody/something from one place to another","example":"He was carrying a suitcase."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have something with you and take it wherever you go","example":"She carried her baby in her arms."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to contain and direct the flow of water, electricity, etc.","example":"The injured were carried away on stretchers."}]],["cat","/kæt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cat”.","cat [kæt] -K3 n. 猫，猫科动物 时态: catted, catting, cats (中高 1775/1712)","欧陆词典释义：cat [kæt] -K3 n. 猫，猫科动物 时态: catted, catting, cats (中高 1775/1712)","'All right, I've been reading it. So what?' — 'Curiosity killed the cat , that's what.'",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small animal with soft fur that people often keep as a pet. Cats","example":"cat food"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a wild animal of the cat family","example":"the big cats ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"Cats mark their territory by spraying."}]],["change","/tʃeɪndʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “change”.","change [tʃeɪndʒ] -K5 n. 变化；找回的零钱 vt. 改变；交换 vi. 改变；兑换 时态: changed, changing, changes (中高 306/226)","欧陆词典释义：change [tʃeɪndʒ] -K5 n. 变化；找回的零钱 vt. 改变；交换 vi. 改变；兑换 时态: changed, changing, changes (中高 306/226)","The ambassador appealed for a change in US policy...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become different","example":"Rick hasn't changed. He looks exactly the same as he did at school."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to make somebody/something different","example":"changing attitudes towards education"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to pass or make somebody/something pass from one state or form into another","example":"Her life changed completely when she won the lottery."}]],["child","/tʃaɪld/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “child”.","child [tʃaɪld] -K5 n. 儿童，小孩，孩子；产物；子孙；幼稚的人；弟子 n. （英）蔡尔德（人名） (中高雅 115/114)","欧陆词典释义：child [tʃaɪld] -K5 n. 儿童，小孩，孩子；产物；子孙；幼稚的人；弟子 n. （英）蔡尔德（人名） (中高雅 115/114)","When I was a child I lived in a country village...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a young human who is not yet an adult","example":"a child of three/a three-year-old child"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a son or daughter of any age","example":"men, women and children"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who is strongly influenced by the ideas and attitudes of a particular time or person","example":"an unborn child"}]],["city","/ˈsɪti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “city”.","city [ˈsɪti] -K4 n. 城市，都市 adj. 城市的；都会的 (中高雅 290/331)","欧陆词典释义：city [ˈsɪti] -K4 n. 城市，都市 adj. 城市的；都会的 (中高雅 290/331)","the city of Bologna.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large and important town","example":"the city centre"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a town that has been given special rights by a king or queen, usually one that has a cathedral","example":"one of the world’s most beautiful cities"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a town that has been given special rights by the state government","example":"a major city"}]],["clean","/kli:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “clean”.","clean [kli:n] -K4 n. 打扫 adj. 清洁的，干净的；清白的 vt. 使干净 vi. 打扫，清扫 adv. 完全地 n. (Clean)人名；(英)克林 时态: cleaned, cleaning, cleans 级别: cleaner, cleanest (中高托雅 1514/1780)","欧陆词典释义：clean [kli:n] -K4 n. 打扫 adj. 清洁的，干净的；清白的 vt. 使干净 vi. 打扫，清扫 adv. 完全地 n. (Clean)人名；(英)克林 时态: cleaned, cleaning, cleans 级别: cleaner, cleanest (中高托雅 1514/1780)","He wore his clean est slacks, a clean shirt and a navy blazer...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not dirty","example":"Are your hands clean?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having a clean","example":"to wipe something clean"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"free from harmful or unpleasant substances","example":"The hotel was spotlessly"}]],["close","/kləʊz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “close”.","close [kləʊz] -K3 n. 结束 adj. 紧密的；亲密的；亲近的 vt. 关；结束；使靠近 vi. 关；结束；关闭 adv. 紧密地 n. (Close)人名；(西)克洛塞；(英、法)克洛斯 时态: closed, closing, closes 级别: closer, closest (中高托 649/647)","欧陆词典释义：close [kləʊz] -K3 n. 结束 adj. 紧密的；亲密的；亲近的 vt. 关；结束；使靠近 vi. 关；结束；关闭 adv. 紧密地 n. (Close)人名；(西)克洛塞；(英、法)克洛斯 时态: closed, closing, closes 级别: closer, closest (中高托 649/647)","If you are cold, close the window...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to put something into a position so that it covers an opening; to get into this position","example":"Would anyone mind if I closed the window?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to move the parts of something together so that it is no longer open","example":"She closed the gate behind her."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"to make the work of a shop/store, etc. stop for a period of time; to not be open for people to use","example":"It's dark now—let's close the curtains."}]],["cloud","/klaʊd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cloud”.","cloud [klaʊd] -K3 n. 云；阴云；云状物；一大群；黑斑 vt. 使混乱；以云遮敝；使忧郁；玷污 vi. 阴沉；乌云密布 n. (Cloud)人名；(法)克卢；(英)克劳德 时态: clouded, clouding, clouds (中高 1914/2333)","欧陆词典释义：cloud [klaʊd] -K3 n. 云；阴云；云状物；一大群；黑斑 vt. 使混乱；以云遮敝；使忧郁；玷污 vi. 阴沉；乌云密布 n. (Cloud)人名；(法)克卢；(英)克劳德 时态: clouded, clouding, clouds (中高 1914/2333)","the varied shapes of the cloud s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a grey or white mass made of very small drops of water, that floats in the sky","example":"The sun went behind a cloud."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a large mass of something in the air, for example dust or smoke, or a number of insects flying all together","example":"It was scorching and there wasn't a cloud in the sky."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"something that makes you feel sad or anxious","example":"The plane was flying in cloud most of the way."}]],["cold","/kəʊld/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cold”.","cold [kəʊld] -K4 n. 寒冷；感冒 adj. 寒冷的；冷淡的，不热情的；失去知觉的 adv. 完全地 级别: colder, coldest (中高研四 885/972)","欧陆词典释义：cold [kəʊld] -K4 n. 寒冷；感冒 adj. 寒冷的；冷淡的，不热情的；失去知觉的 adv. 完全地 级别: colder, coldest (中高研四 885/972)","Rinse the vegetables under cold running water...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a lower than usual temperature; having a temperature lower than the human body","example":"I'm cold. Turn the heating up."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"not heated; cooled after being cooked","example":"to feel/look cold"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"without emotion; unfriendly","example":"cold hands and feet"}]],["color","/'kʌlə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “color”.","color ['kʌlə(r)] n. 颜色；肤色；颜料；脸色 vt. 粉饰；给...涂颜色；歪曲 vi. 变色；获得颜色 时态: colored, coloring, colors (研四雅 697/24372)","欧陆词典释义：color ['kʌlə(r)] n. 颜色；肤色；颜料；脸色 vt. 粉饰；给...涂颜色；歪曲 vi. 变色；获得颜色 时态: colored, coloring, colors (研四雅 697/24372)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “color”.",""],["come","/kʌm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “come”.","come [kʌm] -K5 vi. 来；开始；出现；发生；变成；到达 vt. 做；假装；将满（…岁） int. 嗨！ n. (Come)人名；(英)科姆；(阿尔巴)乔梅 时态: came, come, coming, comes (中高雅 70/65)","欧陆词典释义：come [kʌm] -K5 vi. 来；开始；出现；发生；变成；到达 vt. 做；假装；将满（…岁） int. 嗨！ n. (Come)人名；(英)科姆；(阿尔巴)乔梅 时态: came, come, coming, comes (中高雅 70/65)","Two police officers came into the hall...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move to or towards a person or place","example":"He came into the room and shut the door."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"to arrive at or reach a place","example":"She comes to work by bus."},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"to arrive somewhere in order to do something or get something","example":"My son is coming home soon."}]],["common","/ˈkɒmən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “common”.","common [ˈkɒmən] -K1 n. 普通；平民；公有地 adj. 共同的；普通的；一般的；通常的 n. (Common)人名；(法)科蒙；(英)康芒 (中高研四六雅 710/554)","欧陆词典释义：common [ˈkɒmən] -K1 n. 普通；平民；公有地 adj. 共同的；普通的；一般的；通常的 n. (Common)人名；(法)科蒙；(英)康芒 (中高研四六雅 710/554)","His name was Hansen, a common name in Norway...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"happening often; existing in large numbers or in many places","example":"Jackson is a common English name."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"shared by or belonging to two or more people or by the people in a group","example":"Breast cancer is the most common form of cancer among women in this country."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"ordinary; not unusual or special","example":"Some birds which were once a common sight"}]],["complete","/kəmˈpli:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “complete”.","complete [kəmˈpli:t] -K5 adj. 完整的；完全的；彻底的 vt. 完成 时态: completed, completing, completes (中高研四六托雅 1207/998)","欧陆词典释义：complete [kəmˈpli:t] -K5 adj. 完整的；完全的；彻底的 vt. 完成 时态: completed, completing, completes (中高研四六托雅 1207/998)","The rebels had taken complete control...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used when you are emphasizing something, to mean ‘to the greatest degree possible’","example":"We were in complete agreement."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"including all the parts, etc. that are necessary; whole","example":"a complete change"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"including something as an extra part or feature","example":"in complete silence"}]],["computer","/kəmˈpju:tə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “computer”.","computer [kəmˈpju:tə(r)] -K4 n. 计算机；电脑；电子计算机 (中高雅 589/580)","欧陆词典释义：computer [kəmˈpju:tə(r)] -K4 n. 计算机；电脑；电子计算机 (中高雅 589/580)","The data are then fed into a computer ...",""],["country","/ˈkʌntri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “country”.","country [ˈkʌntri] -K5 n. 国家，国土；国民；乡下，农村；乡村；故乡 adj. 祖国的，故乡的；地方的，乡村的；国家的；粗鲁的；乡村音乐的 (中高雅 166/175)","欧陆词典释义：country [ˈkʌntri] -K5 n. 国家，国土；国民；乡下，农村；乡村；故乡 adj. 祖国的，故乡的；地方的，乡村的；国家的；粗鲁的；乡村音乐的 (中高雅 166/175)","Indonesia is the fourth most populous country in the world.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area of land that has or used to have its own government and laws","example":"European countries"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area of land, especially with particular physical features, suitable for a particular purpose or connected with a particular person or people","example":"leading industrial countries"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the people of a country","example":"She didn't know what life in a foreign country"}]],["cover","/ˈkʌvə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cover”.","cover [ˈkʌvə(r)] -K5 n. 封面，封皮；盖子；掩蔽物;幌子，借口 vt. 包括；采访，报导；涉及 vi. 覆盖；代替 n. (Cover)人名；(英)科弗；(意)科韦尔 时态: covered, covering, covers (中高托雅 560/525)","欧陆词典释义：cover [ˈkʌvə(r)] -K5 n. 封面，封皮；盖子；掩蔽物;幌子，借口 vt. 包括；采访，报导；涉及 vi. 覆盖；代替 n. (Cover)人名；(英)科弗；(意)科韦尔 时态: covered, covering, covers (中高托雅 560/525)","Cover the casserole with a tight-fitting lid...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to place something over or in front of something in order to hide or protect it","example":"Cover the chicken loosely with foil."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to lie or spread over the surface of something","example":"She covered her face with her hands."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to put or spread a layer of liquid, dust, etc. on somebody/something","example":"He laughed to cover ("}]],["create","/kriˈeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “create”.","create [kriˈeɪt] -K5 vt. 创造，创作；造成 时态: created, creating, creates (中高研四六雅 332/449)","欧陆词典释义：create [kriˈeɪt] -K5 vt. 创造，创作；造成 时态: created, creating, creates (中高研四六雅 332/449)","We set business free to create more jobs in Britain...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something happen or exist","example":"Scientists disagree about how the universe was created."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to produce a particular feeling or impression","example":"The main purpose of industry is to create wealth."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give somebody a particular rank or title","example":"The government plans to create more jobs for young people."}]],["cross","/krɒs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cross”.","cross [krɒs] -K2 n. 交叉，十字；十字架，十字形物 adj. 交叉的，相反的；乖戾的；生气的 vt. 杂交；渡过；使相交 vi. 交叉；杂交；横过 时态: crossed, crossing, crosses (中高研四六托宝 1391/1352)","欧陆词典释义：cross [krɒs] -K2 n. 交叉，十字；十字架，十字形物 adj. 交叉的，相反的；乖戾的；生气的 vt. 杂交；渡过；使相交 vi. 交叉；杂交；横过 时态: crossed, crossing, crosses (中高研四六托宝 1391/1352)","She was partly to blame for failing to look as she cross ed the road...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a mark or an object formed by two lines crossing each other (X or +); the mark (X) is often used on paper to show something","example":"I've put a cross on the map to show where the hotel is."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a long vertical piece of wood with a shorter piece across it near the top. In the past people were hung on crosses","example":"Put a tick if the answer is correct and a cross if it's wrong."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the cross","example":"Sign your name on the form where I've put a cross."}]],["cry","/kraɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cry”.","cry [kraɪ] -K4 n. 叫喊；叫声；口号；呼叫 vi. 哭；叫；喊 vt. 叫喊；哭出；大声说 时态: cried, crying, cries (中高 1351/1518)","欧陆词典释义：cry [kraɪ] -K4 n. 叫喊；叫声；口号；呼叫 vi. 哭；叫；喊 vt. 叫喊；哭出；大声说 时态: cried, crying, cries (中高 1351/1518)","I hung up the phone and started to cry ...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to produce tears from your eyes because you are unhappy or hurt","example":"It's all right. Don't cry."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to shout loudly","example":"I just couldn't stop crying."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to make a loud unpleasant noise","example":"The little boy fell over and started to cry."}]],["culture","/ˈkʌltʃə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “culture”.","culture [ˈkʌltʃə(r)] -K4 n. 文化，文明；修养；栽培 vt. [细胞][微] 培养（等于cultivate） (中高研四六托雅 611/983)","欧陆词典释义：culture [ˈkʌltʃə(r)] -K4 n. 文化，文明；修养；栽培 vt. [细胞][微] 培养（等于cultivate） (中高研四六托雅 611/983)","There is just not enough fun and frivolity in culture today.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the customs and beliefs, art, way of life and social organization of a particular country or group","example":"European/Islamic/African/American, etc. culture"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a country, group, etc. with its own beliefs, etc.","example":"working-class culture"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"art, music, literature, etc., thought of as a group","example":"The children are taught to respect different cultures."}]],["dance","/dɑ:ns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dance”.","dance [dɑ:ns] -K4 n. 舞蹈；舞会；舞曲 adj. 舞蹈的；用于跳舞的 vt. 跳舞；使跳跃 vi. 跳舞；跳跃；飘扬 n. (Dance)人名；(英)丹斯；(法)当斯 时态: danced, dancing, dances (中高 1671/2345)","欧陆词典释义：dance [dɑ:ns] -K4 n. 舞蹈；舞会；舞曲 adj. 舞蹈的；用于跳舞的 vt. 跳舞；使跳跃 vi. 跳舞；跳跃；飘扬 n. (Dance)人名；(英)丹斯；(法)当斯 时态: danced, dancing, dances (中高 1671/2345)","Polly had never learned to dance ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a series of movements and steps that are usually performed to music; a particular example of these movements and steps","example":"a dance class/routine"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the art of dancing, especially for entertainment","example":"Find a partner and practise these new dance steps"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an act of dancing","example":"Do you know any other Latin American dances?"}]],["day","/deɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “day”.","day [deɪ] -K5 n. 一天；时期；白昼 adj. 日间的；逐日的 adv. 每天；经常在白天地 n. (Day)人名；(英、法、西)戴；(越)岱；(阿拉伯、土)达伊 (中高雅 90/95)","欧陆词典释义：day [deɪ] -K5 n. 一天；时期；白昼 adj. 日间的；逐日的 adv. 每天；经常在白天地 n. (Day)人名；(英、法、西)戴；(越)岱；(阿拉伯、土)达伊 (中高雅 90/95)","The weather did not help; hot by day , cold at night...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a period of 24 hours","example":"I saw Tom three days ago."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the time between when it becomes light in the morning and when it becomes dark in the evening","example":"‘What day is it today?’ ‘Monday.’"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the hours of the day when you are awake, working, etc.","example":"We’re going away in a few days/in a few days’ time"}]],["decide","/dɪˈsaɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “decide”.","decide [dɪˈsaɪd] -K5 vi. 决定，下决心 vt. 决定；解决；判决 时态: decided, deciding, decides (中高托 456/375)","欧陆词典释义：decide [dɪˈsaɪd] -K5 vi. 决定，下决心 vt. 决定；解决；判决 时态: decided, deciding, decides (中高托 456/375)","She decide d to do a secretarial course...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think carefully about the different possibilities that are available and choose one of them","example":"It's up to you to decide."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make an official or legal judgement","example":"I can't tell you what to do—you'll have to decide for yourself."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to affect the result of something","example":"It was difficult to decide between the two candidates."}]],["deep","/di:p/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deep”.","deep [di:p] -K4 n. 深处；深渊 adj. 深的；低沉的；深奥的 adv. 深入地；深深地；迟 n. (Deep)人名；(英)迪普 级别: deeper, deepest (中高 975/1024)","欧陆词典释义：deep [di:p] -K4 n. 深处；深渊 adj. 深的；低沉的；深奥的 adv. 深入地；深深地；迟 n. (Deep)人名；(英)迪普 级别: deeper, deepest (中高 975/1024)","The water is very deep and mysterious-looking...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a large distance from the top or surface to the bottom","example":"a deep hole/well/river"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"having a large distance from the front edge to the furthest point inside","example":"deep water/snow"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to describe or ask about the depth of something","example":"a deep cut/wound"}]],["different","/ˈdɪfrənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “different”.","different [ˈdɪfrənt] -K5 adj. 不同的；个别的，与众不同的 (中高雅 237/177)","欧陆词典释义：different [ˈdɪfrənt] -K5 adj. 不同的；个别的，与众不同的 (中高雅 237/177)","London was different from most European capitals...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not the same as somebody/something; not like somebody/something else","example":"American English is significantly different from British English."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"separate and individual","example":"It's very different to what I'm used to."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"unusual; not like other people or things","example":"He saw he was no different than anybody else."}]],["difficult","/ˈdɪfɪkəlt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “difficult”.","difficult [ˈdɪfɪkəlt] -K5 adj. 困难的；不随和的；执拗的 (中高雅 608/439)","欧陆词典释义：difficult [ˈdɪfɪkəlt] -K5 adj. 困难的；不随和的；执拗的 (中高雅 608/439)","Hobart found it difficult to get her first book published...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not easy; needing effort or skill to do or to understand","example":"a difficult problem/task/exam"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"full of problems; causing a lot of trouble","example":"It's difficult"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not easy to please; not helpful","example":"It's really difficult to read your writing."}]],["draw","/drɔ:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “draw”.","draw [drɔ:] -K5 n. 平局；抽签 vi. 拉；拖 vt. 画；拉；吸引 n. (Draw)人名；(英)德劳 时态: drew, drawn, drawing, draws (中高托 592/429)","欧陆词典释义：draw [drɔ:] -K5 n. 平局；抽签 vi. 拉；拖 vt. 画；拉；吸引 n. (Draw)人名；(英)德劳 时态: drew, drawn, drawing, draws (中高托 592/429)","She would sit there draw ing with the pencil stub...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make pictures, or a picture of something, with a pencil, pen or chalk","example":"You draw beautifully."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to move something/somebody by pulling it or them gently","example":"to draw a picture/diagram/graph"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to pull a vehicle such as a carriage","example":"She drew a house."}]],["drink","/drɪŋk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “drink”.","drink [drɪŋk] -K4 n. 酒，饮料；喝酒 vt. 喝，饮；吸收；举杯庆贺 vi. 喝酒；饮水；干杯 时态: drank, drunk, drinking, drinks (中高 1232/1284)","欧陆词典释义：drink [drɪŋk] -K4 n. 酒，饮料；喝酒 vt. 喝，饮；吸收；举杯庆贺 vi. 喝酒；饮水；干杯 时态: drank, drunk, drinking, drinks (中高 1232/1284)","He drank his cup of tea...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a liquid for drinking; an amount of a liquid that you drink","example":"Can I have a drink"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"alcohol or an alcoholic drink; something that you drink on a social occasion","example":"soft drinks ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a social occasion where you have alcoholic drinks","example":"a drink of water"}]],["drive","/draɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “drive”.","drive [draɪv] -K5 n. 驱动器；驾车；[心理] 内驱力，推进力；快车道 vi. 开车；猛击；飞跑 vt. 推动，发动（机器等）；驾驶（马车，汽车等）；驱赶 时态: drove, driven, driving, drives (中高 490/640)","欧陆词典释义：drive [draɪv] -K5 n. 驱动器；驾车；[心理] 内驱力，推进力；快车道 vi. 开车；猛击；飞跑 vt. 推动，发动（机器等）；驾驶（马车，汽车等）；驱赶 时态: drove, driven, driving, drives (中高 490/640)","I drove into town and went to a restaurant for dinner...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to operate a vehicle so that it goes in a particular direction","example":"Can you drive?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to take somebody somewhere in a car, taxi, etc.","example":"Don't drive so fast!"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to own or use a particular type of vehicle","example":"I drove to work this morning."}]],["early","/ˈɜ:li/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “early”.","early [ˈɜ:li] -K5 adj. 早期的；早熟的 adv. 提早；在初期 n. (Early)人名；(英)厄尔利 级别: earlier, earliest (中高 365/245)","欧陆词典释义：early [ˈɜ:li] -K5 adj. 早期的；早熟的 adv. 提早；在初期 n. (Early)人名；(英)厄尔利 级别: earlier, earliest (中高 365/245)","I knew I had to get up early ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"near the beginning of a period of time, an event etc.","example":"the early morning"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"arriving, or done before the usual, expected or planned time","example":"my earliest memories"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"Old English","example":"The project is still in the early stages."}]],["earth","/ɜ:θ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “earth”.","earth [ɜ:θ] -K4 n. 地球；地表，陆地；土地，土壤；尘事，俗事；兽穴 vt. 把（电线）[电] 接地；盖（土）；追赶入洞穴 vi. 躲进地洞 时态: earthed, earthing, earths (中高 1547/1026)","欧陆词典释义：earth [ɜ:θ] -K4 n. 地球；地表，陆地；土地，土壤；尘事，俗事；兽穴 vt. 把（电线）[电] 接地；盖（土）；追赶入洞穴 vi. 躲进地洞 时态: earthed, earthing, earths (中高 1547/1026)","The space shuttle Atlantis returned safely to earth today. “",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the world; the planet that we live on","example":"the planet Earth"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"land; the hard surface of the world that is not the sea or the sky; the ground","example":"the history of life on earth"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the substance that plants grow in","example":"the earth’s ozone layer"}]],["easy","/ˈi:zi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “easy”.","easy [ˈi:zi] -K5 adj. 容易的；舒适的 vt. 发出停划命令 adv. 不费力地，从容地 vi. 停止划桨 级别: easier, easiest (中高 549/502)","欧陆词典释义：easy [ˈi:zi] -K5 adj. 容易的；舒适的 vt. 发出停划命令 adv. 不费力地，从容地 vi. 停止划桨 级别: easier, easiest (中高 549/502)","The shower is easy to install...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not difficult; done or obtained without a lot of effort or problems","example":"an easy exam/job"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"comfortable, relaxed and not worried","example":"He didn't make it easy"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"open to attack; not able to defend yourself","example":"Their house isn't the easiest place to get to."}]],["elephant","/ˈelɪfənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “elephant”.","elephant [ˈelɪfənt] -2 n. 象；大号图画纸 (中高研四六 4355/4323)","欧陆词典释义：elephant [ˈelɪfənt] -2 n. 象；大号图画纸 (中高研四六 4355/4323)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “elephant”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a very large animal with thick grey skin, large ears, two curved outer teeth called tusks","example":"herds of elephants/elephant herds"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"a baby elephant"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a problem or question that everyone knows about but does not mention because it is easier not to discuss it","example":"a conservationist who cares for orphaned elephants"}]],["email","/'i:meɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “email”.","email ['i:meɪl] -K n. 电子信函 vt. 给…发电子邮件 n. (Email)人名；(法)埃马伊 (中雅)","欧陆词典释义：email ['i:meɪl] -K n. 电子信函 vt. 给…发电子邮件 n. (Email)人名；(法)埃马伊 (中雅)","You can contact us by e-mail...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a way of sending messages and data to other people by means of computers connected together in a network","example":"to send a message by email"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a message sent by email","example":"Thanks for your email."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 20th cent.","example":"An email arrives in your inbox."}]],["enjoy","/ɪnˈdʒɔɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “enjoy”.","enjoy [ɪnˈdʒɔɪ] -K4 vt. 欣赏，享受；喜爱；使过得快活 时态: enjoyed, enjoying, enjoys (中高 881/685)","欧陆词典释义：enjoy [ɪnˈdʒɔɪ] -K4 vt. 欣赏，享受；喜爱；使过得快活 时态: enjoyed, enjoying, enjoys (中高 881/685)","Ross had always enjoy ed the company of women...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to get pleasure from something","example":"We thoroughly enjoyed our time in New York."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be happy and get pleasure from what you are doing","example":"Thanks for a great evening. I really enjoyed it"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have something good that is an advantage to you","example":"I enjoy playing tennis and squash."}]],["evening","/ˈi:vnɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “evening”.","evening [ˈi:vnɪŋ] -K4 n. 晚上；傍晚；（联欢性的）晚会；后期 adj. 在晚上的；为晚上的；晚上用的 int. 晚上好（等于good evening） 原型: evening 是 even 的现在分词 (中高雅 961/651)","欧陆词典释义：evening [ˈi:vnɪŋ] -K4 n. 晚上；傍晚；（联欢性的）晚会；后期 adj. 在晚上的；为晚上的；晚上用的 int. 晚上好（等于good evening） 原型: evening 是 even 的现在分词 (中高雅 961/651)","All he did that evening was sit around the flat...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the part of the day between the afternoon and the time you go to bed","example":"I'll see you tomorrow evening."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an event of a particular type happening in the evening","example":"Come over on Thursday evening."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"What do you usually do in the evening"}]],["every","/ˈevri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “every”.","every [ˈevri] -K5 adj. 每一的，每个的；每隔…的 n. (Every)人名；(英)埃夫里 (中高 172/210)","欧陆词典释义：every [ˈevri] -K5 adj. 每一的，每个的；每隔…的 n. (Every)人名；(英)埃夫里 (中高 172/210)","Every village has a green, a church, a pub and a manor house...",[{"pos":"determiner","definition":"used with singular nouns to refer to all the members of a group of things or people","example":"She knows every student in the school."},{"pos":"determiner","definition":"all possible","example":"I could hear every word they said."},{"pos":"determiner","definition":"used to say how often something happens or is done","example":"We enjoyed every minute of our stay."}]],["example","/ɪgˈzɑ:mpl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “example”.","example [ɪgˈzɑ:mpl] -K5 n. 例子；榜样 vt. 作为…的例子；为…做出榜样 vi. 举例 (中高雅 852/511)","欧陆词典释义：example [ɪgˈzɑ:mpl] -K5 n. 例子；榜样 vt. 作为…的例子；为…做出榜样 vi. 举例 (中高雅 852/511)","The doctors gave numerous example s of patients being expelled from hospital...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something such as an object, a fact or a situation that shows, explains or supports what you say","example":"Can you give me an example of what you mean?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that is typical of or represents a particular group or set","example":"This dictionary has many examples of how words are used."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person or their behaviour that is thought to be a good model for others to copy","example":"Just to give you an example of his generosity—he gave me his old car and wouldn't take any money for it."}]],["face","/feɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “face”.","face [feɪs] -K5 n. 脸；表面；面子；面容；外观；威信 vi. 向；朝 vt. 面对；面向；承认；抹盖 n. (Face)人名；(法)法斯；(意)法切 时态: faced, facing, faces (中高托雅 330/282)","欧陆词典释义：face [feɪs] -K5 n. 脸；表面；面子；面容；外观；威信 vi. 向；朝 vt. 面对；面向；承认；抹盖 n. (Face)人名；(法)法斯；(意)法切 时态: faced, facing, faces (中高托雅 330/282)","He rolled down his window and stuck his face out...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the front part of the head between the forehead","example":"a pretty/round/freckled face"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an expression that is shown on somebody’s face","example":"He buried his face in his hands."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having the type of face","example":"You should have seen the look on her face"}]],["fact","/fækt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “fact”.","fact [fækt] -K5 n. 事实；实际；真相 (中高研四 235/201)","欧陆词典释义：fact [fækt] -K5 n. 事实；实际；真相 (中高研四 235/201)","His chances do not seem good in view of the fact that the Chief Prosecutor has already voiced his public disapproval...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to refer to a particular situation that exists","example":"I could no longer ignore the fact that he was deeply unhappy."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that is known to be true, especially when it can be proved","example":"Despite the fact that"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"things that are true rather than things that have been invented","example":"Due to the fact that"}]],["far","/fɑ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “far”.","far [fɑ:(r)] -K5 n. 远方 adj. 远的；久远的 adv. 很；遥远地；久远地；到很远的距离；到很深的程度 n. (Far)人名；(德、西、塞)法尔 级别: further, furthest (中高 252/287)","欧陆词典释义：far [fɑ:(r)] -K5 n. 远方 adj. 远的；久远的 adv. 很；遥远地；久远地；到很远的距离；到很深的程度 n. (Far)人名；(德、西、塞)法尔 级别: further, furthest (中高 252/287)","I know a nice little Italian restaurant not far from here...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"a long distance away","example":"We didn't go far."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used when you are asking or talking about the distance between two places or the distance that has been travelled or is to be travelled","example":"Have you come far?"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a long time from the present; for a large part of a particular period of time","example":"It's not far to the beach."}]],["father","/ˈfɑ:ðə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “father”.","father [ˈfɑ:ðə(r)] -K5 n. 父亲，爸爸；神父；祖先；前辈 vt. 发明，创立；当…的父亲 时态: fathered, fathering, fathers (中高 267/364)","欧陆词典释义：father [ˈfɑ:ðə(r)] -K5 n. 父亲，爸爸；神父；祖先；前辈 vt. 发明，创立；当…的父亲 时态: fathered, fathering, fathers (中高 267/364)","His father was a painter...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a male parent of a child or an animal; a person who is acting as the father to a child","example":"Ben's a wonderful father."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person’s ancestors","example":"You've been like a father"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the first man to introduce a new way of thinking about something or of doing something","example":"Our new boss is a father of three"}]],["feel","/fi:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “feel”.","feel [fi:l] -K5 n. 感觉；触摸 vi. 觉得；摸索 vt. 感觉；认为；触摸；试探 时态: felt, feeling, feels (中高雅 134/135)","欧陆词典释义：feel [fi:l] -K5 n. 感觉；触摸 vi. 觉得；摸索 vt. 感觉；认为；触摸；试探 时态: felt, feeling, feels (中高雅 134/135)","I am feel ing very depressed...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to experience a particular feeling or emotion","example":"The heat made him feel faint."},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to notice or be aware of something because it is touching you or having a physical effect on you","example":"She sounded more confident than she felt."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to become aware of something even though you cannot see it, hear it, etc.","example":"I was feeling guilty."}]],["field","/fi:ld/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “field”.","field [fi:ld] -K4 n. 领域；牧场；旷野；战场；运动场 adj. 扫描场；田赛的；野生的 vt. 把暴晒于场上；使上场 vi. 担任场外队员 n. (Field)人名；(英、法、德、葡)菲尔德 时态: fielded, fielding, fields (中高雅 439/495)","欧陆词典释义：field [fi:ld] -K4 n. 领域；牧场；旷野；战场；运动场 adj. 扫描场；田赛的；野生的 vt. 把暴晒于场上；使上场 vi. 担任场外队员 n. (Field)人名；(英、法、德、葡)菲尔德 时态: fielded, fielding, fields (中高雅 439/495)","a field of wheat...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area of land in the country used for growing crops or keeping animals in, usually surrounded by a fence, etc.","example":"People were working in the fields."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an area of land used for the purpose mentioned","example":"a ploughed field"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a large area of land covered with the thing mentioned; an area from which the thing mentioned is obtained","example":"a field of wheat"}]],["find","/faɪnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “find”.","find [faɪnd] -K5 n. 发现 vi. 裁决 vt. 查找，找到；发现；认为；感到；获得 n. (Find)人名；(丹)芬 时态: found, finding, finds (中高 95/92)","欧陆词典释义：find [faɪnd] -K5 n. 发现 vi. 裁决 vt. 查找，找到；发现；认为；感到；获得 n. (Find)人名；(丹)芬 时态: found, finding, finds (中高 95/92)","The police also found a pistol...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to discover somebody/something unexpectedly or by chance","example":"Look what I've found!"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to get back something/somebody that was lost after searching for it/them","example":"We've found a great new restaurant near the office."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to discover something/somebody by searching, studying or thinking carefully","example":"A whale was found washed up on the shore."}]],["fire","/ˈfaɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “fire”.","fire [ˈfaɪə(r)] -K2 n. 火；火灾；炮火；炉火；热情；激情；磨难 vt. 点燃；解雇；开除；使发光；烧制；激动；放枪 vi. 着火；射击；开枪；激动；烧火 时态: fired, firing, fires (中高雅 653/693)","欧陆词典释义：fire [ˈfaɪə(r)] -K2 n. 火；火灾；炮火；炉火；热情；激情；磨难 vt. 点燃；解雇；开除；使发光；烧制；激动；放枪 vi. 着火；射击；开枪；激动；烧火 时态: fired, firing, fires (中高雅 653/693)","They saw a big flash and a huge ball of fire reaching hundreds of feet into the sky...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the flames, light and heat, and often smoke, that are produced when something burns","example":"Most animals are afraid of fire."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"flames that are out of control and destroy buildings, trees, etc.","example":"The car was now on fire"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a pile of burning fuel, such as wood or coal, used for cooking food or heating a room","example":"The warehouse has been badly damaged by fire."}]],["first","/fɜ:st/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “first”.","first [fɜ:st] -K5 num. 第一 n. 第一；开始；冠军 adj. 第一的；基本的；最早的 adv. 第一；首先；优先；宁愿 n. (First)人名；(英)弗斯特；(捷)菲尔斯特 (中高 86/79)","欧陆词典释义：first [fɜ:st] -K5 num. 第一 n. 第一；开始；冠军 adj. 第一的；基本的；最早的 adv. 第一；首先；优先；宁愿 n. (First)人名；(英)弗斯特；(捷)菲尔斯特 (中高 86/79)","She lost 16 pounds in the first month of her diet.",[{"pos":"determiner","definition":"happening or coming before all other similar things or people; 1st","example":"his first wife"},{"pos":"ordinal number","definition":"the most important or best","example":"the first turning on the right"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"Old English","example":"It was the first time they had ever met."}]],["fish","/fɪʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “fish”.","fish [fɪʃ] -K4 n. 鱼，鱼类 vt. 钓鱼，捕鱼；搜寻 vi. 捕鱼，钓鱼；用钩捞取 n. (Fish)人名；(英、西)菲什；(俄)菲施 时态: fished, fishing, fishes (中高雅 947/954)","欧陆词典释义：fish [fɪʃ] -K4 n. 鱼，鱼类 vt. 钓鱼，捕鱼；搜寻 vi. 捕鱼，钓鱼；用钩捞取 n. (Fish)人名；(英、西)菲什；(俄)菲施 时态: fished, fishing, fishes (中高雅 947/954)","I was chatting to an islander who had just caught a fish ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a creature that lives in water, breathes through gills","example":"They caught several fish."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the flesh of fish eaten as food","example":"tropical/marine/freshwater fish"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"shoals"}]],["floor","/flɔ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “floor”.","floor [flɔ:(r)] -K4 n. 地板，地面；楼层；基底；议员席 vt. 铺地板；打倒，击倒；（被困难）难倒 时态: floored, flooring, floors (中高 639/791)","欧陆词典释义：floor [flɔ:(r)] -K4 n. 地板，地面；楼层；基底；议员席 vt. 铺地板；打倒，击倒；（被困难）难倒 时态: floored, flooring, floors (中高 639/791)","Jack's sitting on the floor watching TV...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the surface of a room that you walk on","example":"a wooden/concrete/marble, etc. floor"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the bottom surface of a vehicle","example":"ceramic floor tiles"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"all the rooms that are on the same level of a building","example":"The body was lying on the kitchen floor."}]],["flower","/ˈflaʊə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “flower”.","flower [ˈflaʊə(r)] -K4 n. 花；精华；开花植物 vt. 使开花；用花装饰 vi. 成熟，发育；开花；繁荣；旺盛 n. (Flower)人名；(英)弗劳尔 时态: flowered, flowering, flowers (中高雅 1489/1270)","欧陆词典释义：flower [ˈflaʊə(r)] -K4 n. 花；精华；开花植物 vt. 使开花；用花装饰 vi. 成熟，发育；开花；繁荣；旺盛 n. (Flower)人名；(英)弗劳尔 时态: flowered, flowering, flowers (中高雅 1489/1270)","Each individual flower is tiny.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the coloured part of a plant from which the seed or fruit develops. Flowers","example":"The plant has a beautiful bright red flower."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a plant grown for the beauty of its flowers","example":"The roses are in flower"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a flower with its stem","example":"The crocuses are late coming into flower"}]],["food","/fu:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “food”.","food [fu:d] -K5 n. 食物；养料 (中高雅 366/466)","欧陆词典释义：food [fu:d] -K5 n. 食物；养料 (中高雅 366/466)","Enjoy your food .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"things that people or animals eat","example":"a shortage of food/food shortages"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular type of food","example":"food and drink"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Old English","example":"the food industry"}]],["foot","/fʊt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “foot”.","foot [fʊt] -K5 n. 脚；英尺；步调；末尾 vt. 支付；给……换底 vi. 步行；跳舞；总计 n. (Foot)人名；(英)富特 时态: footed, footing, foots (中高雅 380/459)","欧陆词典释义：foot [fʊt] -K5 n. 脚；英尺；步调；末尾 vt. 支付；给……换底 vi. 步行；跳舞；总计 n. (Foot)人名；(英)富特 时态: footed, footing, foots (中高雅 380/459)","She stamped her foot again.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the lowest part of the leg, below the ankle, on which a person or an animal stands","example":"My feet are aching."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having or using the type or number of foot/feet mentioned","example":"to get/rise to your feet"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the part of a sock, stocking","example":"I've been on my feet"}]],["forest","/ˈfɒrɪst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “forest”.","forest [ˈfɒrɪst] -K3 n. 森林 vt. 植树于，使成为森林 n. (Forest)人名；(法)福雷；(英、西)福雷斯特 时态: forested, foresting, forests (中高研四六雅 1108/1108)","欧陆词典释义：forest [ˈfɒrɪst] -K3 n. 森林 vt. 植树于，使成为森林 n. (Forest)人名；(法)福雷；(英、西)福雷斯特 时态: forested, foresting, forests (中高研四六雅 1108/1108)","Parts of the forest are still dense and inaccessible.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large area of land that is thickly covered with trees","example":"a tropical forest"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a mass of tall narrow objects that are close together","example":"a forest fire"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"Thousands of hectares of forest are destroyed each year."}]],["free","/fri:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “free”.","free [fri:] -K5 adj. 免费的；自由的，不受约束的；[化学] 游离的 vt. 使自由，解放；释放 adv. 自由地；免费 n. (Free)人名；(英)弗里 时态: freed, freeing, frees 级别: freer, freest (中高 473/497)","欧陆词典释义：free [fri:] -K5 adj. 免费的；自由的，不受约束的；[化学] 游离的 vt. 使自由，解放；释放 adv. 自由地；免费 n. (Free)人名；(英)弗里 时态: freed, freeing, frees 级别: freer, freest (中高 473/497)","The seminars are free , with lunch provided.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not under the control or in the power of somebody else; able to do what you want","example":"I have no ambitions other than to have a happy life and be free."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"not restricted or controlled by anyone else; able to do or say what you want","example":"Students have a free choice"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"not a prisoner or slave","example":"You are free to come and go as you please."}]],["fruit","/fru:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “fruit”.","fruit [fru:t] -K4 n. 水果；产物 vt. 使……结果实 vi. 结果实 n. (Fruit)人名；(法)弗吕；(英)弗鲁特 时态: fruited, fruiting, fruits (中高雅 1662/1809)","欧陆词典释义：fruit [fru:t] -K4 n. 水果；产物 vt. 使……结果实 vi. 结果实 n. (Fruit)人名；(法)弗吕；(英)弗鲁特 时态: fruited, fruiting, fruits (中高雅 1662/1809)","Fresh fruit and vegetables provide fibre and vitamins.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the part of a plant that consists of one or more seeds and flesh, can be eaten as food and usually tastes sweet","example":"tropical fruits, such as bananas and pineapples"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a part of a plant or tree that is formed after the flowers have died and in which seeds develop","example":"Eat plenty of fresh fruit and vegetables."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"all the natural things that the earth produces","example":"a piece of fruit"}]],["full","/fʊl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “full”.","full [fʊl] -K5 n. 全部；完整 adj. 完全的，完整的；满的，充满的；丰富的；完美的；丰满的；详尽的 vt. 把衣服缝得宽大 adv. 十分，非常；完全地；整整 级别: fuller, fullest (中高 503/309)","欧陆词典释义：full [fʊl] -K5 n. 全部；完整 adj. 完全的，完整的；满的，充满的；丰富的；完美的；丰满的；详尽的 vt. 把衣服缝得宽大 adv. 十分，非常；完全地；整整 级别: fuller, fullest (中高 503/309)","Once the container is full , it stays shut until you turn it clockwise.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"containing or holding as much or as many as possible; having no empty space","example":"a full bottle of wine"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"having or containing a large number or amount of something","example":"She could only nod, because her mouth was full."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"thinking or talking a lot about a particular thing","example":"My suitcase was full of books."}]],["game","/geɪm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “game”.","game [geɪm] -K5 n. 游戏；比赛 adj. 勇敢的 vi. 赌博 n. (Game)人名；(英)盖姆；(法)加姆；(西)加梅 时态: gamed, gaming, games (中高 273/464)","欧陆词典释义：game [geɪm] -K5 n. 游戏；比赛 adj. 勇敢的 vi. 赌博 n. (Game)人名；(英)盖姆；(法)加姆；(西)加梅 时态: gamed, gaming, games (中高 273/464)","the wonderful game of football.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an activity or a sport with rules in which people or teams compete against each other","example":"card games"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an occasion of playing a game","example":"board games"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the way in which somebody plays a game","example":"a game of chance/skill"}]],["garden","/ˈgɑ:dn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “garden”.","garden [ˈgɑ:dn] -K4 n. 花园；菜园 vt. 栽培花木 vi. 从事园艺；在园中种植 n. (Garden)人名；(英、意、巴基)加登 时态: gardened, gardening, gardens (中高雅 1043/700)","欧陆词典释义：garden [ˈgɑ:dn] -K4 n. 花园；菜园 vt. 栽培花木 vi. 从事园艺；在园中种植 n. (Garden)人名；(英、意、巴基)加登 时态: gardened, gardening, gardens (中高雅 1043/700)","the most beautiful garden on Earth.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of land next to or around your house where you can grow flowers, fruit, vegetables, etc., usually with a lawn","example":"a front/back garden"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an area in a yard where you grow flowers or plants","example":"children playing in the garden"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a public park","example":"garden flowers/plants"}]],["girl","/gɜ:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “girl”.","girl [gɜ:l] -K5 n. 女孩；姑娘，未婚女子；女职员，女演员；（男人的）女朋友 n. （捷）吉尔 (中高 363/362)","欧陆词典释义：girl [gɜ:l] -K5 n. 女孩；姑娘，未婚女子；女职员，女演员；（男人的）女朋友 n. （捷）吉尔 (中高 363/362)","an eleven year old girl ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a female child","example":"a baby girl"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a daughter","example":"a little girl"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a young woman","example":"Hello, girls and boys!"}]],["give","/gɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “give”.","give [gɪv] -K5 n. 弹性；弯曲；伸展性 vi. 捐赠；面向；有弹性；气候转暖 vt. 给；产生；让步；举办；授予 n. (Give)人名；(意)吉韦 时态: gave, given, giving, gives (中高雅 98/71)","欧陆词典释义：give [gɪv] -K5 n. 弹性；弯曲；伸展性 vi. 捐赠；面向；有弹性；气候转暖 vt. 给；产生；让步；举办；授予 n. (Give)人名；(意)吉韦 时态: gave, given, giving, gives (中高雅 98/71)","She stretched her arms out and gave a great yawn...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to hand something to somebody so that they can look at it, use it or keep it for a time","example":"Give the letter to your mother when you've read it."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to hand something to somebody as a present; to allow somebody to have something as a present","example":"She gave her ticket to the woman at the check-in desk."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to provide somebody with something","example":"Give your mother the letter."}]],["glass","/glɑ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “glass”.","glass [glɑ:s] -K4 n. 玻璃；玻璃制品；镜子 vt. 反映；给某物加玻璃 vi. 成玻璃状 n. (Glass)人名；(英、法、德、意)格拉斯 时态: glassed, glassing, glasses (中高雅 820/844)","欧陆词典释义：glass [glɑ:s] -K4 n. 玻璃；玻璃制品；镜子 vt. 反映；给某物加玻璃 vi. 成玻璃状 n. (Glass)人名；(英、法、德、意)格拉斯 时态: glassed, glassing, glasses (中高雅 820/844)","a pane of glass .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a hard, usually transparent, substance used, for example, for making windows and bottles","example":"a sheet/pane of glass"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a container made of glass, used for drinking out of","example":"frosted/toughened glass"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the contents of a glass","example":"a glass bottle/dish/roof"}]],["good","/gʊd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “good”.","good [gʊd] -K5 n. 好处；善行；慷慨的行为 adj. 好的；优良的；愉快的；虔诚的 adv. 好 n. (Good)人名；(英)古德；(瑞典)戈德 级别: better, best (中高雅 110/73)","欧陆词典释义：good [gʊd] -K5 n. 好处；善行；慷慨的行为 adj. 好的；优良的；愉快的；虔诚的 adv. 好 n. (Good)人名；(英)古德；(瑞典)戈德 级别: better, best (中高雅 110/73)","We had a really good time together...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"of high quality or an acceptable standard","example":"a good book"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"pleasant; that you enjoy or want","example":"good food"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"sensible, logical or strongly supporting what is being discussed","example":"The piano was in good condition."}]],["great","/greɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “great”.","great [greɪt] -K5 n. 大师；大人物；伟人们 adj. 伟大的，重大的；极好的，好的；主要的 级别: greater, greatest (中高 160/129)","欧陆词典释义：great [greɪt] -K5 n. 大师；大人物；伟人们 adj. 伟大的，重大的；极好的，好的；主要的 级别: greater, greatest (中高 160/129)","The room had a great bay window.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"very large; much bigger than average in size or quantity","example":"A great crowd had gathered."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to emphasize an adjective of size or quality","example":"People were arriving in great numbers."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"much more than average in degree or quantity","example":"The great majority of"}]],["green","/gri:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “green”.","green [gri:n] -K5 n. 绿色；青春 n. (Green)人名；(英、意)格林；(瑞典、芬)格伦 adj. 绿色的；青春的 vt. 使…变绿色 vi. 变绿色 级别: greener, greenest (中高雅宝 890/985)","欧陆词典释义：green [gri:n] -K5 n. 绿色；青春 n. (Green)人名；(英、意)格林；(瑞典、芬)格伦 adj. 绿色的；青春的 vt. 使…变绿色 vi. 变绿色 级别: greener, greenest (中高雅宝 890/985)","shiny red and green apples...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having the colour of grass or the leaves of most plants and trees","example":"green beans"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"covered with grass or other plants","example":"Wait for the light to turn green ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"not yet ready to eat","example":"green fields/hills"}]],["ground","/graʊnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ground”.","ground [graʊnd] -K5 n. 地面；土地；范围；战场;根据 v. 研磨（grind的过去分词）；压迫 adj. 土地的；地面上的；磨碎的；磨过的 vt. 使接触地面；打基础；使搁浅 vi. 着陆；搁浅 时态: grounded, grinding, grinds 原型: ground 是 grind 的过去式和过去分词 (中高雅 522/455)","欧陆词典释义：ground [graʊnd] -K5 n. 地面；土地；范围；战场;根据 v. 研磨（grind的过去分词）；压迫 adj. 土地的；地面上的；磨碎的；磨过的 vt. 使接触地面；打基础；使搁浅 vi. 着陆；搁浅 时态: grounded, grinding, grinds 原型: ground 是 grind 的过去式和过去分词 (中高雅 522/455)","Forty or fifty women were sitting cross-legged on the ground ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the solid surface of the earth","example":"I found her lying on the ground"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"soil on the surface of the earth","example":"He lost his balance and fell to the ground"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"an area of open land","example":"2 metres above/below ground"}]],["group","/gru:p/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “group”.","group [gru:p] -K5 n. 组；团体 adj. 群的；团体的 vt. 把…聚集；把…分组 vi. 聚合 时态: grouped, grouping, groups (中高雅宝 163/142)","欧陆词典释义：group [gru:p] -K5 n. 组；团体 adj. 群的；团体的 vt. 把…聚集；把…分组 vi. 聚合 时态: grouped, grouping, groups (中高雅宝 163/142)","The trouble involved a small group of football supporters...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a number of people or things that are together in the same place or that are connected in some way","example":"a group of girls/trees/houses"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a number of companies that are owned by the same person or organization","example":"A group of us is/are going to the theatre this evening."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a number of musicians who perform together, especially to play pop music","example":"Students stood around in groups"}]],["grow","/grəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “grow”.","grow [grəʊ] -K5 vi. 发展；生长；渐渐变得… vt. 使生长；种植；扩展 n. (Grow)人名；(英)格罗 时态: grew, grown, growing, grows (中高 353/524)","欧陆词典释义：grow [grəʊ] -K5 vi. 发展；生长；渐渐变得… vt. 使生长；种植；扩展 n. (Grow)人名；(英)格罗 时态: grew, grown, growing, grows (中高 353/524)","We stop grow ing at maturity.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to increase in size, number, strength or quality","example":"The company profits grew by 5% last year."},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to become bigger or taller and develop into an adult","example":"Fears are growing for the safety of a teenager who disappeared a week ago."},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to exist and develop in a particular place; to make plants grow","example":"There is growing opposition to the latest proposals."}]],["guess","/ges/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “guess”.","guess [ges] -K4 n. 猜测；推测 vi. 猜；推测；猜中 vt. 猜测；认为；推测；猜中 n. (Guess)人名；(英)格斯；(德)居斯 n. 盖尔斯（美国服装品牌） 时态: guessed, guessing, guesses (中高 862/2218)","欧陆词典释义：guess [ges] -K4 n. 猜测；推测 vi. 猜；推测；猜中 vt. 猜测；认为；推测；猜中 n. (Guess)人名；(英)格斯；(德)居斯 n. 盖尔斯（美国服装品牌） 时态: guessed, guessing, guesses (中高 862/2218)","The suit was faultless: Wood guess ed that he was a very successful publisher or a banker...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to try and give an answer or make a judgement about something without being sure of all the facts","example":"I don't really know. I'm just guessing."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to find the right answer to a question or the truth without knowing all the facts","example":"We can only guess at her reasons for leaving."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to suppose that something is true or likely","example":"He guessed right/wrong"}]],["hair","/heə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hair”.","hair [heə(r)] -K4 n. 头发；毛发；些微 adj. 毛发的；护理毛发的；用毛发制成的 vt. 除去…的毛发 vi. 生长毛发；形成毛状纤维 (中高 602/668)","欧陆词典释义：hair [heə(r)] -K4 n. 头发；毛发；些微 adj. 毛发的；护理毛发的；用毛发制成的 vt. 除去…的毛发 vi. 生长毛发；形成毛状纤维 (中高 602/668)","I wash my hair every night...",""],["hand","/hænd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hand”.","hand [hænd] -K4 n. 手，手艺；帮助；指针；插手 vt. 传递，交给；支持；搀扶 n. (Hand)人名；(英、瑞典)汉德 时态: handed, handing, hands (中高雅 174/163)","欧陆词典释义：hand [hænd] -K4 n. 手，手艺；帮助；指针；插手 vt. 传递，交给；支持；搀扶 n. (Hand)人名；(英、瑞典)汉德 时态: handed, handing, hands (中高雅 174/163)","I put my hand into my pocket and pulled out the letter...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the part of the body at the end of the arm, including the fingers and thumb","example":"Ian placed a hand on her shoulder."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"using the hand","example":"Put your hand up"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"help in doing something","example":"Keep both hands on the steering wheel at all times."}]],["hard","/hɑ:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hard”.","hard [hɑ:d] -K5 adj. 努力的；硬的；困难的；辛苦的；确实的；严厉的；猛烈的；冷酷无情的 adv. 努力地；困难地；辛苦地；接近地；猛烈地；牢固地 n. (Hard)人名；(英、芬、瑞典)哈德 级别: harder, hardest (中高雅 438/573)","欧陆词典释义：hard [hɑ:d] -K5 adj. 努力的；硬的；困难的；辛苦的；确实的；严厉的；猛烈的；冷酷无情的 adv. 努力地；困难地；辛苦地；接近地；猛烈地；牢固地 n. (Hard)人名；(英、芬、瑞典)哈德 级别: harder, hardest (中高雅 438/573)","He shuffled his feet on the hard wooden floor...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"solid, firm or stiff and difficult to bend or break","example":"Wait for the concrete to go hard."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"difficult to do, understand or answer","example":"a hard mattress"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"full of difficulty and problems, especially because of a lack of money","example":"Diamonds are the hardest known mineral."}]],["head","/hed/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “head”.","head [hed] -K5 n. 头；头痛；上端；最前的部分；理解力 adj. 头的；主要的；在顶端的 vt. 前进；用头顶；作为…的首领；站在…的前头；给…加标题 vi. 出发；成头状物；船驶往 n. (Head)人名；(英)黑德 时态: headed, heading, heads (中高托 251/209)","欧陆词典释义：head [hed] -K5 n. 头；头痛；上端；最前的部分；理解力 adj. 头的；主要的；在顶端的 vt. 前进；用头顶；作为…的首领；站在…的前头；给…加标题 vi. 出发；成头状物；船驶往 n. (Head)人名；(英)黑德 时态: headed, heading, heads (中高托 251/209)","She turned her head away from him...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the part of the body on top of the neck containing the eyes, nose, mouth and brain","example":"She nodded her head"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the mind or brain","example":"He shook his head"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the size of a person’s or animal’s head","example":"The boys hung their heads"}]],["health","/helθ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “health”.","health [helθ] -K5 n. 健康；卫生；保健；兴旺 (中高雅 344/373)","欧陆词典释义：health [helθ] -K5 n. 健康；卫生；保健；兴旺 (中高雅 344/373)","Caffeine is bad for your health .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the condition of a person’s body or mind","example":"Exhaust fumes are bad for your health."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state of being physically and mentally healthy","example":"to be in poor/good/excellent/the best of health"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the work of providing medical services","example":"Smoking can seriously damage your health"}]],["hear","/hɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hear”.","hear [hɪə(r)] -K5 vi. 听；听见 vt. 听到，听；听说；审理 时态: heard, hearing, hears (中高 195/238)","欧陆词典释义：hear [hɪə(r)] -K5 vi. 听；听见 vt. 听到，听；听说；审理 时态: heard, hearing, hears (中高 195/238)","She hear d no further sounds...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be aware of sounds with your ears","example":"I can't hear very well."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to listen or pay attention to somebody/something","example":"She heard footsteps behind her."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be told about something","example":"I couldn’t hear anything."}]],["heart","/hɑ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “heart”.","heart [hɑ:t] -K4 n. 心脏；感情；勇气；心形；要点 vt. 鼓励；铭记 vi. 结心 n. (Heart)人名；(英)哈特 (中高雅 460/654)","欧陆词典释义：heart [hɑ:t] -K4 n. 心脏；感情；勇气；心形；要点 vt. 鼓励；铭记 vi. 结心 n. (Heart)人名；(英)哈特 (中高雅 460/654)","The bullet had passed less than an inch from Andrea's heart ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the organ in the chest that sends blood around the body, usually on the left in humans","example":"The patient's heart stopped beating for a few seconds."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the outside part of the chest where the heart","example":"heart trouble/failure"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the place in a person where the feelings and emotions are thought to be, especially those connected with love","example":"to have a weak heart"}]],["help","/help/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “help”.","help [help] -K5 n. 帮助；补救办法；帮忙者；有益的东西 vt. 帮助；促进；治疗；补救 vi. 帮助；有用；招待 n. (Help)人名；(芬)海尔普 时态: helped, helping, helps (中高 167/204)","欧陆词典释义：help [help] -K5 n. 帮助；补救办法；帮忙者；有益的东西 vt. 帮助；促进；治疗；补救 vi. 帮助；有用；招待 n. (Help)人名；(芬)海尔普 时态: helped, helping, helps (中高 167/204)","He has help ed to raise a lot of money...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make it easier or possible for somebody to do something by doing something for them or by giving them something that they need","example":"Help, I'm stuck!"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to improve a situation; to make it easier for something to happen","example":"He always helps with the housework."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to help somebody move by letting them lean on you, guiding them, etc.","example":"We must all try and help each other."}]],["here","/hɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “here”.","here [hɪə(r)] -K5 n. 这里 adv. 在这里；此时 int. 嘿！；喂！ n. (Here)人名；(罗)赫尔施 (中高 96/117)","欧陆词典释义：here [hɪə(r)] -K5 n. 这里 adv. 在这里；此时 int. 嘿！；喂！ n. (Here)人名；(罗)赫尔施 (中高 96/117)","I'm here all by myself and I know I'm going to get lost...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used after a verb or preposition to mean ‘in, at or to this position or place’","example":"I live here."},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"now; at this point","example":"Put the box here."},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"used when you are giving or showing something to somebody","example":"Let's get out of here."}]],["high","/haɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “high”.","high [haɪ] -K5 n. 高水平；天空；由麻醉品引起的快感；高压地带 adj. 高的；高级的；崇高的；高音调的 adv. 高；奢侈地 n. (High)人名；(英)海伊 级别: higher, highest (中高 141/152)","欧陆词典释义：high [haɪ] -K5 n. 高水平；天空；由麻醉品引起的快感；高压地带 adj. 高的；高级的；崇高的；高音调的 adv. 高；奢侈地 n. (High)人名；(英)海伊 级别: higher, highest (中高 141/152)","a house, with a high wall all around it...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"measuring a long distance from the bottom to the top","example":"What's the highest mountain in the US?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to talk about the distance that something measures from the bottom to the top","example":"The house has a high wall all the way round it."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"at a level which is a long way above the ground or above the level of the sea","example":"shoes with high heels"}]],["history","/ˈhɪstri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “history”.","history [ˈhɪstri] -K5 n. 历史，历史学；历史记录；来历 (中高研四六雅 350/496)","欧陆词典释义：history [ˈhɪstri] -K5 n. 历史，历史学；历史记录；来历 (中高研四六雅 350/496)","The Catholic Church has played a prominent role throughout Polish history .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"all the events that happened in the past","example":"a turning point in human history"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the past events concerned in the development of a particular place, subject, etc.","example":"one of the worst disasters in recent history"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the study of past events as a subject at school or university","example":"a people with no sense of history"}]],["hold","/həʊld/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hold”.","hold [həʊld] -K4 n. 控制；保留 vi. 支持；有效；持续 vt. 持有；拥有；保存；拘留；约束或控制 n. (Hold)人名；(英、德、捷)霍尔德 又作“Hold住”使用，中英混用词汇，表示轻松掌控全局。 [ 过去式 held 过去分词 held或holden 现在分词 holding ] 时态: held, holding, holds (中高雅宝 213/178)","欧陆词典释义：hold [həʊld] -K4 n. 控制；保留 vi. 支持；有效；持续 vt. 持有；拥有；保存；拘留；约束或控制 n. (Hold)人名；(英、德、捷)霍尔德 又作“Hold住”使用，中英混用词汇，表示轻松掌控全局。 [ 过去式 held 过去分词 held或holden 现在分词 holding ] 时态: held, holding, holds (中高雅宝 213/178)","Hold the knife at an angle...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to carry something; to have somebody/something in your hand, arms, etc.","example":"She was holding a large box."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to put your hand on part of your body, usually because it hurts","example":"I held the mouse by its tail."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to keep somebody/something in a particular position","example":"The girl held her father's hand tightly."}]],["holiday","/ˈhɒlədeɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “holiday”.","holiday [ˈhɒlədeɪ] -K4 n. 假日；节日；休息日 vi. 外出度假 n. (Holiday)人名；(英)霍利迪 时态: holidayed, holidaying, holidays (中高雅 1963/948)","欧陆词典释义：holiday [ˈhɒlədeɪ] -K4 n. 假日；节日；休息日 vi. 外出度假 n. (Holiday)人名；(英)霍利迪 时态: holidayed, holidaying, holidays (中高雅 1963/948)","I've just come back from a holiday in the United States...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a period of time when you are not at work or school","example":"the school/summer/Christmas, etc. holidays"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a period of time spent travelling or resting away from home","example":"I'm afraid Mr Walsh is away on holiday"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a day when most people do not go to work or school, especially because of a religious or national celebration","example":"The package includes 20 days' paid holiday"}]],["horse","/hɔ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “horse”.","horse [hɔ:s] -K4 n. 马；骑兵；脚架；海洛因 vt. 使骑马；系马于；捉弄 vi. 骑马；作弄人 n. (Horse)人名；(瑞典)霍尔瑟 时态: horsed, horsing, horses (中高雅 1279/803)","欧陆词典释义：horse [hɔ:s] -K4 n. 马；骑兵；脚架；海洛因 vt. 使骑马；系马于；捉弄 vi. 骑马；作弄人 n. (Horse)人名；(瑞典)霍尔瑟 时态: horsed, horsing, horses (中高雅 1279/803)","A small man on a grey horse had appeared.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large animal with four legs, a mane","example":"He mounted his horse and rode off."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"horse racing","example":"a horse and cart"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"He lost a lot of money on the horses ("}]],["hospital","/ˈhɒspɪtl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hospital”.","hospital [ˈhɒspɪtl] -K5 n. 医院 n. (Hospital)人名；(英)霍斯皮特尔 (中高雅 647/562)","欧陆词典释义：hospital [ˈhɒspɪtl] -K5 n. 医院 n. (Hospital)人名；(英)霍斯皮特尔 (中高雅 647/562)","a children's hospital with 120 beds...",""],["hot","/hɒt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hot”.","hot [hɒt] -K4 adj. 热的；辣的；热情的；激动的；紧迫的 vt. 增加；给…加温 adv. 热；紧迫地 vi. 变热 n. (Hot)人名；(塞)霍特；(法)奥特 级别: hotter, hottest (中高 721/1055)","欧陆词典释义：hot [hɒt] -K4 adj. 热的；辣的；热情的；激动的；紧迫的 vt. 增加；给…加温 adv. 热；紧迫地 vi. 变热 n. (Hot)人名；(塞)霍特；(法)奥特 级别: hotter, hottest (中高 721/1055)","When the oil is hot , add the sliced onion...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a high temperature; producing heat","example":"Do you like this hot weather?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"feeling heat in an unpleasant or uncomfortable way","example":"It's hot today, isn't it?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"making you feel hot","example":"It was hot and getting hotter."}]],["hour","/ˈaʊə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hour”.","hour [ˈaʊə(r)] -K5 n. 小时；钟头；课时；…点钟 n. (Hour)人名；(法)乌尔；(柬)胡 (中高 272/299)","欧陆词典释义：hour [ˈaʊə(r)] -K5 n. 小时；钟头；课时；…点钟 n. (Hour)人名；(法)乌尔；(柬)胡 (中高 272/299)","They waited for about two hour s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"60 minutes; one of the 24 parts that a day is divided into","example":"It will take about an hour to get there."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a period of about an hour, used for a particular purpose","example":"The interview lasted half an hour."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a fixed period of time during which people work, an office is open, etc.","example":"It was a three-hour exam."}]],["idea","/aɪˈdɪə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “idea”.","idea [aɪˈdɪə] -K5 n. 想法；主意；概念 (中高雅 311/268)","欧陆词典释义：idea [aɪˈdɪə] -K5 n. 想法；主意；概念 (中高雅 311/268)","It's a good idea to plan ahead...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a plan, thought or suggestion, especially about what to do in a particular situation","example":"It would be a good idea"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a picture or an impression in your mind of what somebody/something is like","example":"I like the idea of living on a boat."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an opinion or a belief about something","example":"He already had an idea for his next novel."}]],["job","/dʒɒb/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “job”.","job [dʒɒb] -K5 n. 工作；职业 vt. 承包；代客买卖 vi. 做零工 n. (Job)人名；(英)乔布；(法、葡)若布；(?-1605)约伯〈俄〉俄罗斯正教会莫斯科牧首。；(德、塞、捷、荷、意)约布 时态: jobbed, jobbing, jobs (中高雅 243/272)","欧陆词典释义：job [dʒɒb] -K5 n. 工作；职业 vt. 承包；代客买卖 vi. 做零工 n. (Job)人名；(英)乔布；(法、葡)若布；(?-1605)约伯〈俄〉俄罗斯正教会莫斯科牧首。；(德、塞、捷、荷、意)约布 时态: jobbed, jobbing, jobs (中高雅 243/272)","Once I'm in America I can get a job ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"work for which you receive regular payment","example":"He's trying to get a job"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular task or piece of work that you have to do","example":"She took a job"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a responsibility or duty","example":"His brother's just lost his job"}]],["jump","/dʒʌmp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “jump”.","jump [dʒʌmp] -K4 n. 跳跃；暴涨；惊跳 vt. 跳跃；使跳跃；跳过；突升 vi. 跳跃；暴涨；猛增 n. (Jump)人名；(英)江普 时态: jumped, jumping, jumps (中高 1346/1784)","欧陆词典释义：jump [dʒʌmp] -K4 n. 跳跃；暴涨；惊跳 vt. 跳跃；使跳跃；跳过；突升 vi. 跳跃；暴涨；猛增 n. (Jump)人名；(英)江普 时态: jumped, jumping, jumps (中高 1346/1784)","I jump ed over the fence...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move quickly off the ground or away from a surface by pushing yourself with your legs and feet","example":"‘Quick, jump!’ he shouted."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to pass over something by jumping","example":"to jump into the air/over a wall/into the water"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to move quickly and suddenly","example":"The children were jumping up and down with excitement."}]],["keep","/ki:p/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “keep”.","keep [ki:p] -K5 vt. 保持；经营；遵守；饲养 vi. 保持；继续不断 n. 保持；生计；生活费 n. (Keep)人名；(英)基普 时态: kept, keeping, keeps (中高雅 156/171)","欧陆词典释义：keep [ki:p] -K5 vt. 保持；经营；遵守；饲养 vi. 保持；继续不断 n. 保持；生计；生活费 n. (Keep)人名；(英)基普 时态: kept, keeping, keeps (中高雅 156/171)","The noise kept him awake...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to stay in a particular condition or position; to make somebody/something do this","example":"We huddled together to keep warm."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to continue doing something; to do something repeatedly","example":"The notice said ‘Keep off ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to delay somebody","example":"Keep left along the wall."}]],["key","/ki:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “key”.","key [ki:] -K4 n. （打字机等的）键；关键；钥匙 vt. 键入；锁上；调节…的音调；提供线索 vi. 使用钥匙 adj. 关键的 n. (Key)人名；(英)基；(德、荷、瑞典)凯 时态: keyed, keying, keys (中高雅 1093/1267)","欧陆词典释义：key [ki:] -K4 n. （打字机等的）键；关键；钥匙 vt. 键入；锁上；调节…的音调；提供线索 vi. 使用钥匙 adj. 关键的 n. (Key)人名；(英)基；(德、荷、瑞典)凯 时态: keyed, keying, keys (中高雅 1093/1267)","They put the key in the door and entered...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a specially shaped piece of metal used for locking a door, starting a car, etc.","example":"to insert/turn the key"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a thing that makes you able to understand or achieve something","example":"the car keys"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"any of the buttons that you press to operate a computer or typewriter","example":"a bunch of keys"}]],["kind","/kaɪnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “kind”.","kind [kaɪnd] -K2 n. 种类；性质 adj. 和蔼的；宽容的；令人感激的 n. (Kind)人名；(德、俄、法、捷)金德；(瑞典)欣德 级别: kinder, kindest (中高 250/337)","欧陆词典释义：kind [kaɪnd] -K2 n. 种类；性质 adj. 和蔼的；宽容的；令人感激的 n. (Kind)人名；(德、俄、法、捷)金德；(瑞典)欣德 级别: kinder, kindest (中高 250/337)","The party needs a different kind of leadership...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of people or things that are the same in some way; a particular variety or type","example":"three kinds of cakes/cake"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"Old English","example":"music of all/various/different kinds"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"consisting of goods or services, not money","example":"Exercises of this kind are very popular."}]],["kitchen","/ˈkɪtʃɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “kitchen”.","kitchen [ˈkɪtʃɪn] -K4 n. 厨房；炊具；炊事人员 n. (Kitchen)人名；(英)基钦 (中高托雅 1051/1124)","欧陆词典释义：kitchen [ˈkɪtʃɪn] -K4 n. 厨房；炊具；炊事人员 n. (Kitchen)人名；(英)基钦 (中高托雅 1051/1124)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “kitchen”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a room in which meals are cooked or prepared","example":"She's in the kitchen."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"We ate at the kitchen table."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a very large number of things, probably more than is necessary","example":"I sat at the kitchen island eating a bowl of cereal."}]],["know","/nəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “know”.","know [nəʊ] -K3 vt. 知道；认识；懂得 vi. 了解；熟悉；确信 时态: knew, known, knowing, knows (中高 47/49)","欧陆词典释义：know [nəʊ] -K3 vt. 知道；认识；懂得 vi. 了解；熟悉；确信 时态: knew, known, knowing, knows (中高 47/49)","I don't know the name of the place...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have information in your mind as a result of experience or because you have learned or been told it","example":"Do you know his address?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to realize, understand or be aware of something","example":"The cause of the fire is not yet known."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to feel certain about something","example":"All I know"}]],["lake","/leɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “lake”.","lake [leɪk] -K3 n. 湖；深红色颜料；胭脂红 vt. （使）血球溶解 vi. （使）血球溶解 n. (Lake)人名；(德、塞、瑞典)拉克；(英)莱克 (中高雅 1950/1812)","欧陆词典释义：lake [leɪk] -K3 n. 湖；深红色颜料；胭脂红 vt. （使）血球溶解 vi. （使）血球溶解 n. (Lake)人名；(德、塞、瑞典)拉克；(英)莱克 (中高雅 1950/1812)","They can go fishing in the lake ...",""],["land","/lænd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “land”.","land [lænd] -K5 n. 国土；陆地；地面 vt. 使…登陆；使…陷于；将…卸下 vi. 登陆；到达 n. (Land)人名；(英、德、葡、瑞典)兰德 时态: landed, landing, lands (中高托雅 566/472)","欧陆词典释义：land [lænd] -K5 n. 国土；陆地；地面 vt. 使…登陆；使…陷于；将…卸下 vi. 登陆；到达 n. (Land)人名；(英、德、葡、瑞典)兰德 时态: landed, landing, lands (中高托雅 566/472)","Good agricultural land is in short supply.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the surface of the earth that is not sea","example":"It was good to be back on land"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an area of ground, especially of a particular type or used for a particular purpose","example":"We made the journey by land"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the area of ground that somebody owns, especially when you think of it as property that can be bought or sold","example":"In the distance the crew sighted land."}]],["language","/ˈlæŋgwɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “language”.","language [ˈlæŋgwɪdʒ] -K4 n. 语言；语言文字；表达能力 (中高雅 722/436)","欧陆词典释义：language [ˈlæŋgwɪdʒ] -K4 n. 语言；语言文字；表达能力 (中高雅 722/436)","the English language ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the system of communication in speech and writing that is used by people of a particular country or area","example":"the Japanese language"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the use by humans of a system of sounds and words to communicate","example":"It takes a long time to learn to speak a language"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular style of speaking or writing","example":"Italian is my first language"}]],["large","/lɑ:dʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “large”.","large [lɑ:dʒ] -K5 adj. 大的；多数的；广博的 adv. 大大地；夸大地 n. 大 n. (Large)人名；(英)拉奇；(法)拉尔热 级别: larger, largest (中高 220/181)","欧陆词典释义：large [lɑ:dʒ] -K5 adj. 大的；多数的；广博的 adv. 大大地；夸大地 n. 大 n. (Large)人名；(英)拉奇；(法)拉尔热 级别: larger, largest (中高 220/181)","The Pike lives mainly in large rivers and lakes...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"big in size or quantity","example":"a large area/family/house/car/appetite"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used to describe one size in a range of sizes of clothes, food, products used in the house, etc.","example":"a large number of people"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"wide in range and involving many things","example":"very large sums of money"}]],["last","/lɑ:st/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “last”.","last [lɑ:st] -K2 n. 末尾，最后；上个；鞋楦（做鞋的模型） adj. 最后的；最近的，最新的；仅剩的；最不可能…的 vi. 持续；维持，够用；持久 vt. 度过，拖过；使维持 adv. 最后地；上次，最近；最后一点 n. (Last)人名；(英、德、葡、罗、瑞典)拉斯特 时态: lasted, lasting, lasts (高 130/119)","欧陆词典释义：last [lɑ:st] -K2 n. 末尾，最后；上个；鞋楦（做鞋的模型） adj. 最后的；最近的，最新的；仅剩的；最不可能…的 vi. 持续；维持，够用；持久 vt. 度过，拖过；使维持 adv. 最后地；上次，最近；最后一点 n. (Last)人名；(英、德、葡、罗、瑞典)拉斯特 时态: lasted, lasting, lasts (高 130/119)","I got married last July...",[{"pos":"determiner","definition":"happening or coming after all other similar things or people","example":"We caught the last bus home."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"most recent","example":"It's the last house on the left."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"only remaining","example":"She was last to arrive."}]],["late","/leɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “late”.","late [leɪt] -K5 adj. 晚的；迟的；已故的；最近的 adv. 晚；迟；最近；在晚期 级别: later, latest (中高 437/298)","欧陆词典释义：late [leɪt] -K5 adj. 晚的；迟的；已故的；最近的 adv. 晚；迟；最近；在晚期 级别: later, latest (中高 437/298)","It was late in the afternoon...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"near the end of a period of time, a person’s life, etc.","example":"in the late afternoon"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"arriving, happening or done after the expected, arranged or usual time","example":"in late summer"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"near the end of the day","example":"She married in her late twenties ("}]],["laugh","/lɑ:f/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “laugh”.","laugh [lɑ:f] -K5 n. 笑；引人发笑的事或人 vi. 笑 vt. 以笑表示；使…笑得 时态: laughed, laughing, laughs (中高 861/1021)","欧陆词典释义：laugh [lɑ:f] -K5 n. 笑；引人发笑的事或人 vi. 笑 vt. 以笑表示；使…笑得 时态: laughed, laughing, laughs (中高 861/1021)","He was about to offer an explanation, but she was beginning to laugh ...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make the sounds and movements of your face that show you are happy or think something is funny","example":"to laugh loudly/aloud/out loud"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to say that you are in a very good position, especially because you have done something successfully","example":"You never laugh at my jokes!"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"The show was hilarious—I couldn't stop laughing."}]],["learn","/lɜ:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “learn”.","learn [lɜ:n] -K5 vt. 学习；得知；认识到 vi. 学习；获悉 时态: learned, learning, learns (中高雅 304/520)","欧陆词典释义：learn [lɜ:n] -K5 vt. 学习；得知；认识到 vi. 学习；获悉 时态: learned, learning, learns (中高雅 304/520)","Their children were going to learn English...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to gain knowledge or skill by studying, from experience, from being taught, etc.","example":"to learn a language/a musical instrument/a skill"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become aware of something by hearing about it from somebody else","example":"I learned a lot from my father."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to study and repeat something in order to be able to remember it","example":"You can learn a great deal just from watching other players."}]],["leave","/li:v/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “leave”.","leave [li:v] -K5 vt. 离开；留下；遗忘；委托 vi. 离开，出发；留下 n. 许可，同意；休假 时态: left, leaving, leaves (中高雅 150/127)","欧陆词典释义：leave [li:v] -K5 vt. 离开；留下；遗忘；委托 vi. 离开，出发；留下 n. 许可，同意；休假 时态: left, leaving, leaves (中高雅 150/127)","He would not be allowed to leave the country...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to go away from a person or a place","example":"Come on, it's time we left."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to stop living at a place, belonging to a group, working for an employer, etc.","example":"The plane leaves for Dallas at 12.35."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to leave your wife, husband or partner permanently","example":"I hate leaving home."}]],["left","/left/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “left”.","left [left] -K3 adj. 左边的；左派的；剩下的 adv. 在左面 n. 左边；左派；激进分子 v. 离开（leave的过去式） 原型: left 是 leave 的过去式和过去分词 (中高 771/1045)","欧陆词典释义：left [left] -K3 adj. 左边的；左派的；剩下的 adv. 在左面 n. 左边；左派；激进分子 v. 离开（leave的过去式） 原型: left 是 leave 的过去式和过去分词 (中高 771/1045)","Is there any gin left ?...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"on or to the left side","example":"Turn left at the intersection."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"on the side of your body which is towards the west when you are facing north","example":"Look left and right before you cross the road."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"Fewer people write with their left hand than with their right."}]],["leg","/leg/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “leg”.","leg [leg] -K4 n. 腿；支柱 (中高 856/851)","欧陆词典释义：leg [leg] -K4 n. 腿；支柱 (中高 856/851)","He was tapping his walking stick against his leg .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"one of the long parts that connect the feet to the rest of the body","example":"Sit on the floor, stretching your legs out in front of you."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the leg","example":"I broke my leg playing football."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the part of a pair of trousers/pants that covers the leg","example":"How many legs does a centipede have?"}]],["lesson","/ˈlesn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “lesson”.","lesson [ˈlesn] -K3 n. 教训；课 vt. 教训；上课 (中高 1325/1953)","欧陆词典释义：lesson [ˈlesn] -K3 n. 教训；课 vt. 教训；上课 (中高 1325/1953)","It would be his last French lesson for months...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a period of time in which somebody is taught something","example":"She gives piano lessons."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that is intended to be learned","example":"All new students are given lessons in/on"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an experience, especially an unpleasant one, that somebody can learn from so that it does not happen again in the future","example":"I’m having/taking"}]],["letter","/ˈletə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “letter”.","letter [ˈletə(r)] -K5 n. 信；字母，文字；证书；文学，学问；字面意义 vt. 写字母于 vi. 写印刷体字母 n. (Letter)人名；(英)莱特 时态: lettered, lettering, letters (中高雅 628/454)","欧陆词典释义：letter [ˈletə(r)] -K5 n. 信；字母，文字；证书；文学，学问；字面意义 vt. 写字母于 vi. 写印刷体字母 n. (Letter)人名；(英)莱特 时态: lettered, lettering, letters (中高雅 628/454)","I had received a letter from a very close friend.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a message that is written down or printed on paper and usually put in an envelope and sent to somebody","example":"a business/thank-you, etc. letter"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a written or printed sign representing a sound used in speech","example":"a letter of"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a sign in the shape of a letter that is sewn onto clothes to show that a person plays in a school or college sports team","example":"to post a letter"}]],["library","/ˈlaɪbrəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “library”.","library [ˈlaɪbrəri] -K3 n. 图书馆，藏书室；文库 (中高雅 2129/967)","欧陆词典释义：library [ˈlaɪbrəri] -K3 n. 图书馆，藏书室；文库 (中高雅 2129/967)","the local library ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a building in which collections of books, CDs, newspapers, etc. are kept for people to read, study or borrow","example":"a public/reference/university, etc. library"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a room in a large house where most of the books are kept","example":"a library book"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a personal collection of books, CDs, etc.","example":"a toy library"}]],["life","/laɪf/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “life”.","life [laɪf] -K5 n. 生活，生存；寿命 (中高 114/128)","欧陆词典释义：life [laɪf] -K5 n. 生活，生存；寿命 (中高 114/128)","a baby's first minutes of life ...",""],["light","/laɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “light”.","light [laɪt] -K3 n. 光；光线；灯；打火机；领悟；浅色；天窗 adj. 轻的；浅色的；明亮的；轻松的；容易的；清淡的 vi. 点着；变亮；着火 vt. 照亮；点燃；着火 adv. 轻地；清楚地；轻便地 n. (Light)人名；(英)莱特 时态: lit, lighting, lights 级别: lighter, lightest (中高雅 464/529)","欧陆词典释义：light [laɪt] -K3 n. 光；光线；灯；打火机；领悟；浅色；天窗 adj. 轻的；浅色的；明亮的；轻松的；容易的；清淡的 vi. 点着；变亮；着火 vt. 照亮；点燃；着火 adv. 轻地；清楚地；轻便地 n. (Light)人名；(英)莱特 时态: lit, lighting, lights 级别: lighter, lightest (中高雅 464/529)","Cracks of light filtered through the shutters...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the energy from the sun, a lamp, etc. that makes it possible to see things","example":"bright/dim light"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a particular type of light","example":"a room with good natural light"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a thing that produces light, especially an electric light","example":"in the fading light of a summer’s evening"}]],["like","/laɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “like”.","like [laɪk] -K5 vt. 喜欢；想；愿意 vi. 喜欢；希望 prep. 像；如同 adj. 同样的；相似的 n. 爱好；同样的人或物 adv. 可能 conj. 好像 时态: liked, liking, likes (中高 74/88)","欧陆词典释义：like [laɪk] -K5 vt. 喜欢；想；愿意 vi. 喜欢；希望 prep. 像；如同 adj. 同样的；相似的 n. 爱好；同样的人或物 adv. 可能 conj. 好像 时态: liked, liking, likes (中高 74/88)","He looks like Father Christmas...",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"similar to somebody/something","example":"She's wearing a dress like mine."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used to ask somebody’s opinion of somebody/something","example":"He's very like his father."},{"pos":"conjunction","definition":"used to show what is usual or typical for somebody","example":"She looks nothing like"}]],["line","/laɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “line”.","line [laɪn] -K5 n. 路线，航线；排；绳 vt. 排成一行；划线于；以线条标示；使…起皱纹 vi. 排队；站成一排 n. (Line)人名；(英)莱恩；(俄)利涅 时态: lined, lining, lines (中高研四六雅 276/277)","欧陆词典释义：line [laɪn] -K5 n. 路线，航线；排；绳 vt. 排成一行；划线于；以线条标示；使…起皱纹 vi. 排队；站成一排 n. (Line)人名；(英)莱恩；(俄)利涅 时态: lined, lining, lines (中高研四六雅 276/277)","Draw a line down that page's center.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a long thin mark on a surface","example":"a straight/wavy/dotted/diagonal line"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a long thin mark on the ground to show the limit or border of something, especially of a playing area in some sports","example":"a vertical/horizontal line"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a mark like a line on somebody’s skin that people usually get as they get older","example":"parallel lines"}]],["list","/lɪst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “list”.","list [lɪst] -K5 n. [计] 列表；清单；目录 vi. 列于表上 vt. 列出；记入名单内 n. (List)人名；(匈)李斯特；(英、德、法、西、捷)利斯特 时态: listed, listing, lists (中高研四六雅宝 761/716)","欧陆词典释义：list [lɪst] -K5 n. [计] 列表；清单；目录 vi. 列于表上 vt. 列出；记入名单内 n. (List)人名；(匈)李斯特；(英、德、法、西、捷)利斯特 时态: listed, listing, lists (中高研四六雅宝 761/716)","We are making a list of the top ten men we would not want to be married to...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a series of names, items, figures, etc., especially when they are written or printed","example":"a shopping/wine/price list"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the fact of a ship leaning to one side","example":"to make a list"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"to draw up a list"}]],["little","/ˈlɪtl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “little”.","little [ˈlɪtl] -K5 adj. 小的；很少的；短暂的；小巧可爱的 adv. 完全不 n. 少许；没有多少；短时间 n. (Little)人名；(英)利特尔 (中高 256/291)","欧陆词典释义：little [ˈlɪtl] -K5 adj. 小的；很少的；短暂的；小巧可爱的 adv. 完全不 n. 少许；没有多少；短时间 n. (Little)人名；(英)利特尔 (中高 256/291)","I had little money and little free time...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not big; small; smaller than others","example":"a little house"},{"pos":"determiner","definition":"used after an adjective to show affection or dislike, especially in a patronizing","example":"a little group of tourists"},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"young","example":"a little old lady"}]],["live","/lɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “live”.","live [lɪv] -K3 adj. 活的；生动的；实况转播的；精力充沛的 vt. 经历；度过 vi. 活；居住；生存 n. (Live)人名；(法)利夫 时态: lived, living, lives (中高雅 210/267)","欧陆词典释义：live [lɪv] -K3 adj. 活的；生动的；实况转播的；精力充沛的 vt. 经历；度过 vi. 活；居住；生存 n. (Live)人名；(法)利夫 时态: lived, living, lives (中高雅 210/267)","She has live d here for 10 years...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have your home in a particular place","example":"to live in a house"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"to remain alive","example":"Where do you live?"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"to be alive, especially at a particular time","example":"She needs to find somewhere to live"}]],["long","/lɒŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “long”.","long [lɒŋ] -K2 n. 长时间；[语] 长音节；（服装的）长尺寸；长裤 adj. 长的；过长的；做多头的；长时间的；冗长的，长音 vi. 渴望；热望 adv. 长期地；始终 n. （英、法、德、瑞典）朗（人名）；（柬）隆（人名） 时态: longed, longing, longs 级别: longer, longest (中高托 254/217)","欧陆词典释义：long [lɒŋ] -K2 n. 长时间；[语] 长音节；（服装的）长尺寸；长裤 adj. 长的；过长的；做多头的；长时间的；冗长的，长音 vi. 渴望；热望 adv. 长期地；始终 n. （英、法、德、瑞典）朗（人名）；（柬）隆（人名） 时态: longed, longing, longs 级别: longer, longest (中高托 254/217)","Repairs to the cable did not take too long ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"measuring or covering a great length or distance, or a greater length or distance than usual","example":"She had long dark hair."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used for asking or talking about particular lengths or distances","example":"He walked down the long corridor."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"lasting or taking a great amount of time or more time than usual","example":"It was the world's longest bridge."}]],["look","/lʊk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “look”.","look [lʊk] -K5 vt. 看；期待；注意；面向；看上去像 vi. 看；看起来；注意；面向 n. 看；样子；面容 n. (Look)人名；(瑞典)洛克；(英)卢克 时态: looked, looking, looks (中高 85/82)","欧陆词典释义：look [lʊk] -K5 vt. 看；期待；注意；面向；看上去像 vi. 看；看起来；注意；面向 n. 看；样子；面容 n. (Look)人名；(瑞典)洛克；(英)卢克 时态: looked, looking, looks (中高 85/82)","I look ed down the hallway to room number nine...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to turn your eyes in a particular direction","example":"If you look carefully you can just see our house from here."},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to try to find somebody/something","example":"She looked at me and smiled."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to pay attention to something","example":"‘Has the mail come yet?’ ‘I'll look and see"}]],["lose","/lu:z/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “lose”.","lose [lu:z] -K5 vt. 浪费；使沉溺于；使迷路；遗失；错过 vi. 失败；受损失 n. (Lose)人名；(英)洛斯；(德)洛泽 时态: lost, losing, loses (中高研四六 283/329)","欧陆词典释义：lose [lu:z] -K5 vt. 浪费；使沉溺于；使迷路；遗失；错过 vi. 失败；受损失 n. (Lose)人名；(英)洛斯；(德)洛泽 时态: lost, losing, loses (中高研四六 283/329)","A C Milan lost the Italian Cup Final...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be unable to find something/somebody","example":"I've lost my keys."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have something/somebody taken away from you as a result of an accident, getting old, dying, etc.","example":"The tickets seem to have got lost"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have something taken away by somebody/something","example":"She lost her husband in the crowd."}]],["love","/lʌv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “love”.","love [lʌv] -K5 n. 恋爱；亲爱的；酷爱；喜爱的事物；爱情，爱意；疼爱；热爱；爱人，所爱之物 v. 爱，热爱；爱戴；赞美，称赞；喜爱；喜好；喜欢；爱慕 n. （英）洛夫（人名） 时态: loved, loving, loves (中高 390/670)","欧陆词典释义：love [lʌv] -K5 n. 恋爱；亲爱的；酷爱；喜爱的事物；爱情，爱意；疼爱；热爱；爱人，所爱之物 v. 爱，热爱；爱戴；赞美，称赞；喜爱；喜好；喜欢；爱慕 n. （英）洛夫（人名） 时态: loved, loving, loves (中高 390/670)","Oh, Amy, I love you...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a strong feeling of deep affection for somebody/something, especially a member of your family or a friend","example":"a mother’s love for her children"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a strong feeling of affection for somebody that you are sexually attracted to","example":"love of your country"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the strong feeling of enjoyment that something gives you","example":"He seems incapable of love."}]],["lunch","/lʌntʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “lunch”.","lunch [lʌntʃ] -K4 n. 午餐 vt. 吃午餐；供给午餐 vi. 吃午餐；供给午餐 时态: lunched, lunching, lunches (中高雅 1586/1615)","欧陆词典释义：lunch [lʌntʃ] -K4 n. 午餐 vt. 吃午餐；供给午餐 vi. 吃午餐；供给午餐 时态: lunched, lunching, lunches (中高雅 1586/1615)","Shall we meet somewhere for lunch ?...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a meal eaten in the middle of the day","example":"She's gone to lunch."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"early 19th cent.","example":"I'm ready for some lunch."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"behaving in a strange or confused way","example":"What shall we have for lunch"}]],["machine","/məˈʃi:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “machine”.","machine [məˈʃi:n] -K4 n. 机械，机器；机构；机械般工作的人 vt. 用机器制造 n. (Machine)人名；(意)马基内 时态: machined, machining, machines (中高雅 1022/761)","欧陆词典释义：machine [məˈʃi:n] -K4 n. 机械，机器；机构；机械般工作的人 vt. 用机器制造 n. (Machine)人名；(意)马基内 时态: machined, machining, machines (中高雅 1022/761)","I put the coin in the machine and pulled the lever...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of equipment with moving parts that is designed to do a particular job. The power used to work a machine","example":"Machines have replaced human labour in many industries."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular machine, for example in the home, when you do not refer to it by its full name","example":"to operate/run a machine"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a group of people that control an organization or part of an organization","example":"How does this machine work?"}]],["main","/meɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “main”.","main [meɪn] -K5 n. 主要部分，要点；体力；总管道 adj. 主要的，最重要的；全力的 n. (Main)人名；(德)迈因；(西)马因；(英、法)梅因 (中高研四六雅 888/376)","欧陆词典释义：main [meɪn] -K5 n. 主要部分，要点；体力；总管道 adj. 主要的，最重要的；全力的 n. (Main)人名；(德)迈因；(西)马因；(英、法)梅因 (中高研四六雅 888/376)","one of the main tourist areas of Amsterdam...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"being the largest or most important of its kind","example":"Be careful crossing the main road"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"the main course"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"We have our main meal at lunchtime."}]],["make","/meɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “make”.","make [meɪk] -K3 vt. 使得；进行；布置，准备，整理；制造；认为；获得；形成；安排；引起；构成 vi. 开始；前进；增大；被制造 n. 制造；构造；性情 n. (Make)人名；(塞、南非)马克 时态: made, making, makes (中高雅 45/43)","欧陆词典释义：make [meɪk] -K3 vt. 使得；进行；布置，准备，整理；制造；认为；获得；形成；安排；引起；构成 vi. 开始；前进；增大；被制造 n. 制造；构造；性情 n. (Make)人名；(塞、南非)马克 时态: made, making, makes (中高雅 45/43)","I'd just like to make a comment...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to create or prepare something by combining materials or putting parts together","example":"to make a table/dress/cake"},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to write, create or prepare something","example":"to make bread/cement/paper"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to arrange a bed so that it is neat and ready for use","example":"She makes her own clothes."}]],["man","/mæn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “man”.","man [mæn] -K5 n. 人；男人；人类；丈夫；雇工 vt. 操纵；给…配置人员；使增强勇气；在…就位 n. (Man)人名；(俄)马恩；(英、葡、意、罗、捷、尼、老、缅、柬)曼；(日)万 (名) 时态: manned, manning, mans (中高 94/91)","欧陆词典释义：man [mæn] -K5 n. 人；男人；人类；丈夫；雇工 vt. 操纵；给…配置人员；使增强勇气；在…就位 n. (Man)人名；(俄)马恩；(英、葡、意、罗、捷、尼、老、缅、柬)曼；(日)万 (名) 时态: manned, manning, mans (中高 94/91)","He had not expected the young man to reappear before evening...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an adult male human","example":"a good-looking young man"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"humans as a group or from a particular period of history","example":"the relationships between men and women"},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"a person, either male or female","example":"the damage caused by man to the environment"}]],["map","/mæp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “map”.","map [mæp] -K3 vt. 映射；计划；绘制地图；确定基因在染色体中的位置 n. 地图；示意图；染色体图 vi. 基因被安置 n. (Map)人名；(法)马普 时态: mapped, mapping, maps (中高托雅 1542/1681)","欧陆词典释义：map [mæp] -K3 vt. 映射；计划；绘制地图；确定基因在染色体中的位置 n. 地图；示意图；染色体图 vi. 基因被安置 n. (Map)人名；(法)马普 时态: mapped, mapping, maps (中高托雅 1542/1681)","He unfolded the map and set it on the floor...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a drawing or plan of the earth’s surface or part of it, showing countries, towns, rivers, etc.","example":"a map of France"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"early 16th cent.","example":"a street map of Miami"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody/something famous or important","example":"to read a/the map"}]],["market","/ˈmɑ:kɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “market”.","market [ˈmɑ:kɪt] -K5 n. 市场；行情；股票市场；市面；集市；销路；商店 vt. 在市场上出售 vi. 做买卖 n. (Market)人名；(塞)马尔凯特 时态: marketed, marketing, markets (中高雅 402/253)","欧陆词典释义：market [ˈmɑ:kɪt] -K5 n. 市场；行情；股票市场；市面；集市；销路；商店 vt. 在市场上出售 vi. 做买卖 n. (Market)人名；(塞)马尔凯特 时态: marketed, marketing, markets (中高雅 402/253)","He sold boots on a market stall.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an occasion when people buy and sell goods; the open area or building where they meet to do this","example":"a fruit/flower/antiques market"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"business or trade, or the amount of trade in a particular type of goods","example":"an indoor/a street market"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular area, country or section of the population that might buy goods","example":"market stalls/traders"}]],["match","/mætʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “match”.","match [mætʃ] -K5 vt. 使比赛；使相配；敌得过，比得上；相配；与…竞争 vi. 比赛；匹配；相配，相称；相比 n. 比赛，竞赛；匹配；对手；火柴 时态: matched, matching, matches (中高托雅 1972/1097)","欧陆词典释义：match [mætʃ] -K5 vt. 使比赛；使相配；敌得过，比得上；相配；与…竞争 vi. 比赛；匹配；相配，相称；相比 n. 比赛，竞赛；匹配；对手；火柴 时态: matched, matching, matches (中高托雅 1972/1097)","He was watching a football match ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small stick made of wood or cardboard that is used for lighting a fire, cigarette, etc.","example":"a box of matches"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a sports event where people or teams compete against each other","example":"to strike a match"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person who is equal to somebody else in strength, skill, intelligence, etc.","example":"to put a match to something"}]],["matter","/ˈmætə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “matter”.","matter [ˈmætə(r)] -K5 n. 物质；事件 vi. 有关系；要紧 n. (Matter)人名；(英、法)马特；(西)马特尔 (高 528/370)","欧陆词典释义：matter [ˈmætə(r)] -K5 n. 物质；事件 vi. 有关系；要紧 n. (Matter)人名；(英、法)马特；(西)马特尔 (高 528/370)","It was clear that she wanted to discuss some private matter ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a subject or situation that you must consider or deal with","example":"It's a private matter."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the present situation, or the situation that you are talking about","example":"They had important matters to discuss."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used (to ask) if somebody is upset, unhappy, etc. or if there is a problem","example":"She may need your help with some business matters."}]],["meal","/mi:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “meal”.","meal [mi:l] -K3 n. 一餐，一顿饭；膳食 vi. 进餐 (中高雅 1710/1415)","欧陆词典释义：meal [mi:l] -K3 n. 一餐，一顿饭；膳食 vi. 进餐 (中高雅 1710/1415)","She sat next to him throughout the meal ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an occasion when people sit down to eat food, especially breakfast, lunch or dinner","example":"Try not to eat between meals."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the food that is eaten at a meal","example":"Lunch is his main meal of the day."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"grain that has been crushed to produce a powder, used as food for animals and for making flour","example":"to go out for a meal"}]],["mean","/mi:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mean”.","mean [mi:n] -K2 adj. 平均的；卑鄙的；低劣的；吝啬的 vt. 意味；想要；意欲 n. 平均值 vi. 用意 n. (Mean)人名；(柬)棉 时态: meant, meaning, means (中高托雅宝 154/121)","欧陆词典释义：mean [mi:n] -K2 adj. 平均的；卑鄙的；低劣的；吝啬的 vt. 意味；想要；意欲 n. 平均值 vi. 用意 n. (Mean)人名；(柬)棉 时态: meant, meaning, means (中高托雅宝 154/121)","In modern Welsh, 'glas' mean s 'blue'...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have something as a meaning","example":"What does this sentence mean?"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"to intend to say something on a particular occasion","example":"What is meant by"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"to have something as a purpose or intention","example":"Does the name ‘Jos Vos’ mean anything to you"}]],["meet","/mi:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “meet”.","meet [mi:t] -K5 vt. 满足；遇见；对付 vi. 相遇；接触 n. 集会 adj. 合适的；适宜的 n. (Meet)人名；(英)米特 时态: met, meeting, meets (中高宝 288/259)","欧陆词典释义：meet [mi:t] -K5 vt. 满足；遇见；对付 vi. 相遇；接触 n. 集会 adj. 合适的；适宜的 n. (Meet)人名；(英)米特 时态: met, meeting, meets (中高宝 288/259)","I have just met the man I want to spend the rest of my life with...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be in the same place as somebody by chance and talk to them","example":"Maybe we'll meet again some time."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to come together formally in order to discuss something","example":"Did you meet anyone in town?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to come together socially after you have arranged it","example":"The committee meets on Fridays."}]],["member","/ˈmembə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “member”.","member [ˈmembə(r)] -K5 n. 成员；会员；议员 (中高 285/182)","欧陆词典释义：member [ˈmembə(r)] -K5 n. 成员；会员；议员 (中高 285/182)","He refused to name the member s of staff involved...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person, an animal or a plant that belongs to a particular group","example":"a member of staff/society/the family"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person, a country or an organization that has joined a particular group, club or team","example":"characteristics common to all members of the species"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a part of the body, especially an arm or a leg","example":"party/union members"}]],["middle","/ˈmɪdl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “middle”.","middle [ˈmɪdl] -K5 adj. 中间的，中部的；中级的，中等的 n. 中间，中央；腰部 时态: middled, middling, middles (中高 988/1360)","欧陆词典释义：middle [ˈmɪdl] -K5 adj. 中间的，中部的；中级的，中等的 n. 中间，中央；腰部 时态: middled, middling, middles (中高 988/1360)","Howard stood in the middle of the room sipping a cup of coffee...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the part of something that is at an equal distance from all its edges or sides; a point or a period of time between the beginning and the end of something","example":"a lake with an island in the middle"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a person’s waist","example":"He was standing in the middle of the room."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"Old English","example":"The phone rang in the middle of the night."}]],["milk","/mɪlk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “milk”.","milk [mɪlk] -K3 n. 牛奶；乳状物 vt. 榨取；挤…的奶 vi. 挤奶 n. (Milk)人名；(英)米尔克 时态: milked, milking, milks (中高雅宝 2033/1881)","欧陆词典释义：milk [mɪlk] -K3 n. 牛奶；乳状物 vt. 榨取；挤…的奶 vi. 挤奶 n. (Milk)人名；(英)米尔克 时态: milked, milking, milks (中高雅宝 2033/1881)","He popped out to buy a pint of milk .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the white liquid produced by cows, goats","example":"a pint/litre of milk"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the white liquid that is produced by women and female mammals","example":"a bottle/carton of milk"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the white juice of some plants and trees, especially the coconut","example":"fresh/dried/powdered milk"}]],["minute","/'mɪnɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “minute”.","minute ['mɪnɪt] -K1 n. 分，分钟；片刻，一会儿；备忘录，笔记；会议记录 vt. 将…记录下来 adj. 微小的，详细的 [maɪˈnjuːt; US -ˈnuːt; maɪˋnut] (中高托雅 308/348)","欧陆词典释义：minute ['mɪnɪt] -K1 n. 分，分钟；片刻，一会儿；备忘录，笔记；会议记录 vt. 将…记录下来 adj. 微小的，详细的 [maɪˈnjuːt; US -ˈnuːt; maɪˋnut] (中高托雅 308/348)","The pizza will then take about twenty minute s to cook...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"each of the 60 parts of an hour, that are equal to 60 seconds","example":"It's four minutes to six."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a very short time","example":"I'll be back in a few minutes."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"an exact moment in time","example":"Boil the rice for 20 minutes."}]],["money","/ˈmʌni/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “money”.","money [ˈmʌni] -K5 n. 钱；货币；财富 n. (Money)人名；(英)莫尼；(西、法)莫内 (中高雅 232/233)","欧陆词典释义：money [ˈmʌni] -K5 n. 钱；货币；财富 n. (Money)人名；(英)莫尼；(西、法)莫内 (中高雅 232/233)","A lot of the money that you pay at the cinema goes back to the film distributors...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"what you earn by working or selling things, and use to buy things","example":"to borrow/save/spend/earn money"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"coins or paper notes","example":"How much money is there in my account?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person’s wealth including their property","example":"The money is much better in my new job."}]],["month","/mʌnθ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “month”.","month [mʌnθ] -K5 n. 月，一个月的时间 (中高雅 236/214)","欧陆词典释义：month [mʌnθ] -K5 n. 月，一个月的时间 (中高雅 236/214)","The trial is due to begin next month .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"any of the twelve periods of time into which the year is divided, for example May or June","example":"the month of August"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a period of about 30 days, for example, 3 June to 3 July","example":"We're moving house next month"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a long time, especially a period of several months","example":"She earns $1 000 a month"}]],["moon","/mu:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “moon”.","moon [mu:n] -K3 n. 月亮；月球；月光；卫星 vi. 闲荡；出神 vt. 虚度 n. (Moon)人名；(瑞典)莫恩；(柬)蒙；(英)穆恩；(缅)孟 时态: mooned, mooning, moons (中高 2450/2646)","欧陆词典释义：moon [mu:n] -K3 n. 月亮；月球；月光；卫星 vi. 闲荡；出神 vt. 虚度 n. (Moon)人名；(瑞典)莫恩；(柬)蒙；(英)穆恩；(缅)孟 时态: mooned, mooning, moons (中高 2450/2646)","the first man on the moon ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the round object that moves around the earth once every 27½ days and shines at night by light reflected from the sun","example":"the surface of the moon"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the moon","example":"a moon landing"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a natural satellite","example":"a crescent moon"}]],["morning","/ˈmɔ:nɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “morning”.","morning [ˈmɔ:nɪŋ] -K5 n. 早晨；黎明；初期 (中高 357/445)","欧陆词典释义：morning [ˈmɔ:nɪŋ] -K5 n. 早晨；黎明；初期 (中高 357/445)","During the morning your guide will take you around the city...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the early part of the day from the time when people wake up until midday or before lunch","example":"They left for Spain early this morning."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"the part of the day from midnight to midday","example":"See you tomorrow morning"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"in the morning of each day","example":"I prefer coffee in the morning"}]],["mountain","/ˈmaʊntən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mountain”.","mountain [ˈmaʊntən] -K4 n. 山；山脉 n. (Mountain)人名；(英)芒廷 (中高雅 1240/1402)","欧陆词典释义：mountain [ˈmaʊntən] -K4 n. 山；山脉 n. (Mountain)人名；(英)芒廷 (中高雅 1240/1402)","Ben Nevis, in Scotland, is Britain's highest mountain .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a very high hill, often with rocks near the top","example":"a chain/range of mountains"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a very large amount or number of something","example":"to climb a mountain"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"We spent a week walking in the mountains"}]],["mouth","/maʊθ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mouth”.","mouth [maʊθ] -K4 n. 口，嘴；河口 vt. 做作地说，装腔作势地说；喃喃地说出 vi. 装腔作势说话 时态: mouthed, mouthing, mouths (中高托 1060/1011)","欧陆词典释义：mouth [maʊθ] -K4 n. 口，嘴；河口 vt. 做作地说，装腔作势地说；喃喃地说出 vi. 装腔作势说话 时态: mouthed, mouthing, mouths (中高托 1060/1011)","She clamped her hand against her mouth ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the opening in the face used for speaking, eating, etc.; the area inside the head behind this opening","example":"She opened her mouth"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person considered only as somebody who needs to be provided with food","example":"His mouth twisted into a wry smile."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the entrance or opening of something","example":"Their mouths fell open"}]],["move","/mu:v/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “move”.","move [mu:v] -K5 n. 移动；步骤；迁居；策略 vi. 移动；搬家，迁移；离开 vt. 移动；感动 时态: moved, moving, moves (中高 207/220)","欧陆词典释义：move [mu:v] -K5 n. 移动；步骤；迁居；策略 vi. 移动；搬家，迁移；离开 vt. 移动；感动 时态: moved, moving, moves (中高 207/220)","She move d the sheaf of papers into position...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change position or make somebody/something change position in a way that can be seen, heard or felt","example":"Don't move—stay perfectly still."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to change; to change something","example":"The bus was already moving when I jumped onto it."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to make progress in the way or direction mentioned","example":"He could hear someone moving around in the room above."}]],["music","/ˈmju:zɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “music”.","music [ˈmju:zɪk] -K5 n. 音乐，乐曲 (中高雅 392/667)","欧陆词典释义：music [ˈmju:zɪk] -K5 n. 音乐，乐曲 (中高雅 392/667)","classical music .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"sounds that are arranged in a way that is pleasant or exciting to listen to. People sing music","example":"pop/dance/classical/church music"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the art of writing or playing music","example":"to listen to music"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the written or printed signs that represent the sounds to be played or sung in a piece of music","example":"She could hear music playing somewhere."}]],["name","/neɪm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “name”.","name [neɪm] -K5 n. 名称，名字；姓名；名誉 vt. 命名，任命；指定；称呼；提名；叫出 adj. 姓名的；据以取名的 n. (Name)人名；(日)滑(姓)；(英)内姆 时态: named, naming, names (中高 298/271)","欧陆词典释义：name [neɪm] -K5 n. 名称，名字；姓名；名誉 vt. 命名，任命；指定；称呼；提名；叫出 adj. 姓名的；据以取名的 n. (Name)人名；(日)滑(姓)；(英)内姆 时态: named, naming, names (中高 298/271)","'What's his name ?'—'Peter.'...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a word or words that a particular person, animal, place or thing is known by","example":"What's your name?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a reputation that somebody/something has; the opinion that people have about somebody/something","example":"What is/was the name, please? ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having a name or a reputation of the kind mentioned, especially one that is known by a lot of people","example":"Please write your full name and address"}]],["near","/nɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “near”.","near [nɪə(r)] -K5 adj. 近的；亲近的；近似的 adv. 近；接近 prep. 靠近；近似于 时态: neared, nearing, nears 级别: nearer, nearest (中高 706/726)","欧陆词典释义：near [nɪə(r)] -K5 adj. 近的；亲近的；近似的 adv. 近；接近 prep. 靠近；近似于 时态: neared, nearing, nears 级别: nearer, nearest (中高 706/726)","Don't come near me...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a short distance away","example":"His house is very near."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"a short time away in the future","example":"Where's the nearest bank?"},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"coming next after somebody/something","example":"When is your next appointment?"}]],["need","/ni:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “need”.","need [ni:d] -K5 n. 需要，要求；缺乏；必要之物 vt. 需要 vi. 需要 时态: needed, needing, needs (中高 132/132)","欧陆词典释义：need [ni:d] -K5 n. 需要，要求；缺乏；必要之物 vt. 需要 vi. 需要 时态: needed, needing, needs (中高 132/132)","He desperately need ed money...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to require something/somebody because they are essential or very important, not just because you would like to have them","example":"Do you need any help?"},{"pos":"modal verb","definition":"used to show what you should or have to do","example":"It's here if you need it."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"Don't go—I might need you."}]],["nice","/naɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “nice”.","nice [naɪs] -K4 adj. 精密的；美好的；细微的；和蔼的 n. (Nice)人名；(英)尼斯 级别: nicer, nicest (中高宝 897/750)","欧陆词典释义：nice [naɪs] -K4 adj. 精密的；美好的；细微的；和蔼的 n. (Nice)人名；(英)尼斯 级别: nicer, nicest (中高宝 897/750)","I think silk ties can be quite nice ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"pleasant, enjoyable or attractive","example":"a nice day/smile/place"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used before adjectives or adverbs to emphasize how pleasant something is","example":"nice weather"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"kind; friendly","example":"Did you have a nice time"}]],["night","/naɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “night”.","night [naɪt] -K5 n. 夜晚，晚上；黑暗，黑夜 adj. 夜晚的，夜间的 (中高雅 209/216)","欧陆词典释义：night [naɪt] -K5 n. 夜晚，晚上；黑暗，黑夜 adj. 夜晚的，夜间的 (中高雅 209/216)","He didn't sleep a wink all night ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the time between one day and the next when it is dark, when people usually sleep","example":"These animals only come out at night"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the evening until you go to bed","example":"They sleep by day and hunt by night"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an evening when a special event happens","example":"The accident happened on Friday night."}]],["north","/nɔ:θ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “north”.","North [nɔ:θ] -K4 n. 北，北方 adj. 北方的；朝北的 adv. 在北方，向北方 (中高 578/1746)","欧陆词典释义：North [nɔ:θ] -K4 n. 北，北方 adj. 北方的；朝北的 adv. 在北方，向北方 (中高 578/1746)","In the north the ground becomes very cold as the winter snow and ice covers the ground...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the direction that is on your left when you watch the sun rise; one of the four main points of the compass","example":"Which way is north?"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the northern part of a country, a region or the world","example":"cold winds coming from the north"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"the NE states of the US which fought against the South in the American Civil War","example":"Mount Kenya is to the north of"}]],["nose","/nəʊz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “nose”.","nose [nəʊz] -K3 n. 鼻子；嗅觉；突出的部分；探问 vt. 嗅；用鼻子触 vi. 小心探索着前进；探问 时态: nosed, nosing, noses (中高 1735/1887)","欧陆词典释义：nose [nəʊz] -K3 n. 鼻子；嗅觉；突出的部分；探问 vt. 嗅；用鼻子触 vi. 小心探索着前进；探问 时态: nosed, nosing, noses (中高 1735/1887)","She wiped her nose with a tissue...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the part of the face that sticks out above the mouth, used for breathing and smelling things","example":"He broke his nose in the fight."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having the type of nose","example":"She wrinkled her nose in disgust."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the front part of a plane, spacecraft","example":"He pressed his nose up against the window."}]],["note","/nəʊt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “note”.","note [nəʊt] -K4 n. 笔记；音符；票据；注解；纸币；便笺；照会；调子 vt. 注意；记录；注解 n. (Note)人名；(英)诺特 时态: noted, noting, notes (中高托 703/799)","欧陆词典释义：note [nəʊt] -K4 n. 笔记；音符；票据；注解；纸币；便笺；照会；调子 vt. 注意；记录；注解 n. (Note)人名；(英)诺特 时态: noted, noting, notes (中高托 703/799)","Stevens wrote him a note asking him to come to his apartment...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a short piece of writing to help you remember something","example":"Please make a note"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a short informal letter","example":"She made a mental note"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a short comment on a word or passage in a book","example":"Just a quick note to say thank you for a wonderful evening."}]],["number","/ˈnʌmbə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “number”.","number [ˈnʌmbə(r)] -K5 n. 数；（杂志等的）期；号码；数字；算术 vi. 计入；总数达到 vt. 编号；计入；数…的数目；使为数有限 时态: numbered, numbering, numbs 原型: number 是 numb 的比较级 (中高 204/143)","欧陆词典释义：number [ˈnʌmbə(r)] -K5 n. 数；（杂志等的）期；号码；数字；算术 vi. 计入；总数达到 vt. 编号；计入；数…的数目；使为数有限 时态: numbered, numbering, numbs 原型: number 是 numb 的比较级 (中高 204/143)","No, I don't know the room number ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a word or symbol that represents an amount or a quantity","example":"Think of a number and multiply it by two."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used before a figure to show the position of something in a series","example":"a high/low number"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a number","example":"even numbers"}]],["nurse","/nɜ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “nurse”.","nurse [nɜ:s] -K3 vt. 看护，护理；照顾；培养；给…喂奶 vi. 照料，护理；喂奶；当保姆 n. 护士；奶妈，保姆 n. (Nurse)人名；(英)纳斯 时态: nursed, nursing, nurses (中高托雅 1875/1650)","欧陆词典释义：nurse [nɜ:s] -K3 vt. 看护，护理；照顾；培养；给…喂奶 vi. 照料，护理；喂奶；当保姆 n. 护士；奶妈，保姆 n. (Nurse)人名；(英)纳斯 时态: nursed, nursing, nurses (中高托雅 1875/1650)","She had spent 29 years as a nurse ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person whose job is to take care of sick or injured people, usually in a hospital","example":"a qualified/registered nurse"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"(in the past) a woman or girl whose job was to take care of babies or small children in their own homes","example":"student nurses"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"a male nurse"}]],["ocean","/ˈəʊʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ocean”.","ocean [ˈəʊʃn] -K3 n. 海洋；大量；广阔 n. (Ocean)人名；(罗)奥切安 (中高研四雅 1842/3015)","欧陆词典释义：ocean [ˈəʊʃn] -K3 n. 海洋；大量；广阔 n. (Ocean)人名；(罗)奥切安 (中高研四雅 1842/3015)","There were few sights as beautiful as the calm ocean on a warm night.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the mass of salt water that covers most of the earth’s surface","example":"the depths of the ocean"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"one of the five large areas that the ocean","example":"People were swimming in the ocean despite the hurricane warning."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"The plane hit the ocean several miles offshore."}]],["office","/ˈɒfɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “office”.","office [ˈɒfɪs] -K5 n. 办公室；政府机关；官职；营业处 (中高雅 341/303)","欧陆词典释义：office [ˈɒfɪs] -K5 n. 办公室；政府机关；官职；营业处 (中高雅 341/303)","He had an office big enough for his desk and chair, plus his VDU...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a room, set of rooms or building where people work, usually sitting at desks","example":"The company is moving to new offices on the other side of town."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a room in which a particular person works, usually at a desk","example":"Are you going to the office today?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place where a doctor, dentist or vet","example":"an office job"}]],["often","/ˈɒfn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “often”.","often [ˈɒfn] -K5 adv. 常常，时常 (中高 274/230)","欧陆词典释义：often [ˈɒfn] -K5 adv. 常常，时常 (中高 274/230)","They often spent Christmas at Prescott Hill...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"many times","example":"We often go there."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"in many cases","example":"I've often wondered what happened to him."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"Middle English","example":"How often"}]],["old","/əʊld/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “old”.","old [əʊld] -K5 adj. 陈旧的，古老的；年老的 n. 古时 n. (Old)人名；(英)奥尔德 级别: older, oldest (中高 152/126)","欧陆词典释义：old [əʊld] -K5 adj. 陈旧的，古老的；年老的 n. 古时 n. (Old)人名；(英)奥尔德 级别: older, oldest (中高 152/126)","a white-haired old man...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"of a particular age","example":"The baby was only a few hours old."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"having lived for a long time; no longer young","example":"In those days most people left school when they were only fifteen years old."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"old people","example":"At thirty years old, he was already earning £40 000 a year."}]],["once","/wʌns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “once”.","once [wʌns] -K5 adv. 一次；曾经 conj. 一旦 n. 一次，一回 (中高雅 300/548)","欧陆词典释义：once [wʌns] -K5 adv. 一次；曾经 conj. 一旦 n. 一次，一回 (中高雅 300/548)","I met Wilma once , briefly...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"on one occasion only; one time","example":"I've only been there once."},{"pos":"conjunction","definition":"at some time in the past","example":"He cleans his car once a"},{"pos":"conjunction","definition":"used in negative sentences and questions, and after if","example":"She only sees her parents once every"}]],["open","/ˈəʊpən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “open”.","open [ˈəʊpən] -K5 adj. 公开的；敞开的；空旷的；坦率的；营业着的 vi. 开始；展现 vt. 公开；打开 n. 公开；空旷；户外 时态: opened, opening, opens (中高 355/403)","欧陆词典释义：open [ˈəʊpən] -K5 adj. 公开的；敞开的；空旷的；坦率的；营业着的 vi. 开始；展现 vt. 公开；打开 n. 公开；空旷；户外 时态: opened, opening, opens (中高 355/403)","He open ed the window and looked out...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"allowing things or people to go through","example":"A wasp flew in the open window."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"with eyelids","example":"She had left the door wide open"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"spread out; with the edges apart","example":"The door flew open and the children rushed in."}]],["orange","/ˈɒrɪndʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “orange”.","orange [ˈɒrɪndʒ] -K3 adj. 橙色的；橘色的 n. 橙；橙色；桔子 n. (Orange)人名；(英)奥林奇；(法)奥朗热 (中高 3145/3959)","欧陆词典释义：orange [ˈɒrɪndʒ] -K3 adj. 橙色的；橘色的 n. 橙；橙色；桔子 n. (Orange)人名；(英)奥林奇；(法)奥朗热 (中高 3145/3959)","men in bright orange uniforms.",""],["order","/ˈɔ:də(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “order”.","order [ˈɔ:də(r)] -K4 n. 命令；顺序；规则；[贸易] 定单 vt. 命令；整理；定购 vi. 命令；定货 时态: ordered, ordering, orders (中高雅 684/368)","欧陆词典释义：order [ˈɔ:də(r)] -K4 n. 命令；顺序；规则；[贸易] 定单 vt. 命令；整理；定购 vi. 命令；定货 时态: ordered, ordering, orders (中高雅 684/368)","Most schools are extremely unwilling to cut down on staff in order to cut costs.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way in which people or things are placed or arranged in relation to each other","example":"The names are listed in alphabetical order"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the state of being carefully and neatly arranged","example":"in chronological/numerical order"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the state that exists when people obey laws, rules or authority","example":"arranged in order of"}]],["other","/ˈʌðə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “other”.","other [ˈʌðə(r)] -K5 adj. 其他的，另外的 pron. 另外一个 (中高 75/69)","欧陆词典释义：other [ˈʌðə(r)] -K5 adj. 其他的，另外的 pron. 另外一个 (中高 75/69)","They were just like any other young couple...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used to refer to people or things that are additional or different to people or things that have been mentioned or are known about","example":"Mr Harris and Mrs Bate and three other teachers were there."},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"used to refer to the second of two people or things","example":"Are there any other questions?"},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"used to refer to the remaining people or things in a group","example":"I can't see you now— some other time"}]],["outside","/ˌaʊtˈsaɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “outside”.","outside [ˌaʊtˈsaɪd] -K5 adj. 外面的，外部的；外来的 n. 外部；外观 adv. 在外面，向外面；在室外 prep. 在…范围之外 (中高 809/857)","欧陆词典释义：outside [ˌaʊtˈsaɪd] -K5 adj. 外面的，外部的；外来的 n. 外部；外观 adv. 在外面，向外面；在室外 prep. 在…范围之外 (中高 809/857)","the outside of the building...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the outer side or surface of something","example":"The outside of the house needs painting."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the area that is near or around a building, etc.","example":"You can't open the door from the outside."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"the part of a road nearest to the middle","example":"I walked around the outside of the building."}]],["page","/peɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “page”.","page [peɪdʒ] -K5 n. 页；记录；大事件，时期；男侍者 vt. 给…标页码 vi. 翻书页，浏览 n. (Page)人名；(西)帕赫；(英)佩奇；(意)帕杰；(法)帕日 时态: paged, paging, pages (中高 708/658)","欧陆词典释义：page [peɪdʒ] -K5 n. 页；记录；大事件，时期；男侍者 vt. 给…标页码 vi. 翻书页，浏览 n. (Page)人名；(西)帕赫；(英)佩奇；(意)帕杰；(法)帕日 时态: paged, paging, pages (中高 708/658)","Where's your book? Take it out and turn to page 4.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"one side or both sides of a sheet of paper in a book, magazine, etc.","example":"Turn to page 64."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a section of data or information that can be shown on a computer screen at any one time","example":"Someone has torn a page out of this book."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an important event or period of history","example":"a blank/new page"}]],["paint","/peɪnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “paint”.","paint [peɪnt] -K4 vt. 油漆；绘画；装饰；涂色于；描绘；（用语言，文字等）描写；擦脂粉等 vi. 油漆；描绘；绘画；化妆 n. 油漆；颜料，涂料；绘画作品；胭脂等化妆品；色彩，装饰 n. 潘（人名） 时态: painted, painting, paints (中高研四 1555/2040)","欧陆词典释义：paint [peɪnt] -K4 vt. 油漆；绘画；装饰；涂色于；描绘；（用语言，文字等）描写；擦脂粉等 vi. 油漆；描绘；绘画；化妆 n. 油漆；颜料，涂料；绘画作品；胭脂等化妆品；色彩，装饰 n. 潘（人名） 时态: painted, painting, paints (中高研四 1555/2040)","a pot of red paint ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a liquid that is put on surfaces to give them a particular colour; a layer of this liquid when it has dried on a surface","example":"white paint"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"tubes or blocks of paint","example":"gloss/matt/acrylic paint"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"The woodwork has recently been given a fresh coat of paint"}]],["paper","/ˈpeɪpə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “paper”.","paper [ˈpeɪpə(r)] -K5 n. 纸；论文；文件；报纸 adj. 纸做的 vt. 用纸糊；用纸包装 vi. 贴糊墙纸；发交通违章传票 n. (Paper)人名；(俄)帕佩尔 时态: papered, papering, papers (中高雅 519/395)","欧陆词典释义：paper [ˈpeɪpə(r)] -K5 n. 纸；论文；文件；报纸 adj. 纸做的 vt. 用纸糊；用纸包装 vi. 贴糊墙纸；发交通违章传票 n. (Paper)人名；(俄)帕佩尔 时态: papered, papering, papers (中高雅 519/395)","He wrote his name down on a piece of paper for me...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the thin material that you write and draw on and that is also used for wrapping and packing things","example":"a piece/sheet of paper"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a newspaper","example":"a package wrapped in brown paper"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"pieces of paper with writing on them, such as letters, pieces of work or private documents","example":"recycled paper"}]],["parent","/ˈpeərənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “parent”.","parent [ˈpeərənt] -K5 n. 父亲（或母亲）；父母亲；根源 n. (Parent)人名；(法)帕朗；(英、西)帕伦特 (中高雅 327/494)","欧陆词典释义：parent [ˈpeərənt] -K5 n. 父亲（或母亲）；父母亲；根源 n. (Parent)人名；(法)帕朗；(英、西)帕伦特 (中高雅 327/494)","Children need their parent s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person’s father or mother","example":"He's still living with his parents."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an animal or a plant which produces other animals or plants","example":"her adoptive parents"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an organization that produces and owns or controls smaller organizations of the same type","example":"Sue and Ben have recently become parents."}]],["park","/pɑ:k/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “park”.","park [pɑ:k] -K4 n. 公园；[交] 停车场 vt. 停放；放置；寄存 vi. 停放车辆 n. (Park)人名；(英、芬、瑞典)帕克 时态: parked, parking, parks (中高雅 3467/853)","欧陆词典释义：park [pɑ:k] -K4 n. 公园；[交] 停车场 vt. 停放；放置；寄存 vi. 停放车辆 n. (Park)人名；(英、芬、瑞典)帕克 时态: parked, parking, parks (中高雅 3467/853)","Regent's Park...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area of public land in a town or a city where people go to walk, play and relax","example":"Hyde Park"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an area of land used for a particular purpose","example":"We went for a walk in the park."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"(in Britain) an area of land, usually with fields and trees, attached to a large country house","example":"a park bench"}]],["party","/ˈpɑ:ti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “party”.","party [ˈpɑ:ti] -K5 n. 政党，党派；聚会，派对；当事人 [复数 parties] vi. 参加社交聚会 [ 过去式 partied 过去分词 partied 现在分词 partying ] 时态: partied, partying, parties (中高托雅 351/166)","欧陆词典释义：party [ˈpɑ:ti] -K5 n. 政党，党派；聚会，派对；当事人 [复数 parties] vi. 参加社交聚会 [ 过去式 partied 过去分词 partied 现在分词 partying ] 时态: partied, partying, parties (中高托雅 351/166)","a member of the Labour party .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a political organization that you can vote for in elections and whose members have the same aims and ideas","example":"the Democratic and Republican Parties in the United States"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a social occasion, often in a person’s home, at which people eat, drink, talk, dance and enjoy themselves","example":"She belongs to the Labour Party."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a group of people who are doing something together such as travelling or visiting somewhere","example":"the ruling/opposition party"}]],["people","/ˈpi:pl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “people”.","people [ˈpi:pl] -K5 n. 人；人类；民族；公民 vt. 居住于；使住满人 时态: peopled, peopling, peoples (中高 62/75)","欧陆词典释义：people [ˈpi:pl] -K5 n. 人；人类；民族；公民 vt. 居住于；使住满人 时态: peopled, peopling, peoples (中高 62/75)","Millions of people have lost their homes.",""],["perfect","/ˈpɜ:fɪkt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “perfect”.","perfect [ˈpɜ:fɪkt] -K4 n. 完成式 adj. 完美的；最好的；精通的 vt. 使完美；使熟练 n. (Perfect)人名；(英)珀费克特 时态: perfected, perfecting, perfects (中高托雅 1160/1685)","欧陆词典释义：perfect [ˈpɜ:fɪkt] -K4 n. 完成式 adj. 完美的；最好的；精通的 vt. 使完美；使熟练 n. (Perfect)人名；(英)珀费克特 时态: perfected, perfecting, perfects (中高托雅 1160/1685)","He spoke perfect English...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having everything that is necessary; complete and without faults or weaknesses","example":"in perfect condition"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"completely correct; exact and accurate","example":"a perfect set of teeth"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the best of its kind","example":"Well I'm sorry—but nobody's perfect"}]],["person","/ˈpɜ:sn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “person”.","person [ˈpɜ:sn] -K5 n. 人；身体；容貌，外表；人称 n. (Person)人名；(法、俄、德)佩尔松；(瑞典)佩尔松；(英)珀森 (中高雅 345/308)","欧陆词典释义：person [ˈpɜ:sn] -K5 n. 人；身体；容貌，外表；人称 n. (Person)人名；(法、俄、德)佩尔松；(瑞典)佩尔松；(英)珀森 (中高雅 345/308)","At least one person died and several others were injured...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a human as an individual","example":"What sort of person would do a thing like that?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a human, especially one who is not identified","example":"He's a fascinating person."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person working in the area of business mentioned; a person concerned with the thing mentioned","example":"What is she like as a person?"}]],["phone","/fəʊn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “phone”.","phone [fəʊn] -K4 n. 电话；耳机，听筒 vt. 打电话 vi. 打电话 n. (Phone)人名；(老、缅)蓬 时态: phoned, phoning, phones (中研四雅 557/1346)","欧陆词典释义：phone [fəʊn] -K4 n. 电话；耳机，听筒 vt. 打电话 vi. 打电话 n. (Phone)人名；(老、缅)蓬 时态: phoned, phoning, phones (中研四雅 557/1346)","You can buy insurance over the phone ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a system for talking to somebody else over long distances using wires or radio; a machine used for this; a telephone","example":"I have to make a phone call"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the part of a phone that you hold in your hand and speak into; a telephone","example":"The phone rang"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an instrument that uses or makes sound","example":"They like to do business by phone/over the phone"}]],["picture","/ˈpɪktʃə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “picture”.","picture [ˈpɪktʃə(r)] -K4 n. 照片，图画；影片；景色；化身 vt. 画；想像；描写 时态: pictured, picturing, pictures (中高雅 562/626)","欧陆词典释义：picture [ˈpɪktʃə(r)] -K4 n. 照片，图画；影片；景色；化身 vt. 画；想像；描写 时态: pictured, picturing, pictures (中高雅 562/626)","A picture of Rory O'Moore hangs in the dining room at Kildangan.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a painting or drawing, etc. that shows a scene, a person or thing","example":"A picture of flowers hung on the wall."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a photograph","example":"The children were drawing pictures"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an image on a television screen","example":"She wanted a famous artist to paint her picture"}]],["place","/pleɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “place”.","place [pleɪs] -K2 n. 地方；住所；座位 vt. 放置；任命；寄予 vi. 名列前茅；取得名次 n. (Place)人名；(罗)普拉切；(法)普拉斯；(英)普莱斯 时态: placed, placing, places (中高雅 181/162)","欧陆词典释义：place [pleɪs] -K2 n. 地方；住所；座位 vt. 放置；任命；寄予 vi. 名列前茅；取得名次 n. (Place)人名；(罗)普拉切；(法)普拉斯；(英)普莱斯 时态: placed, placing, places (中高雅 181/162)","15 Portland Place , London W1A 4DD.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular position, point or area","example":"Is this the place where it happened?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular city, town, building, etc.","example":"This would be a good place for a picnic."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a building or an area of land used for a particular purpose","example":"I can't be in two places at once."}]],["plan","/plæn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “plan”.","plan [plæn] -K5 n. 计划；平面图 vt. 计划；设计；打算 vi. 计划；打算 n. (Plan)人名；(瑞典)普兰；(法)普朗 时态: planned, planning, plans (中高雅 413/442)","欧陆词典释义：plan [plæn] -K5 n. 计划；平面图 vt. 计划；设计；打算 vi. 计划；打算 n. (Plan)人名；(瑞典)普兰；(法)普朗 时态: planned, planning, plans (中高雅 413/442)","The three leaders had worked out a peace plan ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that you intend to do or achieve","example":"Do you have any plans for the summer?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a set of things to do in order to achieve something, especially one that has been considered in detail in advance","example":"There are no plans to build new offices."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a detailed map of a building, town, etc.","example":"Your best plan"}]],["plant","/plɑ:nt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “plant”.","plant [plɑ:nt] -K5 n. 工厂，车间；植物；设备；庄稼 vt. 种植；培养；栽培；安置 vi. 种植 n. (Plant)人名；(英、西、意)普兰特；(法)普朗 时态: planted, planting, plants (中高雅 623/690)","欧陆词典释义：plant [plɑ:nt] -K5 n. 工厂，车间；植物；设备；庄稼 vt. 种植；培养；栽培；安置 vi. 种植 n. (Plant)人名；(英、西、意)普兰特；(法)普朗 时态: planted, planting, plants (中高雅 623/690)","Water each plant as often as required.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a living thing that grows in the earth and usually has a stem","example":"All plants need light and water."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a factory or place where power is produced or an industrial process takes place","example":"flowering/garden/indoor plants"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the large machinery that is used in industrial processes","example":"a tomato/potato plant"}]],["play","/pleɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “play”.","play [pleɪ] -K5 n. 游戏；比赛；剧本 vt. 游戏；扮演；演奏；播放；同…比赛 vi. 演奏；玩耍；上演；参加比赛 n. (Play)人名；(法、瑞典)普莱 时态: played, playing, plays (中高 200/224)","欧陆词典释义：play [pleɪ] -K5 n. 游戏；比赛；剧本 vt. 游戏；扮演；演奏；播放；同…比赛 vi. 演奏；玩耍；上演；参加比赛 n. (Play)人名；(法、瑞典)普莱 时态: played, playing, plays (中高 200/224)","invite the children round to play ...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to do things for pleasure, as children do; to enjoy yourself, rather than work","example":"You'll have to play inside today."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to pretend to be or do something for fun","example":"There's a time to work and a time to play."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to trick somebody for fun","example":"A group of kids were playing with a ball in the street."}]],["please","/pli:z/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “please”.","please [pli:z] -K4 int. 请（礼貌用语） vt. 使喜欢；使高兴，使满意 vi. 讨人喜欢；令人高兴 时态: pleased, pleasing, pleases (中高 1167/758)","欧陆词典释义：please [pli:z] -K4 int. 请（礼貌用语） vt. 使喜欢；使高兴，使满意 vi. 讨人喜欢；令人高兴 时态: pleased, pleasing, pleases (中高 1167/758)","Can you help us please ?...",[{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"used as a polite way of asking for something or telling somebody to do something","example":"Please sit down."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used to add force to a request or statement","example":"Two coffees, please."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used as a polite way of accepting something","example":"Quiet please!"}]],["point","/pɔɪnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “point”.","point [pɔɪnt] -K5 n. 要点；得分；标点；[机] 尖端 vt. 指向；弄尖；加标点于 vi. 表明；指向 n. (Point)人名；(法)普安 时态: pointed, pointing, points (中高研四六雅 211/176)","欧陆词典释义：point [pɔɪnt] -K5 n. 要点；得分；标点；[机] 尖端 vt. 指向；弄尖；加标点于 vi. 表明；指向 n. (Point)人名；(法)普安 时态: pointed, pointing, points (中高研四六雅 211/176)","We disagree with every point Mr Blunkett makes...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that somebody says or writes giving their opinion or stating a fact","example":"She made"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the main or most important idea in something that is said or done","example":"I take your point"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the purpose or aim of something","example":"He's just saying that to prove a point"}]],["police","/pəˈli:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “police”.","police [pəˈli:s] -K5 n. 警察，警方；治安 adj. 警察的；有关警察的 vt. 监督；管辖；维持治安；为…配备警察 时态: policed, policing, polices (中高研四雅 468/328)","欧陆词典释义：police [pəˈli:s] -K5 n. 警察，警方；治安 adj. 警察的；有关警察的 vt. 监督；管辖；维持治安；为…配备警察 时态: policed, policing, polices (中高研四雅 468/328)","The police are also looking for a second car...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official organization whose job is to make people obey the law and to prevent and solve crime; the people who work for this organization","example":"A man was arrested by the police and held for questioning."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"Get out of the house or I'll call the police"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to go around a particular area to make sure that nobody is breaking the law there","example":"Police suspect a local gang."}]],["pool","/pu:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “pool”.","pool [pu:l] -K3 n. 联营；撞球；水塘；共同资金 vt. 合伙经营 vi. 联营，合伙经营 n. (Pool)人名；(英、西)普尔；(芬、德)波尔 时态: pooled, pooling, pools (中高研四六 1565/1678)","欧陆词典释义：pool [pu:l] -K3 n. 联营；撞球；水塘；共同资金 vt. 合伙经营 vi. 联营，合伙经营 n. (Pool)人名；(英、西)普尔；(芬、德)波尔 时态: pooled, pooling, pools (中高研四六 1565/1678)","a heated indoor pool ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small area of still water, especially one that has formed naturally","example":"Does the hotel have a pool?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a small amount of liquid or light lying on a surface","example":"relaxing by the pool"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a supply of things or money that is shared by a group of people and can be used when needed","example":"freshwater pools"}]],["poor","/pʊə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “poor”.","poor [pʊə(r)] -K4 adj. 贫穷的；可怜的；贫乏的；卑鄙的 n. (Poor)人名；(英、伊朗)普尔 级别: poorer, poorest (中高 713/598)","欧陆词典释义：poor [pʊə(r)] -K4 adj. 贫穷的；可怜的；贫乏的；卑鄙的 n. (Poor)人名；(英、伊朗)普尔 级别: poorer, poorest (中高 713/598)","The reason our schools cannot afford better teachers is because people here are poor ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having very little money; not having enough money for basic needs","example":"They were too poor to buy shoes for the kids."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"people who have very little money","example":"We aim to help the poorest families."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"deserving pity and sympathy","example":"It's among the poorer countries of the world."}]],["popular","/ˈpɒpjələ(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “popular”.","popular [ˈpɒpjələ(r)] -K4 adj. 流行的，通俗的；受欢迎的；大众的；普及的 (中高研四六托雅 924/938)","欧陆词典释义：popular [ˈpɒpjələ(r)] -K4 adj. 流行的，通俗的；受欢迎的；大众的；普及的 (中高研四六托雅 924/938)","This is the most popular ball game ever devised...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"liked or enjoyed by a large number of people","example":"a hugely/immensely popular"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"suited to the taste and knowledge of ordinary people","example":"This is one of our most popular designs."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"shared by a large number of people","example":"Skiing has become very popular recently."}]],["possible","/ˈpɒsəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “possible”.","possible [ˈpɒsəbl] -K5 n. 可能性；合适的人；可能的事物 adj. 可能的；合理的；合适的 (中高 459/256)","欧陆词典释义：possible [ˈpɒsəbl] -K5 n. 可能性；合适的人；可能的事物 adj. 可能的；合理的；合适的 (中高 459/256)","If it is possible to find out where your brother is, we shall...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that can be done or achieved","example":"It is possible to"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"that might exist or happen but is not certain to","example":"Would it be possible for"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"reasonable or acceptable in a particular situation","example":"This wouldn't have been possible without you."}]],["post","/pəʊst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “post”.","post [pəʊst] -K2 n. 岗位；邮件；标杆 vt. 张贴；公布；邮递；布置 vi. 快速行进 n. (Post)人名；(英、西、捷、瑞典、荷)波斯特 时态: posted, posting, posts (中高托雅 2148/895)","欧陆词典释义：post [pəʊst] -K2 n. 岗位；邮件；标杆 vt. 张贴；公布；邮递；布置 vi. 快速行进 n. (Post)人名；(英、西、捷、瑞典、荷)波斯特 时态: posted, posting, posts (中高托雅 2148/895)","You'll receive your book through the post ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the official system used for sending and delivering letters, packages, etc.","example":"I'll send the original to you by post"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"letters, packages, etc. that are sent and delivered","example":"I'll put the information in the post"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an occasion during the day when letters, etc. are collected or delivered","example":"My application got lost in the post"}]],["practice","/ˈpræktɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “practice”.","practice [ˈpræktɪs] -K4 n. 实践；练习；惯例 vt. 练习；实习；实行 vi. 练习；实习；实行 时态: practiced, practicing, practices (中高雅 564/453)","欧陆词典释义：practice [ˈpræktɪs] -K4 n. 实践；练习；惯例 vt. 练习；实习；实行 vi. 练习；实习；实行 时态: practiced, practicing, practices (中高雅 564/453)","Some firms have cut workers' pay below the level set in their contract, a practice that is illegal in Germany...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"action rather than ideas","example":"the theory and practice"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a way of doing something that is the usual or expected way in a particular organization or situation","example":"She's determined to put"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a thing that is done regularly; a habit or a custom","example":"common/current/standard practice"}]],["present","/ˈpreznt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “present”.","present [ˈpreznt] -K2 n. 现在；礼物；瞄准 adj. 现在的；出席的 vt. 提出；介绍；呈现；赠送 vi. 举枪瞄准 时态: presented, presenting, presents (中高雅 817/678)","欧陆词典释义：present [ˈpreznt] -K2 n. 现在；礼物；瞄准 adj. 现在的；出席的 vt. 提出；介绍；呈现；赠送 vi. 举枪瞄准 时态: presented, presenting, presents (中高雅 817/678)","He has brought much of the present crisis on himself...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"existing or happening now","example":"in the present situation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"being in a particular place","example":"the present owner of the house"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"existing in a particular place or thing","example":"a list of all club members, past and present"}]],["pretty","/ˈprɪti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “pretty”.","pretty [ˈprɪti] -K4 n. 有吸引力的事物（尤指饰品）；漂亮的人 adj. 漂亮的；可爱的；优美的 adv. 相当地；颇 n. Pretty，普雷蒂（人名） 级别: prettier, prettiest (中高研四六 797/1782)","欧陆词典释义：pretty [ˈprɪti] -K4 n. 有吸引力的事物（尤指饰品）；漂亮的人 adj. 漂亮的；可爱的；优美的 adv. 相当地；颇 n. Pretty，普雷蒂（人名） 级别: prettier, prettiest (中高研四六 797/1782)","She's a very charming and very pretty girl.",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"to some extent; fairly","example":"I'm pretty sure I'll be going."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"very","example":"The game was pretty good."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"Old English","example":"It's pretty hard to explain."}]],["problem","/ˈprɒbləm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “problem”.","problem [ˈprɒbləm] -K5 n. 难题；引起麻烦的人 adj. 成问题的；难处理的 (中高 171/154)","欧陆词典释义：problem [ˈprɒbləm] -K5 n. 难题；引起麻烦的人 adj. 成问题的；难处理的 (中高 171/154)","the economic problem s of the inner city...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that is difficult to deal with or to understand","example":"big/major/serious problems"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a question that can be answered by using logical thought or mathematics","example":"health/family, etc. problems"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"financial/practical/technical problems"}]],["pull","/pʊl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “pull”.","pull [pʊl] -K4 n. 拉，拉绳；拉力，牵引力；拖 vt. 拉；拔；拖 vi. 拉，拖；拔 n. (Pull)人名；(法)皮尔；(德、瑞典)普尔 时态: pulled, pulling, pulls (中高托雅 471/718)","欧陆词典释义：pull [pʊl] -K4 n. 拉，拉绳；拉力，牵引力；拖 vt. 拉；拔；拖 vi. 拉，拖；拔 n. (Pull)人名；(法)皮尔；(德、瑞典)普尔 时态: pulled, pulling, pulls (中高托雅 471/718)","They have pull ed out patients' teeth unnecessarily...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to hold something firmly and use force in order to move it or try to move it towards yourself","example":"You push and I'll pull."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to remove something from a place by pulling","example":"Don't pull so hard or the handle will come off."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to move somebody/something in a particular direction by pulling","example":"I pulled on the rope to see if it was secure."}]],["push","/pʊʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “push”.","push [pʊʃ] -K4 n. 推，决心；大规模攻势；矢志的追求 vi. 推进；增加；努力争取 vt. 推动，增加；对…施加压力，逼迫；按；说服 时态: pushed, pushing, pushes (中高 695/926)","欧陆词典释义：push [pʊʃ] -K4 n. 推，决心；大规模攻势；矢志的追求 vi. 推进；增加；努力争取 vt. 推动，增加；对…施加压力，逼迫；按；说服 时态: pushed, pushing, pushes (中高 695/926)","The woman push ed back her chair and stood up...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to use your hands, arms or body in order to make somebody/something move forward or away from you; to move part of your body into a particular position","example":"We pushed and pushed but the piano wouldn't move."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to use force to move past somebody/something using your hands, arms, etc.","example":"Push hard when I tell you to."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to affect something so that it reaches a particular level or state","example":"You push and I'll pull."}]],["put","/pʊt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “put”.","put [pʊt] -K5 n. 掷；笨蛋；投击；怪人 adj. 固定不动的 vi. 出发；击；航行；发芽 vt. 放；表达；移动；安置；赋予 n. (Put)人名；(泰、缅)布 时态: put, putting, puts (中高雅 151/116)","欧陆词典释义：put [pʊt] -K5 n. 掷；笨蛋；投击；怪人 adj. 固定不动的 vi. 出发；击；航行；发芽 vt. 放；表达；移动；安置；赋予 n. (Put)人名；(泰、缅)布 时态: put, putting, puts (中高雅 151/116)","Leaphorn put the photograph on the desk...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move something into a particular place or position","example":"Put the cases down there, please."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move something into a particular place or position using force","example":"Did you put sugar in my coffee?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to cause somebody/something to go to a particular place","example":"Put your hand up if you need more paper."}]],["question","/ˈkwestʃən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “question”.","question [ˈkwestʃən] -K5 n. 问题，疑问；询问；疑问句 vt. 询问；怀疑；审问 vi. 询问；怀疑；审问 时态: questioned, questioning, questions (中高 197/221)","欧陆词典释义：question [ˈkwestʃən] -K5 n. 问题，疑问；询问；疑问句 vt. 询问；怀疑；审问 vi. 询问；怀疑；审问 时态: questioned, questioning, questions (中高 197/221)","They asked a great many question s about England...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a sentence, phrase or word that asks for information","example":"to ask/answer a question"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a task or request for information that is intended to test your knowledge or understanding, for example in an exam or a competition","example":"The question is,"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a matter or topic that needs to be discussed or dealt with","example":"The question arises"}]],["quick","/kwɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “quick”.","quick [kwɪk] -K5 n. 核心；伤口的嫩肉 adj. 快的；迅速的，敏捷的；灵敏的 adv. 迅速地，快 n. (Quick)人名；(英、德、瑞典、芬)奎克 级别: quicker, quickest (中高 1303/1431)","欧陆词典释义：quick [kwɪk] -K5 n. 核心；伤口的嫩肉 adj. 快的；迅速的，敏捷的；灵敏的 adv. 迅速地，快 n. (Quick)人名；(英、德、瑞典、芬)奎克 级别: quicker, quickest (中高 1303/1431)","You'll have to be quick . The flight leaves in about three hours...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"done with speed; taking or lasting a short time","example":"She gave him a quick glance."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"moving or doing something fast","example":"These cakes are very quick and easy to make."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"happening very soon or without delay","example":"Would you like a quick drink?"}]],["quiet","/ˈkwaɪət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “quiet”.","quiet [ˈkwaɪət] -K4 n. 安静；和平 adj. 安静的；安定的；不动的；温顺的 vt. 使平息；安慰 vi. 平静下来 时态: quieted, quieting, quiets 级别: quieter, quietest (中高 1435/1437)","欧陆词典释义：quiet [ˈkwaɪət] -K4 n. 安静；和平 adj. 安静的；安定的；不动的；温顺的 vt. 使平息；安慰 vi. 平静下来 时态: quieted, quieting, quiets 级别: quieter, quietest (中高 1435/1437)","Tania kept the children reasonably quiet and contented...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"making very little noise","example":"her quiet voice"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"without many people or much noise or activity","example":"a quieter, more efficient engine"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"not disturbed; peaceful","example":"Could you keep the kids quiet while I'm on the phone?"}]],["radio","/ˈreɪdiəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “radio”.","radio [ˈreɪdiəʊ] -K5 n. 收音机；无线电广播设备 vt. 用无线电发送 vi. 用无线电进行通信 n. (Radio)人名；(西)拉迪奥 时态: radioed, radioing, radios (中高雅 904/1093)","欧陆词典释义：radio [ˈreɪdiəʊ] -K5 n. 收音机；无线电广播设备 vt. 用无线电发送 vi. 用无线电进行通信 n. (Radio)人名；(西)拉迪奥 时态: radioed, radioing, radios (中高雅 904/1093)","The last 12 months have been difficult ones for local radio ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the activity of broadcasting programmes for people to listen to; the programmes that are broadcast","example":"The interview was broadcast on radio"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a piece of equipment used for listening to programmes that are broadcast to the public","example":"The play was written specially for radio."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the process of sending and receiving messages through the air using electromagnetic","example":"I listen to the radio"}]],["rain","/reɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “rain”.","rain [reɪn] -K4 n. 雨；下雨；雨天；雨季 vt. 大量地给；使大量落下 vi. 下雨；降雨 n. (Rain)人名；(法)兰；(英)雷恩；(罗、捷)赖恩 时态: rained, raining, rains (中高 1550/1491)","欧陆词典释义：rain [reɪn] -K4 n. 雨；下雨；雨天；雨季 vt. 大量地给；使大量落下 vi. 下雨；降雨 n. (Rain)人名；(法)兰；(英)雷恩；(罗、捷)赖恩 时态: rained, raining, rains (中高 1550/1491)","I hope you didn't get soaked standing out in the rain ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"water that falls from the sky in separate drops","example":"There will be rain in all parts tomorrow."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the season of heavy continuous rain in tropical countries","example":"Rain is forecast for the weekend."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a large number of things falling from the sky at the same time","example":"Don't go out in the rain."}]],["read","/ri:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “read”.","read [ri:d] -K5 n. 阅读；读物 adj. 有学问的 vi. 读；读起来 vt. 阅读；读懂，理解 n. (Read)人名；(英)里德 时态: read, reading, reads (中高 337/322)","欧陆词典释义：read [ri:d] -K5 n. 阅读；读物 adj. 有学问的 vi. 读；读起来 vt. 阅读；读懂，理解 n. (Read)人名；(英)里德 时态: read, reading, reads (中高 337/322)","Have you read this book?...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to look at and understand the meaning of written or printed words or symbols","example":"She's still learning to read."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to go through written or printed words, etc. in silence or speaking them to other people","example":"Some children can read and write before they go to school."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"to discover or find out about somebody/something by reading","example":"I can't read your writing."}]],["ready","/ˈredi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ready”.","ready [ˈredi] -K4 n. 现款；预备好的状态 adj. 准备好；现成的；迅速的；情愿的；快要…的 vt. 使准备好 adv. 迅速地；预先 n. (Ready)人名；(英)雷迪 时态: readied, readying, readies 级别: readier, readiest (中高托宝 758/976)","欧陆词典释义：ready [ˈredi] -K4 n. 现款；预备好的状态 adj. 准备好；现成的；迅速的；情愿的；快要…的 vt. 使准备好 adv. 迅速地；预先 n. (Ready)人名；(英)雷迪 时态: readied, readying, readies 级别: readier, readiest (中高托宝 758/976)","It took her a long time to get ready for church...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"fully prepared for what you are going to do","example":"Are you nearly ready?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"completed and available to be used","example":"‘Shall we go?’ ‘I'm ready when you are"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"available to be used easily and immediately","example":"I'm just getting"}]],["real","/ˈri:əl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “real”.","real [ˈri:əl] -K5 n. 现实；实数 adj. 实际的；真实的；实在的 adv. 真正地；确实地 n. (Real)人名；(德、西、葡、法)雷亚尔；(英)里尔 (中高研四六 305/425)","欧陆词典释义：real [ˈri:əl] -K5 n. 现实；实数 adj. 实际的；真实的；实在的 adv. 真正地；确实地 n. (Real)人名；(德、西、葡、法)雷亚尔；(英)里尔 (中高研四六 305/425)","No, it wasn't a dream. It was real ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"actually existing or happening and not imagined or pretended","example":"It wasn't a ghost; it was a real person."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"genuine and not false or artificial","example":"pictures of animals, both real and mythological"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"actual or true, rather than what appears to be true","example":"In the movies guns kill people instantly, but it's not like that in real life"}]],["remember","/rɪˈmembə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “remember”.","remember [rɪˈmembə(r)] -K5 vi. 记得，记起 vt. 记得；牢记；纪念；代…问好 时态: remembered, remembering, remembers (中高 379/346)","欧陆词典释义：remember [rɪˈmembə(r)] -K5 vi. 记得，记起 vt. 记得；牢记；纪念；代…问好 时态: remembered, remembering, remembers (中高 379/346)","You wouldn't remember me. I was in another group...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have or keep an image in your memory of an event, a person, a place, etc. from the past","example":"This is Carla. Do you remember her?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to bring back to your mind a fact, piece of information, etc. that you knew","example":"I don't remember my first day at school."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to keep an important fact in your mind","example":"He still remembered her as the lively teenager he'd known years before."}]],["restaurant","/ˈrestrɒnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “restaurant”.","restaurant [ˈrestrɒnt] -K4 n. 餐馆；[经] 饭店 (中高雅 1114/1816)","欧陆词典释义：restaurant [ˈrestrɒnt] -K4 n. 餐馆；[经] 饭店 (中高雅 1114/1816)","They ate in an Italian restaurant in Forth Street...",""],["ride","/raɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ride”.","ride [raɪd] -K4 n. 骑；乘坐；交通工具；可供骑行的路；（乘坐汽车等的）旅行；乘骑；（乘车或骑车的）短途旅程；供乘骑的游乐设施 vi. 骑马；乘车；依靠；漂浮 vt. 骑；乘；控制；（骑马、自行车等）穿越；搭乘；飘浮 n. （英）赖德（人名）；（法、葡）里德（人名） 时态: rode, ridden, riding, rides (中高 1283/1796)","欧陆词典释义：ride [raɪd] -K4 n. 骑；乘坐；交通工具；可供骑行的路；（乘坐汽车等的）旅行；乘骑；（乘车或骑车的）短途旅程；供乘骑的游乐设施 vi. 骑马；乘车；依靠；漂浮 vt. 骑；乘；控制；（骑马、自行车等）穿越；搭乘；飘浮 n. （英）赖德（人名）；（法、葡）里德（人名） 时态: rode, ridden, riding, rides (中高 1283/1796)","I saw a girl riding a horse...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to sit on a horse, etc. and control it as it moves","example":"I learnt to ride as a child."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to spend time riding a horse for pleasure","example":"They rode along narrow country lanes."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to sit on and control a bicycle, motorcycle, etc.","example":"He was riding on a large black horse."}]],["right","/raɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “right”.","right [raɪt] -K3 n. 正确；右边；正义 adj. 正确的；直接的；右方的 vt. 纠正 adv. 正确地；恰当地；彻底地 vi. 复正；恢复平稳 n. (Right)人名；(英)赖特 时态: righted, righting, rights (中高 193/244)","欧陆词典释义：right [raɪt] -K3 n. 正确；右边；正义 adj. 正确的；直接的；右方的 vt. 纠正 adv. 正确地；恰当地；彻底地 vi. 复正；恢复平稳 n. (Right)人名；(英)赖特 时态: righted, righting, rights (中高 193/244)","That's absolutely right ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"morally good or acceptable; correct according to law or a person’s duty","example":"You were quite right to criticize him."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"true or correct as a fact","example":"Is it ever right to kill?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"correct for a particular situation or thing, or for a particular person","example":"It seems only right"}]],["river","/ˈrɪvə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “river”.","river [ˈrɪvə(r)] -K4 n. 河，江 n. (River)人名；(英)里弗 (中高 1327/876)","欧陆词典释义：river [ˈrɪvə(r)] -K4 n. 河，江 n. (River)人名；(英)里弗 (中高 1327/876)","a chemical works on the banks of the river .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a natural flow of water that continues in a long line across land to the sea/ocean","example":"the River Thames"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large amount of liquid that is flowing in a particular direction","example":"the Hudson River"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"on the banks of the river ("}]],["road","/rəʊd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “road”.","road [rəʊd] -K5 n. 公路，马路；道路；手段 adj. （美）巡回的 vt. （狗）沿臭迹追逐（猎物） n. (Road)人名；(英)罗德 (中高雅 489/284)","欧陆词典释义：road [rəʊd] -K5 n. 公路，马路；道路；手段 adj. （美）巡回的 vt. （狗）沿臭迹追逐（猎物） n. (Road)人名；(英)罗德 (中高雅 489/284)","There was very little traffic on the road s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a hard surface built for vehicles to travel on","example":"a main/major/minor road"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used in names of roads, especially in towns","example":"a country/mountain road"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way to achieving something","example":"They live just along/up/down the road"}]],["room","/ru:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “room”.","room [ru:m] -K5 n. 房间；空间；余地；机会；房间里所有的人 vt. 为…提供住处；租房，合住；投宿，住宿；留…住宿 vi. 居住；住宿 n. （英）鲁姆（人名）；（俄）罗姆（人名） 时态: roomed, rooming, rooms (中高雅 227/240)","欧陆词典释义：room [ru:m] -K5 n. 房间；空间；余地；机会；房间里所有的人 vt. 为…提供住处；租房，合住；投宿，住宿；留…住宿 vi. 居住；住宿 n. （英）鲁姆（人名）；（俄）罗姆（人名） 时态: roomed, rooming, rooms (中高雅 227/240)","A minute later he excused himself and left the room ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a part of a building that has its own walls, floor and ceiling and is usually used for a particular purpose","example":"He walked out of the room and slammed the door."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having the number of rooms mentioned","example":"They were in the next room"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a bedroom in a hotel, etc.","example":"a dining/living/sitting room"}]],["round","/raʊnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “round”.","round [raʊnd] -K2 n. 圆；循环；一回合；圆形物 prep. 附近；绕过；大约；在…周围 adj. 圆的；完全的；大概的；肥胖的 vt. 完成；围捕；绕行；弄圆 adv. 在周围；迂回地；朝反方向；挨个 vi. 进展；变圆；环行；发胖 n. (Round)人名；(英)朗德 时态: rounded, rounding, rounds 级别: rounder, roundest (中高 2372/730)","欧陆词典释义：round [raʊnd] -K2 n. 圆；循环；一回合；圆形物 prep. 附近；绕过；大约；在…周围 adj. 圆的；完全的；大概的；肥胖的 vt. 完成；围捕；绕行；弄圆 adv. 在周围；迂回地；朝反方向；挨个 vi. 进展；变圆；环行；发胖 n. (Round)人名；(英)朗德 时态: rounded, rounding, rounds 级别: rounder, roundest (中高 2372/730)","They were sitting round the kitchen table...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"shaped like a circle or a ball","example":"a round plate"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"having a curved shape","example":"These glasses suit people with round faces."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"a round","example":"The fruit are small and round."}]],["rule","/ru:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “rule”.","rule [ru:l] -K5 n. 统治；规则 vt. 统治；规定；管理；裁决；支配 vi. 统治；管辖；裁定 n. (Rule)人名；(英)鲁尔；(塞)鲁莱 时态: ruled, ruling, rules (中高研四六托雅 633/539)","欧陆词典释义：rule [ru:l] -K5 n. 统治；规则 vt. 统治；规定；管理；裁决；支配 vi. 统治；管辖；裁定 n. (Rule)人名；(英)鲁尔；(塞)鲁莱 时态: ruled, ruling, rules (中高研四六托雅 633/539)","a thirty-two-page pamphlet explaining the rule s of basketball...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a statement of what may, must or must not be done in a particular situation or when playing a game","example":"to follow/obey/observe the rules"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a statement of what you are advised to do in a particular situation","example":"It's against all rules and regulations"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a habit; the normal state of things; what is true in most cases","example":"to break a rule"}]],["run","/rʌn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “run”.","run [rʌn] -K5 n. 奔跑；赛跑；趋向；奔跑的路程 vt. 管理，经营；运行；参赛 vi. 经营；奔跑；运转 n. (Run)人名；(塞)鲁恩 时态: ran, run, running, runs (中高 202/208)","欧陆词典释义：run [rʌn] -K5 n. 奔跑；赛跑；趋向；奔跑的路程 vt. 管理，经营；运行；参赛 vi. 经营；奔跑；运转 n. (Run)人名；(塞)鲁恩 时态: ran, run, running, runs (中高 202/208)","I excused myself and ran back to the telephone...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move using your legs, going faster than when you walk","example":"Can you run as fast as Mike?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to travel a particular distance by running","example":"They turned and ran when they saw us coming."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to run as a sport","example":"She came running"}]],["safe","/seɪf/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “safe”.","safe [seɪf] -K4 n. 保险箱；冷藏室；纱橱 adj. 安全的；可靠的；平安的 n. (Safe)人名；(几)萨菲 级别: safer, safest (中高研四六雅宝 1058/1244)","欧陆词典释义：safe [seɪf] -K4 n. 保险箱；冷藏室；纱橱 adj. 安全的；可靠的；平安的 n. (Safe)人名；(几)萨菲 级别: safer, safest (中高研四六雅宝 1058/1244)","Officials arrived to assess whether it is safe to bring emergency food supplies into the city...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"protected from any danger or harm","example":"The children are quite safe here."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"not likely to lead to any physical harm or danger","example":"She didn't feel safe"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"not harmed, damaged, lost, etc.","example":"Will the car be safe parked in the road?"}]],["same","/seɪm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “same”.","same [seɪm] -K5 adj. 相同的；同一的；上述的（通常与the连用）；无变化的 adv. 同样地（通常与the连用） pron. 同样的事物或人（通常与the连用） n. (Same)人名；(意)萨梅 (中高 161/137)","欧陆词典释义：same [seɪm] -K5 adj. 相同的；同一的；上述的（通常与the连用）；无变化的 adv. 同样地（通常与the连用） pron. 同样的事物或人（通常与the连用） n. (Same)人名；(意)萨梅 (中高 161/137)","The houses were all the same — square, close to the street, needing paint...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"exactly the one or ones referred to or mentioned; not different","example":"We have lived in the same house for twenty years."},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"exactly like the one or ones referred to or mentioned","example":"Our children go to the same"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"Middle English","example":"She's still the same"}]],["sand","/sænd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sand”.","sand [sænd] -K3 n. 沙；沙地；沙洲；沙滩；沙子 vt. 撒沙于；以沙掩盖；用砂纸等擦平或磨光某物；使撒沙似地布满；给…掺沙子 vi. 被沙堵塞 n. (Sand)人名；(英、德、意、芬、罗、捷、挪)桑德；(瑞典)桑德；(法)桑 时态: sanded, sanding, sands (中高研四六 2205/2470)","欧陆词典释义：sand [sænd] -K3 n. 沙；沙地；沙洲；沙滩；沙子 vt. 撒沙于；以沙掩盖；用砂纸等擦平或磨光某物；使撒沙似地布满；给…掺沙子 vi. 被沙堵塞 n. (Sand)人名；(英、德、意、芬、罗、捷、挪)桑德；(瑞典)桑德；(法)桑 时态: sanded, sanding, sands (中高研四六 2205/2470)","They all walked barefoot across the damp sand to the water's edge.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a substance that consists of very small fine grains of rock. Sand is found on beaches, in deserts, etc.","example":"a grain of sand"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a large area of sand on a beach","example":"Concrete is a mixture of sand and cement."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"His hair was the colour of sand."}]],["say","/seɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “say”.","say [seɪ] -K5 vt. 讲；说明；例如；声称；假设；指明 vi. 讲；表示；念；假定；背诵 n. (Say)人名；(土)萨伊；(法、老、柬)赛；(英)塞伊；(匈、罗)绍伊 时态: said, saying, says (中高雅 19/32)","欧陆词典释义：say [seɪ] -K5 vt. 讲；说明；例如；声称；假设；指明 vi. 讲；表示；念；假定；背诵 n. (Say)人名；(土)萨伊；(法、老、柬)赛；(英)塞伊；(匈、罗)绍伊 时态: said, saying, says (中高雅 19/32)","'I'm sorry,' he said...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to speak or tell somebody something, using words","example":"‘Hello!’ she said."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to repeat words, phrases, etc.","example":"‘That was marvellous,’ said Daniel."},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"to express an opinion on something","example":"Be quiet, I have something to say."}]],["sea","/si:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sea”.","sea [si:] -K4 n. 海；海洋；许多；大量 (中高 989/721)","欧陆词典释义：sea [si:] -K4 n. 海；海洋；许多；大量 (中高 989/721)","Most of the kids have never seen the sea ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the salt water that covers most of the earth’s surface and surrounds its continents and islands","example":"to travel by sea"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large area of salt water that is part of an ocean or surrounded by land","example":"a cottage by the sea"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the movement of the waves of the sea","example":"The waste was dumped in the sea"}]],["seat","/si:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “seat”.","seat [si:t] -K4 n. 座位；所在地；职位 vt. 使…坐下；可容纳…的；使就职 时态: seated, seating, seats (中高雅 894/912)","欧陆词典释义：seat [si:t] -K4 n. 座位；所在地；职位 vt. 使…坐下；可容纳…的；使就职 时态: seated, seating, seats (中高雅 894/912)","Stephen returned to his seat ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place where you can sit, for example a chair","example":"She sat back in her seat."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"with the number of seats mentioned","example":"He put his shopping on the seat behind him."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the part of a chair, etc. on which you actually sit","example":"Please take a seat"}]],["second","/ˈsekənd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “second”.","second [ˈsekənd] -K5 num. 第二 n. 秒；第二名；瞬间；二等品 adj. 第二的；次要的；附加的 vt. 支持 adv. 第二；其次；居第二位 n. (Second)人名；(法)塞孔 时态: seconded, seconding, seconds (中高雅 381/242)","欧陆词典释义：second [ˈsekənd] -K5 num. 第二 n. 秒；第二名；瞬间；二等品 adj. 第二的；次要的；附加的 vt. 支持 adv. 第二；其次；居第二位 n. (Second)人名；(法)塞孔 时态: seconded, seconding, seconds (中高雅 381/242)","For a few second s nobody said anything...",[{"pos":"determiner","definition":"happening or coming next after the first in a series of similar things or people; 2nd","example":"This is the second time it's happened."},{"pos":"ordinal number","definition":"next in order of importance, size, quality, etc. to one other person or thing","example":"Italy scored a second goal just after half-time."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"another; in addition to one that you already own or use","example":"the second of June/June 2nd"}]],["see","/si:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “see”.","see [si:] -K5 vi. 看；看见；领会 vt. 看见；理解；领会 n. (See)人名；(英)西伊；(柬)塞；(德)泽 时态: saw, seen, seeing, sees (中高 67/47)","欧陆词典释义：see [si:] -K5 vi. 看；看见；领会 vt. 看见；理解；领会 n. (See)人名；(英)西伊；(柬)塞；(德)泽 时态: saw, seen, seeing, sees (中高 67/47)","You can't see colours at night...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become aware of somebody/something by using your eyes","example":"She looked for him but couldn't see him in the crowd."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to have or use the power of sight","example":"I looked out of the window but saw nothing."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to watch a game, television programme, performance, etc.","example":"The opera was the place to see and be seen"}]],["sell","/sel/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sell”.","sell [sel] -K5 n. 销售；失望；推销术 vt. 销售；推销；出卖；欺骗 vi. 卖；出售；受欢迎；有销路 n. (Sell)人名；(德)泽尔；(英、芬、瑞典)塞尔 时态: sold, selling, sells (中高 443/461)","欧陆词典释义：sell [sel] -K5 n. 销售；失望；推销术 vt. 销售；推销；出卖；欺骗 vi. 卖；出售；受欢迎；有销路 n. (Sell)人名；(德)泽尔；(英、芬、瑞典)塞尔 时态: sold, selling, sells (中高 443/461)","I sold everything I owned except for my car and my books...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give something to somebody in exchange for money","example":"I sold my car to James for £800."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to offer something for people to buy","example":"I sold James my car for £800."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be bought by people in the way or in the numbers mentioned; to be offered at the price mentioned","example":"They sold"}]],["send","/send/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “send”.","send [send] -K5 n. 上升运动 vi. 派人；寄信 vt. 发送，寄；派遣；使进入；发射 n. (Send)人名；(德)森德 时态: sent, sending, sends (中高 404/366)","欧陆词典释义：send [send] -K5 n. 上升运动 vi. 派人；寄信 vt. 发送，寄；派遣；使进入；发射 n. (Send)人名；(德)森德 时态: sent, sending, sends (中高 404/366)","Myra Cunningham sent me a note thanking me for dinner...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something go or be taken to a place, especially by post/mail, email, radio, etc.","example":"to send a letter/package/cheque/fax/email"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to tell somebody something by sending them a message","example":"She sent the letter by airmail."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to tell somebody to go somewhere or to do something; to arrange for somebody to go somewhere","example":"to send something by post"}]],["set","/set/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “set”.","set [set] -K3 n. [数] 集合；一套；布景；[机] 装置 adj. 固定的；规定的；固执的 vi. (日,月)落沉；凝固；结果 vt. 树立；点燃；点缀； n. (Set)人名；(瑞典)塞特；(俄)谢特 时态: set, setting, sets (中高雅 294/213)","欧陆词典释义：set [set] -K3 n. [数] 集合；一套；布景；[机] 装置 adj. 固定的；规定的；固执的 vi. (日,月)落沉；凝固；结果 vt. 树立；点燃；点缀； n. (Set)人名；(瑞典)塞特；(俄)谢特 时态: set, setting, sets (中高雅 294/213)","There must be one set of laws for the whole of the country...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to put something/somebody in a particular place or position","example":"She set a tray down on the table."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to cause somebody/something to be in a particular state; to start something happening","example":"They ate everything that was set in front of them."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"to place the action of a play, novel or film/movie in a particular place, time, etc.","example":"The house is set ("}]],["seven","/ˈsevn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “seven”.","seven [ˈsevn] -5 num. 七个，七 n. 七个，七 adj. 七的；七个的 n. (Seven)人名；(土库、阿塞)谢文；(土)塞文 (中高 734/575)","欧陆词典释义：seven [ˈsevn] -5 num. 七个，七 n. 七个，七 adj. 七的；七个的 n. (Seven)人名；(土库、阿塞)谢文；(土)塞文 (中高 734/575)","Sarah and Ella have been friends for seven years.",[{"pos":"number","definition":"7","example":"I haven't had time to clear up, so I'm all at sixes and sevens."},{"pos":"number","definition":"Old English","example":"I haven't had time to clear up, so I'm all at sixes and sevens."},{"pos":"number","definition":"in confusion; not well organized","example":"I haven't had time to clear up, so I'm all at sixes and sevens."}]],["share","/ʃeə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “share”.","share [ʃeə(r)] -K5 n. 份额；股份 vt. 分享，分担；分配 vi. 共享；分担 n. (Share)人名；(阿拉伯)沙雷 时态: shared, sharing, shares (中高研四六 711/620)","欧陆词典释义：share [ʃeə(r)] -K5 n. 份额；股份 vt. 分享，分担；分配 vi. 共享；分担 n. (Share)人名；(阿拉伯)沙雷 时态: shared, sharing, shares (中高研四六 711/620)","This is why Sir Colin Marshall, British Airways' chairman, has been so keen to buy share s in US-AIR...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have or use something at the same time as somebody else","example":"Sue shares a house with three other students."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to divide something between two or more people","example":"There isn't an empty table. Would you mind sharing?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to give some of what you have to somebody else; to let somebody use something that is yours","example":"We shared the pizza between the four of us."}]],["sheep","/ʃi:p/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sheep”.","sheep [ʃi:p] -K2 n. 羊，绵羊；胆小鬼 (中高雅 4210/2697)","欧陆词典释义：sheep [ʃi:p] -K2 n. 羊，绵羊；胆小鬼 (中高雅 4210/2697)","grassland on which a flock of sheep were grazing.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an animal with a thick coat, kept on farms for its meat (called mutton","example":"a flock of sheep"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"Sheep were grazing in the fields."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to imagine that sheep are jumping over a fence and to count them, as a way of getting to sleep","example":"He sees it as his duty to take care of the lost sheep of the world."}]],["ship","/ʃɪp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ship”.","ship [ʃɪp] -K4 n. 船；舰；太空船 vt. 运送，乘船；以船运送 vi. 上船；乘船旅行；当船员 n. (Ship)人名；(中)摄(广东话·威妥玛) 时态: shipped, shipping, ships (中高雅 1219/1356)","欧陆词典释义：ship [ʃɪp] -K4 n. 船；舰；太空船 vt. 运送，乘船；以船运送 vi. 上船；乘船旅行；当船员 n. (Ship)人名；(中)摄(广东话·威妥玛) 时态: shipped, shipping, ships (中高雅 1219/1356)","Within ninety minutes the ship was ready for departure...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large boat that carries people or goods by sea","example":"There are two restaurants on board ship"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"a sailing/cargo/cruise ship"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used to talk about people who leave an organization, a company, etc. that is having difficulties, without caring about the people who are left","example":"a ship’s captain/crew/company/cook"}]],["shirt","/ʃɜ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “shirt”.","shirt [ʃɜ:t] -K3 n. 衬衫；汗衫，内衣 (中高 1771/2401)","欧陆词典释义：shirt [ʃɜ:t] -K3 n. 衬衫；汗衫，内衣 (中高 1771/2401)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “shirt”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of clothing (usually for men), worn on the upper part of the body, made of light cloth, with sleeves and usually with a collar","example":"to wear a shirt and tie"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"a short-sleeved shirt"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to tell somebody not to get angry","example":"a football shirt"}]],["shoe","/ʃu:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “shoe”.","shoe [ʃu:] -K3 n. 鞋；蹄铁；外胎 vt. 给……穿上鞋；穿……鞋 n. (Shoe)人名；(英)休 时态: shod, shoeing, shoes (中高 1423/1885)","欧陆词典释义：shoe [ʃu:] -K3 n. 鞋；蹄铁；外胎 vt. 给……穿上鞋；穿……鞋 n. (Shoe)人名；(英)休 时态: shod, shoeing, shoes (中高 1423/1885)","a pair of shoe s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"one of a pair of outer coverings for your feet, usually made of leather or plastic","example":"a pair of shoes"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"He took his shoes and socks off."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be in, or imagine that you are in, another person’s situation, especially when it is an unpleasant or difficult one","example":"What's your shoe size?"}]],["shop","/ʃɒp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “shop”.","shop [ʃɒp] -K4 n. 商店；店铺 vt. 购物 vi. 购物；买东西 时态: shopped, shopping, shops (中高雅 1338/648)","欧陆词典释义：shop [ʃɒp] -K4 n. 商店；店铺 vt. 购物 vi. 购物；买东西 时态: shopped, shopping, shops (中高雅 1338/648)","health food shop s.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a building or part of a building where you can buy goods or services","example":"a shoe shop"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a place where things are made or repaired, especially part of a factory where a particular type of work is done","example":"There's a little gift shop around the corner."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an act of going shopping, especially for food and other items needed in the house","example":"a butcher’s shop"}]],["short","/ʃɔ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “short”.","short [ʃɔ:t] -K2 n. 短；缺乏；短路；短裤 adj. 短的；不足的；矮的，低的 adv. 不足；突然；唐突地 n. (Short)人名；(英)肖特 时态: shorted, shorting, shorts 级别: shorter, shortest (中高雅 627/500)","欧陆词典释义：short [ʃɔ:t] -K2 n. 短；缺乏；短路；短裤 adj. 短的；不足的；矮的，低的 adv. 不足；突然；唐突地 n. (Short)人名；(英)肖特 时态: shorted, shorting, shorts 级别: shorter, shortest (中高雅 627/500)","The announcement was made a short time ago...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"measuring or covering a small length or distance, or a smaller length or distance than usual","example":"He had short curly hair."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"small in height","example":"a short walk"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"lasting or taking a small amount of time or less time than usual","example":"a short skirt"}]],["show","/ʃəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “show”.","show [ʃəʊ] -K5 n. 显示；表演；炫耀 vt. 显示；说明；演出；展出 vi. 显示；说明；指示 n. (Show)人名；(中)邵(普通话·威妥玛)；(英)肖 时态: showed, shown, showing, shows (中高 177/147)","欧陆词典释义：show [ʃəʊ] -K5 n. 显示；表演；炫耀 vt. 显示；说明；演出；展出 vi. 显示；说明；指示 n. (Show)人名；(中)邵(普通话·威妥玛)；(英)肖 时态: showed, shown, showing, shows (中高 177/147)","Research show s that a high-fibre diet may protect you from bowel cancer...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something clear; to prove something","example":"The figures clearly show that her claims are false."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to let somebody see something","example":"The government's popularity is declining rapidly, as the opinion polls show."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to help somebody to do something by letting them watch you do it or by explaining it","example":"Market research has shown us that people want quality, not just low prices."}]],["sick","/sɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sick”.","sick [sɪk] -K3 adj. 厌恶的；病态的；不舒服；渴望的；恶心的 ；生病的 n. 病人 n. (Sick)人名；(德、西)西克 vt. 使狗去咬；呕吐；追击 级别: sicker, sickest (中高托雅 1746/2044)","欧陆词典释义：sick [sɪk] -K3 adj. 厌恶的；病态的；不舒服；渴望的；恶心的 ；生病的 n. 病人 n. (Sick)人名；(德、西)西克 vt. 使狗去咬；呕吐；追击 级别: sicker, sickest (中高托雅 1746/2044)","He's very sick . He needs medication...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"physically or mentally ill","example":"a sick child"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"feeling that you want to vomit","example":"Her mother's very sick."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"feeling sick as a result of travelling on a ship, plane, etc.","example":"Peter has been off sick"}]],["side","/saɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “side”.","side [saɪd] -K5 n. 方面；侧面；旁边 adj. 旁的，侧的 vt. 同意，支持 vi. 支持；赞助；偏袒 n. (Side)人名；(英)赛德 时态: sided, siding, sides (中高雅 249/212)","欧陆词典释义：side [saɪd] -K5 n. 方面；侧面；旁边 adj. 旁的，侧的 vt. 同意，支持 vi. 支持；赞助；偏袒 n. (Side)人名；(英)赛德 时态: sided, siding, sides (中高雅 249/212)","On one side of the main entrance there's a red plaque.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"either of the two halves of a surface, an object or an area that is divided by an imaginary central line","example":"They drive on the left-hand side of the road in Japan."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a position or an area to the left or right of something","example":"the right side of the brain"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"one of the flat surfaces of something that is not the top or bottom, front or back","example":"satellite links to the other side of the world"}]],["sign","/saɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sign”.","sign [saɪn] -K5 n. 迹象；符号；记号；手势；指示牌 vt. 签署；示意 vi. 签署；签名 时态: signed, signing, signs (高研四六雅 759/935)","欧陆词典释义：sign [saɪn] -K5 n. 迹象；符号；记号；手势；指示牌 vt. 签署；示意 vi. 签署；签名 时态: signed, signing, signs (高研四六雅 759/935)","Equations are generally written with a two-bar equals sign .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an event, an action, a fact, etc. that shows that something exists, is happening or may happen in the future","example":"Headaches may be a sign of stress."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a piece of paper, wood or metal that has writing or a picture on it that gives you information, instructions, a warning, etc.","example":"There is no sign of John anywhere."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a movement or sound that you make to tell somebody something","example":"Call the police at the first sign of trouble."}]],["sing","/sɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sing”.","sing [sɪŋ] -K4 n. 演唱；鸣声；呼啸声 vt. 唱；用诗赞颂；唱着使 vi. 唱歌；歌颂；鸣叫；呼号 n. (Sing)人名；(老、德、泰)辛 时态: sang, sung, singing, sings (中高 1013/1509)","欧陆词典释义：sing [sɪŋ] -K4 n. 演唱；鸣声；呼啸声 vt. 唱；用诗赞颂；唱着使 vi. 唱歌；歌颂；鸣叫；呼号 n. (Sing)人名；(老、德、泰)辛 时态: sang, sung, singing, sings (中高 1013/1509)","I can't sing ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an act of singing","example":"Let's have a sing."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make musical sounds with your voice in the form of a song or tune","example":"She usually sings in the shower."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make high musical sounds","example":"I just can't sing in tune!"}]],["sister","/ˈsɪstə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sister”.","sister [ˈsɪstə(r)] -K5 n. 姐妹；（称志同道合者）姐妹；修女；护士 adj. 姐妹般的；同类型的 (中高 823/1049)","欧陆词典释义：sister [ˈsɪstə(r)] -K5 n. 姐妹；（称志同道合者）姐妹；修女；护士 adj. 姐妹般的；同类型的 (中高 823/1049)","His sister Sarah helped him.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a girl or woman who has the same mother and father as another person","example":"She's my sister."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used for talking to or about other members of a women’s organization or other women who have the same ideas, purpose, etc. as yourself","example":"an older/younger sister"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a senior female nurse who is in charge of a hospital ward","example":"a big/little/kid sister"}]],["sit","/sɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sit”.","sit [sɪt] -K5 vi. 坐；位于 vt. 使就座 n. (Sit)人名；(东南亚国家华语)硕；(罗)西特 时态: sat, sitting, sits (中高 268/302)","欧陆词典释义：sit [sɪt] -K5 vi. 坐；位于 vt. 使就座 n. (Sit)人名；(东南亚国家华语)硕；(罗)西特 时态: sat, sitting, sits (中高 268/302)","Mother was sit ting in her chair in the kitchen...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to rest your weight on your bottom with your back vertical, for example on/in a chair","example":"She sat and stared at the letter in front of her."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to put somebody in a sitting position","example":"May I sit here?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be in a particular place","example":"Just sit still!"}]],["six","/sɪks/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “six”.","six [sɪks] -5 num. 六，六个 n. 六，六个 n. (Six)人名；(法、德)西克斯 (中高 424/293)","欧陆词典释义：six [sɪks] -5 num. 六，六个 n. 六，六个 n. (Six)人名；(法、德)西克斯 (中高 424/293)","a glorious career spanning more than six decades.",[{"pos":"number","definition":"6","example":"I haven't had time to clear up, so I'm all at sixes and sevens."},{"pos":"number","definition":"Old English","example":"The business over the lawsuit had really knocked her for six."},{"pos":"number","definition":"in confusion; not well organized","example":"I haven't had time to clear up, so I'm all at sixes and sevens."}]],["size","/saɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “size”.","size [saɪz] -K4 n. 大小；尺寸 adj. 一定尺寸的 vt. 依大小排列 vi. 可比拟 时态: sized, sizing, sizes (中高雅 752/697)","欧陆词典释义：size [saɪz] -K4 n. 大小；尺寸 adj. 一定尺寸的 vt. 依大小排列 vi. 可比拟 时态: sized, sizing, sizes (中高雅 752/697)","Scientists have found the bones of a hoofed grazing animal about the size of a small horse...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"how large or small a person or thing is","example":"an area the size of"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the large amount or extent of something","example":"They complained about the size of their gas bill."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"one of a number of standard measurements in which clothes, shoes and other goods are made and sold","example":"Dogs come in all shapes and sizes"}]],["skill","/skɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “skill”.","skill [skɪl] -K4 n. 技能，技巧；本领，技术 n. (Skill)人名；(瑞典)希尔 (中高研四六雅 821/801)","欧陆词典释义：skill [skɪl] -K4 n. 技能，技巧；本领，技术 n. (Skill)人名；(瑞典)希尔 (中高研四六雅 821/801)","Most of us will know someone who is always learning new skill s, or studying new fields.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to do something well","example":"The job requires skill and an eye for detail."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular ability or type of ability","example":"What made him remarkable as a photographer was his skill in capturing the moment."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Old English","example":"We need people with practical skills like carpentry."}]],["sky","/skaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sky”.","sky [skaɪ] -K3 n. 天空；顶点 vt. 把…投向空中；把…挂得过高 vi. 踢或击高空球；把桨叶翘得过高；飞涨 n. (Sky)人名；(英)斯凯 时态: skied, skying, skies (中高 1147/1674)","欧陆词典释义：sky [skaɪ] -K3 n. 天空；顶点 vt. 把…投向空中；把…挂得过高 vi. 踢或击高空球；把桨叶翘得过高；飞涨 n. (Sky)人名；(英)斯凯 时态: skied, skying, skies (中高 1147/1674)","The sun is already high in the sky .",""],["sleep","/sli:p/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sleep”.","sleep [sli:p] -K4 n. 睡眠 vi. 睡，睡觉 n. (Sleep)人名；(英)斯利普 时态: slept, sleeping, sleeps (中高雅 1172/1408)","欧陆词典释义：sleep [sli:p] -K4 n. 睡眠 vi. 睡，睡觉 n. (Sleep)人名；(英)斯利普 时态: slept, sleeping, sleeps (中高雅 1172/1408)","They were exhausted from lack of sleep ...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to rest with your eyes closed and your mind and body not active","example":"to sleep well/deeply/soundly/badly"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to have enough beds for a particular number of people","example":"I couldn't sleep"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"I had to sleep on the sofa."}]],["small","/smɔ:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “small”.","small [smɔ:l] -K5 n. 小件物品；矮小的人 adj. 少的，小的；微弱的；几乎没有的；不重要的；幼小的 adv. 小小地；卑鄙地 n. (Small)人名；(英)斯莫尔 级别: smaller, smallest (中高 203/168)","欧陆词典释义：small [smɔ:l] -K5 n. 小件物品；矮小的人 adj. 少的，小的；微弱的；几乎没有的；不重要的；幼小的 adv. 小小地；卑鄙地 n. (Small)人名；(英)斯莫尔 级别: smaller, smallest (中高 203/168)","She is small for her age...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not large in size, number, degree, amount, etc.","example":"a small house/town/car/man"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used to describe one size in a range of sizes of clothes, food, products used in the house, etc.","example":"A much smaller number of students passed than I had expected."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"not as big as something else of the same kind","example":"They're having a relatively small wedding."}]],["smile","/smaɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “smile”.","smile [smaɪl] -K4 n. 微笑；笑容；喜色 vt. 微笑着表示 vi. 微笑 n. (Smile)人名；(塞)斯米莱 时态: smiled, smiling, smiles (中高 1068/892)","欧陆词典释义：smile [smaɪl] -K4 n. 微笑；笑容；喜色 vt. 微笑着表示 vi. 微笑 n. (Smile)人名；(塞)斯米莱 时态: smiled, smiling, smiles (中高 1068/892)","When he saw me, he smile d and waved...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make a smile appear on your face","example":"to smile sweetly/faintly/broadly, etc."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to say or express something with a smile","example":"He smiled with relief."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to give a smile of a particular type","example":"He never seems to smile."}]],["snow","/snəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “snow”.","snow [snəʊ] -K3 n. 雪，积雪；下雪 vt. 使纷纷落下；使变白 vi. 降雪 n. (Snow)人名；(英)斯诺 时态: snowed, snowing, snows (中高 1781/2665)","欧陆词典释义：snow [snəʊ] -K3 n. 雪，积雪；下雪 vt. 使纷纷落下；使变白 vi. 降雪 n. (Snow)人名；(英)斯诺 时态: snowed, snowing, snows (中高 1781/2665)","In Mid-Wales six inches of snow blocked roads...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"small soft white pieces (called flakes","example":"Snow was falling"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an amount of snow that falls in one particular place or at one particular time","example":"We had snow in May this year."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"The snow was beginning to melt."}]],["song","/sɒŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “song”.","song [sɒŋ] -K4 n. 歌曲；歌唱；诗歌；鸣声 n. (Song)人名；(泰)颂；(柬)松；(英)桑；(老)宋；(越)双；(东南亚国家华语)松 (中高 851/1405)","欧陆词典释义：song [sɒŋ] -K4 n. 歌曲；歌唱；诗歌；鸣声 n. (Song)人名；(泰)颂；(柬)松；(英)桑；(老)宋；(越)双；(东南亚国家华语)松 (中高 851/1405)","a voice singing a Spanish song .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a short piece of music with words that you sing","example":"a folk/love/pop, etc. song"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"songs in general; music for singing","example":"We sang a song"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the musical sounds that birds make","example":"She taught us the words of a French song."}]],["soon","/su:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “soon”.","soon [su:n] -K5 adv. 快；不久，一会儿；立刻；宁愿 (中高 610/615)","欧陆词典释义：soon [su:n] -K5 adv. 快；不久，一会儿；立刻；宁愿 (中高 610/615)","You'll be hearing from us very soon ...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"in a short time from now; a short time after something else has happened","example":"We’ll be home soon./We’ll soon be home."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"early; quickly","example":"She sold the house soon after"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"Old English","example":"I soon realized the mistake."}]],["sound","/saʊnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sound”.","sound [saʊnd] -K2 n. 声音，语音；噪音；海峡；吵闹；听力范围；[医] 探条 adj. 健全的，健康的；合理的；可靠的；有效彻底的 vt. 听（诊）；测量，测…深；使发声；试探；宣告 vi. 听起来；发出声音；回响；测深 adv. 彻底地，充分地 时态: sounded, sounding, sounds 级别: sounder, soundest (中高雅 702/780)","欧陆词典释义：sound [saʊnd] -K2 n. 声音，语音；噪音；海峡；吵闹；听力范围；[医] 探条 adj. 健全的，健康的；合理的；可靠的；有效彻底的 vt. 听（诊）；测量，测…深；使发声；试探；宣告 vi. 听起来；发出声音；回响；测深 adv. 彻底地，充分地 时态: sounded, sounding, sounds 级别: sounder, soundest (中高雅 702/780)","Peter heard the sound of gunfire...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that you can hear","example":"a high/low sound"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"continuous rapid movements (called vibrations","example":"a clicking/buzzing/scratching, etc. sound"},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"what you can hear coming from a television, radio, etc., or as part of a film/movie","example":"the different sounds and smells of the forest"}]],["south","/saʊθ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “south”.","south [saʊθ] -K4 n. 南方，南边；南部 adj. 南的，南方的 adv. 在南方，向南方 n. (South)人名；(老)苏；(英)索思 (中高 636/601)","欧陆词典释义：south [saʊθ] -K4 n. 南方，南边；南部 adj. 南的，南方的 adv. 在南方，向南方 n. (South)人名；(老)苏；(英)索思 (中高 636/601)","The town lies ten miles to the south of here...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the direction that is on your right when you watch the sun rise; one of the four main points of the compass","example":"Which way is south?"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the southern part of a country, a region or the world","example":"warmer weather coming from the south"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"the southern states of the US","example":"He lives to the south of"}]],["speak","/spi:k/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “speak”.","speak [spi:k] -K5 vi. 说话；演讲；表明；陈述 vt. 讲话；发言；讲演 时态: spoke, spoken, speaking, speaks (中高 335/352)","欧陆词典释义：speak [spi:k] -K5 vi. 说话；演讲；表明；陈述 vt. 讲话；发言；讲演 时态: spoke, spoken, speaking, speaks (中高 335/352)","He tried to speak , but for once, his voice had left him...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to talk to somebody about something; to have a conversation with somebody","example":"I've spoken to the manager about it."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to use your voice to say something","example":"The President refused to speak to the waiting journalists."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to mention or describe something/somebody","example":"‘Can I speak to Susan?’ ‘Speaking.’ ("}]],["special","/ˈspeʃl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “special”.","special [ˈspeʃl] -K5 n. 特使，特派人员；特刊；特色菜；专车；特价商品 adj. 特别的；专门的，专用的 (中高研四六雅 520/438)","欧陆词典释义：special [ˈspeʃl] -K5 n. 特使，特派人员；特刊；特色菜；专车；特价商品 adj. 特别的；专门的，专用的 (中高研四六雅 520/438)","You're very special to me, darling...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not ordinary or usual; different from what is normal","example":"The school will only allow this in special circumstances."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"more important than others; deserving or getting more attention than usual","example":"Some of the officials have special privileges."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"organized or intended for a particular purpose","example":"There is something special"}]],["spell","/spel/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “spell”.","spell [spel] -K3 n. 符咒；一段时间；魅力 vi. 拼字；轮替 vt. 拼，拼写；意味着；招致；拼成；迷住；轮值 n. (Spell)人名；(英)斯佩尔 时态: spelt, spelling, spells (中高研四六宝 4299/3382)","欧陆词典释义：spell [spel] -K3 n. 符咒；一段时间；魅力 vi. 拼字；轮替 vt. 拼，拼写；意味着；招致；拼成；迷住；轮值 n. (Spell)人名；(英)斯佩尔 时态: spelt, spelling, spells (中高研四六宝 4299/3382)","He gave his name and then helpfully spelt it...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to say or write the letters of a word in the correct order","example":"How do you spell your surname?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to form words correctly from individual letters","example":"I thought her name was Catherine, but it's Kathryn spelt with a ‘K’."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to form words when they are put together in a particular order","example":"I've never been able to spell."}]],["spend","/spend/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “spend”.","spend [spend] -K5 n. 预算 vt. 度过，消磨（时光）；花费；浪费；用尽 vi. 花钱；用尽，耗尽 时态: spent, spending, spends (中高 342/424)","欧陆词典释义：spend [spend] -K5 n. 预算 vt. 度过，消磨（时光）；花费；浪费；用尽 vi. 花钱；用尽，耗尽 时态: spent, spending, spends (中高 342/424)","By the end of the holiday I had spent all my money...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give money to pay for goods, services, etc.","example":"I've spent all my money already."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to use time for a particular purpose; to pass time","example":"She spent £100 on a new dress."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to use energy, effort, etc., especially until it has all been used","example":"The company has spent thousands of pounds updating their computer systems."}]],["sport","/spɔ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sport”.","sport [spɔ:t] -K4 n. 运动；游戏；娱乐；运动会；玩笑 adj. 运动的 vt. 游戏；参加体育运动；夸耀 vi. 游戏 时态: sported, sporting, sports (中高雅宝 666/1122)","欧陆词典释义：sport [spɔ:t] -K4 n. 运动；游戏；娱乐；运动会；玩笑 adj. 运动的 vt. 游戏；参加体育运动；夸耀 vi. 游戏 时态: sported, sporting, sports (中高雅宝 666/1122)","I'd say football is my favourite sport ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"activity that you do for pleasure and that needs physical effort or skill, usually done in a special area and according to fixed rules","example":"There are excellent facilities for sport and recreation."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular form of sport","example":"I'm not interested in sport."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used as a friendly way of addressing somebody, especially a man","example":"the use of drugs in sport"}]],["spring","/sprɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “spring”.","spring [sprɪŋ] -K4 n. 春天；弹簧；泉水；活力；跳跃 adj. 春天的 vt. 使跳起；使爆炸；突然提出；使弹开 vi. 生长；涌出；跃出；裂开 n. (Spring)人名；(德)施普林；(英、芬、瑞典)斯普林 时态: sprang, sprung, springing, springs (中高托雅 901/1503)","欧陆词典释义：spring [sprɪŋ] -K4 n. 春天；弹簧；泉水；活力；跳跃 adj. 春天的 vt. 使跳起；使爆炸；突然提出；使弹开 vi. 生长；涌出；跃出；裂开 n. (Spring)人名；(德)施普林；(英、芬、瑞典)斯普林 时态: sprang, sprung, springing, springs (中高托雅 901/1503)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “spring”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the season between winter and summer when plants begin to grow","example":"flowers that bloom in spring/in the spring"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a twisted piece of metal that can be pushed, pressed or pulled but which always returns to its original shape or position afterwards","example":"He was born in the spring of 1944."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the ability of a spring","example":"There's a feeling of spring in the air today."}]],["stand","/stænd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “stand”.","stand [stænd] -K5 n. 站立；立场；看台；停止 vi. 站立；位于；停滞 vt. 使站立；忍受；抵抗 时态: stood, standing, stands (中高托雅 281/273)","欧陆词典释义：stand [stænd] -K5 n. 站立；立场；看台；停止 vi. 站立；位于；停滞 vt. 使站立；忍受；抵抗 时态: stood, standing, stands (中高托雅 281/273)","She was stand ing beside my bed staring down at me...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be on your feet; to be in a vertical position","example":"She was too weak to stand."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to get up onto your feet from another position","example":"a bird standing on one leg"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to put something/somebody in a vertical position somewhere","example":"Don't just stand there"}]],["star","/stɑ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “star”.","star [stɑ:(r)] -K5 n. 星，恒星；明星；星形物 adj. 明星的，主角的；星形的 vt. 用星号标于；由…主演，由…担任主角 vi. 担任主角 n. (Star)人名；(瑞典)斯塔尔；(德)施塔尔 时态: starred, starring, stars (中高雅 538/1001)","欧陆词典释义：star [stɑ:(r)] -K5 n. 星，恒星；明星；星形物 adj. 明星的，主角的；星形的 vt. 用星号标于；由…主演，由…担任主角 vi. 担任主角 n. (Star)人名；(瑞典)斯塔尔；(德)施塔尔 时态: starred, starring, stars (中高雅 538/1001)","The night was dark, the star s hidden behind cloud.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large ball of burning gas in space that we see as a point of light in the sky at night","example":"There was a big moon and hundreds of stars were shining overhead."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an object, a decoration, a mark, etc., usually with five or six points, whose shape represents a star","example":"Sirius is the brightest star in the sky."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a mark that represents a star","example":"We camped out under the stars"}]],["start","/stɑ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “start”.","start [stɑ:t] -K5 n. 开始；起点 vt. 开始；启动 vi. 出发 时态: started, starting, starts (中高 173/205)","欧陆词典释义：start [stɑ:t] -K5 n. 开始；起点 vt. 开始；启动 vi. 出发 时态: started, starting, starts (中高 173/205)","John then unlocked the front door and I start ed to follow him up the stairs...",""],["station","/ˈsteɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “station”.","station [ˈsteɪʃn] -K4 n. 车站；驻地；地位；身份 vt. 配置；安置；驻扎 时态: stationed, stationing, stations (中高雅 841/736)","欧陆词典释义：station [ˈsteɪʃn] -K4 n. 车站；驻地；地位；身份 vt. 配置；安置；驻扎 时态: stationed, stationing, stations (中高雅 841/736)","Ingrid went with him to the railway station to see him off...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place where trains stop so that passengers can get on and off; the buildings connected with this","example":"I get off at the next station."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a place where buses stop; the buildings connected with this","example":"the main station"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a place or building where a service is organized and provided or a special type of work is done","example":"Penn Station"}]],["stay","/steɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “stay”.","stay [steɪ] -K5 n. 逗留；停止；支柱 vi. 停留；坚持；暂住；停下 vt. 坚持；暂住；抑制 时态: stayed, staying, stays (中高 409/549)","欧陆词典释义：stay [steɪ] -K5 n. 逗留；停止；支柱 vi. 停留；坚持；暂住；停下 vt. 坚持；暂住；抑制 时态: stayed, staying, stays (中高 409/549)","'Stay here,' Trish said. 'I'll bring the car down the drive to take you back.'...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to continue to be in a particular place for a period of time without moving away","example":"to stay in bed"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to continue to be in a particular state or situation","example":"‘Do you want a drink?’ ‘No, thanks, I can't stay.’"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to live in a place temporarily as a guest or visitor","example":"Stay there and don't move!"}]],["stop","/stɒp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “stop”.","stop [stɒp] -K5 n. 停止；车站；障碍；逗留 vi. 停止；中止；逗留；被塞住 vt. 停止；堵塞；断绝 时态: stopped, stopping, stops (中高 329/359)","欧陆词典释义：stop [stɒp] -K5 n. 停止；车站；障碍；逗留 vi. 停止；中止；逗留；被塞住 vt. 停止；堵塞；断绝 时态: stopped, stopping, stops (中高 329/359)","Stop throwing those stones!...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to no longer move; to make somebody/something no longer move","example":"The car stopped at the traffic lights."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to no longer continue to do something; to make somebody/something no longer do something","example":"Ann stopped in front of the house."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to end or finish; to make something end or finish","example":"This train doesn’t stop at Oxford."}]],["street","/stri:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “street”.","street [stri:t] -K5 n. 街道 adj. 街道的 n. (Street)人名；(英、葡)斯特里特；(德)施特雷特 (中高雅 554/380)","欧陆词典释义：street [stri:t] -K5 n. 街道 adj. 街道的 n. (Street)人名；(英、葡)斯特里特；(德)施特雷特 (中高雅 554/380)","He lived at 66 Bingfield Street...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a public road in a city or town that has houses and buildings on one side or both sides","example":"The bank is just across the street."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the ideas and opinions of ordinary people, especially people who live in cities, which are considered important","example":"to walk along/down/up the street"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"Old English","example":"the town’s narrow cobbled streets"}]],["strong","/strɒŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “strong”.","strong [strɒŋ] -K5 adj. 坚强的；强壮的；牢固的；擅长的 adv. 强劲地；猛烈地 n. (Strong)人名；(英)斯特朗 级别: stronger, strongest (中高 458/506)","欧陆词典释义：strong [strɒŋ] -K5 adj. 坚强的；强壮的；牢固的；擅长的 adv. 强劲地；猛烈地 n. (Strong)人名；(英)斯特朗 级别: stronger, strongest (中高 458/506)","I'm not strong enough to carry him...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a lot of physical power so that you can lift heavy weights, do hard physical work, etc.","example":"strong muscles"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having great power","example":"She wasn't a strong swimmer ("},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a powerful effect on the body or mind","example":"He's strong enough to lift a car!"}]],["student","/ˈstju:dnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “student”.","student [ˈstju:dnt] -K5 n. 学生；学者 n. (Student)人名；(德)施图登特 (中高雅 157/432)","欧陆词典释义：student [ˈstju:dnt] -K5 n. 学生；学者 n. (Student)人名；(德)施图登特 (中高雅 157/432)","Warren's eldest son is an art student , at St Martin's.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who is studying at a university or college","example":"a medical/science, etc. student"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who is studying at a school, especially a secondary school","example":"a graduate/postgraduate/research student"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who is very interested in a particular subject","example":"an overseas student"}]],["study","/ˈstʌdi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “study”.","study [ˈstʌdi] -K5 n. 学习，研究；课题；书房；学问 vt. 学习；考虑；攻读；细察 vi. 研究；用功 n. (Study)人名；(英)斯塔迪 时态: studied, studying, studies (中高雅 240/270)","欧陆词典释义：study [ˈstʌdi] -K5 n. 学习，研究；课题；书房；学问 vt. 学习；考虑；攻读；细察 vi. 研究；用功 n. (Study)人名；(英)斯塔迪 时态: studied, studying, studies (中高雅 240/270)","a relaxed and happy atmosphere that will allow you to study to your full potential...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the activity of learning or gaining knowledge, either from books or by examining things in the world","example":"a room set aside for private study"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular person’s learning activities, for example at a college or university","example":"academic/literary/scientific, etc. study"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used in the names of some academic subjects","example":"It is important to develop good study skills"}]],["table","/ˈteɪbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “table”.","table [ˈteɪbl] -K4 n. 桌子；表格；平地层 vt. 制表；搁置；嵌合 adj. 桌子的 n. (Table)人名；(罗)塔布莱 时态: tabled, tabling, tables (中高雅宝 539/410)","欧陆词典释义：table [ˈteɪbl] -K4 n. 桌子；表格；平地层 vt. 制表；搁置；嵌合 adj. 桌子的 n. (Table)人名；(罗)塔布莱 时态: tabled, tabling, tables (中高雅宝 539/410)","She was sitting at the kitchen table eating a currant bun...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of furniture that consists of a flat top supported by legs","example":"a kitchen table"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the people sitting at a table for a meal or to play cards, etc.","example":"A table for two, please ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a list of facts or numbers arranged in a special order, usually in rows and columns","example":"I'd like to book a table"}]],["take","/teɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “take”.","take [teɪk] -K1 vi. 拿；获得 vt. 拿，取；采取；接受（礼物等）；买，花费；耗费（时间等） n. 捕获量；看法；利益，盈益；（入场券的）售得金额 时态: took, taken, taking, takes (中高雅 63/51)","欧陆词典释义：take [teɪk] -K1 vi. 拿；获得 vt. 拿，取；采取；接受（礼物等）；买，花费；耗费（时间等） n. 捕获量；看法；利益，盈益；（入场券的）售得金额 时态: took, taken, taking, takes (中高雅 63/51)","She was too tired to take a shower...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to carry or move something from one place to another","example":"I forgot to take my bag with me when I got off the bus."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to go with somebody from one place to another, especially to guide or lead them","example":"Take this to the bank for me, would you?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to make somebody/something go from one level, situation, etc. to another","example":"Shall I take a gift to my host family?"}]],["talk","/tɔ:k/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “talk”.","talk [tɔ:k] -K5 n. 谈话；演讲；空谈 vi. 谈话；说闲话 vt. 说；谈话；讨论 时态: talked, talking, talks (中高 168/289)","欧陆词典释义：talk [tɔ:k] -K5 n. 谈话；演讲；空谈 vi. 谈话；说闲话 vt. 说；谈话；讨论 时态: talked, talking, talks (中高 168/289)","He was too distressed to talk ...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to say things; to speak in order to give information or to express feelings, ideas, etc.","example":"Stop talking and listen!"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to discuss something, usually something serious or important","example":"We talked on the phone for over an hour."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to say words in a language","example":"Who were you talking to just now?"}]],["tall","/tɔ:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “tall”.","tall [tɔ:l] -K3 adj. 高的；长的；过分的；夸大的 adv. 夸大地 n. (Tall)人名；(马里、阿拉伯)塔勒；(芬、罗、瑞典)塔尔；(英)托尔；(土)塔勒 级别: taller, tallest (中高 1524/1757)","欧陆词典释义：tall [tɔ:l] -K3 adj. 高的；长的；过分的；夸大的 adv. 夸大地 n. (Tall)人名；(马里、阿拉伯)塔勒；(芬、罗、瑞典)塔尔；(英)托尔；(土)塔勒 级别: taller, tallest (中高 1524/1757)","Being tall can make you feel incredibly self-confident...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a greater than average height","example":"She's tall and thin."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used to describe or ask about the height of somebody/something","example":"tall chimneys"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"the tallest building in the world"}]],["teacher","/ˈti:tʃə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “teacher”.","teacher [ˈti:tʃə(r)] -K n. 教师；导师 n. (Teacher)人名；(英)蒂彻 (中高雅 371/486)","欧陆词典释义：teacher [ˈti:tʃə(r)] -K n. 教师；导师 n. (Teacher)人名；(英)蒂彻 (中高雅 371/486)","I'm a teacher with 21 years' experience.",""],["team","/ti:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “team”.","team [ti:m] -K5 n. 队；组 vt. 使合作 vi. 合作 n. (Team)人名；(柬)甸 时态: teamed, teaming, teams (中高研四六托雅 307/427)","欧陆词典释义：team [ti:m] -K5 n. 队；组 vt. 使合作 vi. 合作 n. (Team)人名；(柬)甸 时态: teamed, teaming, teams (中高研四六托雅 307/427)","The team failed to qualify for the African Nations Cup finals...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of people who play a particular game or sport against another group of people","example":"a football/baseball, etc. team"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a group of people who work together at a particular job","example":"a team event"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"two or more animals that are used together to pull a cart","example":"Whose team are you in?"}]],["tell","/tel/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “tell”.","tell [tel] -K5 vt. 告诉，说；辨别；吩咐；断定 vi. 讲述；告发，泄密；识别 n. (Tell)人名；(英、德、瑞典)特尔；(罗、意)泰尔；(阿拉伯)塔勒 时态: told, telling, tells (中高 103/107)","欧陆词典释义：tell [tel] -K5 vt. 告诉，说；辨别；吩咐；断定 vi. 讲述；告发，泄密；识别 n. (Tell)人名；(英、德、瑞典)特尔；(罗、意)泰尔；(阿拉伯)塔勒 时态: told, telling, tells (中高 103/107)","In the evening I returned to tell Phyllis our relationship was over...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give information to somebody by speaking or writing","example":"He told the news to everybody he saw."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give information about something","example":"He told everybody he saw the news."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to express something in words","example":"Did she tell you her name?"}]],["ten","/ten/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ten”.","ten [ten] -5 num. 十个，十 n. (Ten)人名；(英)坦恩；(意)泰恩；(柬)登 (中高 838/469)","欧陆词典释义：ten [ten] -5 num. 十个，十 n. (Ten)人名；(英)坦恩；(意)泰恩；(柬)登 (中高 838/469)","Over the past ten years things have changed.",[{"pos":"number","definition":"10","example":"Not brilliant, Robyn, but I'll give you ten out of ten for effort."},{"pos":"number","definition":"Old English","example":"Ten to one he'll be late."},{"pos":"number","definition":"used to say that somebody has guessed something correctly or done something very well","example":"Not brilliant, Robyn, but I'll give you ten out of ten for effort."}]],["thank","/θæŋk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “thank”.","thank [θæŋk] -K5 n. 感谢 vt. 感谢 int. 谢谢 时态: thanked, thanking, thanks (中高 498/768)","欧陆词典释义：thank [θæŋk] -K5 n. 感谢 vt. 感谢 int. 谢谢 时态: thanked, thanking, thanks (中高 498/768)","Thank you very much for your call...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to tell somebody that you are grateful for something","example":"I must write and thank Mary for the present."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"In his speech, he thanked everyone for all their hard work."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used when you are saying who is responsible for something","example":"She said goodbye and thanked us for coming."}]],["theater","/'θɪətə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “theater”.","theater ['θɪətə] n. 电影院，戏院，剧场；戏剧；手术室 (研托 1535/39534)","欧陆词典释义：theater ['θɪətə] n. 电影院，戏院，剧场；戏剧；手术室 (研托 1535/39534)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “theater”.",""],["their","/ðeə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “their”.","their [ðeə(r)] -K5 pron. 他们的，她们的；它们的 n. (Their)人名；(英)蒂尔；(芬、瑞典)泰尔 原型: they (中高 36/36)","欧陆词典释义：their [ðeə(r)] -K5 pron. 他们的，她们的；它们的 n. (Their)人名；(英)蒂尔；(芬、瑞典)泰尔 原型: they (中高 36/36)","Janis and Kurt have announced their engagement...",[{"pos":"determiner","definition":"of or belonging to them","example":"Their parties are always fun."},{"pos":"determiner","definition":"used instead of his","example":"Which is their house?"},{"pos":"determiner","definition":"Middle English","example":"If anyone calls, ask for their number so I can call them back."}]],["then","/ðen/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “then”.","then [ðen] -K5 conj. 然后，当时 n. 那时 adv. 然后；那么；于是；当时；此外 n. (Then)人名；(德)特恩 (中高 77/59)","欧陆词典释义：then [ðen] -K5 conj. 然后，当时 n. 那时 adv. 然后；那么；于是；当时；此外 n. (Then)人名；(德)特恩 (中高 77/59)","He wanted to have a source of income after his retirement; until then , he wouldn't require additional money...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used to refer to a particular time in the past or future","example":"Life was harder then because neither of us had a job."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used to introduce the next item in a series of actions, events, instructions, etc.","example":"Things were very different back then"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used to show the logical result of a particular statement or situation","example":"She grew up in Zimbabwe, or Rhodesia as it then was."}]],["there","/ðeə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “there”.","there [ðeə(r)] -K5 n. 那个地方 adv. 在那里；在那边；在那点上 int. 你瞧 (中高 53/37)","欧陆词典释义：there [ðeə(r)] -K5 n. 那个地方 adv. 在那里；在那边；在那点上 int. 你瞧 (中高 53/37)","There are roadworks between Camblesforth and Carlton...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used to show that something exists or happens","example":"There's a restaurant around the corner."},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"in, at or to that place or position","example":"There are two people waiting outside."},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"existing or available","example":"Has there been an accident?"}]],["thing","/θɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “thing”.","thing [θɪŋ] -K5 n. 事情；东西；事物；情况 (中高 97/106)","欧陆词典释义：thing [θɪŋ] -K5 n. 事情；东西；事物；情况 (中高 97/106)","'What's that thing in the middle of the fountain?' — 'Some kind of statue, I guess.'...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an object whose name you do not use because you do not need to or want to, or because you do not know it","example":"Can you pass me that thing over there?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an object that is not alive in the way that people and plants are","example":"She's very fond of sweet things ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"objects, clothing or tools that belong to somebody or are used for a particular purpose","example":"He's just bought one of those exercise things."}]],["think","/θɪŋk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “think”.","think [θɪŋk] -K5 n. 想；想法 adj. 思想的 vi. 想；认为 vt. 想；认为；想起；想像；打算 时态: thought, thinking, thinks (中高 56/64)","欧陆词典释义：think [θɪŋk] -K5 n. 想；想法 adj. 思想的 vi. 想；认为 vt. 想；认为；想起；想像；打算 时态: thought, thinking, thinks (中高 56/64)","I certainly think there should be a ban on tobacco advertising...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have a particular idea or opinion about something/somebody; to believe something","example":"Do you think (that) they’ll come?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to use your mind to consider something, to form connected ideas, to try to solve problems, etc.","example":"I thought I heard a scream."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to have ideas, words or images in your mind","example":"I didn't think you liked sports."}]],["third","/θɜ:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “third”.","third [θɜ:d] -4 num. 第三；三分之一 adj. 第三的；三分之一的 (中高雅 584/465)","欧陆词典释义：third [θɜ:d] -4 num. 第三；三分之一 adj. 第三的；三分之一的 (中高雅 584/465)","I sleep on the third floor...",[{"pos":"ordinal number","definition":"3rd","example":"According to this pie chart, a third of"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"One in five"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used when you have failed to do something twice and hope that you will succeed the third time","example":"Socializing accounts for"}]],["this","/ðɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “this”.","this [ðɪs] -K5 adj. 这；本；这个；今 pron. 这；这个；这里 adv. 这样地；这么 n. (This)人名；(法)蒂斯 (中高 20/23)","欧陆词典释义：this [ðɪs] -K5 adj. 这；本；这个；今 pron. 这；这个；这里 adv. 这样地；这么 n. (This)人名；(法)蒂斯 (中高 20/23)","When food comes out of any oven, it should stand a while. During this delay the centre carries on cooking...",[{"pos":"determiner","definition":"used to refer to a particular person, thing or event that is close to you, especially compared with another","example":"How long have you been living in this country?"},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"used to refer to something/somebody that has already been mentioned","example":"Well, make up your mind. Which do you want? This one or that one?"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used for introducing somebody or showing something to somebody","example":"I think you'll find these more comfortable than those."}]],["ticket","/ˈtɪkɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ticket”.","ticket [ˈtɪkɪt] -K4 n. 票；入场券，标签；（美）候选人名单；证明书；交通罚款单 vt. 加标签于；指派；对…开出交通违规罚单 时态: ticketed, ticketing, tickets (中高托雅 1576/1884)","欧陆词典释义：ticket [ˈtɪkɪt] -K4 n. 票；入场券，标签；（美）候选人名单；证明书；交通罚款单 vt. 加标签于；指派；对…开出交通违规罚单 时态: ticketed, ticketing, tickets (中高托雅 1576/1884)","I queued for two hours to get a ticket to see the football game...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a printed piece of paper that gives you the right to travel on a particular bus, train, etc. or to go into a theatre, etc.","example":"a bus/theatre/plane, etc. ticket"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a printed piece of paper with a number or numbers on it, that you buy in order to have the chance of winning a prize if the number or numbers are later chosen","example":"free tickets to the show"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a label that is attached to something in a shop/store giving details of its price, size, etc.","example":"Tickets are available from the Arts Centre at £5.00."}]],["time","/taɪm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “time”.","time [taɪm] -K5 n. 时间；时代；次数；节拍；倍数 adj. 定时的；定期的；分期的 vt. 计时；测定…的时间；安排…的速度 n. (Time)人名；(俄)季梅；(英)泰姆；(罗)蒂梅 时态: timed, timing, times (中高雅 52/50)","欧陆词典释义：time [taɪm] -K5 n. 时间；时代；次数；节拍；倍数 adj. 定时的；定期的；分期的 vt. 计时；测定…的时间；安排…的速度 n. (Time)人名；(俄)季梅；(英)泰姆；(罗)蒂梅 时态: timed, timing, times (中高雅 52/50)","a two-week period of time ...",""],["tired","/ˈtaɪəd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “tired”.","tired [ˈtaɪəd] -K3 v. 疲倦；对…腻烦（tire的过去分词形式） adj. 疲倦的；厌倦的，厌烦的 原型: tired 是 tire 的过去式 (中高 1959/2210)","欧陆词典释义：tired [ˈtaɪəd] -K3 v. 疲倦；对…腻烦（tire的过去分词形式） adj. 疲倦的；厌倦的，厌烦的 原型: tired 是 tire 的过去式 (中高 1959/2210)","Michael is tired and he has to rest after his long trip.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"feeling that you would like to sleep or rest; needing rest","example":"to be/look/feel tired"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"feeling that you have had enough of somebody/something because you no longer find them/it interesting or because they make you angry or unhappy","example":"I'm too tired even to think."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"boring because it is too familiar or has been used too much","example":"They were cold, hungry and tired out"}]],["title","/ˈtaɪtl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “title”.","title [ˈtaɪtl] -K4 n. 冠军；标题；头衔；权利；字幕 adj. 冠军的；标题的；头衔的 vt. 加标题于；赋予头衔；把…称为 时态: titled, titling, titles (高研四六托雅 1323/855)","欧陆词典释义：title [ˈtaɪtl] -K4 n. 冠军；标题；头衔；权利；字幕 adj. 冠军的；标题的；头衔的 vt. 加标题于；赋予头衔；把…称为 时态: titled, titling, titles (高研四六托雅 1323/855)","'Patience and Sarah' was first published in 1969 under the title 'A Place for Us'.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the name of a book, poem, painting, piece of music, etc.","example":"His poems were published under the title of ‘Love and Reason’."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular book or magazine","example":"the title track"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a word in front of a person’s name to show their rank or profession, whether or not they are married, etc.","example":"She has sung the title role in ‘Carmen’ ("}]],["today","/təˈdeɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “today”.","today [təˈdeɪ] -K5 n. 今天；现今 adv. 今天；现今 n. (Today)人名；(英)托迪 (中高 214/350)","欧陆词典释义：today [təˈdeɪ] -K5 n. 今天；现今 adv. 今天；现今 n. (Today)人名；(英)托迪 (中高 214/350)","How are you feeling today ?...",""],["together","/təˈgeðə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “together”.","together [təˈgeðə(r)] -K5 adj. 新潮的；情绪稳定的，做事有效率的 adv. 一起；同时；相互；连续地；总共 (中高 324/288)","欧陆词典释义：together [təˈgeðə(r)] -K5 adj. 新潮的；情绪稳定的，做事有效率的 adv. 一起；同时；相互；连续地；总共 (中高 324/288)","We went on long bicycle rides together ...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"with or near to somebody/something else; with each other","example":"We grew up together."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"so that two or more things touch or are joined to or combined with each other","example":"Together they climbed the dark stairs."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"in a close relationship, for example a marriage","example":"Get all the ingredients together before you start cooking."}]],["tomorrow","/təˈmɒrəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “tomorrow”.","tomorrow [təˈmɒrəʊ] -K4 n. 明天；未来 adv. 明天；未来地（等于to-morrow） (中高 1334/1075)","欧陆词典释义：tomorrow [təˈmɒrəʊ] -K4 n. 明天；未来 adv. 明天；未来地（等于to-morrow） (中高 1334/1075)","Bye, see you tomorrow ...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"on or during the day after today","example":"I'm off now. See you tomorrow."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"She's leaving tomorrow."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"good things that are promised for the future but never happen","example":"They arrive a week tomorrow/tomorrow week"}]],["town","/taʊn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “town”.","town [taʊn] -K5 n. 城镇，市镇；市内商业区 n. (Town)人名；(英)汤 (中高雅 488/433)","欧陆词典释义：town [taʊn] -K5 n. 城镇，市镇；市内商业区 n. (Town)人名；(英)汤 (中高雅 488/433)","Saturday night in the small town of Braintree, Essex...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place with many houses, shops/stores, etc. where people live and work. It is larger than a village but smaller than a city","example":"a university town"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the people who live in a particular town","example":"They live in a rough part of town."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the area of a town","example":"The nearest town is ten miles away."}]],["train","/treɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “train”.","train [treɪn] -K4 n. 火车；行列；长队；裙裾 v. 培养；训练；瞄准 n. (Train)人名；(英)特雷恩；(法)特兰；(意)特拉因 时态: trained, training, trains (中高雅 1516/1186)","欧陆词典释义：train [treɪn] -K4 n. 火车；行列；长队；裙裾 v. 培养；训练；瞄准 n. (Train)人名；(英)特雷恩；(法)特兰；(意)特拉因 时态: trained, training, trains (中高雅 1516/1186)","The train pulled into a station...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a railway/railroad engine pulling a number of coaches/cars or trucks, taking people and goods from one place to another","example":"to get on/off a train"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a number of people or animals moving in a line","example":"I like travelling by train"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a series of events or actions that are connected","example":"a passenger/commuter/goods/freight train"}]],["travel","/ˈtrævl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “travel”.","travel [ˈtrævl] -K4 n. 旅行；游历；漫游 vt. 经过；在…旅行 vi. 旅行；行进；步行；交往 时态: travelled, travelling, travels (中高雅 1081/1132)","欧陆词典释义：travel [ˈtrævl] -K4 n. 旅行；游历；漫游 vt. 经过；在…旅行 vi. 旅行；行进；步行；交往 时态: travelled, travelling, travels (中高雅 1081/1132)","You had better travel to Helsinki tomorrow...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to go from one place to another, especially over a long distance","example":"to travel around the world"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to go or move at a particular speed, in a particular direction, or a particular distance","example":"I go to bed early if I'm travelling the next day."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be still in good condition after a long journey","example":"I love travelling by train."}]],["tree","/tri:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “tree”.","tree [tri:] -K4 n. 树；木料；树状物 vt. 把...赶上树 vi. 爬上树；逃上树 n. (Tree)人名；(英)特里 时态: treed, treeing, trees (中高雅 596/680)","欧陆词典释义：tree [tri:] -K4 n. 树；木料；树状物 vt. 把...赶上树 vi. 爬上树；逃上树 n. (Tree)人名；(英)特里 时态: treed, treeing, trees (中高雅 596/680)","I planted those apple tree s.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a tall plant that can live a long time. Trees","example":"an oak tree"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"to plant a tree"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a child usually behaves in a similar way to his or her parent(s)","example":"to chop/cut down a tree"}]],["trip","/trɪp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “trip”.","trip [trɪp] -K4 n. 旅行；绊倒；差错 vt. 绊倒；使犯错 vi. 绊倒；远足；犯错误；轻快地走 n. (Trip)人名；(荷)特里普 时态: tripped, tripping, trips (中高托雅 962/1664)","欧陆词典释义：trip [trɪp] -K4 n. 旅行；绊倒；差错 vt. 绊倒；使犯错 vi. 绊倒；远足；犯错误；轻快地走 n. (Trip)人名；(荷)特里普 时态: tripped, tripping, trips (中高托雅 962/1664)","On the Thursday we went out on a day trip ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a journey to a place and back again, especially a short one for pleasure or a particular purpose","example":"Did you have a good trip?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the experience that somebody has if they take a powerful drug that affects the mind and makes them imagine things","example":"We went on a trip"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an act of falling or nearly falling down, because you hit your foot against something","example":"a day trip"}]],["trouble","/ˈtrʌbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “trouble”.","trouble [ˈtrʌbl] -K4 n. 麻烦；烦恼；故障；动乱 vt. 麻烦；使烦恼；折磨 vi. 费心，烦恼 时态: troubled, troubling, troubles (中高托雅 981/1005)","欧陆词典释义：trouble [ˈtrʌbl] -K4 n. 麻烦；烦恼；故障；动乱 vt. 麻烦；使烦恼；折磨 vi. 费心，烦恼 时态: troubled, troubling, troubles (中高托雅 981/1005)","I had trouble parking...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a problem, worry, difficulty, etc. or a situation causing this","example":"We have trouble"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"illness or pain","example":"He could make trouble for me"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"something that is wrong with a machine, vehicle, etc.","example":"The trouble with you is"}]],["true","/tru:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “true”.","true [tru:] -K4 n. 真实；准确 adj. 真实的；正确的 vt. 装准 adv. 真实地；准确地 n. (TRUE)人名；(英)特鲁 时态: trued, truing, trues 级别: truer, truest (中高 492/547)","欧陆词典释义：true [tru:] -K4 n. 真实；准确 adj. 真实的；正确的 vt. 装准 adv. 真实地；准确地 n. (TRUE)人名；(英)特鲁 时态: trued, truing, trues 级别: truer, truest (中高 492/547)","Everything I had heard about him was true ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with facts rather than things that have been invented or guessed","example":"Indicate whether the following statements are true or false"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"real or exact, especially when this is different from how something seems","example":"Is it true she's leaving?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"having the qualities or characteristics of the thing mentioned","example":"Can you prove that what you say is true?"}]],["try","/traɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “try”.","try [traɪ] -K5 n. 尝试；努力；试验 vt. 试图，努力；试验；审判；考验 vi. 尝试；努力；试验 n. (Try)人名；(英、印尼)特里；(柬)德里 时态: tried, trying, tries (中高 127/159)","欧陆词典释义：try [traɪ] -K5 n. 尝试；努力；试验 vt. 试图，努力；试验；审判；考验 vi. 尝试；努力；试验 n. (Try)人名；(英、印尼)特里；(柬)德里 时态: tried, trying, tries (中高 127/159)","He secretly tried to block her advancement in the Party...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make an attempt or effort to do or get something","example":"I don't know if I can come but I'll try."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to use, do or test something in order to see if it is good, suitable, etc.","example":"What are you trying to do?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to examine evidence in court and decide whether somebody is innocent or guilty","example":"I tried hard not to laugh."}]],["turn","/tɜ:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “turn”.","turn [tɜ:n] -K5 n. 转弯；变化；(损害或有益于别人的)行为，举动，举止 vi. 转向；转变；转动 vt. 转动，使旋转；转弯；翻过来；兑换 n. (Turn)人名；(德、匈)图恩 时态: turned, turning, turns (中高 170/183)","欧陆词典释义：turn [tɜ:n] -K5 n. 转弯；变化；(损害或有益于别人的)行为，举动，举止 vi. 转向；转变；转动 vt. 转动，使旋转；转弯；翻过来；兑换 n. (Turn)人名；(德、匈)图恩 时态: turned, turning, turns (中高 170/183)","He turn ed abruptly and walked away...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move or make something move around a central point","example":"The wheels of the car began to turn."},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to move your body or part of your body so as to face or start moving in a different direction","example":"I can't get the screw to turn."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to move something so that it is in a different position or facing a different direction","example":"He turned the key in the lock."}]],["twelve","/twelv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “twelve”.","twelve [twelv] -5 num. 十二；十二个 n. 十二；十二个 adj. 十二的；十二个的 (中高 3218/1447)","欧陆词典释义：twelve [twelv] -5 num. 十二；十二个 n. 十二；十二个 adj. 十二的；十二个的 (中高 3218/1447)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “twelve”.",""],["twenty","/ˈtwenti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “twenty”.","twenty [ˈtwenti] -5 num. 二十 n. 二十；二十年代 adj. 二十的 (中高 2086/605)","欧陆词典释义：twenty [ˈtwenti] -5 num. 二十 n. 二十；二十年代 adj. 二十的 (中高 2086/605)","They're both in their twenties and both married with children of their own.",[{"pos":"number","definition":"20","example":""},{"pos":"noun","definition":"numbers, years or temperatures from 20 to 29","example":""},{"pos":"noun","definition":"between the ages of 20 and 29","example":""}]],["two","/tu:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “two”.","two [tu:] -5 num. 二 n. 两个 adj. 两个的 (中高 80/60)","欧陆词典释义：two [tu:] -5 num. 二 n. 两个 adj. 两个的 (中高 80/60)","Divorce is never the fault of one partner; it takes two ...",[{"pos":"number","definition":"2","example":"I was in two minds about the book ("},{"pos":"number","definition":"Old English","example":"She's in two minds about accepting his invitation."},{"pos":"number","definition":"to be unable to decide what you think about somebody/something, or whether to do something or not","example":"May I borrow it for a day or two?"}]],["under","/ˈʌndə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “under”.","under [ˈʌndə(r)] -K5 prep. 低于，少于；在...之下 adj. 下面的；从属的 adv. 在下面；在下方 (中高 225/158)","欧陆词典释义：under [ˈʌndə(r)] -K5 prep. 低于，少于；在...之下 adj. 下面的；从属的 adv. 在下面；在下方 (中高 225/158)","They found a labyrinth of tunnels under the ground.",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"in, to or through a position that is below something","example":"Have you looked under the bed?"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"below the surface of something; covered by something","example":"She placed the ladder under ("},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"less than; younger than","example":"The dog squeezed under the gate and ran into the road."}]],["understand","/ˌʌndəˈstænd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “understand”.","understand [ˌʌndəˈstænd] -K5 vi. 理解；懂得；熟悉 vt. 理解；懂；获悉；推断；省略 时态: understood, understanding, understands (中高托 320/391)","欧陆词典释义：understand [ˌʌndəˈstænd] -K5 vi. 理解；懂得；熟悉 vt. 理解；懂；获悉；推断；省略 时态: understood, understanding, understands (中高托 320/391)","I think you heard and also understand me...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to know or realize the meaning of words, a language, what somebody says, etc.","example":"Can you understand French?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to know or realize how or why something happens, how it works or why it is important","example":"Do you understand the instructions?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to know somebody’s character, how they feel and why they behave in the way they do","example":"She didn't understand the form she was signing."}]],["uncle","/ˈʌŋkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “uncle”.","uncle [ˈʌŋkl] -K3 n. 叔叔；伯父；伯伯；舅父；姨丈；姑父 (中高 3345/2301)","欧陆词典释义：uncle [ˈʌŋkl] -K3 n. 叔叔；伯父；伯伯；舅父；姨丈；姑父 (中高 3345/2301)","My uncle was the mayor of Memphis...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the brother of your mother or father; the husband of your aunt","example":"Uncle Ian"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used by children, with a first name, to address a man who is a close friend of their parents","example":"I'm going to visit my uncle."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"I've just become an uncle ("}]],["until","/ənˈtɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “until”.","until [ənˈtɪl] -K5 prep. 在…以前；到…为止 conj. 在…以前；直到…时 (中高 270/382)","欧陆词典释义：until [ənˈtɪl] -K5 prep. 在…以前；到…为止 conj. 在…以前；直到…时 (中高 270/382)","Until 1982 he was senior lecturer in botany at Durham University.",""],["use","/ju:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “use”.","use [ju:s] -K4 n. 使用；用途；发挥 vt. 利用；耗费 vi. 使用，运用 n. (Use)人名；(德)乌泽 时态: used, using, uses (中高 92/87)","欧陆词典释义：use [ju:s] -K4 n. 使用；用途；发挥 vt. 利用；耗费 vi. 使用，运用 n. (Use)人名；(德)乌泽 时态: used, using, uses (中高 92/87)","Trim off the excess pastry using a sharp knife...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to do something with a machine, a method, an object, etc. for a particular purpose","example":"Can I use your phone?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to take a particular amount of a liquid, substance, etc. in order to achieve or make something","example":"Have you ever used this software before?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to say or write particular words or a particular type of language","example":"How often do you use ("}]],["usually","/ˈju:ʒuəli/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “usually”.","usually [ˈju:ʒuəli] -K4 adv. 通常，经常 (高 724/526)","欧陆词典释义：usually [ˈju:ʒuəli] -K4 adv. 通常，经常 (高 724/526)","The best information about hotels usually comes from friends and acquaintances who have been there...",""],["vegetable","/ˈvedʒtəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “vegetable”.","vegetable [ˈvedʒtəbl] -K3 n. 蔬菜；植物；植物人 adj. 蔬菜的；植物的 (中高托雅 1934/2818)","欧陆词典释义：vegetable [ˈvedʒtəbl] -K3 n. 蔬菜；植物；植物人 adj. 蔬菜的；植物的 (中高托雅 1934/2818)","A good general diet should include plenty of fresh vegetable s.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a plant or part of a plant that is eaten as food. Potatoes, beans","example":"green vegetables"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who is physically alive but not capable of much mental or physical activity, for example because of an accident or illness","example":"root vegetables"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who has a boring life","example":"a salad of raw vegetables"}]],["very","/ˈveri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “very”.","very [ˈveri] -K5 adv. 非常，很；完全 adj. 恰好是，正是；甚至；十足的；特有的 n. (Very)人名；(英)维里 (中高 105/80)","欧陆词典释义：very [ˈveri] -K5 adv. 非常，很；完全 adj. 恰好是，正是；甚至；十足的；特有的 n. (Very)人名；(英)维里 (中高 105/80)","The problem and the answer are very simple...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used before adjectives, adverbs and determiners to mean ‘in a high degree’ or ‘extremely’","example":"very small"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used to emphasize a superlative adjective or before own","example":"very quickly"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"exactly the same","example":"Very few people know that."}]],["village","/ˈvɪlɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “village”.","village [ˈvɪlɪdʒ] -K4 n. 村庄；村民；（动物的）群落 (中高雅 1245/735)","欧陆词典释义：village [ˈvɪlɪdʒ] -K4 n. 村庄；村民；（动物的）群落 (中高雅 1245/735)","He lives quietly in the country in a village near Lahti.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a very small town located in a country area","example":"We visited towns and villages all over Spain."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the people who live in a village","example":"a fishing/mountain/seaside village"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"the village shop"}]],["visit","/ˈvɪzɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “visit”.","visit [ˈvɪzɪt] -K5 n. 访问；参观；逗留 vt. 访问；参观；视察 vi. 访问；暂住；闲谈 n. (Visit)人名；(老)维西；(泰)威实 时态: visited, visiting, visits (中高 905/867)","欧陆词典释义：visit [ˈvɪzɪt] -K5 n. 访问；参观；逗留 vt. 访问；参观；视察 vi. 访问；暂住；闲谈 n. (Visit)人名；(老)维西；(泰)威实 时态: visited, visiting, visits (中高 905/867)","He wanted to visit his brother in Worcester...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to go to see a person or a place for a period of time","example":"She went to visit relatives in Wales."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to go to a website on the Internet","example":"The Prime Minister is visiting Japan at the moment."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to stay somewhere for a short time","example":"You should visit your dentist at least twice a year."}]],["voice","/vɔɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “voice”.","voice [vɔɪs] -K4 n. 声音；嗓音；发言权；愿望 vt. 表达；吐露 时态: voiced, voicing, voices (中高研四六 465/487)","欧陆词典释义：voice [vɔɪs] -K4 n. 声音；嗓音；发言权；愿望 vt. 表达；吐露 时态: voiced, voicing, voices (中高研四六 465/487)","Miriam's voice was strangely calm...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the sound or sounds produced through the mouth by a person speaking or singing","example":"I could hear voices in the next room."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having a voice of the type mentioned","example":"He recognized Sarah's voice."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the right to express your opinion and influence decisions","example":"to speak in a deep/soft/loud/quiet, etc. voice"}]],["wait","/weɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wait”.","wait [weɪt] -K5 n. 等待；等候 vi. 等待；耽搁；伺候用餐 vt. 等候；推迟；延缓 n. (Wait)人名；(英)韦特；(捷)魏特 时态: waited, waiting, waits (中高 400/463)","欧陆词典释义：wait [weɪt] -K5 n. 等待；等候 vi. 等待；耽搁；伺候用餐 vt. 等候；推迟；延缓 n. (Wait)人名；(英)韦特；(捷)魏特 时态: waited, waiting, waits (中高 400/463)","I walk to a street corner and wait for the school bus...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to stay where you are or delay doing something until somebody/something comes or something happens","example":"She rang the bell and waited."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to hope or watch for something to happen, especially for a long time","example":"The President agreed to speak to the waiting journalists."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be ready for somebody to have or use","example":"Have you been waiting long?"}]],["wake","/weɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wake”.","wake [weɪk] -K3 n. 尾迹；守夜；守丧 vt. 叫醒；激发 vi. 醒来；唤醒；警觉 n. (Wake)人名；(英)韦克 时态: woke, woken, waking, wakes (中高 1764/2178)","欧陆词典释义：wake [weɪk] -K3 n. 尾迹；守夜；守丧 vt. 叫醒；激发 vi. 醒来；唤醒；警觉 n. (Wake)人名；(英)韦克 时态: woke, woken, waking, wakes (中高 1764/2178)","It was cold and dark when I woke at 6.30...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to stop sleeping; to make somebody stop sleeping","example":"What time do you usually wake up in the morning?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to make somebody remember something or feel something again","example":"I always wake early in the summer."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"Wake up! It's eight o'clock."}]],["walk","/wɔ:k/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “walk”.","walk [wɔ:k] -K5 n. 步行，走；散步 vi. 走，步行；散步 vt. 散步；走过 n. (Walk)人名；(德、葡)瓦尔克；(英)沃克 时态: walked, walking, walks (中高 358/458)","欧陆词典释义：walk [wɔ:k] -K5 n. 步行，走；散步 vi. 走，步行；散步 vt. 散步；走过 n. (Walk)人名；(德、葡)瓦尔克；(英)沃克 时态: walked, walking, walks (中高 358/458)","Rosanna and Forbes walk ed in silence for some while...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move or go somewhere by putting one foot in front of the other on the ground, but without running","example":"The baby is just learning to walk."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to spend time walking for pleasure","example":"‘How did you get here?’ ‘I walked.’"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to go somewhere with somebody on foot, especially in order to make sure they get there safely","example":"He walked slowly away from her."}]],["wall","/wɔ:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wall”.","wall [wɔ:l] -K5 n. 墙壁，围墙；似墙之物 adj. 墙壁的 vt. 用墙围住，围以墙 n. (Wall)人名；(英)沃尔；(德、芬、捷、瑞典)瓦尔 时态: walled, walling, walls (中高雅 571/577)","欧陆词典释义：wall [wɔ:l] -K5 n. 墙壁，围墙；似墙之物 adj. 墙壁的 vt. 用墙围住，围以墙 n. (Wall)人名；(英)沃尔；(德、芬、捷、瑞典)瓦尔 时态: walled, walling, walls (中高雅 571/577)","Kathryn leaned against the wall of the church...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a long vertical solid structure, made of stone, brick or concrete, that surrounds, divides or protects an area of land","example":"The fields were divided by stone walls."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"any of the vertical sides of a building or room","example":"He sat on the wall and watched the others playing."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"something that forms a barrier or stops you from making progress","example":"I'm going to paint the walls white and the ceiling pink."}]],["want","/wɒnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “want”.","want [wɒnt] -K5 n. 需要；缺乏；贫困；必需品 vt. 需要；希望；应该；缺少 vi. 需要；缺少 时态: wanted, wanting, wants (中高宝 83/94)","欧陆词典释义：want [wɒnt] -K5 n. 需要；缺乏；贫困；必需品 vt. 需要；希望；应该；缺少 vi. 需要；缺少 时态: wanted, wanting, wants (中高宝 83/94)","I want a drink...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have a desire or a wish for something","example":"Do you want some more tea?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to need something","example":"She's always wanted a large family."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to need somebody to be present in the place or for the purpose mentioned","example":"All I want is"}]],["warm","/wɔ:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “warm”.","warm [wɔ:m] -K4 n. 取暖；加热 adj. 温暖的；热情的 vt. 使…兴奋；使…温暖；使…感兴趣 vi. 同情；激动；变温暖 n. (Warm)人名；(英)沃姆；(德)瓦姆 时态: warmed, warming, warms 级别: warmer, warmest (中高雅 1356/1353)","欧陆词典释义：warm [wɔ:m] -K4 n. 取暖；加热 adj. 温暖的；热情的 vt. 使…兴奋；使…温暖；使…感兴趣 vi. 同情；激动；变温暖 n. (Warm)人名；(英)沃姆；(德)瓦姆 时态: warmed, warming, warms 级别: warmer, warmest (中高雅 1356/1353)","Wheat is grown in places which have cold winters and warm , dry summers...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"at a fairly high temperature in a way that is pleasant, rather than being hot or cold","example":"a warm breeze"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"keeping you warm","example":"Wash the blouse in warm soapy water."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"showing enthusiasm and/or affection; friendly","example":"It's nice and warm"}]],["wash","/wɒʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wash”.","wash [wɒʃ] -K3 n. 洗涤；洗的衣服；化妆水；冲积物 vt. 洗涤；洗刷；冲走；拍打 vi. 洗澡；被冲蚀 n. (Wash)人名；(英)沃什；(尼日利)瓦什 时态: washed, washing, washes (中高 2143/1853)","欧陆词典释义：wash [wɒʃ] -K3 n. 洗涤；洗的衣服；化妆水；冲积物 vt. 洗涤；洗刷；冲走；拍打 vi. 洗澡；被冲蚀 n. (Wash)人名；(英)沃什；(尼日利)瓦什 时态: washed, washing, washes (中高 2143/1853)","He got a job wash ing dishes in a pizza parlour...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something/somebody clean using water and usually soap","example":"These jeans need washing."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to make yourself clean using water and usually soap","example":"to wash the car"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be able to be washed without losing colour or being damaged","example":"to wash your hands"}]],["watch","/wɒtʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “watch”.","watch [wɒtʃ] -K3 n. 手表；监视；守护；值班人 vt. 观察；注视；看守；警戒 vi. 观看，注视；守侯，看守 时态: watched, watching, watches (中高托 323/490)","欧陆词典释义：watch [wɒtʃ] -K3 n. 手表；监视；守护；值班人 vt. 观察；注视；看守；警戒 vi. 观看，注视；守侯，看守 时态: watched, watching, watches (中高托 323/490)","The man was standing in his doorway watch ing him...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to look at somebody/something for a time, paying attention to what happens","example":"to watch television/a football game"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to take care of somebody/something for a short time","example":"He watched the house for signs of activity."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be careful about something","example":"He watched for signs of activity in the house."}]],["way","/weɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “way”.","way [weɪ] -K5 n. 方法；道路；方向；行业；习惯 adj. 途中的 adv. 大大地；远远地 n. (Way)人名；(中)见 Wei；(英、缅)韦 (中高托 84/86)","欧陆词典释义：way [weɪ] -K5 n. 方法；道路；方向；行业；习惯 adj. 途中的 adv. 大大地；远远地 n. (Way)人名；(中)见 Wei；(英、缅)韦 (中高托 84/86)","Freezing isn't a bad way of preserving food...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a method, style or manner of doing something","example":"That's not the right way"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"a particular manner or style of behaviour","example":"That's no way"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"the typical way of behaving and living of a particular group of people","example":"I'm not happy with this way of working."}]],["wear","/weə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wear”.","wear [weə(r)] -K4 n. 衣物；磨损；耐久性 v. 穿着；用旧；耗损；面露 时态: wore, worn, wearing, wears (中高托雅 518/673)","欧陆词典释义：wear [weə(r)] -K4 n. 衣物；磨损；耐久性 v. 穿着；用旧；耗损；面露 时态: wore, worn, wearing, wears (中高托雅 518/673)","He was wear ing a brown uniform...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have something on your body as a piece of clothing, a decoration, etc.","example":"She was wearing a new coat."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to have your hair in a particular style; to have a beard or moustache","example":"Do I have to wear a tie?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to have a particular expression on your face","example":"Was she wearing a seat belt?"}]],["weather","/ˈweðə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “weather”.","weather [ˈweðə(r)] -K4 n. 天气；气象；气候；处境 vt. 经受住；使风化；侵蚀；使受风吹雨打 adj. 露天的；迎风的 vi. 风化；受侵蚀；经受风雨 n. (Weather)人名；(英)韦瑟 时态: weathered, weathering, weathers (中高托雅宝 1614/1610)","欧陆词典释义：weather [ˈweðə(r)] -K4 n. 天气；气象；气候；处境 vt. 经受住；使风化；侵蚀；使受风吹雨打 adj. 露天的；迎风的 vi. 风化；受侵蚀；经受风雨 n. (Weather)人名；(英)韦瑟 时态: weathered, weathering, weathers (中高托雅宝 1614/1610)","The weather was bad...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the condition of the atmosphere at a particular place and time, such as the temperature, and if there is wind, rain, sun, etc.","example":"hot/cold/wet/fine/summer/windy, etc. weather"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a report of what the weather will be like, that is on the radio or television, or in the newspapers","example":"Did you have good weather"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"I'm not going out in this weather!"}]],["week","/wi:k/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “week”.","week [wi:k] -K5 n. 周，星期 (中高 188/180)","欧陆词典释义：week [wi:k] -K5 n. 周，星期 (中高 188/180)","I had a letter from my mother last week ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a period of seven days, either from Monday to Sunday or from Sunday to Saturday","example":"last/this/next week"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"any period of seven days","example":"It rained all week."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the five days other than Saturday and Sunday","example":"What day of the week"}]],["welcome","/ˈwelkəm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “welcome”.","welcome [ˈwelkəm] -K4 n. 欢迎 vt. 欢迎 adj. 受欢迎的 int. 欢迎 n. (Welcome)人名；(英)韦尔科姆 时态: welcomed, welcoming, welcomes (中高 1545/1647)","欧陆词典释义：welcome [ˈwelkəm] -K4 n. 欢迎 vt. 欢迎 adj. 受欢迎的 int. 欢迎 n. (Welcome)人名；(英)韦尔科姆 时态: welcomed, welcoming, welcomes (中高 1545/1647)","Several people came by to welcome me...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to say hello to somebody in a friendly way when they arrive somewhere","example":"They were at the door to welcome us."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"to be pleased that somebody has come or has joined an organization, activity, etc.","example":"a welcoming smile"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be pleased to receive or accept something","example":"It is a pleasure to welcome you to our home."}]],["well","/wel/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “well”.","well [wel] -K2 n. 井；源泉 adj. 良好的；健康的；适宜的 adv. 很好地；充分地；满意地；适当地 v. 涌出 n. (Well)人名；(英、德、荷)韦尔 时态: welled, welling, wells (中高托 100/84)","欧陆词典释义：well [wel] -K2 n. 井；源泉 adj. 良好的；健康的；适宜的 adv. 很好地；充分地；满意地；适当地 v. 涌出 n. (Well)人名；(英、德、荷)韦尔 时态: welled, welling, wells (中高托 100/84)","Sylvia shook hands. 'Well, you go get yourselves some breakfast.'...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"in a good, right or acceptable way","example":"The kids all behaved well."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"thoroughly and completely","example":"The conference was very well organized."},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"to a great extent or degree","example":"Well done!"}]],["where","/weə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “where”.","where [weə(r)] -K5 conj. 在…的地方 n. 地点 adv. 在哪里 pron. 哪里 (中高 169/131)","欧陆词典释义：where [weə(r)] -K5 conj. 在…的地方 n. 地点 adv. 在哪里 pron. 哪里 (中高 169/131)","Where did you meet him?...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"in or to what place or situation","example":"Where do you live?"},{"pos":"conjunction","definition":"used after words or phrases that refer to a place or situation to mean ‘at, in or to which’","example":"I wonder where they will take us to."},{"pos":"conjunction","definition":"the place or situation in which","example":"Where ("}]],["which","/wɪtʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “which”.","which [wɪtʃ] -K5 adj. 哪一个；哪一些 pron. 哪/那一个；哪/那一些 (中高 58/28)","欧陆词典释义：which [wɪtʃ] -K5 adj. 哪一个；哪一些 pron. 哪/那一个；哪/那一些 (中高 58/28)","Which do they want me to do? declare war or surrender?...",[{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"used in questions to ask somebody to be exact about one or more people or things from a limited number","example":"Which is better exercise—swimming or tennis?"},{"pos":"determiner","definition":"used to be exact about the thing or things that you mean","example":"Which of the applicants has got the job?"},{"pos":"determiner","definition":"used to give more information about something","example":"Which of the patients have recovered?"}]],["white","/waɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “white”.","white [waɪt] -K5 n. 白色；洁白；白种人 adj. 白色的；白种的；纯洁的 时态: whited, whiting, whites 级别: whiter, whitest (中高 301/475)","欧陆词典释义：white [waɪt] -K5 n. 白色；洁白；白种人 adj. 白色的；白种的；纯洁的 时态: whited, whiting, whites 级别: whiter, whitest (中高 301/475)","He had nice square white teeth...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having the colour of fresh snow or of milk","example":"a crisp white shirt"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"belonging to or connected with a race of people who have pale skin","example":"white bread"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"pale because of emotion or illness","example":"a set of perfect white teeth"}]],["who","/hu:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “who”.","who [hu:] -K5 pron. 谁；什么人 (中高 38/45)","欧陆词典释义：who [hu:] -K5 pron. 谁；什么人 (中高 38/45)","Who's there?...",""],["why","/waɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “why”.","why [waɪ] -K5 int. 哎呀！什么？ adv. 为什么 (中高 158/169)","欧陆词典释义：why [waɪ] -K5 int. 哎呀！什么？ adv. 为什么 (中高 158/169)","Why hasn't he brought the whisky?...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used in questions to ask the reason for or purpose of something","example":"Why were you late?"},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"used in questions to suggest that it is not necessary to do something","example":"Tell me why you did it."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to give or talk about a reason","example":"‘I would like you to go.’ ‘ Why me?"}]],["wide","/waɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wide”.","wide [waɪd] -K5 n. 大千世界 adj. 广泛的；宽的，广阔的；张大的；远离目标的 adv. 广泛地；广阔地；充分地 n. (Wide)人名；(瑞典、芬)维德 级别: wider, widest (中高雅 940/600)","欧陆词典释义：wide [waɪd] -K5 n. 大千世界 adj. 广泛的；宽的，广阔的；张大的；远离目标的 adv. 广泛地；广阔地；充分地 n. (Wide)人名；(瑞典、芬)维德 级别: wider, widest (中高雅 940/600)","All worktops should be wide enough to allow plenty of space for food preparation.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"measuring a lot from one side to the other","example":"a wide river"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"measuring a particular distance from one side to the other","example":"Sam has a wide mouth."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"including a large number or variety of different people or things; covering a large area","example":"a jacket with wide lapels"}]],["wife","/waɪf/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wife”.","wife [waɪf] -K5 n. 妻子，已婚妇女；夫人 (中高 466/531)","欧陆词典释义：wife [waɪf] -K5 n. 妻子，已婚妇女；夫人 (中高 466/531)","He married his wife Jane 37 years ago...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the woman that somebody is married to; a married woman","example":"the doctor’s wife"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"She's his second wife."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a man and woman who are married to each other","example":"an increase in the number of working wives"}]],["will","/wɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “will”.","will [wɪl] -K4 n. 意志；决心；情感；遗嘱；意图；心愿 vt. 决心要；遗赠；用意志力使 vi. 愿意；下决心 aux. 将；愿意；必须 时态: willed, willing, wills (中高 48/31)","欧陆词典释义：will [wɪl] -K4 n. 意志；决心；情感；遗嘱；意图；心愿 vt. 决心要；遗赠；用意志力使 vi. 愿意；下决心 aux. 将；愿意；必须 时态: willed, willing, wills (中高 48/31)","The Prime Minister is now 64 years old and in all probability this will be the last election that he is likely to contest...",[{"pos":"modal verb","definition":"used for talking about or predicting the future","example":"You'll be in time if you hurry."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used for showing that somebody is willing to do something","example":"How long will you be staying in Paris?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used for asking somebody to do something","example":"Fred said he'd be leaving soon."}]],["win","/wɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “win”.","win [wɪn] -K5 n. 赢；胜利 vt. 赢得；在…中获胜；劝诱 vi. 赢；获胜；成功 n. (Win)人名；(德、荷、缅)温；(英)温(女子教名Winifred的昵称) 时态: won, winning, wins (中高研四六 361/388)","欧陆词典释义：win [wɪn] -K5 n. 赢；胜利 vt. 赢得；在…中获胜；劝诱 vi. 赢；获胜；成功 n. (Win)人名；(德、荷、缅)温；(英)温(女子教名Winifred的昵称) 时态: won, winning, wins (中高研四六 361/388)","He does not have any realistic chance of win ning the election...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be the most successful in a competition, race, battle, etc.","example":"Which team won?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to get something as the result of a competition, race, election, etc.","example":"to win at cards/chess, etc."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to achieve or get something that you want, especially by your own efforts","example":"France won by six goals to two against Denmark."}]],["window","/ˈwɪndəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “window”.","window [ˈwɪndəʊ] -K4 n. 窗；窗口；窗户 (中高雅 607/517)","欧陆词典释义：window [ˈwɪndəʊ] -K4 n. 窗；窗口；窗户 (中高雅 607/517)","He stood at the window , moodily staring out...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an opening in the wall or roof of a building, car, etc., usually covered with glass, that allows light and air to come in and people to see out; the glass in a window","example":"She looked out of the window"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area within a frame on a computer screen, in which a particular program is operating or in which information of a particular type is shown","example":"to open/close the window"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small area of something that you can see through, for example to talk to somebody or read something on the other side","example":"the bedroom/car/kitchen, etc. window"}]],["winter","/ˈwɪntə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “winter”.","winter [ˈwɪntə(r)] -K3 n. 冬季；年岁；萧条期 adj. 冬天的；越冬的 vi. 过冬 n. (Winter)人名；(英、德、匈、罗、捷、西、芬、瑞典、法)温特 时态: wintered, wintering, winters (中高 1244/1300)","欧陆词典释义：winter [ˈwɪntə(r)] -K3 n. 冬季；年岁；萧条期 adj. 冬天的；越冬的 vi. 过冬 n. (Winter)人名；(英、德、匈、罗、捷、西、芬、瑞典、法)温特 时态: wintered, wintering, winters (中高 1244/1300)","In winter the nights are long and cold.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the coldest season of the year, between autumn/fall and spring","example":"a mild/severe/hard winter"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"Our house can be very cold in (the) winter"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"in the coldest part of winter","example":"They worked on the building all through the winter."}]],["wish","/wɪʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wish”.","wish [wɪʃ] -K4 n. 希望；祝福；心愿 vt. 祝愿；渴望；向…致问候语 vi. 愿望；需要 n. (Wish)人名；(英)威什 时态: wished, wishing, wishes (中高 1055/586)","欧陆词典释义：wish [wɪʃ] -K4 n. 希望；祝福；心愿 vt. 祝愿；渴望；向…致问候语 vi. 愿望；需要 n. (Wish)人名；(英)威什 时态: wished, wishing, wishes (中高 1055/586)","She was sincere and genuine in her wish to make amends for the past...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to want something to happen or to be true even though it is unlikely or impossible","example":"I wish I were taller."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to want to do something; to want something to happen","example":"I wish I was taller."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to think very hard that you want something, especially something that can only be achieved by good luck or magic","example":"I wish I hadn't eaten so much."}]],["with","/wɪð/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “with”.","with [wɪð] -K5 prep. 用；随着；支持；和…在一起 n. (With)人名；(德、芬、丹、瑞典)维特 (中高 16/16)","欧陆词典释义：with [wɪð] -K5 prep. 用；随着；支持；和…在一起 n. (With)人名；(德、芬、丹、瑞典)维特 (中高 16/16)","With her were her son and daughter-in-law...",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"in the company or presence of somebody/something","example":"She lives with her parents."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"having or carrying something","example":"I have a client with me right now."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"using something","example":"a nice steak with a bottle of red wine"}]],["woman","/ˈwʊmən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “woman”.","woman [ˈwʊmən] -K5 n. 妇女；女性；成年女子 (中高 111/130)","欧陆词典释义：woman [ˈwʊmən] -K5 n. 妇女；女性；成年女子 (中高 111/130)","a young Lithuanian woman named Dayva.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an adult female human","example":"men, women and children"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"female humans in general","example":"a 24-year-old woman"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a woman who comes from the place mentioned or whose job or interest is connected with the thing mentioned","example":"I prefer to see a woman doctor."}]],["wonder","/ˈwʌndə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wonder”.","wonder [ˈwʌndə(r)] -K4 n. 惊奇；奇迹；惊愕 adj. 奇妙的；非凡的 vi. 怀疑；想知道；惊讶 vt. 怀疑；惊奇；对…感到惊讶 n. (Wonder)人名；(英)旺德 时态: wondered, wondering, wonders (中高研四六托 790/815)","欧陆词典释义：wonder [ˈwʌndə(r)] -K4 n. 惊奇；奇迹；惊愕 adj. 奇妙的；非凡的 vi. 怀疑；想知道；惊讶 vt. 怀疑；惊奇；对…感到惊讶 n. (Wonder)人名；(英)旺德 时态: wondered, wondering, wonders (中高研四六托 790/815)","I wonder ed what that noise was...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think about something and try to decide what is true, what will happen, what you should do, etc.","example":"I wonder who she is."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used as a polite way of asking a question or asking somebody to do something","example":"I wonder why he left his job."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be very surprised by something","example":"I was just beginning to wonder where you were."}]],["wood","/wʊd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wood”.","wood [wʊd] -K4 n. 木材；木制品；树林 vt. 植林于；给…添加木柴 vi. 收集木材 n. (Wood)人名；(英、法、西、葡、阿拉伯)伍德 (中高研四六雅 1236/1414)","欧陆词典释义：wood [wʊd] -K4 n. 木材；木制品；树林 vt. 植林于；给…添加木柴 vi. 收集木材 n. (Wood)人名；(英、法、西、葡、阿拉伯)伍德 (中高研四六雅 1236/1414)","Their dishes were made of wood ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the hard material that the trunk","example":"He chopped some wood for the fire."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area of trees, smaller than a forest","example":"a plank of wood"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a heavy wooden ball used in the game of bowls","example":"All the furniture was made of wood"}]],["word","/wɜ:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “word”.","word [wɜ:d] -K5 n. [语] 单词；话语；消息；诺言；命令 vt. 用言辞表达 n. (Word)人名；(英)沃德 时态: worded, wording, words (中高 244/196)","欧陆词典释义：word [wɜ:d] -K5 n. [语] 单词；话语；消息；诺言；命令 vt. 用言辞表达 n. (Word)人名；(英)沃德 时态: worded, wording, words (中高 244/196)","The word s stood out clearly on the page...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a single unit of language which means something and can be spoken or written","example":"Do not write more than 200 words."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a thing that you say; a remark or statement","example":"Do you know the words to this song?"},{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"a promise or guarantee that you will do something or that something will happen or is true","example":"What's the Spanish word for"}]],["work","/wɜ:k/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “work”.","work [wɜ:k] -K5 n. 工作；[物] 功；产品；操作；职业；行为；事业；工厂；著作；文学、音乐或艺术作品 vt. 使工作；操作；经营；使缓慢前进 vi. 工作；运作；起作用 n. （英、埃塞）沃克（人名） 时态: worked, working, works (中高 117/125)","欧陆词典释义：work [wɜ:k] -K5 n. 工作；[物] 功；产品；操作；职业；行为；事业；工厂；著作；文学、音乐或艺术作品 vt. 使工作；操作；经营；使缓慢前进 vi. 工作；运作；起作用 n. （英、埃塞）沃克（人名） 时态: worked, working, works (中高 117/125)","Weiner work s for the US Department of Transport...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to do something that involves physical or mental effort, especially as part of a job","example":"I can't work if I'm cold."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to have a job","example":"I've been working at my assignment all day."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to make yourself/somebody work, especially very hard","example":"He is working on a new novel."}]],["world","/wɜ:ld/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “world”.","world [wɜ:ld] -K5 n. 世界；领域；世俗；全人类；物质生活 (中高雅 123/146)","欧陆词典释义：world [wɜ:ld] -K5 n. 世界；领域；世俗；全人类；物质生活 (中高雅 123/146)","It's a beautiful part of the world ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the earth, with all its countries, peoples and natural features","example":"to sail around the world"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular part of the earth; a particular group of countries or people; a particular period of history and the people of that period","example":"travelling (all over) the world"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a planet like the earth","example":"a map of the world"}]],["worry","/ˈwʌri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “worry”.","worry [ˈwʌri] -K4 n. 担心；烦恼；撕咬 vi. 担心；烦恼；撕咬 vt. 担心；发愁；折磨 时态: worried, worrying, worries (中高 970/1537)","欧陆词典释义：worry [ˈwʌri] -K4 n. 担心；烦恼；撕咬 vi. 担心；烦恼；撕咬 vt. 担心；发愁；折磨 时态: worried, worrying, worries (中高 970/1537)","Don't worry , your luggage will come on afterwards by taxi...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to keep thinking about unpleasant things that might happen or about problems that you have","example":"Don't worry"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to make somebody/yourself anxious about somebody/something","example":"Don't worry about me. I'll be all right."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to annoy or disturb somebody","example":"He's always worrying about his weight."}]],["write","/raɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “write”.","write [raɪt] -K5 vi. 写，写字；写作，作曲；写信 vt. 写，书写；写信给；著述 时态: wrote, written, writing, writes (中高 228/211)","欧陆词典释义：write [raɪt] -K5 vi. 写，写字；写作，作曲；写信 vt. 写，书写；写信给；著述 时态: wrote, written, writing, writes (中高 228/211)","If you'd like one, simply write your name and address on a postcard and send it to us...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make letters or numbers on a surface, especially using a pen or a pencil","example":"In some countries children don't start learning to read and write"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to produce something in written form so that people can read, perform or use it, etc.","example":"Please write in pen on both sides of the paper."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to put information, a message of good wishes, etc. in a letter and send it to somebody","example":"I haven't got anything to write with."}]],["wrong","/rɒŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wrong”.","wrong [rɒŋ] -K4 n. 坏事；不公正 adj. 错误的；失常的；不适当的 vt. 委屈；无理地对待；诽谤 adv. 错误地；邪恶地，不正当地 n. (Wrong)人名；(英)朗 时态: wronged, wronging, wrongs (中高 655/672)","欧陆词典释义：wrong [rɒŋ] -K4 n. 坏事；不公正 adj. 错误的；失常的；不适当的 vt. 委屈；无理地对待；诽谤 adv. 错误地；邪恶地，不正当地 n. (Wrong)人名；(英)朗 时态: wronged, wronging, wrongs (中高 655/672)","Pain is the body's way of telling us that something is wrong ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not right or correct","example":"I got all the answers wrong."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"not right about something/somebody","example":"He was driving on the wrong side of the road."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"causing problems or difficulties; not as it should be","example":"Sorry, I must have dialled the wrong number."}]],["year","/jɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “year”.","year [jɪə(r)] -K5 n. 年；年度；历年；年纪；一年的期间；某年级的学生 (中高 54/56)","欧陆词典释义：year [jɪə(r)] -K5 n. 年；年度；历年；年纪；一年的期间；某年级的学生 (中高 54/56)","The year was 1840...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the period from 1 January to 31 December, that is 365 or 366 days, divided into 12 months","example":"in the year 1865"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a period of 12 months, measured from any particular time","example":"I lost my job earlier this year."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a period of 12 months connected with a particular activity","example":"Elections take place every year."}]],["yellow","/ˈjeləʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “yellow”.","yellow [ˈjeləʊ] -K3 n. 黄色；黄种人；黄色颜料 adj. 黄色的；黄皮肤的 vt. 使变黄或发黄 vi. 变黄或发黄 时态: yellowed, yellowing, yellows 级别: yellower, yellowest (中高雅 1665/2173)","欧陆词典释义：yellow [ˈjeləʊ] -K3 n. 黄色；黄种人；黄色颜料 adj. 黄色的；黄皮肤的 vt. 使变黄或发黄 vi. 变黄或发黄 时态: yellowed, yellowing, yellows 级别: yellower, yellowest (中高雅 1665/2173)","The walls have been painted bright yellow ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having the colour of lemons or butter","example":"pale yellow flowers"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an offensive word used to describe the light brown skin of people from some E Asian countries","example":"a bright yellow waterproof jacket"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"easily frightened","example":"Her teeth were rather yellow."}]],["yes","/jes/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “yes”.","yes [jes] -K5 n. 是（表示肯定） adv. 是, 是的 (中高 258/144)","欧陆词典释义：yes [jes] -K5 n. 是（表示肯定） adv. 是, 是的 (中高 258/144)","'Are you a friend of Nick's?' — 'Yes.'...",[{"pos":"exclamation","definition":"used to answer a question and say that something is correct or true","example":"‘Is this your car?’ ‘Yes, it is.’"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to show that you agree with what has been said","example":"‘Are you coming? Yes or no?’"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to disagree with something negative that somebody has just said","example":"‘I enjoyed her latest novel.’ ‘Yes, me too.’"}]],["yesterday","/ˈjestədeɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “yesterday”.","yesterday [ˈjestədeɪ] -K5 n. 昨天；往昔 adv. 昨天 (中高 1505/513)","欧陆词典释义：yesterday [ˈjestədeɪ] -K5 n. 昨天；往昔 adv. 昨天 (中高 1505/513)","She left yesterday ...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"on the day before today","example":"They arrived yesterday."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"I can remember our wedding as if it were yesterday."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"Old English","example":"Where were you yesterday morning?"}]],["young","/jʌŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “young”.","young [jʌŋ] -K5 n. 年轻人；（动物的）崽，仔 adj. 年轻的；初期的；没有经验的 n. (Young)人名；(中)杨(广东话·威妥玛)；(柬)永；(英、葡)扬 级别: younger, youngest (中高 234/228)","欧陆词典释义：young [jʌŋ] -K5 n. 年轻人；（动物的）崽，仔 adj. 年轻的；初期的；没有经验的 n. (Young)人名；(中)杨(广东话·威妥玛)；(柬)永；(英、葡)扬 级别: younger, youngest (中高 234/228)","In Scotland, young people can marry at 16...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having lived or existed for only a short time; not fully developed","example":"young babies"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"not yet old; not as old as others","example":"a young country"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"consisting of young people or young children; with a low average age","example":"Caterpillars eat the young leaves of this plant."}]],["zero","/ˈzɪərəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “zero”.","zero [ˈzɪərəʊ] -K2 num. 零 n. 零点，零度 n. (Zero)人名；(意)泽罗 时态: zeroed, zeroing, zeroes (中高雅 4886/4296)","欧陆词典释义：zero [ˈzɪərəʊ] -K2 num. 零 n. 零点，零度 n. (Zero)人名；(意)泽罗 时态: zeroed, zeroing, zeroes (中高雅 4886/4296)","Visibility at the city's airport came down to zero , bringing air traffic to a standstill.",[{"pos":"number","definition":"0","example":"Five, four, three, two, one, zero… We have lift-off."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a temperature, pressure, etc. that is equal to zero","example":"It was ten degrees below zero last night ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the lowest possible amount or level; nothing at all","example":"The thermometer had fallen to zero."}]],["zoo","/zu:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “zoo”.","zoo [zu:] -2 n. 动物园; &lt;美俚&gt;（铁路货车的最后一节）守车; &lt;美俚&gt;核粒子园 (中高雅 6286/6119)","欧陆词典释义：zoo [zu:] -2 n. 动物园; &lt;美俚&gt;（铁路货车的最后一节）守车; &lt;美俚&gt;核粒子园 (中高雅 6286/6119)","He took his son Christopher to the zoo .",""],["address","/əˈdres/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “address”.","address [əˈdres] -K4 n. 地址；演讲；致辞；说话的技巧；称呼 vt. 演说；从事；忙于；写姓名地址；向…致辞；与…说话；提出；处理 时态: addressed, addressing, addresses (中高研四六托雅宝 1028/1522)","欧陆词典释义：address [əˈdres] -K4 n. 地址；演讲；致辞；说话的技巧；称呼 vt. 演说；从事；忙于；写姓名地址；向…致辞；与…说话；提出；处理 时态: addressed, addressing, addresses (中高研四六托雅宝 1028/1522)","The address is 2025 M Street, Northwest, Washington, DC, 20036...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"details of where somebody lives or works and where letters, etc. can be sent","example":"What's your name and address"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a series of words and symbols that tells you where you can find something using a computer, for example on the Internet","example":"I'll give you my address and phone number."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a formal speech that is made in front of an audience","example":"Is that your home address"}]],["age","/eɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “age”.","age [eɪdʒ] -K5 n. 年龄；时代；寿命，使用年限；阶段 vt. 使成熟；使变老，使上年纪 vi. 成熟；变老 n. (Age)人名；(瑞典)阿格；(日)扬 (姓)；(西、荷)阿赫 时态: aged, ageing, ages (中高托雅 386/363)","欧陆词典释义：age [eɪdʒ] -K5 n. 年龄；时代；寿命，使用年限；阶段 vt. 使成熟；使变老，使上年纪 vi. 成熟；变老 n. (Age)人名；(瑞典)阿格；(日)扬 (姓)；(西、荷)阿赫 时态: aged, ageing, ages (中高托雅 386/363)","She has a nephew who is just ten years of age ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the number of years that a person has lived or a thing has existed","example":"He left school at the age of"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular period of a person’s life","example":"She needs more friends of her own age."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular period of history","example":"children from 5–10 years of age"}]],["airport","/ˈeəpɔ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “airport”.","airport [ˈeəpɔ:t] -K4 n. 机场；航空站 (中高雅 1765/2541)","欧陆词典释义：airport [ˈeəpɔ:t] -K4 n. 机场；航空站 (中高雅 1765/2541)","Heathrow Airport, the busiest international airport in the world.",""],["alarm","/əˈlɑ:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “alarm”.","alarm [əˈlɑ:m] -K3 n. 闹钟；警报，警告器；惊慌 vt. 警告；使惊恐 时态: alarmed, alarming, alarms (高研四托雅 3693/3004)","欧陆词典释义：alarm [əˈlɑ:m] -K3 n. 闹钟；警报，警告器；惊慌 vt. 警告；使惊恐 时态: alarmed, alarming, alarms (高研四托雅 3693/3004)","The news was greeted with alarm by MPs...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"fear and anxiety that somebody feels when something dangerous or unpleasant might happen","example":"‘What have you done?’ Ellie cried in alarm"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a loud noise or a signal that warns people of danger or of a problem","example":"I felt a growing sense of alarm when he did not return that night."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a device that warns people of a particular danger","example":"The doctor said there was no cause for alarm"}]],["all","/ɔ:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “all”.","all [ɔ:l] -K5 n. 全部 adj. 全部的 adv. 全然地；越发 pron. 全部 n. (All)人名；(瑞典)阿尔；(英)奥尔 (中高雅 43/39)","欧陆词典释义：all [ɔ:l] -K5 n. 全部 adj. 全部的 adv. 全然地；越发 pron. 全部 n. (All)人名；(瑞典)阿尔；(英)奥尔 (中高雅 43/39)","the restaurant that Hugh and all his friends go to...",[{"pos":"determiner","definition":"the whole number of","example":"All horses are animals, but not all animals are horses."},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"the whole amount of","example":"Cars were coming from all directions ("},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used with singular nouns showing something has been happening for a whole period of time","example":"All the people you invited are coming."}]],["alone","/əˈləʊn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “alone”.","alone [əˈləʊn] -K4 adj. 独自的；单独的；孤独的 adv. 独自地；单独地 (中高研四托雅 1097/1297)","欧陆词典释义：alone [əˈləʊn] -K4 adj. 独自的；单独的；孤独的 adv. 独自地；单独地 (中高研四托雅 1097/1297)","There is nothing so fearful as to be alone in a combat situation...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"without any other people","example":"I don't like going out alone at night."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"without the help of other people or things","example":"He lives alone."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"lonely and unhappy or without any friends","example":"Finally the two of us were alone together"}]],["already","/ɔ:lˈredi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “already”.","already [ɔ:lˈredi] -K5 adv. 已经，早已；先前 (中高 334/255)","欧陆词典释义：already [ɔ:lˈredi] -K5 adv. 已经，早已；先前 (中高 334/255)","They had already voted for him at the first ballot...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"before now or before a particular time in the past","example":"‘Lunch?’ ‘No thanks, I've already eaten.’"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used to express surprise that something has happened so soon or so early","example":"We got there early but Mike had already left."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used to emphasize that a situation or problem exists","example":"I already did it."}]],["always","/ˈɔ:lweɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “always”.","always [ˈɔ:lweɪz] -K5 adv. 永远，一直；总是；常常 原型: always 是 alway 的复数 (中高 206/185)","欧陆词典释义：always [ˈɔ:lweɪz] -K5 adv. 永远，一直；总是；常常 原型: always 是 alway 的复数 (中高 206/185)","Whenever I get into a relationship, I always fall madly in love...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"at all times; on every occasion","example":"There's always somebody at home in the evenings."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"for a long time; since you can remember","example":"Always lock your car."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"for all future time","example":"She always arrives at 7.30."}]],["amazing","/əˈmeɪzɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “amazing”.","amazing [əˈmeɪzɪŋ] -K3 adj. 令人惊异的 v. 使吃惊（amaze的ing形式） (高托雅 2294/3667)","欧陆词典释义：amazing [əˈmeɪzɪŋ] -K3 adj. 令人惊异的 v. 使吃惊（amaze的ing形式） (高托雅 2294/3667)","It's amazing what we can remember with a little prompting...",""],["apartment","/əˈpɑ:tmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “apartment”.","apartment [əˈpɑ:tmənt] -K3 n. 公寓；房间 (高研四雅 1273/3711)","欧陆词典释义：apartment [əˈpɑ:tmənt] -K3 n. 公寓；房间 (高研四雅 1273/3711)","Christina has her own apartment , with her own car.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a set of rooms for living in, usually on one floor of a building","example":"self-catering holiday apartments"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a set of rooms used for a holiday/vacation","example":"You can visit the whole palace except for the private apartments."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a room in a house, especially a large or famous house","example":"Apartment dwellers can participate in community gardens."}]],["around","/əˈraʊnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “around”.","around [əˈraʊnd] -K5 prep. 四处；在…周围 adv. 大约；到处；在附近 (中高 264/397)","欧陆词典释义：around [əˈraʊnd] -K5 prep. 四处；在…周围 adv. 大约；到处；在附近 (中高 264/397)","She looked at the papers around her...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"approximately","example":"He arrived around five o'clock."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"on every side; surrounding somebody/something","example":"The cost would be somewhere around £1 500."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"moving in a circle","example":"I could hear laughter all around."}]],["aunt","/ɑ:nt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “aunt”.","aunt [ɑ:nt] -K4 n. 阿姨；姑妈；伯母；舅妈 (中高 4166/2569)","欧陆词典释义：aunt [ɑ:nt] -K4 n. 阿姨；姑妈；伯母；舅妈 (中高 4166/2569)","She wrote to her aunt in America...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the sister of your father or mother; the wife of your uncle","example":"Aunt Alice"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used by children, with a first name, to address a woman who is a friend of their parents","example":"My aunt lives in Canada."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"Great Aunt Emily"}]],["autumn","/ˈɔ:təm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “autumn”.","autumn [ˈɔ:təm] -K3 n. 秋天；成熟期；渐衰期，凋落期 adj. 秋天的，秋季的 n. (Autumn)人名；(英)奥特姆 (中高 5010/2252)","欧陆词典释义：autumn [ˈɔ:təm] -K3 n. 秋天；成熟期；渐衰期，凋落期 adj. 秋天的，秋季的 n. (Autumn)人名；(英)奥特姆 (中高 5010/2252)","We are always plagued by wasps in autumn .",""],["away","/əˈweɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “away”.","away [əˈweɪ] -K5 adv. 离去，离开；在远处 (中高 269/237)","欧陆词典释义：away [əˈweɪ] -K5 adv. 离去，离开；在远处 (中高 269/237)","An injured policeman was led away by colleagues...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"to or at a distance from somebody/something in space or time","example":"The beach is a mile away."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"to a different place or in a different direction","example":"Christmas is still months away."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"not present","example":"The station is a few minutes' walk away from here."}]],["bank","/bæŋk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bank”.","bank [bæŋk] -K1 n. 银行；岸；浅滩；储库 vt. 将…存入银行；倾斜转弯 vi. 堆积；倾斜转弯 n. (Bank)人名；(英、德、俄)班克；(法、匈)邦克 时态: banked, banking, banks (中高雅 663/406)","欧陆词典释义：bank [bæŋk] -K1 n. 银行；岸；浅滩；储库 vt. 将…存入银行；倾斜转弯 vi. 堆积；倾斜转弯 n. (Bank)人名；(英、德、俄)班克；(法、匈)邦克 时态: banked, banking, banks (中高雅 663/406)","Which bank offers you the service that best suits your financial needs?...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an organization that provides various financial services, for example keeping or lending money","example":"My salary is paid directly into my bank."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a supply of money or things that are used as money in some games, especially those in which gambling is involved","example":"I need to go to the bank ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an amount of something that is collected; a place where something is stored ready for use","example":"a bank loan"}]],["bathroom","/ˈbɑ:θru:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bathroom”.","bathroom [ˈbɑ:θru:m] -K3 n. 浴室；厕所；盥洗室 (中高研四雅 2404/2821)","欧陆词典释义：bathroom [ˈbɑ:θru:m] -K3 n. 浴室；厕所；盥洗室 (中高研四雅 2404/2821)","She had gone in to use the bathroom .",""],["beach","/bi:tʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “beach”.","beach [bi:tʃ] -K3 n. 海滩；湖滨 vt. 将…拖上岸 vi. 搁浅；定居 n. (Beach)人名；(英)比奇 时态: beached, beaching, beaches (中高研四雅 1937/1900)","欧陆词典释义：beach [bi:tʃ] -K3 n. 海滩；湖滨 vt. 将…拖上岸 vi. 搁浅；定居 n. (Beach)人名；(英)比奇 时态: beached, beaching, beaches (中高研四雅 1937/1900)","a beautiful sandy beach ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area of sand or small stones (called shingle","example":"tourists sunbathing on the beach"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 16th cent.","example":"a sandy/pebble/shingle beach"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"a beach bar"}]],["because","/bɪˈkɒz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “because”.","because [bɪˈkɒz] -K5 conj. 因为 (中高 89/101)","欧陆词典释义：because [bɪˈkɒz] -K5 conj. 因为 (中高 89/101)","He is called Mitch, because his name is Mitchell...",""],["bedroom","/ˈbedru:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bedroom”.","bedroom [ˈbedru:m] -K3 n. 卧室 adj. 两性关系的；城郊住宅区的 (中高雅 1869/1570)","欧陆词典释义：bedroom [ˈbedru:m] -K3 n. 卧室 adj. 两性关系的；城郊住宅区的 (中高雅 1869/1570)","the spare bedroom .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a room for sleeping in","example":"the spare bedroom"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having the number of bedrooms mentioned","example":"a hotel with 20 bedrooms"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used as a way of referring to sexual activity","example":"This is the master bedroom"}]],["believe","/bɪˈli:v/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “believe”.","believe [bɪˈli:v] -K5 vi. 信任；料想；笃信宗教 vt. 相信；认为；信任 时态: believed, believing, believes (中高 212/252)","欧陆词典释义：believe [bɪˈli:v] -K5 vi. 信任；料想；笃信宗教 vt. 相信；认为；信任 时态: believed, believing, believes (中高 212/252)","Experts believe that the coming drought will be extensive...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to feel certain that something is true or that somebody is telling you the truth","example":"I don't believe you!"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think that something is true or possible, although you are not completely certain","example":"The man claimed to be a social worker and the old woman believed him."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have the opinion that something is right or true","example":"Believe me, she's not right for you."}]],["below","/bɪˈləʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “below”.","below [bɪˈləʊ] -K4 prep. 在…下面 adv. 在下面，在较低处；在本页下面 n. (Below)人名；(英、德、芬、瑞典)贝洛 (中高托 1450/1136)","欧陆词典释义：below [bɪˈləʊ] -K4 prep. 在…下面 adv. 在下面，在较低处；在本页下面 n. (Below)人名；(英、德、芬、瑞典)贝洛 (中高托 1450/1136)","He appeared from the apartment directly below Leonard's...",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"at or to a lower level or position than somebody/something","example":"He dived below the surface of the water."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"of a lower amount or standard than somebody/something","example":"Please do not write below this line."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"of a lower rank or of less importance than somebody/something","example":"Skirts will be worn below ("}]],["beside","/bɪˈsaɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “beside”.","beside [bɪˈsaɪd] -K3 prep. 在旁边；与…相比；和…无关 (中高 1981/1623)","欧陆词典释义：beside [bɪˈsaɪd] -K3 prep. 在旁边；与…相比；和…无关 (中高 1981/1623)","On the table beside an empty plate was a pile of books...",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"next to or at the side of somebody/something","example":"He sat beside her all night."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"compared with somebody/something","example":"a mill beside a stream"},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"Old English","example":"Sit here beside me."}]],["bicycle","/ˈbaɪsɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bicycle”.","bicycle [ˈbaɪsɪkl] -K2 n. 自行车 vt. 骑自行车运送 vi. 骑脚踏车 时态: bicycled, bicycling, bicycles (中高研四雅 4366/5312)","欧陆词典释义：bicycle [ˈbaɪsɪkl] -K2 n. 自行车 vt. 骑自行车运送 vi. 骑脚踏车 时态: bicycled, bicycling, bicycles (中高研四雅 4366/5312)","I bicycle d on towards the sea.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a road vehicle with two wheels that you ride by pushing the pedals","example":"He got on his bicycle and rode off."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 19th cent.","example":"We went for a bicycle ride"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to go somewhere on a bicycle","example":"Did you come by bicycle?"}]],["birthday","/ˈbɜ:θdeɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “birthday”.","birthday [ˈbɜ:θdeɪ] -K3 n. 生日，诞辰；诞生的日子 (中高 2433/2488)","欧陆词典释义：birthday [ˈbɜ:θdeɪ] -K3 n. 生日，诞辰；诞生的日子 (中高 2433/2488)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “birthday”.",""],["bottle","/ˈbɒtl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bottle”.","bottle [ˈbɒtl] -K4 n. 瓶子；一瓶的容量 vt. 控制；把…装入瓶中 vi. （街头艺人演出后）收拢钱币 时态: bottled, bottling, bottles (中高 1740/1584)","欧陆词典释义：bottle [ˈbɒtl] -K4 n. 瓶子；一瓶的容量 vt. 控制；把…装入瓶中 vi. （街头艺人演出后）收拢钱币 时态: bottled, bottling, bottles (中高 1740/1584)","There were two empty beer bottle s on the table...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a glass or plastic container, usually round with straight sides and a narrow neck, used especially for storing liquids","example":"a wine/beer/milk bottle"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the amount contained in a bottle","example":"Put the top back on the bottle."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"alcoholic drink","example":"He drank a whole bottle of wine."}]],["breakfast","/ˈbrekfəst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “breakfast”.","breakfast [ˈbrekfəst] -K3 n. 早餐；早饭 vt. 为…供应早餐 vi. 吃早餐 时态: breakfasted, breakfasting, breakfasts (中高雅 2382/2019)","欧陆词典释义：breakfast [ˈbrekfəst] -K3 n. 早餐；早饭 vt. 为…供应早餐 vi. 吃早餐 时态: breakfasted, breakfasting, breakfasts (中高雅 2382/2019)","What's for breakfast ?",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the first meal of the day","example":"a big/hearty/light breakfast"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"a cooked breakfast"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a thing that has been done badly","example":"Do you want bacon and eggs for breakfast"}]],["bridge","/brɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bridge”.","bridge [brɪdʒ] -K4 n. 桥；桥牌；桥接器；船桥 vt. 架桥；渡过 n. (Bridge)人名；(英)布里奇 时态: bridged, bridging, bridges (中高雅 1687/1434)","欧陆词典释义：bridge [brɪdʒ] -K4 n. 桥；桥牌；桥接器；船桥 vt. 架桥；渡过 n. (Bridge)人名；(英)布里奇 时态: bridged, bridging, bridges (中高雅 1687/1434)","He walked back over the railway bridge .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a structure that is built over a road, railway/railroad, river, etc. so that people or vehicles can cross from one side to the other","example":"We crossed the bridge over the River Windrush."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a thing that provides a connection or contact between two different things","example":"The book serves as a bridge between ancient wisdom and modern science."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the part of a ship where the captain and other officers stand when they are controlling and steering the ship","example":"Cultural exchanges are a way of building bridges"}]],["business","/ˈbɪznəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “business”.","business [ˈbɪznəs] -K5 n. 商业；[贸易] 生意；[贸易] 交易；事情 (中高研四六雅 246/215)","欧陆词典释义：business [ˈbɪznəs] -K5 n. 商业；[贸易] 生意；[贸易] 交易；事情 (中高研四六雅 246/215)","young people seeking a career in business ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the activity of making, buying, selling or supplying goods or services for money","example":"business contacts/affairs/interests"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"work that is part of your job","example":"a business investment"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount of work done by a company, etc.; the rate or quality of this work","example":"It's been a pleasure to do business with"}]],["busy","/ˈbɪzi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “busy”.","busy [ˈbɪzi] -K3 adj. 忙碌的；热闹的；正被占用的 vt. 使忙于 n. (Busy)人名；(匈)布希；(法)比西 时态: busied, busying, busies 级别: busier, busiest (中高 1924/1753)","欧陆词典释义：busy [ˈbɪzi] -K3 adj. 忙碌的；热闹的；正被占用的 vt. 使忙于 n. (Busy)人名；(匈)布希；(法)比西 时态: busied, busying, busies 级别: busier, busiest (中高 1924/1753)","What is it? I'm busy ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a lot to do; perhaps not free to do something else because you are working on something","example":"Are you busy tonight?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"spending a lot of time on something","example":"I'm afraid the doctor is busy at the moment. Can he call you back?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"full of people, activity, vehicles, etc.","example":"I'll be too busy to come to the meeting."}]],["butter","/ˈbʌtə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “butter”.","butter [ˈbʌtə(r)] -K3 n. 黄油；奶油；奉承话 vt. 涂黄油于；讨好 n. (Butter)人名；(英)巴特；(德、匈)布特 时态: buttered, buttering, butters (中高研四托 2402/3403)","欧陆词典释义：butter [ˈbʌtə(r)] -K3 n. 黄油；奶油；奉承话 vt. 涂黄油于；讨好 n. (Butter)人名；(英)巴特；(德、匈)布特 时态: buttered, buttering, butters (中高研四托 2402/3403)","bread and butter ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a soft yellow food made from cream, used in cooking and for spreading on bread","example":"Fry the onions in butter."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"Do you want butter or margarine on your toast?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used to say that somebody seems to be innocent, kind, etc. when they are not really","example":"Cream the butter and icing sugar together until light and fluffy."}]],["button","/ˈbʌtn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “button”.","button [ˈbʌtn] -K3 n. 按钮；纽扣 vt. 扣住；扣紧；在…上装纽扣 vi. 扣住；装有纽扣；扣上纽扣 n. (Button)人名；(英)巴顿 时态: buttoned, buttoning, buttons (高研四六 2645/2977)","欧陆词典释义：button [ˈbʌtn] -K3 n. 按钮；纽扣 vt. 扣住；扣紧；在…上装纽扣 vi. 扣住；装有纽扣；扣上纽扣 n. (Button)人名；(英)巴顿 时态: buttoned, buttoning, buttons (高研四六 2645/2977)","a coat with brass button s.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small round piece of metal, plastic, etc. that is sewn onto a piece of clothing and used for fastening two parts together","example":"to do up/undo your buttons"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a small part of a machine that you press to make it work","example":"to button/unbutton your buttons"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a small area on a computer screen that you click on to make it do something","example":"to sew on a button"}]],["west","/west/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “west”.","west [west] -K5 n. 西；西方；西部 adj. 西方的；朝西的 adv. 在西方；向西方；自西方 n. (West)人名；(英、德、芬、瑞典)韦斯特 (中高雅 665/789)","欧陆词典释义：west [west] -K5 n. 西；西方；西部 adj. 西方的；朝西的 adv. 在西方；向西方；自西方 n. (West)人名；(英、德、芬、瑞典)韦斯特 (中高雅 665/789)","I pushed on towards Flagstaff, a hundred miles to the west...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the direction that you look towards to see the sun go down; one of the four main points of the compass","example":"Which way is west?"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"Europe, N America and Canada, contrasted with Eastern countries","example":"Rain is spreading from the west."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"the western side of the US","example":"He lives to the west of"}]],["wet","/wet/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wet”.","wet [wet] -K3 n. 雨天；湿气 adj. [气象][物] 潮湿的；有雨的 vt. 弄湿 vi. 变湿 n. (Wet)人名；(英、纳米、南非)韦特 时态: wet, wetting, wets 级别: wetter, wettest (中高 2471/2343)","欧陆词典释义：wet [wet] -K3 n. 雨天；湿气 adj. [气象][物] 潮湿的；有雨的 vt. 弄湿 vi. 变湿 n. (Wet)人名；(英、纳米、南非)韦特 时态: wet, wetting, wets 级别: wetter, wettest (中高 2471/2343)","He towelled his wet hair...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"covered with or containing liquid, especially water","example":"wet clothes"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"with rain","example":"wet grass"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"not yet dry","example":"You'll get wet"}]],["what","/wɒt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “what”.","what [wɒt] -K5 pron. 什么；多么；多少 adv. 到什么程度，在哪一方面 adj. 什么；多么；何等 int. 什么；多么 (中高 34/38)","欧陆词典释义：what [wɒt] -K5 pron. 什么；多么；多少 adv. 到什么程度，在哪一方面 adj. 什么；多么；何等 int. 什么；多么 (中高 34/38)","What do you want?...",[{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"used in questions to ask for particular information about somebody/something","example":"What is your name?"},{"pos":"determiner","definition":"the thing or things that; whatever","example":"What ("},{"pos":"determiner","definition":"used to say that you think that something is especially good, bad, etc.","example":"What time is it?"}]],["wheel","/wi:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wheel”.","wheel [wi:l] -K3 n. 车轮；方向盘；转动 vt. 转动；使变换方向；给…装轮子 vi. 旋转；突然转变方向；盘旋飞行 时态: wheeled, wheeling, wheels (中高研四六雅 1999/2175)","欧陆词典释义：wheel [wi:l] -K3 n. 车轮；方向盘；转动 vt. 转动；使变换方向；给…装轮子 vi. 旋转；突然转变方向；盘旋飞行 时态: wheeled, wheeling, wheels (中高研四六雅 1999/2175)","The car wheel s spun and slipped on some oil on the road.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"one of the round objects under a car, bicycle, bus, etc. that turns when it moves","example":"He braked suddenly, causing the front wheels to skid."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the round object used to steer a car, etc. or ship","example":"One of the boys was pushing the other along in a little box on wheels"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a car","example":"She was killed when she was crushed under the wheels of a bus."}]],["when","/wen/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “when”.","when [wen] -K5 conj. 考虑到；既然；当…时；在…时；如果 n. 时间，时候；日期；场合 adv. 什么时候，何时；（用于时间的表达方式之后）在那时；其时；当时 pron. 那时；什么时侯 (中高 57/54)","欧陆词典释义：when [wen] -K5 conj. 考虑到；既然；当…时；在…时；如果 n. 时间，时候；日期；场合 adv. 什么时候，何时；（用于时间的表达方式之后）在那时；其时；当时 pron. 那时；什么时侯 (中高 57/54)","When are you going home?...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"at what time; on what occasion","example":"When did you last see him?"},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"used after an expression of time to mean ‘at which’ or ‘on which’","example":"When can I see you?"},{"pos":"conjunction","definition":"at which time; on which occasion","example":"When ("}]],["whether","/ˈweðə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “whether”.","whether [ˈweðə(r)] -K5 conj. 是否；不论 pron. 两个中的哪一个 (中高 321/265)","欧陆词典释义：whether [ˈweðə(r)] -K5 conj. 是否；不论 pron. 两个中的哪一个 (中高 321/265)","To this day, it's unclear whether he shot himself or was murdered...",[{"pos":"conjunction","definition":"used to express a doubt or choice between two possibilities","example":"He seemed undecided whether"},{"pos":"conjunction","definition":"used to show that something is true in either of two cases","example":"It remains to be seen whether or not"},{"pos":"conjunction","definition":"Old English","example":"I asked him whether"}]],["whole","/həʊl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “whole”.","whole [həʊl] -K5 n. 整体；全部 adj. 完整的；纯粹的 (中高研四六 467/452)","欧陆词典释义：whole [həʊl] -K5 n. 整体；全部 adj. 完整的；纯粹的 (中高研四六 467/452)","He has said he will make an apology to the whole of Asia for his country's past behaviour...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"full; complete","example":"He spent the whole day writing."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to emphasize how large or important something is","example":"We drank a whole bottle each."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"not broken or damaged","example":"The whole country ("}]],["whose","/hu:z/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “whose”.","whose [hu:z] -K5 pron. 谁的（疑问代词） (中高 527/501)","欧陆词典释义：whose [hu:z] -K5 pron. 谁的（疑问代词） (中高 527/501)","I saw a man shouting at a driver whose car was blocking the street.",[{"pos":"determiner","definition":"used in questions to ask who something belongs to","example":"Whose house is that?"},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"used to say which person or thing you mean","example":"I wonder whose this is."},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"used to give more information about a person or thing","example":"He's a man whose opinion I respect."}]],["wild","/waɪld/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wild”.","wild [waɪld] -K4 n. 荒野 adj. 野生的；野蛮的；狂热的；荒凉的 adv. 疯狂地；胡乱地 n. (Wild)人名；(英)怀尔德；(法、德、葡、捷、匈)维尔德 级别: wilder, wildest (高研四六 1292/1698)","欧陆词典释义：wild [waɪld] -K4 n. 荒野 adj. 野生的；野蛮的；狂热的；荒凉的 adv. 疯狂地；胡乱地 n. (Wild)人名；(英)怀尔德；(法、德、葡、捷、匈)维尔德 级别: wilder, wildest (高研四六 1292/1698)","We saw two more wild cats creeping towards us in the darkness...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"living or growing in natural conditions; not kept in a house or on a farm","example":"wild animals/flowers"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"in its natural state; not changed by people","example":"a wild rabbit"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"lacking discipline or control","example":"wild strawberries"}]],["wind","/wɪnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wind”.","wind [wɪnd] -K4 vi. 缠绕；上发条；吹响号角 n. 风；呼吸；气味；卷绕 vt. 缠绕；上发条；使弯曲；吹号角；绕住或缠住某人 n. (Wind)人名；(英、德、瑞典)温德 时态: wound, winding, winds (中高雅 1092/1179)","欧陆词典释义：wind [wɪnd] -K4 vi. 缠绕；上发条；吹响号角 n. 风；呼吸；气味；卷绕 vt. 缠绕；上发条；使弯曲；吹号角；绕住或缠住某人 n. (Wind)人名；(英、德、瑞典)温德 时态: wound, winding, winds (中高雅 1092/1179)","There was a strong wind blowing...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"air that moves quickly as a result of natural forces","example":"strong/high winds"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"air that you swallow with food or drink; gas that is produced in your stomach or intestines","example":"gale-force winds"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"breath that you need when you do exercise or blow into a musical instrument","example":"a light wind"}]],["winner","/ˈwɪnə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “winner”.","winner [ˈwɪnə(r)] -K4 n. 胜利者 n. (Winner)人名；(英、德、瑞典)温纳 (中高四六 1916/1790)","欧陆词典释义：winner [ˈwɪnə(r)] -K4 n. 胜利者 n. (Winner)人名；(英、德、瑞典)温纳 (中高四六 1916/1790)","She will present the trophies to the award winner s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person, a team, an animal, etc. that wins something","example":"The winners of the competition will be announced next month."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing or person that is successful or likely to be successful","example":"There are no winners in a divorce ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a goal or point that causes a team or a person to win a game","example":"the Champions League winners"}]],["without","/wɪˈðaʊt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “without”.","without [wɪˈðaʊt] -K5 prep. 没有；超过；在…外面 n. 外部；外面 adv. 户外；在外面；没有或不显示某事物 (中高 218/188)","欧陆词典释义：without [wɪˈðaʊt] -K5 prep. 没有；超过；在…外面 n. 外部；外面 adv. 户外；在外面；没有或不显示某事物 (中高 218/188)","I don't like myself without a beard...",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"not having, experiencing or showing something","example":"They had gone two days without food."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"not in the company of somebody","example":"He found the place without difficulty."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"not using or taking something","example":"She spoke without much enthusiasm."}]],["wolf","/wʊlf/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wolf”.","wolf [wʊlf] -1 n. 狼；色狼；残忍贪婪之人 vt. 大吃；狼吞虎咽地吃 n. (Wolf)人名；(以、捷、芬、瑞典、德、匈、法、罗、荷、英)沃尔夫 时态: wolfed, wolfing, wolfs (中高研四六 4150/5062)","欧陆词典释义：wolf [wʊlf] -1 n. 狼；色狼；残忍贪婪之人 vt. 大吃；狼吞虎咽地吃 n. (Wolf)人名；(以、捷、芬、瑞典、德、匈、法、罗、荷、英)沃尔夫 时态: wolfed, wolfing, wolfs (中高研四六 4150/5062)","I was back in the changing room wolf ing tea and sandwiches.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large wild animal of the dog family, that lives and hunts in groups","example":"a pack of wolves"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"A lone wolf howled under the full moon."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to call for help when you do not need it, with the result that when you do need it people do not believe you","example":"Labour groups are often seen as the big bad wolf."}]],["wonderful","/ˈwʌndəfl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wonderful”.","wonderful [ˈwʌndəfl] -K4 adj. 极好的，精彩的，绝妙的；奇妙的；美妙；胜；神妙 (中高研四六 1405/1864)","欧陆词典释义：wonderful [ˈwʌndəfl] -K4 adj. 极好的，精彩的，绝妙的；奇妙的；美妙；胜；神妙 (中高研四六 1405/1864)","The cold, misty air felt wonderful on his face...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"very good, pleasant or enjoyable","example":"a wonderful surprise"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"making you feel surprise or admiration","example":"We had a wonderful time last night."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Old English","example":"You've all been absolutely wonderful"}]],["wool","/wʊl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “wool”.","wool [wʊl] -K2 n. 羊毛；毛线；绒线；毛织品；毛料衣物 n. (Wool)人名；(英)伍尔 (研四六托 5569/3791)","欧陆词典释义：wool [wʊl] -K2 n. 羊毛；毛线；绒线；毛织品；毛料衣物 n. (Wool)人名；(英)伍尔 (研四六托 5569/3791)","a wool overcoat...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the soft fine hair that covers the body of sheep, goats","example":"a ball of wool"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"long thick thread made from animal’s wool","example":"She’s knitting a jumper in pure wool."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"cloth made from animal’s wool","example":"She spun wool by hand to weave into clothing."}]],["worse","/wɜ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “worse”.","worse [wɜ:s] -K1 n. 更坏的事；更恶劣的事 adj. 更坏的；更差的；更恶劣的（bad的比较级）；（病情）更重的（ill的比较级） adv. 更糟；更坏；更恶劣地；更坏地 原型: worse 是 bad 的比较级 (高研四六 25899/6841)","欧陆词典释义：worse [wɜ:s] -K1 n. 更坏的事；更恶劣的事 adj. 更坏的；更差的；更恶劣的（bad的比较级）；（病情）更重的（ill的比较级） adv. 更糟；更坏；更恶劣地；更坏地 原型: worse 是 bad 的比较级 (高研四六 25899/6841)","For the past couple of years my life has gone from bad to worse .",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"of poorer quality or lower standard; less good or more unpleasant","example":"The rooms were awful and the food was worse."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"more serious or severe","example":"The weather got worse"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"more ill/sick or unhappy","example":"I've been to far worse"}]],["worst","/wɜ:st/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “worst”.","worst [wɜ:st] -1 n. 最坏；最坏的时候 adj. 最差的，最坏的；最不利的；效能最低的 adv. 最坏地；最不利地 n. (Worst)人名；(英、德)沃斯特 原型: worst 是 bad 的最高级 (高研四六 33505/13770)","欧陆词典释义：worst [wɜ:st] -1 n. 最坏；最坏的时候 adj. 最差的，最坏的；最不利的；效能最低的 adv. 最坏地；最不利地 n. (Worst)人名；(英、德)沃斯特 原型: worst 是 bad 的最高级 (高研四六 33505/13770)","Though mine safety has much improved, miners' families still fear the worst ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"of the poorest quality or lowest standard; worse than any other person or thing of a similar kind","example":"It was by far the worst"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"Old English","example":"What's the worst thing that could happen?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be the cause of your own problems","example":"What she said confirmed my worst fears"}]],["worth","/wɜ:θ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “worth”.","worth [wɜ:θ] -K4 n. 价值；财产 adj. 值…的 n. (Worth)人名；(英)沃思；(德)沃特 (中高 1353/975)","欧陆词典释义：worth [wɜ:θ] -K4 n. 价值；财产 adj. 值…的 n. (Worth)人名；(英)沃思；(德)沃特 (中高 1353/975)","These books might be worth £80 or £",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a value in money, etc.","example":"Our house is worth about £100 000."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to recommend the action mentioned because you think it may be useful, enjoyable, etc.","example":"How much is this painting worth?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"important, good or enjoyable enough to make somebody feel satisfied, especially when difficulty or effort is involved","example":"to be worth a bomb/packet/fortune"}]],["writer","/ˈraɪtə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “writer”.","writer [ˈraɪtə(r)] -K n. 作家；作者 (四六雅 980/1314)","欧陆词典释义：writer [ˈraɪtə(r)] -K n. 作家；作者 (四六雅 980/1314)","Turner is a writer and critic.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person whose job is writing books, stories, articles, etc.","example":"writers of poetry"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who has written a particular thing","example":"a travel/cookery, etc. writer"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who forms letters in a particular way when they are writing","example":"the writer of this letter"}]],["activity","/ækˈtɪvəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “activity”.","activity [ækˈtɪvəti] -K4 n. 活动；行动；活跃 (中高研四雅 537/412)","欧陆词典释义：activity [ækˈtɪvəti] -K4 n. 活动；行动；活跃 (中高研四雅 537/412)","an extraordinary level of activity in the government bonds market.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a situation in which something is happening or a lot of things are being done","example":"economic activity"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that you do for interest or pleasure, or in order to achieve a particular aim","example":"The streets were noisy and full of activity."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Muscles contract and relax during physical activity."}]],["adult","/ˈædʌlt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adult”.","adult [ˈædʌlt] -K4 n. 成年人 adj. 成年的；成熟的 (高研四雅 969/1236)","欧陆词典释义：adult [ˈædʌlt] -K4 n. 成年人 adj. 成年的；成熟的 (高研四雅 969/1236)","Becoming a father signified that he was now an adult ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a fully grown person who is legally responsible for their actions","example":"Children must be accompanied by an adult."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a fully grown animal","example":"Why can't you two act like civilized adults?"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"mid 16th cent.","example":"The fish return to the river as adults in order to breed."}]],["adventure","/ədˈventʃə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adventure”.","adventure [ədˈventʃə(r)] -K2 n. 冒险；冒险精神；投机活动 vt. 冒险；大胆说出 vi. 冒险 时态: adventured, adventuring, adventures (高研四托 2862/3561)","欧陆词典释义：adventure [ədˈventʃə(r)] -K2 n. 冒险；冒险精神；投机活动 vt. 冒险；大胆说出 vi. 冒险 时态: adventured, adventuring, adventures (高研四托 2862/3561)","I set off for a new adventure in the United States on the first day of the new year.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an unusual, exciting or dangerous experience, journey or series of events","example":"her adventures travelling in Africa"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"excitement and the willingness to take risks, try new ideas, etc.","example":"When you're a child, life is one big adventure."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"adventure stories"}]],["advice","/ədˈvaɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “advice”.","advice [ədˈvaɪs] -K4 n. 建议；忠告；劝告；通知 (中高研四六托雅 1641/962)","欧陆词典释义：advice [ədˈvaɪs] -K4 n. 建议；忠告；劝告；通知 (中高研四六托雅 1641/962)","Don't be afraid to ask for advice about ordering the meal...",""],["afraid","/əˈfreɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “afraid”.","afraid [əˈfreɪd] -K3 adj. 害怕的；恐怕；担心的 (中高 1400/1562)","欧陆词典释义：afraid [əˈfreɪd] -K3 adj. 害怕的；恐怕；担心的 (中高 1400/1562)","She did not seem at all afraid ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"feeling fear; frightened because you think that you might be hurt or suffer","example":"Don't be afraid."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"worried about what might happen","example":"It's all over. There's nothing to be afraid of now."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"worried or frightened that something unpleasant, dangerous, etc. will happen to a particular person or thing","example":"Are you afraid of spiders?"}]],["again","/əˈgen/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “again”.","again [əˈgen] -K5 adv. 又，此外；再一次；再说；增加 n. （英、保）阿盖恩 (中高 184/156)","欧陆词典释义：again [əˈgen] -K5 adv. 又，此外；再一次；再说；增加 n. （英、保）阿盖恩 (中高 184/156)","He kissed her again ...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"one more time; on another occasion","example":"Could you say it again, please?"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"showing that somebody/something is in the same place or state that they were in originally","example":"When will I see you again?"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"added to an amount that is already there","example":"This must never happen again."}]],["against","/əˈgenst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “against”.","against [əˈgenst] -K5 prep. 反对，违反；靠；倚；防备 adj. 不利的；对立的 (中高研四 180/155)","欧陆词典释义：against [əˈgenst] -K5 prep. 反对，违反；靠；倚；防备 adj. 不利的；对立的 (中高研四 180/155)","She leaned against him...",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"opposing or disagreeing with somebody/something","example":"the fight against terrorism"},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"not to the advantage or favour of somebody/something","example":"We're playing against the league champions next week."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"close to, touching or hitting somebody/something","example":"We were rowing against the current."}]],["ago","/əˈgəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ago”.","ago [əˈgəʊ] -K5 adj. 以前的；过去的 adv. 以前，以往 n. (Ago)人名；(英、西、意、塞、瑞典)阿戈 (中高 316/504)","欧陆词典释义：ago [əˈgəʊ] -K5 adj. 以前的；过去的 adv. 以前，以往 n. (Ago)人名；(英、西、意、塞、瑞典)阿戈 (中高 316/504)","He was killed a few days ago in a skiing accident...",""],["ahead","/əˈhed/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ahead”.","ahead [əˈhed] -K4 adj. 向前；在前的；领先 adv. 向前地；领先地；在（某人或某事物的）前面；预先；在将来，为未来 (高 1025/1504)","欧陆词典释义：ahead [əˈhed] -K4 adj. 向前；在前的；领先 adv. 向前地；领先地；在（某人或某事物的）前面；预先；在将来，为未来 (高 1025/1504)","Brett looked straight ahead ...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"further forward in space or time; in front","example":"I'll run ahead and warn them."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"earlier","example":"The road ahead was blocked."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"winning; further advanced","example":"We've got a lot of hard work ahead."}]],["album","/ˈælbəm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “album”.","album [ˈælbəm] -4 n. 相簿；唱片集；集邮簿；签名纪念册 (高研六雅 2215/2991)","欧陆词典释义：album [ˈælbəm] -4 n. 相簿；唱片集；集邮簿；签名纪念册 (高研六雅 2215/2991)","Chris likes music and has a large collection of album s and cassettes.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a book in which you keep photographs, stamps, etc.","example":"a photo album"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a collection of pieces of music released as a single item, usually on a CD or on the Internet","example":"an online album ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"the band’s latest album"}]],["America","/ә'merikә/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “America”.","America [ә'merikә] n. 美洲（包括北美和南美洲）；美国 (中高雅 -/973)","欧陆词典释义：America [ә'merikә] n. 美洲（包括北美和南美洲）；美国 (中高雅 -/973)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “America”.",""],["among","/əˈmʌŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “among”.","among [əˈmʌŋ] -K5 prep. 在…中间；在…之中 (中高 279/418)","欧陆词典释义：among [əˈmʌŋ] -K5 prep. 在…中间；在…之中 (中高 279/418)","youths in their late teens sitting among adults...",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"surrounded by somebody/something; in the middle of somebody/something","example":"a house among the trees"},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"being included or happening in groups of things or people","example":"They strolled among the crowds."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"used when you are dividing or choosing something, and three or more people or things are involved","example":"I found the letter amongst his papers."}]],["angry","/ˈæŋgri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “angry”.","angry [ˈæŋgri] -K3 adj. 生气的；愤怒的；狂暴的；（伤口等）发炎的 级别: angrier, angriest (中高雅 1705/2084)","欧陆词典释义：angry [ˈæŋgri] -K3 adj. 生气的；愤怒的；狂暴的；（伤口等）发炎的 级别: angrier, angriest (中高雅 1705/2084)","She had been very angry at the person who stole her new bike...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having strong feelings about something that you dislike very much or about an unfair situation","example":"Her behaviour really made me angry"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"red and infected","example":"Thousands of angry demonstrators filled the square."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"dark and stormy","example":"The comments provoked an angry response from union leaders."}]],["another","/əˈnʌðə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “another”.","another [əˈnʌðə(r)] -K5 prep. 另一个；另一个人 adj. 又一，另一；另外的；不同的 pron. 另一个；又一个 (中高 145/150)","欧陆词典释义：another [əˈnʌðə(r)] -K5 prep. 另一个；另一个人 adj. 又一，另一；另外的；不同的 pron. 另一个；又一个 (中高 145/150)","Mrs. Madrigal buttered another piece of toast...",[{"pos":"determiner","definition":"one more; an extra thing or person","example":"Would you like another drink?"},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"different; a different person or thing","example":"‘Finished?’ ‘No, I've got another three questions to do.’"},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"a person or thing of a very similar type","example":"We've still got another ("}]],["anything","/ˈeniθɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “anything”.","anything [ˈeniθɪŋ] -K5 pron. 任何事 (中高 331/315)","欧陆词典释义：anything [ˈeniθɪŋ] -K5 pron. 任何事 (中高 331/315)","We can't do anything ...",[{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"used instead of something","example":"Would you like anything else?"},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"any thing at all, when it does not matter which","example":"There's never anything worth watching on TV."},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"any thing of importance","example":"If you remember anything at all, please let us know."}]],["anywhere","/ˈeniweə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “anywhere”.","anywhere [ˈeniweə(r)] -K3 n. 任何地方 adv. 在任何地方；无论何处 (中高研四 1879/2157)","欧陆词典释义：anywhere [ˈeniweə(r)] -K3 n. 任何地方 adv. 在任何地方；无论何处 (中高研四 1879/2157)","I haven't got anywhere to live...",[{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"used in negative sentences and in questions instead of somewhere","example":"I don't have anywhere to stay."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used in negative sentences and in questions instead of somewhere","example":"Do you know anywhere I can buy a second-hand computer?"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"in, at or to any place, when it does not matter where","example":"I can't see it anywhere."}]],["appearance","/əˈpɪərəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “appearance”.","appearance [əˈpɪərəns] -K4 n. 外貌，外观；出现，露面 (高研四雅 1684/1435)","欧陆词典释义：appearance [əˈpɪərəns] -K4 n. 外貌，外观；出现，露面 (高研四雅 1684/1435)","It was the president's second public appearance to date...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way that somebody/something looks on the outside; what somebody/something seems to be","example":"the physical/outward/external appearance"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of somebody/something arriving, especially when it is not expected","example":"She had never been greatly concerned about her appearance."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the moment at which something begins to exist or starts to be seen or used","example":"The dog was similar in general appearance to a spaniel."}]],["April","/'eɪprəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “April”.","April ['eɪprəl] -K4 n. 四月 (中高雅 -/684)","欧陆词典释义：April ['eɪprəl] -K4 n. 四月 (中高雅 -/684)","The changes will be introduced in April ...",""],["arm","/ɑ:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “arm”.","arm [ɑ:m] -K5 n. 手臂；武器；袖子；装备；部门 vt. 武装；备战 vi. 武装起来 时态: armed, arming, arms (中高 491/491)","欧陆词典释义：arm [ɑ:m] -K5 n. 手臂；武器；袖子；装备；部门 vt. 武装；备战 vi. 武装起来 时态: armed, arming, arms (中高 491/491)","She stretched her arm s out...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"either of the two long parts that stick out from the top of the body and connect the shoulders to the hands","example":"He escaped with only a broken arm."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the part of a piece of clothing that covers the arm","example":"She threw her arms around his neck."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the part of a chair, etc. on which you rest your arms","example":"The officer grabbed him by the arm"}]],["army","/ˈɑ:mi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “army”.","army [ˈɑ:mi] -K5 n. 陆军，军队 (中高研四雅 1539/818)","欧陆词典释义：army [ˈɑ:mi] -K5 n. 陆军，军队 (中高研四雅 1539/818)","After returning from France, he joined the army ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large organized group of soldiers who are trained to fight on land","example":"The two opposing armies faced each other across the battlefield."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the part of a country’s armed forces that fights on land","example":"Her husband is in the army"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large number of people or things, especially when they are organized in some way or involved in a particular activity","example":"After leaving school, Mike went into the army"}]],["art","/ɑ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “art”.","art [ɑ:t] -K5 n. 艺术；美术；艺术品 v. 是（be的变体） adj. 艺术的；艺术品的 n. (Art)人名；(泰、柬)阿；(英)阿特 (中高研四雅 346/477)","欧陆词典释义：art [ɑ:t] -K5 n. 艺术；美术；艺术品 v. 是（be的变体） adj. 艺术的；艺术品的 n. (Art)人名；(泰、柬)阿；(英)阿特 (中高研四雅 346/477)","the first exhibition of such art in the West.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the use of the imagination to express ideas or feelings, particularly in painting, drawing or sculpture","example":"modern/contemporary/American art"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"examples of objects such as paintings, drawings or sculptures","example":"an art critic/historian/lover"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the skill of creating objects such as paintings and drawings, especially when you study it","example":"Can we call television art?"}]],["artist","/ˈɑ:tɪst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “artist”.","artist [ˈɑ:tɪst] -K4 n. 艺术家；美术家（尤指画家）；大师 (高研四 736/1218)","欧陆词典释义：artist [ˈɑ:tɪst] -K4 n. 艺术家；美术家（尤指画家）；大师 (高研四 736/1218)","the studio of a great artist ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who creates works of art, especially paintings or drawings","example":"an exhibition of work by contemporary British artists"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a professional entertainer such as a singer, a dancer or an actor","example":"a graphic artist"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 16th cent.","example":"a make-up artist"}]],["Asia","/'eɪʒə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “Asia”.","Asia ['eɪʒə] n. 亚洲 (中高雅 -/2720)","欧陆词典释义：Asia ['eɪʒə] n. 亚洲 (中高雅 -/2720)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “Asia”.",""],["August","/ɔ:ˈgʌst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “August”.","august [ɔ:ˈgʌst] -K4 n. 八月（简写为Aug） n. (August)人名；(法、葡、西、俄、罗、英、德、瑞典、挪)奥古斯特 adj. 威严的；令人敬畏的 (中高雅宝 22206/1239)","欧陆词典释义：august [ɔ:ˈgʌst] -K4 n. 八月（简写为Aug） n. (August)人名；(法、葡、西、俄、罗、英、德、瑞典、挪)奥古斯特 adj. 威严的；令人敬畏的 (中高雅宝 22206/1239)","Being so near the august person of the Empress, he was overcome with awe.",""],["Australia","/ɒ'streiljә/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “Australia”.","Australia [ɒ'streiljә] n. 澳大利亚，澳洲 (中高雅 -/1834)","欧陆词典释义：Australia [ɒ'streiljә] n. 澳大利亚，澳洲 (中高雅 -/1834)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “Australia”.",""],["average","/ˈævərɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “average”.","average [ˈævərɪdʒ] -K4 n. 平均；平均数；海损 adj. 平均的；普通的；通常的 vt. 算出…的平均数；将…平均分配；使…平衡 vi. 平均为；呈中间色 时态: averaged, averaging, averages (高研四托雅 1299/1527)","欧陆词典释义：average [ˈævərɪdʒ] -K4 n. 平均；平均数；海损 adj. 平均的；普通的；通常的 vt. 算出…的平均数；将…平均分配；使…平衡 vi. 平均为；呈中间色 时态: averaged, averaging, averages (高研四托雅 1299/1527)","Take the average of those ratios and multiply by a hundred.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"calculated by adding several amounts together, finding a total, and dividing the total by the number of amounts","example":"an average rate/cost/price"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"typical or normal","example":"Average earnings are around £20 000 per annum."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"ordinary; not special","example":"at an average speed of 100 miles per hour"}]],["bag","/bæg/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bag”.","bag [bæg] -K4 n. 袋；猎获物；（俚）一瓶啤酒 vt. 猎获；把…装入袋中；占据，私吞；使膨大 vi. 松垂 时态: bagged, bagging, bags (中高 1008/1292)","欧陆词典释义：bag [bæg] -K4 n. 袋；猎获物；（俚）一瓶啤酒 vt. 猎获；把…装入袋中；占据，私吞；使膨大 vi. 松垂 时态: bagged, bagging, bags (中高 1008/1292)","She left the hotel carrying a shopping bag .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a container made of paper or plastic, that opens at the top, used especially in shops/stores","example":"a plastic/polythene/paper bag"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a strong container made from cloth, plastic, leather, etc., usually with one or two handles, used to carry things in when shopping or travelling","example":"a laundry/mail bag"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the amount contained in a bag","example":"a black plastic rubbish/garbage bag"}]],["ball","/bɔ:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ball”.","ball [bɔ:l] -K4 n. 球；舞会 vt. 捏成球形 vi. 成团块 n. (Ball)人名；(土)巴勒；(英、西)鲍尔；(法、德、俄、罗、捷)巴尔 时态: balled, balling, balls (中高 912/1121)","欧陆词典释义：ball [bɔ:l] -K4 n. 球；舞会 vt. 捏成球形 vi. 成团块 n. (Ball)人名；(土)巴勒；(英、西)鲍尔；(法、德、俄、罗、捷)巴尔 时态: balled, balling, balls (中高 912/1121)","a golf ball .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a round object used for throwing, hitting or kicking in games and sports","example":"a golf/tennis/cricket ball"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a round object or a thing that has been formed into a round shape","example":"Bounce the ball and try and hit it over the net."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a kick, hit or throw of the ball in some sports","example":"The sun was a huge ball of fire low on the horizon."}]],["band","/bænd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “band”.","band [bænd] -K4 n. 带，环；[物] 波段；(演奏流行音乐的) 乐队 n. n.乐队；队；一群 vi. 用带绑扎；给...镶边 时态: banded, banding, bands (高研四托雅宝 1277/1145)","欧陆词典释义：band [bænd] -K4 n. 带，环；[物] 波段；(演奏流行音乐的) 乐队 n. n.乐队；队；一群 vi. 用带绑扎；给...镶边 时态: banded, banding, bands (高研四托雅宝 1277/1145)","He was a drummer in a rock band ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small group of musicians who play popular music together, often with a singer or singers","example":"a rock/jazz band"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a group of musicians who play brass","example":"She's a singer with a band."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a group of people who do something together or who have the same ideas","example":"a military band"}]],["base","/beɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “base”.","base [beɪs] -K5 n. 基础；底部；垒 adj. 卑鄙的；低劣的 vt. 以…作基础 n. (Base)人名；(日)马濑(姓) 时态: based, basing, bases 级别: baser, basest (高研四宝 536/514)","欧陆词典释义：base [beɪs] -K5 n. 基础；底部；垒 adj. 卑鄙的；低劣的 vt. 以…作基础 n. (Base)人名；(日)马濑(姓) 时态: based, basing, bases 级别: baser, basest (高研四宝 536/514)","There was a cycle path running along this side of the wall, right at its base ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the lowest part of something, especially the part or surface on which it rests or stands","example":"the base of a column/glass"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an idea, a fact, a situation, etc. from which something is developed","example":"a pain at the base of the spine"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the people, activity, etc. from which somebody/something gets most of their support, income, power, etc.","example":"The lamp has a heavy base."}]],["basketball","/ˈbɑ:skɪtbɔ:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “basketball”.","basketball [ˈbɑ:skɪtbɔ:l] -2 n. 篮球；篮球运动 (中高 1799/16051)","欧陆词典释义：basketball [ˈbɑ:skɪtbɔ:l] -2 n. 篮球；篮球运动 (中高 1799/16051)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “basketball”.",""],["battle","/ˈbætl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “battle”.","battle [ˈbætl] -K4 n. 战役；斗争 vt. 与…作战 vi. 斗争；作战 n. (Battle)人名；(英)巴特尔；(法)巴特勒；(西)巴特莱 时态: battled, battling, battles (高研四六托 1199/1330)","欧陆词典释义：battle [ˈbætl] -K4 n. 战役；斗争 vt. 与…作战 vi. 斗争；作战 n. (Battle)人名；(英)巴特尔；(法)巴特勒；(西)巴特莱 时态: battled, battling, battles (高研四六托 1199/1330)","the victory of King William III at the Battle of the Boyne.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a fight between armies, ships or planes, especially during a war; a violent fight between groups of people","example":"the battle of Waterloo"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a competition, an argument or a struggle between people or groups of people trying to win power or control","example":"to be killed in battle"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a determined effort that somebody makes to solve a difficult problem or succeed in a difficult situation","example":"a gun battle"}]],["cook","/kʊk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cook”.","cook [kʊk] -K4 n. 厨师，厨子 vt. 烹调，煮 vi. 烹调，做菜 n. (Cook)人名；(英、印)库克 时态: cooked, cooking, cooks (中高 1419/2338)","欧陆词典释义：cook [kʊk] -K4 n. 厨师，厨子 vt. 烹调，煮 vi. 烹调，做菜 n. (Cook)人名；(英、印)库克 时态: cooked, cooking, cooks (中高 1419/2338)","I have to go and cook the dinner...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to prepare food by heating it, for example by boiling, baking or frying it","example":"Where did you learn to cook?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be prepared by boiling, baking, frying, etc.","example":"What's the best way to cook trout?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be planned secretly","example":"Who's going to cook supper?"}]],["cookie","/ˈkʊki/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cookie”.","cookie [ˈkʊki] -K1 n. 饼干；小甜点 (高 3269/21236)","欧陆词典释义：cookie [ˈkʊki] -K1 n. 饼干；小甜点 (高 3269/21236)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cookie”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small flat sweet cake for one person, usually baked until crisp","example":"chocolate chip cookies"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a smart/tough person","example":"a cookie jar"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a computer file with information in it that is sent to the central server","example":"Girl Scouts went around the neighborhood selling cookies."}]],["corner","/ˈkɔ:nə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “corner”.","corner [ˈkɔ:nə(r)] -K4 n. 角落，拐角处；地区，偏僻处；困境，窘境 vt. 垄断；迫至一隅；使陷入绝境；把…难住 vi. 囤积；相交成角 n. (Corner)人名；(法)科尔内；(英)科纳 时态: cornered, cornering, corners (中高 1127/1104)","欧陆词典释义：corner [ˈkɔ:nə(r)] -K4 n. 角落，拐角处；地区，偏僻处；困境，窘境 vt. 垄断；迫至一隅；使陷入绝境；把…难住 vi. 囤积；相交成角 n. (Corner)人名；(法)科尔内；(英)科纳 时态: cornered, cornering, corners (中高 1127/1104)","He saw the corner of a magazine sticking out from under the blanket...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a part of something where two or more sides, lines or edges join","example":"the four corners of a square"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"with the number of corners mentioned; involving the number of groups mentioned","example":"Write your address in the top right-hand corner of the letter."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the place inside a room or a box where two sides join; the area around this place","example":"I hit my knee on the corner of the table."}]],["cousin","/ˈkʌzn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cousin”.","cousin [ˈkʌzn] -K4 n. 堂兄弟姊妹；表兄弟姊妹 (中高研四六 2714/3010)","欧陆词典释义：cousin [ˈkʌzn] -K4 n. 堂兄弟姊妹；表兄弟姊妹 (中高研四六 2714/3010)","My cousin Mark helped me...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a child of your aunt or uncle","example":"She's my cousin."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who is in your wider family but who is not closely related to you","example":"We're cousins."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a way of describing people from another country who are similar in some way to people in your own country","example":"He's a distant cousin of mine."}]],["cow","/kaʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cow”.","cow [kaʊ] -K3 n. 奶牛，母牛；母兽 vt. 威胁，恐吓 时态: cowed, cowing, cows (中高研四六宝 3078/2944)","欧陆词典释义：cow [kaʊ] -K3 n. 奶牛，母牛；母兽 vt. 威胁，恐吓 时态: cowed, cowing, cows (中高研四六宝 3078/2944)","He kept a few dairy cow s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large animal kept on farms to produce milk or beef","example":"cow’s milk"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the female of the elephant","example":"a herd of dairy cows ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an offensive word for a woman","example":"You stupid cow!"}]],["cup","/kʌp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cup”.","cup [kʌp] -K5 n. 杯子；奖杯；酒杯 vt. 使成杯状；为…拔火罐 时态: cupped, cupping, cups (中高雅 780/749)","欧陆词典释义：cup [kʌp] -K5 n. 杯子；奖杯；酒杯 vt. 使成杯状；为…拔火罐 时态: cupped, cupping, cups (中高雅 780/749)"," cup s and saucers.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small container shaped like a bowl, usually with a handle, used for drinking tea, coffee, etc.","example":"a teacup"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the contents of a cup","example":"a coffee cup"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a unit for measuring quantity used in cooking in the US; a metal or plastic container used to measure this quantity","example":"a cup and saucer"}]],["cut","/kʌt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cut”.","cut [kʌt] -K5 n. 伤口；切口；削减；（服装等的）式样；削球；切入 adj. 割下的；雕过的；缩减的 vt. [机] 切割；削减；缩短；刺痛 vi. [机] 切割；相交；切牌；停拍；不出席 时态: cut, cutting, cuts (中高雅 414/541)","欧陆词典释义：cut [kʌt] -K5 n. 伤口；切口；削减；（服装等的）式样；削球；切入 adj. 割下的；雕过的；缩减的 vt. [机] 切割；削减；缩短；刺痛 vi. [机] 切割；相交；切牌；停拍；不出席 时态: cut, cutting, cuts (中高雅 414/541)","Mrs. Haines stood nearby, holding scissors to cut a ribbon...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make an opening or a wound in something, especially with a sharp tool such as a knife or scissors","example":"She cut her finger on a piece of glass."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to remove something or a part of something, using a knife, etc.","example":"He cut himself ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to make or form something by removing material with a knife, etc.","example":"She had fallen and cut"}]],["daughter","/ˈdɔ:tə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “daughter”.","daughter [ˈdɔ:tə(r)] -K5 n. 女儿；[遗][农学] 子代 adj. 女儿的；子代的 (中高 634/871)","欧陆词典释义：daughter [ˈdɔ:tə(r)] -K5 n. 女儿；[遗][农学] 子代 adj. 女儿的；子代的 (中高 634/871)","Flora and her daughter Catherine.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person’s female child","example":"We have two sons and a daughter."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a woman who belongs to a particular place or country, etc.","example":"They have three grown-up daughters."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"She's the daughter of an Oxford professor."}]],["desk","/desk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “desk”.","desk [desk] -K4 n. 办公桌；服务台；编辑部；（美）讲道台；乐谱架 adj. 书桌的；桌上用的；伏案做的 (中高雅 1659/1862)","欧陆词典释义：desk [desk] -K4 n. 办公桌；服务台；编辑部；（美）讲道台；乐谱架 adj. 书桌的；桌上用的；伏案做的 (中高雅 1659/1862)","I spoke to the girl on the reception desk ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of furniture like a table, usually with drawers in it, that you sit at to read, write, work, etc.","example":"He used to be a pilot but now he has a desk job"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place where you can get information or be served at an airport, a hotel, etc.","example":"the check-in desk"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an office at a newspaper, television company, etc. that deals with a particular subject","example":"the reception desk"}]],["dinner","/ˈdɪnə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dinner”.","dinner [ˈdɪnə(r)] -K4 n. 晚餐，晚宴；宴会；正餐 n. (Dinner)人名；(法)迪内 (中高雅 1076/1422)","欧陆词典释义：dinner [ˈdɪnə(r)] -K4 n. 晚餐，晚宴；宴会；正餐 n. (Dinner)人名；(法)迪内 (中高雅 1076/1422)","She invited us to her house for dinner ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the main meal of the day, eaten either in the middle of the day or in the evening","example":"It's time for dinner."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large formal social gathering at which dinner is eaten","example":"When do you have dinner"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"What time do you serve dinner?"}]],["doctor","/ˈdɒktə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “doctor”.","doctor [ˈdɒktə(r)] -K4 vt. 修理；篡改，伪造；为…治病；授以博士学位 n. 医生；博士 vi. 就医；行医 时态: doctored, doctoring, doctors (中高雅 570/665)","欧陆词典释义：doctor [ˈdɒktə(r)] -K4 vt. 修理；篡改，伪造；为…治病；授以博士学位 n. 医生；博士 vi. 就医；行医 时态: doctored, doctoring, doctors (中高雅 570/665)","Do not discontinue the treatment without consulting your doctor ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who has been trained in medical science, whose job is to treat people who are ill/sick or injured","example":"You'd better see a doctor"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a place where a doctor sees patients","example":"Doctor Staples ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person who has received the highest university degree","example":"an appointment at the doctor’s"}]],["dollar","/ˈdɒlə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dollar”.","dollar [ˈdɒlə(r)] -K5 n. 美元 n. (Dollar)人名；(英)多拉尔 (中高 -/2340)","欧陆词典释义：dollar [ˈdɒlə(r)] -K5 n. 美元 n. (Dollar)人名；(英)多拉尔 (中高 -/2340)","She gets paid seven dollar s an hour...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the unit of money in the US, Canada, Australia and several other countries","example":"You will be paid in American dollars."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a banknote","example":"Do you have a dollar?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the value of the US dollar compared with the value of the money of other countries","example":"a dollar bill"}]],["down","/daʊn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “down”.","down [daʊn] -K2 prep. 沿着，往下 n. 软毛，绒毛；[地质] 开阔的高地 adj. 向下的 vt. 打倒，击败 adv. 向下，下去；在下面 vi. 下降；下去 n. (Down)人名；(英)唐 时态: downed, downing, downs (中高托宝 118/102)","欧陆词典释义：down [daʊn] -K2 prep. 沿着，往下 n. 软毛，绒毛；[地质] 开阔的高地 adj. 向下的 vt. 打倒，击败 adv. 向下，下去；在下面 vi. 下降；下去 n. (Down)人名；(英)唐 时态: downed, downing, downs (中高托宝 118/102)","We're going down a mountain...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"to or at a lower place or position","example":"She jumped down off the chair."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"from a standing or vertical position to a sitting or horizontal one","example":"He looked down at her."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"at a lower level or rate","example":"We watched as the sun went down."}]],["drawer","/drɔ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “drawer”.","drawer [drɔ:(r)] -K2 n. 抽屉；开票人；出票人；起草者；酒馆侍 n. n.（德）德拉韦尔（人名） (中高研四六托雅 4212/4175)","欧陆词典释义：drawer [drɔ:(r)] -K2 n. 抽屉；开票人；出票人；起草者；酒馆侍 n. n.（德）德拉韦尔（人名） (中高研四六托雅 4212/4175)","He opened a drawer in his writing-table.",""],["dress","/dres/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dress”.","dress [dres] -K4 n. 连衣裙；女装 vt. 给…穿衣 vi. 穿衣 n. (Dress)人名；(法、德、西)德雷斯 时态: dressed, dressing, dresses (中高雅 1437/1673)","欧陆词典释义：dress [dres] -K4 n. 连衣裙；女装 vt. 给…穿衣 vi. 穿衣 n. (Dress)人名；(法、德、西)德雷斯 时态: dressed, dressing, dresses (中高雅 1437/1673)","She was wearing a black dress .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of women’s clothing that is made in one piece and covers the body down to the legs, sometimes reaching to below the knees, or to the ankles","example":"a long white dress"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"clothes for either men or women","example":"a wedding dress"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"to wear casual/formal dress"}]],["driver","/ˈdraɪvə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “driver”.","driver [ˈdraɪvə(r)] -K n. 驾驶员；驱动程序；起子；传动器 n. (Driver)人名；(德)德里弗；(英)德赖弗 (中高雅 1226/1225)","欧陆词典释义：driver [ˈdraɪvə(r)] -K n. 驾驶员；驱动程序；起子；传动器 n. (Driver)人名；(德)德里弗；(英)德赖弗 (中高雅 1226/1225)","The driver got out of his van.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who drives a vehicle","example":"a bus/train/ambulance/taxi driver"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a club","example":"She climbed into the driver's seat."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"software that controls the sending of data between a computer and a piece of equipment that is attached to it, such as a printer","example":"The accident was the other driver's fault."}]],["during","/ˈdjʊərɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “during”.","during [ˈdjʊərɪŋ] -K5 prep. 在…的时候，在…的期间 n. (During)人名；(法)迪兰；(瑞典、利比)杜林 (中高 198/192)","欧陆词典释义：during [ˈdjʊərɪŋ] -K5 prep. 在…的时候，在…的期间 n. (During)人名；(法)迪兰；(瑞典、利比)杜林 (中高 198/192)","Sandstorms are common during the Saudi Arabian winter...",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"all through a period of time","example":"during the 1990s"},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"at some point in a period of time","example":"There are extra flights to Colorado during the winter."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Please remain seated during the performance."}]],["each","/i:tʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “each”.","each [i:tʃ] -K5 adj. 每；各自的 pron. 每个；各自 adv. 每个；各自 (中高 192/170)","欧陆词典释义：each [i:tʃ] -K5 adj. 每；各自的 pron. 每个；各自 adv. 每个；各自 (中高 192/170)","Each book is beautifully illustrated...",""],["east","/i:st/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “east”.","east [i:st] -K5 n. 东方；东风；东方国家 adj. 东方的；向东的；从东方来的 adv. 向东方，在东方 n. (East)人名；(英)伊斯特 (中高 733/785)","欧陆词典释义：east [i:st] -K5 n. 东方；东风；东方国家 adj. 东方的；向东的；从东方来的 adv. 向东方，在东方 n. (East)人名；(英)伊斯特 (中高 733/785)","the vast swamps which lie to the east of the River Nile...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the direction that you look towards to see the sun rise; one of the four main points of the compass","example":"Which way is east?"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the eastern part of a country, region or city","example":"A gale was blowing from the east."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"the countries of Asia, especially China, Japan and India","example":"a town to the east of"}]],["egg","/eg/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “egg”.","egg [eg] -K4 n. 蛋；卵子；家伙；鸡蛋 vt. 煽动；怂恿 n. (Egg)人名；(法、英)埃格 时态: egged, egging, eggs (中高 1376/1532)","欧陆词典释义：egg [eg] -K4 n. 蛋；卵子；家伙；鸡蛋 vt. 煽动；怂恿 n. (Egg)人名；(法、英)埃格 时态: egged, egging, eggs (中高 1376/1532)","a baby bird hatching from its egg .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small oval","example":"The female sits on the eggs until they hatch."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a bird’s egg","example":"The fish lay thousands of eggs at one time."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a cell that combines with a sperm","example":"crocodile eggs"}]],["eight","/eɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “eight”.","eight [eɪt] -5 num. 八；八个；第八 n. 八字形 adj. 八的 (中高 739/579)","欧陆词典释义：eight [eɪt] -5 num. 八；八个；第八 n. 八字形 adj. 八的 (中高 739/579)","So far eight workers have been killed.",""],["eighty","/ˈeɪti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “eighty”.","eighty [ˈeɪti] -5 num. 八十 n. 八十；八十岁；八十年代 adj. 八十的，八十个的；八十岁的 (中高研四 7486/1944)","欧陆词典释义：eighty [ˈeɪti] -5 num. 八十 n. 八十；八十岁；八十年代 adj. 八十的，八十个的；八十岁的 (中高研四 7486/1944)","Eighty horses trotted up.",[{"pos":"number","definition":"80","example":""},{"pos":"noun","definition":"numbers, years or temperatures from 80 to 89","example":""},{"pos":"noun","definition":"between the ages of 80 and 89","example":""}]],["eleven","/ɪˈlevn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “eleven”.","eleven [ɪˈlevn] -5 num. 十一；十一个 n. 十一；十一个 adj. 十一的；十一个的 (中高 4273/2299)","欧陆词典释义：eleven [ɪˈlevn] -5 num. 十一；十一个 n. 十一；十一个 adj. 十一的；十一个的 (中高 4273/2299)","the Princess and her eleven friends.",[{"pos":"number","definition":"11","example":"She was chosen for the first eleven."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a team of eleven players for football ( soccer","example":"She was chosen for the first eleven."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"at the last possible moment; just in time","example":"She was chosen for the first eleven."}]],["else","/els/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “else”.","else [els] -K5 adj. 别的；其他的 adv. 其他；否则；另外 n. (Else)人名；(英)埃尔斯；(德)埃尔泽；(芬、丹)埃尔塞 (中高 440/471)","欧陆词典释义：else [els] -K5 adj. 别的；其他的 adv. 其他；否则；另外 n. (Else)人名；(英)埃尔斯；(德)埃尔泽；(芬、丹)埃尔塞 (中高 440/471)","If I can't make a living at painting, at least I can teach someone else to paint...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"in addition to something already mentioned","example":"What else did he say?"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"different","example":"I don't want anything else, thanks."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"Old English","example":"I'm taking a few clothes and some books, not much else."}]],["empty","/ˈempti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “empty”.","empty [ˈempti] -K3 n. 空车；空的东西 adj. 空的；无意义的；无知的；徒劳的 vt. 使失去；使…成为空的 vi. 成为空的；流空 时态: emptied, emptying, empties 级别: emptier, emptiest (中高托雅 1644/1735)","欧陆词典释义：empty [ˈempti] -K3 n. 空车；空的东西 adj. 空的；无意义的；无知的；徒劳的 vt. 使失去；使…成为空的 vi. 成为空的；流空 时态: emptied, emptying, empties 级别: emptier, emptiest (中高托雅 1644/1735)","The room was bare and empty .",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"with no people or things inside","example":"an empty box/glass"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"with no meaning; not meaning what is said","example":"empty hands ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"unhappy because life does not seem to have a purpose, usually after something sad has happened","example":"an empty plate ("}]],["engine","/ˈendʒɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “engine”.","engine [ˈendʒɪn] -K4 n. 引擎，发动机；机车，火车头；工具 (高研四六雅 1569/1374)","欧陆词典释义：engine [ˈendʒɪn] -K4 n. 引擎，发动机；机车，火车头；工具 (高研四六雅 1569/1374)","He got into the driving seat and started the engine .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the part of a vehicle that produces power to make the vehicle move","example":"a diesel/petrol engine"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a vehicle that pulls a train","example":"My car had to have a new engine."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"having the type or number of engines","example":"engine trouble"}]],["English","/'iŋgliʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “English”.","English ['iŋgliʃ] n. 英语；英国人；英文；英格兰人 adj. 英国人的；英国的；英文的 vt. 把…译成英语 (中高 1782/18425)","欧陆词典释义：English ['iŋgliʃ] n. 英语；英国人；英文；英格兰人 adj. 英国人的；英国的；英文的 vt. 把…译成英语 (中高 1782/18425)","the English way of life...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the language, originally of England, now spoken in many other countries and used as a language of international communication throughout the world","example":"She speaks good English."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"English language or literature as a subject of study","example":"I need to improve my English."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the people of England (sometimes wrongly used to mean the British, including the Scots, the Welsh and the Northern Irish)","example":"world Englishes"}]],["enough","/ɪˈnʌf/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “enough”.","enough [ɪˈnʌf] -K5 n. 很多；充足 adj. 充足的 adv. 足够地，充足地 int. 够了！ (中高 374/378)","欧陆词典释义：enough [ɪˈnʌf] -K5 n. 很多；充足 adj. 充足的 adv. 足够地，充足地 int. 够了！ (中高 374/378)","They had enough cash for a one-way ticket...",[{"pos":"determiner","definition":"used before plural or uncountable nouns to mean ‘as many or as much as somebody needs or wants’","example":"Have you made enough copies?"},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"Old English","example":"Is there enough room for me?"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"as many or as much as somebody needs or wants","example":"I didn't have enough clothes to last a week."}]],["entrance","/ˈentrəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “entrance”.","entrance [ˈentrəns] -K1 n. 入口；进入 vt. 使出神，使入迷 时态: entranced, entrancing, entrances (高研四六托雅宝 2877/2465)","欧陆词典释义：entrance [ˈentrəns] -K1 n. 入口；进入 vt. 使出神，使入迷 时态: entranced, entrancing, entrances (高研四六托雅宝 2877/2465)","Beside the entrance to the church, turn right...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a door, gate, passage, etc. used for entering a room, building or place","example":"the entrance to the museum/the museum entrance"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the act of entering a room, building or place, especially in a way that attracts the attention of other people","example":"A lighthouse marks the entrance to the harbour."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the right or opportunity to enter a building or place","example":"the front/back/side entrance"}]],["eraser","/ɪˈreɪzə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “eraser”.","eraser [ɪˈreɪzə(r)] n. 橡皮；擦除器；[计] 清除器 (中高 16590/35588)","欧陆词典释义：eraser [ɪˈreɪzə(r)] n. 橡皮；擦除器；[计] 清除器 (中高 16590/35588)","a large, flat, pink India-rubber eraser .",""],["excited","/ɪkˈsaɪtɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “excited”.","excited [ɪkˈsaɪtɪd] -K2 v. 激动；唤起（excite的过去分词） adj. 兴奋的；激动的；活跃的 原型: excited 是 excite 的过去式 (3426/4106)","欧陆词典释义：excited [ɪkˈsaɪtɪd] -K2 v. 激动；唤起（excite的过去分词） adj. 兴奋的；激动的；活跃的 原型: excited 是 excite 的过去式 (3426/4106)","I'm very excited about the possibility of playing for England's first team...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"feeling or showing happiness and enthusiasm","example":"The children were excited about opening their presents."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"nervous or upset and unable to relax","example":"I'm really excited at the prospect of working abroad."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"feeling sexual desire","example":"Don't get too excited by the sight of your name in print."}]],["exercise","/ˈeksəsaɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “exercise”.","exercise [ˈeksəsaɪz] -K4 n. 运动；练习；运用；操练；礼拜；典礼 vt. 锻炼；练习；使用；使忙碌；使惊恐 vi. 运动；练习 时态: exercised, exercising, exercises (中高雅 1487/1233)","欧陆词典释义：exercise [ˈeksəsaɪz] -K4 n. 运动；练习；运用；操练；礼拜；典礼 vt. 锻炼；练习；使用；使忙碌；使惊恐 vi. 运动；练习 时态: exercised, exercising, exercises (中高雅 1487/1233)","They are merely exercising their right to free speech...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"physical or mental activity that you do to stay healthy or become stronger","example":"Swimming is good exercise."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a set of movements or activities that you do to stay healthy or develop a skill","example":"I don't get much exercise"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a set of questions in a book that tests your knowledge or practises a skill","example":"The mind needs exercise as well as the body."}]],["exit","/ˈeksɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “exit”.","exit [ˈeksɪt] -K2 n. 出口，通道；退场 vi. 退出；离去 时态: exited, exiting, exits (高研四六托 3798/4923)","欧陆词典释义：exit [ˈeksɪt] -K2 n. 出口，通道；退场 vi. 退出；离去 时态: exited, exiting, exits (高研四六托 3798/4923)","He picked up the case and walked towards the exit ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a way out of a public building or vehicle","example":"Where's the exit?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an act of leaving, especially of an actor from the stage","example":"There is a fire exit"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a place where vehicles can leave a road to join another road","example":"The emergency exit"}]],["eye","/aɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “eye”.","eye [aɪ] -K5 n. 眼睛；视力；眼光；见解，观点 vt. 注视，看 n. (Eye)人名；(德)艾厄；(英)艾 时态: eyed, eyeing, eyes (中高雅 242/219)","欧陆词典释义：eye [aɪ] -K5 n. 眼睛；视力；眼光；见解，观点 vt. 注视，看 n. (Eye)人名；(德)艾厄；(英)艾 时态: eyed, eyeing, eyes (中高雅 242/219)","I opened my eye s and looked...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"either of the two organs on the face that you see with","example":"The suspect has dark hair and green eyes."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having the type or number of eyes","example":"to close/open"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the ability to see","example":"to drop/lower"}]],["farm","/fɑ:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “farm”.","farm [fɑ:m] -K4 n. 农场；农家；畜牧场 vt. 养殖；耕种；佃出（土地） vi. 种田，务农；经营农场 时态: farmed, farming, farms (中高雅 1258/1167)","欧陆词典释义：farm [fɑ:m] -K4 n. 农场；农家；畜牧场 vt. 养殖；耕种；佃出（土地） vi. 种田，务农；经营农场 时态: farmed, farming, farms (中高雅 1258/1167)","Farms in France are much smaller than those in the United States or even Britain.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area of land, and the buildings on it, used for growing crops and/or keeping animals","example":"a 200-hectare farm"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the main house on a farm, where the farmer lives","example":"a farm worker/labourer"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a place where particular fish or animals are bred","example":"farm buildings/machinery"}]],["fast","/fɑ:st/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “fast”.","fast [fɑ:st] -K4 n. 斋戒；绝食 adj. 快速的，迅速的；紧的，稳固的 adv. 迅速地；紧紧地；彻底地 vi. 禁食，斋戒 n. (Fast)人名；(德、英、俄、芬、捷、瑞典)法斯特 时态: fasted, fasting, fasts 级别: faster, fastest (中高宝 1096/1833)","欧陆词典释义：fast [fɑ:st] -K4 n. 斋戒；绝食 adj. 快速的，迅速的；紧的，稳固的 adv. 迅速地；紧紧地；彻底地 vi. 禁食，斋戒 n. (Fast)人名；(德、英、俄、芬、捷、瑞典)法斯特 时态: fasted, fasting, fasts 级别: faster, fastest (中高宝 1096/1833)"," fast cars with flashing lights and sirens...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"moving or able to move quickly","example":"a fast car/horse"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"happening in a short time or without delay","example":"the world’s fastest runner"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"able to do something quickly","example":"the fastest rate of increase for years"}]],["fat","/fæt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “fat”.","fat [fæt] -K4 n. 脂肪，肥肉 adj. 肥的，胖的；油腻的；丰满的 vt. 养肥；在…中加入脂肪 vi. 长肥 n. (Fat)人名；(法、西、塞)法特；(东南亚国家华语)发 时态: fatted, fatting, fats 级别: fatter, fattest (中高研 1575/2848)","欧陆词典释义：fat [fæt] -K4 n. 脂肪，肥肉 adj. 肥的，胖的；油腻的；丰满的 vt. 养肥；在…中加入脂肪 vi. 长肥 n. (Fat)人名；(法、西、塞)法特；(东南亚国家华语)发 时态: fatted, fatting, fats 级别: fatter, fattest (中高研 1575/2848)","I could eat what I liked without getting fat ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having too much flesh on it and weighing too much","example":"a big fat man/woman"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"thick or wide","example":"You'll get fat"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"large in quantity; worth a lot of money","example":"He grew fatter and fatter."}]],["favourite","/ˈfeɪvərɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “favourite”.","favourite [ˈfeɪvərɪt] -K4 n. 特别喜爱的人（或物） adj. 特别受喜爱的 (中高 22274/2527)","欧陆词典释义：favourite [ˈfeɪvərɪt] -K4 n. 特别喜爱的人（或物） adj. 特别受喜爱的 (中高 22274/2527)","a bottle of his favourite champagne...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"liked more than others of the same kind","example":"It's one of my favourite movies."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"Who is your favourite writer?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a performer, politician, sports player, etc., who is popular where they were born","example":"January is my least favourite month."}]],["fifty","/ˈfɪfti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “fifty”.","fifty [ˈfɪfti] -5 n. 五十；五十个；编号为50的东西 adj. 五十的；五十个的；众多的 (中高 3038/1041)","欧陆词典释义：fifty [ˈfɪfti] -5 n. 五十；五十个；编号为50的东西 adj. 五十的；五十个的；众多的 (中高 3038/1041)","I probably look as if I'm in my fifties rather than my seventies.",[{"pos":"number","definition":"50","example":"She was born in the fifties."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"numbers, years or temperatures from 50 to 59","example":"He retired in his fifties."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"between the ages of 50 and 59","example":"She was born in the fifties."}]],["film","/fɪlm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “film”.","film [fɪlm] -K5 n. 电影；薄膜；胶卷；轻烟 vt. 在…上覆以薄膜；把…拍成电影 vi. 摄制电影；生薄膜；变得朦胧 时态: filmed, filming, films (中高雅 593/739)","欧陆词典释义：film [fɪlm] -K5 n. 电影；薄膜；胶卷；轻烟 vt. 在…上覆以薄膜；把…拍成电影 vi. 摄制电影；生薄膜；变得朦胧 时态: filmed, filming, films (中高雅 593/739)","Everything about the film was good. Good acting, good story, good fun.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a series of moving pictures recorded with sound that tells a story, shown on television or at the cinema/movie theater","example":"Let's go to the cinema— there's a good film on"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the art or business of making films/movies","example":"Let's stay in and watch a film"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"moving pictures of real events, shown for example on television","example":"a horror/documentary/feature film"}]],["final","/ˈfaɪnl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “final”.","final [ˈfaɪnl] -K5 n. 决赛；期末考试；当日报纸的末版 adj. 最终的；决定性的；不可更改的 (中高研四托雅 887/778)","欧陆词典释义：final [ˈfaɪnl] -K5 n. 决赛；期末考试；当日报纸的末版 adj. 最终的；决定性的；不可更改的 (中高研四托雅 887/778)","Astronauts will make a final attempt today to rescue a communications satellite from its useless orbit...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"being or happening at the end of a series of events, actions, statements, etc.","example":"his final act as party leader"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"being the result of a particular process","example":"The referee blew the final whistle."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"that cannot be argued with or changed","example":"The project is in its final stages."}]],["finger","/ˈfɪŋgə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “finger”.","finger [ˈfɪŋgə(r)] -K4 n. 手指；指针，指状物 vt. 伸出；用手指拨弄 vi. 用指触摸；拨弄 n. (Finger)人名；(英、德、捷)芬格；(俄)芬格尔 时态: fingered, fingering, fingers (中高研四六 1042/1109)","欧陆词典释义：finger [ˈfɪŋgə(r)] -K4 n. 手指；指针，指状物 vt. 伸出；用手指拨弄 vi. 用指触摸；拨弄 n. (Finger)人名；(英、德、捷)芬格；(俄)芬格尔 时态: fingered, fingering, fingers (中高研四六 1042/1109)","She suddenly held up a small, bony finger and pointed across the room...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"one of the four long thin parts that stick out from the hand (or five, if the thumb is included)","example":"She ran her fingers"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having the type of fingers","example":"Hold the material between finger and thumb."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the part of a glove that covers the finger","example":"He was about to speak but she raised a finger to her lips."}]],["finish","/ˈfɪnɪʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “finish”.","finish [ˈfɪnɪʃ] -K4 n. 结束；完美；回味（葡萄酒） vt. 完成；结束；用完 vi. 结束，终止；终结 时态: finished, finishing, finishes (中高托 916/842)","欧陆词典释义：finish [ˈfɪnɪʃ] -K4 n. 结束；完美；回味（葡萄酒） vt. 完成；结束；用完 vi. 结束，终止；终结 时态: finished, finishing, finishes (中高托 916/842)","As soon as he'd finish ed eating, he excused himself...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to stop doing something or making something because it is complete","example":"Haven't you finished your homework yet?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to come to an end; to bring something to an end","example":"She finished law school last year."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to eat, drink or use what remains of something","example":"I thought you'd never finish!"}]],["five","/faɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “five”.","five [faɪv] -5 num. 五，五个 n. 五，五个；五美元钞票 adj. 五的；五个的 n. (Five)人名；(挪)菲弗 (中高 299/207)","欧陆词典释义：five [faɪv] -5 num. 五，五个 n. 五，五个；五美元钞票 adj. 五的；五个的 n. (Five)人名；(挪)菲弗 (中高 299/207)","Eric Edward Bullus was born in Peterborough, the second of five children.",""],["forty","/ˈfɔ:ti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “forty”.","forty [ˈfɔ:ti] -5 n. 四十 adj. 四十的；四十个的 (中高 3734/1350)","欧陆词典释义：forty [ˈfɔ:ti] -5 n. 四十 adj. 四十的；四十个的 (中高 3734/1350)","He was a big man in his forties, smartly dressed in a suit and tie.",[{"pos":"number","definition":"40","example":""},{"pos":"noun","definition":"numbers, years or temperatures from 40 to 49","example":""},{"pos":"noun","definition":"between the ages of 40 and 49","example":""}]],["four","/fɔ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “four”.","four [fɔ:(r)] -5 num. 四；四个 adj. 四的；四个的 n. (Four)人名；(西)福尔；(法)富尔 (中高 247/184)","欧陆词典释义：four [fɔ:(r)] -5 num. 四；四个 adj. 四的；四个的 n. (Four)人名；(西)福尔；(法)富尔 (中高 247/184)","Judith is married with four children.",[{"pos":"number","definition":"4","example":"to make up a four"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of four people or things","example":"a coach and four ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a shot that scores four runs","example":"We were crawling around on all fours."}]],["Friday","/'fraidi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “Friday”.","Friday ['fraidi] -K4 n. 星期五 (中高雅 -/1621)","欧陆词典释义：Friday ['fraidi] -K4 n. 星期五 (中高雅 -/1621)","Mr Cook is intending to go to the Middle East on Friday .",""],["fun","/fʌn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “fun”.","fun [fʌn] -K4 n. 乐趣；玩笑；有趣的人或事 adj. 供娱乐用的 vi. 开玩笑 (中高 1888/2497)","欧陆词典释义：fun [fʌn] -K4 n. 乐趣；玩笑；有趣的人或事 adj. 供娱乐用的 vi. 开玩笑 (中高 1888/2497)","This year promises to be terrifically good fun ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"enjoyment; pleasure; a thing that gives enjoyment or pleasure and makes you feel happy","example":"We had a lot of fun at Sarah's party."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"behaviour or activities that are not serious but come from a sense of enjoyment","example":"Sailing is good fun"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late 17th cent.","example":"Have fun!"}]],["funny","/ˈfʌni/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “funny”.","funny [ˈfʌni] -K3 n. 滑稽人物；笑话，有趣的故事；滑稽连环漫画栏；（英）（比赛用）单人双桨小艇 adj. 有趣的，好笑的，滑稽的；（口）稀奇的，古怪的，奇异的；有病的，不舒服的；狡猾的，欺骗（性）的，可疑的，不光明 级别: funnier, funniest (中高研四 1789/1942)","欧陆词典释义：funny [ˈfʌni] -K3 n. 滑稽人物；笑话，有趣的故事；滑稽连环漫画栏；（英）（比赛用）单人双桨小艇 adj. 有趣的，好笑的，滑稽的；（口）稀奇的，古怪的，奇异的；有病的，不舒服的；狡猾的，欺骗（性）的，可疑的，不光明 级别: funnier, funniest (中高研四 1789/1942)","Wade was smart and not bad-looking, and he could be funny when he wanted to...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"making you laugh; amusing","example":"a funny story"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"difficult to explain or understand","example":"That's the funniest thing I've ever heard."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"suspicious and probably illegal or dishonest","example":"It's not funny! Someone could have been hurt."}]],["museum","/mjuˈzi:əm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “museum”.","museum [mjuˈzi:əm] -K4 n. 博物馆 (中高研四六雅 1723/1209)","欧陆词典释义：museum [mjuˈzi:əm] -K4 n. 博物馆 (中高研四六雅 1723/1209)","For months Malcolm had wanted to visit the Parisian art museum s.",""],["Monday","/'mʌndeɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “Monday”.","Monday ['mʌndeɪ] -K4 n. 星期一 (中高雅 -/1679)","欧陆词典释义：Monday ['mʌndeɪ] -K4 n. 星期一 (中高雅 -/1679)","I went back to work on Monday ...",""],["neighbour","/'neɪbə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “neighbour”.","neighbour ['neɪbə(r)] -K3 n. n. 邻居;同胞；仁慈的人 vt. 邻接 vi. 住在邻近；毗邻；友善，和睦 adj. 邻居的；邻近的 时态: neighboured, neighbouring, neighbours (中高四六 -/1847)","欧陆词典释义：neighbour ['neɪbə(r)] -K3 n. n. 邻居;同胞；仁慈的人 vt. 邻接 vi. 住在邻近；毗邻；友善，和睦 adj. 邻居的；邻近的 时态: neighboured, neighbouring, neighbours (中高四六 -/1847)","I got chatting with my neighbour in the garden.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who lives next to you or near you","example":"We've had a lot of support from all our friends and neighbours"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a country that is next to or near another country","example":"Our next-door neighbours"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person or thing that is standing or located next to another person or thing","example":"What is Britain's nearest neighbour?"}]],["newspaper","/ˈnju:zpeɪpə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “newspaper”.","newspaper [ˈnju:zpeɪpə(r)] -K4 n. 报纸 报社 旧报纸 (中高雅 1064/1164)","欧陆词典释义：newspaper [ˈnju:zpeɪpə(r)] -K4 n. 报纸 报社 旧报纸 (中高雅 1064/1164)","He was carrying a newspaper ...",""],["noise","/nɔɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “noise”.","noise [nɔɪz] -K3 n. [环境] 噪音；响声；杂音 vt. 谣传 vi. 发出声音；大声议论 n. (Noise)人名；(英)诺伊斯 时态: noised, noising, noises (中高雅 2012/1667)","欧陆词典释义：noise [nɔɪz] -K3 n. [环境] 噪音；响声；杂音 vt. 谣传 vi. 发出声音；大声议论 n. (Noise)人名；(英)诺伊斯 时态: noised, noising, noises (中高雅 2012/1667)","There was too much noise in the room and he needed peace...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a sound, especially when it is loud, unpleasant or disturbing","example":"a rattling noise"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"extra electrical or electronic signals that are not part of the signal that is being broadcast or transmitted","example":"What's that noise?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"information that is not wanted and that can make it difficult for the important or useful information to be seen clearly","example":"Don't make a noise"}]],["November","/nəʊ'vembə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “November”.","November [nəʊ'vembə(r)] -K4 n. 十一月 (中高雅 -/1059)","欧陆词典释义：November [nəʊ'vembə(r)] -K4 n. 十一月 (中高雅 -/1059)","He arrived in London in November 1939...",""],["October","/ɒk'tәubә/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “October”.","October [ɒk'tәubә] -K4 n. [天] 十月 (中高雅 -/940)","欧陆词典释义：October [ɒk'tәubә] -K4 n. [天] 十月 (中高雅 -/940)","Most seasonal hiring is done in early October ...",""],["online","/ˌɒnˈlaɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “online”.","online [ˌɒnˈlaɪn] adj. 联机的；在线的 adv. 在线地 (雅 2257/9396)","欧陆词典释义：online [ˌɒnˈlaɪn] adj. 联机的；在线的 adv. 在线地 (雅 2257/9396)","the first bank to go online .",""],["opposite","/ˈɒpəzɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “opposite”.","opposite [ˈɒpəzɪt] -K3 adj. 相反的；对面的；对立的 n. 对立面；反义词 prep. 在…的对面 adv. 在对面 (高研四六托雅 2222/2574)","欧陆词典释义：opposite [ˈɒpəzɪt] -K3 adj. 相反的；对面的；对立的 n. 对立面；反义词 prep. 在…的对面 adv. 在对面 (高研四六托雅 2222/2574)","Jennie had sat opposite her at breakfast.",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"on the other side of a particular area from somebody/something and usually facing them","example":"There's a newly married couple living opposite ("},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"on the other side of a particular area from somebody/something and usually facing them","example":"See opposite ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"facing the speaker or somebody/something that has been mentioned","example":"Answers are given on the opposite page."}]],["own","/əʊn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “own”.","own [əʊn] -K5 vt. 拥有；承认 vi. 承认 adj. 自己的；特有的 n. 自己的 n. (Own)人名；(阿拉伯)奥恩 时态: owned, owning, owns (中高 148/118)","欧陆词典释义：own [əʊn] -K5 vt. 拥有；承认 vi. 承认 adj. 自己的；特有的 n. 自己的 n. (Own)人名；(阿拉伯)奥恩 时态: owned, owning, owns (中高 148/118)","My wife decided I should have my own shop...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used to emphasize that something belongs to or is connected with somebody","example":"It was her own idea."},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"done or produced by and for yourself","example":"I saw it with my own eyes ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"Is the car your own?"}]],["package","/ˈpækɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “package”.","package [ˈpækɪdʒ] -K4 n. 包，包裹；套装软件，[计] 程序包 adj. 一揽子的 vt. 打包；将…包装 时态: packaged, packaging, packages (中高研四六托雅 1685/1336)","欧陆词典释义：package [ˈpækɪdʒ] -K4 n. 包，包裹；套装软件，[计] 程序包 adj. 一揽子的 vt. 打包；将…包装 时态: packaged, packaging, packages (中高研四六托雅 1685/1336)","I tore open the package .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a box, bag, etc. in which things are wrapped or packed; the contents of a box, etc.","example":"A large package has arrived for you."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a set of items or ideas that must be bought or accepted together","example":"Check the list of ingredients on the side of the package."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a set of related programs for a particular type of task, sold and used as a single unit","example":"a package of hamburger buns"}]],["panda","/ˈpændə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “panda”.","panda [ˈpændə] -1 n. 熊猫；猫熊 n. (Panda)人名；(印、塞)潘达 (中高研四 14691/15519)","欧陆词典释义：panda [ˈpændə] -1 n. 熊猫；猫熊 n. (Panda)人名；(印、塞)潘达 (中高研四 14691/15519)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “panda”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large black and white animal like a bear","example":""},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an Asian animal like a raccoon","example":""},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 19th cent.","example":""}]],["passport","/ˈpɑ:spɔ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “passport”.","passport [ˈpɑ:spɔ:t] -K2 n. 护照，通行证；手段 (中高雅 6239/5283)","欧陆词典释义：passport [ˈpɑ:spɔ:t] -K2 n. 护照，通行证；手段 (中高雅 6239/5283)","You should take your passport with you when changing money.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official document that identifies you as a citizen of a particular country, and that you may have to show when you enter or leave a country","example":"a valid passport"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that makes something possible or enables you to achieve something","example":"a South African passport"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"I was stopped as I went through passport control"}]],["pencil","/ˈpensl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “pencil”.","pencil [ˈpensl] -K2 n. 铅笔；笔状物 vt. 用铅笔写；用眉笔涂 vi. 成铅笔状 时态: pencilled, pencilling, pencils (中高 4410/4530)","欧陆词典释义：pencil [ˈpensl] -K2 n. 铅笔；笔状物 vt. 用铅笔写；用眉笔涂 vi. 成铅笔状 时态: pencilled, pencilling, pencils (中高 4410/4530)","I found a pencil and some blank paper in her desk...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a narrow piece of wood, or a metal or plastic case, containing a black or coloured substance, used for drawing or writing","example":"a pencil drawing"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"I'll get a pencil and paper."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to write, draw or mark something with a pencil","example":"She scribbled a note in pencil"}]],["piano","/piˈænəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “piano”.","piano [piˈænəʊ] -K2 n. 钢琴 n. (Piano)人名；(法、意、葡)皮亚诺 (中高雅宝 3299/3449)","欧陆词典释义：piano [piˈænəʊ] -K2 n. 钢琴 n. (Piano)人名；(法、意、葡)皮亚诺 (中高雅宝 3299/3449)","I taught myself how to play the piano ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"played or sung quietly","example":"to play the piano"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large musical instrument played by pressing the black and white keys on the keyboard. The sound is produced by small hammers","example":"playing jazz on the piano"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"early 19th cent.","example":"piano music"}]],["picnic","/ˈpɪknɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “picnic”.","picnic [ˈpɪknɪk] -2 n. 野餐 vi. 去野餐 时态: picnicked, picnicking, picnic (中高研四雅 5619/6512)","欧陆词典释义：picnic [ˈpɪknɪk] -2 n. 野餐 vi. 去野餐 时态: picnicked, picnicking, picnic (中高研四雅 5619/6512)","We're going on a picnic tomorrow...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an occasion when people pack a meal and take it to eat outdoors, especially in the countryside","example":"It's a nice day. Let's go for a picnic"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the meal, usually consisting of sandwiches","example":"We had a picnic"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 18th cent.","example":"Let's eat our picnic by the lake."}]],["pilot","/ˈpaɪlət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “pilot”.","pilot [ˈpaɪlət] -K3 n. 飞行员；领航员 adj. 试点的 v. 驾驶；领航；试用 n. (Pilot)人名；(意、印)皮洛特；(法)皮洛 时态: piloted, piloting, pilots (中高研四六托雅宝 1772/2085)","欧陆词典释义：pilot [ˈpaɪlət] -K3 n. 飞行员；领航员 adj. 试点的 v. 驾驶；领航；试用 n. (Pilot)人名；(意、印)皮洛特；(法)皮洛 时态: piloted, piloting, pilots (中高研四六托雅宝 1772/2085)","He spent seventeen years as an airline pilot .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who operates the controls of an aircraft, especially as a job","example":"an airline pilot"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person with special knowledge of a difficult area of water, for example, the entrance to a harbour","example":"a fighter pilot"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a single television programme that is made in order to find out whether people will like it and want to watch further programmes","example":"The accident was caused by pilot error."}]],["pizza","/ˈpi:tsə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “pizza”.","pizza [ˈpi:tsə] -2 n. 比萨饼（一种涂有乳酪核番茄酱的意大利式有馅烘饼） n. (Pizza)人名；(意)皮扎 (3918/7979)","欧陆词典释义：pizza [ˈpi:tsə] -2 n. 比萨饼（一种涂有乳酪核番茄酱的意大利式有馅烘饼） n. (Pizza)人名；(意)皮扎 (3918/7979)","the last piece of pizza ...",""],["plane","/pleɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “plane”.","plane [pleɪn] -K4 n. 飞机；平面；程度，水平 adj. 平的；平面的 vt. 刨平；用刨子刨；掠过水面 vi. 刨；乘飞机旅行；翱翔 n. (Plane)人名；(塞、瑞典、法)普拉内 时态: planed, planing, planes (中高宝 1150/2000)","欧陆词典释义：plane [pleɪn] -K4 n. 飞机；平面；程度，水平 adj. 平的；平面的 vt. 刨平；用刨子刨；掠过水面 vi. 刨；乘飞机旅行；翱翔 n. (Plane)人名；(塞、瑞典、法)普拉内 时态: planed, planing, planes (中高宝 1150/2000)","He had plenty of time to catch his plane ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a flying vehicle with wings and one or more engines","example":"She left by plane"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"any flat or level surface, or an imaginary flat surface through or joining material objects","example":"a plane crash"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a level of thought, existence or development","example":"I caught the"}]],["planet","/ˈplænɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “planet”.","planet [ˈplænɪt] -K3 n. 行星 n. (Planet)人名；(法)普拉内；(西、葡)普拉内特 (中高研四六托宝 1592/3115)","欧陆词典释义：planet [ˈplænɪt] -K3 n. 行星 n. (Planet)人名；(法)普拉内；(西、葡)普拉内特 (中高研四六托宝 1592/3115)","The picture shows six of the eight planet s in the solar system.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large round object in space that moves around a star (such as the sun) and receives light from it","example":"the planets of our solar system"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to mean ‘the world’, especially when talking about the environment","example":"the planet Earth/Venus/Mars"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"the battle to save the planet"}]],["player","/ˈpleɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “player”.","player [ˈpleɪə(r)] -K5 n. 运动员，比赛者；游戏者，做游戏的人；演奏者，表演者；演员；播放器 (高四六雅 513/732)","欧陆词典释义：player [ˈpleɪə(r)] -K5 n. 运动员，比赛者；游戏者，做游戏的人；演奏者，表演者；演员；播放器 (高四六雅 513/732)","his greatness as a player ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who takes part in a game or sport","example":"a tennis/rugby/chess, etc. player"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a company or person involved in a particular area of business or politics","example":"a game for four players"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a machine for reproducing sound or pictures that have been recorded on CDs, etc.","example":"a midfield player"}]],["pocket","/ˈpɒkɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “pocket”.","pocket [ˈpɒkɪt] -K3 n. 口袋；钱；容器 adj. 小型的，袖珍的；金钱上的 vt. 隐藏；忍受；将…放入衣袋 vi. 形成袋或囊 时态: pocketed, pocketing, pockets (中高研四六雅 1620/1786)","欧陆词典释义：pocket [ˈpɒkɪt] -K3 n. 口袋；钱；容器 adj. 小型的，袖珍的；金钱上的 vt. 隐藏；忍受；将…放入衣袋 vi. 形成袋或囊 时态: pocketed, pocketing, pockets (中高研四六雅 1620/1786)","He took his flashlight from his jacket pocket and switched it on...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small piece of material like a small bag sewn into or onto a piece of clothing so that you can carry things in it","example":"a coat pocket"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a small bag or container fastened to something so that you can put things in it, for example, in a car door or in a bag","example":"I put the note in my pocket."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used to talk about the amount of money that you have to spend","example":"Turn out your pockets"}]],["potato","/pəˈteɪtəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “potato”.","potato [pəˈteɪtəʊ] -K3 n. [作物] 土豆，[作物] 马铃薯 (中高 2253/3013)","欧陆词典释义：potato [pəˈteɪtəʊ] -K3 n. [作物] 土豆，[作物] 马铃薯 (中高 2253/3013)","a political hot potato such as abortion.",""],["program","/ˈprəʊgræm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “program”.","program [ˈprəʊgræm] -K4 n. 程序；计划；大纲 vt. 用程序指令；为…制订计划；为…安排节目 vi. 编程序；安排节目；设计电脑程式 时态: programmed, programming, programs (四六雅 194/1660)","欧陆词典释义：program [ˈprəʊgræm] -K4 n. 程序；计划；大纲 vt. 用程序指令；为…制订计划；为…安排节目 vi. 编程序；安排节目；设计电脑程式 时态: programmed, programming, programs (四六雅 194/1660)","The chances of an error occurring in a computer program increase with the size of the program .",""],["purple","/ˈpɜ:pl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “purple”.","purple [ˈpɜ:pl] -K2 n. 紫色；紫袍 adj. 紫色的；帝王的；华而不实的 vt. 使成紫色 vi. 变成紫色 时态: purpled, purpling, purples (中高研四六托 3894/5326)","欧陆词典释义：purple [ˈpɜ:pl] -K2 n. 紫色；紫袍 adj. 紫色的；帝王的；华而不实的 vt. 使成紫色 vi. 变成紫色 时态: purpled, purpling, purples (中高研四六托 3894/5326)","She wore purple and green silk.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the colour of blue and red mixed together","example":"She was dressed in purple."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having the colour of blue and red mixed together","example":"a purple flower"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"writing or a piece of writing that is too grand in style","example":"His face was purple with rage."}]],["rabbit","/ˈræbɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “rabbit”.","rabbit [ˈræbɪt] -2 n. 兔子，野兔 vt. 让…见鬼去吧 vi. 猎兔 时态: rabbited, rabbiting, rabbits (中高研四六 4373/3037)","欧陆词典释义：rabbit [ˈræbɪt] -2 n. 兔子，野兔 vt. 让…见鬼去吧 vi. 猎兔 时态: rabbited, rabbiting, rabbits (中高研四六 4373/3037)"," rabbit stew.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small animal with soft fur, long ears and a short tail. Rabbits","example":"a rabbit hutch"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"meat from a rabbit","example":"A frightened rabbit will bolt for its hole."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Rabbits breed very fast."}]],["railway","/ˈreɪlweɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “railway”.","railway [ˈreɪlweɪ] -K3 n. （英）铁路；轨道；铁道部门 vi. 乘火车旅行 (中高雅 8369/1099)","欧陆词典释义：railway [ˈreɪlweɪ] -K3 n. （英）铁路；轨道；铁道部门 vi. 乘火车旅行 (中高雅 8369/1099)","The road ran beside a railway .",""],["reach","/ri:tʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “reach”.","reach [ri:tʃ] -K5 n. 范围；延伸；河段；横风行驶 vi. 达到；延伸；伸出手；传开 vt. 达到；影响；抵达；伸出 n. (Reach)人名；(柬)列 时态: reached, reaching, reaches (中高研四六 422/404)","欧陆词典释义：reach [ri:tʃ] -K5 n. 范围；延伸；河段；横风行驶 vi. 达到；延伸；伸出手；传开 vt. 达到；影响；抵达；伸出 n. (Reach)人名；(柬)列 时态: reached, reaching, reaches (中高研四六 422/404)","He did not stop until he reach ed the door...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to arrive at the place that you have been travelling to","example":"They didn't reach the border until after dark."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to come to somebody’s attention","example":"The beach can only be reached by boat."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to increase to a particular level, speed, etc. over a period of time","example":"I hope this letter reaches you."}]],["recycle","/ˌri:ˈsaɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “recycle”.","recycle [ˌri:ˈsaɪkl] -2 n. 再生；再循环；重复利用 vt. 使再循环；使…重新利用 vi. 重复利用 时态: recycled, recycling, recycles (高研六托雅 5806/7344)","欧陆词典释义：recycle [ˌri:ˈsaɪkl] -2 n. 再生；再循环；重复利用 vt. 使再循环；使…重新利用 vi. 重复利用 时态: recycled, recycling, recycles (高研六托雅 5806/7344)","The objective would be to recycle 98 per cent of domestic waste...",""],["red","/red/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “red”.","red [red] -K5 n. 红色，红颜料；赤字 n. (Red)人名；(英、德)雷德 adj. 红色的；红肿的，充血的 级别: redder, reddest (中高 598/796)","欧陆词典释义：red [red] -K5 n. 红色，红颜料；赤字 n. (Red)人名；(英、德)雷德 adj. 红色的；红肿的，充血的 级别: redder, reddest (中高 598/796)","a bunch of red roses...",""],["relax","/rɪˈlæks/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “relax”.","relax [rɪˈlæks] -K3 vi. 放松，休息；松懈，松弛；变从容；休养 vt. 放松；使休息；使松弛；缓和；使松懈 时态: relaxed, relaxing, relaxes (中高研四六托 2861/2535)","欧陆词典释义：relax [rɪˈlæks] -K3 vi. 放松，休息；松懈，松弛；变从容；休养 vt. 放松；使休息；使松弛；缓和；使松懈 时态: relaxed, relaxing, relaxes (中高研四六托 2861/2535)","I ought to relax and stop worrying about it...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to rest while you are doing something enjoyable, especially after work or effort","example":"Just relax and enjoy the movie."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become or make somebody become calmer and less worried","example":"I'm going to spend the weekend just relaxing."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become or make something become less tight or stiff","example":"When I get home from work I like to relax with the newspaper."}]],["reply","/rɪˈplaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “reply”.","reply [rɪˈplaɪ] -K4 n. 回答；[法] 答辩 vt. 回答；答复 vi. 回答；[法] 答辩；回击 时态: replied, replying, replies (中高研四六 2219/1286)","欧陆词典释义：reply [rɪˈplaɪ] -K4 n. 回答；[法] 答辩 vt. 回答；答复 vi. 回答；[法] 答辩；回击 时态: replied, replying, replies (中高研四六 2219/1286)","'That's a nice dress,' said Michael. 'Thanks,' she replied solemnly...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to say or write something as an answer to somebody/something","example":"to reply to a question/an advertisement"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to do something as a reaction to something that somebody has said or done","example":"He never replied to any of my letters."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"She only replied with a smile."}]],["return","/rɪˈtɜ:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “return”.","return [rɪˈtɜ:n] -K5 vi. 返回；报答 adj. 报答的；回程的；返回的 vt. 返回；报答 n. 返回；归还；回球 时态: returned, returning, returns (中高雅 472/428)","欧陆词典释义：return [rɪˈtɜ:n] -K5 vi. 返回；报答 adj. 报答的；回程的；返回的 vt. 返回；报答 n. 返回；归还；回球 时态: returned, returning, returns (中高雅 472/428)","Blair will return to London tonight...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to come or go back from one place to another","example":"I waited a long time for him to return."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to bring, give, put or send something back to somebody/something","example":"She's returning to Australia tomorrow after six months in Europe."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to come back again","example":"I returned from work to find the house empty."}]],["rice","/raɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “rice”.","rice [raɪs] -K3 n. 稻；米饭 vt. 把…捣成米糊状 n. (Rice)人名；(瑞典)里瑟；(塞)里采；(英)赖斯 时态: riced, ricing, rices (中高雅 2740/4143)","欧陆词典释义：rice [raɪs] -K3 n. 稻；米饭 vt. 把…捣成米糊状 n. (Rice)人名；(瑞典)里瑟；(塞)里采；(英)赖斯 时态: riced, ricing, rices (中高雅 2740/4143)","a meal consisting of chicken, rice and vegetables...",""],["robot","/ˈrəʊbɒt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “robot”.","robot [ˈrəʊbɒt] -1 n. 机器人；遥控设备，自动机械；机械般工作的人 (中高研四六 4523/6669)","欧陆词典释义：robot [ˈrəʊbɒt] -1 n. 机器人；遥控设备，自动机械；机械般工作的人 (中高研四六 4523/6669)","very light-weight robot s that we could send to the moon for planetary exploration.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a machine that can perform a complicated series of tasks automatically","example":"These cars are built by robots."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"(especially in stories) a machine that is made to look like a human and that can do some things that a human can do","example":"Turn left at the first robot."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a traffic light","example":"These cars are built by robots."}]],["rose","/rəʊz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “rose”.","rose [rəʊz] -1 n. 玫瑰；粉红色；蔷薇（花）；粉红色的葡萄酒 adj. 玫瑰花的；玫瑰色的；粉红色的；带有玫瑰香味的 vt. 使成玫瑰色，使（面颊）发红；使有玫瑰香味 vi. 起义( rise的过去式)；升起；（数量）增加；休会 原型: rose 是 rise 的过去式和过去分词 (中高研四六 23633/2179)","欧陆词典释义：rose [rəʊz] -1 n. 玫瑰；粉红色；蔷薇（花）；粉红色的葡萄酒 adj. 玫瑰花的；玫瑰色的；粉红色的；带有玫瑰香味的 vt. 使成玫瑰色，使（面颊）发红；使有玫瑰香味 vi. 起义( rise的过去式)；升起；（数量）增加；休会 原型: rose 是 rise 的过去式和过去分词 (中高研四六 23633/2179)","She bent to pick a red rose .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a flower with a sweet smell that grows on a bush with thorns","example":"a bunch of red roses"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a pink colour","example":"a rose bush/garden"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a piece of metal or plastic with small holes in it that is attached to the end of a pipe or watering can","example":"a climbing/rambling rose"}]],["sad","/sæd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sad”.","sad [sæd] -K4 adj. 难过的；悲哀的，令人悲痛的；凄惨的，阴郁的（形容颜色） 级别: sadder, saddest (中高 2145/2373)","欧陆词典释义：sad [sæd] -K4 adj. 难过的；悲哀的，令人悲痛的；凄惨的，阴郁的（形容颜色） 级别: sadder, saddest (中高 2145/2373)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sad”.",""],["salad","/ˈsæləd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “salad”.","salad [ˈsæləd] -K2 n. 色拉；尤指莴苣 n. (Salad)人名；(阿拉伯)萨拉德 (中高研四六雅 2773/4643)","欧陆词典释义：salad [ˈsæləd] -K2 n. 色拉；尤指莴苣 n. (Salad)人名；(阿拉伯)萨拉德 (中高研四六雅 2773/4643)","a salad of tomato, onion and cucumber.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a mixture of raw vegetables such as lettuce","example":"All main courses come with salad or vegetables."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"meat, fish, cheese, etc. served with salad","example":"Is cold meat and salad OK for lunch?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"raw or cooked vegetables, etc. that are cut into small pieces, often mixed with mayonnaise","example":"a side salad"}]],["Saturday","/'sætәdi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “Saturday”.","Saturday ['sætәdi] -K4 n. 星期六 (中高雅 -/1159)","欧陆词典释义：Saturday ['sætәdi] -K4 n. 星期六 (中高雅 -/1159)","She had a call from him on Saturday morning at the studio...",""],["science","/ˈsaɪəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “science”.","science [ˈsaɪəns] -K4 n. 科学；技术；学科；理科 n. (Science)人名；(英)赛恩斯 (中高雅 889/794)","欧陆词典释义：science [ˈsaɪəns] -K4 n. 科学；技术；学科；理科 n. (Science)人名；(英)赛恩斯 (中高雅 889/794)","The best discoveries in science are very simple.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"knowledge about the structure and behaviour of the natural and physical world, based on facts that you can prove, for example by experiments","example":"new developments in science and technology"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the study of science","example":"the advance of modern science"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular branch of science","example":"the laws of science"}]],["seafood","/ˈsi:fu:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “seafood”.","seafood [ˈsi:fu:d] -1 n. 海鲜；海味；海产食品 (雅 6817/15996)","欧陆词典释义：seafood [ˈsi:fu:d] -1 n. 海鲜；海味；海产食品 (雅 6817/15996)","a seafood restaurant.",""],["season","/ˈsi:zn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “season”.","season [ˈsi:zn] -K5 n. 时期；季节；赛季 vt. 给…调味；使适应 vi. 变得成熟；变干燥 时态: seasoned, seasoning, seasons (中高托雅 506/833)","欧陆词典释义：season [ˈsi:zn] -K5 n. 时期；季节；赛季 vt. 给…调味；使适应 vi. 变得成熟；变干燥 时态: seasoned, seasoning, seasons (中高托雅 506/833)","Autumn's my favourite season .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"any of the four main periods of the year: spring, summer, autumn/fall and winter","example":"the changing seasons"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a period of the year in tropical countries when it is either very dry or it rains a lot","example":"the cricket/hunting/shooting, etc. season"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a period of time during a year when a particular activity happens or is done","example":"He scored his first goal of the season on Saturday."}]],["September","/sep'tembə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “September”.","September [sep'tembə(r)] -K4 n. 九月 (中高雅 -/964)","欧陆词典释义：September [sep'tembə(r)] -K4 n. 九月 (中高雅 -/964)","Her son, Jerome, was born in September ...",""],["several","/ˈsevrəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “several”.","several [ˈsevrəl] -K5 adj. 几个的；各自的 pron. 几个；数个 (中高雅 310/389)","欧陆词典释义：several [ˈsevrəl] -K5 adj. 几个的；各自的 pron. 几个；数个 (中高雅 310/389)","I had lived two doors away from this family for several years...",[{"pos":"determiner","definition":"more than two but not very many","example":"Several letters arrived this morning."},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"He's written several books about India."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"separate","example":"Several more people than usual came to the meeting."}]],["shadow","/ˈʃædəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “shadow”.","shadow [ˈʃædəʊ] -K3 n. 阴影；影子；幽灵；庇护；隐蔽处 adj. 影子内阁的 vt. 遮蔽；使朦胧；尾随；预示 vi. 渐变；变阴暗 时态: shadowed, shadowing, shadows (高研四六 1668/2006)","欧陆词典释义：shadow [ˈʃædəʊ] -K3 n. 阴影；影子；幽灵；庇护；隐蔽处 adj. 影子内阁的 vt. 遮蔽；使朦胧；尾随；预示 vi. 渐变；变阴暗 时态: shadowed, shadowing, shadows (高研四六 1668/2006)","An oak tree cast its shadow over a tiny round pool...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the dark shape that somebody/something’s form makes on a surface, for example on the ground, when they are between the light and the surface","example":"The children were having fun, chasing each other's shadows."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"darkness","example":"The ship's sail cast a shadow"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a very small amount of something","example":"The shadows lengthened as the sun went down."}]],["shoulder","/ˈʃəʊldə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “shoulder”.","shoulder [ˈʃəʊldə(r)] -K4 n. 肩，肩膀；肩部 vi. 用肩推挤，用肩顶 vt. 肩负，承担 时态: shouldered, shouldering, shoulders (中高研四六宝 986/1149)","欧陆词典释义：shoulder [ˈʃəʊldə(r)] -K4 n. 肩，肩膀；肩部 vi. 用肩推挤，用肩顶 vt. 肩负，承担 时态: shouldered, shouldering, shoulders (中高研四六宝 986/1149)","She led him to an armchair, with her arm round his shoulder ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"either of the two parts of the body between the top of each arm and the neck","example":"He slung the bag over his shoulder."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having the type of shoulders","example":"She tapped him on the shoulder."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the part of a piece of clothing that covers the shoulder","example":"He looked back over his shoulder."}]],["shower","/ˈʃaʊə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “shower”.","shower [ˈʃaʊə(r)] -K2 n. 淋浴；（倾泻般出现的）一阵，一大批；阵雨 vt. 大量地给予；把……弄湿 vi. 淋浴；下阵雨 时态: showered, showering, showers (中高研四六托雅 3204/3712)","欧陆词典释义：shower [ˈʃaʊə(r)] -K2 n. 淋浴；（倾泻般出现的）一阵，一大批；阵雨 vt. 大量地给予；把……弄湿 vi. 淋浴；下阵雨 时态: showered, showering, showers (中高研四六托雅 3204/3712)","She heard him turn on the shower .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of equipment producing a spray of water that you stand under to wash yourself; the small room or part of a room that contains a shower","example":"a hotel room with bath and shower"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the act of washing yourself with a shower","example":"He's in the shower"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a short period of rain or snow","example":"a shower cubicle"}]],["singer","/ˈsɪŋə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “singer”.","singer [ˈsɪŋə(r)] -K3 n. 歌手，歌唱家 n. (Singer)人名；(英、德、瑞典、塞、罗、捷、葡、土)辛格；(法)桑热 (高四六 2823/3552)","欧陆词典释义：singer [ˈsɪŋə(r)] -K3 n. 歌手，歌唱家 n. (Singer)人名；(英、德、瑞典、塞、罗、捷、葡、土)辛格；(法)桑热 (高四六 2823/3552)","My mother was a singer in a dance band.",""],["slow","/sləʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “slow”.","slow [sləʊ] -K4 adj. 慢的；减速的；迟钝的 vt. 放慢；阻碍 vi. 变慢；变萧条 adv. 慢慢地；迟缓地 n. (Slow)人名；(英)斯洛 时态: slowed, slowing, slows 级别: slower, slowest (中高 1761/1661)","欧陆词典释义：slow [sləʊ] -K4 adj. 慢的；减速的；迟钝的 vt. 放慢；阻碍 vi. 变慢；变萧条 adv. 慢慢地；迟缓地 n. (Slow)人名；(英)斯洛 时态: slowed, slowing, slows 级别: slower, slowest (中高 1761/1661)","The traffic is heavy and slow ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not moving, acting or done quickly; taking a long time; not fast","example":"a slow driver"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"not going or allowing you to go at a fast speed","example":"Progress was slower than expected."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"hesitating to do something or not doing something immediately","example":"The country is experiencing slow but steady economic growth."}]],["smart","/smɑ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “smart”.","smart [smɑ:t] -K3 adj. 聪明的；巧妙的；敏捷的；厉害的；潇洒的；剧烈的；时髦的 n. (Smart)人名；(法)斯马尔；(英、德)斯马特 时态: smarted, smarting, smarts 级别: smarter, smartest (中高研四六托雅宝 1856/4098)","欧陆词典释义：smart [smɑ:t] -K3 adj. 聪明的；巧妙的；敏捷的；厉害的；潇洒的；剧烈的；时髦的 n. (Smart)人名；(法)斯马尔；(英、德)斯马特 时态: smarted, smarting, smarts 级别: smarter, smartest (中高研四六托雅宝 1856/4098)","He was smart and well groomed but not good looking...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"looking clean and neat; well dressed in fashionable and/or formal clothes","example":"You look very smart in that suit."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"clean, neat and looking new and attractive","example":"I have to be smart for work."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"intelligent","example":"They were wearing their smartest clothes."}]],["snake","/sneɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “snake”.","snake [sneɪk] -K2 n. 蛇；阴险的人 vt. 拉（木材等）；迂回前进 vi. 迂回前进 时态: snaked, snaking, snakes (中高研四六托 3481/5064)","欧陆词典释义：snake [sneɪk] -K2 n. 蛇；阴险的人 vt. 拉（木材等）；迂回前进 vi. 迂回前进 时态: snaked, snaking, snakes (中高研四六托 3481/5064)","The road snake d through forested mountains...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a reptile","example":"a snake coiled up in the grass"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"Venomous snakes spit and hiss when they are cornered."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person who pretends to be your friend but who cannot be trusted","example":"A small green snake slithered across the wet road."}]],["soap","/səʊp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “soap”.","soap [səʊp] -K2 n. 肥皂 vt. 将肥皂涂在……上；对……拍马屁（俚语） vi. 用肥皂擦洗 时态: soaped, soaping, soaps (中高研四六托 4344/4288)","欧陆词典释义：soap [səʊp] -K2 n. 肥皂 vt. 将肥皂涂在……上；对……拍马屁（俚语） vi. 用肥皂擦洗 时态: soaped, soaping, soaps (中高研四六托 4344/4288)","a bar of lavender soap .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a substance that you use with water for washing your body","example":"soap and water"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"a bar/piece of soap"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to rub yourself/somebody/something with soap","example":"soap bubbles"}]],["soldier","/ˈsəʊldʒə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “soldier”.","soldier [ˈsəʊldʒə(r)] -K4 n. 军人；[昆] 兵蚁；懒汉；一片烤面包 vi. 当兵；磨洋工；坚持干；假称害病 时态: soldiered, soldiering, soldiers (中高托 1003/1731)","欧陆词典释义：soldier [ˈsəʊldʒə(r)] -K4 n. 军人；[昆] 兵蚁；懒汉；一片烤面包 vi. 当兵；磨洋工；坚持干；假称害病 时态: soldiered, soldiering, soldiers (中高托 1003/1731)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “soldier”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a member of an army, especially one who is not an officer","example":"soldiers in uniform"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"soldiers on duty"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"At least 19 people were killed when soldiers opened fire on a peaceful demonstration."}]],["somebody","/ˈsʌmbədi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “somebody”.","somebody [ˈsʌmbədi] -K4 n. 大人物；重要人物 pron. 有人；某人 (中高 1000/1321)","欧陆词典释义：somebody [ˈsʌmbədi] -K4 n. 大人物；重要人物 pron. 有人；某人 (中高 1000/1321)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “somebody”.",""],["sometimes","/ˈsʌmtaɪmz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sometimes”.","sometimes [ˈsʌmtaɪmz] -K4 adv. 有时，间或 (中高 445/478)","欧陆词典释义：sometimes [ˈsʌmtaɪmz] -K4 adv. 有时，间或 (中高 445/478)","During the summer, my skin sometimes gets greasy...",""],["son","/sʌn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “son”.","son [sʌn] -K5 n. 儿子；孩子（对年轻人的称呼）；男性后裔 n. (Son)人名；(土、老、柬)松；(法、罗)索恩；(日)存(名)；(日)孙(姓)；(越)山 (中高 481/599)","欧陆词典释义：son [sʌn] -K5 n. 儿子；孩子（对年轻人的称呼）；男性后裔 n. (Son)人名；(土、老、柬)松；(法、罗)索恩；(日)存(名)；(日)孙(姓)；(越)山 (中高 481/599)","He shared a pizza with his son Laurence...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person’s male child","example":"We have two sons and a daughter."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a friendly form of address that is used by an older man to a young man or boy","example":"They have three grown-up sons."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a man who belongs to a particular place or country, etc.","example":"He's the son of an Oxford professor."}]],["space","/speɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “space”.","space [speɪs] -K4 n. 空间；太空；距离 vt. 隔开 vi. 留间隔 时态: spaced, spacing, spaces (中高研四六雅 521/715)","欧陆词典释义：space [speɪs] -K4 n. 空间；太空；距离 vt. 隔开 vi. 留间隔 时态: spaced, spacing, spaces (中高研四六雅 521/715)","Under the plan, bits of open space — fields, golf-course borders and small parks — will be preserved.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an amount of an area or of a place that is empty or that is available for use","example":"floor/office/shelf, etc. space"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an area or a place that is empty","example":"We must make good use of the available space."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the quality of being large and empty, allowing you to move freely","example":"That desk takes up"}]],["spoon","/spu:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “spoon”.","spoon [spu:n] -K2 n. 匙，勺子；一杓的量 vt. 用匙舀；使成匙状 vi. 轻轻向上击 时态: spooned, spooning, spoons (中高研四六托 4339/6114)","欧陆词典释义：spoon [spu:n] -K2 n. 匙，勺子；一杓的量 vt. 用匙舀；使成匙状 vi. 轻轻向上击 时态: spooned, spooning, spoons (中高研四六托 4339/6114)","He stirred his coffee with a spoon .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a tool that has a handle with a shallow bowl at the end, used for stirring, serving and eating food","example":"a soup spoon"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"a wooden spoon"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having rich parents","example":"Remove the onion from the oil with a slotted spoon."}]],["square","/skweə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “square”.","square [skweə(r)] -K4 n. 平方；广场；正方形 adj. 平方的；正方形的；直角的；正直的 vt. 使成方形；与…一致 vi. 一致；成方形 adv. 成直角地 时态: squared, squaring, squares (中高研四六托雅宝 2747/1802)","欧陆词典释义：square [skweə(r)] -K4 n. 平方；广场；正方形 adj. 平方的；正方形的；直角的；正直的 vt. 使成方形；与…一致 vi. 一致；成方形 adv. 成直角地 时态: squared, squaring, squares (中高研四六托雅宝 2747/1802)","Serve the cake warm or at room temperature, cut in square s...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having four straight equal sides and four angles of 90°","example":"a square room"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"forming an angle of 90° exactly or approximately","example":"The book had rounded, not square, corners."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used after a unit of measurement to say that something measures the same amount on each of four sides","example":"square shoulders"}]],["account","/əˈkaʊnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “account”.","account [əˈkaʊnt] -K5 n. 账户；解释；账目，账单；理由；描述 vt. 认为；把…视为 vi. 解释；导致；报账 时态: accounted, accounting, accounts (高研四托雅 1071/498)","欧陆词典释义：account [əˈkaʊnt] -K5 n. 账户；解释；账目，账单；理由；描述 vt. 认为；把…视为 vi. 解释；导致；报账 时态: accounted, accounting, accounts (高研四托雅 1071/498)","Some banks make it difficult to open an account ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an arrangement that somebody has with a bank, etc. to keep money there, take some out, etc.","example":"I don't have a bank account."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a written record of money that is owed to a business and of money that has been paid by it","example":"to have an account at/with"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an arrangement with a shop/store or business to pay bills for goods or services at a later time, for example in regular amounts every month","example":"to open/close an account"}]],["add","/æd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “add”.","add [æd] -K5 n. 加法，加法运算 vi. 加；增加；加起来；做加法 vt. 增加，添加；补充说；计算…总和 时态: added, adding, adds (中高研四 340/330)","欧陆词典释义：add [æd] -K5 n. 加法，加法运算 vi. 加；增加；加起来；做加法 vt. 增加，添加；补充说；计算…总和 时态: added, adding, adds (中高研四 340/330)","Add the grated cheese to the sauce...",""],["agree","/əˈgri:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “agree”.","agree [əˈgri:] -K5 vi. vi. 同意，意见一致；约定，商定 vt. 同意，赞成；承认；约定，商定 时态: agreed, agreeing, agrees (中高 514/401)","欧陆词典释义：agree [əˈgri:] -K5 vi. vi. 同意，意见一致；约定，商定 vt. 同意，赞成；承认；约定，商定 时态: agreed, agreeing, agrees (中高 514/401)","If we agree d all the time it would be a bit boring, wouldn't it?...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have the same opinion as somebody; to say that you have the same opinion","example":"When he said that, I had to agree."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"if people are agreed","example":"‘That's true’, she agreed."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to say ‘yes’; to say that you will do what somebody wants or that you will allow something to happen","example":"He agreed with them about the need for change."}]],["airplane","/ˈeəpleɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “airplane”.","airplane [ˈeəpleɪn] -2 n. 飞机 (中高四 3519/21702)","欧陆词典释义：airplane [ˈeəpleɪn] -2 n. 飞机 (中高四 3519/21702)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “airplane”.",""],["any","/ˈeni/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “any”.","any [ˈeni] -K5 adj. 任何的；所有的；丝毫 pron. 任何；任何一个；若干 adv. 稍微；少许 n. (Any)人名；(法、罗)阿尼 (中高 109/78)","欧陆词典释义：any [ˈeni] -K5 adj. 任何的；所有的；丝毫 pron. 任何；任何一个；若干 adv. 稍微；少许 n. (Any)人名；(法、罗)阿尼 (中高 109/78)","I never make any big decisions...",[{"pos":"determiner","definition":"used with uncountable or plural nouns in negative sentences and questions, after if","example":"I didn't eat any meat."},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"used with singular countable nouns to refer to one of a number of things or people, when it does not matter which one","example":"Are there any stamps?"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used to show that somebody/something is special","example":"I've got hardly any money."}]],["April","/'eɪprəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “April”.","April ['eɪprəl] -K4 n. 四月 (中高雅 -/684)","欧陆词典释义：April ['eɪprəl] -K4 n. 四月 (中高雅 -/684)","The changes will be introduced in April ...",""],["August","/ɔ:ˈgʌst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “August”.","august [ɔ:ˈgʌst] -K4 n. 八月（简写为Aug） n. (August)人名；(法、葡、西、俄、罗、英、德、瑞典、挪)奥古斯特 adj. 威严的；令人敬畏的 (中高雅宝 22206/1239)","欧陆词典释义：august [ɔ:ˈgʌst] -K4 n. 八月（简写为Aug） n. (August)人名；(法、葡、西、俄、罗、英、德、瑞典、挪)奥古斯特 adj. 威严的；令人敬畏的 (中高雅宝 22206/1239)","Being so near the august person of the Empress, he was overcome with awe.",""],["backpack","/ˈbækpæk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “backpack”.","backpack [ˈbækpæk] n. 双肩背包，背包；远足用的背包 vt. 挑运；把…放入背包 vi. 背负简便行李旅行；挑运 (托 6456/25243)","欧陆词典释义：backpack [ˈbækpæk] n. 双肩背包，背包；远足用的背包 vt. 挑运；把…放入背包 vi. 背负简便行李旅行；挑运 (托 6456/25243)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “backpack”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large bag, often supported on a light metal frame, carried on the back and used especially by people who go climbing or walking","example":"She swung her backpack over her shoulder."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a piece of equipment that is carried on the back","example":"He was wearing a heavy backpack."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to travel on holiday/vacation carrying your equipment and clothes in a backpack","example":"a weed-sprayer backpack"}]],["banana","/bəˈnɑ:nə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “banana”.","banana [bəˈnɑ:nə] -2 n. 香蕉；喜剧演员；大鹰钩鼻 n. (Banana)人名；(葡、津)巴纳纳 (中高 4677/5663)","欧陆词典释义：banana [bəˈnɑ:nə] -2 n. 香蕉；喜剧演员；大鹰钩鼻 n. (Banana)人名；(葡、津)巴纳纳 (中高 4677/5663)","a bunch of banana s.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a long curved fruit with a thick yellow skin and soft flesh, that grows on trees in hot countries","example":"a bunch of bananas"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"The company has acquired an unhappy knack of slipping on banana skins."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to become angry, crazy or silly","example":"He lost his job and just went bananas."}]],["basket","/ˈbɑ:skɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “basket”.","basket [ˈbɑ:skɪt] -2 n. 篮子；（篮球比赛的）得分；一篮之量；篮筐 vt. 装入篮 (中高 3255/3828)","欧陆词典释义：basket [ˈbɑ:skɪt] -2 n. 篮子；（篮球比赛的）得分；一篮之量；篮筐 vt. 装入篮 (中高 3255/3828)","big wicker picnic basket s filled with sandwiches.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a container for holding or carrying things. Baskets","example":"a shopping basket"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount contained in a basket","example":"a picnic basket"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a facility on a website that records the items that you select to buy","example":"a clothes/laundry basket"}]],["bed","/bed/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bed”.","bed [bed] -K4 n. 床；基础；河底， 海底 vt. 使睡觉；安置，嵌入；栽种 vi. 上床；分层 时态: bedded, bedding, beds (中高 683/563)","欧陆词典释义：bed [bed] -K4 n. 床；基础；河底， 海底 vt. 使睡觉；安置，嵌入；栽种 vi. 上床；分层 时态: bedded, bedding, beds (中高 683/563)","She went into her bed room and lay down on the bed ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of furniture for sleeping on","example":"a single/double bed"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the bottom of a river, the sea, etc.","example":"She lay on the bed"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an area of ground in a garden/yard or park for growing flowers, vegetables, etc.","example":"He lay in bed"}]],["beginning","/bɪˈgɪnɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “beginning”.","beginning [bɪˈgɪnɪŋ] -K3 n. 开始；起点 v. 开始；创建（begin的ing形式） 原型: beginning 是 begin 的现在分词 (高研四六雅 1200/1242)","欧陆词典释义：beginning [bɪˈgɪnɪŋ] -K3 n. 开始；起点 v. 开始；创建（begin的ing形式） 原型: beginning 是 begin 的现在分词 (高研四六雅 1200/1242)","This was also the beginning of her recording career...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the time when something starts; the first part of an event, a story, etc.","example":"We're going to Japan at the beginning of"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the first or early ideas, signs or stages of something","example":"She's been working there since the beginning of"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the first sign of something ending","example":"We missed the beginning of the movie."}]],["belt","/belt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “belt”.","belt [belt] -K3 n. 带；腰带；地带 vt. 用带子系住；用皮带抽打 vi. 猛击 n. (Belt)人名；(英、法、德、西)贝尔特 时态: belted, belting, belts (高研四托 2430/2870)","欧陆词典释义：belt [belt] -K3 n. 带；腰带；地带 vt. 用带子系住；用皮带抽打 vi. 猛击 n. (Belt)人名；(英、法、德、西)贝尔特 时态: belted, belting, belts (高研四托 2430/2870)","He wore a belt with a large brass buckle.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a long narrow piece of leather, cloth, etc. that you wear around the waist","example":"to do up/fasten/tighten a belt"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a continuous band of material that moves round and is used to carry things along or to drive machinery","example":"a belt buckle"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an area with particular characteristics or where a particular group of people live","example":"the country’s corn/industrial belt"}]],["bike","/baɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bike”.","bike [baɪk] -3 n. 自行车；脚踏车 vi. 骑自行车（或摩托车） n. (Bike)人名；(土、土库、塞)比克 时态: biked, biking, bikes (中 2163/3241)","欧陆词典释义：bike [baɪk] -3 n. 自行车；脚踏车 vi. 骑自行车（或摩托车） n. (Bike)人名；(土、土库、塞)比克 时态: biked, biking, bikes (中 2163/3241)","I bike d home from the beach.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a bicycle","example":"She got on her bike and rode off."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a motorcycle","example":"I usually go to work by bike"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 19th cent.","example":"He got on his bike and rode off."}]],["blanket","/ˈblæŋkɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “blanket”.","blanket [ˈblæŋkɪt] -2 n. 毛毯，毯子；毯状物，覆盖层 adj. 总括的，全体的；没有限制的 vt. 覆盖，掩盖；用毯覆盖 时态: blanketed, blanketing, blankets (高研四托雅 3306/3938)","欧陆词典释义：blanket [ˈblæŋkɪt] -2 n. 毛毯，毯子；毯状物，覆盖层 adj. 总括的，全体的；没有限制的 vt. 覆盖，掩盖；用毯覆盖 时态: blanketed, blanketing, blankets (高研四托雅 3306/3938)","The mud disappeared under a blanket of snow...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large cover, often made of wool, used especially on beds to keep people warm","example":"It’s cold tonight—can I have another blanket?"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a thick layer or covering of something","example":"The baby was wrapped in a blanket."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"a blanket of fog/snow/cloud"}]],["boat","/bəʊt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “boat”.","boat [bəʊt] -K4 n. 小船；轮船 vi. 划船 时态: boated, boating, boats (中高雅 1231/1303)","欧陆词典释义：boat [bəʊt] -K4 n. 小船；轮船 vi. 划船 时态: boated, boating, boats (中高雅 1231/1303)","One of the best ways to see the area is in a small boat ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a vehicle (smaller than a ship) that travels on water, moved by oars","example":"a rowing/sailing boat"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"any ship","example":"a fishing boat"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"You can take a boat trip"}]],["bookstore","/'bʊkstɔ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bookstore”.","bookstore ['bʊkstɔ:(r)] -1 n. 书店（等于bookshop） (高 6186/33117)","欧陆词典释义：bookstore ['bʊkstɔ:(r)] -1 n. 书店（等于bookshop） (高 6186/33117)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bookstore”.",""],["bowl","/bəʊl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bowl”.","bowl [bəʊl] -K3 n. 碗；木球；大酒杯 vt. 投球；旋转；平稳快速移动 vi. 玩保龄球；滑动；平稳快速移动 时态: bowled, bowling, bowls (中高研四托 1829/2707)","欧陆词典释义：bowl [bəʊl] -K3 n. 碗；木球；大酒杯 vt. 投球；旋转；平稳快速移动 vi. 玩保龄球；滑动；平稳快速移动 时态: bowled, bowling, bowls (中高研四托 1829/2707)","Put all the ingredients into a large bowl ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a deep round dish with a wide open top, used especially for holding food or liquid","example":"a salad/fruit/sugar, etc. bowl"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the amount contained in a bowl","example":"a washing-up bowl"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the part of some objects that is shaped like a bowl","example":"a bowl of soup"}]],["box","/bɒks/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “box”.","box [bɒks] -K4 n. 箱，盒子；包厢；一拳 vt. 拳击；装…入盒中；打耳光 vi. 拳击 n. (Box)人名；(英、法、西)博克斯 时态: boxed, boxing, boxes (中高 795/874)","欧陆词典释义：box [bɒks] -K4 n. 箱，盒子；包厢；一拳 vt. 拳击；装…入盒中；打耳光 vi. 拳击 n. (Box)人名；(英、法、西)博克斯 时态: boxed, boxing, boxes (中高 795/874)","He reached into the cardboard box beside him...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a container made of wood, cardboard, metal, etc. with a flat stiff base and sides and often a lid, used especially for holding solid things","example":"She kept all the letters in a box."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a box and its contents","example":"a money box"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a small area in a theatre or court separated off from where other people sit","example":"cardboard boxes"}]],["break","/breɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “break”.","break [breɪk] -K5 vi. 打破；折断；弄坏；削弱 vt. （使）破；打破（纪录）；（常指好天气）突变；开始 vi. （嗓音）突变；突破；破晓；（价格）突然下跌 n. 破裂；间断；（持续一段时间的状况的）改变；间歇 时态: broke, broken, breaking, breaks (中高雅 494/519)","欧陆词典释义：break [breɪk] -K5 vi. 打破；折断；弄坏；削弱 vt. （使）破；打破（纪录）；（常指好天气）突变；开始 vi. （嗓音）突变；突破；破晓；（价格）突然下跌 n. 破裂；间断；（持续一段时间的状况的）改变；间歇 时态: broke, broken, breaking, breaks (中高雅 494/519)","He fell through the window, break ing the glass...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be damaged and separated into two or more parts , as a result of force; to damage something in this way","example":"All the windows broke with the force of the blast."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to stop working as a result of being damaged; to damage something and stop it from working","example":"The bag broke under the weight of the bottles inside it."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to cut the surface of the skin and make it bleed","example":"She dropped the plate and it broke into pieces"}]],["brush","/brʌʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “brush”.","brush [brʌʃ] -K3 n. 刷子；画笔；毛笔；争吵；与某人有效冲突；灌木丛地带；矮树丛；狐狸尾巴 vi. 刷；擦过；掠过；（经过时）轻触 vt. 刷；画； 时态: brushed, brushing, brushes (中高 3223/3418)","欧陆词典释义：brush [brʌʃ] -K3 n. 刷子；画笔；毛笔；争吵；与某人有效冲突；灌木丛地带；矮树丛；狐狸尾巴 vi. 刷；擦过；掠过；（经过时）轻触 vt. 刷；画； 时态: brushed, brushing, brushes (中高 3223/3418)","We gave him paint and brush es...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an object made of short stiff hairs (called bristles","example":"a paintbrush"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an act of brushing","example":"a hairbrush"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a light touch made in passing something/somebody","example":"a toothbrush"}]],["calendar","/ˈkælɪndə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “calendar”.","calendar [ˈkælɪndə(r)] -2 n. 日历；[天] 历法；日程表 vt. 将…列入表中；将…排入日程表 时态: calendared, calendaring, calendars (研四六托雅 4689/4695)","欧陆词典释义：calendar [ˈkælɪndə(r)] -2 n. 日历；[天] 历法；日程表 vt. 将…列入表中；将…排入日程表 时态: calendared, calendaring, calendars (研四六托雅 4689/4695)","There was a calendar on the wall above, with large squares around the dates.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a page or series of pages showing the days, weeks and months of a particular year, especially one that you hang on a wall","example":"a calendar for 2010"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a record of what you have to do each day; the book or piece of software in which you write this down","example":"This is one of the biggest weeks in the racing calendar."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a list of important events or dates of a particular type during the year","example":"a major festival in the church’s calendar"}]],["camera","/ˈkæmərə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “camera”.","camera [ˈkæmərə] -K4 n. 照相机；摄影机 n. (Camera)人名；(英、意、西)卡梅拉 (中高研四六雅 949/2246)","欧陆词典释义：camera [ˈkæmərə] -K4 n. 照相机；摄影机 n. (Camera)人名；(英、意、西)卡梅拉 (中高研四六雅 949/2246)","Her gran lent her a camera for a school trip to Venice and Egypt.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of equipment for taking photographs, moving pictures or television pictures","example":"Just point the camera and press the button."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 19th cent.","example":"Cameras started clicking as soon as she stepped out of the car."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 17th cent. (denoting a council or legislative chamber in Italy or Spain)","example":"a TV/video camera"}]],["camp","/kæmp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “camp”.","camp [kæmp] -K4 n. 露营 vt. 扎营；使扎营 vi. 露营；扎营 n. (Camp)人名；(英)坎普；(瑞典)坎普；(法)康 时态: camped, camping, camps 级别: camper, campest (中高研四六托雅 1188/2079)","欧陆词典释义：camp [kæmp] -K4 n. 露营 vt. 扎营；使扎营 vi. 露营；扎营 n. (Camp)人名；(英)坎普；(瑞典)坎普；(法)康 时态: camped, camping, camps 级别: camper, campest (中高研四六托雅 1188/2079)","a refugee camp ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place where people live temporarily in tents or temporary buildings","example":"Let's return to camp."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a place where young people go on holiday/vacation and take part in various activities or a particular activity","example":"to pitch/make camp"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a place where people are kept in temporary buildings or tents, especially by a government and often for long periods","example":"to break camp ("}]],["candy","/ˈkændi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “candy”.","candy [ˈkændi] -K1 n. 糖果（等于sweets）；冰糖（等于sugar candy，rock candy）；毒品 adj. 新潮的（服饰）；甜言蜜语的 vt. 用糖煮；使结晶为砂糖；美化 vi. 糖煮；成为结晶 时态: candied, candying, candies (中高研四 3446/10657)","欧陆词典释义：candy [ˈkændi] -K1 n. 糖果（等于sweets）；冰糖（等于sugar candy，rock candy）；毒品 adj. 新潮的（服饰）；甜言蜜语的 vt. 用糖煮；使结晶为砂糖；美化 vi. 糖煮；成为结晶 时态: candied, candying, candies (中高研四 3446/10657)","a piece of candy ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"sweet food made of sugar and/or chocolate, eaten between meals; a piece of this","example":"a box of candy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"a candy store"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"a candy bar"}]],["captain","/ˈkæptɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “captain”.","captain [ˈkæptɪn] -K4 n. 队长，首领；船长；上尉；海军上校 vt. 指挥；率领 时态: captained, captaining, captains (中高研四六 3347/1680)","欧陆词典释义：captain [ˈkæptɪn] -K4 n. 队长，首领；船长；上尉；海军上校 vt. 指挥；率领 时态: captained, captaining, captains (中高研四六 3347/1680)","Captain Mark Phillips.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the person in charge of a ship or commercial aircraft","example":"Captain Cook"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an officer of fairly high rank in the navy, the army and the US air force","example":"The captain gave the order to abandon ship."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the leader of a group of people, especially a sports team","example":"Captain Jones and his co-pilot"}]],["carrot","/ˈkærət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “carrot”.","carrot [ˈkærət] -K2 n. 胡萝卜 诱饵 (高研四六雅 4597/6034)","欧陆词典释义：carrot [ˈkærət] -K2 n. 胡萝卜 诱饵 (高研四六雅 4597/6034)","They will be set targets, with a carrot of extra cash and pay if they achieve them...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a long pointed orange root vegetable","example":"grated carrot"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a reward promised to somebody in order to persuade them to do something","example":"a pound of carrots"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"They are holding out a carrot of $120 million in economic aid."}]],["castle","/ˈkɑ:sl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “castle”.","castle [ˈkɑ:sl] -K3 n. 城堡；象棋中的车 vt. 置…于城堡中；筑城堡防御 n. (Castle)人名；(英)卡斯尔 时态: castled, castling, castles (高研四六雅 5844/1765)","欧陆词典释义：castle [ˈkɑ:sl] -K3 n. 城堡；象棋中的车 vt. 置…于城堡中；筑城堡防御 n. (Castle)人名；(英)卡斯尔 时态: castled, castling, castles (高研四六雅 5844/1765)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “castle”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large strong building with thick high walls and towers, built in the past by kings or queens, or other important people, to defend themselves against attack","example":"Windsor Castle"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"any of the four pieces placed in the corner squares of the board at the start of the game, usually made to look like a castle","example":"a medieval castle"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Old English","example":"Edinburgh castle was loyally held in the queen’s name."}]],["celebration","/ˌselɪˈbreɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “celebration”.","celebration [ˌselɪˈbreɪʃn] -K3 n. 庆典，庆祝会；庆祝；颂扬 (高 2996/3379)","欧陆词典释义：celebration [ˌselɪˈbreɪʃn] -K3 n. 庆典，庆祝会；庆祝；颂扬 (高 2996/3379)","I can tell you, there was a celebration in our house that night.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a special event that people organize in order to celebrate something","example":"birthday/wedding celebrations"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of celebrating something","example":"Her triumph was a cause for celebration"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 16th cent.","example":"a party in celebration of"}]],["chair","/tʃeə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “chair”.","chair [tʃeə(r)] -K4 n. 椅子；讲座；（会议的）主席位；大学教授的职位 vt. 担任（会议的）主席；使…入座；使就任要职 n. (Chair)人名；(法)谢尔 时态: chaired, chairing, chairs (中高雅 946/1029)","欧陆词典释义：chair [tʃeə(r)] -K4 n. 椅子；讲座；（会议的）主席位；大学教授的职位 vt. 担任（会议的）主席；使…入座；使就任要职 n. (Chair)人名；(法)谢尔 时态: chaired, chairing, chairs (中高雅 946/1029)","He rose from his chair and walked to the window.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of furniture for one person to sit on, with a back, a seat and four legs","example":"a table and chairs"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the position of being in charge of a meeting or committee; the person who holds this position","example":"Sit on your chair!"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the position of being in charge of a department in a university","example":"an old man asleep in a chair ("}]],["cheese","/tʃi:z/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cheese”.","cheese [tʃi:z] -K3 n. [食品] 奶酪；干酪；要人 adj. 叛变的；胆小的 vt. 停止 时态: cheesed, cheesing, cheese (中高研四雅 2104/2717)","欧陆词典释义：cheese [tʃi:z] -K3 n. [食品] 奶酪；干酪；要人 adj. 叛变的；胆小的 vt. 停止 时态: cheesed, cheesing, cheese (中高研四雅 2104/2717)","bread and cheese .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a type of food made from milk that can be either soft or hard and is usually white or yellow in colour; a particular type of this food","example":"Cheddar cheese"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"what you ask somebody to say before you take their photograph","example":"goat’s cheese ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"a cheese sandwich/salad"}]],["chicken","/ˈtʃɪkɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “chicken”.","chicken [ˈtʃɪkɪn] -K3 n. 鸡肉；小鸡；胆小鬼，懦夫 adj. 鸡肉的；胆怯的；幼小的 (中高研四六 1538/3030)","欧陆词典释义：chicken [ˈtʃɪkɪn] -K3 n. 鸡肉；小鸡；胆小鬼，懦夫 adj. 鸡肉的；胆怯的；幼小的 (中高研四六 1538/3030)","Lionel built a coop so that they could raise chicken s and have a supply of fresh eggs.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large bird that is often kept for its eggs or meat","example":"They keep chickens in the back yard."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"meat from a chicken","example":"free-range chickens"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"Old English","example":"fried/roast chicken"}]],["circle","/ˈsɜ:kl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “circle”.","circle [ˈsɜ:kl] -K4 n. 循环，周期；圆；圈子；圆形物 vt. 画圆圈；环绕…移动 vi. 盘旋，旋转；环行 时态: circled, circling, circles (中高研四六托雅 1506/1832)","欧陆词典释义：circle [ˈsɜ:kl] -K4 n. 循环，周期；圆；圈子；圆形物 vt. 画圆圈；环绕…移动 vi. 盘旋，旋转；环行 时态: circled, circling, circles (中高研四六托雅 1506/1832)","The flag was red, with a large white circle in the center...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a completely round flat shape","example":"Cut out two circles of paper."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the line that forms the edge of a circle","example":"Draw a circle."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a thing or a group of people or things shaped like a circle","example":"She walked the horse round in a circle"}]],["classroom","/ˈklɑ:sru:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “classroom”.","classroom [ˈklɑ:sru:m] -K2 n. 教室 (中高雅 1479/2842)","欧陆词典释义：classroom [ˈklɑ:sru:m] -K2 n. 教室 (中高雅 1479/2842)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “classroom”.",""],["climb","/klaɪm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “climb”.","climb [klaɪm] -K3 n. 爬；攀登 vi. 爬；攀登；上升 vt. 爬；攀登；上升 时态: climbed, climbing, climbs (中高研四六 1566/1646)","欧陆词典释义：climb [klaɪm] -K3 n. 爬；攀登 vi. 爬；攀登；上升 vt. 爬；攀登；上升 时态: climbed, climbing, climbs (中高研四六 1566/1646)","Climbing the first hill took half an hour...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to go up something towards the top","example":"to climb a mountain/hill/tree/wall"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to move somewhere, especially with difficulty or effort","example":"She climbed up the stairs."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to go up mountains or climb rocks as a hobby or sport","example":"The car slowly climbed the hill."}]],["clock","/klɒk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “clock”.","clock [klɒk] -K3 n. 时钟；计时器 vt. 记录；记时 vi. 打卡；记录时间 n. (Clock)人名；(英)克洛克 时态: clocked, clocking, clocks (中高研四雅 2635/2543)","欧陆词典释义：clock [klɒk] -K3 n. 时钟；计时器 vt. 记录；记时 vi. 打卡；记录时间 n. (Clock)人名；(英)克洛克 时态: clocked, clocking, clocks (中高研四雅 2635/2543)","He was conscious of a clock ticking...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an instrument for measuring and showing time, in a room, on the wall of a building or on a computer screen (not worn or carried like a watch)","example":"It was ten past six by the kitchen clock."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The clock struck"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"if you do something against the clock","example":"The clock is fast/slow"}]],["clothes","/kləʊðz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “clothes”.","clothes [kləʊðz] -K4 n. 衣服 原型: clothes 是 clothe 的第三人称单数 (中高雅 1434/1315)","欧陆词典释义：clothes [kləʊðz] -K4 n. 衣服 原型: clothes 是 clothe 的第三人称单数 (中高雅 1434/1315)","Moira walked upstairs to change her clothes ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the things that you wear, such as trousers/pants, dresses and jackets","example":"I bought some new clothes for the trip."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"to put on/take off your clothes"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to describe a situation in which everybody suddenly realizes that they were mistaken in believing that somebody/something was very good, important, etc.","example":"Bring a change of clothes"}]],["coffee","/ˈkɒfi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coffee”.","coffee [ˈkɒfi] -K3 n. 咖啡；咖啡豆；咖啡色 n. (Coffee)人名；(英)科菲 (中高雅 1388/1403)","欧陆词典释义：coffee [ˈkɒfi] -K3 n. 咖啡；咖啡豆；咖啡色 n. (Coffee)人名；(英)科菲 (中高雅 1388/1403)","Would you like some coffee ?...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the roasted","example":"decaffeinated/instant coffee"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a hot drink made from coffee powder and boiling water. It may be drunk with milk and/or sugar added.","example":"ground/real coffee"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a cup of coffee","example":"a jar of coffee"}]],["company","/ˈkʌmpəni/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “company”.","company [ˈkʌmpəni] -K5 n. 公司；陪伴，同伴；连队 vt. 陪伴 vi. 交往 n. (Company)人名；(西)孔帕尼；(英)康帕尼 时态: companied, companying, companies (中高托雅 189/151)","欧陆词典释义：company [ˈkʌmpəni] -K5 n. 公司；陪伴，同伴；连队 vt. 陪伴 vi. 交往 n. (Company)人名；(西)孔帕尼；(英)康帕尼 时态: companied, companying, companies (中高托雅 189/151)","Sheila found some work as a secretary in an insurance company .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a business organization that makes money by producing or selling goods or services","example":"the largest computer company in the world"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of people who work or perform together","example":"the National Bus Company"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of being with somebody else and not alone","example":"She joined the company in 2009."}]],["concert","/ˈkɒnsət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “concert”.","concert [ˈkɒnsət] -K3 n. 音乐会；一致；和谐 adj. 音乐会用的；在音乐会上演出的 vt. 使协调；协同安排 vi. 协调；协力 (中高研四六托雅 2515/2941)","欧陆词典释义：concert [ˈkɒnsət] -K3 n. 音乐会；一致；和谐 adj. 音乐会用的；在音乐会上演出的 vt. 使协调；协同安排 vi. 协调；协力 (中高研四六托雅 2515/2941)","a short concert of piano music...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a public performance of music","example":"a concert of music by Bach"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"a classical/rock/pop concert"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"working together with somebody/something","example":"They're in concert"}]],["crayon","/ˈkreɪən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “crayon”.","crayon [ˈkreɪən] -1 n. 蜡笔，有色粉笔 n. (Crayon)人名；(英)克雷恩 vt. 以蜡笔作画，用颜色粉笔画 时态: crayoned, crayoning, crayons (中高托宝 12296/15597)","欧陆词典释义：crayon [ˈkreɪən] -1 n. 蜡笔，有色粉笔 n. (Crayon)人名；(英)克雷恩 vt. 以蜡笔作画，用颜色粉笔画 时态: crayoned, crayoning, crayons (中高托宝 12296/15597)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “crayon”.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to draw or colour something using a crayon","example":"She coloured the picture in with crayons."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a coloured pencil or stick of soft coloured chalk","example":"She used crayons to draw the picture."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"The notice was written in crayon."}]],["crowd","/kraʊd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “crowd”.","crowd [kraʊd] -K4 n. 群众,一伙;一堆,许多,大众 v. 拥挤,挤满,挤进 vt. 挤满,将...塞进;催促,催逼 vi. 挤,拥挤,聚集 时态: crowded, crowding, crowds (高研四六托 1270/1686)","欧陆词典释义：crowd [kraʊd] -K4 n. 群众,一伙;一堆,许多,大众 v. 拥挤,挤满,挤进 vt. 挤满,将...塞进;催促,催逼 vi. 挤,拥挤,聚集 时态: crowded, crowding, crowds (高研四六托 1270/1686)","A huge crowd gathered in a square outside the Kremlin walls...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large number of people gathered together in a public place, for example in the streets or at a sports game","example":"He pushed his way through the crowd."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular group of people","example":"A small crowd had gathered outside the church."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"ordinary people, not special or unusual in any way","example":"Police had to break up the crowd."}]],["daily","/ˈdeɪli/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “daily”.","daily [ˈdeɪli] -K4 n. 日报；朝来夜去的女佣 adj. 日常的；每日的 adv. 日常地；每日；天天 n. (Daily)人名；(英)戴利 (中高研四雅 1483/1702)","欧陆词典释义：daily [ˈdeɪli] -K4 n. 日报；朝来夜去的女佣 adj. 日常的；每日的 adv. 日常地；每日；天天 n. (Daily)人名；(英)戴利 (中高研四雅 1483/1702)","Cathay Pacific flies daily non-stop to Hong Kong from Heathrow...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"happening, done or produced every day","example":"a daily routine/visit/newspaper"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"connected with one day’s work","example":"events affecting the daily lives"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Invoices are signed on a daily basis"}]],["December","/dɪ'sembə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “December”.","December [dɪ'sembə(r)] -K4 n. 十二月 (中高雅 -/1060)","欧陆词典释义：December [dɪ'sembə(r)] -K4 n. 十二月 (中高雅 -/1060)","a bright morning in mid- December ...",""],["diary","/ˈdaɪəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “diary”.","diary [ˈdaɪəri] -K3 n. 日志，日记；日记簿 (中高研四六雅 4334/2934)","欧陆词典释义：diary [ˈdaɪəri] -K3 n. 日志，日记；日记簿 (中高研四六雅 4334/2934)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “diary”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a book with spaces for each day of the year in which you can write down things you have to do in the future","example":"a desk diary"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a book in which you can write down the experiences you have each day, your private thoughts, etc.","example":"I'll make a note of our next meeting in my diary."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"Do you keep a diary"}]],["dinosaur","/ˈdaɪnəsɔ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dinosaur”.","dinosaur [ˈdaɪnəsɔ:(r)] -2 n. 恐龙；过时、落伍的人或事物 (高托 5326/7298)","欧陆词典释义：dinosaur [ˈdaɪnəsɔ:(r)] -2 n. 恐龙；过时、落伍的人或事物 (高托 5326/7298)","industrial dinosaur s.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an animal that lived millions of years ago but is now extinct","example":""},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person or thing that is old-fashioned and cannot change in the changing conditions of modern life","example":""},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 19th cent.","example":""}]],["gift","/gɪft/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “gift”.","gift [gɪft] -K3 n. 礼物；天赋；赠品 vt. 赋予；向…赠送 n. (Gift)人名；(英)吉夫特 时态: gifted, gifting, gifts (中高 1382/1914)","欧陆词典释义：gift [gɪft] -K3 n. 礼物；天赋；赠品 vt. 赋予；向…赠送 n. (Gift)人名；(英)吉夫特 时态: gifted, gifting, gifts (中高 1382/1914)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that you give to somebody, especially on a special occasion or to say thank you","example":"The watch was a gift from my mother."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a natural ability","example":"Thank you for your generous gift."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a thing that is very easy to do or cheap to buy","example":"a free gift"}]],["grandfather","/ˈgrænfɑ:ðə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “grandfather”.","grandfather [ˈgrænfɑ:ðə(r)] -K2 n. 祖父；始祖 vt. 不受新规定限制 (中四六 2950/4184)","欧陆词典释义：grandfather [ˈgrænfɑ:ðə(r)] -K2 n. 祖父；始祖 vt. 不受新规定限制 (中四六 2950/4184)",null,""],["grandmother","/ˈgrænmʌðə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “grandmother”.","grandmother [ˈgrænmʌðə(r)] -K2 n. 祖母；女祖先 vt. 当…的祖母 vi. 当祖母 (中研四六 2495/4338)","欧陆词典释义：grandmother [ˈgrænmʌðə(r)] -K2 n. 祖母；女祖先 vt. 当…的祖母 vi. 当祖母 (中研四六 2495/4338)",null,""],["grass","/grɑ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “grass”.","grass [grɑ:s] -K3 n. 草；草地，草坪 vt. 放牧；使……长满草；使……吃草 vi. 长草 n. (Grass)人名；(法、德、俄、瑞典、英)格拉斯 时态: grassed, grassing, grasses (中高雅 2014/2003)","欧陆词典释义：grass [grɑ:s] -K3 n. 草；草地，草坪 vt. 放牧；使……长满草；使……吃草 vi. 长草 n. (Grass)人名；(法、德、俄、瑞典、英)格拉斯 时态: grassed, grassing, grasses (中高雅 2014/2003)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a common wild plant with narrow green leaves and stems","example":"a blade of grass"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"any type of grass","example":"The dry grass caught fire."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an area of ground covered with grass","example":"ornamental grasses"}]],["guitar","/gɪˈtɑ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “guitar”.","guitar [gɪˈtɑ:(r)] -3 n. 吉他，六弦琴 vi. 弹吉他 (中高研六雅 3658/2516)","欧陆词典释义：guitar [gɪˈtɑ:(r)] -3 n. 吉他，六弦琴 vi. 弹吉他 (中高研六雅 3658/2516)",null,""],["gym","/dʒɪm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “gym”.","gym [dʒɪm] -2 n. 健身房；体育；体育馆 (中雅 3876/9878)","欧陆词典释义：gym [dʒɪm] -2 n. 健身房；体育；体育馆 (中雅 3876/9878)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a room or hall with equipment for doing physical exercise, for example in a school","example":"to play basketball in the gym"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"physical exercises done in a gym","example":"The school has recently built a new gym."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 19th cent.","example":"I don't enjoy gym."}]],["half","/hɑ:f/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “half”.","half [hɑ:f] -K5 n. 一半；半场；半学年 adj. 一半的；不完全的；半途的 adv. 一半地；部分地 n. (Half)人名；(阿拉伯)哈勒夫；(德)哈尔夫；(英)哈夫 (中高 547/470)","欧陆词典释义：half [hɑ:f] -K5 n. 一半；半场；半学年 adj. 一半的；不完全的；半途的 adv. 一半地；部分地 n. (Half)人名；(阿拉伯)哈勒夫；(德)哈尔夫；(英)哈夫 (中高 547/470)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"either of two equal parts into which something is or can be divided","example":"two and a half kilos ("},{"pos":"determiner","definition":"either of two periods of time into which a sports game, concert, etc. is divided","example":"One and a half hours are allowed for the exam."},{"pos":"pronoun","definition":"half a pint of beer or a similar drink","example":"An hour and a half is allowed for the exam."}]],["hamburger","/ˈhæmbɜ:gə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hamburger”.","hamburger [ˈhæmbɜ:gə(r)] -1 n. 汉堡包，火腿汉堡；牛肉饼，肉饼；碎牛肉 n. (Hamburger)人名；(英)汉堡；(瑞典)汉布里耶；(德)汉布格尔 (中高研四六托 7483/14356)","欧陆词典释义：hamburger [ˈhæmbɜ:gə(r)] -1 n. 汉堡包，火腿汉堡；牛肉饼，肉饼；碎牛肉 n. (Hamburger)人名；(英)汉堡；(瑞典)汉布里耶；(德)汉布格尔 (中高研四六托 7483/14356)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"finely chopped beef made into a flat round shape that is then fried, often served in a bread roll","example":""},{"pos":"noun","definition":"beef that has been finely chopped in a special machine","example":""},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 19th cent.","example":""}]],["hat","/hæt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hat”.","hat [hæt] -K3 n. 帽子 vt. 给……戴上帽子 vi. 供应帽子；制造帽子 n. (Hat)人名；(中)核(广东话·威妥玛) 时态: hatted, hatting, hats (中高雅 2015/2209)","欧陆词典释义：hat [hæt] -K3 n. 帽子 vt. 给……戴上帽子 vi. 供应帽子；制造帽子 n. (Hat)人名；(中)核(广东话·威妥玛) 时态: hatted, hatting, hats (中高雅 2015/2209)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a covering made to fit the head, often with a brim","example":"a straw/woolly, etc. hat"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a position or role, especially an official or professional role, when you have more than one such role","example":"to put on/take off a hat"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"I'm wearing two hats tonight—parent and teacher."}]],["heavy","/ˈhevi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “heavy”.","heavy [ˈhevi] -K4 n. 重物；严肃角色 adj. 沉重的；繁重的，巨大的；拥挤的；阴沉的 adv. 大量地；笨重地 级别: heavier, heaviest (中高雅 1005/943)","欧陆词典释义：heavy [ˈhevi] -K4 n. 重物；严肃角色 adj. 沉重的；繁重的，巨大的；拥挤的；阴沉的 adv. 大量地；笨重地 级别: heavier, heaviest (中高雅 1005/943)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"weighing a lot; difficult to lift or move","example":"She was struggling with a heavy suitcase."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"more or worse than usual in amount, degree, etc.","example":"My brother is much heavier than me."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"large and solid; not delicate","example":"He tried to push the heavy door open."}]],["height","/haɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “height”.","height [haɪt] -K3 n. 高地；高度；身高；顶点 (中高研四六托雅 2040/1913)","欧陆词典释义：height [haɪt] -K3 n. 高地；高度；身高；顶点 (中高研四六托雅 2040/1913)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the measurement of how tall a person or thing is","example":"Height: 210 mm. Width: 57 mm. Length: 170 mm."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality of being tall or high","example":"Please state your height and weight."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular distance above the ground","example":"It is almost 2 metres in height"}]],["hill","/hɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hill”.","hill [hɪl] -K3 n. 小山；丘陵；斜坡；山冈 n. (Hill)人名；(法、西)伊尔；(德、英、匈、捷、罗、芬、瑞典)希尔 时态: hilled, hilling, hills (中高 1800/1134)","欧陆词典释义：hill [hɪl] -K3 n. 小山；丘陵；斜坡；山冈 n. (Hill)人名；(法、西)伊尔；(德、英、匈、捷、罗、芬、瑞典)希尔 时态: hilled, hilling, hills (中高 1800/1134)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area of land that is higher than the land around it, but not as high as a mountain","example":"a region of gently rolling hills"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a slope on a road","example":"a hill farm/town/fort"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Old English","example":"The house is built on the side of a hill"}]],["hobby","/ˈhɒbi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hobby”.","hobby [ˈhɒbi] -K2 n. 嗜好；业余爱好 n. (Hobby)人名；(英)霍比 (中高雅 6554/6000)","欧陆词典释义：hobby [ˈhɒbi] -K2 n. 嗜好；业余爱好 n. (Hobby)人名；(英)霍比 (中高雅 6554/6000)",null,""],["honey","/ˈhʌni/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “honey”.","honey [ˈhʌni] -2 n. 蜂蜜；宝贝；甜蜜 adj. 甘美的；蜂蜜似的 vt. 对…说甜言蜜语；加蜜使甜 vi. 奉承；说甜言蜜语 n. (Honey)人名；(英)霍尼 时态: honied, honeying, honeys (高研四 2932/5334)","欧陆词典释义：honey [ˈhʌni] -2 n. 蜂蜜；宝贝；甜蜜 adj. 甘美的；蜂蜜似的 vt. 对…说甜言蜜语；加蜜使甜 vi. 奉承；说甜言蜜语 n. (Honey)人名；(英)霍尼 时态: honied, honeying, honeys (高研四 2932/5334)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a sweet sticky yellow substance made by bees","example":"Have you seen my keys, honey?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a way of addressing somebody that you like or love","example":"He can be a real honey when he wants to be."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person that you like or love and think is very kind","example":"How do bees make honey?"}]],["hotel","/həʊˈtel/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hotel”.","hotel [həʊˈtel] -K4 n. 旅馆，饭店；客栈 vt. 使…在饭店下榻 vi. 进行旅馆式办公 n. (Hotel)人名；(法)奥泰尔 (中高雅 1002/731)","欧陆词典释义：hotel [həʊˈtel] -K4 n. 旅馆，饭店；客栈 vt. 使…在饭店下榻 vi. 进行旅馆式办公 n. (Hotel)人名；(法)奥泰尔 (中高雅 1002/731)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a building where people stay, usually for a short time, paying for their rooms and meals","example":"We stayed at/in a hotel."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a pub","example":"hotel rooms/guests"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a restaurant","example":"a two-star/five-star, etc. hotel"}]],["hundred","/ˈhʌndrəd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hundred”.","hundred [ˈhʌndrəd] -5 num. 百；百个 n. 一百；许多 adj. 一百的；许多的 (中高 621/413)","欧陆词典释义：hundred [ˈhʌndrəd] -5 num. 百；百个 n. 一百；许多 adj. 一百的；许多的 (中高 621/413)",null,[{"pos":"number","definition":"100","example":"One hundred (of the children) have already been placed with foster families."},{"pos":"number","definition":"a large amount","example":"There were just a hundred of them there."},{"pos":"number","definition":"the numbers from 100 to 999","example":"This vase is worth several hundred dollars."}]],["ice","/aɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ice”.","ice [aɪs] -K4 n. 冰；冰淇淋；矜持；（俚）钻石 adj. 冰的 vt. 冰镇；结冰 vi. 结冰 n. (Ice)人名；(英)艾斯；(法)伊斯 时态: iced, icing, ices (中高雅 1230/2164)","欧陆词典释义：ice [aɪs] -K4 n. 冰；冰淇淋；矜持；（俚）钻石 adj. 冰的 vt. 冰镇；结冰 vi. 结冰 n. (Ice)人名；(英)艾斯；(法)伊斯 时态: iced, icing, ices (中高雅 1230/2164)",null,""],["icecream","","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “icecream”.","icecream n. 冰淇淋 a. 乳白色的 (-/36919)","欧陆词典释义：icecream n. 冰淇淋 a. 乳白色的 (-/36919)",null,""],["important","/ɪmˈpɔ:tnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “important”.","important [ɪmˈpɔ:tnt] -K5 adj. 重要的，重大的；有地位的；有权力的 (中高雅 266/218)","欧陆词典释义：important [ɪmˈpɔ:tnt] -K5 adj. 重要的，重大的；有地位的；有权力的 (中高雅 266/218)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a great effect on people or things; of great value","example":"an important decision/factor"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having great influence or authority","example":"I have an important announcement to make."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Money played an important role in his life."}]],["inside","/ˌɪnˈsaɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “inside”.","inside [ˌɪnˈsaɪd] -K4 prep. 少于；在…之内 n. 里面；内部；内情；内脏 adj. 里面的；内部的；秘密的 adv. 在里面 (中高研四六 964/1301)","欧陆词典释义：inside [ˌɪnˈsaɪd] -K4 prep. 少于；在…之内 n. 里面；内部；内情；内脏 adj. 里面的；内部的；秘密的 adv. 在里面 (中高研四六 964/1301)",null,[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"on or to the inner part of something/somebody; within something/somebody","example":"Go inside the house."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"in less than the amount of time mentioned","example":"Inside the box was a gold watch."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"For years we had little knowledge of what life was like inside China."}]],["internet","/'intənet/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “internet”.","internet ['intənet] -K n. 因特网 (中高研四雅 1467/31055)","欧陆词典释义：internet ['intənet] -K n. 因特网 (中高研四雅 1467/31055)",null,""],["island","/ˈaɪlənd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “island”.","island [ˈaɪlənd] -K4 n. 岛；岛屿；安全岛；岛状物 adj. 岛的 vt. 孤立；使成岛状 n. (Island)人名；(英)艾兰 (中高研四六雅 1512/982)","欧陆词典释义：island [ˈaɪlənd] -K4 n. 岛；岛屿；安全岛；岛状物 adj. 岛的 vt. 孤立；使成岛状 n. (Island)人名；(英)艾兰 (中高研四六雅 1512/982)",null,""],["jacket","/ˈdʒækɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “jacket”.","jacket [ˈdʒækɪt] -K3 n. 羽绒滑雪衫；西装短外套；短上衣，夹克；土豆皮；书籍的护封；文件套，公文夹 vt. 给…穿夹克；给…装护套；给…包上护封；〈口〉打 时态: jacketed, jacketing, jackets (中高研四六雅 2267/2400)","欧陆词典释义：jacket [ˈdʒækɪt] -K3 n. 羽绒滑雪衫；西装短外套；短上衣，夹克；土豆皮；书籍的护封；文件套，公文夹 vt. 给…穿夹克；给…装护套；给…包上护封；〈口〉打 时态: jacketed, jacketing, jackets (中高研四六雅 2267/2400)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of clothing worn on the top half of the body over a shirt, etc. that has sleeves and fastens down the front; a short, light coat","example":"a denim/tweed jacket"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a loose paper cover for a book, usually with a design or picture on it","example":"I have to wear a jacket and tie to work."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an outer cover around a hot water pipe, etc., for example to reduce loss of heat","example":"potatoes baked in their jackets"}]],["January","/'dʒænjuəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “January”.","January ['dʒænjuəri] -K4 n. 一月 (中高雅 -/984)","欧陆词典释义：January ['dʒænjuəri] -K4 n. 一月 (中高雅 -/984)",null,""],["jeans","/dʒi:nz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “jeans”.","jeans [dʒi:nz] -K2 n. 牛仔裤；工装裤 n. (Jeans)人名；(英、意)琼斯 原型: jeans 是 jean 的复数 (中高研四雅 3421/4826)","欧陆词典释义：jeans [dʒi:nz] -K2 n. 牛仔裤；工装裤 n. (Jeans)人名；(英、意)琼斯 原型: jeans 是 jean 的复数 (中高研四雅 3421/4826)",null,""],["juice","/dʒu:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “juice”.","juice [dʒu:s] -K3 n. （水果）汁，液；果汁 (中高托雅 2310/3724)","欧陆词典释义：juice [dʒu:s] -K3 n. （水果）汁，液；果汁 (中高托雅 2310/3724)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the liquid that comes from fruit or vegetables; a drink made from this","example":"Add the juice of two lemons."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the liquid that comes out of a piece of meat when it is cooked","example":"a carton of apple juice"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the liquid in the stomach that helps you to digest","example":"Two orange juices, please."}]],["July","/dʒu:'lai/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “July”.","July [dʒu:'lai] -K4 n. 七月 (中高雅 -/847)","欧陆词典释义：July [dʒu:'lai] -K4 n. 七月 (中高雅 -/847)",null,""],["June","/dʒu:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “June”.","June [dʒu:n] -K4 n. 六月；琼（人名，来源于拉丁语，含义是“年轻气盛的六月”） (中高雅 -/691)","欧陆词典释义：June [dʒu:n] -K4 n. 六月；琼（人名，来源于拉丁语，含义是“年轻气盛的六月”） (中高雅 -/691)",null,""],["kangaroo","/ˌkæŋgəˈru:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “kangaroo”.","kangaroo [ˌkæŋgəˈru:] -1 n. 袋鼠 (高雅宝 15706/15573)","欧陆词典释义：kangaroo [ˌkæŋgəˈru:] -1 n. 袋鼠 (高雅宝 15706/15573)",null,""],["kilometre","/ˈkɪləmi:tə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “kilometre”.","kilometre [ˈkɪləmi:tə(r)] -K3 n. [计量] 公里；[计量] 千米 (中研 -/4574)","欧陆词典释义：kilometre [ˈkɪləmi:tə(r)] -K3 n. [计量] 公里；[计量] 千米 (中研 -/4574)",null,""],["king","/ kɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “king”.","king [ kɪŋ] -K4 n. 国王；最有势力者；王棋 vi. 统治；做国王 vt. 立…为王 adj. 主要的，最重要的，最大的 n. (King)人名；(德、英、葡、捷、西)金；(中)金(普通话·威妥玛)；(泰)京；(东南亚国家华语)京 (中高研四雅 2080/612)","欧陆词典释义：king [ kɪŋ] -K4 n. 国王；最有势力者；王棋 vi. 统治；做国王 vt. 立…为王 adj. 主要的，最重要的，最大的 n. (King)人名；(德、英、葡、捷、西)金；(中)金(普通话·威妥玛)；(泰)京；(东南亚国家华语)京 (中高研四雅 2080/612)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the male ruler of an independent state that has a royal family","example":"the kings and queens of England"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person, an animal or a thing that is thought to be the best or most important of a particular type","example":"to be crowned king"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used in compounds with the names of animals or plants to describe a very large type of the thing mentioned","example":"King George V"}]],["knife","/naɪf/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “knife”.","knife [naɪf] -K3 n. 刀；匕首 vt. 用刀切；（口）伤害 vi. 劈开；划过 时态: knifed, knifing, knifes (中高雅 2240/2471)","欧陆词典释义：knife [naɪf] -K3 n. 刀；匕首 vt. 用刀切；（口）伤害 vi. 劈开；划过 时态: knifed, knifing, knifes (中高雅 2240/2471)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a sharp blade with a handle, used for cutting or as a weapon","example":"knives and forks"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Old English","example":"a sharp knife"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the situation has become so bad that people are preparing to make one person take the blame, for example by taking away their job","example":"a bread knife ("}]],["knock","/nɒk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “knock”.","knock [nɒk] -K3 vi. 敲；打；敲击 vt. 敲；打；敲击；批评 n. 敲；敲打；爆震声 时态: knocked, knocking, knocks (中高 2087/1958)","欧陆词典释义：knock [nɒk] -K3 vi. 敲；打；敲击 vt. 敲；打；敲击；批评 n. 敲；敲打；爆震声 时态: knocked, knocking, knocks (中高 2087/1958)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to hit a door, etc. firmly in order to attract attention","example":"He knocked three times and waited."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to hit something, often by accident, with a short, hard blow","example":"Somebody was knocking on the window."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to put somebody/something into a particular state by hitting them/it","example":"Be careful you don't knock your head on this low beam."}]],["lady","/ˈleɪdi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “lady”.","lady [ˈleɪdi] -K4 n. 女士，夫人；小姐；妻子 (中高研四 1517/774)","欧陆词典释义：lady [ˈleɪdi] -K4 n. 女士，夫人；小姐；妻子 (中高研四 1517/774)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a word used to mean ‘woman’ that some people, especially older people, consider is more polite","example":"There's a lady waiting to see you."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a woman who is polite and well educated, has excellent manners and always behaves well","example":"He was with an attractive young lady."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used when speaking to or about a girl or woman, especially somebody you do not know","example":"the ladies’ golf championship"}]],["lamp","/læmp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “lamp”.","lamp [læmp] -K2 n. 灯；照射器 vt. 照亮 vi. 发亮 n. (Lamp)人名；(英、德、匈、瑞典)兰普 (中高研四六托雅 3936/3340)","欧陆词典释义：lamp [læmp] -K2 n. 灯；照射器 vt. 照亮 vi. 发亮 n. (Lamp)人名；(英、德、匈、瑞典)兰普 (中高研四六托雅 3936/3340)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a device that uses electricity, oil or gas to produce light","example":"a table/desk/bicycle, etc. lamp"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an electrical device that produces rays","example":"to switch on/turn off a lamp"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"a street lamp"}]],["leaf","/li:f/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “leaf”.","leaf [li:f] -K3 n. 叶子；（书籍等的）一张；扇页 vi. 生叶；翻书页 vt. 翻…的页，匆匆翻阅 n. (Leaf)人名；(英)利夫 时态: leafed, leafing, leafs (中高研四六 1559/1823)","欧陆词典释义：leaf [li:f] -K3 n. 叶子；（书籍等的）一张；扇页 vi. 生叶；翻书页 vt. 翻…的页，匆匆翻阅 n. (Leaf)人名；(英)利夫 时态: leafed, leafing, leafs (中高研四六 1559/1823)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a flat green part of a plant, growing from a stem","example":"lettuce/cabbage/oak leaves"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having leaves","example":"The trees are just coming into leaf"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a sheet of paper, especially a page in a book","example":"the dead leaves of autumn/the fall"}]],["lemon","/ˈlemən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “lemon”.","lemon [ˈlemən] -K2 adj. 柠檬色的 n. 柠檬 n. (Lemon)人名；(英、德、捷、瑞典)莱蒙；(法)勒蒙 (高研四雅 3179/4583)","欧陆词典释义：lemon [ˈlemən] -K2 adj. 柠檬色的 n. 柠檬 n. (Lemon)人名；(英、德、捷、瑞典)莱蒙；(法)勒蒙 (高研四雅 3179/4583)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a yellow citrus","example":"lemon tea"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"lemon","example":"a gin and tonic with ice and lemon"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a pale yellow colour","example":"Squeeze the juice of half a lemon over the fish."}]],["lion","/ˈlaɪən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “lion”.","lion [ˈlaɪən] -2 n. 狮子；名人；勇猛的人；社交场合的名流 n. (Lion)人名；(西、葡)利昂；(德、法、意、捷、瑞典)利翁；(英)莱昂 (中高研四六 4305/3397)","欧陆词典释义：lion [ˈlaɪən] -2 n. 狮子；名人；勇猛的人；社交场合的名流 n. (Lion)人名；(西、葡)利昂；(德、法、意、捷、瑞典)利翁；(英)莱昂 (中高研四六 4305/3397)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large powerful animal of the cat family, that hunts in groups and lives in parts of Africa and southern Asia. Lions","example":"Young Masai men gather for traditional lion hunts."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"Young Masai men gather for traditional lion hunts."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a difficult situation in which you have to face a person or people who are unfriendly or aggressive towards you","example":"Young Masai men gather for traditional lion hunts."}]],["lock","/lɒk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “lock”.","lock [lɒk] -K3 vt. 锁，锁上；隐藏 vi. 锁；锁住；卡住 n. 锁；水闸；刹车 n. (Lock)人名；(英、丹、德、瑞典)洛克 时态: locked, locking, locks (中高研四雅 2221/2332)","欧陆词典释义：lock [lɒk] -K3 vt. 锁，锁上；隐藏 vi. 锁；锁住；卡住 n. 锁；水闸；刹车 n. (Lock)人名；(英、丹、德、瑞典)洛克 时态: locked, locking, locks (中高研四雅 2221/2332)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to fasten something with a lock; to be fastened with a lock","example":"Did you lock the door?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to put something in a safe place and lock it","example":"The gates are locked at 6 o'clock."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to become or make something become fixed in one position and unable to move","example":"This suitcase doesn't lock."}]],["London","/'lʌndən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “London”.","London ['lʌndən] n. 伦敦 (中高雅 -/248)","欧陆词典释义：London ['lʌndən] n. 伦敦 (中高雅 -/248)",null,""],["loud","/laʊd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “loud”.","loud [laʊd] -K3 adj. 大声的，高声的；不断的；喧吵的 adv. 大声地，高声地，响亮地 n. (Loud)人名；(英)劳德 级别: louder, loudest (中高研四 3094/3207)","欧陆词典释义：loud [laʊd] -K3 adj. 大声的，高声的；不断的；喧吵的 adv. 大声地，高声地，响亮地 n. (Loud)人名；(英)劳德 级别: louder, loudest (中高研四 3094/3207)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"making a lot of noise","example":"loud laughter"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"talking very loudly, too much and in a way that is annoying","example":"a deafeningly loud"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"too bright and lacking good taste","example":"She spoke in a very loud voice."}]],["low","/ləʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “low”.","low [ləʊ] -K5 adj. 低的，浅的；卑贱的；粗俗的；消沉的 adv. 低声地；谦卑地，低下地 n. 低；低价；低点；牛叫声 vi. 牛叫 n. (Low)人名；(英、德)洛 时态: lowed, lowing, lows 级别: lower, lowest (中高宝 360/318)","欧陆词典释义：low [ləʊ] -K5 adj. 低的，浅的；卑贱的；粗俗的；消沉的 adv. 低声地；谦卑地，低下地 n. 低；低价；低点；牛叫声 vi. 牛叫 n. (Low)人名；(英、德)洛 时态: lowed, lowing, lows 级别: lower, lowest (中高宝 360/318)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not high or tall; not far above the ground","example":"a low wall/building/table"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"at or near the bottom of something","example":"a low range of hills"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"not high at the neck","example":"low clouds"}]],["lucky","/ˈlʌki/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “lucky”.","lucky [ˈlʌki] -K3 adj. 幸运的；侥幸的 级别: luckier, luckiest (中高研四 2126/2137)","欧陆词典释义：lucky [ˈlʌki] -K3 adj. 幸运的；侥幸的 级别: luckier, luckiest (中高研四 2126/2137)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having good luck","example":"His friend was killed and he knows he is lucky to be alive."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"being the result of good luck","example":"She was lucky enough to be chosen for the team."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"bringing good luck","example":"You were lucky (that) you spotted the danger in time."}]],["March","/mɑ:tʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “March”.","march [mɑ:tʃ] -K3 n. 三月 时态: marched, marching, marches (中高托雅 3483/695)","欧陆词典释义：march [mɑ:tʃ] -K3 n. 三月 时态: marched, marching, marches (中高托雅 3483/695)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to walk with stiff regular steps like a soldier","example":"Soldiers were marching up and down outside the government buildings."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to walk somewhere quickly in a determined way","example":"Quick march! ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to walk through the streets in a large group in order to protest about something","example":"They marched 20 miles to reach the capital."}]],["May","/meɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “May”.","may [meɪ] -K4 aux. 可以，能够；可能，也许；祝，愿；会，能 (中高雅 119/83)","欧陆词典释义：may [meɪ] -K4 aux. 可以，能够；可能，也许；祝，愿；会，能 (中高雅 119/83)",null,[{"pos":"modal verb","definition":"used to say that something is possible","example":"That may or may not be true."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used when admitting that something is true before introducing another point, argument, etc.","example":"He may have ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to ask for or give permission","example":"They may well"}]],["message","/ˈmesɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “message”.","message [ˈmesɪdʒ] -K4 n. 消息；差使；启示；预言；广告词 vi. 报信，报告；[通信] 报文 vt. 通知 时态: messaged, messaging, messages (中高研四六 807/1120)","欧陆词典释义：message [ˈmesɪdʒ] -K4 n. 消息；差使；启示；预言；广告词 vi. 报信，报告；[通信] 报文 vt. 通知 时态: messaged, messaging, messages (中高研四六 807/1120)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a written or spoken piece of information, etc. that you send to somebody or leave for somebody when you cannot speak to them yourself","example":"There were no messages for me at the hotel."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a piece of information sent in electronic form, for example by email or mobile/cell phone","example":"We've had an urgent message saying that your father's ill."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an important moral, social or political idea that a book, speech, etc. is trying to communicate","example":"Jenny's not here at the moment. Can I take a message?"}]],["million","/ˈmɪljən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “million”.","million [ˈmɪljən] -5 n. 百万；无数 adj. 百万的；无数的 num. 百万 n. (Million)人名；(法、罗、埃塞)米利翁 (高雅 222/336)","欧陆词典释义：million [ˈmɪljən] -5 n. 百万；无数 adj. 百万的；无数的 num. 百万 n. (Million)人名；(法、罗、埃塞)米利翁 (高雅 222/336)",null,[{"pos":"number","definition":"1 000 000","example":"a population of half a million"},{"pos":"number","definition":"a very large amount","example":"tens of millions of dollars"},{"pos":"number","definition":"late Middle English","example":"It must be worth a million ("}]],["mirror","/ˈmɪrə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mirror”.","mirror [ˈmɪrə(r)] -K3 n. 镜子；真实的写照；榜样 vt. 反射；反映 时态: mirrored, mirroring, mirrors (中高研四六 1853/2086)","欧陆词典释义：mirror [ˈmɪrə(r)] -K3 n. 镜子；真实的写照；榜样 vt. 反射；反映 时态: mirrored, mirroring, mirrors (中高研四六 1853/2086)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of special flat glass that reflects images, so that you can see yourself when you look in it","example":"He looked at himself in the mirror"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"something that shows what something else is like","example":"a rear-view mirror ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"=","example":"a wing mirror ("}]],["model","/ˈmɒdl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “model”.","model [ˈmɒdl] -K4 n. 模型；典型；模范；模特儿；样式 vt. 模拟；塑造；模仿 vi. 做模型；做模特儿 adj. 模范的；作模型用的 n. (Model)人名；(德、俄、英)莫德尔 时态: modelled, modelling, models (中高研四雅 504/551)","欧陆词典释义：model [ˈmɒdl] -K4 n. 模型；典型；模范；模特儿；样式 vt. 模拟；塑造；模仿 vi. 做模型；做模特儿 adj. 模范的；作模型用的 n. (Model)人名；(德、俄、英)莫德尔 时态: modelled, modelling, models (中高研四雅 504/551)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a copy of something, usually smaller than the original object","example":"a working model"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular design or type of product","example":"a model aeroplane"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a simple description of a system, used for explaining how something works or calculating what might happen, etc.","example":"The architect had produced a scale model"}]],["modern","/ˈmɒdn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “modern”.","modern [ˈmɒdn] -K4 adj. 现代的，近代的；时髦的 n. 现代人；有思想的人 (中高雅 1046/762)","欧陆词典释义：modern [ˈmɒdn] -K4 adj. 现代的，近代的；时髦的 n. 现代人；有思想的人 (中高雅 1046/762)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"of the present time or recent times","example":"the modern industrial world"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"new and intended to be different from traditional styles","example":"Modern European history"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"using the latest technology, designs, materials, etc.","example":"modern Greek"}]],["motorcycle","/ˈməʊtəsaɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “motorcycle”.","motorcycle [ˈməʊtəsaɪkl] -K1 n. 摩托车；机动车 vi. 骑摩托车 时态: motorcycled, motorcycling, motorcycles (中高雅 6059/9757)","欧陆词典释义：motorcycle [ˈməʊtəsaɪkl] -K1 n. 摩托车；机动车 vi. 骑摩托车 时态: motorcycled, motorcycling, motorcycles (中高雅 6059/9757)",null,""],["mouse","/maʊs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mouse”.","mouse [maʊs] -K2 n. 鼠标；老鼠；胆小羞怯的人 vt. 探出 vi. 捕鼠；窥探 时态: moused, mousing, mouses (中高研四六 3305/2845)","欧陆词典释义：mouse [maʊs] -K2 n. 鼠标；老鼠；胆小羞怯的人 vt. 探出 vi. 捕鼠；窥探 时态: moused, mousing, mouses (中高研四六 3305/2845)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small animal that is covered in fur and has a long thin tail. Mice","example":"a field mouse"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a small device that is moved by hand across a surface to control the movement of the cursor","example":"a house mouse"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"The stores were overrun with rats and mice."}]],["natural","/ˈnætʃrəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “natural”.","natural [ˈnætʃrəl] -K4 adj. 自然的；物质的；天生的；不做作的 n. 自然的事情；白痴；本位音 n. (Natural)人名；(西)纳图拉尔 (中高研四六托雅 715/709)","欧陆词典释义：natural [ˈnætʃrəl] -K4 adj. 自然的；物质的；天生的；不做作的 n. 自然的事情；白痴；本位音 n. (Natural)人名；(西)纳图拉尔 (中高研四六托雅 715/709)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"existing in nature; not made or caused by humans","example":"natural disasters"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"normal; as you would expect","example":"the natural world"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to describe behaviour that is part of the character that a person or an animal was born with","example":"a country’s natural resources"}]],["neck","/nek/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “neck”.","neck [nek] -K3 n. 脖子；衣领；海峡 vi. 搂著脖子亲吻；变狭窄 vt. 使变细；与…搂著脖子亲吻 n. (Neck)人名；(德、意、英)内克 时态: necked, necking, necks (中高研四六托雅 1521/1569)","欧陆词典释义：neck [nek] -K3 n. 脖子；衣领；海峡 vi. 搂著脖子亲吻；变狭窄 vt. 使变细；与…搂著脖子亲吻 n. (Neck)人名；(德、意、英)内克 时态: necked, necking, necks (中高研四六托雅 1521/1569)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the part of the body between the head and the shoulders","example":"He tied a scarf around his neck."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the part of a piece of clothing that fits around the neck","example":"I woke up with a stiff neck."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"having the type of neck","example":"Giraffes have very long necks."}]],["new","/nju:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “new”.","new [nju:] -K5 adj. 新的，新鲜的；更新的；初见的 adv. 新近 n. (New)人名；(英)纽 级别: newer, newest (中高 88/81)","欧陆词典释义：new [nju:] -K5 adj. 新的，新鲜的；更新的；初见的 adv. 新近 n. (New)人名；(英)纽 级别: newer, newest (中高 88/81)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not existing before; recently made, invented, introduced, etc.","example":"Have you read her new novel?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that is new","example":"new ways of doing things"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"recently bought","example":"This idea isn't new."}]],["ninth","/naɪnθ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ninth”.","ninth [naɪnθ] -4 num. 第九 adj. 第九的；九分之一的 n. 九分之一 (中高 5059/5636)","欧陆词典释义：ninth [naɪnθ] -4 num. 第九 adj. 第九的；九分之一的 n. 九分之一 (中高 5059/5636)",null,""],["ninety","/ˈnaɪnti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ninety”.","ninety [ˈnaɪnti] -5 n. 九十 adj. 九十的；九十岁的 num. 九十 (中高 8279/1948)","欧陆词典释义：ninety [ˈnaɪnti] -5 n. 九十 adj. 九十的；九十岁的 num. 九十 (中高 8279/1948)",null,[{"pos":"number","definition":"90","example":"The temperature must be in the nineties today."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"numbers, years or temperatures from 90 to 99","example":"The temperature must be in the nineties today."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"between the ages of 90 and 99","example":"The temperature must be in the nineties today."}]],["noodle","/ˈnu:dl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “noodle”.","noodle [ˈnu:dl] -1 n. 面条；笨蛋 (中高研 7939/21573)","欧陆词典释义：noodle [ˈnu:dl] -1 n. 面条；笨蛋 (中高研 7939/21573)",null,""]],"exam":[["analyze","/'ænəlaɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “analyze”.","analyze ['ænəlaɪz] vt. 对…进行分析，分解（等于analyse） 时态: analyzed, analyzing, analyzes (高四托宝 2316/13046)","欧陆词典释义：analyze ['ænəlaɪz] vt. 对…进行分析，分解（等于analyse） 时态: analyzed, analyzing, analyzes (高四托宝 2316/13046)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “analyze”.",""],["approach","/əˈprəʊtʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “approach”.","approach [əˈprəʊtʃ] -K4 n. 方法；途径；接近 vt. 接近；着手处理 vi. 靠近 时态: approached, approaching, approaches (高研四六托雅宝 750/583)","欧陆词典释义：approach [əˈprəʊtʃ] -K4 n. 方法；途径；接近 vt. 接近；着手处理 vi. 靠近 时态: approached, approaching, approaches (高研四六托雅宝 750/583)","He didn't approach the front door at once...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to come near to somebody/something in distance or time","example":"We heard the sound of an approaching car/a car approaching."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to speak to somebody about something, especially to ask them for something or to offer to do something","example":"Winter is approaching."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to come close to something in amount, level or quality","example":"The time is fast approaching when we shall have to make a decision."}]],["argument","/ˈɑ:gjumənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “argument”.","argument [ˈɑ:gjumənt] -K4 n. 论证；论据；争吵；内容提要 (高研四雅 1185/832)","欧陆词典释义：argument [ˈɑ:gjumənt] -K4 n. 论证；论据；争吵；内容提要 (高研四雅 1185/832)","There's a strong argument for lowering the price...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a conversation or discussion in which two or more people disagree, often angrily","example":"to win/lose an argument"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a reason or set of reasons that somebody uses to show that something is true or correct","example":"After some heated argument a decision was finally taken."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of disagreeing in a conversation or discussion using a reason or set of reasons","example":"We had an argument"}]],["assess","/əˈses/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assess”.","assess [əˈses] -4 vt. 评定；估价；对…征税 时态: assessed, assessing, assesses (高研四六托雅宝 2042/1488)","欧陆词典释义：assess [əˈses] -4 vt. 评定；估价；对…征税 时态: assessed, assessing, assesses (高研四六托雅宝 2042/1488)","Our correspondent has been assess ing the impact of the sanctions...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make a judgement about the nature or quality of somebody/something","example":"It's difficult to assess the effects of these changes."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to calculate the amount or value of something","example":"to assess a patient’s needs"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Interviews allow you to assess the suitability of candidates."}]],["assume","/əˈsju:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assume”.","assume [əˈsju:m] -K4 vt. 僭取；篡夺；夺取；擅用；侵占 vi. 假定；设想；承担；采取 时态: assumed, assuming, assumes (高研四六托雅宝 1091/886)","欧陆词典释义：assume [əˈsju:m] -K4 vt. 僭取；篡夺；夺取；擅用；侵占 vi. 假定；设想；承担；采取 时态: assumed, assuming, assumes (高研四六托雅宝 1091/886)","It is a misconception to assume that the two continents are similar...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think or accept that something is true but without having proof of it","example":"It is reasonable to assume (that)"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take or begin to have power or responsibility","example":"Let us assume"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to begin to have a particular quality or appearance","example":"She would, he assumed, be home at the usual time."}]],["benefit","/ˈbenɪfɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “benefit”.","benefit [ˈbenɪfɪt] -K4 n. 利益，好处；救济金 vt. 有益于，对…有益 vi. 受益，得益 时态: benefited, benefiting, benefits (高研四六托雅 812/656)","欧陆词典释义：benefit [ˈbenɪfɪt] -K4 n. 利益，好处；救济金 vt. 有益于，对…有益 vi. 受益，得益 时态: benefited, benefiting, benefits (高研四六托雅 812/656)","Each family farms individually and reaps the benefit of its labor...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an advantage that something gives you; a helpful and useful effect that something has","example":"I've had the benefit of"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"money provided by the government to people who need financial help because they are unemployed, ill/sick, etc.","example":"The new regulations will be of benefit to"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an advantage that you get from a company in addition to the money that you earn","example":"It will be to your benefit"}]],["challenge","/ˈtʃæləndʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “challenge”.","challenge [ˈtʃæləndʒ] -K4 n. 挑战；怀疑 vt. 向…挑战；对…质疑 时态: challenged, challenging, challenges (高研四六托雅 984/1506)","欧陆词典释义：challenge [ˈtʃæləndʒ] -K4 n. 挑战；怀疑 vt. 向…挑战；对…质疑 时态: challenged, challenging, challenges (高研四六托雅 984/1506)","I like a big challenge and they don't come much bigger than this...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a new or difficult task that tests somebody’s ability and skill","example":"an exciting/interesting challenge"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an invitation or a suggestion to somebody that they should enter a competition, fight, etc.","example":"The role will be the biggest challenge of his acting career."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a statement or an action that shows that somebody refuses to accept something and questions whether it is right, legal, etc.","example":"to face a challenge"}]],["character","/ˈkærəktə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “character”.","character [ˈkærəktə(r)] -K4 n. 性格，品质；特性；角色；[计] 字符 vt. 印，刻；使具有特征 n. (Character)人名；(英)克拉克特 时态: charactered, charactering, characters (高研四六托 786/805)","欧陆词典释义：character [ˈkærəktə(r)] -K4 n. 性格，品质；特性；角色；[计] 字符 vt. 印，刻；使具有特征 n. (Character)人名；(英)克拉克特 时态: charactered, charactering, characters (高研四六托 786/805)","Perhaps there is a negative side to his character that you haven't seen yet...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"all the qualities and features that make a person, groups of people, and places different from others","example":"to have a strong/weak character"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way that something is, or a particular quality or feature that a thing, an event or a place has","example":"character traits/defects"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"strong personal qualities such as the ability to deal with difficult or dangerous situations","example":"The book gives a fascinating insight into Mrs Obama's character."}]],["circumstance","/ˈsɜ:kəmstəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “circumstance”.","circumstance [ˈsɜ:kəmstəns] -K3 n. 环境，情况；事件；境遇 (高四六托雅 1780/905)","欧陆词典释义：circumstance [ˈsɜ:kəmstəns] -K3 n. 环境，情况；事件；境遇 (高四六托雅 1780/905)","Recent opinion polls show that 60 percent favor abortion under certain circumstance s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the conditions and facts that are connected with and affect a situation, an event or an action","example":"The company reserves the right to cancel this agreement in certain circumstances."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the conditions of a person’s life, especially the money they have","example":"changing social and political circumstances"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"situations and events that affect and influence your life and that are not in your control","example":"I know I can trust her in any circumstance."}]],["communicate","/kəˈmju:nɪkeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “communicate”.","communicate [kəˈmju:nɪkeɪt] -K3 vi. 通讯，传达；相通；交流；感染 vt. 传达；感染；显露 时态: communicated, communicating, communicates (中高研四六托宝 2672/3006)","欧陆词典释义：communicate [kəˈmju:nɪkeɪt] -K3 vi. 通讯，传达；相通；交流；感染 vt. 传达；感染；显露 时态: communicated, communicating, communicates (中高研四六托宝 2672/3006)","My natural mother has never communicate d with me...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to exchange information, news, ideas, etc. with somebody","example":"We only communicate by email."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make your ideas, feelings, thoughts, etc. known to other people so that they understand them","example":"They communicated in sign language."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have a good relationship because you are able to understand and talk about your own and other people’s thoughts, feelings, etc.","example":"Dolphins use sound to communicate with each other."}]],["compare","/kəmˈpeə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compare”.","compare [kəmˈpeə(r)] -K3 vi. 相比，匹敌；比较，区别；比拟（常与to连用） vt. 比拟，喻为；[语]构成 n. 比较 n. (Compare)人名；(意)孔帕雷 时态: compared, comparing, compares (中高研四六托雅 831/773)","欧陆词典释义：compare [kəmˈpeə(r)] -K3 vi. 相比，匹敌；比较，区别；比拟（常与to连用） vt. 比拟，喻为；[语]构成 n. 比较 n. (Compare)人名；(意)孔帕雷 时态: compared, comparing, compares (中高研四六托雅 831/773)","Compare the two illustrations in Fig 60...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to examine people or things to see how they are similar and how they are different","example":"It is interesting to compare their situation and ours."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be similar to somebody/something else, either better or worse","example":"We compared the two reports carefully."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to show or state that somebody/something is similar to somebody/something else","example":"We carefully compared the first report with the second."}]],["complex","/ˈkɒmpleks/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “complex”.","complex [ˈkɒmpleks] -K4 n. 复合体；综合设施 adj. 复杂的；合成的 (高研四六托雅 1598/1339)","欧陆词典释义：complex [ˈkɒmpleks] -K4 n. 复合体；综合设施 adj. 复杂的；合成的 (高研四六托雅 1598/1339)","in-depth coverage of today's complex issues.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"made of many different things or parts that are connected; difficult to understand","example":"complex machinery"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"containing one main part (= the root","example":"the complex structure of the human brain"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"a complex road system"}]],["concept","/ˈkɒnsept/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “concept”.","concept [ˈkɒnsept] -K3 n. 观念，概念 (高研四六托 1158/1101)","欧陆词典释义：concept [ˈkɒnsept] -K3 n. 观念，概念 (高研四六托 1158/1101)","She added that the concept of arranged marriages is misunderstood in the west.",""],["conclude","/kənˈklu:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conclude”.","conclude [kənˈklu:d] -K3 vi. 推断；断定；决定 vt. 推断；决定，作结论；结束 时态: concluded, concluding, concludes (高研四六托 1670/1687)","欧陆词典释义：conclude [kənˈklu:d] -K3 vi. 推断；断定；决定 vt. 推断；决定，作结论；结束 时态: concluded, concluding, concludes (高研四六托 1670/1687)","Larry had conclude d that he had no choice but to accept Paul's words as the truth...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to decide or believe something as a result of what you have heard or seen","example":"What do you conclude from that?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to come to an end; to bring something to an end","example":"The report concluded (that) the cheapest option was to close the laboratory."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to arrange and settle an agreement with somebody formally and finally","example":"He concluded from their remarks that they were not in favour of the plan."}]],["conduct","/kənˈdʌkt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conduct”.","conduct [kənˈdʌkt] -K4 n. 进行；行为；实施 vi. 导电；带领 vt. 管理；引导；表现 时态: conducted, conducting, conducts (高研四六托宝 1162/1792)","欧陆词典释义：conduct [kənˈdʌkt] -K4 n. 进行；行为；实施 vi. 导电；带领 vt. 管理；引导；表现 时态: conducted, conducting, conducts (高研四六托宝 1162/1792)","I decided to conduct an experiment...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to organize and/or do a particular activity","example":"to conduct an experiment/an inquiry/a survey"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to direct a group of people who are singing or playing music","example":"The negotiations have been conducted in a positive manner."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to lead or guide somebody through or around a place","example":"They conducted a vigorous campaign for a shorter working week."}]],["consequence","/ˈkɒnsɪkwəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consequence”.","consequence [ˈkɒnsɪkwəns] -K3 n. 结果；重要性；推论 (高研四六托雅宝 1626/1234)","欧陆词典释义：consequence [ˈkɒnsɪkwəns] -K3 n. 结果；重要性；推论 (高研四六托雅宝 1626/1234)","Her lawyer said she understood the consequence s of her actions and was prepared to go to jail...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a result of something that has happened","example":"This decision could have serious consequences"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"importance","example":"Two hundred people lost their jobs as a"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a game in which each player writes the first line of a story on a piece of paper and then passes it to the next player who writes the second line, and so on. Each player folds the paper so that the next player cannot see what is already written. The result is a number of crazy and often funny stories. The stories follow a pattern that always begins with the names of two people and ends with the sentence 'And the consequence was…’","example":"He drove too fast with tragic consequences."}]],["consider","/kənˈsɪdə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consider”.","consider [kənˈsɪdə(r)] -K5 vi. 考虑；认为；细想 vt. 考虑；认为；考虑到；细想 时态: considered, considering, considers (中高研四六托 394/312)","欧陆词典释义：consider [kənˈsɪdə(r)] -K5 vi. 考虑；认为；细想 vt. 考虑；认为；考虑到；细想 时态: considered, considering, considers (中高研四六托 394/312)","We don't consider our customers to be mere consumers; we consider them to be our friends...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think about something carefully, especially in order to make a decision","example":"I'd like some time to consider."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think of somebody/something in a particular way","example":"She considered her options."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think about something, especially the feelings of other people, and be influenced by it when making a decision, etc.","example":"Let us consider the facts."}]],["consistent","/kənˈsɪstənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consistent”.","consistent [kənˈsɪstənt] -3 adj. 始终如一的，一致的；坚持的 (高研四六托宝 2225/2670)","欧陆词典释义：consistent [kənˈsɪstənt] -3 adj. 始终如一的，一致的；坚持的 (高研四六托宝 2225/2670)","Becker has never been the most consistent of players anyway.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"always behaving in the same way, or having the same opinions, standards, etc.","example":"She's not very consistent in the way she treats her children."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"happening in the same way and continuing for a period of time","example":"He has been Milan's most consistent ("},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"in agreement with something; not contradicting","example":"We must be consistent in applying the rules."}]],["constitute","/ˈkɒnstɪtju:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “constitute”.","constitute [ˈkɒnstɪtju:t] -2 vt. 组成，构成；建立；任命 时态: constituted, constituting, constitutes (研六托雅宝 2887/2270)","欧陆词典释义：constitute [ˈkɒnstɪtju:t] -2 vt. 组成，构成；建立；任命 时态: constituted, constituting, constitutes (研六托雅宝 2887/2270)","Testing patients without their consent would constitute a professional and legal offence...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be considered to be something","example":"Does such an activity constitute a criminal offence?"},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to be the parts that together form something","example":"The increase in racial tension constitutes a threat to our society."},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to form a group legally or officially","example":"His action was interpreted as constituting a threat to the community."}]],["contribute","/kənˈtrɪbju:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contribute”.","contribute [kənˈtrɪbju:t] -K3 vt. 贡献，出力；投稿；捐献 vi. 贡献，出力；投稿；捐献 [ 过去式 contributed 过去分词 contributed 现在分词 contributing ] 时态: contributed, contributing, contributes (高研四六托雅 1312/1483)","欧陆词典释义：contribute [kənˈtrɪbju:t] -K3 vt. 贡献，出力；投稿；捐献 vi. 贡献，出力；投稿；捐献 [ 过去式 contributed 过去分词 contributed 现在分词 contributing ] 时态: contributed, contributing, contributes (高研四六托雅 1312/1483)","The three sons also contribute to the family business...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give something, especially money or goods, to help somebody/something","example":"We contributed £5 000 to the earthquake fund."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be one of the causes of something","example":"Would you like to contribute to our collection?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to increase, improve or add to something","example":"Do you wish to contribute?"}]],["create","/kriˈeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “create”.","create [kriˈeɪt] -K5 vt. 创造，创作；造成 时态: created, creating, creates (中高研四六雅 332/449)","欧陆词典释义：create [kriˈeɪt] -K5 vt. 创造，创作；造成 时态: created, creating, creates (中高研四六雅 332/449)","We set business free to create more jobs in Britain...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something happen or exist","example":"Scientists disagree about how the universe was created."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to produce a particular feeling or impression","example":"The main purpose of industry is to create wealth."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give somebody a particular rank or title","example":"The government plans to create more jobs for young people."}]],["culture","/ˈkʌltʃə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “culture”.","culture [ˈkʌltʃə(r)] -K4 n. 文化，文明；修养；栽培 vt. [细胞][微] 培养（等于cultivate） (中高研四六托雅 611/983)","欧陆词典释义：culture [ˈkʌltʃə(r)] -K4 n. 文化，文明；修养；栽培 vt. [细胞][微] 培养（等于cultivate） (中高研四六托雅 611/983)","There is just not enough fun and frivolity in culture today.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the customs and beliefs, art, way of life and social organization of a particular country or group","example":"European/Islamic/African/American, etc. culture"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a country, group, etc. with its own beliefs, etc.","example":"working-class culture"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"art, music, literature, etc., thought of as a group","example":"The children are taught to respect different cultures."}]],["decline","/dɪˈklaɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “decline”.","decline [dɪˈklaɪn] -K4 n. 下降；衰退；斜面 vt. 谢绝；婉拒 vi. 下降；衰落；谢绝 时态: declined, declining, declines (高研四六托雅宝 2000/2190)","欧陆词典释义：decline [dɪˈklaɪn] -K4 n. 下降；衰退；斜面 vt. 谢绝；婉拒 vi. 下降；衰落；谢绝 时态: declined, declining, declines (高研四六托雅宝 2000/2190)","The number of staff has decline d from 217,000 to 114,000...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a continuous decrease in the number, value, quality, etc. of something","example":"a rapid/sharp/gradual decline"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"urban/economic decline"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become smaller, fewer, weaker, etc.","example":"The company reported a small decline in its profits."}]],["define","/dɪˈfaɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “define”.","define [dɪˈfaɪn] -K3 vt. 定义；使明确；规定 n. (Define)人名；(英)德法恩；(葡)德菲内 时态: defined, defining, defines (研四六 1210/1053)","欧陆词典释义：define [dɪˈfaɪn] -K3 vt. 定义；使明确；规定 n. (Define)人名；(英)德法恩；(葡)德菲内 时态: defined, defining, defines (研四六 1210/1053)","We were unable to define what exactly was wrong with him...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to say or explain what the meaning of a word or phrase is","example":"The term ‘mental illness’ is difficult to define."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to describe or show something accurately","example":"Life imprisonment is defined as 60 years under state law."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show clearly a line, shape or edge","example":"It is important to clarify what is meant by"}]],["demonstrate","/ˈdemənstreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “demonstrate”.","demonstrate [ˈdemənstreɪt] -K3 vt. 证明；展示；论证 vi. 示威 时态: demonstrated, demonstrating, demonstrates (研四六托雅宝 1379/1392)","欧陆词典释义：demonstrate [ˈdemənstreɪt] -K3 vt. 证明；展示；论证 vi. 示威 时态: demonstrated, demonstrating, demonstrates (研四六托雅宝 1379/1392)","The study also demonstrate d a direct link between obesity and mortality...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show something clearly by giving proof or evidence","example":"These results demonstrate convincingly that our campaign is working."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show by your actions that you have a particular quality, feeling or opinion","example":"Let me demonstrate to you some of the difficulties we are facing."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show and explain how something works or how to do something","example":"His sudden departure had demonstrated how unreliable he was."}]],["derive","/dɪˈraɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “derive”.","derive [dɪˈraɪv] -K2 vt. 源于；得自；获得 vi. 起源 n. (Derive)人名；(法)德里夫 时态: derived, deriving, derives (研四六托雅 3051/1798)","欧陆词典释义：derive [dɪˈraɪv] -K2 vt. 源于；得自；获得 vi. 起源 n. (Derive)人名；(法)德里夫 时态: derived, deriving, derives (研四六托雅 3051/1798)","Mr Ying is one of those happy people who derive pleasure from helping others.",""],["design","/dɪˈzaɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “design”.","design [dɪˈzaɪn] -K5 n. 设计；图案 vt. 设计；计划；构思 vi. 设计 时态: designed, designing, designs (高研四六托雅 834/679)","欧陆词典释义：design [dɪˈzaɪn] -K5 n. 设计；图案 vt. 设计；计划；构思 vi. 设计 时态: designed, designing, designs (高研四六托雅 834/679)","They wanted to design a machine that was both attractive and practical.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the general arrangement of the different parts of something that is made, such as a building, book, machine, etc.","example":"The basic design of the car is very similar to that of earlier models."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the art or process of deciding how something will look, work, etc. by drawing plans, making models, etc.","example":"special new design features"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a drawing or plan from which something may be made","example":"The machine's unique design prevents it from overheating."}]],["develop","/dɪˈveləp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “develop”.","develop [dɪˈveləp] -K5 vi. 发育；生长；进化；显露 vt. 开发；进步；使成长；使显影 时态: developed, developing, develops (中高托 484/400)","欧陆词典释义：develop [dɪˈveləp] -K5 vi. 发育；生长；进化；显露 vt. 开发；进步；使成长；使显影 时态: developed, developing, develops (中高托 484/400)","As children develop , some of the most important things they learn have to do with their sense of self...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to gradually grow or become bigger, more advanced, stronger, etc.; to make something do this","example":"The child is developing normally."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think of or produce a new idea, product, etc. and make it successful","example":"The place has rapidly developed from a small fishing community into a thriving tourist resort."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to begin to have something such as a disease or a problem; to start to affect somebody/something","example":"She developed the company from nothing."}]],["distribution","/ˌdɪstrɪˈbju:ʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “distribution”.","distribution [ˌdɪstrɪˈbju:ʃn] -K3 n. 分布；分配 (四六托雅 2373/1456)","欧陆词典释义：distribution [ˌdɪstrɪˈbju:ʃn] -K3 n. 分布；分配 (四六托雅 2373/1456)","the council which controls the distribution of foreign aid...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way that something is shared or exists over a particular area or among a particular group of people","example":"the unfair distribution of wealth"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of giving or delivering something to a number of people","example":"The map shows the distribution of this species across the world."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the system of transporting and delivering goods","example":"They studied the geographical distribution of the disease."}]],["economy","/ɪˈkɒnəmi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “economy”.","economy [ɪˈkɒnəmi] -K5 n. 经济；节约；理财 n. (Economy)人名；(英)伊科诺米 (研四六雅 645/817)","欧陆词典释义：economy [ɪˈkɒnəmi] -K5 n. 经济；节约；理财 n. (Economy)人名；(英)伊科诺米 (研四六雅 645/817)","Zimbabwe boasts Africa's most industrialised economy .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the relationship between production, trade and the supply of money in a particular country or region","example":"The economy is in recession."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a country, when you are thinking about its economic system","example":"the world economy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the use of the time, money, etc. that is available in a way that avoids waste","example":"a market economy ("}]],["education","/ˌedʒuˈkeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “education”.","education [ˌedʒuˈkeɪʃn] -K5 n. 教育；培养；教育学 (中高研四托雅 376/353)","欧陆词典释义：education [ˌedʒuˈkeɪʃn] -K5 n. 教育；培养；教育学 (中高研四托雅 376/353)","They're cutting funds for education ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a process of teaching, training and learning, especially in schools or colleges, to improve knowledge and develop skills","example":"primary/elementary education"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular kind of teaching or training","example":"secondary education"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the institutions or people involved in teaching and training","example":"further/higher/post-secondary education"}]],["emphasize","/ˈemfəsaɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “emphasize”.","emphasize [ˈemfəsaɪz] -K3 vt. 强调，着重 时态: emphasized, emphasizing, emphasizes (研四六托雅 1975/3599)","欧陆词典释义：emphasize [ˈemfəsaɪz] -K3 vt. 强调，着重 时态: emphasized, emphasizing, emphasizes (研四六托雅 1975/3599)","But it's also been emphasize d that no major policy changes can be expected to come out of the meeting...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give special importance to something","example":"His speech emphasized the importance of attracting industry to the town."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something more noticeable","example":"She emphasized that their plan would mean sacrifices and hard work."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give extra force to a word or phrase when you are speaking, especially to show that it is important","example":"He emphasized how little was known about the disease."}]],["environment","/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “environment”.","environment [ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt] -K4 n. 环境，外界 (中高研四六雅 855/702)","欧陆词典释义：environment [ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt] -K4 n. 环境，外界 (中高研四六雅 855/702)","Pupils in our schools are taught in a safe, secure environment ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the conditions that affect the behaviour and development of somebody/something; the physical conditions that somebody/something exists in","example":"a pleasant working/learning environment"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the natural world in which people, animals and plants live","example":"An unhappy home environment"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the complete structure within which a user, computer or program operates","example":"They have created an environment in which productivity should flourish."}]],["establish","/ɪˈstæblɪʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “establish”.","establish [ɪˈstæblɪʃ] -K4 vi. 植物定植 vt. 建立；创办；安置 时态: established, establishing, establishes (研四六雅 896/576)","欧陆词典释义：establish [ɪˈstæblɪʃ] -K4 vi. 植物定植 vt. 建立；创办；安置 时态: established, establishing, establishes (研四六雅 896/576)","The UN has establish ed detailed criteria for who should be allowed to vote...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to start or create an organization, a system, etc. that is meant to last for a long time","example":"The committee was established in 1912."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to start having a relationship, especially a formal one, with another person, group or country","example":"The new treaty establishes a free trade zone."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to hold a position for long enough or succeed in something well enough to make people accept and respect you","example":"Let’s establish some ground rules."}]],["evaluate","/ɪˈvæljueɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “evaluate”.","evaluate [ɪˈvæljueɪt] -2 vt. 评价；估价；求…的值 vi. 评价；估价 时态: evaluated, evaluating, evaluates (高研四六托雅 2339/3168)","欧陆词典释义：evaluate [ɪˈvæljueɪt] -2 vt. 评价；估价；求…的值 vi. 评价；估价 时态: evaluated, evaluating, evaluates (高研四六托雅 2339/3168)","They will first send in trained nurses to evaluate the needs of the individual situation...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to form an opinion of the amount, value or quality of something after thinking about it carefully","example":"Our research attempts to evaluate the effectiveness of the different drugs."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 19th cent.","example":"We need to evaluate how well the policy is working."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 18th cent.","example":"It was impossible to evaluate the safety of the new drug."}]],["evidence","/ˈevɪdəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “evidence”.","evidence [ˈevɪdəns] -K4 n. 证据，证明；迹象；明显 vt. 证明 时态: evidenced, evidencing, evidences (高研四六托雅 606/456)","欧陆词典释义：evidence [ˈevɪdəns] -K4 n. 证据，证明；迹象；明显 vt. 证明 时态: evidenced, evidencing, evidences (高研四六托雅 606/456)","Ganley said he'd seen no evidence of widespread fraud...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the facts, signs or objects that make you believe that something is true","example":"There is convincing evidence of a link between exposure to sun and skin cancer."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the information that is used in court to try to prove something","example":"The room bore evidence of a struggle."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"We found further scientific evidence for this theory."}]],["factor","/ˈfæktə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “factor”.","factor [ˈfæktə(r)] -K4 n. 因素；要素；[物] 因数；代理人 vt. 把…作为因素计入；代理经营；把…分解成 vi. 做代理商 n. (Factor)人名；(英)法克特 时态: factored, factoring, factors (研四托雅 729/666)","欧陆词典释义：factor [ˈfæktə(r)] -K4 n. 因素；要素；[物] 因数；代理人 vt. 把…作为因素计入；代理经营；把…分解成 vi. 做代理商 n. (Factor)人名；(英)法克特 时态: factored, factoring, factors (研四托雅 729/666)","Physical activity is an important factor in maintaining fitness.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"one of several things that cause or influence something","example":"economic factors"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a number that divides into another number exactly","example":"The closure of the mine was the single most important"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the amount by which something increases or decreases","example":"the key/crucial/deciding factor"}]],["feature","/ˈfi:tʃə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “feature”.","feature [ˈfi:tʃə(r)] -K4 n. 特色，特征；容貌；特写或专题节目 vt. 特写；以…为特色；由…主演 vi. 起重要作用 时态: featured, featuring, features (研四六雅宝 1190/741)","欧陆词典释义：feature [ˈfi:tʃə(r)] -K4 n. 特色，特征；容貌；特写或专题节目 vt. 特写；以…为特色；由…主演 vi. 起重要作用 时态: featured, featuring, features (研四六雅宝 1190/741)","Patriotic songs have long been a feature of Kuwaiti life...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something important, interesting or typical of a place or thing","example":"An interesting feature of the city is the old market."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a part of somebody’s face such as their nose, mouth and eyes","example":"Teamwork is a key feature"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"(in newspapers, on television, etc.) a special article or programme about somebody/something","example":"Which features do you look for when choosing a car?"}]],["function","/ˈfʌŋkʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “function”.","function [ˈfʌŋkʃn] -K4 n. 功能；[数] 函数；职责；盛大的集会 vi. 运行；活动；行使职责 时态: functioned, functioning, functions (高研四六雅 1442/782)","欧陆词典释义：function [ˈfʌŋkʃn] -K4 n. 功能；[数] 函数；职责；盛大的集会 vi. 运行；活动；行使职责 时态: functioned, functioning, functions (高研四六雅 1442/782)","The main function of the merchant banks is to raise capital for industry.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a special activity or purpose of a person or thing","example":"to fulfil/perform a function"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a social event or official ceremony","example":"bodily functions"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a quantity whose value depends on the varying values of others. In the statement 2x=y, y is a function","example":"The function of the heart is to pump blood through the body."}]],["identify","/aɪˈdentɪfaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “identify”.","identify [aɪˈdentɪfaɪ] -K4 vt. 确定；鉴定；识别，辨认出；使参与；把…看成一样 vi. 确定；认同；一致 时态: identified, identifying, identifies (研四六托雅 770/757)","欧陆词典释义：identify [aɪˈdentɪfaɪ] -K4 vt. 确定；鉴定；识别，辨认出；使参与；把…看成一样 vi. 确定；认同；一致 时态: identified, identifying, identifies (研四六托雅 770/757)","There are a number of distinguishing characteristics by which you can identify a Hollywood epic...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to recognize somebody/something and be able to say who or what they are","example":"The bodies were identified as those of two suspected drug dealers."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to find or discover somebody/something","example":"She was able to identify her attacker."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make it possible to recognize who or what somebody/something is","example":"Passengers were asked to identify their own suitcases before they were put on the plane."}]],["impact","/ˈɪmpækt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “impact”.","impact [ˈɪmpækt] -K4 vi. 影响；撞击；冲突；压紧（on，upon，with） n. 影响；效果；碰撞；冲击力 vt. 挤入，压紧；撞击；对…产生影响 时态: impacted, impacting, impacts (研四六托雅宝 919/1263)","欧陆词典释义：impact [ˈɪmpækt] -K4 vi. 影响；撞击；冲突；压紧（on，upon，with） n. 影响；效果；碰撞；冲击力 vt. 挤入，压紧；撞击；对…产生影响 时态: impacted, impacting, impacts (研四六托雅宝 919/1263)","They say they expect the meeting to have a marked impact on the future of the country...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the powerful effect that something has on somebody/something","example":"the environmental impact of tourism"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the act of one object hitting another; the force with which this happens","example":"The report assesses the impact of AIDS on the gay community."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"Her speech made a profound impact on everyone."}]],["indicate","/ˈɪndɪkeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “indicate”.","indicate [ˈɪndɪkeɪt] -K4 vt. 表明；指出；预示；象征 时态: indicated, indicating, indicates (高研四六托宝 785/812)","欧陆词典释义：indicate [ˈɪndɪkeɪt] -K4 vt. 表明；指出；预示；象征 时态: indicated, indicating, indicates (高研四六托宝 785/812)","A survey of retired people has indicate d that most are independent and enjoying life...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show that something is true or exists","example":"Record profits in the retail market indicate a boom in the economy."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be a sign of something; to show that something is possible or likely","example":"A yellowing of the skin indicates jaundice."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to mention something, especially in an indirect way","example":"The article claims that an increase in crime indicates a decline in moral standards."}]],["individual","/ˌɪndɪˈvɪdʒuəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “individual”.","individual [ˌɪndɪˈvɪdʒuəl] -K4 n. 个人，个体 adj. 个人的；个别的；独特的 (研四六雅宝 762/738)","欧陆词典释义：individual [ˌɪndɪˈvɪdʒuəl] -K4 n. 个人，个体 adj. 个人的；个别的；独特的 (研四六雅宝 762/738)","They wait for the group to decide rather than making individual decisions...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"considered separately rather than as part of a group","example":"We interviewed each individual"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"connected with one person; designed for one person","example":"The minister refused to comment on individual cases."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"typical of one particular person or thing in a way that is different from others","example":"respect for individual freedom"}]],["interpret","/ɪnˈtɜ:prɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “interpret”.","interpret [ɪnˈtɜ:prɪt] -K2 vi. 解释；翻译 vt. 说明；口译 时态: interpreted, interpreting, interprets (研四六托雅 2755/2094)","欧陆词典释义：interpret [ɪnˈtɜ:prɪt] -K2 vi. 解释；翻译 vt. 说明；口译 时态: interpreted, interpreting, interprets (研四六托雅 2755/2094)","The whole speech might well be interpret ed as a coded message to the Americans...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to explain the meaning of something","example":"The students were asked to interpret the poem."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to decide that something has a particular meaning and to understand it in this way","example":"I didn't know whether to interpret her silence as acceptance or refusal."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to translate one language into another as you hear it","example":"The data can be interpreted in many different ways."}]],["involve","/ɪnˈvɒlv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “involve”.","involve [ɪnˈvɒlv] -K4 vt. 包含；牵涉；使陷于；潜心于 时态: involved, involving, involves (研四六托雅 656/419)","欧陆词典释义：involve [ɪnˈvɒlv] -K4 vt. 包含；牵涉；使陷于；潜心于 时态: involved, involving, involves (研四六托雅 656/419)","Running a kitchen involve s a great deal of discipline and speed...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"if a situation, an event or an activity involves","example":"Any investment involves an element of risk."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"if a situation, an event or an activity involves","example":"Many of the crimes involved drugs."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody take part in something","example":"The test will involve answering questions about a photograph."}]],["issue","/ˈɪʃu:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “issue”.","issue [ˈɪʃu:] -K5 n. 问题；流出；期号；发行物 vt. 发行，发布；发给；放出，排出 vi. 发行；流出；造成…结果；传下 时态: issued, issuing, issues (研四六托雅宝 248/341)","欧陆词典释义：issue [ˈɪʃu:] -K5 n. 问题；流出；期号；发行物 vt. 发行，发布；发给；放出，排出 vi. 发行；流出；造成…结果；传下 时态: issued, issuing, issues (研四六托雅宝 248/341)","Agents will raise the issue of prize-money for next year's world championships...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an important topic that people are discussing or arguing about","example":"a key/sensitive/controversial issue"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a problem or worry that somebody has with something","example":"This is a big issue"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"one of a regular series of magazines or newspapers","example":"She usually writes about environmental issues."}]],["maintain","/meɪnˈteɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “maintain”.","maintain [meɪnˈteɪn] -K4 vt. 维持；继续；维修；主张；供养 时态: maintained, maintaining, maintains (研四六托雅 922/825)","欧陆词典释义：maintain [meɪnˈteɪn] -K4 vt. 维持；继续；维修；主张；供养 时态: maintained, maintaining, maintains (研四六托雅 922/825)","The Department maintain s many close contacts with the chemical industry...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something continue at the same level, standard, etc.","example":"to maintain law and order/standards/a balance"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to keep a building, a machine, etc. in good condition by checking or repairing it regularly","example":"The two countries have always maintained close relations."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to keep stating that something is true, even though other people do not agree or do not believe it","example":"She maintained a dignified silence."}]],["method","/ˈmeθəd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “method”.","method [ˈmeθəd] -K4 n. 方法；条理；类函数 adj. 使用体验派表演方法的 (中高研四六雅 998/561)","欧陆词典释义：method [ˈmeθəd] -K4 n. 方法；条理；类函数 adj. 使用体验派表演方法的 (中高研四六雅 998/561)","The pill is the most efficient method of birth control.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular way of doing something","example":"a reliable/effective/scientific method"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality of being well planned and organized","example":"a new method of solving the problem"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"traditional/alternative methods"}]],["occur","/əˈkɜ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “occur”.","occur [əˈkɜ:(r)] -K4 vi. 发生；出现；存在 时态: occurred, occurring, occurs (高研四六托雅 756/634)","欧陆词典释义：occur [əˈkɜ:(r)] -K4 vi. 发生；出现；存在 时态: occurred, occurring, occurs (高研四六托雅 756/634)","If headaches only occur at night, lack of fresh air and oxygen is often the cause...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to happen","example":"When exactly did the incident occur?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to exist or be found somewhere","example":"Something unexpected occurred."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"Sugar occurs naturally in fruit."}]],["participate","/pɑ:ˈtɪsɪpeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “participate”.","participate [pɑ:ˈtɪsɪpeɪt] -3 vi. 参与，参加；分享 vt. 分享；分担 [ 过去式participated 过去分词participated 现在分词participating ] 时态: participated, participating, participates (高研四六托雅 1482/2783)","欧陆词典释义：participate [pɑ:ˈtɪsɪpeɪt] -3 vi. 参与，参加；分享 vt. 分享；分担 [ 过去式participated 过去分词participated 现在分词participating ] 时态: participated, participating, participates (高研四六托雅 1482/2783)","They expected him to participate in the ceremony...",""],["period","/ˈpɪəriəd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “period”.","period [ˈpɪəriəd] -K4 n. 周期，期间；时期；月经；课时；（语法学）句点，句号 adj. 某一时代的 (中高研四六托雅 617/324)","欧陆词典释义：period [ˈpɪəriəd] -K4 n. 周期，期间；时期；月经；课时；（语法学）句点，句号 adj. 某一时代的 (中高研四六托雅 617/324)","This crisis might last for a long period of time.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular length of time","example":"a period of consultation/mourning/uncertainty"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"a length of time in the life of a particular person or in the history of a particular country","example":"The factory will be closed down over a 2-year period/a period of two years."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a length of time which is a division of an era","example":"This compares with a 4% increase for the same period last year."}]],["policy","/ˈpɒləsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “policy”.","policy [ˈpɒləsi] -K5 n. 政策，方针；保险单 (中高研四六雅 388/250)","欧陆词典释义：policy [ˈpɒləsi] -K5 n. 政策，方针；保险单 (中高研四六雅 388/250)","plans which include changes in foreign policy and economic reforms.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a plan of action agreed or chosen by a political party, a business, etc.","example":"the present government’s policy on education"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a principle that you believe in that influences how you behave; a way in which you usually behave","example":"The company has adopted a"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a written statement of a contract of insurance","example":"We have tried to pursue a policy"}]],["principle","/ˈprɪnsəpl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “principle”.","principle [ˈprɪnsəpl] -K4 n. 原理，原则；主义，道义；本质，本义；根源，源泉 (高研四六宝 1341/722)","欧陆词典释义：principle [ˈprɪnsəpl] -K4 n. 原理，原则；主义，道义；本质，本义；根源，源泉 (高研四六宝 1341/722)","Buck never allowed himself to be bullied into doing anything that went against his principle s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a moral rule or a strong belief that influences your actions","example":"He has high moral principles."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a law, a rule or a theory that something is based on","example":"I refuse to lie about it; it's against my principles"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a belief that is accepted as a reason for acting or thinking in a particular way","example":"Stick to your principles"}]],["process","/ˈprəʊses/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “process”.","process [ˈprəʊses] -K5 n. 过程，进行；方法，步骤；作用；程序；推移 adj. 经过特殊加工（或处理）的 vt. 处理；加工 vi. 列队前进 时态: processed, processing, processes (高研四六托雅 391/343)","欧陆词典释义：process [ˈprəʊses] -K5 n. 过程，进行；方法，步骤；作用；程序；推移 adj. 经过特殊加工（或处理）的 vt. 处理；加工 vi. 列队前进 时态: processed, processing, processes (高研四六托雅 391/343)","There was total agreement to start the peace process as soon as possible...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a series of things that are done in order to achieve a particular result","example":"a consultation process"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a series of things that happen, especially ones that result in natural changes","example":"to begin the difficult process of reforming the education system"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a method of doing or making something, especially one that is used in industry","example":"I'm afraid getting things changed will be a slow process."}]],["require","/rɪˈkwaɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “require”.","require [rɪˈkwaɪə(r)] -K4 vt. 需要；要求；命令 时态: required, requiring, requires (中高研四六 446/321)","欧陆词典释义：require [rɪˈkwaɪə(r)] -K4 vt. 需要；要求；命令 时态: required, requiring, requires (中高研四六 446/321)","If you require further information, you should consult the registrar...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to need something; to depend on somebody/something","example":"These pets require a lot of care and attention."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody do or have something, especially because it is necessary according to a particular law or set of rules","example":"Deciphering the code requires an expert."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"This condition requires urgent treatment."}]],["research","/rɪˈsɜ:tʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “research”.","research [rɪˈsɜ:tʃ] -K5 n. 研究；调查 vt. 研究；调查 vi. 研究；调查 [ 过去式 researched 过去分词 researched 现在分词 researching ] 时态: researched, researching, researches (中高研四六雅 362/357)","欧陆词典释义：research [rɪˈsɜ:tʃ] -K5 n. 研究；调查 vt. 研究；调查 vi. 研究；调查 [ 过去式 researched 过去分词 researched 现在分词 researching ] 时态: researched, researching, researches (中高研四六雅 362/357)","65 percent of the 1987 budget went for nuclear weapons research and production.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a careful study of a subject, especially in order to discover new facts or information about it","example":"medical/historical/scientific, etc. research"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"to do/conduct/undertake research"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to study something carefully and try to discover new facts about it","example":"He has carried out extensive research into renewable energy sources."}]],["respond","/rɪˈspɒnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “respond”.","respond [rɪˈspɒnd] -K4 n. 应答；唱和 vi. 回答；作出反应；承担责任 vt. 以…回答 时态: responded, responding, responds (高研四六托 920/1313)","欧陆词典释义：respond [rɪˈspɒnd] -K4 n. 应答；唱和 vi. 回答；作出反应；承担责任 vt. 以…回答 时态: responded, responding, responds (高研四六托 920/1313)","They are likely to respond positively to the President's request for aid...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give a spoken or written answer to somebody/something","example":"I asked him his name, but he didn't respond."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to do something as a reaction to something that somebody has said or done","example":"She never responded to my letter."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to react quickly or in the correct way to something/somebody","example":"More than fifty people responded to the advertisement."}]],["significant","/sɪgˈnɪfɪkənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “significant”.","significant [sɪgˈnɪfɪkənt] -K4 n. 象征；有意义的事物 adj. 重大的；有效的；有意义的；值得注意的；意味深长的 (研四六托雅宝 719/841)","欧陆词典释义：significant [sɪgˈnɪfɪkənt] -K4 n. 象征；有意义的事物 adj. 重大的；有效的；有意义的；值得注意的；意味深长的 (研四六托雅宝 719/841)","A small but significant number of 11-year-olds are illiterate.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"large or important enough to have an effect or to be noticed","example":"a highly significant discovery"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a particular meaning","example":"The results of the experiment are not statistically significant"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a special or secret meaning that is not understood by everyone","example":"There are no significant differences between the two groups of students."}]],["source","/sɔ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “source”.","source [sɔ:s] -K4 n. 来源；水源；原始资料 n. (Source)人名；(法)苏尔斯 时态: sourced, sourcing, sources (研四六雅 597/633)","欧陆词典释义：source [sɔ:s] -K4 n. 来源；水源；原始资料 n. (Source)人名；(法)苏尔斯 时态: sourced, sourcing, sources (研四六雅 597/633)","over 40 per cent of British adults use television as their major source of information about the arts...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place, person or thing that you get something from","example":"renewable energy sources"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person, book or document that provides information, especially for study, a piece of written work or news","example":"Your local library will be a useful source of"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person or thing that causes something, especially a problem","example":"What is their main source of income?"}]],["theory","/ˈθɪəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “theory”.","theory [ˈθɪəri] -K4 n. 理论；原理；学说；推测 (高研四六雅 918/596)","欧陆词典释义：theory [ˈθɪəri] -K4 n. 理论；原理；学说；推测 (高研四六雅 918/596)","Marx produced a new theory about historical change based upon conflict between competing groups...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a formal set of ideas that is intended to explain why something happens or exists","example":"According to the theory of relativity, nothing can travel faster than light."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the principles on which a particular subject is based","example":"The debate is centred around two conflicting theories."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an opinion or idea that somebody believes is true but that is not proved","example":"the theory and practice of language teaching"}]],["academic","/ˌækəˈdemɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “academic”.","academic [ˌækəˈdemɪk] -K3 n. 大学生，大学教师；学者 adj. 学术的；理论的；学院的 (高研四六托雅宝 1465/1941)","欧陆词典释义：academic [ˌækəˈdemɪk] -K3 n. 大学生，大学教师；学者 adj. 学术的；理论的；学院的 (高研四六托雅宝 1465/1941)","Their academic standards are high...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with education, especially studying in schools and universities","example":"The students return in October for the start of the new academic year."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"involving a lot of reading and studying rather than practical or technical skills","example":"high/low academic standards"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"good at subjects involving a lot of reading and studying","example":"an academic career"}]],["achieve","/əˈtʃi:v/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “achieve”.","achieve [əˈtʃi:v] -K4 vt. 取得；获得；实现；成功 vi. 达到预期的目的，实现预期的结果，如愿以偿 时态: achieved, achieving, achieves (中高研四六托雅 1152/592)","欧陆词典释义：achieve [əˈtʃi:v] -K4 vt. 取得；获得；实现；成功 vi. 达到预期的目的，实现预期的结果，如愿以偿 时态: achieved, achieving, achieves (中高研四六托雅 1152/592)","There are many who will work hard to achieve these goals...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to succeed in reaching a particular goal, status or standard, especially by making an effort for a long time","example":"He had finally achieved success."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to succeed in doing something or causing something to happen","example":"They could not achieve their target of less than 3% inflation."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be successful","example":"I haven't achieved very much today."}]],["acquire","/əˈkwaɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “acquire”.","acquire [əˈkwaɪə(r)] -K3 vt. 获得；取得；学到；捕获 时态: acquired, acquiring, acquires (高研四六托雅 2063/1407)","欧陆词典释义：acquire [əˈkwaɪə(r)] -K3 vt. 获得；取得；学到；捕获 时态: acquired, acquiring, acquires (高研四六托雅 2063/1407)","General Motors acquire d a 50% stake in Saab for about $400m...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to gain something by your own efforts, ability or behaviour","example":"She has acquired a good knowledge of English."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to obtain something by buying or being given it","example":"How long will it take to acquire the necessary skills?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"He has acquired a reputation for dishonesty."}]],["affect","/əˈfekt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “affect”.","affect [əˈfekt] -K4 n. 情感；引起感情的因素 vt. 影响；感染；感动；假装 vi. 倾向；喜欢 时态: affected, affecting, affects (高研四六托雅 963/754)","欧陆词典释义：affect [əˈfekt] -K4 n. 情感；引起感情的因素 vt. 影响；感染；感动；假装 vi. 倾向；喜欢 时态: affected, affecting, affects (高研四六托雅 963/754)","Nicotine adversely affect s the functioning of the heart and arteries...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to produce a change in somebody/something","example":"How will these changes affect us?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to attack somebody or a part of the body; to make somebody become ill/sick","example":"Your opinion will not affect my decision."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody have strong feelings of sadness, pity, etc.","example":"The south of the country was worst affected by the drought."}]],["alternative","/ɔ:lˈtɜ:nətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “alternative”.","alternative [ɔ:lˈtɜ:nətɪv] -K4 n. 二中择一；供替代的选择 adj. 供选择的；选择性的；交替的 (高研四六托雅 2073/1752)","欧陆词典释义：alternative [ɔ:lˈtɜ:nətɪv] -K4 n. 二中择一；供替代的选择 adj. 供选择的；选择性的；交替的 (高研四六托雅 2073/1752)","New ways to treat arthritis may provide an alternative to painkillers.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that you can choose to do or have out of two or more possibilities","example":"We can agree to their terms or else pull out of the deal completely: those are the two alternatives."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"mid 16th cent.","example":"We had no alternative but to"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that can be used instead of something else","example":"There is a vegetarian alternative on the menu every day."}]],["apparent","/əˈpærənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “apparent”.","apparent [əˈpærənt] -K3 adj. 显然的；表面上的 (高研四六雅 2502/1770)","欧陆词典释义：apparent [əˈpærənt] -K3 adj. 显然的；表面上的 (高研四六雅 2502/1770)","I was a bit depressed by our apparent lack of progress...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"easy to see or understand","example":"Their devotion was apparent."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that seems to be real or true but may not be","example":"Then, for no apparent reason"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"It was apparent from her face that she was really upset."}]],["available","/əˈveɪləbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “available”.","available [əˈveɪləbl] -K5 adj. 可获得的；可购得的；可找到的；有空的 (中高研四六托雅宝 622/334)","欧陆词典释义：available [əˈveɪləbl] -K5 adj. 可获得的；可购得的；可找到的；有空的 (中高研四六托雅宝 622/334)","Since 1978, the amount of money available to buy books has fallen by 17%...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that you can get, buy or find","example":"available resources/facilities"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"free to see or talk to people","example":"readily/freely/publicly/generally available"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Tickets are available free of charge from the school."}]],["calculate","/ˈkælkjuleɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “calculate”.","calculate [ˈkælkjuleɪt] -K2 vt. 计算；预测；认为；打算 vi. 计算；以为；作打算 时态: calculated, calculating, calculates (高研四托 3039/2168)","欧陆词典释义：calculate [ˈkælkjuleɪt] -K2 vt. 计算；预测；认为；打算 vi. 计算；以为；作打算 时态: calculated, calculating, calculates (高研四托 3039/2168)","From this you can calculate the total mass in the Galaxy...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to use numbers to find out a total number, amount, distance, etc.","example":"Use the formula to calculate the volume of the container."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to guess something or form an opinion by using all the information available","example":"Benefit is calculated on the basis of average weekly earnings."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"We haven’t really calculated the cost of the vacation yet."}]],["category","/ˈkætəgəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “category”.","category [ˈkætəgəri] -K3 n. 种类，分类；[数] 范畴 (高研六托雅宝 1461/1419)","欧陆词典释义：category [ˈkætəgəri] -K3 n. 种类，分类；[数] 范畴 (高研六托雅宝 1461/1419)","This book clearly falls into the category of fictionalised autobiography...",""],["chapter","/ˈtʃæptə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “chapter”.","chapter [ˈtʃæptə(r)] -K4 n. 章，回；（俱乐部、协会等的）分会；人生或历史上的重要时期 vt. 把…分成章节 (高研四六雅 2976/593)","欧陆词典释义：chapter [ˈtʃæptə(r)] -K4 n. 章，回；（俱乐部、协会等的）分会；人生或历史上的重要时期 vt. 把…分成章节 (高研四六雅 2976/593)","Chromium supplements were used successfully in the treatment of diabetes (see Chapter 4)...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a separate section of a book, usually with a number or title","example":"I've just finished Chapter 3."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a period of time in a person’s life or in history","example":"in the previous/next/last chapter"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"all the priests of a cathedral","example":"Have you read the chapter on the legal system?"}]],["commission","/kəˈmɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “commission”.","commission [kəˈmɪʃn] -K4 n. 委员会；佣金；犯；委任；委任状 vt. 委任；使服役；委托制作 时态: commissioned, commissioning, commissions (研四六托雅宝 2379/898)","欧陆词典释义：commission [kəˈmɪʃn] -K4 n. 委员会；佣金；犯；委任；委任状 vt. 委任；使服役；委托制作 时态: commissioned, commissioning, commissions (研四六托雅宝 2379/898)","The Ministry of Agriculture commission ed a study into low-input farming...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official group of people who have been given responsibility to control something, or to find out about something, usually for the government","example":"the European Commission"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an amount of money that is paid to somebody for selling goods and which increases with the amount of goods that are sold","example":"The government has set up a commission of inquiry"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an amount of money that is charged by a bank, etc. for providing a particular service","example":"a commission on human rights"}]],["compensate","/ˈkɒmpenseɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compensate”.","compensate [ˈkɒmpenseɪt] -2 vt. 补偿，赔偿；付报酬 vi. 补偿，赔偿；抵消 时态: compensated, compensating, compensates (高研六托雅宝 5037/4464)","欧陆词典释义：compensate [ˈkɒmpenseɪt] -2 vt. 补偿，赔偿；付报酬 vi. 补偿，赔偿；抵消 时态: compensated, compensating, compensates (高研六托雅宝 5037/4464)","The official promise to compensate people for the price rise clearly hadn't been worked out properly...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to provide something good to balance or reduce the bad effects of damage, loss, etc.","example":"Nothing can compensate for the loss of a loved one."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to pay somebody money because they have suffered some damage, loss, injury, etc.","example":"Her lawyers say she should be compensated for the suffering she had been caused."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"His voice doesn’t have much range but he compensates with clever lyrics."}]],["concentrate","/ˈkɒnsntreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “concentrate”.","concentrate [ˈkɒnsntreɪt] -K3 n. 浓缩，精选；浓缩液 vi. 集中；浓缩；全神贯注；聚集 vt. 集中；浓缩 时态: concentrated, concentrating, concentrates (高研四六雅宝 2358/1341)","欧陆词典释义：concentrate [ˈkɒnsntreɪt] -K3 n. 浓缩，精选；浓缩液 vi. 集中；浓缩；全神贯注；聚集 vt. 集中；浓缩 时态: concentrated, concentrating, concentrates (高研四六雅宝 2358/1341)","It was up to him to concentrate on his studies and make something of himself...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give all your attention to something and not think about anything else","example":"I can't concentrate with all that noise going on."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to bring something together in one place","example":"Nothing concentrates the mind"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to increase the strength of a substance by reducing its volume, for example by boiling it","example":"I decided to concentrate"}]],["context","/ˈkɒntekst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “context”.","context [ˈkɒntekst] -K3 n. 环境；上下文；来龙去脉 (研六托雅宝 1427/1019)","欧陆词典释义：context [ˈkɒntekst] -K3 n. 环境；上下文；来龙去脉 (研六托雅宝 1427/1019)","We are doing this work in the context of reforms in the economic, social and cultural spheres.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the situation in which something happens and that helps you to understand it","example":"This speech needs to be set in the context of"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the words that come just before and after a word, phrase or statement and help you to understand its meaning","example":"His decision can only be understood in context"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Such databases are being used in a wide range of contexts."}]],["contract","/ˈkɒntrækt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contract”.","contract [ˈkɒntrækt] -K4 n. 合同；婚约 vt. 感染；订约；使缩短 vi. 收缩；感染；订约 时态: contracted, contracting, contracts (研四六托雅宝 1269/628)","欧陆词典释义：contract [ˈkɒntrækt] -K4 n. 合同；婚约 vt. 感染；订约；使缩短 vi. 收缩；感染；订约 时态: contracted, contracting, contracts (研四六托雅宝 1269/628)","The company won a prestigious contract for work on Europe's tallest building...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official written agreement","example":"a contract of employment"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an agreement to kill somebody for money","example":"a research contract"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"to enter into/make/sign a contract"}]],["contrast","/ˈkɒntrɑ:st/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contrast”.","contrast [ˈkɒntrɑ:st] -K3 n. 对比；差别；对照物 vt. 使对比；使与…对照 vi. 对比；形成对照 时态: contrasted, contrasting, contrasts (研四六托雅宝 1762/1451)","欧陆词典释义：contrast [ˈkɒntrɑ:st] -K3 n. 对比；差别；对照物 vt. 使对比；使与…对照 vi. 对比；形成对照 时态: contrasted, contrasting, contrasts (研四六托雅宝 1762/1451)","the contrast between town and country...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a difference between two or more people or things that you can see clearly when they are compared or put close together; the fact of comparing two or more things in order to show the differences between them","example":"There is an obvious contrast between the cultures of East and West."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person or thing that is clearly different from somebody/something else","example":"The company lost $7 million this quarter in contrast to"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"differences in colour or in light and dark, used in photographs and paintings to create a special effect","example":"The situation when we arrived was in marked contrast"}]],["criterion","/kraɪˈtɪəriən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “criterion”.","criterion [kraɪˈtɪəriən] -K2 n. （批评判断的）标准；准则；规范；准据 (高研六雅宝 -/1799)","欧陆词典释义：criterion [kraɪˈtɪəriən] -K2 n. （批评判断的）标准；准则；规范；准据 (高研六雅宝 -/1799)","The most important criterion for entry is that applicants must design and make their own work...",""],["data","/ˈdeɪtə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “data”.","data [ˈdeɪtə] -K4 n. 数据（datum的复数）；资料 n. (Data)人名；(日)驮太 (姓)；(印、葡)达塔 原型: data 是 datum 的复数 (高研四雅 559/552)","欧陆词典释义：data [ˈdeɪtə] -K4 n. 数据（datum的复数）；资料 n. (Data)人名；(日)驮太 (姓)；(印、葡)达塔 原型: data 是 datum 的复数 (高研四雅 559/552)","The study was based on data from 2,100 women...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"facts or information, especially when examined and used to find out things or to make decisions","example":"This data was collected from 69 countries."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"information that is stored by a computer","example":"the analysis/interpretation of the data"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"raw data ("}]],["debate","/dɪˈbeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “debate”.","debate [dɪˈbeɪt] -K4 n. 辩论；辩论会 vt. 辩论，争论，讨论 vi. 辩论，争论，讨论 时态: debated, debating, debates (高研四六托宝 1082/1210)","欧陆词典释义：debate [dɪˈbeɪt] -K4 n. 辩论；辩论会 vt. 辩论，争论，讨论 vi. 辩论，争论，讨论 时态: debated, debating, debates (高研四六托宝 1082/1210)","An intense debate is going on within the Israeli government...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a formal discussion of an issue at a public meeting or in a parliament. In a debate","example":"a debate on abortion"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an argument or a discussion expressing different opinions","example":"The minister opened the debate ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"The motion under debate"}]],["despite","/dɪˈspaɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “despite”.","despite [dɪˈspaɪt] -K4 prep. 尽管，不管 n. 轻视；憎恨；侮辱 (研四六 742/686)","欧陆词典释义：despite [dɪˈspaɪt] -K4 prep. 尽管，不管 n. 轻视；憎恨；侮辱 (研四六 742/686)","Despite a thorough investigation, no trace of Dr Southwell has been found...",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"used to show that something happened or is true although something else might have happened to prevent it","example":"Her voice was shaking despite all her efforts to control it."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"used to show that somebody did not intend to do the thing mentioned","example":"Despite applying for hundreds of jobs, he is still out of work."},{"pos":"preposition","definition":"Middle English","example":"She was good at physics despite the fact that"}]],["dimension","/daɪˈmenʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dimension”.","dimension [daɪˈmenʃn] -2 n. 方面;[数] 维；尺寸；次元；容积 vt. 标出尺寸 adj. 规格的 时态: dimensioned, dimensioning, dimensions (高研四六托雅宝 2420/2699)","欧陆词典释义：dimension [daɪˈmenʃn] -2 n. 方面;[数] 维；尺寸；次元；容积 vt. 标出尺寸 adj. 规格的 时态: dimensioned, dimensioning, dimensions (高研四六托雅宝 2420/2699)","There is a political dimension to the accusations...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a measurement in space, for example the height, width or length of something","example":"We measured the dimensions of the kitchen."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the size and extent of a situation","example":"computer design tools that work in three dimensions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an aspect, or way of looking at or thinking about something","example":"a problem of considerable dimensions"}]],["domestic","/dəˈmestɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “domestic”.","domestic [dəˈmestɪk] -K4 n. 国货；佣人 adj. 国内的；家庭的；驯养的；一心只管家务的 (研四六托雅 1547/1381)","欧陆词典释义：domestic [dəˈmestɪk] -K4 n. 国货；佣人 adj. 国内的；家庭的；驯养的；一心只管家务的 (研四六托雅 1547/1381)","over 100 domestic flights a day to 15 UK destinations.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"of or inside a particular country; not foreign or international","example":"domestic affairs/politics"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used in the home; connected with the home or family","example":"domestic flights"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"liking home life; enjoying or good at cooking, cleaning the house, etc.","example":"Output consists of both exports and sales on the domestic market."}]],["element","/ˈelɪmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “element”.","element [ˈelɪmənt] -K4 n. 元素；要素；原理；成分；自然环境 n. (Element)人名；(德)埃勒门特；(英)埃利门特 (研四六托 1214/843)","欧陆词典释义：element [ˈelɪmənt] -K4 n. 元素；要素；原理；成分；自然环境 n. (Element)人名；(德)埃勒门特；(英)埃利门特 (研四六托 1214/843)","The exchange of prisoners of war was one of the key element s of the UN's peace plan.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a necessary or typical part of something","example":"Cost was a key element"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small amount of a quality or feeling","example":"The story has all the elements of a soap opera."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of people who form a part of a larger group or society","example":"Customer relations is an important element of the job."}]],["eliminate","/ɪˈlɪmɪneɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “eliminate”.","eliminate [ɪˈlɪmɪneɪt] -3 vt. 消除；排除 时态: eliminated, eliminating, eliminates (研四六托雅宝 1838/3110)","欧陆词典释义：eliminate [ɪˈlɪmɪneɪt] -3 vt. 消除；排除 时态: eliminated, eliminating, eliminates (研四六托雅宝 1838/3110)","The Sex Discrimination Act has not eliminate d discrimination in employment...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to remove or get rid of something/somebody","example":"Credit cards eliminate the need to carry a lot of cash."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to defeat a person or a team so that they no longer take part in a competition, etc.","example":"The police have eliminated two suspects from their investigation."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to kill somebody, especially an enemy or opponent","example":"This diet claims to eliminate toxins from the body."}]],["emerge","/iˈmɜ:dʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “emerge”.","emerge [iˈmɜ:dʒ] -K4 vi. 浮现；摆脱；暴露 时态: emerged, emerging, emerges (研四六托雅 1300/1252)","欧陆词典释义：emerge [iˈmɜ:dʒ] -K4 vi. 浮现；摆脱；暴露 时态: emerged, emerging, emerges (研四六托雅 1300/1252)","Richard was waiting outside the door as she emerge d...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to come out of a dark, confined or hidden place.","example":"The swimmer emerged from the lake."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become known","example":"She finally emerged from her room at noon."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to start to exist; to appear or become known","example":"He emerged from the shadows."}]],["estimate","/ˈestɪmət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “estimate”.","estimate [ˈestɪmət] -K4 n. 估计，估价；判断，看法 vt. 估计，估量；判断，评价 vi. 估计，估价 时态: estimated, estimating, estimates (研四六托雅 1798/1826)","欧陆词典释义：estimate [ˈestɪmət] -K4 n. 估计，估价；判断，看法 vt. 估计，估量；判断，评价 vi. 估计，估价 时态: estimated, estimating, estimates (研四六托雅 1798/1826)","Try to estimate how many steps it will take to get to a close object...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a judgement that you make without having the exact details or figures about the size, amount, cost, etc. of something","example":"I can give you a rough estimate"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a statement of how much a piece of work will probably cost","example":"a ballpark estimate"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"official government estimates of traffic growth over the next decade"}]],["exceed","/ɪkˈsi:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “exceed”.","exceed [ɪkˈsi:d] -2 vt. 超过；胜过 vi. 超过其他 时态: exceeded, exceeding, exceeds (研四六托雅宝 3281/2718)","欧陆词典释义：exceed [ɪkˈsi:d] -2 vt. 超过；胜过 vi. 超过其他 时态: exceeded, exceeding, exceeds (研四六托雅宝 3281/2718)","Its research budget exceed s $700 million a year...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be greater than a particular number or amount","example":"The price will not exceed £100."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to do more than the law or an order, etc. allows you to do","example":"His achievements have exceeded expectations"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"She was exceeding the speed limit ("}]],["exclude","/ɪkˈsklu:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “exclude”.","exclude [ɪkˈsklu:d] -K2 vt. 排除；排斥；拒绝接纳；逐出 时态: excluded, excluding, excludes (研四六托雅宝 3470/1940)","欧陆词典释义：exclude [ɪkˈsklu:d] -K2 vt. 排除；排斥；拒绝接纳；逐出 时态: excluded, excluding, excludes (研四六托雅宝 3470/1940)","The Academy exclude d women from its classes...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to deliberately not include something in what you are doing or considering","example":"The cost of borrowing has been excluded from the inflation figures."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to prevent somebody/something from entering a place or taking part in something","example":"Try excluding fat from your diet."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to decide that something is not possible","example":"Buses run every hour, Sundays excluded."}]],["export","/ˈekspɔ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “export”.","export [ˈekspɔ:t] -K4 n. 输出，出口；出口商品 vt. 输出，出口 vi. 输出物资 时态: exported, exporting, exports (高研四雅 3456/2231)","欧陆词典释义：export [ˈekspɔ:t] -K4 n. 输出，出口；出口商品 vt. 输出，出口 vi. 输出物资 时态: exported, exporting, exports (高研四雅 3456/2231)","The nation also export s beef...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to sell and send goods to another country","example":"The islands export sugar and fruit."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to introduce an idea or activity to another country or area","example":"90% of the engines are exported to Europe."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to send data to another program, changing its form so that the other program can read it","example":"American pop music has been exported around the world."}]],["external","/ɪkˈstɜ:nl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “external”.","external [ɪkˈstɜ:nl] -2 n. 外部；外观；外面 adj. 外部的；表面的；[药] 外用的；外国的；外面的 (研四六托雅 2864/1870)","欧陆词典释义：external [ɪkˈstɜ:nl] -2 n. 外部；外观；外面 adj. 外部的；表面的；[药] 外用的；外国的；外面的 (研四六托雅 2864/1870)","a much reduced heat loss through external walls.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with or located on the outside of something/somebody","example":"the external walls of the building"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"happening or coming from outside a place, an organization, your particular situation, etc.","example":"The lotion is for external use"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"coming from or arranged by somebody from outside a school, a university or an organization","example":"A combination of internal and external factors caused the company to close down."}]],["finance","/ˈfaɪnæns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “finance”.","finance [ˈfaɪnæns] -K4 n. 财政，财政学；金融 vt. 负担经费，供给…经费 vi. 筹措资金 n. (Finance)人名；(法)菲南斯 时态: financed, financing, finances (高研四六托雅 2808/1515)","欧陆词典释义：finance [ˈfaɪnæns] -K4 n. 财政，财政学；金融 vt. 负担经费，供给…经费 vi. 筹措资金 n. (Finance)人名；(法)菲南斯 时态: financed, financing, finances (高研四六托雅 2808/1515)","The fund has been used largely to finance the construction of federal prisons...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"money used to run a business, an activity or a project","example":"Finance for education comes from taxpayers."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the activity of managing money, especially by a government or commercial organization","example":"The project will only go ahead if they can raise the necessary finance."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the money available to a person, an organization or a country; the way this money is managed","example":"the Minister of Finance"}]],["framework","/ˈfreɪmwɜ:k/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “framework”.","framework [ˈfreɪmwɜ:k] -2 n. 框架，骨架；结构，构架 (高研四六托雅 2968/2177)","欧陆词典释义：framework [ˈfreɪmwɜ:k] -2 n. 框架，骨架；结构，构架 (高研四六托雅 2968/2177)"," within the framework of federal regulations.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the parts of a building or an object that support its weight and give it shape","example":"built on a wooden/metal framework"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a set of beliefs, ideas or rules that is used as the basis for making judgements, decisions, etc.","example":"the structure of the building/​human body"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the structure of a particular system","example":"the social structure of society"}]],["gender","/ˈdʒendə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “gender”.","gender [ˈdʒendə(r)] -2 n. 性；性别；性交 vt. 生（过去式gendered，过去分词gendered，现在分词gendering，第三人称单数genders，形容词genderless） (研雅 1824/3608)","欧陆词典释义：gender [ˈdʒendə(r)] -2 n. 性；性别；性交 vt. 生（过去式gendered，过去分词gendered，现在分词gendering，第三人称单数genders，形容词genderless） (研雅 1824/3608)","Women are sometimes denied opportunities solely because of their gender .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of being male or female, especially when considered with reference to social and cultural differences, not differences in biology","example":"issues of class, race and gender"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"each of the classes ( masculine","example":"traditional concepts of gender"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"gender differences/relations/roles"}]],["goal","/gəʊl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “goal”.","goal [gəʊl] -K4 n. 目标；球门，得分数；终点 vi. 攻门，射门得分 (高研四六托雅 681/930)","欧陆词典释义：goal [gəʊl] -K4 n. 目标；球门，得分数；终点 vi. 攻门，射门得分 (高研四六托雅 681/930)","David Seaman was back in the Arsenal goal after breaking a knuckle.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a frame with a net into which players must kick or hit the ball in order to score a point","example":"He headed the ball into an open goal ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of kicking or hitting the ball into the goal","example":"Who is in goal"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that you hope to achieve","example":"The winning goal"}]],["grant","/grɑ:nt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “grant”.","grant [grɑ:nt] -K4 n. 拨款；[法] 授予物 vt. 授予；允许；承认 vi. 同意 n. (Grant)人名；(瑞典、葡、西、俄、罗、英、塞、德、意)格兰特；(法)格朗 时态: granted, granting, grants (研四六雅宝 1907/1395)","欧陆词典释义：grant [grɑ:nt] -K4 n. 拨款；[法] 授予物 vt. 授予；允许；承认 vi. 同意 n. (Grant)人名；(瑞典、葡、西、俄、罗、英、塞、德、意)格兰特；(法)格朗 时态: granted, granting, grants (研四六雅宝 1907/1395)","They'd got a special grant to encourage research...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to agree to give somebody what they ask for, especially formal or legal permission to do something","example":"My request was granted."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to admit that something is true, although you may not like or agree with it","example":"I was granted permission to visit the palace."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"She was granted a divorce."}]],["illustrate","/ˈɪləstreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “illustrate”.","illustrate [ˈɪləstreɪt] -K3 vi. 举例 vt. 阐明，举例说明；图解 时态: illustrated, illustrating, illustrates (研四六托雅宝 2348/1676)","欧陆词典释义：illustrate [ˈɪləstreɪt] -K3 vi. 举例 vt. 阐明，举例说明；图解 时态: illustrated, illustrating, illustrates (研四六托雅宝 2348/1676)","The example of the United States illustrate s this point...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to use pictures, photographs, diagrams, etc. in a book, etc.","example":"an illustrated textbook"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make the meaning of something clearer by using examples, pictures, etc.","example":"His lecture was illustrated with photos taken during the expedition."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show that something is true or that a situation exists","example":"To illustrate my point"}]],["immigrate","/ˈɪmɪgreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “immigrate”.","immigrate [ˈɪmɪgreɪt] vi. 移入 vt. 使移居入境 时态: immigrated, immigrating, immigrates (四六托 13831/-)","欧陆词典释义：immigrate [ˈɪmɪgreɪt] vi. 移入 vt. 使移居入境 时态: immigrated, immigrating, immigrates (四六托 13831/-)","a Russian-born professor who had immigrate d to the United States...",""],["implement","/ˈɪmplɪment/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “implement”.","implement [ˈɪmplɪment] -3 n. 工具，器具；手段 vt. 实施，执行；实现，使生效 时态: implemented, implementing, implements (研四六托雅宝 2285/2149)","欧陆词典释义：implement [ˈɪmplɪment] -3 n. 工具，器具；手段 vt. 实施，执行；实现，使生效 时态: implemented, implementing, implements (研四六托雅宝 2285/2149)","The government promised to implement a new system to control financial loan institutions...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something that has been officially decided start to happen or be used","example":"to implement changes/decisions/policies/reforms"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"A new work programme for young people will be implemented."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a tool or an instrument, often one that is quite simple and that is used outdoors","example":"It’s a simple, easily implemented system."}]],["implication","/ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “implication”.","implication [ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn] -K3 n. 含义；暗示；牵连，卷入；可能的结果，影响 (研四六托宝 2434/1627)","欧陆词典释义：implication [ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn] -K3 n. 含义；暗示；牵连，卷入；可能的结果，影响 (研四六托宝 2434/1627)","The Attorney General was aware of the political implication s of his decision to prosecute...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a possible effect or result of an action or a decision","example":"They failed to consider the wider implications of their actions."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that is suggested or indirectly stated (","example":"The development of the site will have implications for"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of being involved, or of involving somebody, in something, especially a crime","example":"The implication in his article is that being a housewife is greatly inferior to every other occupation."}]],["income","/ˈɪnkʌm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “income”.","income [ˈɪnkʌm] -K4 n. 收入，收益；所得 (高研四六 1138/744)","欧陆词典释义：income [ˈɪnkʌm] -K4 n. 收入，收益；所得 (高研四六 1138/744)","Many families on low income s will be unable to afford to buy their own home...",""],["internal","/ɪnˈtɜ:nl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “internal”.","internal [ɪnˈtɜ:nl] -K3 n. 内脏；本质 adj. 内部的；里面的；体内的；（机构）内部的 (研四六托雅 1728/1418)","欧陆词典释义：internal [ɪnˈtɜ:nl] -K3 n. 内脏；本质 adj. 内部的；里面的；体内的；（机构）内部的 (研四六托雅 1728/1418)","The country stepped up internal security...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with the inside of something","example":"the internal structure of a building"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with the inside of your body","example":"internal doors"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"involving or concerning only the people who are part of a particular organization rather than people from outside it","example":"internal organs/injuries"}]],["legal","/ˈli:gl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “legal”.","legal [ˈli:gl] -K4 adj. 法律的；合法的；法定的；依照法律的 n. (Legal)人名；(法)勒加尔 (高研四六托雅 883/764)","欧陆词典释义：legal [ˈli:gl] -K4 adj. 法律的；合法的；法定的；依照法律的 n. (Legal)人名；(法)勒加尔 (高研四六托雅 883/764)","He vowed to take legal action.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with the law","example":"the legal profession/system"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"allowed or required by law","example":"to take/seek legal advice"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"a legal adviser"}]],["major","/ˈmeɪdʒə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “major”.","major [ˈmeɪdʒə(r)] -K5 adj. 主要的；重要的；主修的；较多的 n. [人类] 成年人；主修科目；陆军少校 vi. 主修 n. (Major)人名；(西)马霍尔；(法)马若尔；(捷、德、塞、瑞典)马约尔；(英)梅杰 时态: majored, majoring, majors (高研四六托雅 444/392)","欧陆词典释义：major [ˈmeɪdʒə(r)] -K5 adj. 主要的；重要的；主修的；较多的 n. [人类] 成年人；主修科目；陆军少校 vi. 主修 n. (Major)人名；(西)马霍尔；(法)马若尔；(捷、德、塞、瑞典)马约尔；(英)梅杰 时态: majored, majoring, majors (高研四六托雅 444/392)","The major factor in the decision to stay or to leave was usually professional...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"very large or important","example":"a major road"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"serious","example":"major international companies"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"based on a scale","example":"to play a major role in something"}]],["minor","/ˈmaɪnə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “minor”.","minor [ˈmaɪnə(r)] -K3 adj. 未成年的；次要的；较小的；小调的；二流的 n. 未成年人；小调；副修科目 vi. 副修 n. (Minor)人名；(英)迈纳；(德、法、波、俄)米诺尔 (研四六 2610/1912)","欧陆词典释义：minor [ˈmaɪnə(r)] -K3 adj. 未成年的；次要的；较小的；小调的；二流的 n. 未成年人；小调；副修科目 vi. 副修 n. (Minor)人名；(英)迈纳；(德、法、波、俄)米诺尔 (研四六 2610/1912)","She is known in Italy for a number of minor roles in films...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not very large, important or serious","example":"a minor road"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"based on a scale","example":"minor injuries"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"to undergo minor surgery"}]],["negative","/ˈnegətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “negative”.","negative [ˈnegətɪv] -K3 adj. [数] 负的；消极的；否定的；阴性的 n. 否定；负数；[摄] 底片 vt. 否定；拒绝 时态: negatived, negativing, negatives (研四六托雅 1470/2015)","欧陆词典释义：negative [ˈnegətɪv] -K3 adj. [数] 负的；消极的；否定的；阴性的 n. 否定；负数；[摄] 底片 vt. 否定；拒绝 时态: negatived, negativing, negatives (研四六托雅 1470/2015)","The news from overseas is overwhelmingly negative ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"bad or harmful","example":"The crisis had a negative effect on"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"considering only the bad side of something/somebody; lacking enthusiasm or hope","example":"The whole experience was definitely more positive than negative."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"expressing the answer ‘no’","example":"Scientists have a fairly negative attitude"}]],["network","/ˈnetwɜ:k/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “network”.","network [ˈnetwɜ:k] -K4 n. 网络；广播网；网状物 时态: networked, networking, networks (高研四六雅 882/1102)","欧陆词典释义：network [ˈnetwɜ:k] -K4 n. 网络；广播网；网状物 时态: networked, networking, networks (高研四六雅 882/1102)","Strasbourg, with its rambling network of medieval streets...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a complicated system of roads, lines, tubes, nerves, etc. that cross each other and are connected to each other","example":"a rail/road/canal network"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a closely connected group of people, companies, etc. that exchange information, etc.","example":"a network of veins"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a number of computers and other devices that are connected together so that equipment and information can be shared","example":"a communications/distribution network"}]],["objective","/əbˈdʒektɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “objective”.","objective [əbˈdʒektɪv] -K3 adj. 客观的；目标的；宾格的 n. 目的；目标；[光] 物镜；宾格 (研四六托雅宝 2406/1322)","欧陆词典释义：objective [əbˈdʒektɪv] -K3 adj. 客观的；目标的；宾格的 n. 目的；目标；[光] 物镜；宾格 (研四六托雅宝 2406/1322)","Our main objective was the recovery of the child safe and well...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that you are trying to achieve","example":"the main/primary/principal objective"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the lens","example":"to meet/achieve"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"You must set realistic aims and objectives"}]],["option","/ˈɒpʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “option”.","option [ˈɒpʃn] -K4 n. [计] 选项；选择权；买卖的特权 (研四六托雅 1102/1086)","欧陆词典释义：option [ˈɒpʃn] -K4 n. [计] 选项；选择权；买卖的特权 (研四六托雅 1102/1086)","He's argued from the start that America and its allies are putting too much emphasis on the military option ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that you can choose to have or do; the freedom to choose what you do","example":"As I see it, we have two options…"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a subject that a student can choose to study, but that they do not have to do","example":"There are various options open to you."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the right to buy or sell something at some time in the future","example":"We are currently studying all the options available."}]],["outcome","/ˈaʊtkʌm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “outcome”.","outcome [ˈaʊtkʌm] -3 n. 结果，结局；成果 (高研四六托雅 1747/1957)","欧陆词典释义：outcome [ˈaʊtkʌm] -3 n. 结果，结局；成果 (高研四六托雅 1747/1957)","Mr. Singh said he was pleased with the outcome ...",""],["overall","/ˌəʊvərˈɔ:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “overall”.","overall [ˌəʊvərˈɔ:l] -K4 adj. 全部的；全体的；一切在内的 adv. 全部地；总的说来 n. 工装裤；罩衫 (研四六托雅 1941/1565)","欧陆词典释义：overall [ˌəʊvərˈɔ:l] -K4 adj. 全部的；全体的；一切在内的 adv. 全部地；总的说来 n. 工装裤；罩衫 (研四六托雅 1941/1565)","the overall rise in unemployment...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"including all the things or people that are involved in a particular situation; general","example":"the person with overall responsibility"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"including everything or everyone; in total","example":"There will be winners in each of three age groups, and one overall winner"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"generally; when you consider everything","example":"an overall improvement"}]],["potential","/pəˈtenʃl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “potential”.","potential [pəˈtenʃl] -K4 n. 潜能；可能性；[电] 电势 adj. 潜在的；可能的；势的 (高研四六托雅宝 1260/1438)","欧陆词典释义：potential [pəˈtenʃl] -K4 n. 潜能；可能性；[电] 电势 adj. 潜在的；可能的；势的 (高研四六托雅宝 1260/1438)","The firm has identified 60 potential customers at home and abroad...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that can develop into something or be developed in the future","example":"potential customers"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"a potential source of conflict"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the possibility of something happening or being developed or used","example":"the potential benefits of European integration"}]],["previous","/ˈpri:viəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “previous”.","previous [ˈpri:viəs] -K4 adj. 以前的；早先的；过早的 adv. 在先；在…以前 (研四六托雅宝 1276/824)","欧陆词典释义：previous [ˈpri:viəs] -K4 adj. 以前的；早先的；过早的 adv. 在先；在…以前 (研四六托雅宝 1276/824)","She has a teenage daughter from a previous marriage...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"happening or existing before the event or object that you are talking about","example":"No previous experience is necessary for this job."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"immediately before the time you are talking about","example":"The car has only had one previous owner."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"She is his daughter from a previous marriage."}]],["primary","/ˈpraɪməri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “primary”.","primary [ˈpraɪməri] -K3 n. 原色；最主要者 adj. 主要的；初级的；基本的 (中高研四六托雅 1504/1172)","欧陆词典释义：primary [ˈpraɪməri] -K3 n. 原色；最主要者 adj. 主要的；初级的；基本的 (中高研四六托雅 1504/1172)","That's the primary reason the company's share price has held up so well...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"main; most important; basic","example":"The primary aim of this course is to improve your spoken English."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"developing or happening first; earliest","example":"Our primary concern must be the children."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"connected with the education of children between the ages of about five and eleven","example":"Good health care is of primary importance."}]],["professional","/prəˈfeʃənl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “professional”.","professional [prəˈfeʃənl] -K4 n. 专业人员；职业运动员 adj. 专业的；职业的；职业性的 (研四六托雅 1094/947)","欧陆词典释义：professional [prəˈfeʃənl] -K4 n. 专业人员；职业运动员 adj. 专业的；职业的；职业性的 (研四六托雅 1094/947)","His professional career started at Liverpool University.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with a job that needs special training or skill, especially one that needs a high level of education","example":"professional qualifications/skills"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"having a job which needs special training and a high level of education","example":"professional standards/practice"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"showing that somebody is well trained and extremely skilled","example":"an opportunity for professional development"}]],["project","/ˈprɒdʒekt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “project”.","project [ˈprɒdʒekt] -K4 n. 工程；计划；事业 vt. 设计；计划；发射；放映 vi. 设计；计划；表达；投射 时态: projected, projecting, projects (高研四六托雅 534/509)","欧陆词典释义：project [ˈprɒdʒekt] -K4 n. 工程；计划；事业 vt. 设计；计划；发射；放映 vi. 设计；计划；表达；投射 时态: projected, projecting, projects (高研四六托雅 534/509)","Money will also go into local development project s in Vietnam...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a planned piece of work that is designed to find information about something, to produce something new, or to improve something","example":"a research project"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a piece of work involving careful study of a subject over a period of time, done by school or college students","example":"a building project"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a set of aims, ideas or activities that somebody is interested in or wants to bring to people’s attention","example":"to set up a project to computerize the library system"}]],["promote","/prəˈməʊt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “promote”.","promote [prəˈməʊt] -K4 vi. 成为王后或其他大于卒的子 vt. 促进；提升；推销；发扬 时态: promoted, promoting, promotes (高研四六托雅宝 1328/1433)","欧陆词典释义：promote [prəˈməʊt] -K4 vi. 成为王后或其他大于卒的子 vt. 促进；提升；推销；发扬 时态: promoted, promoting, promotes (高研四六托雅宝 1328/1433)","You don't have to sacrifice environmental protection to promote economic growth...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to help something to happen or develop","example":"policies to promote economic growth"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to help sell a product, service, etc. or make it more popular by advertising it or offering it at a special price","example":"a campaign to promote awareness of environmental issues"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move somebody to a higher rank or more senior job","example":"The band has gone on tour to promote their new album."}]],["proportion","/prəˈpɔ:ʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “proportion”.","proportion [prəˈpɔ:ʃn] -K3 n. 比例，占比；部分；面积；均衡 vt. 使成比例；使均衡；分摊 时态: proportioned, proportioning, proportions (研四六托雅 3063/1247)","欧陆词典释义：proportion [prəˈpɔ:ʃn] -K3 n. 比例，占比；部分；面积；均衡 vt. 使成比例；使均衡；分摊 时态: proportioned, proportioning, proportions (研四六托雅 3063/1247)","A large proportion of the dolphins in that area will eventually die...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a part or share of a whole","example":"Water covers a large proportion of the earth's surface."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the relationship of one thing to another in size, amount, etc.","example":"Loam is a soil with roughly equal proportions of clay, sand and silt."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the correct relationship in size, degree, importance, etc. between one thing and another or between the parts of a whole","example":"The proportion of regular smokers increases with age."}]],["publish","/ˈpʌblɪʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “publish”.","publish [ˈpʌblɪʃ] -K4 vi. 出版；发行；刊印 vt. 出版；发表；公布 时态: published, publishing, publishes (高研四六 1116/828)","欧陆词典释义：publish [ˈpʌblɪʃ] -K4 vi. 出版；发行；刊印 vt. 出版；发表；公布 时态: published, publishing, publishes (高研四六 1116/828)","They publish reference books...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to produce a book, magazine, CD-ROM","example":"The first edition was published in 2007."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to print a letter, an article, etc. in a newspaper or magazine","example":"He works for a company that publishes reference books."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something available to the public on the Internet","example":"Most of our titles are also published on CD-ROM."}]],["region","/ˈri:dʒən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “region”.","region [ˈri:dʒən] -K4 n. 地区；范围；部位 (研四六雅 793/713)","欧陆词典释义：region [ˈri:dʒən] -K4 n. 地区；范围；部位 (研四六雅 793/713)","Barcelona, capital of the autonomous region of Catalonia.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large area of land, usually without exact limits or borders","example":"the Arctic/tropical/desert, etc. regions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"one of the areas that a country is divided into, that has its own customs and/or its own government","example":"one of the most densely populated regions of North America"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"all of a country except the capital city","example":"the Basque region of Spain"}]],["regulation","/ˌregjuˈleɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “regulation”.","regulation [ˌregjuˈleɪʃn] -K3 n. 管理；规则；校准 adj. 规定的；平常的 (高研四六托雅 1675/1400)","欧陆词典释义：regulation [ˌregjuˈleɪʃn] -K3 n. 管理；规则；校准 adj. 规定的；平常的 (高研四六托雅 1675/1400)","The European Union has proposed new regulation s to control the hours worked by its employees...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official rule made by a government or some other authority","example":"too many rules and regulations"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"controlling something by means of rules","example":"fire/safety/building, etc. regulations"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that must be worn or used according to the official rules","example":"to comply with the regulations"}]],["access","/ˈækses/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “access”.","access [ˈækses] -K3 n. 进入；使用权；通路 vt. 使用；存取；接近 时态: accessed, accessing, accesses (高研四六托雅宝 1113/999)","欧陆词典释义：access [ˈækses] -K3 n. 进入；使用权；通路 vt. 使用；存取；接近 时态: accessed, accessing, accesses (高研四六托雅宝 1113/999)","The facilities have been adapted to give access to wheelchair users.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a way of entering or reaching a place","example":"The police gained access"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the opportunity or right to use something or to see somebody/something","example":"There is easy access by road."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"The only access to the farmhouse is across the fields."}]],["adapt","/əˈdæpt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adapt”.","adapt [əˈdæpt] -K2 vi. 适应 vt. 使适应；改编 时态: adapted, adapting, adapts (高研四六托雅宝 2933/2816)","欧陆词典释义：adapt [əˈdæpt] -K2 vi. 适应 vt. 使适应；改编 时态: adapted, adapting, adapts (高研四六托雅宝 2933/2816)","The world will be different, and we will have to be prepared to adapt to the change...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change something in order to make it suitable for a new use or situation","example":"These styles can be adapted to suit individual tastes."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change your behaviour in order to deal more successfully with a new situation","example":"Most of these tools have been specially adapted for use by disabled people."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change a book or play so that it can be made into a play, film/movie, television programme, etc.","example":"It's amazing how soon you adapt."}]],["adequate","/ˈædɪkwət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adequate”.","adequate [ˈædɪkwət] -K3 adj. 充足的；适当的；胜任的 (高研四六托雅宝 3297/2398)","欧陆词典释义：adequate [ˈædɪkwət] -K3 adj. 充足的；适当的；胜任的 (高研四六托雅宝 3297/2398)","One in four people worldwide are without adequate homes...",""],["annual","/ˈænjuəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “annual”.","annual [ˈænjuəl] -K4 n. 年刊，年鉴；一年生植物 adj. 年度的；每年的 (高研四托雅 1361/1215)","欧陆词典释义：annual [ˈænjuəl] -K4 n. 年刊，年鉴；一年生植物 adj. 年度的；每年的 (高研四托雅 1361/1215)","the annual conference of Britain's trade union movement...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"happening or done once every year","example":"an annual meeting/event/report"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"relating to a period of one year","example":"an annual income/subscription/budget"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"an average annual growth rate of 8%"}]],["appropriate","/əˈprəʊpriət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “appropriate”.","appropriate [əˈprəʊpriət] -K3 adj. 适当的；恰当的；合适的 vt. 占用，拨出 时态: appropriated, appropriating, appropriates (高研四六托雅宝 1493/883)","欧陆词典释义：appropriate [əˈprəʊpriət] -K3 adj. 适当的；恰当的；合适的 vt. 占用，拨出 时态: appropriated, appropriating, appropriates (高研四六托雅宝 1493/883)","It is appropriate that Irish names dominate the list...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"suitable, acceptable or correct for the particular circumstances","example":"an appropriate response/measure/method"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Now that the problem has been identified, appropriate action can be taken."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take something, somebody’s ideas, etc. for your own use, especially illegally or without permission","example":"Is now an appropriate time to make a speech?"}]],["area","/ˈeəriə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “area”.","area [ˈeəriə] -K5 n. 区域，地区；面积；范围 n. (Area)人名；(西)阿雷亚 (中高研四雅 230/149)","欧陆词典释义：area [ˈeəriə] -K5 n. 区域，地区；面积；范围 n. (Area)人名；(西)阿雷亚 (中高研四雅 230/149)","the large number of community groups in the area ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"part of a place, town, etc., or a region of a country or the world","example":"mountainous/desert areas"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a part of a room, building or particular space that is used for a special purpose","example":"rural/urban/inner-city areas"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular place on an object","example":"There is heavy traffic in the downtown area tonight."}]],["aspect","/ˈæspekt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “aspect”.","aspect [ˈæspekt] -K4 n. 方面；方向；形势；外貌 (高研四六托宝 1357/862)","欧陆词典释义：aspect [ˈæspekt] -K4 n. 方面；方向；形势；外貌 (高研四六托宝 1357/862)","Climate and weather affect every aspect of our lives...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular part or feature of a situation, an idea, a problem, etc.; a way in which it may be considered","example":"The book aims to cover all aspects of city life."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the appearance of a place, a situation or a person","example":"the most important aspect of the debate"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the direction in which a building, window, piece of land, etc. faces; the side of a building that faces a particular direction","example":"She felt she had looked at the problem from every aspect."}]],["authority","/ɔ:ˈθɒrəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “authority”.","authority [ɔ:ˈθɒrəti] -K5 n. 权威；权力；当局 (高研四六托雅 832/285)","欧陆词典释义：authority [ɔ:ˈθɒrəti] -K5 n. 权威；权力；当局 (高研四六托雅 832/285)","This provided a pretext for the authorities to cancel the elections...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the power to give orders to people","example":"in a position of authority"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the power or right to do something","example":"She now has authority over"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"official permission to do something","example":"Nothing will be done because no one in authority"}]],["behalf","/bɪˈhɑ:f/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “behalf”.","behalf [bɪˈhɑ:f] -K3 n. 代表；利益 (高研四六托雅 4434/4681)","欧陆词典释义：behalf [bɪˈhɑ:f] -K3 n. 代表；利益 (高研四六托雅 4434/4681)","She made an emotional public appeal on her son's behalf ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"We collected money in behalf of the homeless."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"in order to help somebody","example":"On behalf of the department I would like to thank you all."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"as the representative of somebody or instead of them","example":"Mr Knight cannot be here, so his wife will accept the prize on his behalf."}]],["boundary","/ˈbaʊndri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “boundary”.","boundary [ˈbaʊndri] -2 n. 边界；范围；分界线 (高研四六托雅 2776/2050)","欧陆词典释义：boundary [ˈbaʊndri] -2 n. 边界；范围；分界线 (高研四六托雅 2776/2050)","the Bow Brook which forms the western boundary of the wood...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a real or imagined line that marks the limits or edges of something and separates it from other things or places; a dividing line","example":"national boundaries"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a hit of the ball that crosses the boundary","example":"county boundaries"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"boundary changes/disputes"}]],["brief","/bri:f/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “brief”.","brief [bri:f] -K4 n. 摘要，简报；概要，诉书 adj. 简短的，简洁的；短暂的，草率的 vt. 简报，摘要；作…的提要 n. (Brief)人名；(英)布里夫 时态: briefed, briefing, briefs 级别: briefer, briefest (高研四托 2146/1863)","欧陆词典释义：brief [bri:f] -K4 n. 摘要，简报；概要，诉书 adj. 简短的，简洁的；短暂的，草率的 vt. 简报，摘要；作…的提要 n. (Brief)人名；(英)布里夫 时态: briefed, briefing, briefs 级别: briefer, briefest (高研四托 2146/1863)","She once made a brief appearance on television...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"lasting only a short time; short","example":"a brief visit/meeting/conversation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"using few words","example":"a brief pause/silence"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"short and not covering much of the body","example":"Mozart's life was brief."}]],["capacity","/kəˈpæsəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “capacity”.","capacity [kəˈpæsəti] -K3 n. 能力；容量；资格，地位；生产力 (研四六托雅 1777/1507)","欧陆词典释义：capacity [kəˈpæsəti] -K3 n. 能力；容量；资格，地位；生产力 (研四六托雅 1777/1507)","Our capacity for giving care, love and attention is limited...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the number of things or people that a container or space can hold","example":"The theatre has a seating capacity of 2 000."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to understand or to do something","example":"a fuel tank with a capacity of 50 litres"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the official position or function that somebody has","example":"The hall was filled to capacity"}]],["civil","/ˈsɪvl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “civil”.","civil [ˈsɪvl] -K4 adj. 公民的；民间的；文职的；有礼貌的；根据民法的 n. (Civil)人名；(土)吉维尔；(法)西维尔 (高研四六托宝 1050/1158)","欧陆词典释义：civil [ˈsɪvl] -K4 adj. 公民的；民间的；文职的；有礼貌的；根据民法的 n. (Civil)人名；(土)吉维尔；(法)西维尔 (高研四六托宝 1050/1158)"," civil unrest.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with the people who live in a country","example":"civil unrest ("},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with the state rather than with religion or with the armed forces","example":"a civil marriage ceremony"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"involving personal legal matters and not criminal law","example":"a civil court"}]],["code","/kəʊd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “code”.","code [kəʊd] -K3 n. 代码，密码；编码；法典 vt. 编码；制成法典 vi. 指定遗传密码 n. (Code)人名；(英、法、西)科德 时态: coded, coding, codes (研四雅宝 1648/1469)","欧陆词典释义：code [kəʊd] -K3 n. 代码，密码；编码；法典 vt. 编码；制成法典 vi. 指定遗传密码 n. (Code)人名；(英、法、西)科德 时态: coded, coding, codes (研四雅宝 1648/1469)","Article 159 of the Turkish Penal Code.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a system of words, letters, numbers or symbols that represent a message or record information secretly or in a shorter form","example":"to break/crack a code"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a system of computer programming instructions","example":"It's written in code"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a set of moral principles or rules of behaviour that are generally accepted by society or a social group","example":"Tap your code number"}]],["community","/kəˈmju:nəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “community”.","community [kəˈmju:nəti] -K5 n. 社区；[生态] 群落；共同体；团体 (研四六托雅 296/335)","欧陆词典释义：community [kəˈmju:nəti] -K5 n. 社区；[生态] 群落；共同体；团体 (研四六托雅 296/335)","He's well liked by people in the community ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"all the people who live in a particular area, country, etc. when talked about as a group","example":"The local community"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of people who share the same religion, race, job, etc.","example":"health workers based in the community ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the feeling of sharing things and belonging to a group in the place where you live","example":"the international community"}]],["component","/kəmˈpəʊnənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “component”.","component [kəmˈpəʊnənt] -3 n. 成分；组件；[电子] 元件 adj. 组成的，构成的 (高研四六托雅宝 1760/1631)","欧陆词典释义：component [kəmˈpəʊnənt] -3 n. 成分；组件；[电子] 元件 adj. 组成的，构成的 (高研四六托雅宝 1760/1631)","Enriched uranium is a key component of a nuclear weapon...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used to describe one of several parts of which something is made","example":"Break the problem down into its component parts"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"one of several parts of which something is made","example":"the components of a machine"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"the car component industry"}]],["compound","/ˈkɒmpaʊnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compound”.","compound [ˈkɒmpaʊnd] -2 n. [化学] 化合物；混合物；复合词 adj. 复合的；混合的 v. 合成；混合；恶化，加重；和解，妥协 时态: compounded, compounding, compounds (研四六托雅宝 3428/3595)","欧陆词典释义：compound [ˈkɒmpaʊnd] -2 n. [化学] 化合物；混合物；复合词 adj. 复合的；混合的 v. 合成；混合；恶化，加重；和解，妥协 时态: compounded, compounding, compounds (研四六托雅宝 3428/3595)","Police fired on them as they fled into the embassy compound .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing consisting of two or more separate things combined together","example":"Common salt is a compound of sodium and chlorine."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a substance formed by a chemical reaction of two or more elements in fixed amounts relative to each other","example":"a prison compound"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a noun, an adjective or a verb made of two or more words or parts of words, written as one or more words, or joined by a hyphen. Travel agent","example":"Dalton believed that the simplest compound of two elements must have one atom of each."}]],["corporate","/ˈkɔ:pərət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “corporate”.","corporate [ˈkɔ:pərət] -3 adj. 法人的；共同的，全体的；社团的；公司的；企业的 (六雅宝 1579/1983)","欧陆词典释义：corporate [ˈkɔ:pərət] -3 adj. 法人的；共同的，全体的；社团的；公司的；企业的 (六雅宝 1579/1983)","top US corporate executives.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with a corporation","example":"corporate finance/planning/strategy"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"forming a corporation","example":"corporate identity"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"involving or shared by all the members of a group","example":"corporate hospitality"}]],["core","/kɔ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “core”.","CORE [kɔ:(r)] -K3 n. 核心；要点；果心；[计] 磁心 vt. 挖...的核 n. (Core)人名；(英)科尔；(西、意)科雷 时态: cored, coring, cores (研四六托宝 1954/2380)","欧陆词典释义：CORE [kɔ:(r)] -K3 n. 核心；要点；果心；[计] 磁心 vt. 挖...的核 n. (Core)人名；(英)科尔；(西、意)科雷 时态: cored, coring, cores (研四六托宝 1954/2380)","Someone threw an apple core ...",""],["credit","/ˈkredɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “credit”.","credit [ˈkredɪt] -K4 n. 信用，信誉；[金融] 贷款；学分；信任；声望 vt. 相信，信任；把…归给，归功于；赞颂 时态: credited, crediting, credits (高托雅宝 1125/1262)","欧陆词典释义：credit [ˈkredɪt] -K4 n. 信用，信誉；[金融] 贷款；学分；信任；声望 vt. 相信，信任；把…归给，归功于；赞颂 时态: credited, crediting, credits (高托雅宝 1125/1262)","The group can't get credit to buy farming machinery...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an arrangement that you make, with a shop/store for example, to pay later for something you buy","example":"to get/refuse credit"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"money that you borrow from a bank; a loan","example":"We bought the dishwasher on credit"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the status of being trusted to pay back money to somebody who lends it to you","example":"to offer interest-free credit"}]],["cycle","/ˈsaɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cycle”.","cycle [ˈsaɪkl] -K3 n. 循环；周期；自行车；整套；一段时间 vt. 使循环；使轮转 vi. 循环；骑自行车；轮转 时态: cycled, cycling, cycles (高研四六雅 2220/2200)","欧陆词典释义：cycle [ˈsaɪkl] -K3 n. 循环；周期；自行车；整套；一段时间 vt. 使循环；使轮转 vi. 循环；骑自行车；轮转 时态: cycled, cycling, cycles (高研四六雅 2220/2200)","He cycle d to Ingwold...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a bicycle or motorcycle","example":"We went for a cycle ride on Sunday."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the fact of a series of events being repeated many times, always in the same order","example":"a cycle route/track"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a complete set or series, for example of movements in a machine","example":"the cycle of the seasons"}]],["device","/dɪˈvaɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “device”.","device [dɪˈvaɪs] -K3 n. 装置；策略；图案 (研四六托 1507/1825)","欧陆词典释义：device [dɪˈvaɪs] -K3 n. 装置；策略；图案 (研四六托 1507/1825)","an electronic device that protects your vehicle 24 hours a day.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an object or a piece of equipment that has been designed to do a particular job","example":"a water-saving device"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a bomb or weapon that will explode","example":"devices such as tablet PCs and mobile phones"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a method of doing something that produces a particular result or effect","example":"This device enables deaf people to communicate by typing messages instead of speaking."}]],["display","/dɪˈspleɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “display”.","display [dɪˈspleɪ] -K4 n. 显示；炫耀 vt. 显示；表现；陈列 adj. 展览的；陈列用的 vi. [动] 作炫耀行为 时态: displayed, displaying, displays (研四六托雅 2092/1683)","欧陆词典释义：display [dɪˈspleɪ] -K4 n. 显示；炫耀 vt. 显示；表现；陈列 adj. 展览的；陈列用的 vi. [动] 作炫耀行为 时态: displayed, displaying, displays (研四六托雅 2092/1683)","Among the protesters and war veterans proudly display ing their medals was Aubrey Rose...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to put something in a place where people can see it easily; to show something to people","example":"The exhibition gives local artists an opportunity to display their work."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to show signs of something, especially a quality or feeling","example":"She displayed her bruises for all to see."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to show information","example":"I have rarely seen her display any sign of emotion."}]],["dominate","/ˈdɒmɪneɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dominate”.","dominate [ˈdɒmɪneɪt] -K4 vt. 控制；支配；占优势；在…中占主要地位 vi. 占优势；处于支配地位 时态: dominated, dominating, dominates (研四六托雅宝 2312/2041)","欧陆词典释义：dominate [ˈdɒmɪneɪt] -K4 vt. 控制；支配；占优势；在…中占主要地位 vi. 占优势；处于支配地位 时态: dominated, dominating, dominates (研四六托雅宝 2312/2041)","The book is expected to dominate the best-seller lists...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to control or have a lot of influence over somebody/something, especially in an unpleasant way","example":"As a child he was dominated by his father."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be the most important or noticeable feature of something","example":"He tended to dominate the conversation."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be the largest, highest or most obvious thing in a place","example":"She always says a lot in meetings, but she doesn't dominate."}]],["draft","/drɑ:ft/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “draft”.","draft [drɑ:ft] -K3 n. 汇票；草稿；选派；（尤指房间、烟囱、炉子等供暖系统中的）（小股）气流 vt. 起草；制定；征募 vi. 拟稿；绘样；作草图 adj. 初步画出或（写出）的；（设计、草图、提纲或版本）正在起草中的，草拟的；以草稿形式的；草图的 时态: drafted, drafting, drafts (高研四六托雅宝 2624/2834)","欧陆词典释义：draft [drɑ:ft] -K3 n. 汇票；草稿；选派；（尤指房间、烟囱、炉子等供暖系统中的）（小股）气流 vt. 起草；制定；征募 vi. 拟稿；绘样；作草图 adj. 初步画出或（写出）的；（设计、草图、提纲或版本）正在起草中的，草拟的；以草稿形式的；草图的 时态: drafted, drafting, drafts (高研四六托雅宝 2624/2834)","I rewrote his rough draft , which was published under my name...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a rough written version of something that is not yet in its final form","example":"I've made a rough draft"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a written order to a bank to pay money to somebody","example":"This is only the first draft of my speech."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"In the US the draft is administered by US government's Selective Service System. Formerly young people were required by law to serve in the armed forces. This requirement was replaced in 1973 by a system in which people may join the forces only if they wish to. However, young men must still add their names to the draft list","example":"the final draft"}]],["duration","/djuˈreɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “duration”.","duration [djuˈreɪʃn] -2 n. 持续，持续的时间，期间 [语音学]音长，音延 (研四六托雅宝 5426/3698)","欧陆词典释义：duration [djuˈreɪʃn] -2 n. 持续，持续的时间，期间 [语音学]音长，音延 (研四六托雅宝 5426/3698)","He was given the task of protecting her for the duration of the trial...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the length of time that something lasts or continues","example":"The school was used as a hospital for the duration of the war."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"a contract of three years’ duration"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"until the end of a particular situation","example":"She stayed there for the duration of the journey."}]],["enable","/ɪˈneɪbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “enable”.","enable [ɪˈneɪbl] -K3 vt. 使能够，使成为可能；授予权利或方法 时态: enabled, enabling, enables (研四六托 2192/991)","欧陆词典释义：enable [ɪˈneɪbl] -K3 vt. 使能够，使成为可能；授予权利或方法 时态: enabled, enabling, enables (研四六托 2192/991)","The new test should enable doctors to detect the disease early.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make it possible for somebody to do something","example":"The software enables you to create your own DVDs."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make it possible for something to happen or exist by creating the necessary conditions","example":"a new programme to enable older people to study at college"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Insulin enables the body to use and store sugar."}]],["energy","/ˈenədʒi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “energy”.","energy [ˈenədʒi] -K4 n. [物] 能量；精力；活力；精神 (中研四六雅 615/765)","欧陆词典释义：energy [ˈenədʒi] -K4 n. [物] 能量；精力；活力；精神 (中研四六雅 615/765)","He was saving his energy for next week's race in Belgium...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to put effort and enthusiasm into an activity, work, etc.","example":"It's a waste of time and energy."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the physical and mental effort that you use to do something","example":"She's always full of energy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a source of power, such as fuel, used for driving machines, providing heat, etc.","example":"nervous energy"}]],["executive","/ɪgˈzekjətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “executive”.","executive [ɪgˈzekjətɪv] -K4 n. 总经理；执行委员会；执行者；经理主管人员 adj. 行政的；经营的；执行的，经营管理的 (研四六托雅 863/1094)","欧陆词典释义：executive [ɪgˈzekjətɪv] -K4 n. 总经理；执行委员会；执行者；经理主管人员 adj. 行政的；经营的；执行的，经营管理的 (研四六托雅 863/1094)","an advertising executive .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who has an important job as a manager of a company or an organization","example":"advertising/business/sales, etc. executives"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a group of people who run a company or an organization","example":"a chief/senior/top executive"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the part of a government responsible for putting laws into effect","example":"The union’s executive has/have yet to reach a decision."}]],["expand","/ɪkˈspænd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “expand”.","expand [ɪkˈspænd] -K3 vt. 扩张；使膨胀；详述 vi. 发展；张开，展开 时态: expanded, expanding, expands (高研四六托雅宝 1572/2124)","欧陆词典释义：expand [ɪkˈspænd] -K3 vt. 扩张；使膨胀；详述 vi. 发展；张开，展开 时态: expanded, expanding, expands (高研四六托雅宝 1572/2124)","Engineers noticed that the pipes were not expand ing as expected...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become greater in size, number or importance; to make something greater in size, number or importance","example":"Metals expand when they are heated."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"if a business expands","example":"Student numbers are expanding rapidly."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to talk more; to add details to what you are saying","example":"A child's vocabulary expands through reading."}]],["exposure","/ɪkˈspəʊʒə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “exposure”.","exposure [ɪkˈspəʊʒə(r)] -3 n. 暴露；曝光；揭露；陈列 (研四六托雅宝 2229/3141)","欧陆词典释义：exposure [ɪkˈspəʊʒə(r)] -3 n. 暴露；曝光；揭露；陈列 (研四六托雅宝 2229/3141)","Exposure to lead is known to damage the brains of young children.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state of being in a place or situation where there is no protection from something harmful or unpleasant","example":"prolonged exposure to harmful radiation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state of having the true facts about somebody/something told after they have been hidden because they are bad, immoral or illegal","example":"the company’s exposure on the foreign exchange markets ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of being discussed or mentioned on television, in newspapers, etc.","example":"his exposure as a liar and a fraud"}]],["final","/ˈfaɪnl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “final”.","final [ˈfaɪnl] -K5 n. 决赛；期末考试；当日报纸的末版 adj. 最终的；决定性的；不可更改的 (中高研四托雅 887/778)","欧陆词典释义：final [ˈfaɪnl] -K5 n. 决赛；期末考试；当日报纸的末版 adj. 最终的；决定性的；不可更改的 (中高研四托雅 887/778)","Astronauts will make a final attempt today to rescue a communications satellite from its useless orbit...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"being or happening at the end of a series of events, actions, statements, etc.","example":"his final act as party leader"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"being the result of a particular process","example":"The referee blew the final whistle."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"that cannot be argued with or changed","example":"The project is in its final stages."}]],["flexible","/ˈfleksəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “flexible”.","flexible [ˈfleksəbl] -3 adj. 灵活的；柔韧的；易弯曲的 (高研四六托雅宝 4227/3127)","欧陆词典释义：flexible [ˈfleksəbl] -3 adj. 灵活的；柔韧的；易弯曲的 (高研四六托雅宝 4227/3127)","brushes with long, flexible bristles.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"able to change to suit new conditions or situations","example":"a more flexible approach"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"able to bend easily without breaking","example":"flexible working hours"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Our plans need to be flexible enough to cater for the needs of everyone."}]],["foundation","/faʊnˈdeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “foundation”.","foundation [faʊnˈdeɪʃn] -K3 n. 基础；地基；基金会；根据；创立 (研四六 2256/1824)","欧陆词典释义：foundation [faʊnˈdeɪʃn] -K3 n. 基础；地基；基金会；根据；创立 (研四六 2256/1824)","Best friends are the foundation of my life...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a layer of bricks, concrete, etc. that forms the solid underground base of a building","example":"The builders are now beginning to lay the foundations"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a principle, an idea or a fact that something is based on and that it grows from","example":"The explosion shook the foundations of the houses nearby."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an organization that is established to provide money for a particular purpose, for example for scientific research or charity","example":"Footnotes are given at the bottom of each page."}]],["fund","/fʌnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “fund”.","fund [fʌnd] -K5 n. 基金；资金；存款 vt. 投资；资助 n. (Fund)人名；(德)丰德 时态: funded, funding, funds (研四六托 754/852)","欧陆词典释义：fund [fʌnd] -K5 n. 基金；资金；存款 vt. 投资；资助 n. (Fund)人名；(德)丰德 时态: funded, funding, funds (研四六托 754/852)","The concert will raise fund s for research into Aids.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an amount of money that has been saved or has been made available for a particular purpose","example":"a disaster relief fund"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"money that is available to be spent","example":"the company’s pension fund"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an amount or a supply of something","example":"the International Monetary Fund"}]],["generate","/ˈdʒenəreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “generate”.","generate [ˈdʒenəreɪt] -K3 vt. 使形成；发生；生殖；产生物理反应 时态: generated, generating, generates (研四六托雅宝 1692/1716)","欧陆词典释义：generate [ˈdʒenəreɪt] -K3 vt. 使形成；发生；生殖；产生物理反应 时态: generated, generating, generates (研四六托雅宝 1692/1716)","The Employment Minister said the reforms would generate new jobs.",""],["global","/ˈgləʊbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “global”.","global [ˈgləʊbl] -K3 adj. 全球的；总体的；球形的 (研四六托雅 1110/2410)","欧陆词典释义：global [ˈgləʊbl] -K3 adj. 全球的；总体的；球形的 (研四六托雅 1110/2410)","a global ban on nuclear testing...",""],["image","/ˈɪmɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “image”.","image [ˈɪmɪdʒ] -K4 n. 影像；想象；肖像；偶像 vt. 想象；反映；象征；作…的像 n. (Image)人名；(法)伊马热 时态: imaged, imaging, images (研四六托雅 555/904)","欧陆词典释义：image [ˈɪmɪdʒ] -K4 n. 影像；想象；肖像；偶像 vt. 想象；反映；象征；作…的像 n. (Image)人名；(法)伊马热 时态: imaged, imaging, images (研四六托雅 555/904)","The image of art theft as a gentleman's crime is outdated...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the impression that a person, an organization or a product, etc. gives to the public","example":"His public image is very different from the real person."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a mental picture that you have of what somebody/something is like or looks like","example":"The advertisements are intended to improve the company's image."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a copy of somebody/something in the form of a picture or statue","example":"Image is very important in the music world."}]],["institute","/ˈɪnstɪtju:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “institute”.","institute [ˈɪnstɪtju:t] -K4 n. 学会，协会；学院 vt. 开始（调查）；制定；创立；提起（诉讼） 时态: instituted, instituting, institutes (高研四六托雅宝 7980/1630)","欧陆词典释义：institute [ˈɪnstɪtju:t] -K4 n. 学会，协会；学院 vt. 开始（调查）；制定；创立；提起（诉讼） 时态: instituted, instituting, institutes (高研四六托雅宝 7980/1630)","the National Cancer Institute.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an organization that has a particular purpose, especially one that is connected with education or a particular profession; the building used by this organization","example":"a research institute"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"the Institute of Chartered Accountants"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to introduce a system, policy, etc. or start a process","example":"institutes of higher education"}]],["invest","/ɪnˈvest/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “invest”.","invest [ɪnˈvest] -K3 vi. 投资，入股；花钱买 vt. 投资；覆盖；耗费；授予；包围 时态: invested, investing, invests (研四六雅 2001/2329)","欧陆词典释义：invest [ɪnˈvest] -K3 vi. 投资，入股；花钱买 vt. 投资；覆盖；耗费；授予；包围 时态: invested, investing, invests (研四六雅 2001/2329)","They intend to invest directly in shares...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to buy property, shares in a company, etc. in the hope of making a profit","example":"Now is a good time to invest in the property market."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to spend money on something in order to make it better or more successful","example":"He invested his life savings in his daughter's business."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to spend time, energy, effort, etc. on something that you think is good or useful","example":"The government has invested heavily"}]],["journal","/ˈdʒɜ:nl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “journal”.","journal [ˈdʒɜ:nl] -4 n. 日报，杂志；日记；分类账 (研四六托雅 2780/2500)","欧陆词典释义：journal [ˈdʒɜ:nl] -4 n. 日报，杂志；日记；分类账 (研四六托雅 2780/2500)","All our results are published in scientific journal s.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a newspaper or magazine that deals with a particular subject or profession","example":"a scientific/trade journal"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used in the title of some newspapers","example":"the British Medical Journal"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a written record of the things you do, see, etc. every day","example":"the Wall Street Journal"}]],["layer","/ˈleɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “layer”.","layer [ˈleɪə(r)] -K3 n. 层，层次；膜；[植]压条；放置者，计划者 vt. 把…分层堆放；借助压条法；生根繁殖；将（头发）剪成不同层次 vi. 形成或分成层次；[植]通过压条法而生根 时态: layered, layering, layers (研四六托雅 2168/2248)","欧陆词典释义：layer [ˈleɪə(r)] -K3 n. 层，层次；膜；[植]压条；放置者，计划者 vt. 把…分层堆放；借助压条法；生根繁殖；将（头发）剪成不同层次 vi. 形成或分成层次；[植]通过压条法而生根 时态: layered, layering, layers (研四六托雅 2168/2248)","A fresh layer of snow covered the street...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a quantity or thickness of something that lies over a surface or between surfaces","example":"A thin layer of dust covered everything."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a level or part within a system or set of ideas","example":"How many layers of clothing are you wearing?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"There were too many layers of management in the company."}]],["link","/lɪŋk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “link”.","link [lɪŋk] -K4 n. [计] 链环，环节；联系，关系 vt. 连接，连结；联合，结合 vi. 连接起来；联系在一起；将人或物连接或联系起来 n. (Link)人名；(英、德、塞、捷、匈、瑞典)林克 时态: linked, linking, links (高研四六雅 1730/1277)","欧陆词典释义：link [lɪŋk] -K4 n. [计] 链环，环节；联系，关系 vt. 连接，连结；联合，结合 vi. 连接起来；联系在一起；将人或物连接或联系起来 n. (Link)人名；(英、德、塞、捷、匈、瑞典)林克 时态: linked, linking, links (高研四六雅 1730/1277)","the link between smoking and lung cancer.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a connection between two or more people or things","example":"Police suspect there may be a link between the two murders."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a relationship between two or more people, countries or organizations","example":"evidence for a strong causal link between exposure to sun and skin cancer"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a means of travelling or communicating between two places","example":"to establish trade links"}]],["location","/ləʊˈkeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “location”.","location [ləʊˈkeɪʃn] -K3 n. 位置（形容词locational）；地点；外景拍摄场地 (研四六托雅 1433/1705)","欧陆词典释义：location [ləʊˈkeɪʃn] -K3 n. 位置（形容词locational）；地点；外景拍摄场地 (研四六托雅 1433/1705)","The first thing he looked at was his office's location ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place where something happens or exists; the position of something","example":"a honeymoon in a secret location"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place outside a film studio where scenes of a film/movie are made","example":"What is the exact location of the ship?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of finding the position of somebody/something","example":"This would be a good place for a picnic."}]],["media","/ˈmi:diə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “media”.","media [ˈmi:diə] -K4 n. 媒体；媒质（medium的复数）；血管中层；浊塞音；中脉 原型: media 是 medium 的复数 (高四六托雅 757/-)","欧陆词典释义：media [ˈmi:diə] -K4 n. 媒体；媒质（medium的复数）；血管中层；浊塞音；中脉 原型: media 是 medium 的复数 (高四六托雅 757/-)","It is hard work and not a glamorous job as portrayed by the media .",""],["mental","/ˈmentl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mental”.","mental [ˈmentl] -K3 adj. 精神的；脑力的；疯的 n. 精神病患者 (高研四六托雅 1584/1620)","欧陆词典释义：mental [ˈmentl] -K3 adj. 精神的；脑力的；疯的 n. 精神病患者 (高研四六托雅 1584/1620)","the mental development of children.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with or happening in the mind; involving the process of thinking","example":"the mental process of remembering"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with the state of health of the mind or with the treatment of illnesses of the mind","example":"Do you have a mental picture"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"crazy","example":"I made a mental note"}]],["normal","/ˈnɔ:ml/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “normal”.","normal [ˈnɔ:ml] -K4 adj. 正常的；正规的，标准的 n. 正常；标准；常态 n. (Normal)人名；(德)诺马尔 (中高研四六托雅 1217/811)","欧陆词典释义：normal [ˈnɔ:ml] -K4 adj. 正常的；正规的，标准的 n. 正常；标准；常态 n. (Normal)人名；(德)诺马尔 (中高研四六托雅 1217/811)","He has occasional injections to maintain his good health but otherwise he lives a normal life...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"typical, usual or ordinary; what you would expect","example":"quite/perfectly"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"not suffering from any mental disorder","example":"Her temperature is normal."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"It's normal to"}]],["paragraph","/ˈpærəgrɑ:f/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “paragraph”.","paragraph [ˈpærəgrɑ:f] -2 n. 段落；短评；段落符号 vt. 将…分段 时态: paragraphed, paragraphing, paragraphs (高研四六 5897/2495)","欧陆词典释义：paragraph [ˈpærəgrɑ:f] -2 n. 段落；短评；段落符号 vt. 将…分段 时态: paragraphed, paragraphing, paragraphs (高研四六 5897/2495)","The length of a paragraph depends on the information it conveys...",""],["parallel","/ˈpærəlel/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “parallel”.","parallel [ˈpærəlel] -K2 n. 平行线；对比 adj. 平行的；类似的，相同的 vt. 使…与…平行 时态: parallelled, paralleling, parallels (高研四六托雅宝 5840/3869)","欧陆词典释义：parallel [ˈpærəlel] -K2 n. 平行线；对比 adj. 平行的；类似的，相同的 vt. 使…与…平行 时态: parallelled, paralleling, parallels (高研四六托雅宝 5840/3869)","Readers familiar with English history will find a vague parallel to the suppression of the monasteries...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"two or more lines that run parallel","example":"The road and the canal run parallel"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"in a way that is very similar or takes place at the same time","example":"The plane flew parallel to the coast."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"two or more lines that are parallel","example":"The team's findings run parallel"}]],["phase","/feɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “phase”.","phase [feɪz] -K3 n. 月相 n. （月亮的）盈亏 n. 时期 时态: phased, phasing, phases (研四六托雅 2244/1682)","欧陆词典释义：phase [feɪz] -K3 n. 月相 n. （月亮的）盈亏 n. 时期 时态: phased, phasing, phases (研四六托雅 2244/1682)","This autumn, 6000 residents will participate in the first phase of the project...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a stage in a process of change or development","example":"during the first/next/last phase"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"each of the shapes of the moon as we see it from the earth at different times of the month","example":"the initial/final phase"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"early 19th cent.","example":"a critical/decisive phase"}]],["population","/ˌpɒpjuˈleɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “population”.","population [ˌpɒpjuˈleɪʃn] -K4 n. 人口；[生物] 种群，[生物] 群体；全体居民 (中高研四六雅 642/683)","欧陆词典释义：population [ˌpɒpjuˈleɪʃn] -K4 n. 人口；[生物] 种群，[生物] 群体；全体居民 (中高研四六雅 642/683)","Bangladesh now has a population of about 110 million.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"all the people who live in a particular area, city or country; the total number of people who live there","example":"One third of the world’s population consumes/consume two thirds of the world’s resources."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular group of people or animals living in a particular area","example":"The entire population of the town was at the meeting."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"countries with ageing populations"}]],["positive","/ˈpɒzətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “positive”.","positive [ˈpɒzətɪv] -K4 n. 正数；[摄] 正片 adj. 积极的；[数] 正的，[医][化学] 阳性的；确定的，肯定的；实际的，真实的；绝对的 (研四六托雅 1049/1198)","欧陆词典释义：positive [ˈpɒzətɪv] -K4 n. 正数；[摄] 正片 adj. 积极的；[数] 正的，[医][化学] 阳性的；确定的，肯定的；实际的，真实的；绝对的 (研四六托雅 1049/1198)","Be positive about your future and get on with living a normal life...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"thinking about what is good in a situation; feeling confident and sure that something good will happen","example":"a positive attitude/outlook"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"directed at dealing with something or producing a successful result","example":"the power of positive thought"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"expressing agreement or support","example":"She tried to be more positive about her new job."}]],["procedure","/prəˈsi:dʒə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “procedure”.","procedure [prəˈsi:dʒə(r)] -K3 n. 程序，手续；步骤 (高研四六托雅 1369/897)","欧陆词典释义：procedure [prəˈsi:dʒə(r)] -K3 n. 程序，手续；步骤 (高研四六托雅 1369/897)","A biopsy is usually a minor surgical procedure ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a way of doing something, especially the usual or correct way","example":"maintenance procedures"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the official or formal order or way of doing something, especially in business, law or politics","example":"emergency/safety/disciplinary procedures"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a medical operation","example":"to follow normal/standard/accepted procedure"}]],["purpose","/ˈpɜ:pəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “purpose”.","purpose [ˈpɜ:pəs] -K4 n. 目的；用途；意志 vt. 决心；企图；打算 时态: purposed, purposing, purposes (中高研四六雅 1014/655)","欧陆词典释义：purpose [ˈpɜ:pəs] -K4 n. 目的；用途；意志 vt. 决心；企图；打算 时态: purposed, purposing, purposes (中高研四六雅 1014/655)","The purpose of the occasion was to raise money for medical supplies...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the intention, aim or function of something; the thing that something is supposed to achieve","example":"Our campaign's main purpose is to raise money."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"what is needed in a particular situation","example":"The purpose of the book is to provide a complete guide to the university."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"meaning that is important and valuable to you","example":"A meeting was called for the purpose of"}]],["range","/reɪndʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “range”.","range [reɪndʒ] -K4 n. 范围；幅度；排；山脉 vt. 漫游；放牧；使并列；归类于；来回走动 vi. （在...内）变动；平行，列为一行；延伸；漫游；射程达到 时态: ranged, ranging, ranges (高研四六托雅 972/484)","欧陆词典释义：range [reɪndʒ] -K4 n. 范围；幅度；排；山脉 vt. 漫游；放牧；使并列；归类于；来回走动 vi. （在...内）变动；平行，列为一行；延伸；漫游；射程达到 时态: ranged, ranging, ranges (高研四六托雅 972/484)","A wide range of colours and patterns are available...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a variety of things of a particular type","example":"The hotel offers a wide range of"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the limits between which something varies","example":"There is a full range of"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a set of products of a particular type","example":"This material is available in a huge range of colours."}]],["relevant","/ˈreləvənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “relevant”.","relevant [ˈreləvənt] -K3 adj. 相关的；切题的；中肯的；有重大关系的；有意义的，目的明确的 (高研四六托雅 2814/1241)","欧陆词典释义：relevant [ˈreləvənt] -K3 adj. 相关的；切题的；中肯的；有重大关系的；有意义的，目的明确的 (高研四六托雅 2814/1241)","We are trying to make politics more relevant to younger people.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"closely connected with the subject you are discussing or the situation you are thinking about","example":"a relevant suggestion/question/point"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having ideas that are valuable and useful to people in their lives and work","example":"Do you have the relevant experience?"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"early 16th cent.","example":"Send me all the relevant information."}]],["rely","/rɪˈlaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “rely”.","rely [rɪˈlaɪ] -3 vi. 依靠；信赖 时态: relied, relying, relies (高研四六托雅 1857/1734)","欧陆词典释义：rely [rɪˈlaɪ] -3 vi. 依靠；信赖 时态: relied, relying, relies (高研四六托雅 1857/1734)","They relied heavily on the advice of their professional advisers...",""],["resource","/rɪˈsɔ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “resource”.","resource [rɪˈsɔ:s] -K4 n. 资源，财力；办法；智谋 (研四六托雅 769/786)","欧陆词典释义：resource [rɪˈsɔ:s] -K4 n. 资源，财力；办法；智谋 (研四六托雅 769/786)","Some families don't have the resource s to feed themselves properly...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a supply of something that a country, an organization or a person has and can use, especially to increase their wealth","example":"the exploitation of minerals and other natural resources"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"something that can be used to help achieve an aim, especially a book, equipment, etc. that provides information for teachers and students","example":"We do not have the resources ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"personal qualities such as courage and imagination that help you deal with difficult situations","example":"We must make the most efficient use of the available financial resources."}]],["role","/rəʊl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “role”.","role [rəʊl] -K5 n. 角色；任务 n. (Role)人名；(意、塞、赤几)罗莱 (中高研四六托雅 451/468)","欧陆词典释义：role [rəʊl] -K5 n. 角色；任务 n. (Role)人名；(意、塞、赤几)罗莱 (中高研四六托雅 451/468)","the drug's role in preventing more serious effects of infection...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the function or position that somebody has or is expected to have in an organization, in society or in a relationship","example":"the role of the teacher in the classroom"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an actor’s part in a play, film/movie, etc.","example":"She refused to take on the traditional woman's role."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the degree to which somebody/something is involved in a situation or an activity and the effect that they have on it","example":"In many marriages there has been a complete role reversal"}]],["section","/ˈsekʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “section”.","section [ˈsekʃn] -K4 n. 截面；部分；部门；地区；章节 vt. 把…分段；将…切片；对…进行划分 vi. 被切割成片；被分成部分 时态: sectioned, sectioning, sections (高研四六托雅 818/409)","欧陆词典释义：section [ˈsekʃn] -K4 n. 截面；部分；部门；地区；章节 vt. 把…分段；将…切片；对…进行划分 vi. 被切割成片；被分成部分 时态: sectioned, sectioning, sections (高研四六托雅 818/409)","He said it was wrong to single out any section of society for Aids testing...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"any of the parts into which something is divided","example":"That section of the road is still closed."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a separate part of a structure from which the whole can be put together","example":"The library has a large biology section."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a separate part of a document, book, etc.","example":"the tail section of the plane"}]],["advice","/ədˈvaɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “advice”.","advice [ədˈvaɪs] -K4 n. 建议；忠告；劝告；通知 (中高研四六托雅 1641/962)","欧陆词典释义：advice [ədˈvaɪs] -K4 n. 建议；忠告；劝告；通知 (中高研四六托雅 1641/962)","Don't be afraid to ask for advice about ordering the meal...",""],["agency","/ˈeɪdʒənsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “agency”.","agency [ˈeɪdʒənsi] -K4 n. 代理，中介；代理处，经销处 (高研四雅 694/1036)","欧陆词典释义：agency [ˈeɪdʒənsi] -K4 n. 代理，中介；代理处，经销处 (高研四雅 694/1036)","We had to hire maids through an agency .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a business or an organization that provides a particular service especially on behalf of other businesses or organizations","example":"an advertising/employment agency"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a government department that provides a particular service","example":"You can book at your local travel agency"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"international aid agencies"}]],["agreement","/əˈgri:mənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “agreement”.","agreement [əˈgri:mənt] -K4 n. 协议；同意，一致 (中高雅 1059/623)","欧陆词典释义：agreement [əˈgri:mənt] -K4 n. 协议；同意，一致 (中高雅 1059/623)","It looks as though a compromise agreement has now been reached...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an arrangement, a promise or a contract made with somebody","example":"an international peace agreement"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state of sharing the same opinion or feeling","example":"The agreement ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of somebody approving of something and allowing it to happen","example":"They have a free trade agreement with Australia."}]],["analysis","/əˈnæləsɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “analysis”.","analysis [əˈnæləsɪs] -K3 n. 分析；分解；验定 (高研四六托雅 811/707)","欧陆词典释义：analysis [əˈnæləsɪs] -K3 n. 分析；分解；验定 (高研四六托雅 811/707)","Her criteria defy analysis ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the detailed study or examination of something in order to understand more about it; the result of the study","example":"statistical analysis"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a careful examination of a substance in order to find out what it consists of","example":"The book is an analysis of poverty and its causes."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"At the meeting they presented a detailed analysis of twelve schools in a London borough."}]],["application","/ˌæplɪˈkeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “application”.","application [ˌæplɪˈkeɪʃn] -K3 n. 应用；申请；应用程序；敷用 (高研四六托雅宝 1519/608)","欧陆词典释义：application [ˌæplɪˈkeɪʃn] -K3 n. 应用；申请；应用程序；敷用 (高研四六托雅宝 1519/608)","His application for membership of the organisation was rejected...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a formal (often written) request for something, such as a job, permission to do something or a place at a college or university","example":"a planning/passport application"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the practical use of something, especially a theory, discovery, etc.","example":"an application form"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an act of putting or spreading something, such as paint or medical creams, onto something else","example":"an application for membership/a loan/a licence"}]],["article","/ˈɑ:tɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “article”.","article [ˈɑ:tɪkl] -K4 n. 文章；物品；条款；[语] 冠词 vt. 订约将…收为学徒或见习生；使…受协议条款的约束 vi. 签订协议；进行控告 时态: articled, articling, articles (中高研四托雅 731/1027)","欧陆词典释义：article [ˈɑ:tɪkl] -K4 n. 文章；物品；条款；[语] 冠词 vt. 订约将…收为学徒或见习生；使…受协议条款的约束 vi. 签订协议；进行控告 时态: articled, articling, articles (中高研四托雅 731/1027)","a newspaper article ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of writing about a particular subject in a newspaper or magazine","example":"Have you seen that article about young fashion designers?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a separate item in an agreement or a contract","example":"Article 10 of the European Convention guarantees free speech."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular item or separate thing, especially one of a set","example":"articles of clothing"}]],["awareness","/əˈweənəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “awareness”.","awareness [əˈweənəs] n. 意识，认识；明白，知道 n. 人群对品牌或产品的认知 (托雅 2784/2404)","欧陆词典释义：awareness [əˈweənəs] n. 意识，认识；明白，知道 n. 人群对品牌或产品的认知 (托雅 2784/2404)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “awareness”.",""],["budget","/ˈbʌdʒɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “budget”.","budget [ˈbʌdʒɪt] -K4 n. 预算，预算费 adj. 廉价的 vt. 安排，预定；把…编入预算 vi. 编预算，做预算 时态: budgeted, budgeting, budgets (高研四六托雅宝 1054/1062)","欧陆词典释义：budget [ˈbʌdʒɪt] -K4 n. 预算，预算费 adj. 廉价的 vt. 安排，预定；把…编入预算 vi. 编预算，做预算 时态: budgeted, budgeting, budgets (高研四六托雅宝 1054/1062)","She will design a fantastic new kitchen for you — and all within your budget ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the money that is available to a person or an organization and a plan of how it will be spent over a period of time","example":"a monthly/an annual/a family budget"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an official statement by the government of a country’s income from taxes, etc. and how it will be spent","example":"the education/defence budget"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"an advertising budget of $2 million"}]],["class","/klɑ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “class”.","class [klɑ:s] -K5 n. 阶级；班级；种类；班；等级 adj. 极好的；很好的，优秀的，出色的 vt. 分类；把…分等级；把…归入某等级，把…看作（或分类、归类）；把…编入某一班级 vi. 属于…类（或等级），被列为某类（或某级） n. （英、德）克拉斯（人名） 时态: classed, classing, classes (中高雅 431/387)","欧陆词典释义：class [klɑ:s] -K5 n. 阶级；班级；种类；班；等级 adj. 极好的；很好的，优秀的，出色的 vt. 分类；把…分等级；把…归入某等级，把…看作（或分类、归类）；把…编入某一班级 vi. 属于…类（或等级），被列为某类（或某级） n. （英、德）克拉斯（人名） 时态: classed, classing, classes (中高雅 431/387)","He had to spend about six months in a class with younger students...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of students who are taught together","example":"We were in the same class at school."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an occasion when a group of students meets to be taught","example":"She is the youngest in her class."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a series of classes on a particular subject","example":"He came top of the class"}]],["client","/ˈklaɪənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “client”.","client [ˈklaɪənt] -K3 n. [经] 客户；顾客；委托人 (研六雅 1157/907)","欧陆词典释义：client [ˈklaɪənt] -K3 n. [经] 客户；顾客；委托人 (研六雅 1157/907)","a solicitor and his client ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who uses the services or advice of a professional person or organization","example":"a lawyer with many famous clients"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a computer that is linked to a server","example":"to act on behalf of a client"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Social workers must always consider the best interests of their clients."}]],["comment","/ˈkɒment/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “comment”.","comment [ˈkɒment] -K4 n. 评论；意见；批评 vi. 发表评论；发表意见 vt. 为…作评语 n. (Comment)人名；(德)科门特；(法)科芒 时态: commented, commenting, comments (高研四六托雅 1363/1279)","欧陆词典释义：comment [ˈkɒment] -K4 n. 评论；意见；批评 vi. 发表评论；发表意见 vt. 为…作评语 n. (Comment)人名；(德)科门特；(法)科芒 时态: commented, commenting, comments (高研四六托雅 1363/1279)","So far, Mr Cook has not comment ed on these reports...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that you say or write which gives an opinion on or explains somebody/something","example":"Have you any comment to make about the cause of the disaster?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"criticism that shows the faults of something","example":"She made"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The director was not available for comment."}]],["communication","/kəˌmju:nɪˈkeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “communication”.","communication [kəˌmju:nɪˈkeɪʃn] -K3 n. 通讯，[通信] 通信；交流；信函 (中高研四六托雅 1250/1039)","欧陆词典释义：communication [kəˌmju:nɪˈkeɪʃn] -K3 n. 通讯，[通信] 通信；交流；信函 (中高研四六托雅 1250/1039)","a communication s satellite.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the activity or process of expressing ideas and feelings or of giving people information","example":"Speech is the fastest method of communication between people."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"methods of sending information, especially telephones, radio, computers, etc. or roads and railways","example":"All channels of communication need to be kept open."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a message, letter or telephone call","example":"Doctors do not always have good communication skills"}]],["concern","/kənˈsɜ:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “concern”.","concern [kənˈsɜ:n] -K5 n. 关系；关心；关心的事；忧虑 vt. 涉及，关系到；使担心 时态: concerned, concerning, concerns (高研四六雅 717/836)","欧陆词典释义：concern [kənˈsɜ:n] -K5 n. 关系；关心；关心的事；忧虑 vt. 涉及，关系到；使担心 时态: concerned, concerning, concerns (高研四六雅 717/836)","The group has expressed concern about reports of political violence in Africa...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to affect somebody/something; to involve somebody/something","example":"Don't interfere in what doesn't concern you."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be about something","example":"The loss was a tragedy for all concerned"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to worry somebody","example":"Where our children's education is concerned, no compromise is acceptable."}]],["conference","/ˈkɒnfərəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conference”.","conference [ˈkɒnfərəns] -K5 n. 会议；讨论；协商；联盟；（正式）讨论会；[工会、工党用语]（每年的）大会 vi. 举行或参加（系列）会议 (中高研四六托雅宝 965/890)","欧陆词典释义：conference [ˈkɒnfərəns] -K5 n. 会议；讨论；协商；联盟；（正式）讨论会；[工会、工党用语]（每年的）大会 vi. 举行或参加（系列）会议 (中高研四六托雅宝 965/890)","The President summoned all the state governors to a conference on education.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large official meeting, usually lasting for a few days, at which people with the same work or interests come together to discuss their views","example":"The hotel is used for exhibitions, conferences and social events."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a meeting at which people have formal discussions","example":"a conference room/centre/hall"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of sports teams that play against each other in a league","example":"She is attending a three-day conference on AIDS education."}]],["consumer","/kənˈsju:mə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consumer”.","consumer [kənˈsju:mə(r)] -K4 n. 消费者；用户，顾客 (四六托雅 1052/1428)","欧陆词典释义：consumer [kənˈsju:mə(r)] -K4 n. 消费者；用户，顾客 (四六托雅 1052/1428)","claims that tobacco companies failed to warn consumer s about the dangers of smoking.",""],["content","/'kɒntent/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “content”.","content ['kɒntent] -K2 n. 内容，目录；满足；容量 adj. 满意的 vt. 使满足 n. (Content)人名；(法)孔唐 时态: contented, contenting, contents (高研四六托雅宝 1732/1281)","欧陆词典释义：content ['kɒntent] -K2 n. 内容，目录；满足；容量 adj. 满意的 vt. 使满足 n. (Content)人名；(法)孔唐 时态: contented, contenting, contents (高研四六托雅宝 1732/1281)","Empty the content s of the pan into the sieve...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the things that are contained in something","example":"He tipped the contents of the bag onto the table."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the different sections that are contained in a book","example":"Fire has caused severe damage to the contents of the building."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the subject matter of a book, speech, programme, etc.","example":"She hadn't read the letter and so was unaware of its contents."}]],["cooperation","/kəʊˌɒpəˈreɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cooperation”.","cooperation [kəʊˌɒpəˈreɪʃn] n. 合作，协作；[劳经] 协力 (托雅 2668/5122)","欧陆词典释义：cooperation [kəʊˌɒpəˈreɪʃn] n. 合作，协作；[劳经] 协力 (托雅 2668/5122)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cooperation”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of doing something together or of working together towards a shared aim","example":"a report produced by the government in cooperation with the chemical industry"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"willingness to be helpful and do as you are asked","example":"We would like to see closer cooperation between parents and schools."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"We would be grateful for your cooperation in clearing the hall as quickly as possible."}]],["decision","/dɪˈsɪʒn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “decision”.","decision [dɪˈsɪʒn] -K5 n. 决定，决心；决议 (中高研四六雅 479/381)","欧陆词典释义：decision [dɪˈsɪʒn] -K5 n. 决定，决心；决议 (中高研四六雅 479/381)","A decision was taken to discipline Marshall...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a choice or judgement that you make after thinking and talking about what is the best thing to do","example":"to make a decision"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to decide something clearly and quickly","example":"to take a decision"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of deciding something","example":"We need a decision on this by next week."}]],["demand","/dɪˈmɑ:nd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “demand”.","demand [dɪˈmɑ:nd] -K5 n. [经] 需求；要求；需要 vt. 要求；需要；查询 vi. 需要；请求；查问 n. (Demand)人名；(德)德曼德 时态: demanded, demanding, demands (高研四六宝 1287/723)","欧陆词典释义：demand [dɪˈmɑ:nd] -K5 n. [经] 需求；要求；需要 vt. 要求；需要；查询 vi. 需要；请求；查问 n. (Demand)人名；(德)德曼德 时态: demanded, demanding, demands (高研四六宝 1287/723)","Mr Byers last night demand ed an immediate explanation from the Education Secretary...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a very firm request for something; something that somebody needs","example":"a demand for higher pay"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"things that somebody/something makes you do, especially things that are difficult, make you tired, worried, etc.","example":"demands that the law on gun ownership should be changed"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the desire or need of customers for goods or services which they want to buy or use","example":"firms attempting to meet/satisfy"}]],["department","/dɪˈpɑ:tmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “department”.","department [dɪˈpɑ:tmənt] -K5 n. 部；部门；系；科；局 (高研四六雅 1198/447)","欧陆词典释义：department [dɪˈpɑ:tmənt] -K5 n. 部；部门；系；科；局 (高研四六雅 1198/447)","the U.S. Department of Health, Education and Welfare...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a section of a large organization such as a government, business, university, etc.","example":"the Department of Health"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"the Treasury Department"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be something that somebody is responsible for or knows a lot about","example":"a government/university, etc. department"}]],["description","/dɪˈskrɪpʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “description”.","description [dɪˈskrɪpʃn] -K3 n. 描述，描写；类型；说明书 (高研四六雅 2171/1441)","欧陆词典释义：description [dɪˈskrɪpʃn] -K3 n. 描述，描写；类型；说明书 (高研四六雅 2171/1441)","Police have issued a description of the man who was aged between fifty and sixty...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of writing or speech that says what somebody/something is like; the act of writing or saying in words what somebody/something is like","example":"to give a detailed/full description"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"of some, etc. type","example":"a brief/general description"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Police have issued a description of the gunman."}]],["detail","/ˈdi:teɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “detail”.","detail [ˈdi:teɪl] -K4 n. 细节，详情 vt. 详述；选派 vi. 画详图 时态: detailed, detailing, details (研四六雅 997/566)","欧陆词典释义：detail [ˈdi:teɪl] -K4 n. 细节，详情 vt. 详述；选派 vi. 画详图 时态: detailed, detailing, details (研四六雅 997/566)","The detail s of the plan are still being worked out...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small individual fact or item; a less important fact or item","example":"an expedition planned down to the last detail"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the small facts or features of something, when you consider them all together","example":"He stood still, absorbing every detail of the street."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"information about something","example":"Tell me the main points now; leave the details"}]],["difference","/ˈdɪfrəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “difference”.","difference [ˈdɪfrəns] -K4 n. 差异；不同；争执 (中高研四雅 496/528)","欧陆词典释义：difference [ˈdɪfrəns] -K4 n. 差异；不同；争执 (中高研四雅 496/528)","That is the fundamental difference between the two societies...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way in which two people or things are not like each other; the way in which somebody/something has changed","example":"There are no significant differences between the education systems of the two countries."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount that something is greater or smaller than something else","example":"He was studying the complex similarities and differences between humans and animals."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a disagreement between people","example":"There's no difference in the results."}]],["direct","/dəˈrekt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “direct”.","direct [dəˈrekt] -K5 adj. 直接的；直系的；亲身的；恰好的 vt. 管理；指挥；导演；指向 adv. 直接地；正好；按直系关系 vi. 指导；指挥 时态: directed, directing, directs (中高研四六托雅 1478/960)","欧陆词典释义：direct [dəˈrekt] -K5 adj. 直接的；直系的；亲身的；恰好的 vt. 管理；指挥；导演；指向 adv. 直接地；正好；按直系关系 vi. 指导；指挥 时态: directed, directing, directs (中高研四六托雅 1478/960)","They'd come on a direct flight from Athens.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"happening or done without involving other people, actions, etc. in between","example":"They are in direct contact with the hijackers."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"going in the straightest line between two places without stopping or changing direction","example":"His death was a direct result of your action."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"with nothing between something and the source of the heat or light","example":"She has direct responsibility for all new trainees."}]],["discussion","/dɪˈskʌʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “discussion”.","discussion [dɪˈskʌʃn] -K4 n. 讨论，议论 (中高四六雅 1041/860)","欧陆词典释义：discussion [dɪˈskʌʃn] -K4 n. 讨论，议论 (中高四六雅 1041/860)","There was a lot of discussion about the wording of the report...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of discussing somebody/something; a conversation about somebody/something","example":"a topic/subject for discussion"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a speech or a piece of writing that discusses many different aspects of a subject","example":"After considerable discussion, they decided to accept our offer."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"The plans have been under discussion"}]],["effective","/ɪˈfektɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “effective”.","effective [ɪˈfektɪv] -K4 adj. 有效的，起作用的；实际的，实在的；给人深刻印象 (研四六托雅 1133/1007)","欧陆词典释义：effective [ɪˈfektɪv] -K4 adj. 有效的，起作用的；实际的，实在的；给人深刻印象 (研四六托雅 1133/1007)","The project looks at how we could be more effective in encouraging students to enter teacher training...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"producing the result that is wanted or intended; producing a successful result","example":"Long prison sentences can be a very effective deterrent for offenders."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"in reality, although not officially intended","example":"Aspirin is a simple but highly effective treatment."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"coming into use","example":"drugs that are effective against cancer"}]],["employment","/ɪmˈplɔɪmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “employment”.","employment [ɪmˈplɔɪmənt] -K3 n. 使用；职业；雇用 (研四六雅 2534/933)","欧陆词典释义：employment [ɪmˈplɔɪmənt] -K3 n. 使用；职业；雇用 (研四六雅 2534/933)","She was unable to find employment ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"work, especially when it is done to earn money; the state of being employed","example":"to be in paid employment"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the situation in which people have work","example":"full-time/part-time employment"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of employing somebody","example":"conditions/terms of employment"}]],["equipment","/ɪˈkwɪpmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “equipment”.","equipment [ɪˈkwɪpmənt] -K4 n. 设备，装备；器材 (高研四六托雅 1352/1117)","欧陆词典释义：equipment [ɪˈkwɪpmənt] -K4 n. 设备，装备；器材 (高研四六托雅 1352/1117)","computers, electronic equipment and machine tools.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the things that are needed for a particular purpose or activity","example":"a useful piece of equipment"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of providing a place or person with necessary things","example":"office equipment"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 18th cent.","example":"new equipment for the sports club"}]],["exchange","/ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “exchange”.","exchange [ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ] -K4 n. 交换；交流；交易所；兑换 vt. 交换；交易；兑换 vi. 交换；交易；兑换 时态: exchanged, exchanging, exchanges (高研四六托雅 1513/1084)","欧陆词典释义：exchange [ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ] -K4 n. 交换；交流；交易所；兑换 vt. 交换；交易；兑换 vi. 交换；交易；兑换 时态: exchanged, exchanging, exchanges (高研四六托雅 1513/1084)","We exchange d addresses and Christmas cards...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an act of giving something to somebody or doing something for somebody and receiving something in return","example":"The exchange of prisoners took place this morning."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a conversation or an argument","example":"We need to promote an open exchange of ideas and information."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the process of changing an amount of one currency","example":"an exchange of glances/insults"}]],["existence","/ɪgˈzɪstəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “existence”.","existence [ɪgˈzɪstəns] -K n. 存在，实在；生存，生活；存在物，实在物 (高研四六雅 2213/1454)","欧陆词典释义：existence [ɪgˈzɪstəns] -K n. 存在，实在；生存，生活；存在物，实在物 (高研四六雅 2213/1454)","the existence of other galaxies...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state or fact of being real or living or of being present","example":"I was unaware of his existence until today."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a way of living especially when this is difficult or boring","example":"This is the oldest Hebrew manuscript in existence"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Pakistan came into existence"}]],["expert","/ˈekspɜ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “expert”.","expert [ˈekspɜ:t] -K4 n. 专家；行家；能手 adj. 熟练的；内行的；老练的 vt. 当专家；在…中当行家 n. (Expert)人名；(法)埃克斯佩 (高研四雅 899/1335)","欧陆词典释义：expert [ˈekspɜ:t] -K4 n. 专家；行家；能手 adj. 熟练的；内行的；老练的 vt. 当专家；在…中当行家 n. (Expert)人名；(法)埃克斯佩 (高研四雅 899/1335)","Our team of expert s will be on hand to offer help and advice between 12 noon and 7pm daily.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person with special knowledge, skill or training in something","example":"a computer/medical expert"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"Middle English","example":"an expert in child psychology"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"done with, having or involving great knowledge or skill","example":"an expert on modern literature"}]],["extent","/ɪkˈstent/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “extent”.","extent [ɪkˈstent] -K3 n. 程度；范围；长度 (研四六托雅 1758/990)","欧陆词典释义：extent [ɪkˈstent] -K3 n. 程度；范围；长度 (研四六托雅 1758/990)","The government itself has little information on the extent of industrial pollution...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"how large, important, serious, etc. something is","example":"It is difficult to assess the full extent"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the physical size of an area","example":"She was exaggerating the true extent"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"I was amazed at the extent of his knowledge."}]],["facility","/fəˈsɪləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “facility”.","facility [fəˈsɪləti] -K4 n. 设施；设备；容易；灵巧 (研四六托雅 1297/1014)","欧陆词典释义：facility [fəˈsɪləti] -K4 n. 设施；设备；容易；灵巧 (研四六托雅 1297/1014)","What recreational facilities are now available?...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"buildings, services, equipment, etc. that are provided for a particular purpose","example":"sports/leisure facilities"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a special feature of a machine, service, etc. that makes it possible to do something extra","example":"conference facilities"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place, usually including buildings, used for a particular purpose or activity","example":"shopping/banking/cooking facilities"}]],["figure","/ˈfɪgə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “figure”.","figure [ˈfɪgə(r)] -K5 n. 数字；人物；图形；价格；（人的）体形；画像 vt. 计算；认为；描绘；象征 vi. 计算；出现；扮演角色 时态: figured, figuring, figures (高研四六托雅 552/325)","欧陆词典释义：figure [ˈfɪgə(r)] -K5 n. 数字；人物；图形；价格；（人的）体形；画像 vt. 计算；认为；描绘；象征 vi. 计算；出现；扮演角色 时态: figured, figuring, figures (高研四六托雅 552/325)","It would be very nice if we had a true figure of how many people in this country haven't got a job...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a number representing a particular amount, especially one given in official information","example":"the latest trade/sales/unemployment, etc. figures"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a symbol rather than a word representing one of the numbers between 0 and 9","example":"Viewing figures for the series have dropped dramatically."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the area of mathematics that deals with adding, multiplying, etc. numbers","example":"Figures for April show a slight improvement on previous months"}]],["formula","/ˈfɔ:mjələ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “formula”.","formula [ˈfɔ:mjələ] -K3 n. [数] 公式，准则；配方；婴儿食品 (研四六托雅宝 3340/2600)","欧陆词典释义：formula [ˈfɔ:mjələ] -K3 n. [数] 公式，准则；配方；婴儿食品 (研四六托雅宝 3340/2600)","It is difficult to imagine how the North and South could ever agree on a formula to unify the divided peninsula.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a series of letters, numbers or symbols that represent a rule or law","example":"This formula is used to calculate the area of a circle."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"letters and symbols that show the parts of a chemical compound","example":"CO is the formula for carbon monoxide."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular method of doing or achieving something","example":"They're trying to work out a peace formula"}]],["frequency","/ˈfri:kwənsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “frequency”.","frequency [ˈfri:kwənsi] -2 n. 频率；频繁 (研四六雅宝 3009/2406)","欧陆词典释义：frequency [ˈfri:kwənsi] -2 n. 频率；频繁 (研四六雅宝 3009/2406)","The frequency of Kara's phone calls increased rapidly...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the rate at which something happens or is repeated","example":"Fatal road accidents have decreased in frequency over recent years."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of something happening often","example":"a society with a high/low frequency"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the rate at which a sound or electromagnetic","example":"The program can show us word frequency"}]],["instruction","/ɪnˈstrʌkʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “instruction”.","instruction [ɪnˈstrʌkʃn] -K2 n. 指令，命令；指示；教导；用法说明 (中高研四六托雅 1563/1594)","欧陆词典释义：instruction [ɪnˈstrʌkʃn] -K2 n. 指令，命令；指示；教导；用法说明 (中高研四六托雅 1563/1594)","Two lawyers were told not to leave the building but no reason for this instruction was given.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"detailed information on how to do or use something","example":"Follow the instructions"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"something that somebody tells you to do","example":"Always read the instructions"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a piece of information that tells a computer to perform a particular operation.","example":"The plant comes with full instructions"}]],["intelligence","/ɪnˈtelɪdʒəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “intelligence”.","intelligence [ɪnˈtelɪdʒəns] -K3 n. 智力；情报工作；情报机关；理解力；才智，智慧；天分 (高研四六托雅 1417/2444)","欧陆词典释义：intelligence [ɪnˈtelɪdʒəns] -K3 n. 智力；情报工作；情报机关；理解力；才智，智慧；天分 (高研四六托雅 1417/2444)","She's a woman of exceptional intelligence .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to learn, understand and think in a logical way about things; the ability to do this well","example":"a person of high/average/low intelligence"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"secret information that is collected, for example about a foreign country, especially one that is an enemy; the people that collect this information","example":"He didn't even have the intelligence to call for an ambulance."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"intelligence reports"}]],["introduction","/ˌɪntrəˈdʌkʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “introduction”.","introduction [ˌɪntrəˈdʌkʃn] -K2 n. 介绍；引进；采用；入门；传入 (中高研四六雅 2904/1379)","欧陆词典释义：introduction [ˌɪntrəˈdʌkʃn] -K2 n. 介绍；引进；采用；入门；传入 (中高研四六雅 2904/1379)","Ellen Malos, in her introduction to 'The Politics of Housework', provides a summary of the debates.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of bringing something into use or existence for the first time, or of bringing something to a place for the first time","example":"the introduction of new manufacturing methods"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that is brought into use or introduced to a place for the first time","example":"the introduction of compulsory military service"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of making one person formally known to another, in which you tell each the other’s name","example":"the 1 000th anniversary of the introduction of Christianity to Russia"}]],["knowledge","/ˈnɒlɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “knowledge”.","knowledge [ˈnɒlɪdʒ] -K4 n. 知识，学问；知道，认识；学科 n. (Knowledge)人名；(南非)诺利奇 (中高研四六雅 839/689)","欧陆词典释义：knowledge [ˈnɒlɪdʒ] -K4 n. 知识，学问；知道，认识；学科 n. (Knowledge)人名；(南非)诺利奇 (中高研四六雅 839/689)","She told Parliament she had no knowledge of the affair.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the information, understanding and skills that you gain through education or experience","example":"practical/medical/scientific knowledge"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state of knowing about a particular fact or situation","example":"He has a wide knowledge of painting and music."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"working with information rather than producing goods","example":"There is a lack of knowledge about the tax system."}]],["labour","/'leɪbə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “labour”.","labour ['leɪbə(r)] -K5 n. （英国）工党 时态: laboured, labouring, labours (中高四六 16348/724)","欧陆词典释义：labour ['leɪbə(r)] -K5 n. （英国）工党 时态: laboured, labouring, labours (中高四六 16348/724)","the labour of seeding, planting and harvesting...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"work, especially physical work","example":"manual labour"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a task or period of work","example":"The price will include the labour and materials."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the people who work or are available for work in a country or company","example":"The company wants to keep down labour costs"}]],["limit","/ˈlɪmɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “limit”.","limit [ˈlɪmɪt] -K4 n. 限制；限度；界线 vt. 限制；限定 时态: limited, limiting, limits (高研四六 1348/1439)","欧陆词典释义：limit [ˈlɪmɪt] -K4 n. 限制；限度；界线 vt. 限制；限定 时态: limited, limiting, limits (高研四六 1348/1439)","Her love for him was being tested to its limit s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a point at which something stops being possible or existing","example":"There is a limit to the amount of pain we can bear."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the greatest or smallest amount of something that is allowed","example":"The team performed to the limit"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the furthest edge of an area or a place","example":"She knew the limits of her power."}]],["literature","/ˈlɪtrətʃə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “literature”.","literature [ˈlɪtrətʃə(r)] -K3 n. 文学；文献；文艺；著作 (高研四六雅 1549/1766)","欧陆词典释义：literature [ˈlɪtrətʃə(r)] -K3 n. 文学；文献；文艺；著作 (高研四六雅 1549/1766)","classic works of literature .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"pieces of writing that are valued as works of art, especially novels, plays and poems (in contrast to technical books and newspapers, magazines, etc.)","example":"French literature"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"pieces of writing or printed information on a particular subject","example":"great works of literature"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"I've read all the available literature on keeping rabbits."}]],["management","/ˈmænɪdʒmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “management”.","management [ˈmænɪdʒmənt] -K4 n. 管理；管理人员；管理部门；操纵；经营手段 (研四六雅 906/446)","欧陆词典释义：management [ˈmænɪdʒmənt] -K4 n. 管理；管理人员；管理部门；操纵；经营手段 (研四六雅 906/446)","The zoo needed better management rather than more money...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of running and controlling a business or similar organization","example":"a career in management"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the people who run and control a business or similar organization","example":"hotel/project management"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act or skill of dealing with people or situations in a successful way","example":"a management training course"}]],["material","/məˈtɪəriəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “material”.","material [məˈtɪəriəl] -K4 adj. 重要的；物质的，实质性的；肉体的 n. 材料，原料；物资；布料 (高研四六雅 641/499)","欧陆词典释义：material [məˈtɪəriəl] -K4 adj. 重要的；物质的，实质性的；肉体的 n. 材料，原料；物资；布料 (高研四六雅 641/499)","electrons in a conducting material such as a metal.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"cloth used for making clothes, curtains, etc.","example":"a piece of material"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a substance that things can be made from","example":"‘What material is this dress made of?’ ‘Cotton.’"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"things that are needed in order to do a particular activity","example":"cotton fabric"}]],["measure","/ˈmeʒə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “measure”.","measure [ˈmeʒə(r)] -K4 n. 测量；措施；程度；尺寸 vt. 测量；估量；权衡 vi. 测量；估量 时态: measured, measuring, measures (高研四六雅 941/889)","欧陆词典释义：measure [ˈmeʒə(r)] -K4 n. 测量；措施；程度；尺寸 vt. 测量；估量；权衡 vi. 测量；估量 时态: measured, measuring, measures (高研四六雅 941/889)","I continued to measure his progress against the charts in the doctor's office...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to find the size, quantity, etc. of something in standard units","example":"A ship's speed is measured in knots."},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to be a particular size, length, amount, etc.","example":"a device that measures the level of radiation in the atmosphere"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to judge the importance, value or effect of something","example":"measuring equipment/instruments"}]],["mechanism","/ˈmekənɪzəm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mechanism”.","mechanism [ˈmekənɪzəm] -3 n. 机制；原理，途径；进程；机械装置；技巧 (研六托雅宝 2677/1869)","欧陆词典释义：mechanism [ˈmekənɪzəm] -3 n. 机制；原理，途径；进程；机械装置；技巧 (研六托雅宝 2677/1869)","the locking mechanism ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a set of moving parts in a machine that performs a task","example":"a delicate watch mechanism"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a method or a system for achieving something","example":"The mechanism for locking the door of the washing machine is childproof."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a system of parts in a living thing that together perform a particular function","example":"mechanisms for dealing with complaints from the general public"}]],["model","/ˈmɒdl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “model”.","model [ˈmɒdl] -K4 n. 模型；典型；模范；模特儿；样式 vt. 模拟；塑造；模仿 vi. 做模型；做模特儿 adj. 模范的；作模型用的 n. (Model)人名；(德、俄、英)莫德尔 时态: modelled, modelling, models (中高研四雅 504/551)","欧陆词典释义：model [ˈmɒdl] -K4 n. 模型；典型；模范；模特儿；样式 vt. 模拟；塑造；模仿 vi. 做模型；做模特儿 adj. 模范的；作模型用的 n. (Model)人名；(德、俄、英)莫德尔 时态: modelled, modelling, models (中高研四雅 504/551)","an architect's model of a wooden house.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a copy of something, usually smaller than the original object","example":"a working model"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular design or type of product","example":"a model aeroplane"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a simple description of a system, used for explaining how something works or calculating what might happen, etc.","example":"The architect had produced a scale model"}]],["motive","/ˈməʊtɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “motive”.","motive [ˈməʊtɪv] -2 n. 动机，目的；主题 adj. 发动的；成为动机的 vt. 使产生动机，激起 (研四六托 3578/3406)","欧陆词典释义：motive [ˈməʊtɪv] -2 n. 动机，目的；主题 adj. 发动的；成为动机的 vt. 使产生动机，激起 (研四六托 3578/3406)","Police have ruled out robbery as a motive for the killing.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a reason for doing something","example":"There seemed to be no motive for the murder."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"I'm suspicious of his motives."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"causing movement or action","example":"the profit motive ("}]],["organisation","/ˌɔ:gənaɪ'zeɪʃən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “organisation”.","organisation [ˌɔ:gənaɪ'zeɪʃən] n. 组织；团体（等于organization） (-/751)","欧陆词典释义：organisation [ˌɔ:gənaɪ'zeɪʃən] n. 组织；团体（等于organization） (-/751)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “organisation”.",""],["pattern","/ˈpætn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “pattern”.","pattern [ˈpætn] -K4 n. 模式；图案；样品 vt. 模仿；以图案装饰 vi. 形成图案 时态: patterned, patterning, patterns (高研四六雅 1017/676)","欧陆词典释义：pattern [ˈpætn] -K4 n. 模式；图案；样品 vt. 模仿；以图案装饰 vi. 形成图案 时态: patterned, patterning, patterns (高研四六雅 1017/676)","All three attacks followed the same pattern ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the regular way in which something happens or is done","example":"changing patterns"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an excellent example to copy","example":"an irregular sleeping pattern"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a regular arrangement of lines, shapes, colours, etc. as a design on material, carpets, etc.","example":"The murders all seem to follow a (similar) pattern"}]],["physical","/ˈfɪzɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “physical”.","physical [ˈfɪzɪkl] -K4 n. 体格检查 adj. [物] 物理的；身体的；物质的；根据自然规律的，符合自然法则的 (高研四六雅 802/1047)","欧陆词典释义：physical [ˈfɪzɪkl] -K4 n. 体格检查 adj. [物] 物理的；身体的；物质的；根据自然规律的，符合自然法则的 (高研四六雅 802/1047)","the physical and mental problems caused by the illness...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with a person’s body rather than their mind","example":"physical fitness"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"connected with things that actually exist or are present and can be seen, felt, etc. rather than things that only exist in a person’s mind","example":"physical appearance"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"according to the laws of nature","example":"The ordeal has affected both her mental and physical health."}]],["predict","/prɪˈdɪkt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “predict”.","predict [prɪˈdɪkt] -K3 vi. 作出预言；作预料，作预报 vt. 预报，预言；预知 时态: predicted, predicting, predicts (高研四六托 1613/2288)","欧陆词典释义：predict [prɪˈdɪkt] -K3 vi. 作出预言；作预料，作预报 vt. 预报，预言；预知 时态: predicted, predicting, predicts (高研四六托 1613/2288)","The latest opinion polls are predict ing a very close contest...",""],["product","/ˈprɒdʌkt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “product”.","product [ˈprɒdʌkt] -K5 n. 产品；结果；[数] 乘积；作品 (高研四六雅 569/451)","欧陆词典释义：product [ˈprɒdʌkt] -K5 n. 产品；结果；[数] 乘积；作品 (高研四六雅 569/451)","Try to get the best product at the lowest price...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that is grown or produced, usually for sale","example":"dairy/meat/pharmaceutical, etc. products"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing produced during a natural, chemical or industrial process","example":"investment in product development"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person or thing that is the result of something","example":"to launch a new product"}]],["public","/ˈpʌblɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “public”.","public [ˈpʌblɪk] -K5 n. 公众；社会；公共场所 adj. 公众的；政府的；公用的；公立的 n. (Public)人名；(英)帕布利克 (中高研四六雅 333/319)","欧陆词典释义：public [ˈpʌblɪk] -K5 n. 公众；社会；公共场所 adj. 公众的；政府的；公用的；公立的 n. (Public)人名；(英)帕布利克 (中高研四六雅 333/319)","Lauderdale House is now open to the public ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with ordinary people in society in general","example":"The campaign is designed to increase public awareness of the issues."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"provided, especially by the government, for the use of people in general","example":"Levels of waste from the factory may be a danger to public health."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"connected with the government and the services it provides","example":"Why would the closure of hospitals be in the public interest"}]],["quality","/ˈkwɒləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “quality”.","quality [ˈkwɒləti] -K4 n. 质量，[统计] 品质；特性；才能 adj. 优质的；高品质的；&lt;英俚&gt;棒极了 (高研四六托雅 764/536)","欧陆词典释义：quality [ˈkwɒləti] -K4 n. 质量，[统计] 品质；特性；才能 adj. 优质的；高品质的；&lt;英俚&gt;棒极了 (高研四六托雅 764/536)","Everyone can greatly improve the quality of life...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the standard of something when it is compared to other things like it; how good or bad something is","example":"to be of good/poor/top quality"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a high standard","example":"goods of a high quality"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a thing that is part of a person’s character, especially something good","example":"high-quality goods"}]],["recovery","/rɪˈkʌvəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “recovery”.","recovery [rɪˈkʌvəri] -3 n. 恢复，复原；痊愈；重获 (研四六 2443/2256)","欧陆词典释义：recovery [rɪˈkʌvəri] -3 n. 恢复，复原；痊愈；重获 (研四六 2443/2256)","He made a remarkable recovery from a shin injury...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of becoming well again after an illness or injury","example":"My father has made a"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of improving or becoming stronger again","example":"to make a remarkable/quick/speedy/slow, etc. recovery"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the action or process of getting something back that has been lost or stolen","example":"She is on the road to"}]],["reference","/ˈrefrəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “reference”.","reference [ˈrefrəns] -K3 n. 参考，参照；涉及，提及；参考书目；介绍信；证明书 vt. 引用 vi. 引用 时态: referenced, referencing, references (高研四六雅 1904/1016)","欧陆词典释义：reference [ˈrefrəns] -K3 n. 参考，参照；涉及，提及；参考书目；介绍信；证明书 vt. 引用 vi. 引用 时态: referenced, referencing, references (高研四六雅 1904/1016)","He made no reference to any agreement...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing you say or write that mentions somebody/something else; the act of mentioning somebody/something","example":"The book is full of references to growing up in India."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the act of looking at something for information","example":"She made"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the act of asking somebody for help or advice","example":"the President’s passing reference to"}]],["responsibility","/rɪˌspɒnsəˈbɪləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “responsibility”.","responsibility [rɪˌspɒnsəˈbɪləti] -K4 n. 责任，职责；义务 (高研四六托雅 1067/830)","欧陆词典释义：responsibility [rɪˌspɒnsəˈbɪləti] -K4 n. 责任，职责；义务 (高研四六托雅 1067/830)","Each manager had responsibility for just under 600 properties...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a duty to deal with or take care of somebody/something, so that you may be blamed if something goes wrong","example":"We are recruiting a sales manager with responsibility for the European market."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"blame for something bad that has happened","example":"They have responsibility for ensuring that the rules are enforced."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a duty to help or take care of somebody because of your job, position, etc.","example":"The responsibility for doing this rests with the department managers."}]],["schedule","/ˈʃedju:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “schedule”.","schedule [ˈʃedju:l] -K4 n. 时间表；计划表；一览表 vt. 安排，计划；编制目录；将……列入计划表 时态: scheduled, scheduling, schedules (高研四六托雅 2144/2702)","欧陆词典释义：schedule [ˈʃedju:l] -K4 n. 时间表；计划表；一览表 vt. 安排，计划；编制目录；将……列入计划表 时态: scheduled, scheduling, schedules (高研四六托雅 2144/2702)","He has been forced to adjust his schedule ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a plan that lists all the work that you have to do and when you must do each thing","example":"I have a hectic schedule for the next few days."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a list of the television and radio programmes that are on a particular channel and the times that they start","example":"We're working to a tight schedule"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a written list of things, for example prices, rates or conditions","example":"Filming began on schedule"}]],["survey","/ˈsɜ:veɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “survey”.","survey [ˈsɜ:veɪ] -K4 n. 调查；测量；审视；纵览 vt. 调查；勘测；俯瞰 vi. 测量土地 时态: surveyed, surveying, surveys (研四六托雅 1241/1015)","欧陆词典释义：survey [ˈsɜ:veɪ] -K4 n. 调查；测量；审视；纵览 vt. 调查；勘测；俯瞰 vi. 测量土地 时态: surveyed, surveying, surveys (研四六托雅 1241/1015)","The council conducted a survey of the uses to which farm buildings are put...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an investigation of the opinions, behaviour, etc. of a particular group of people, which is usually done by asking them questions","example":"A recent survey showed 75% of those questioned were in favour of the plan."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the act of examining and recording the measurements, features, etc. of an area of land in order to make a map or plan of it","example":"The survey revealed"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an examination of the condition of a house, etc., usually done for somebody who is thinking of buying it","example":"to conduct/carry out a survey"}]],["strategy","/ˈstrætədʒi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “strategy”.","strategy [ˈstrætədʒi] -K4 n. 战略，策略 (研四六托雅 844/1127)","欧陆词典释义：strategy [ˈstrætədʒi] -K4 n. 战略，策略 (研四六托雅 844/1127)","Next week, health ministers gather in Amsterdam to agree a strategy for controlling malaria...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a plan that is intended to achieve a particular purpose","example":"the government’s economic strategy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of planning something or putting a plan into operation in a skilful way","example":"to develop a strategy for dealing with unemployment"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the skill of planning the movements of armies in a battle or war; an example of doing this","example":"It's all part of an overall strategy to gain promotion."}]],["style","/staɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “style”.","style [staɪl] -K4 n. 风格；时尚；类型；字体 vt. 设计；称呼；使合潮流 vi. 设计式样；用刻刀作装饰画 n. (Style)人名；(英)斯泰尔 时态: styled, styling, styles (高研四六雅 968/790)","欧陆词典释义：style [staɪl] -K4 n. 风格；时尚；类型；字体 vt. 设计；称呼；使合潮流 vi. 设计式样；用刻刀作装饰画 n. (Style)人名；(英)斯泰尔 时态: styled, styling, styles (高研四六雅 968/790)","Our children's different needs and learning style s created many problems...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the particular way in which something is done","example":"a style of management"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular design of something, especially clothes","example":"a management style"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the quality of being fashionable in the clothes that you wear","example":"furniture to suit your style of living"}]],["subject","/ˈsʌbdʒɪkt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “subject”.","subject [ˈsʌbdʒɪkt] -K4 n. 主题；科目；[语] 主语；国民 adj. 服从的；易患…的；受制于…的 vt. 使…隶属；使屈从于… 时态: subjected, subjecting, subjects (高雅宝 670/358)","欧陆词典释义：subject [ˈsʌbdʒɪkt] -K4 n. 主题；科目；[语] 主语；国民 adj. 服从的；易患…的；受制于…的 vt. 使…隶属；使屈从于… 时态: subjected, subjecting, subjects (高雅宝 670/358)","It was I who first raised the subject of plastic surgery.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing or person that is being discussed, described or dealt with","example":"an unpleasant subject of conversation"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"an area of knowledge studied in a school, college, etc.","example":"books on many different subjects"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person or thing that is the main feature of a picture or photograph, or that a work of art is based on","example":"a magazine article on the subject of"}]],["sufficient","/səˈfɪʃnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sufficient”.","sufficient [səˈfɪʃnt] -K3 adj. 足够的；充分的 (研四六托雅宝 3099/1582)","欧陆词典释义：sufficient [səˈfɪʃnt] -K3 adj. 足够的；充分的 (研四六托雅宝 3099/1582)","One metre of fabric is sufficient to cover the exterior of an 18-in-diameter hatbox...",""],["summary","/ˈsʌməri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “summary”.","summary [ˈsʌməri] -K2 n. 概要，摘要，总结 adj. 简易的；扼要的 (高研四六雅宝 4917/2708)","欧陆词典释义：summary [ˈsʌməri] -K2 n. 概要，摘要，总结 adj. 简易的；扼要的 (高研四六雅宝 4917/2708)","What follows is a brief summary of the process...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a short statement that gives only the main points of something, not the details","example":"The following is a summary of our conclusions."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"a news summary"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"giving only the main points of something, not the details","example":"a two-page summary of a government report"}]],["supply","/səˈplaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “supply”.","supply [səˈplaɪ] -K4 n. 供给，补给；供应品 vt. 供给，提供；补充 vi. 供给；替代 时态: supplied, supplying, supplies (中高研四六雅 1494/1048)","欧陆词典释义：supply [səˈplaɪ] -K4 n. 供给，补给；供应品 vt. 供给，提供；补充 vi. 供给；替代 时态: supplied, supplying, supplies (中高研四六雅 1494/1048)","an agreement not to produce or supply chemical weapons.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an amount of something that is provided or available to be used","example":"The water supply is unsafe."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the things such as food, medicines, fuel, etc. that are needed by a group of people, for example an army or expedition","example":"Supplies of food are almost exhausted."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the act of supplying something","example":"We cannot guarantee adequate supplies of raw materials."}]],["support","/səˈpɔ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “support”.","support [səˈpɔ:t] -K5 n. 支持，维持；支援，供养；支持者，支撑物 vt. 支持，支撑，支援；扶持，帮助；赡养，供养 时态: supported, supporting, supports (高研四六雅 524/481)","欧陆词典释义：support [səˈpɔ:t] -K5 n. 支持，维持；支援，供养；支持者，支撑物 vt. 支持，支撑，支援；扶持，帮助；赡养，供养 时态: supported, supporting, supports (高研四六雅 524/481)","The vice president insisted that he support ed the hard-working people of New York...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to help or encourage somebody/something by saying or showing that you agree with them/it","example":"to support a proposal"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to give or be ready to give help to somebody if they need it","example":"These measures are strongly supported"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to help or encourage something to be successful by giving it money","example":"If you raise it at the meeting, I'll support you."}]],["task","/tɑ:sk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “task”.","task [tɑ:sk] -K4 n. 工作，作业；任务 vt. 分派任务 时态: tasked, tasking, tasks (中高研四六 1047/779)","欧陆词典释义：task [tɑ:sk] -K4 n. 工作，作业；任务 vt. 分派任务 时态: tasked, tasking, tasks (中高研四六 1047/779)","Walker had the unenviable task of breaking the bad news to Hill...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of work that somebody has to do, especially a hard or unpleasant one","example":"to perform/carry out/complete/undertake a task"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an activity which is designed to help achieve a particular learning goal, especially in language teaching","example":"a daunting/an impossible/a formidable/an unenviable, etc. task"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"a thankless task"}]],["technology","/tekˈnɒlədʒi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “technology”.","technology [tekˈnɒlədʒi] -K4 n. 技术；工艺；术语 (中高研四六雅 585/756)","欧陆词典释义：technology [tekˈnɒlədʒi] -K4 n. 技术；工艺；术语 (中高研四六雅 585/756)","Technology is changing fast...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"scientific knowledge used in practical ways in industry, for example in designing new machines","example":"science and technology"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"machinery or equipment designed using technology","example":"recent advances in medical technology"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"to make use of the most modern technologies"}]],["temporary","/ˈtemprəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “temporary”.","temporary [ˈtemprəri] -K3 n. 临时工，临时雇员 adj. 暂时的，临时的 (高研四六托雅 3150/2302)","欧陆词典释义：temporary [ˈtemprəri] -K3 n. 临时工，临时雇员 adj. 暂时的，临时的 (高研四六托雅 3150/2302)","His job here is only temporary ...",""],["term","/tɜ:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “term”.","term [tɜ:m] -K5 n. 术语；学期；期限；条款；(代数式等的)项 vt. 把…叫做 n. (Term)人名；(泰)丁 时态: termed, terming, terms (中高研四六托雅 626/316)","欧陆词典释义：term [tɜ:m] -K5 n. 术语；学期；期限；条款；(代数式等的)项 vt. 把…叫做 n. (Term)人名；(泰)丁 时态: termed, terming, terms (中高研四六托雅 626/316)","Our goods compete in term s of product quality, reliability and above all variety...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a word or phrase used as the name of something, especially one connected with a particular type of language","example":"a technical/legal/scientific, etc. term"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"(especially in Britain) one of the three periods in the year during which classes are held in schools, universities, etc.","example":"a term of abuse"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a period of time for which something lasts; a fixed or limited time","example":"‘Register’ is the term commonly used to describe different levels of formality in language."}]],["text","/tekst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “text”.","text [tekst] -K3 n. [计] 文本；课文；主题 vt. 发短信 (中高雅 1289/1002)","欧陆词典释义：text [tekst] -K3 n. [计] 文本；课文；主题 vt. 发短信 (中高雅 1289/1002)","The text is precise and informative.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the main printed part of a book or magazine, not the notes, pictures, etc.","example":"My job is to lay out the text and graphics on the page."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"any form of written material","example":"a computer that can process text"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the written form of a speech, a play, an article, etc.","example":"printed text"}]],["traditional","/trəˈdɪʃənl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “traditional”.","traditional [trəˈdɪʃənl] -K4 adj. 传统的；惯例的 (中高四六雅 925/1006)","欧陆词典释义：traditional [trəˈdɪʃənl] -K4 adj. 传统的；惯例的 (中高四六雅 925/1006)"," traditional teaching methods.",""],["transfer","/trænsˈfɜ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “transfer”.","transfer [trænsˈfɜ:(r)] -K4 n. 转让；转移；传递；过户 vt. 使转移；调任 vi. 转让；转学；换车 时态: transferred, transferring, transfers (研四六托雅宝 2315/1593)","欧陆词典释义：transfer [trænsˈfɜ:(r)] -K4 n. 转让；转移；传递；过户 vt. 使转移；调任 vi. 转让；转学；换车 时态: transferred, transferring, transfers (研四六托雅宝 2315/1593)","Remove the wafers with a spoon and transfer them to a plate...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move from one place to another; to move something/somebody from one place to another","example":"The film studio is transferring to Hollywood."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to move from one job, school, situation, etc. to another; to arrange for somebody to move","example":"If I spend a semester in Madrid, will my credits transfer?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"if you transfer","example":"How can I transfer money from my bank account to his?"}]],["transport","/ˈtrænspɔ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “transport”.","transport [ˈtrænspɔ:t] -K4 n. 运输；运输机；狂喜；流放犯 vt. 运输；流放；使狂喜 时态: transported, transporting, transports (高研四六雅宝 4640/1202)","欧陆词典释义：transport [ˈtrænspɔ:t] -K4 n. 运输；运输机；狂喜；流放犯 vt. 运输；流放；使狂喜 时态: transported, transporting, transports (高研四六雅宝 4640/1202)","Have you got your own transport ?...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a system for carrying people or goods from one place to another using vehicles, roads, etc.","example":"air/freight/road transport"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a vehicle or method of travel","example":"the government’s transport policy"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the activity or business of carrying goods from one place to another using lorries/trucks, trains, etc.","example":"Applicants must have their own transport."}]],["trend","/trend/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “trend”.","trend [trend] -K3 n. 趋势，倾向；走向 vt. 使…趋向 vi. 趋向，伸向 n. (Trend)人名；(英)特伦德 时态: trended, trending, trends (高研四六托雅宝 1697/1949)","欧陆词典释义：trend [trend] -K3 n. 趋势，倾向；走向 vt. 使…趋向 vi. 趋向，伸向 n. (Trend)人名；(英)特伦德 时态: trended, trending, trends (高研四六托雅宝 1697/1949)","This is a growing trend .",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change or develop in a general direction","example":"Prices have been trending upwards."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be discussed a lot on a social media","example":"See what's trending on Twitter in your local area right now."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a general direction in which a situation is changing or developing","example":"economic/social/political trends"}]],["treatment","/ˈtri:tmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “treatment”.","treatment [ˈtri:tmənt] -K4 n. 治疗，疗法；处理；对待 (中高四六托雅 745/766)","欧陆词典释义：treatment [ˈtri:tmənt] -K4 n. 治疗，疗法；处理；对待 (中高四六托雅 745/766)","Many patients are not getting the medical treatment they need.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that is done to cure an illness or injury, or to make somebody look and feel good","example":"He is receiving treatment for shock."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a way of behaving towards or dealing with a person or thing","example":"She is responding"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a way of dealing with or discussing a subject, work of art, etc.","example":"to require hospital/medical treatment"}]],["unit","/ˈju:nɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “unit”.","unit [ˈju:nɪt] -K4 n. 单位，单元；装置；[军] 部队；部件 (中高研四六 966/560)","欧陆词典释义：unit [ˈju:nɪt] -K4 n. 单位，单元；装置；[军] 部队；部件 (中高研四六 966/560)","Agriculture was based in the past on the family as a unit .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a single thing, person or group that is complete by itself but can also form part of something larger","example":"The cell is the unit of which all living organisms are composed."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a single item of the type of product that a company sells","example":"The basic unit"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of people who work or live together, especially for a particular purpose","example":"The game's selling price was $15 per unit."}]],["valid","/ˈvælɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “valid”.","valid [ˈvælɪd] -K2 adj. 有效的；有根据的；合法的；正当的 (高研四六托 4703/3211)","欧陆词典释义：valid [ˈvælɪd] -K2 adj. 有效的；有根据的；合法的；正当的 (高研四六托 4703/3211)","They put forward many valid reasons for not exporting...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that is legally or officially acceptable","example":"a valid passport"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"based on what is logical or true","example":"a bus pass valid for 1 month"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that is accepted by the system","example":"They have a valid claim to compensation."}]],["value","/ˈvælju:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “value”.","value [ˈvælju:] -K5 n. 值；价值；价格；重要性；确切涵义 vt. 评价；重视；估价 时态: valued, valuing, values (中高研四六雅 499/367)","欧陆词典释义：value [ˈvælju:] -K5 n. 值；价值；价格；重要性；确切涵义 vt. 评价；重视；估价 时态: valued, valuing, values (中高研四六雅 499/367)","The value of this work experience should not be underestimated...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"how much something is worth in money or other goods for which it can be exchanged","example":"to go up/rise/increase in value"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"how much something is worth compared with its price","example":"to go down/fall/drop in value"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the quality of being useful or important","example":"rising property values"}]],["variety","/vəˈraɪəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “variety”.","variety [vəˈraɪəti] -K4 n. 多样；种类；杂耍；变化，多样化 (高研四六托雅 1171/977)","欧陆词典释义：variety [vəˈraɪəti] -K4 n. 多样；种类；杂耍；变化，多样化 (高研四六托雅 1171/977)","Susan's idea of freedom was to have variety in her life style...",""],["vehicle","/ˈvi:əkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “vehicle”.","vehicle [ˈvi:əkl] -K4 n. [车辆] 车辆；工具；交通工具；运载工具；传播媒介；媒介物 (中高研四六托雅宝 1293/1319)","欧陆词典释义：vehicle [ˈvi:əkl] -K4 n. [车辆] 车辆；工具；交通工具；运载工具；传播媒介；媒介物 (中高研四六托雅宝 1293/1319)","The vehicle would not have the capacity to make the journey on one tank of fuel.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that is used for transporting people or goods from one place to another, such as a car or lorry/truck","example":"motor vehicles ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that can be used to express your ideas or feelings or as a way of achieving something","example":"Are you the driver of this vehicle?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"rows of parked vehicles"}]],["version","/ˈvɜ:ʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “version”.","version [ˈvɜ:ʃn] -K4 n. 版本；译文；倒转术 (高研四六托雅 1130/953)","欧陆词典释义：version [ˈvɜ:ʃn] -K4 n. 版本；译文；倒转术 (高研四六托雅 1130/953)","an updated version of his book...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a form of something that is slightly different from an earlier form or from other forms of the same thing","example":"There are two versions of the game, a long one and a short one."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a description of an event from the position of a particular person or group of people","example":"the latest version"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a film/movie, play, piece of music, etc. that is based on a particular piece of work but is in a different form, style or language","example":"the de luxe/luxury version"}]],["view","/vju:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “view”.","view [vju:] -K5 n. 观察；视野；意见；风景 vt. 观察；考虑；查看 时态: viewed, viewing, views (高研四六雅 485/311)","欧陆词典释义：view [vju:] -K5 n. 观察；视野；意见；风景 vt. 观察；考虑；查看 时态: viewed, viewing, views (高研四六雅 485/311)","Washington and Moscow are believed to have similar view s on Kashmir...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a personal opinion about something; an attitude towards something","example":"to have different/conflicting/opposing views"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a way of understanding or thinking about something","example":"to have strong"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"used when you are talking about whether you can see something or whether something can be seen in a particular situation","example":"His views on the subject were well known."}]],["vision","/ˈvɪʒn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “vision”.","vision [ˈvɪʒn] -K3 n. 视力；美景；眼力；幻象；想象力；幻视（漫威漫画旗下超级英雄） vt. 想象；显现；梦见 (研四六托 1216/1921)","欧陆词典释义：vision [ˈvɪʒn] -K3 n. 视力；美景；眼力；幻象；想象力；幻视（漫威漫画旗下超级英雄） vt. 想象；显现；梦见 (研四六托 1216/1921)","I have a vision of a society that is free of exploitation and injustice...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to see; the area that you can see from a particular position","example":"to have good/perfect/poor/blurred/normal vision"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an idea or a picture in your imagination","example":"20–20 vision"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a dream or similar experience, especially of a religious kind","example":"Cats have good night vision"}]],["volume","/ˈvɒlju:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “volume”.","volume [ˈvɒlju:m] -K4 n. 量；体积；卷；音量；大量；册 adj. 大量的 vt. 把…收集成卷 vi. 成团卷起 (研四六托雅 1917/1358)","欧陆词典释义：volume [ˈvɒlju:m] -K4 n. 量；体积；卷；音量；大量；册 adj. 大量的 vt. 把…收集成卷 vi. 成团卷起 (研四六托雅 1917/1358)","Senior officials will be discussing how the volume of sales might be reduced.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount of space that an object or a substance fills; the amount of space that a container has","example":"How do you measure the volume of a gas?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount of something","example":"jars of different volumes"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount of sound that is produced by a television, radio, etc.","example":"Wait until the dough doubles in volume before kneading it again."}]],["welfare","/ˈwelfeə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “welfare”.","welfare [ˈwelfeə(r)] -3 n. 福利；幸福；福利事业；安宁 adj. 福利的；接受社会救济的 (高研四六托雅 1933/1883)","欧陆词典释义：welfare [ˈwelfeə(r)] -3 n. 福利；幸福；福利事业；安宁 adj. 福利的；接受社会救济的 (高研四六托雅 1933/1883)","I do not think he is considering Emma's welfare ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the general health, happiness and safety of a person, an animal or a group","example":"We are concerned about the child's welfare."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"practical or financial help that is provided, often by the government, for people or animals that need it","example":"The state is still the main provider of welfare."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"money that the government pays regularly to people who are poor, unemployed, sick, etc.","example":"child welfare"}]],["widespread","/ˈwaɪdspred/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “widespread”.","widespread [ˈwaɪdspred] -3 adj. 普遍的，广泛的；分布广的 (高研四六托 3282/2621)","欧陆词典释义：widespread [ˈwaɪdspred] -3 adj. 普遍的，广泛的；分布广的 (高研四六托 3282/2621)","There is widespread support for the new proposals...",""],["accessibility","/əkˌsesə'bɪlətɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accessibility”.","accessibility [əkˌsesə'bɪlətɪ] n. 易接近；可亲；可以得到 (托 10407/12242)","欧陆词典释义：accessibility [əkˌsesə'bɪlətɪ] n. 易接近；可亲；可以得到 (托 10407/12242)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accessibility”.",""],["administration","/ədˌmɪnɪˈstreɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “administration”.","administration [ədˌmɪnɪˈstreɪʃn] -4 n. 管理；行政；实施；行政机构 (高研四六托雅 635/1383)","欧陆词典释义：administration [ədˌmɪnɪˈstreɪʃn] -4 n. 管理；行政；实施；行政机构 (高研四六托雅 635/1383)","Too much time is spent on administration .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the activities that are done in order to plan, organize and run a business, school or other institution","example":"Administration costs are passed on to the customer."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process or act of organizing the way that something is done","example":"the day-to-day administration of a company"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the people who plan, organize and run a business, an institution, etc.","example":"I work in the Sales Administration department."}]],["assessment","/əˈsesmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assessment”.","assessment [əˈsesmənt] n. 评定；估价 (高六托雅宝 1552/1249)","欧陆词典释义：assessment [əˈsesmənt] n. 评定；估价 (高六托雅宝 1552/1249)","There is little assessment of the damage to the natural environment...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an opinion or a judgement about somebody/something that has been thought about very carefully","example":"a detailed assessment of the risks involved"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of judging or forming an opinion about somebody/something","example":"his assessment of the situation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an amount that has been calculated and that must be paid","example":"An adequate environmental impact assessment was not carried out on the bypass project."}]],["association","/əˌsəʊʃiˈeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “association”.","association [əˌsəʊʃiˈeɪʃn] -K4 n. 协会，联盟，社团；联合；联想 (高研四六托雅 1859/742)","欧陆词典释义：association [əˌsəʊʃiˈeɪʃn] -K4 n. 协会，联盟，社团；联合；联想 (高研四六托雅 1859/742)","the British Olympic Association...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official group of people who have joined together for a particular purpose","example":"Do you belong to any professional or trade associations?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a connection or relationship between people or organizations","example":"the Football Association"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an idea or a memory that is suggested by somebody/something; a mental connection between ideas","example":"a residents’ association"}]],["assumption","/əˈsʌmpʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assumption”.","assumption [əˈsʌmpʃn] -3 n. 假定；设想；担任；采取 (高研四六托雅宝 2606/1693)","欧陆词典释义：assumption [əˈsʌmpʃn] -3 n. 假定；设想；担任；采取 (高研四六托雅宝 2606/1693)","They have taken a wrong turning in their assumption that all men and women think alike...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a belief or feeling that something is true or that something will happen, although there is no proof","example":"an underlying/implicit assumption"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of taking or beginning to have power or responsibility","example":"We need to challenge some of the basic assumptions of Western philosophy."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"We are working on the assumption that"}]],["attitude","/ˈætɪtju:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attitude”.","attitude [ˈætɪtju:d] -K4 n. 态度；看法；意见；姿势 (高研四 1155/920)","欧陆词典释义：attitude [ˈætɪtju:d] -K4 n. 态度；看法；意见；姿势 (高研四 1155/920)","the general change in attitude towards handicapped people...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way that you think and feel about somebody/something; the way that you behave towards somebody/something that shows how you think and feel","example":"changes in public attitudes to/about marriage"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"confident, sometimes aggressive behaviour that shows you do not care about other people’s opinions and that you want to do things in an individual way","example":"social attitudes to/towards/about/on education"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a position of the body","example":"the government’s attitude towards single parents"}]],["availability","/əˌveɪlə'bɪlətɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “availability”.","availability [əˌveɪlə'bɪlətɪ] n. 可用性；有效性；实用性 (六 4777/3746)","欧陆词典释义：availability [əˌveɪlə'bɪlətɪ] n. 可用性；有效性；实用性 (六 4777/3746)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “availability”.",""],["background","/ˈbækgraʊnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “background”.","background [ˈbækgraʊnd] -K3 n. 背景；隐蔽的位置 adj. 背景的；发布背景材料的 vt. 作…的背景 (中高研四托雅 1402/1369)","欧陆词典释义：background [ˈbækgraʊnd] -K3 n. 背景；隐蔽的位置 adj. 背景的；发布背景材料的 vt. 作…的背景 (中高研四托雅 1402/1369)","Moulded by his background , he could not escape the traditional role of strict father...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the details of a person’s family, education, experience, etc.","example":"a person’s family/social/cultural/educational/class background"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the circumstances or past events that help explain why something is how it is; information about these","example":"The job would suit someone with a business background."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the part of a picture, photograph or view behind the main objects, people, etc.","example":"In spite of their very different backgrounds, they immediately became friends."}]],["behavior","/bɪ'heɪvjə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “behavior”.","behavior [bɪ'heɪvjə] n. 行为，举止；态度；反应 (研四六托雅 658/28403)","欧陆词典释义：behavior [bɪ'heɪvjə] n. 行为，举止；态度；反应 (研四六托雅 658/28403)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “behavior”.",""],["competition","/ˌkɒmpəˈtɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “competition”.","competition [ˌkɒmpəˈtɪʃn] -K4 n. 竞争；比赛，竞赛 (中高研四六托雅 1345/992)","欧陆词典释义：competition [ˌkɒmpəˈtɪʃn] -K4 n. 竞争；比赛，竞赛 (中高研四六托雅 1345/992)","There's been some fierce competition for the title...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a situation in which people or organizations compete with each other for something that not everyone can have","example":"There is now intense competition between schools to attract students."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an event in which people compete with each other to find out who is the best at something","example":"We are in competition with"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the people who are competing against somebody","example":"We won the contract in the face of stiff competition"}]],["conclusion","/kənˈklu:ʒn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conclusion”.","conclusion [kənˈklu:ʒn] -K3 n. 结论；结局；推论 (高研四六雅 1666/1282)","欧陆词典释义：conclusion [kənˈklu:ʒn] -K3 n. 结论；结局；推论 (高研四六雅 1666/1282)","Over the years I've come to the conclusion that she's a very great musician...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that you decide when you have thought about all the information connected with the situation","example":"I've come to the conclusion"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the end of something such as a speech or a piece of writing","example":"It took the jury some time to reach the conclusion"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the formal and final arrangement of something official","example":"New evidence might lead to the conclusion"}]],["condition","/kənˈdɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “condition”.","condition [kənˈdɪʃn] -K5 n. 条件；情况；环境；身份 vt. 决定；使适应；使健康；以…为条件 时态: conditioned, conditioning, conditions (中高研四六托雅 629/399)","欧陆词典释义：condition [kənˈdɪʃn] -K5 n. 条件；情况；环境；身份 vt. 决定；使适应；使健康；以…为条件 时态: conditioned, conditioning, conditions (中高研四六托雅 629/399)","He remains in a critical condition in a California hospital...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state that something is in","example":"to be in bad/good/excellent condition"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the state of somebody’s health or how fit they are","example":"a used car in perfect condition"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an illness or a medical problem that you have for a long time because it is not possible to cure it","example":"The house is in a generally poor condition."}]],["construction","/kənˈstrʌkʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “construction”.","construction [kənˈstrʌkʃn] -K3 n. 建设；建筑物；解释；造句 (高研四六托雅 1415/1442)","欧陆词典释义：construction [kənˈstrʌkʃn] -K3 n. 建设；建筑物；解释；造句 (高研四六托雅 1415/1442)","He'd already started construction on a hunting lodge.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process or method of building or making something, especially roads, buildings, bridges, etc.","example":"the construction industry"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way that something has been built or made","example":"road construction"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that has been built or made","example":"Work has begun on the construction of the new airport."}]],["contemporary","/kənˈtemprəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contemporary”.","contemporary [kənˈtemprəri] -K3 n. 同时代的人；同时期的东西 adj. 当代的；同时代的；属于同一时期的 (高研四六托雅 1947/2068)","欧陆词典释义：contemporary [kənˈtemprəri] -K3 n. 同时代的人；同时期的东西 adj. 当代的；同时代的；属于同一时期的 (高研四六托雅 1947/2068)","She writes a lot of contemporary music for people like Whitney Houston...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"belonging to the same time","example":"We have no contemporary account of the battle ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"belonging to the present time","example":"He was contemporary with the dramatist Congreve."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"life in contemporary Britain"}]],["contribution","/ˌkɒntrɪˈbju:ʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contribution”.","contribution [ˌkɒntrɪˈbju:ʃn] -K n. 贡献；捐献；投稿 (高研四雅 1776/1201)","欧陆词典释义：contribution [ˌkɒntrɪˈbju:ʃn] -K n. 贡献；捐献；投稿 (高研四雅 1776/1201)","American economists have made important contribution s to the field of financial and corporate economics...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a sum of money that is given to a person or an organization in order to help pay for something","example":"to make a contribution"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a sum of money that you pay regularly to your employer or the government in order to pay for benefits such as health insurance, a pension, etc.","example":"a substantial contribution"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an action or a service that helps to cause or increase something","example":"All contributions will be gratefully received."}]],["convention","/kənˈvenʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “convention”.","convention [kənˈvenʃn] -K3 n. 大会；[法] 惯例；[计] 约定；[法] 协定；习俗 (研四六托雅 2472/1947)","欧陆词典释义：convention [kənˈvenʃn] -K3 n. 大会；[法] 惯例；[计] 约定；[法] 协定；习俗 (研四六托雅 2472/1947)","It's just a social convention that men don't wear skirts...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way in which something is done that most people in a society expect and consider to be polite or the right way to do it","example":"social conventions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large meeting of the members of a profession, a political party, etc.","example":"By convention"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official agreement between countries or leaders","example":"She is a young woman who enjoys flouting conventions."}]],["creation","/kriˈeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “creation”.","creation [kriˈeɪʃn] -2 n. 创造，创作；创作物，产物 (雅 2114/1844)","欧陆词典释义：creation [kriˈeɪʃn] -2 n. 创造，创作；创作物，产物 (雅 2114/1844)","the Creation of the universe as told in Genesis Chapter One...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act or process of making something that is new, or of causing something to exist that did not exist before","example":"the process of database creation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that somebody has made, especially something that shows ability or imagination","example":"wealth creation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the making of the world, especially by God as described in the Bible","example":"He had been with the company since its creation in 1989."}]],["definition","/ˌdefɪˈnɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “definition”.","definition [ˌdefɪˈnɪʃn] -K3 n. 定义；[物] 清晰度；解说 (研四六托宝 2110/1533)","欧陆词典释义：definition [ˌdefɪˈnɪʃn] -K3 n. 定义；[物] 清晰度；解说 (研四六托宝 2110/1533)","There is no general agreement on a standard definition of intelligence...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an explanation of the meaning of a word or phrase, especially in a dictionary; the act of stating the meanings of words and phrases","example":"clear simple definitions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"what an idea, etc. means","example":"Neighbours by definition"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality of being clear and easy to see","example":"It is important to clarify what is meant by"}]],["delivery","/dɪˈlɪvəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “delivery”.","delivery [dɪˈlɪvəri] -K3 n. [贸易] 交付；分娩；递送 (研四六雅 2804/2169)","欧陆词典释义：delivery [dɪˈlɪvəri] -K3 n. [贸易] 交付；分娩；递送 (研四六雅 2804/2169)","Please allow 28 days for delivery ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of taking goods, letters, etc. to the people they have been sent to","example":"a delivery van"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of giving birth to a baby","example":"Please pay for goods on delivery"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way in which somebody speaks, sings a song, etc. in public","example":"Allow 28 days for delivery"}]],["development","/dɪˈveləpmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “development”.","development [dɪˈveləpmənt] -K5 n. 发展；开发；发育；住宅小区（专指由同一开发商开发的）；[摄] 显影 (中高雅 448/234)","欧陆词典释义：development [dɪˈveləpmənt] -K5 n. 发展；开发；发育；住宅小区（专指由同一开发商开发的）；[摄] 显影 (中高雅 448/234)","an ideal system for studying the development of the embryo...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the gradual growth of something so that it becomes more advanced, stronger, etc.","example":"a baby’s development in the womb"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of producing or creating something new or more advanced; a new or advanced product","example":"the development of basic skills such as literacy and numeracy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a new event or stage that is likely to affect what happens in a continuing situation","example":"career development"}]],["disadvantage","/ˌdɪsədˈvɑ:ntɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “disadvantage”.","disadvantage [ˌdɪsədˈvɑ:ntɪdʒ] -K2 n. 缺点；不利条件；损失 时态: disadvantaged, disadvantaging, disadvantages (高四六托 6291/3518)","欧陆词典释义：disadvantage [ˌdɪsədˈvɑ:ntɪdʒ] -K2 n. 缺点；不利条件；损失 时态: disadvantaged, disadvantaging, disadvantages (高四六托 6291/3518)","His two main rivals suffer the disadvantage of having been long-term political exiles...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to cause problems and tend to stop somebody/something from succeeding or making progress","example":"Some pension plans may disadvantage women."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that causes problems and tends to stop somebody/something from succeeding or making progress","example":"a serious/severe/considerable disadvantage"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"One major disadvantage"}]],["economic","/ˌi:kəˈnɒmɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “economic”.","economic [ˌi:kəˈnɒmɪk] -K5 adj. 经济的，经济上的；经济学的 (研四六托雅 453/402)","欧陆词典释义：economic [ˌi:kəˈnɒmɪk] -K5 adj. 经济的，经济上的；经济学的 (研四六托雅 453/402)","Poland's radical economic reforms...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with the trade, industry and development of wealth of a country, an area or a society","example":"social, economic and political issues"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"producing enough profit to continue","example":"economic growth/cooperation/development/reform"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"the government’s economic policy"}]],["emphasis","/ˈemfəsɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “emphasis”.","emphasis [ˈemfəsɪs] -K3 n. 重点；强调；加强语气 (研四六托 2346/1719)","欧陆词典释义：emphasis [ˈemfəsɪs] -K3 n. 重点；强调；加强语气 (研四六托 2346/1719)","Too much emphasis is placed on research...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"special importance that is given to something","example":"The emphasis is very much on learning the spoken language."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the extra force given to a word or phrase when spoken, especially in order to show that it is important; a way of writing a word (for example drawing a line underneath it) to show that it is important","example":"to put/lay/place emphasis"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"Increased emphasis is now being placed on corporate image."}]],["engineering","/ˌendʒɪˈnɪərɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “engineering”.","engineering [ˌendʒɪˈnɪərɪŋ] -K3 n. 工程，工程学 v. 设计；管理（engineer的ing形式）；建造 (研四六雅 2385/1815)","欧陆词典释义：engineering [ˌendʒɪˈnɪərɪŋ] -K3 n. 工程，工程学 v. 设计；管理（engineer的ing形式）；建造 (研四六雅 2385/1815)","the design and engineering of aircraft and space vehicles.",""],["evaluation","/ɪˌvæljʊ'eɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “evaluation”.","evaluation [ɪˌvæljʊ'eɪʃn] n. 评价；[审计] 评估；估价；求值 (六宝 2354/2732)","欧陆词典释义：evaluation [ɪˌvæljʊ'eɪʃn] n. 评价；[审计] 评估；估价；求值 (六宝 2354/2732)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “evaluation”.",""],["examination","/ɪgˌzæmɪˈneɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “examination”.","examination [ɪgˌzæmɪˈneɪʃn] -K3 n. 考试；检查；查问 (中四六雅 3069/1531)","欧陆词典释义：examination [ɪgˌzæmɪˈneɪʃn] -K3 n. 考试；检查；查问 (中四六雅 3069/1531)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “examination”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of looking at or considering something very carefully","example":"to sit an examination in mathematics"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a close look at something/somebody, especially to see if there is anything wrong or to find the cause of a problem","example":"successful candidates in GCSE examinations"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Applicants are selected for jobs on the results of a competitive examination."}]],["expectation","/ˌekspekˈteɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “expectation”.","expectation [ˌekspekˈteɪʃn] -K3 n. 期待；预期；指望 (高研四六 1890/1970)","欧陆词典释义：expectation [ˌekspekˈteɪʃn] -K3 n. 期待；预期；指望 (高研四六 1890/1970)","Students' expectation s were as varied as their expertise...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a belief that something will happen because it is likely","example":"We are confident in our expectation of a full recovery."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a hope that something good will happen","example":"There was a general expectation that he would win."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a strong belief about the way something should happen or how somebody should behave","example":"The expectation is that property prices will rise."}]],["experiment","/ɪkˈsperɪmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “experiment”.","experiment [ɪkˈsperɪmənt] -K3 n. 实验，试验；尝试 vi. 尝试；进行实验 时态: experimented, experimenting, experiments (中高研四六雅 1990/1651)","欧陆词典释义：experiment [ɪkˈsperɪmənt] -K3 n. 实验，试验；尝试 vi. 尝试；进行实验 时态: experimented, experimenting, experiments (中高研四六雅 1990/1651)","The astronauts are conducting a series of experiment s to learn more about how the body adapts to weightlessness...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a scientific test that is done in order to study what happens and to gain new knowledge","example":"to do/perform/conduct an experiment"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a new activity, idea or method that you try out to see what happens or what effect it has","example":"proved by experiment"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"laboratory experiments"}]],["explanation","/ˌekspləˈneɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “explanation”.","explanation [ˌekspləˈneɪʃn] -K3 n. 说明，解释；辩解 (高研四六 2054/1492)","欧陆词典释义：explanation [ˌekspləˈneɪʃn] -K3 n. 说明，解释；辩解 (高研四六 2054/1492)","She told the court she would give a full explanation of the prosecution's decision on Monday...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a statement, fact, or situation that tells you why something happened; a reason given for something","example":"The most likely explanation is that his plane was delayed."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a statement or piece of writing that tells you how something works or makes something easier to understand","example":"to offer/provide an explanation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"I can't think of any possible explanation for his absence."}]],["account","/əˈkaʊnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “account”.","account [əˈkaʊnt] -K5 n. 账户；解释；账目，账单；理由；描述 vt. 认为；把…视为 vi. 解释；导致；报账 时态: accounted, accounting, accounts (高研四托雅 1071/498)","欧陆词典释义：account [əˈkaʊnt] -K5 n. 账户；解释；账目，账单；理由；描述 vt. 认为；把…视为 vi. 解释；导致；报账 时态: accounted, accounting, accounts (高研四托雅 1071/498)","Some banks make it difficult to open an account ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an arrangement that somebody has with a bank, etc. to keep money there, take some out, etc.","example":"I don't have a bank account."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a written record of money that is owed to a business and of money that has been paid by it","example":"to have an account at/with"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an arrangement with a shop/store or business to pay bills for goods or services at a later time, for example in regular amounts every month","example":"to open/close an account"}]],["act","/ækt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “act”.","act [ækt] -K5 n. 行为，行动；法令，法案；（戏剧，歌剧的）一幕，段；装腔作势 vt. 扮演；装作，举动像 vi. 行动；扮演，充当；表现，举止；假装，演戏；起作用，见效 时态: acted, acting, acts (中高研四 837/371)","欧陆词典释义：act [ækt] -K5 n. 行为，行动；法令，法案；（戏剧，歌剧的）一幕，段；装腔作势 vt. 扮演；装作，举动像 vi. 行动；扮演，充当；表现，举止；假装，演戏；起作用，见效 时态: acted, acting, acts (中高研四 837/371)","The deaths occurred when police act ed to stop widespread looting and vandalism...",""],["advantage","/ədˈvɑ:ntɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “advantage”.","advantage [ədˈvɑ:ntɪdʒ] -K4 n. 优势；利益；有利条件 vt. 有利于；使处于优势 vi. 获利 时态: advantaged, advantaging, advantages (中高研四 1301/969)","欧陆词典释义：advantage [ədˈvɑ:ntɪdʒ] -K4 n. 优势；利益；有利条件 vt. 有利于；使处于优势 vi. 获利 时态: advantaged, advantaging, advantages (中高研四 1301/969)","They are deliberately flouting the law in order to obtain an advantage over their competitors...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that helps you to be better or more successful than other people","example":"a big/great/definite advantage"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a quality of something that makes it better or more useful","example":"an unfair advantage ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the first point scored after a score of 40–40.","example":"She had the advantage of"}]],["allocation","/ˌæləˈkeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “allocation”.","allocation [ˌæləˈkeɪʃn] n. 分配，配置；安置 (7082/3262)","欧陆词典释义：allocation [ˌæləˈkeɪʃn] n. 分配，配置；安置 (7082/3262)","The aid allocation for Pakistan was still under review...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an amount of money, space, etc. that is given to somebody for a particular purpose","example":"We have spent our entire allocation for the year."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of giving something to somebody for a particular purpose","example":"the allocation of food to those who need it most"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The allocation must be made according to a strict set of criteria."}]],["amendment","/əˈmendmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “amendment”.","amendment [əˈmendmənt] -3 n. 修正案；改善；改正 (托宝 3667/2864)","欧陆词典释义：amendment [əˈmendmənt] -3 n. 修正案；改善；改正 (托宝 3667/2864)","an amendment to the defense bill.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small change or improvement that is made to a law or a document; the process of changing a law or a document","example":"to introduce/propose/table an amendment"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a statement of a change to the Constitution","example":"Parliament passed the bill without further amendment."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"In the US the first ten amendments to the Constitution are called the Bill of Rights","example":"She made several minor amendments to her essay."}]],["applicant","/ˈæplɪkənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “applicant”.","applicant [ˈæplɪkənt] -2 n. 申请人，申请者；请求者 (高四托雅宝 5512/3159)","欧陆词典释义：applicant [ˈæplɪkənt] -2 n. 申请人，申请者；请求者 (高四托雅宝 5512/3159)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “applicant”.",""],["appointment","/əˈpɔɪntmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “appointment”.","appointment [əˈpɔɪntmənt] -K3 n. 任命；约定；任命的职位 (高研四六托雅 3021/1558)","欧陆词典释义：appointment [əˈpɔɪntmənt] -K3 n. 任命；约定；任命的职位 (高研四六托雅 3021/1558)","His appointment to the Cabinet would please the right-wing.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a formal arrangement to meet or visit somebody at a particular time, especially for a reason connected with their work","example":"I've got a dental appointment"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of choosing a person for a job or position of responsibility; the fact of being chosen for a job, etc.","example":"Do you have an appointment?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a job or position of responsibility","example":"to make/keep an appointment"}]],["architecture","/ˈɑ:kɪtektʃə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “architecture”.","architecture [ˈɑ:kɪtektʃə(r)] -2 n. 建筑学；建筑风格；建筑式样；架构 (高研四六托雅 3509/2712)","欧陆词典释义：architecture [ˈɑ:kɪtektʃə(r)] -2 n. 建筑学；建筑风格；建筑式样；架构 (高研四六托雅 3509/2712)","He studied classical architecture and design in Rome.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the art and study of designing buildings","example":"to study architecture"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the design or style of a building or buildings","example":"the architecture of the eighteenth century"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the design and structure of a computer system","example":"modern architecture"}]],["assistance","/əˈsɪstəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assistance”.","assistance [əˈsɪstəns] -K3 n. 援助，帮助；辅助设备 (高研托雅 2081/2096)","欧陆词典释义：assistance [əˈsɪstəns] -K3 n. 援助，帮助；辅助设备 (高研托雅 2081/2096)","Since 1976 he has been operating the shop with the assistance of volunteers...",""],["atmosphere","/ˈætməsfɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “atmosphere”.","atmosphere [ˈætməsfɪə(r)] -K3 n. 气氛；大气；空气 (高研四六托 2217/1855)","欧陆词典释义：atmosphere [ˈætməsfɪə(r)] -K3 n. 气氛；大气；空气 (高研四六托 2217/1855)","dangerous levels of pollution in the Earth's atmosphere ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the mixture of gases that surrounds the earth","example":"the upper atmosphere"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a mixture of gases that surrounds another planet or a star","example":"pollution of the atmosphere"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the air in a room or in a confined space; the air around a place","example":"Saturn’s atmosphere"}]],["audience","/ˈɔ:diəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “audience”.","audience [ˈɔ:diəns] -K4 n. 观众；听众；读者；接见；正式会见；拜会 (高研四六托雅宝 1074/1463)","欧陆词典释义：audience [ˈɔ:diəns] -K4 n. 观众；听众；读者；接见；正式会见；拜会 (高研四六托雅宝 1074/1463)","The entire audience broke into loud applause...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the group of people who have gathered to watch or listen to something (a play, concert, somebody speaking, etc.)","example":"The audience was/were clapping for 10 minutes."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a number of people or a particular group of people who watch, read or listen to the same thing","example":"an audience of 10 000"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a formal meeting with an important person","example":"The debate was televised in front of a live audience"}]],["balance","/ˈbæləns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “balance”.","balance [ˈbæləns] -K4 n. 平衡；余额；匀称 vt. 使平衡；结算；使相称 vi. 保持平衡；相称；抵销 n. (Balance)人名；(西)巴兰塞 时态: balanced, balancing, balances (高研四托雅 1631/1176)","欧陆词典释义：balance [ˈbæləns] -K4 n. 平衡；余额；匀称 vt. 使平衡；结算；使相称 vi. 保持平衡；相称；抵销 n. (Balance)人名；(西)巴兰塞 时态: balanced, balancing, balances (高研四托雅 1631/1176)","I balance d on the ledge...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a situation in which different things exist in equal, correct or good amounts","example":"This newspaper maintains a good balance in its presentation of different opinions."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the ability to keep steady with an equal amount of weight on each side of the body","example":"Tourists often disturb the delicate balance of nature on the island."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the amount that is left after taking numbers or money away from a total","example":"His wife's death disturbed the balance of his mind"}]],["basis","/ˈbeɪsɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “basis”.","basis [ˈbeɪsɪs] -K4 n. 基础；底部；主要成分；基本原则或原理 (高研四雅 1307/694)","欧陆词典释义：basis [ˈbeɪsɪs] -K4 n. 基础；底部；主要成分；基本原则或原理 (高研四雅 1307/694)","We're going to be meeting there on a regular basis ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the reason why people take a particular action","example":"She was chosen for the job on the basis of"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way things are organized or arranged","example":"Some movies have been banned on the basis that"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the important facts, ideas or events that support something and that it can develop from","example":"He said no but he didn’t give a reason."}]],["campaign","/kæmˈpeɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “campaign”.","campaign [kæmˈpeɪn] -K5 n. 运动；活动；战役 vi. 作战；参加竞选；参加活动 时态: campaigned, campaigning, campaigns (高研四六托雅宝 640/956)","欧陆词典释义：campaign [kæmˈpeɪn] -K5 n. 运动；活动；战役 vi. 作战；参加竞选；参加活动 时态: campaigned, campaigning, campaigns (高研四六托雅宝 640/956)","During his election campaign he promised to put the economy back on its feet...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a series of planned activities that are intended to achieve a particular social, commercial or political aim","example":"to conduct a campaign"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a series of attacks and battles that are intended to achieve a particular military aim during a war","example":"a campaign against ageism in the workplace"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"the campaign for parliamentary reform"}]],["characteristic","/ˌkærəktəˈrɪstɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “characteristic”.","characteristic [ˌkærəktəˈrɪstɪk] -K3 n. 特征；特性；特色 adj. 典型的；特有的；表示特性的 (高研四六托雅宝 2032/1811)","欧陆词典释义：characteristic [ˌkærəktəˈrɪstɪk] -K3 n. 特征；特性；特色 adj. 典型的；特有的；表示特性的 (高研四六托雅宝 2032/1811)","Genes determine the characteristic s of every living thing.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"very typical of something or of somebody’s character","example":"She spoke with characteristic enthusiasm."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"a problem that was fairly characteristic of late eighteenth century society"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a typical feature or quality that something/somebody has","example":"his highly characteristic features"}]],["citation","/saɪˈteɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “citation”.","citation [saɪˈteɪʃn] -1 n. 引用，引证；[法] 传票；褒扬 (宝 8370/8272)","欧陆词典释义：citation [saɪˈteɪʃn] -1 n. 引用，引证；[法] 传票；褒扬 (宝 8370/8272)","His citation says he showed outstanding and exemplary courage.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"words or lines taken from a book or a speech","example":"The report contained several citations taken from her PhD thesis."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official statement about something special that somebody has done, especially about acts of courage in a war","example":"a citation for bravery"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an act of citing","example":"Space does not permit the citation of the examples."}]],["clarification","/ˌklærəfɪ'keɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “clarification”.","clarification [ˌklærəfɪ'keɪʃn] n. 澄清，说明；净化 (托 11316/8909)","欧陆词典释义：clarification [ˌklærəfɪ'keɪʃn] n. 澄清，说明；净化 (托 11316/8909)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “clarification”.",""],["climate","/ˈklaɪmət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “climate”.","climate [ˈklaɪmət] -K3 n. 气候；风气；思潮；风土 (高研四托 2103/2643)","欧陆词典释义：climate [ˈklaɪmət] -K3 n. 气候；风气；思潮；风土 (高研四托 2103/2643)","the hot and humid climate of Cyprus.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the regular pattern of weather conditions of a particular place","example":"a mild/temperate/warm/wet climate"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area with particular weather conditions","example":"the harsh climate of the Arctic regions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a general attitude or feeling; an atmosphere or a situation which exists in a particular place","example":"They wanted to move to a warmer climate."}]],["collaboration","/kəˌlæbəˈreɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “collaboration”.","collaboration [kəˌlæbəˈreɪʃn] -2 n. 合作；勾结；通敌 (六托雅 4176/4618)","欧陆词典释义：collaboration [kəˌlæbəˈreɪʃn] -2 n. 合作；勾结；通敌 (六托雅 4176/4618)","There is substantial collaboration with neighbouring departments...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of working with another person or group of people to create or produce something","example":"It was a collaboration that produced extremely useful results."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of work produced by two or more people or groups of people working together","example":"The new plane was a triumph of European industrial and technical collaboration."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of helping the enemy during a war when they have taken control of your country","example":"She wrote the book in collaboration"}]],["collection","/kəˈlekʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “collection”.","collection [kəˈlekʃn] -K4 n. 采集，聚集；[税收] 征收；收藏品；募捐 (高研四六雅宝 1045/1038)","欧陆词典释义：collection [kəˈlekʃn] -K4 n. 采集，聚集；[税收] 征收；收藏品；募捐 (高研四六雅宝 1045/1038)","Robert's collection of prints and paintings has been bought over the years...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of objects, often of the same sort, that have been collected","example":"a stamp/coin, etc. collection"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of objects or people","example":"The painting comes from his private collection."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an act of taking something away from a place; an act of bringing things together into one place","example":"There was a collection of books and shoes on the floor."}]],["combination","/ˌkɒmbɪˈneɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “combination”.","combination [ˌkɒmbɪˈneɪʃn] -K3 n. 结合；组合；联合；[化学] 化合 (研四六托 1808/1732)","欧陆词典释义：combination [ˌkɒmbɪˈneɪʃn] -K3 n. 结合；组合；联合；[化学] 化合 (研四六托 1808/1732)","a fantastic combination of colours.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"two or more things joined or mixed together to form a single unit","example":"His treatment was a combination of surgery, radiation and drugs."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of joining or mixing together two or more things to form a single unit","example":"What an unusual combination of flavours!"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a series of numbers or letters used to open a combination lock","example":"Technology and good management. That's a winning combination"}]],["committee","/kəˈmɪti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “committee”.","committee [kəˈmɪti] -K5 n. 委员会 (高研四六托雅 1428/450)","欧陆词典释义：committee [kəˈmɪti] -K5 n. 委员会 (高研四六托雅 1428/450)","a committee of ministers.",""],["comparison","/kəmˈpærɪsn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “comparison”.","comparison [kəmˈpærɪsn] -K3 n. 比较；对照；比喻；比较关系 (研四宝 2166/1968)","欧陆词典释义：comparison [kəmˈpærɪsn] -K3 n. 比较；对照；比喻；比较关系 (研四宝 2166/1968)","a comparison of the British and German economies...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of comparing two or more people or things","example":"Comparison with other oil-producing countries is extremely interesting."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an occasion when two or more people or things are compared","example":"I enclose the two plans for comparison"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"The education system bears/stands no comparison with"}]],["composition","/ˌkɒmpəˈzɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “composition”.","composition [ˌkɒmpəˈzɪʃn] -1 n. 作文，作曲，作品；[材] 构成；合成物；成分 (中高研四六托雅 3000/2911)","欧陆词典释义：composition [ˌkɒmpəˈzɪʃn] -1 n. 作文，作曲，作品；[材] 构成；合成物；成分 (中高研四六托雅 3000/2911)","Television has transformed the size and social composition of the audience at great sporting occasions...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the different parts which something is made of; the way in which the different parts are organized","example":"the chemical composition of the soil"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of music or art, or a poem","example":"the composition of the board of directors"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of composing","example":"the size and composition of an average class"}]],["conflict","/ˈkɒnflɪkt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conflict”.","conflict [ˈkɒnflɪkt] -K4 n. 冲突，矛盾；斗争；争执 vi. 冲突，抵触；争执；战斗 时态: conflicted, conflicting, conflicts (高研四六托雅宝 1179/1364)","欧陆词典释义：conflict [ˈkɒnflɪkt] -K4 n. 冲突，矛盾；斗争；争执 vi. 冲突，抵触；争执；战斗 时态: conflicted, conflicting, conflicts (高研四六托雅宝 1179/1364)","Try to keep any conflict between you and your ex-partner to a minimum...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a situation in which people, groups or countries are involved in a serious disagreement or argument","example":"a conflict between two cultures"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a violent situation or period of fighting between two countries","example":"The violence was the result of political and ethnic conflicts."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a situation in which there are opposing ideas, opinions, feelings or wishes; a situation in which it is difficult to choose","example":"She found herself in conflict with"}]],["consent","/kənˈsent/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consent”.","consent [kənˈsent] -2 n. 同意；（意见等的）一致；赞成 vi. 同意；赞成；答应 n. (Consent)人名；(法)孔桑 时态: consented, consenting, consents (研四六雅宝 4391/2503)","欧陆词典释义：consent [kənˈsent] -2 n. 同意；（意见等的）一致；赞成 vi. 同意；赞成；答应 n. (Consent)人名；(法)孔桑 时态: consented, consenting, consents (研四六雅宝 4391/2503)","At approximately 11:30 p.m., Pollard finally gave his consent to the search...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"permission to do something, especially given by somebody in authority","example":"Children under 16 cannot give consent"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"agreement about something","example":"The written consent of a parent is required."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an official document giving permission for something","example":"to refuse/withhold"}]],["constraint","/kənˈstreɪnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “constraint”.","constraint [kənˈstreɪnt] -2 n. [数] 约束；局促，态度不自然；强制 (六托宝 4643/2988)","欧陆词典释义：constraint [kənˈstreɪnt] -2 n. [数] 约束；局促，态度不自然；强制 (六托宝 4643/2988)","Their decision to abandon the trip was made because of financial constraint s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that limits or restricts something, or your freedom to do something","example":"constraints of time/money/space"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"strict control over the way that you behave or are allowed to behave","example":"financial/economic/legal/political constraints"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"This decision will impose serious constraints on all schools."}]],["consultation","/ˌkɒnslˈteɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consultation”.","consultation [ˌkɒnslˈteɪʃn] -1 n. 咨询；磋商；[临床] 会诊；讨论会 (5710/2792)","欧陆词典释义：consultation [ˌkɒnslˈteɪʃn] -1 n. 咨询；磋商；[临床] 会诊；讨论会 (5710/2792)","Next week he'll be in Florida for consultation s with President Mitterrand...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of discussing something with somebody or with a group of people before making a decision about it","example":"a consultation document/paper/period/process"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a formal meeting to discuss something","example":"acting in consultation with"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a meeting with an expert, especially a doctor, to get advice or treatment","example":"The decision was taken after close consultation with local residents."}]],["contact","/ˈkɒntækt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contact”.","contact [ˈkɒntækt] -K4 n. 接触，联系 vt. 使接触，联系 vi. 使接触，联系 时态: contacted, contacting, contacts (研四六托雅宝 1480/1196)","欧陆词典释义：contact [ˈkɒntækt] -K4 n. 接触，联系 vt. 使接触，联系 vi. 使接触，联系 时态: contacted, contacting, contacts (研四六托雅宝 1480/1196)","Opposition leaders are denying any contact with the government in Kabul...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of communicating with somebody, especially regularly","example":"I don't have much contact with my uncle."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the state of touching something","example":"There is little contact between the two organizations."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the state of meeting somebody or having to deal with something","example":"Have you kept in contact with"}]],["consumption","/kənˈsʌmpʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consumption”.","consumption [kənˈsʌmpʃn] -2 n. 消费；消耗；肺痨 (研四六托雅 3146/2561)","欧陆词典释义：consumption [kənˈsʌmpʃn] -2 n. 消费；消耗；肺痨 (研四六托雅 3146/2561)","The laws have led to a reduction in fuel consumption in the US.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of using energy, food or materials; the amount used","example":"the production of fuel for domestic consumption"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of buying and using products","example":"Gas and oil consumption always increases in cold weather."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a serious infectious disease of the lungs","example":"The meat was declared unfit for human consumption"}]],["conversion","/kənˈvɜ:ʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conversion”.","conversion [kənˈvɜ:ʃn] -2 n. 转换；变换；[金融] 兑换；改变信仰 (研四六托雅 4664/3129)","欧陆词典释义：conversion [kənˈvɜ:ʃn] -2 n. 转换；变换；[金融] 兑换；改变信仰 (研四六托雅 4664/3129)","the conversion of disused rail lines into cycle routes...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act or process of changing something from one form, use or system to another","example":"the conversion of farm buildings into family homes"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process or experience of changing your religion or beliefs","example":"Conversion to gas central heating will save you a lot of money."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a way of scoring extra points after scoring a try","example":"No conversion from analogue to digital data is needed."}]],["destination","/ˌdestɪˈneɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “destination”.","destination [ˌdestɪˈneɪʃn] -2 n. 目的地，终点 (高研四六托雅 3883/4309)","欧陆词典释义：destination [ˌdestɪˈneɪʃn] -2 n. 目的地，终点 (高研四六托雅 3883/4309)","Spain is still our most popular holiday destination ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place to which somebody/something is going or being sent","example":"popular holiday destinations"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"to arrive at/reach your destination"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a hotel, store, etc. that people will make a special trip to visit","example":"Our luggage was checked all the way through to our final destination"}]],["detection","/dɪˈtekʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “detection”.","detection [dɪˈtekʃn] -1 n. 侦查，探测；发觉，发现；察觉 (四六宝 6216/6133)","欧陆词典释义：detection [dɪˈtekʃn] -1 n. 侦查，探测；发觉，发现；察觉 (四六宝 6216/6133)","the early detection of breast cancer.",""],["discipline","/ˈdɪsəplɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “discipline”.","discipline [ˈdɪsəplɪn] -K3 n. 学科；纪律；训练；惩罚 vt. 训练，训导；惩戒 时态: disciplined, disciplining, disciplines (研四六托雅宝 2278/1450)","欧陆词典释义：discipline [ˈdɪsəplɪn] -K3 n. 学科；纪律；训练；惩罚 vt. 训练，训导；惩戒 时态: disciplined, disciplining, disciplines (研四六托雅宝 2278/1450)","Order and discipline have been placed in the hands of headmasters and governing bodies.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the practice of training people to obey rules and orders and punishing them if they do not; the controlled behaviour or situation that results from this training","example":"The school has a reputation for high standards of discipline."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a method of training your mind or body or of controlling your behaviour; an area of activity where this is necessary","example":"Strict discipline is imposed on army recruits."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the ability to control your behaviour or the way you live, work, etc.","example":"She keeps good discipline in class."}]],["discount","/ˈdɪskaʊnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “discount”.","discount [ˈdɪskaʊnt] -K3 n. 折扣；贴现率 vt. 打折扣；将…贴现；贬损；低估；忽视 vi. 贴现；打折扣出售商品 时态: discounted, discounting, discounts (高研四六托雅宝 4504/3143)","欧陆词典释义：discount [ˈdɪskaʊnt] -K3 n. 折扣；贴现率 vt. 打折扣；将…贴现；贬损；低估；忽视 vi. 贴现；打折扣出售商品 时态: discounted, discounting, discounts (高研四六托雅宝 4504/3143)","They are often available at a discount ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an amount of money that is taken off the usual cost of something","example":"to get/give/offer a discount"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"discount rates/prices"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think or say that something is not important or not true","example":"They're offering a 10% discount on all sofas this month."}]],["diversity","/daɪˈvɜ:səti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “diversity”.","diversity [daɪˈvɜ:səti] -2 n. 多样性；差异 (托宝 2531/4642)","欧陆词典释义：diversity [daɪˈvɜ:səti] -2 n. 多样性；差异 (托宝 2531/4642)","the cultural diversity of British society.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a range of many people or things that are very different from each other","example":"the biological diversity of the rainforests"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality or fact of including a range of many people or things","example":"a great/wide/rich diversity"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"There is a need for greater diversity and choice in education."}]],["document","/ˈdɒkjumənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “document”.","document [ˈdɒkjumənt] -K4 n. 文件，公文；[计] 文档；证件 vt. 用文件证明 时态: documented, documenting, documents (高研四六托宝 1389/1052)","欧陆词典释义：document [ˈdɒkjumənt] -K4 n. 文件，公文；[计] 文档；证件 vt. 用文件证明 时态: documented, documenting, documents (高研四六托宝 1389/1052)","The foreign ministers of the two countries signed the document s today.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official paper or book that gives information about something, or that can be used as evidence or proof of something","example":"legal documents"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a computer file that contains text that has a name that identifies it","example":"travel documents"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Copies of the relevant documents must be filed at court."}]],["effect","/ɪˈfekt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “effect”.","effect [ɪˈfekt] -K5 n. 影响；效果；作用 vt. 产生；达到目的 时态: effected, effecting, effects (高研四六托雅 427/262)","欧陆词典释义：effect [ɪˈfekt] -K5 n. 影响；效果；作用 vt. 产生；达到目的 时态: effected, effecting, effects (高研四六托雅 427/262)","Parents worry about the effect of music on their adolescent's behavior...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a change that somebody/something causes in somebody/something else; a result","example":"the effect of heat on metal"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular look, sound or impression that somebody, such as an artist or a writer, wants to create","example":"dramatic/long-term effects"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"your personal possessions","example":"to learn to distinguish between cause and effect"}]],["engagement","/ɪnˈgeɪdʒmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “engagement”.","engagement [ɪnˈgeɪdʒmənt] -2 n. 婚约；约会；交战；诺言 n. 参与度（指用户点赞、转发、评论、下载文档、观看视频、咨询等交互行为） (研六雅 3812/3950)","欧陆词典释义：engagement [ɪnˈgeɪdʒmənt] -2 n. 婚约；约会；交战；诺言 n. 参与度（指用户点赞、转发、评论、下载文档、观看视频、咨询等交互行为） (研六雅 3812/3950)","He had an engagement at a restaurant in Greek Street at eight.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an agreement to marry somebody; the period during which two people are engaged","example":"Their engagement was announced in the local paper."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an arrangement to do something at a particular time, especially something official or something connected with your job","example":"She has broken off her engagement"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"fighting between two armies, etc.","example":"an engagement party"}]],["enterprise","/ˈentəpraɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “enterprise”.","enterprise [ˈentəpraɪz] -3 n. 企业；事业；进取心；事业心 (高研六托雅宝 2499/1566)","欧陆词典释义：enterprise [ˈentəpraɪz] -3 n. 企业；事业；进取心；事业心 (高研六托雅宝 2499/1566)","There are plenty of small industrial enterprise s.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a company or business","example":"an enterprise with a turnover of $26 billion"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large project, especially one that is difficult","example":"state-owned/public enterprises"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the development of businesses by the people of a country rather than by the government","example":"small and medium-sized enterprises"}]],["equation","/ɪˈkweɪʒn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “equation”.","equation [ɪˈkweɪʒn] -2 n. 方程式，等式；相等；[化学] 反应式 (研四六托雅宝 3982/2458)","欧陆词典释义：equation [ɪˈkweɪʒn] -2 n. 方程式，等式；相等；[化学] 反应式 (研四六托雅宝 3982/2458)","The equation is simple: research breeds new products...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a statement showing that two amounts or values are equal, for example 2x + y = 54","example":"The equation of wealth with happiness can be dangerous."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of making something equal or considering something as equal (","example":"When children enter the equation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a problem or situation in which several things must be considered and dealt with","example":"Money also comes into the equation."}]],["ethical","/ˈeθɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ethical”.","ethical [ˈeθɪkl] -2 n. 处方药 adj. 伦理的；道德的；凭处方出售的 (六 3454/5465)","欧陆词典释义：ethical [ˈeθɪkl] -2 n. 处方药 adj. 伦理的；道德的；凭处方出售的 (六 3454/5465)","the moral and ethical standards in the school.",""],["event","/ɪˈvent/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “event”.","event [ɪˈvent] -K5 n. 事件，大事；项目；结果 (高研四雅 525/473)","欧陆词典释义：event [ɪˈvent] -K5 n. 事件，大事；项目；结果 (高研四雅 525/473)","the event s of Black Wednesday...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that happens, especially something important","example":"The election was the main event of 2008."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a planned public or social occasion","example":"In the light of later events the decision was proved right."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"one of the races or competitions in a sports programme","example":"The decisions we take now may influence the course of events"}]],["exhibition","/ˌeksɪˈbɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “exhibition”.","exhibition [ˌeksɪˈbɪʃn] -K3 n. 展览，显示；展览会；展览品 (高研四六托雅 2476/1426)","欧陆词典释义：exhibition [ˌeksɪˈbɪʃn] -K3 n. 展览，显示；展览会；展览品 (高研四六托雅 2476/1426)","an exhibition of expressionist art.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a collection of things, for example works of art, that are shown to the public","example":"Have you seen the Picasso exhibition?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of showing something, for example works of art, to the public","example":"an exhibition of old photographs"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of showing a skill, a feeling, or a kind of behaviour","example":"She refused to allow the exhibition of her husband's work."}]],["expansion","/ɪkˈspænʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “expansion”.","expansion [ɪkˈspænʃn] n. 膨胀；阐述；扩张物 (研四六托雅 2734/2360)","欧陆词典释义：expansion [ɪkˈspænʃn] n. 膨胀；阐述；扩张物 (研四六托雅 2734/2360)","the rapid expansion of private health insurance.",""],["expense","/ɪkˈspens/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “expense”.","expense [ɪkˈspens] -K3 n. 损失，代价；消费；开支 vt. 向…收取费用 vi. 被花掉 (高研四 2137/1919)","欧陆词典释义：expense [ɪkˈspens] -K3 n. 损失，代价；消费；开支 vt. 向…收取费用 vi. 被花掉 (高研四 2137/1919)","He's bought a specially big TV at vast expense so that everyone can see properly...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the money that you spend on something","example":"The garden was transformed at great expense"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that makes you spend money","example":"No expense was spared"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"money spent in doing a particular job, or for a particular purpose","example":"He's arranged everything, no expense spared"}]],["feedback","/ˈfi:dbæk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “feedback”.","feedback [ˈfi:dbæk] -2 n. 反馈；成果，资料；回复 (研四六雅宝 3888/4828)","欧陆词典释义：feedback [ˈfi:dbæk] -2 n. 反馈；成果，资料；回复 (研四六雅宝 3888/4828)","Continue to ask for feedback on your work...",""],["format","/ˈfɔ:mæt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “format”.","format [ˈfɔ:mæt] -2 n. 格式；版式；开本 vt. 使格式化；规定…的格式 vi. 设计版式 时态: formatted, formatting, formats (高研托雅 3730/3080)","欧陆词典释义：format [ˈfɔ:mæt] -2 n. 格式；版式；开本 vt. 使格式化；规定…的格式 vi. 设计版式 时态: formatted, formatting, formats (高研托雅 3730/3080)","I had met with him to explain the format of the programme and what we had in mind.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the general arrangement, plan, design, etc. of something","example":"The format of the new quiz show has proved popular."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the shape and size of a book, magazine, etc.","example":"They've brought out the magazine in a new format."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the way in which data is stored or held to be worked on by a computer","example":"The images are stored in a digital format within the database."}]],["guidance","/ˈgaɪdns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “guidance”.","guidance [ˈgaɪdns] -2 n. 指导，引导；领导 (高研四六雅 3869/2601)","欧陆词典释义：guidance [ˈgaɪdns] -2 n. 指导，引导；领导 (高研四六雅 3869/2601)","an opportunity for young people to improve their performance under the guidance of professional coaches...",""],["housing","/ˈhaʊzɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “housing”.","housing [ˈhaʊzɪŋ] -K4 n. 房屋；住房供给；[机] 外壳；遮盖物；机器等的防护外壳或外罩 原型: housing 是 house 的现在分词 (研雅 2147/1446)","欧陆词典释义：housing [ˈhaʊzɪŋ] -K4 n. 房屋；住房供给；[机] 外壳；遮盖物；机器等的防护外壳或外罩 原型: housing 是 house 的现在分词 (研雅 2147/1446)","a shortage of affordable housing ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"houses, flats/apartments, etc. that people live in, especially when referring to their type, price or condition","example":"public/private housing"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the job of providing houses, flats/apartments, etc. for people to live in","example":"poor housing conditions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a hard cover that protects part of a machine","example":"the housing shortage"}]],["innovation","/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “innovation”.","innovation [ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn] -2 n. 创新，革新；新方法 (研六托雅宝 3657/3151)","欧陆词典释义：innovation [ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn] -2 n. 创新，革新；新方法 (研六托雅宝 3657/3151)","The vegetarian burger was an innovation which was rapidly exported to Britain.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the introduction of new things, ideas or ways of doing something","example":"an age of technological innovation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a new idea, way of doing something, etc. that has been introduced or discovered","example":"The company is very interested in product design and innovation."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"recent innovations in steel-making technology"}]],["inspection","/ɪnˈspekʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “inspection”.","inspection [ɪnˈspekʃn] n. 视察，检查 (四六托雅宝 3588/3194)","欧陆词典释义：inspection [ɪnˈspekʃn] n. 视察，检查 (四六托雅宝 3588/3194)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “inspection”.",""],["instance","/ˈɪnstəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “instance”.","instance [ˈɪnstəns] -K4 n. 实例；情况；建议 vt. 举...为例 时态: instanced, instancing, instances (研四六 2957/2441)","欧陆词典释义：instance [ˈɪnstəns] -K4 n. 实例；情况；建议 vt. 举...为例 时态: instanced, instancing, instances (研四六 2957/2441)","There are a number of improvements; for instance , both mouse buttons can now be used...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular example or case of something","example":"The report highlights a number of instances of injustice."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"In most instances, there will be no need for further treatment."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"for example","example":"I would normally suggest taking time off work, but in this instance"}]],["institution","/ˌɪnstɪˈtju:ʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “institution”.","institution [ˌɪnstɪˈtju:ʃn] -K4 n. 制度；建立；（社会或宗教等）公共机构；习俗 (高研四六托雅宝 987/880)","欧陆词典释义：institution [ˌɪnstɪˈtju:ʃn] -K4 n. 制度；建立；（社会或宗教等）公共机构；习俗 (高研四六托雅宝 987/880)","the Institution of Civil Engineers...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large important organization that has a particular purpose, for example, a university or bank","example":"an educational/financial, etc. institution"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a building where people with special needs are taken care of, for example because they are old or mentally ill","example":"the Smithsonian Institution"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a custom or system that has existed for a long time among a particular group of people","example":"a mental institution"}]],["interaction","/ˌɪntər'ækʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “interaction”.","interaction [ˌɪntər'ækʃn] n. 相互作用；[数] 交互作用 n. 互动 (四六托宝 2075/2517)","欧陆词典释义：interaction [ˌɪntər'ækʃn] n. 相互作用；[数] 交互作用 n. 互动 (四六托宝 2075/2517)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “interaction”.",""],["interview","/ˈɪntəvju:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “interview”.","interview [ˈɪntəvju:] -K4 n. 接见，采访；面试，面谈 vt. 采访；接见；对…进行面谈；对某人进行面试 时态: interviewed, interviewing, interviews (中高研四六雅 944/1421)","欧陆词典释义：interview [ˈɪntəvju:] -K4 n. 接见，采访；面试，面谈 vt. 采访；接见；对…进行面谈；对某人进行面试 时态: interviewed, interviewing, interviews (中高研四六雅 944/1421)","When I went for my first interview for this job I arrived extremely early...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a formal meeting at which somebody is asked questions to see if they are suitable for a particular job, or for a course of study at a college, university, etc.","example":"a job interview"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a meeting (often a public one) at which a journalist asks somebody questions in order to find out their opinions","example":"to be called for (an) interview"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a private meeting between people when questions are asked and answered","example":"He has an interview"}]],["abandon","/əˈbændən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abandon”.","abandon [əˈbændən] -K3 n. 放任；狂热 vt. 遗弃；放弃 时态: abandoned, abandoning, abandons (高研四六托宝 2182/2057)","欧陆词典释义：abandon [əˈbændən] -K3 n. 放任；狂热 vt. 遗弃；放弃 时态: abandoned, abandoning, abandons (高研四六托宝 2182/2057)","He claimed that his parents had abandon ed him...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to leave somebody, especially somebody you are responsible for, with no intention of returning","example":"The baby had been abandoned by its mother."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to leave a thing or place, especially because it is impossible or dangerous to stay","example":"People often simply abandon their pets when they go abroad."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to stop doing something, especially before it is finished; to stop having something","example":"The study showed a deep fear among the elderly of being abandoned to the care of strangers."}]],["absence","/ˈæbsəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “absence”.","absence [ˈæbsəns] -K3 n. 没有；缺乏；缺席；不注意 (高研四六托 2524/1585)","欧陆词典释义：absence [ˈæbsəns] -K3 n. 没有；缺乏；缺席；不注意 (高研四六托 2524/1585)","a bundle of letters which had arrived for me in my absence ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of somebody being away from a place where they are usually expected to be; the occasion or period of time when somebody is away","example":"The decision was made in my absence"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of somebody/something not existing or not being available; a lack of something","example":"We did not receive any news during his long absence."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"absence from work"}]],["accommodation","/əˌkɒməˈdeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accommodation”.","accommodation [əˌkɒməˈdeɪʃn] -K2 n. 住处，膳宿；调节；和解；预订铺位 (高研四六雅 5369/2048)","欧陆词典释义：accommodation [əˌkɒməˈdeɪʃn] -K2 n. 住处，膳宿；调节；和解；预订铺位 (高研四六雅 5369/2048)","The government will provide temporary accommodation for up to three thousand people...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place to live, work or stay in","example":"rented/temporary/furnished accommodation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"somewhere to live or stay, often also providing food or other services","example":"Hotel accommodation is included in the price of your holiday."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an agreement or arrangement between people or groups with different opinions which is acceptable to everyone; the process of reaching this agreement","example":"The building plans include much needed new office accommodation."}]],["additional","/əˈdɪʃənl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “additional”.","additional [əˈdɪʃənl] -K adj. 附加的，额外的 (研四六托雅 1319/1310)","欧陆词典释义：additional [əˈdɪʃənl] -K adj. 附加的，额外的 (研四六托雅 1319/1310)","The US is sending additional troops to the region...",""],["adjustment","/əˈdʒʌstmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adjustment”.","adjustment [əˈdʒʌstmənt] n. 调整，调节；调节器 (高托 3121/3424)","欧陆词典释义：adjustment [əˈdʒʌstmənt] n. 调整，调节；调节器 (高托 3121/3424)","Compensation could be made by adjustment s to taxation...",""],["admission","/ədˈmɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “admission”.","admission [ədˈmɪʃn] -2 n. 承认；入场费；进入许可；坦白；录用 (高研四六托雅宝 3031/2768)","欧陆词典释义：admission [ədˈmɪʃn] -2 n. 承认；入场费；进入许可；坦白；录用 (高研四六托雅宝 3031/2768)","Students apply for admission to a particular college...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of accepting somebody into an institution, organization, etc.; the right to enter a place or to join an institution or organization","example":"Hospital admission is not necessary in most cases."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a statement in which somebody admits that something is true, especially something wrong or bad that they have done","example":"Hospital admissions for asthma attacks have doubled."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount of money that you pay to go into a building or to an event","example":"the university admissions policy/office"}]],["appeal","/əˈpi:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “appeal”.","appeal [əˈpi:l] -K4 n. 呼吁，请求；吸引力，感染力；上诉；诉诸裁判 vt. 将…上诉，对…上诉 vi. 呼吁，恳求；上诉；诉诸，求助；有吸引力，迎合爱好；（体育比赛中）诉诸裁判 时态: appealed, appealing, appeals (高研四六托雅宝 1852/942)","欧陆词典释义：appeal [əˈpi:l] -K4 n. 呼吁，请求；吸引力，感染力；上诉；诉诸裁判 vt. 将…上诉，对…上诉 vi. 呼吁，恳求；上诉；诉诸，求助；有吸引力，迎合爱好；（体育比赛中）诉诸裁判 时态: appealed, appealing, appeals (高研四六托雅宝 1852/942)","The Prime Minister appeal ed to young people to use their vote...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a formal request to a court or to somebody in authority for a judgement or a decision to be changed","example":"to lodge an appeal"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a quality that makes somebody/something attractive or interesting","example":"to file an appeal"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an urgent and deeply felt request for money, help or information, especially one made by a charity or by the police","example":"an appeal court/judge"}]],["approval","/əˈpru:vl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “approval”.","approval [əˈpru:vl] -K3 n. 批准；认可；赞成 (研四六托雅 2549/2223)","欧陆词典释义：approval [əˈpru:vl] -K3 n. 批准；认可；赞成 (研四六托雅 2549/2223)","efforts to win congressional approval for an aid package for Moscow...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the feeling that somebody/something is good or acceptable; a positive opinion of somebody/something","example":"She desperately wanted to win her father's approval."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"agreement to, or permission for something, especially a plan or request","example":"Do the plans meet with your approval"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"if you buy goods or if goods are sold on approval","example":"Several people nodded in approval"}]],["arrangement","/əˈreɪndʒmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “arrangement”.","arrangement [əˈreɪndʒmənt] -K3 n. 布置；整理；准备 (高四托 2357/1092)","欧陆词典释义：arrangement [əˈreɪndʒmənt] -K3 n. 布置；整理；准备 (高四托 2357/1092)","The staff is working frantically on final arrangement s for the summit...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a plan or preparation that you make so that something can happen","example":"travel arrangements"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way things are done or organized","example":"I'll make arrangements"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an agreement that you make with somebody that you can both accept","example":"She's happy with her unusual living arrangements."}]],["attachment","/əˈtætʃmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attachment”.","attachment [əˈtætʃmənt] n. 附件；依恋；连接物；扣押财产 (六托 5689/5553)","欧陆词典释义：attachment [əˈtætʃmənt] n. 附件；依恋；连接物；扣押财产 (六托 5689/5553)","As a teenager she formed a strong attachment to one of her teachers...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a strong feeling of affection for somebody/something","example":"a child’s strong attachment to its parents"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"belief in and support for an idea or a set of values","example":"the popular attachment to democratic government"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a tool that you can fix onto a machine, to make it do another job","example":"an electric drill with a range of different attachments"}]],["attempt","/əˈtempt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attempt”.","attempt [əˈtempt] -K5 n. 企图，试图；攻击 vt. 企图，试图；尝试 时态: attempted, attempting, attempts (高研四六托雅 1227/740)","欧陆词典释义：attempt [əˈtempt] -K5 n. 企图，试图；攻击 vt. 企图，试图；尝试 时态: attempted, attempting, attempts (高研四六托雅 1227/740)","The only time that we attempt ed to do something like that was in the city of Philadelphia...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an act of trying to do something, especially something difficult, often with no success","example":"I passed my driving test at the first attempt"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an act of trying to kill somebody","example":"Two factories were closed in an attempt"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an effort to do better than something, such as a very good performance in sport","example":"They made no attempt"}]],["biological","/ˌbaɪəˈlɒdʒɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “biological”.","biological [ˌbaɪəˈlɒdʒɪkl] -2 adj. 生物的；生物学的 (雅 2564/3586)","欧陆词典释义：biological [ˌbaɪəˈlɒdʒɪkl] -2 adj. 生物的；生物学的 (雅 2564/3586)","The living organisms somehow concentrated the minerals by biological processes...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with the science of biology","example":"the biological sciences"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with the processes that take place within living things","example":"the biological effects of radiation"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"using enzymes","example":"the biological control"}]],["certificate","/səˈtɪfɪkət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “certificate”.","certificate [səˈtɪfɪkət] -K2 n. 证书；执照，文凭 vt. 发给证明书；以证书形式授权给…；用证书批准 时态: certificated, certificating, certificates (高研四六雅 5237/2341)","欧陆词典释义：certificate [səˈtɪfɪkət] -K2 n. 证书；执照，文凭 vt. 发给证明书；以证书形式授权给…；用证书批准 时态: certificated, certificating, certificates (高研四六雅 5237/2341)","birth certificate s.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official document that may be used to prove that the facts it states are true","example":"a birth/marriage/death certificate"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an official document proving that you have completed a course of study or passed an exam; a qualification obtained after a course of study or an exam","example":"a Postgraduate Certificate in Education ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The police are waiting for the doctor to issue a death certificate."}]],["channel","/ˈtʃænl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “channel”.","channel [ˈtʃænl] -K4 n. 通道；频道；海峡 vt. 引导，开导；形成河道 时态: channelled, channelling, channels (高研四六托雅 2518/1617)","欧陆词典释义：channel [ˈtʃænl] -K4 n. 通道；频道；海峡 vt. 引导，开导；形成河道 时态: channelled, channelling, channels (高研四六托雅 2518/1617)","the only serious current affairs programme on either channel .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a television station","example":"What's on Channel 4 tonight?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a band of radio waves used for broadcasting television or radio programmes","example":"a movie/sports channel"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a method or system that people use to get information, to communicate, or to send something somewhere","example":"to change/switch channels"}]],["choice","/tʃɔɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “choice”.","choice [tʃɔɪs] -K4 n. 选择；选择权；精选品 adj. 精选的；仔细推敲的 (中高研四六托雅宝 630/725)","欧陆词典释义：choice [tʃɔɪs] -K4 n. 选择；选择权；精选品 adj. 精选的；仔细推敲的 (中高研四六托雅宝 630/725)","It's available in a choice of colours...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an act of choosing between two or more possibilities; something that you can choose","example":"women forced to make a choice between family and career"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the right to choose or the possibility of choosing","example":"We are faced with a difficult choice."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a person or thing that is chosen","example":"We aim to help students make more informed career choices."}]],["clause","/klɔ:z/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “clause”.","clause [klɔ:z] -2 n. 条款；[计] 子句 n. (Clause)人名；(法)克洛斯 (研托雅宝 6415/1871)","欧陆词典释义：clause [klɔ:z] -2 n. 条款；[计] 子句 n. (Clause)人名；(法)克洛斯 (研托雅宝 6415/1871)","He has a clause in his contract which entitles him to a percentage of the profits.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of words that includes a subject and a verb, and forms a sentence or part of a sentence","example":"In the sentence ‘They often go to Italy because they love the food’, ‘They often go to Italy’ is the main clause and ‘because they love the food’ is a subordinate clause."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an item in a legal document that says that a particular thing must or must not be done","example":"There is a clause in the contract forbidding tenants to sublet."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"The contract contains a confidentiality clause."}]],["colleague","/ˈkɒli:g/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “colleague”.","colleague [ˈkɒli:g] -K4 n. 同事，同僚 (高研四六托 1518/1338)","欧陆词典释义：colleague [ˈkɒli:g] -K4 n. 同事，同僚 (高研四六托 1518/1338)","Without consulting his colleague s he flew from Lisbon to Split...",""],["complaint","/kəmˈpleɪnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “complaint”.","complaint [kəmˈpleɪnt] -K3 n. 抱怨；诉苦；疾病；委屈 (研四六托雅 2325/1996)","欧陆词典释义：complaint [kəmˈpleɪnt] -K3 n. 抱怨；诉苦；疾病；委屈 (研四六托雅 2325/1996)","There's been a record number of complaint s about the standard of service on Britain's railways...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a reason for not being satisfied; a statement that somebody makes saying that they are not satisfied","example":"The most common complaint is about poor service."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of complaining","example":"We received a number of complaints from customers about the lack of parking facilities."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an illness, especially one that is not serious, and often one that affects a particular part of the body","example":"I'd like to make a complaint"}]],["completion","/kəmˈpli:ʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “completion”.","completion [kəmˈpli:ʃn] n. 完成，结束；实现 (六 5019/3047)","欧陆词典释义：completion [kəmˈpli:ʃn] n. 完成，结束；实现 (六 5019/3047)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “completion”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act or process of finishing something; the state of being finished and complete","example":"the completion of the new hospital building"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the formal act of completing the sale of property, for example the sale of a house","example":"Satisfactory completion of the course does not ensure you a job."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"The project is due for completion"}]],["concentration","/ˌkɒnsnˈtreɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “concentration”.","concentration [ˌkɒnsnˈtreɪʃn] -K3 n. 浓度；集中；浓缩；专心；集合 (研四六 2752/1564)","欧陆词典释义：concentration [ˌkɒnsnˈtreɪʃn] -K3 n. 浓度；集中；浓缩；专心；集合 (研四六 2752/1564)","Neal kept interrupting, breaking my concentration ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to direct all your effort and attention on one thing, without thinking of other things","example":"This book requires a great deal of concentration."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of people directing effort and attention on a particular thing","example":"Tiredness affects your powers of concentration."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a lot of something in one place","example":"a need for greater concentration on environmental issues"}]],["coordination","/kəʊˌɔ:dɪˈneɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coordination”.","coordination [kəʊˌɔ:dɪˈneɪʃn] n. 协调，调和；对等，同等 (托 6072/9109)","欧陆词典释义：coordination [kəʊˌɔ:dɪˈneɪʃn] n. 协调，调和；对等，同等 (托 6072/9109)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coordination”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of making parts of something, groups of people, etc. work together in an efficient and organized way","example":"a need for greater coordination between departments"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to control your movements well","example":"a lack of coordination in conservation policy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"a pamphlet produced by the government in coordination with"}]],["cost","/kɒst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cost”.","cost [kɒst] -K5 n. 费用，代价，成本；损失 vt. 花费；使付出；使花许多钱 vi. 花费 n. (Cost)人名；(英、罗)科斯特 时态: cost, costing, costs (中高雅 550/342)","欧陆词典释义：cost [kɒst] -K5 n. 费用，代价，成本；损失 vt. 花费；使付出；使花许多钱 vi. 花费 n. (Cost)人名；(英、罗)科斯特 时态: cost, costing, costs (中高雅 550/342)","The cost of a loaf of bread has increased five-fold...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount of money that you need in order to buy, make or do something","example":"the high/low cost"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the total amount of money that needs to be spent by a business","example":"A new computer system has been installed at a cost of"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the effort, loss or damage that is involved in order to do or achieve something","example":"The plan had to be abandoned on grounds of cost."}]],["coverage","/ˈkʌvərɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coverage”.","coverage [ˈkʌvərɪdʒ] -3 n. 覆盖，覆盖范围；新闻报道 (研托雅 1877/3338)","欧陆词典释义：coverage [ˈkʌvərɪdʒ] -3 n. 覆盖，覆盖范围；新闻报道 (研托雅 1877/3338)","Now a special TV network gives live coverage of most races...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the reporting of news and sport in newspapers and on the radio and television","example":"media/newspaper/press coverage"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the range or quality of information that is included in a book or course of study, on television, etc.","example":"tonight’s live coverage"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount of something that something provides; the extent to which something covers an area or a group of people","example":"There was blanket coverage"}]],["decade","/ˈdekeɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “decade”.","decade [ˈdekeɪd] -K4 n. 十年，十年期；十 (高研四六雅 730/1539)","欧陆词典释义：decade [ˈdekeɪd] -K4 n. 十年，十年期；十 (高研四六雅 730/1539)","the last decade of the nineteenth century.",""],["declaration","/ˌdekləˈreɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “declaration”.","declaration [ˌdekləˈreɪʃn] -3 n. （纳税品等的）申报；宣布；公告；申诉书 (研六托雅 5595/3227)","欧陆词典释义：declaration [ˌdekləˈreɪʃn] -3 n. （纳税品等的）申报；宣布；公告；申诉书 (研六托雅 5595/3227)","They will sign the declaration tomorrow...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official or formal statement, especially about the plans of a government or an organization; the act of making such a statement","example":"to issue/sign a declaration"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a written or spoken statement, especially about what people feel or believe","example":"the declaration of war"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official written statement giving information","example":"the Declaration of Independence ("}]],["dependency","/dɪˈpendənsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dependency”.","dependency [dɪˈpendənsi] -1 n. 属国；从属；从属物 (7839/6214)","欧陆词典释义：dependency [dɪˈpendənsi] -1 n. 属国；从属；从属物 (7839/6214)","the tiny British dependency of Montserrat in the eastern Caribbean.",""],["dialogue","/'daɪəlɒɡ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dialogue”.","dialogue ['daɪəlɒɡ] -3 n. 对话；意见交换 vt. 用对话表达 vi. 对话 (中高托雅 2794/3654)","欧陆词典释义：dialogue ['daɪəlɒɡ] -3 n. 对话；意见交换 vt. 用对话表达 vi. 对话 (中高托雅 2794/3654)","People of all social standings should be given equal opportunities for dialogue ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"conversations in a book, play, or film/movie","example":"The novel has long descriptions and not much dialogue."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a formal discussion between two groups or countries, especially when they are trying to solve a problem, end a disagreement, etc.","example":"dialogues for language learners"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"Discussions are still taking place between the two leaders."}]],["discrimination","/dɪˌskrɪmɪˈneɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “discrimination”.","discrimination [dɪˌskrɪmɪˈneɪʃn] -2 n. 歧视；区别，辨别；识别力 (高研四六托 3167/3592)","欧陆词典释义：discrimination [dɪˌskrɪmɪˈneɪʃn] -2 n. 歧视；区别，辨别；识别力 (高研四六托 3167/3592)","She is exempt from sex discrimination laws.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the practice of treating somebody or a particular group in society less fairly than others","example":"age/racial/sex/sexual discrimination"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to judge what is good, true, etc.","example":"discrimination against the elderly"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to recognize a difference between one thing and another; a difference that is recognized","example":"discrimination in favour of the young"}]],["disposal","/dɪˈspəʊzl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “disposal”.","disposal [dɪˈspəʊzl] -2 n. 处理；支配；清理；安排 (研四六托雅宝 5580/3208)","欧陆词典释义：disposal [dɪˈspəʊzl] -2 n. 处理；支配；清理；安排 (研四六托雅宝 5580/3208)","Do you have this information at your disposal ?...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of getting rid of something","example":"a bomb disposal squad"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the sale of part of a business, property, etc.","example":"sewage disposal systems"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"available for use as you prefer/somebody prefers","example":"the disposal of nuclear waste"}]],["distance","/ˈdɪstəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “distance”.","distance [ˈdɪstəns] -K4 n. 距离；远方；疏远；间隔 vt. 疏远；把…远远甩在后面 时态: distanced, distancing, distances (高研四六托雅 1235/1275)","欧陆词典释义：distance [ˈdɪstəns] -K4 n. 距离；远方；疏远；间隔 vt. 疏远；把…远远甩在后面 时态: distanced, distancing, distances (高研四六托雅 1235/1275)","the distance between the island and the nearby shore...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount of space between two places or things","example":"a short/long distance"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"being far away in space or in time","example":"the distance of the earth from the sun"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a point that is a particular amount of space away from something else","example":"a distance of"}]],["edition","/ɪˈdɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “edition”.","edition [ɪˈdɪʃn] -K4 n. 版本 版次 集 (高研四六雅 3155/2537)","欧陆词典释义：edition [ɪˈdɪʃn] -K4 n. 版本 版次 集 (高研四六雅 3155/2537)","A paperback edition is now available at bookshops.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the form in which a book is published","example":"a paperback/hardback edition"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular newspaper or magazine, or radio or television programme, especially one in a regular series","example":"She collects first editions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the total number of copies of a book, newspaper or magazine, etc. published at one time","example":"the online edition of ‘The Guardian’"}]],["election","/ɪˈlekʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “election”.","election [ɪˈlekʃn] -K5 n. 选举；当选；选择权；上帝的选拔 (四六托 801/638)","欧陆词典释义：election [ɪˈlekʃn] -K5 n. 选举；当选；选择权；上帝的选拔 (四六托 801/638)","the first fully free election s for more than fifty years...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of choosing a person or a group of people for a position, especially a political position, by voting","example":"election campaigns/results"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of having been chosen by election","example":"How many candidates are standing for election"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"to run for election"}]],["employee","/ɪmˈplɔɪi:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “employee”.","employee [ɪmˈplɔɪi:] -K4 n. 雇员；从业员工 (研四六托雅 930/1129)","欧陆词典释义：employee [ɪmˈplɔɪi:] -K4 n. 雇员；从业员工 (研四六托雅 930/1129)","He is an employee of Fuji Bank...",""],["employer","/ɪmˈplɔɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “employer”.","employer [ɪmˈplɔɪə(r)] -K3 n. 雇主，老板 (研四六托雅 2297/1318)","欧陆词典释义：employer [ɪmˈplɔɪə(r)] -K3 n. 雇主，老板 (研四六托雅 2297/1318)","He had been sent to Rome by his employer ...",""],["entertainment","/ˌentəˈteɪnmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “entertainment”.","entertainment [ˌentəˈteɪnmənt] -K3 n. 娱乐；消遣；款待 (高研四六托雅 2350/3187)","欧陆词典释义：entertainment [ˌentəˈteɪnmənt] -K3 n. 娱乐；消遣；款待 (高研四六托雅 2350/3187)","the world of entertainment and international stardom...",""],["entry","/ˈentri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “entry”.","entry [ˈentri] -K4 n. 进入；入口；条目；登记；报关手续；对土地的侵占 (高研四六托雅宝 2338/1373)","欧陆词典释义：entry [ˈentri] -K4 n. 进入；入口；条目；登记；报关手续；对土地的侵占 (高研四六托雅宝 2338/1373)","Bill was among the first to gain entry to Buckingham Palace when it opened to the public recently...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an act of going into or getting into a place","example":"She made her entry"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the right or opportunity to enter a place","example":"The children were surprised by the sudden entry of their teacher."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the right or opportunity to take part in something or become a member of a group","example":"How did the thieves gain entry"}]],["equality","/iˈkwɒləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “equality”.","equality [iˈkwɒləti] n. 平等；相等；[数] 等式 (高研四六托 4590/4197)","欧陆词典释义：equality [iˈkwɒləti] n. 平等；相等；[数] 等式 (高研四六托 4590/4197)"," equality of the sexes.",""],["extension","/ɪkˈstenʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “extension”.","extension [ɪkˈstenʃn] -K2 n. 延长；延期；扩大；伸展；电话分机 (高研四六托雅 3190/2123)","欧陆词典释义：extension [ɪkˈstenʃn] -K2 n. 延长；延期；扩大；伸展；电话分机 (高研四六托雅 3190/2123)","the Jubilee Line extension .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of increasing the area of activity, group of people, etc. that is affected by something","example":"the extension of new technology into developing countries"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a new room or rooms that are added to a house","example":"a gradual extension of the powers of central government"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a new part that is added to a building","example":"The bank plans various extensions to its credit facilities."}]],["focus","/ˈfəʊkəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “focus”.","focus [ˈfəʊkəs] -K4 n. 焦点；中心；清晰；焦距 vt. 使集中；使聚焦 vi. 集中；聚焦；调节焦距 n. (Focus)人名；(瑞典)福库斯 时态: focused, focusing, focuses (高研四六托雅 688/1918)","欧陆词典释义：focus [ˈfəʊkəs] -K4 n. 焦点；中心；清晰；焦距 vt. 使集中；使聚焦 vi. 集中；聚焦；调节焦距 n. (Focus)人名；(瑞典)福库斯 时态: focused, focusing, focuses (高研四六托雅 688/1918)","The research effort has focus ed on tracing the effects of growing levels of five compounds...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give attention, effort, etc. to one particular subject, situation or person rather than another","example":"The discussion focused on three main problems."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to adapt or be adjusted so that things can be seen clearly; to adjust something so that you can see things clearly","example":"Each exercise focuses on a different grammar point."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to aim light onto a particular point using a lens","example":"The visit helped to focus world attention on the plight of the refugees."}]],["formation","/fɔ:ˈmeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “formation”.","formation [fɔ:ˈmeɪʃn] -2 n. 形成；构造；编队 (研四六托宝 3045/2062)","欧陆词典释义：formation [fɔ:ˈmeɪʃn] -2 n. 形成；构造；编队 (研四六托宝 3045/2062)","the formation of a new government.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the action of forming something; the process of being formed","example":"the formation of a new government"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that has been formed, especially in a particular place or in a particular way","example":"evidence of recent star formation in the galaxy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular arrangement or pattern","example":"rock formations"}]],["goods","/gʊdz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “goods”.","goods [gʊdz] -K4 n. 商品；动产；合意的人；真本领 原型: goods 是 good 的复数 (高研四六雅 -/995)","欧陆词典释义：goods [gʊdz] -K4 n. 商品；动产；合意的人；真本领 原型: goods 是 good 的复数 (高研四六雅 -/995)","Money can be exchanged for goods or services.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"things that are produced to be sold","example":"cheap/expensive goods"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"possessions that can be moved","example":"leather/cotton/paper goods"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"things (not people) that are transported by rail or road","example":"electrical/sports goods"}]],["growth","/grəʊθ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “growth”.","growth [grəʊθ] -K4 n. 增长；发展；生长；种植 (高研四六雅 787/770)","欧陆词典释义：growth [grəʊθ] -K4 n. 增长；发展；生长；种植 (高研四六雅 787/770)","the growth of nationalism.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of growing physically, mentally or emotionally","example":"Lack of water will stunt the plant's growth."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an increase in the size, amount or degree of something","example":"Remove dead leaves to encourage new growth."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an increase in economic activity","example":"a concern with personal ("}]],["industry","/ˈɪndəstri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “industry”.","industry [ˈɪndəstri] -K5 n. 产业；工业；勤勉 (中高研四六雅 551/383)","欧陆词典释义：industry [ˈɪndəstri] -K5 n. 产业；工业；勤勉 (中高研四六雅 551/383)","British industry suffers through insufficient investment in research.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the production of goods from raw materials, especially in factories","example":"heavy/light industry"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the people and activities involved in producing a particular thing, or in providing a particular service","example":"the needs of British industry"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality of working hard","example":"She got a job in industry"}]],["influence","/ˈɪnfluəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “influence”.","influence [ˈɪnfluəns] -K4 n. 影响；势力；感化；有影响的人或事 vt. 影响；改变 时态: influenced, influencing, influences (中高研四六雅 1392/1061)","欧陆词典释义：influence [ˈɪnfluəns] -K4 n. 影响；势力；感化；有影响的人或事 vt. 影响；改变 时态: influenced, influencing, influences (中高研四六雅 1392/1061)","As Hugh grew older, she had less influence and couldn't control him...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the effect that somebody/something has on the way a person thinks or behaves or on the way that something works or develops","example":"to have/exert"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the power that somebody/something has to make somebody/something behave in a particular way","example":"the influence of the climate on agricultural production"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a person or thing that affects the way a person behaves and thinks","example":"What exactly is the influence of television on children?"}]],["insurance","/ɪnˈʃʊərəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “insurance”.","insurance [ɪnˈʃʊərəns] -K4 n. 保险；保险费；保险契约；赔偿金 (高研四六雅 1197/1347)","欧陆词典释义：insurance [ɪnˈʃʊərəns] -K4 n. 保险；保险费；保险契约；赔偿金 (高研四六雅 1197/1347)","The insurance company paid out for the stolen jewellery and silver...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an arrangement with a company in which you pay them regular amounts of money and they agree to pay the costs, for example, if you die or are ill/sick, or if you lose or damage something","example":"life/car/travel/household, etc. insurance"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the business of providing people with insurance","example":"to have adequate insurance cover"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"money paid by or to an insurance","example":"to take out insurance"}]],["intention","/ɪnˈtenʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “intention”.","intention [ɪnˈtenʃn] -K3 n. 意图；目的；意向；愈合 (中高研四六托 2517/1523)","欧陆词典释义：intention [ɪnˈtenʃn] -K3 n. 意图；目的；意向；愈合 (中高研四六托 2517/1523)","Beveridge announced his intention of standing for parliament...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"what you intend or plan to do; your aim","example":"I have no intention"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"He left England with the intention of"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"it is not enough to intend to do good things; you must actually do them","example":"I have every intention"}]],["item","/ˈaɪtəm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “item”.","item [ˈaɪtəm] -K4 n. 条款，项目；一则；一件商品（或物品） adj. 又，同上 v. 记下；逐条列出 (研四雅 1031/950)","欧陆词典释义：item [ˈaɪtəm] -K4 n. 条款，项目；一则；一件商品（或物品） adj. 又，同上 v. 记下；逐条列出 (研四雅 1031/950)","The most valuable item on show will be a Picasso drawing...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"one thing on a list of things to buy, do, talk about, etc.","example":"What's the next item on the agenda?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a single article or object","example":"Can I pay for each item separately?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a single piece of news in a newspaper, on television, etc.","example":"The computer was my largest single item of expenditure."}]],["leadership","/ˈli:dəʃɪp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “leadership”.","leadership [ˈli:dəʃɪp] -4 n. 领导能力；领导阶层 (研四六托 1304/1873)","欧陆词典释义：leadership [ˈli:dəʃɪp] -4 n. 领导能力；领导阶层 (研四六托 1304/1873)","He is expected to hold talks with both the Croatian and Slovenian leadership s.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state or position of being a leader","example":"a leadership contest"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to be a leader or the qualities a good leader should have","example":"The party thrived under his leadership"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of leaders of a particular organization, etc.","example":"Who will take over the leadership of the club?"}]],["licence","/ˈlaɪsns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “licence”.","licence [ˈlaɪsns] -K3 n. 许可证，执照；特许 vt. 特许，许可；发给执照 时态: licenced, licencing, licences (四雅 29631/2055)","欧陆词典释义：licence [ˈlaɪsns] -K3 n. 许可证，执照；特许 vt. 特许，许可；发给执照 时态: licenced, licencing, licences (四雅 29631/2055)","Payne lost his driving licence a year ago for drink-driving...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official document that shows that permission has been given to do, own or use something","example":"a driving licence"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"freedom to do or say whatever you want, often something bad or unacceptable","example":"James lost his licence for six months ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"freedom to behave in a way that is considered sexually immoral","example":"a licence for the software"}]],["loan","/ləʊn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “loan”.","loan [ləʊn] -K4 n. 贷款；借款 vi. 借出 vt. 借；借给 时态: loaned, loaning, loans (研四六托雅 1699/1468)","欧陆词典释义：loan [ləʊn] -K4 n. 贷款；借款 vi. 借出 vt. 借；借给 时态: loaned, loaning, loans (研四六托雅 1699/1468)","The country has no access to foreign loan s or financial aid...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"money that an organization such as a bank lends and somebody borrows","example":"to take out/repay a loan"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the act of lending something; the state of being lent","example":"bank loans"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"It took three years to repay my student loan"}]],["loss","/lɒs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “loss”.","loss [lɒs] -K4 n. 减少；亏损；失败；遗失 n. (Loss)人名；(匈)洛什；(法、德、意)洛斯 (高研四六雅 788/649)","欧陆词典释义：loss [lɒs] -K4 n. 减少；亏损；失败；遗失 n. (Loss)人名；(匈)洛什；(法、德、意)洛斯 (高研四六雅 788/649)"," loss of sight...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state of no longer having something or as much of something; the process that leads to this","example":"I want to report the loss of a package."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"money that has been lost by a business or an organization","example":"loss of blood"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the death of a person","example":"weight loss"}]],["maintenance","/ˈmeɪntənəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “maintenance”.","maintenance [ˈmeɪntənəns] -2 n. 维护，维修；保持；生活费用 (研四六托雅宝 3067/2198)","欧陆词典释义：maintenance [ˈmeɪntənəns] -2 n. 维护，维修；保持；生活费用 (研四六托雅宝 3067/2198)"," maintenance work on government buildings...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of keeping something in good condition by checking or repairing it regularly","example":"The school pays for heating and the maintenance of the buildings."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of making a state or situation continue","example":"car maintenance"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"money that somebody must pay regularly to their former wife, husband or partner, especially when they have had children together","example":"the maintenance of international peace"}]],["maximum","/ˈmæksɪməm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “maximum”.","maximum [ˈmæksɪməm] -K3 n. [数] 极大，最大限度；最大量 adj. 最高的；最多的；最大极限的 (高研四六托雅 3603/2427)","欧陆词典释义：maximum [ˈmæksɪməm] -K3 n. [数] 极大，最大限度；最大量 adj. 最高的；最多的；最大极限的 (高研四六托雅 3603/2427)","Under planning law the maximum height for a fence or hedge is 2 metres...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"as large, fast, etc. as is possible, or the most that is possible or allowed","example":"the maximum speed/temperature/volume"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"For maximum effect"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the greatest amount, size, speed, etc. that is possible, recorded or allowed","example":"Turn it right up to the maximum volume."}]],["minimum","/ˈmɪnɪməm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “minimum”.","minimum [ˈmɪnɪməm] -K3 n. 最小值；最低限度；最小化；最小量 adj. 最小的；最低的 (高研四六托雅 3633/2715)","欧陆词典释义：minimum [ˈmɪnɪməm] -K3 n. 最小值；最低限度；最小化；最小量 adj. 最小的；最低的 (高研四六托雅 3633/2715)","He was only five feet nine, the minimum height for a policeman.",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used after amounts to show that the amount is the lowest possible","example":"You'll need £200 minimum for your holiday expenses."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the smallest that is possible or allowed; extremely small","example":"a minimum charge/price"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"the minimum age for retirement"}]],["notice","/ˈnəʊtɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “notice”.","notice [ˈnəʊtɪs] -K4 n. 通知，布告；注意；公告 vt. 通知；注意到；留心 vi. 引起注意 时态: noticed, noticing, notices (中高研四六托雅 1044/1034)","欧陆词典释义：notice [ˈnəʊtɪs] -K4 n. 通知，布告；注意；公告 vt. 通知；注意到；留心 vi. 引起注意 时态: noticed, noticing, notices (中高研四六托雅 1044/1034)","People should not hesitate to contact the police if they've notice d anyone acting suspiciously...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of somebody paying attention to somebody/something or knowing about something","example":"Don't take any notice of"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a sheet of paper giving written or printed information, usually put in a public place","example":"Take no notice"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a board or sign giving information, an instruction or a warning","example":"These protests have really made the government sit up and take notice"}]],["operation","/ˌɒpəˈreɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “operation”.","operation [ˌɒpəˈreɪʃn] -K5 n. 操作；经营；[外科] 手术；[数][计] 运算 (中高研四六 826/619)","欧陆词典释义：operation [ˌɒpəˈreɪʃn] -K5 n. 操作；经营；[外科] 手术；[数][计] 运算 (中高研四六 826/619)","The rescue operation began on Friday afternoon...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of cutting open a part of a person’s body in order to remove or repair a damaged part","example":"Will I need to have an operation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an organized activity that involves several people doing different things","example":"He underwent a three-hour heart operation."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a business or company involving many parts","example":"an operation on her lung to remove a tumour"}]],["opportunity","/ˌɒpəˈtju:nəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “opportunity”.","opportunity [ˌɒpəˈtju:nəti] -K4 n. 时机，机会 (研四六托雅 625/618)","欧陆词典释义：opportunity [ˌɒpəˈtju:nəti] -K4 n. 时机，机会 (研四六托雅 625/618)","I had an opportunity to go to New York and study...",""],["ability","/əˈbɪləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ability”.","ability [əˈbɪləti] -K4 n. 能力，能耐；才能 (中高研四托雅 783/946)","欧陆词典释义：ability [əˈbɪləti] -K4 n. 能力，能耐；才能 (中高研四托雅 783/946)","The public never had faith in his ability to handle the job...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact that somebody/something is able to do something","example":"The system has the ability to run more than one program at the same time."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a level of skill or intelligence","example":"Everyone has the right to good medical care regardless of their ability to pay."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"A gentle form of exercise will increase your ability to relax."}]],["acceptance","/əkˈseptəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “acceptance”.","acceptance [əkˈseptəns] -2 n. 接纳；赞同；容忍 (研四六 3443/2899)","欧陆词典释义：acceptance [əkˈseptəns] -2 n. 接纳；赞同；容忍 (研四六 3443/2899)","The Party is being degraded by its acceptance of secret donations...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of accepting a gift, an invitation, an offer, etc.","example":"Please confirm your acceptance of this offer in writing."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of agreeing with something and approving of it","example":"He made a short acceptance speech/speech"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of allowing somebody to join something or be a member of a group","example":"Invitations have been sent out and 80 acceptances have already been received."}]],["achievement","/əˈtʃi:vmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “achievement”.","achievement [əˈtʃi:vmənt] -K2 n. 成就；完成；达到；成绩 (高四六托雅 2021/1978)","欧陆词典释义：achievement [əˈtʃi:vmənt] -K2 n. 成就；完成；达到；成绩 (高四六托雅 2021/1978)","Reaching this agreement so quickly was a great achievement ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that somebody has done successfully, especially using their own effort and skill","example":"the greatest scientific achievement of the decade"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act or process of achieving something","example":"It was a remarkable achievement for such a young player."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a reward that you can earn in some video games by completing a challenge or level","example":"They were proud of their children's achievements."}]],["acquisition","/ˌækwɪˈzɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “acquisition”.","acquisition [ˌækwɪˈzɪʃn] -3 n. 获得物，获得；收购 (高研四六托雅 3856/2567)","欧陆词典释义：acquisition [ˌækwɪˈzɪʃn] -3 n. 获得物，获得；收购 (高研四六托雅 3856/2567)","the acquisition of a profitable paper recycling company.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of getting something, especially knowledge, a skill, etc.","example":"theories of child language acquisition"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that somebody buys to add to what they already own, usually something valuable","example":"His latest acquisition is a racehorse."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a company, piece of land, etc. bought by somebody, especially another company; the act of buying it","example":"The money will be spent on acquisitions for the university library."}]],["advertising","/ˈædvətaɪzɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “advertising”.","advertising [ˈædvətaɪzɪŋ] -K n. 广告；广告业；登广告 adj. 广告的；广告业的 v. 公告；为…做广告（advertise的ing形式） (雅 2640/2180)","欧陆词典释义：advertising [ˈædvətaɪzɪŋ] -K n. 广告；广告业；登广告 adj. 广告的；广告业的 v. 公告；为…做广告（advertise的ing形式） (雅 2640/2180)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “advertising”.",""],["agriculture","/ˈægrɪkʌltʃə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “agriculture”.","agriculture [ˈægrɪkʌltʃə(r)] -3 n. 农业；农耕；农业生产；农艺，农学 (高研四六托雅 4165/2274)","欧陆词典释义：agriculture [ˈægrɪkʌltʃə(r)] -3 n. 农业；农耕；农业生产；农艺，农学 (高研四六托雅 4165/2274)","The Ukraine is strong both in industry and agriculture .",""],["aid","/eɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “aid”.","aid [eɪd] -K5 n. 援助；帮助；助手；帮助者 vt. 援助；帮助；有助于 vi. 帮助 n. (Aid)人名；(阿拉伯、印、英)艾德 时态: aided, aiding, aids (高研四六 1640/1096)","欧陆词典释义：aid [eɪd] -K5 n. 援助；帮助；助手；帮助者 vt. 援助；帮助；有助于 vi. 帮助 n. (Aid)人名；(阿拉伯、印、英)艾德 时态: aided, aiding, aids (高研四六 1640/1096)","regular flights carrying humanitarian aid to Cambodia...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"money, food, etc. that is sent to help countries in difficult situations","example":"economic/humanitarian/emergency aid"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"help that you need to perform a particular task","example":"An extra £10 million in foreign aid"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"help that is given to a person","example":"aid agencies"}]],["allowance","/əˈlaʊəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “allowance”.","allowance [əˈlaʊəns] -2 n. 津贴，零用钱；允许；限额 vt. 定量供应 时态: allowanced, allowancing, allowances (高研六雅宝 7677/2481)","欧陆词典释义：allowance [əˈlaʊəns] -2 n. 津贴，零用钱；允许；限额 vt. 定量供应 时态: allowanced, allowancing, allowances (高研六雅宝 7677/2481)","He lives on a single parent's allowance of £70 a week...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an amount of money that is given to somebody regularly or for a particular purpose","example":"an allowance of $20 a day"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount of something that is allowed in a particular situation","example":"a clothing/living/travel allowance"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an amount of money that can be earned or received before you start paying tax","example":"Do you get an allowance for clothing?"}]],["ambassador","/æmˈbæsədə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ambassador”.","ambassador [æmˈbæsədə(r)] -3 n. 大使；代表；使节 (高研六雅 4520/4614)","欧陆词典释义：ambassador [æmˈbæsədə(r)] -3 n. 大使；代表；使节 (高研六雅 4520/4614)","the German ambassador to Poland.",""],["amount","/əˈmaʊnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “amount”.","amount [əˈmaʊnt] -K4 n. 数量；总额，总数 vi. 总计，合计；相当于；共计；产生…结果 时态: amounted, amounting, amounts (高研四托雅 782/584)","欧陆词典释义：amount [əˈmaʊnt] -K4 n. 数量；总额，总数 vi. 总计，合计；相当于；共计；产生…结果 时态: amounted, amounting, amounts (高研四托雅 782/584)","He needs that amount of money to survive...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a sum of money","example":"The insurance company will refund any amount due to you."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a quantity of something","example":"You will receive a bill for the full amount."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"Small amounts will be paid in cash."}]],["announcement","/əˈnaʊnsmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “announcement”.","announcement [əˈnaʊnsmənt] -3 n. 公告；宣告；发表；通告 (高托雅 3604/2825)","欧陆词典释义：announcement [əˈnaʊnsmənt] -3 n. 公告；宣告；发表；通告 (高托雅 3604/2825)","Sir Robert made his announcement after talks with the President...",""],["arrival","/əˈraɪvl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “arrival”.","arrival [əˈraɪvl] -K3 n. 到来；到达；到达者 (高研四雅 3194/2281)","欧陆词典释义：arrival [əˈraɪvl] -K3 n. 到来；到达；到达者 (高研四雅 3194/2281)","the day after his arrival in England...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an act of coming or being brought to a place","example":"Guests receive dinner on/upon arrival"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person or thing that comes to a place","example":"We apologize for the late arrival of the train."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the time when a new technology or idea is introduced","example":"the arrival of the mail in the morning"}]],["asset","/ˈæset/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “asset”.","asset [ˈæset] -4 n. 资产；优点；有用的东西；有利条件；财产；有价值的人或物 n. （法）阿塞（人名） (研六托雅宝 2094/1498)","欧陆词典释义：asset [ˈæset] -4 n. 资产；优点；有用的东西；有利条件；财产；有价值的人或物 n. （法）阿塞（人名） (研六托雅宝 2094/1498)","Her leadership qualities were the greatest asset of the Conservative Party...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person or thing that is valuable or useful to somebody/something","example":"In his job, patience is an invaluable asset."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing of value, especially property, that a person or company owns, which can be used or sold to pay debts","example":"Being able to speak a foreign language is a major asset."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 16th cent.","example":"I’m not sure if his forcefulness is an asset or a liability."}]],["award","/əˈwɔ:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “award”.","award [əˈwɔ:d] -K4 n. 奖品；判决 vt. 授予；判定 时态: awarded, awarding, awards (高研四六雅 2573/590)","欧陆词典释义：award [əˈwɔ:d] -K4 n. 奖品；判决 vt. 授予；判定 时态: awarded, awarding, awards (高研四六雅 2573/590)","the Booker prize, Britain's top award for fiction...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a prize such as money, etc. for something that somebody has done","example":"He was nominated for the best actor award."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an increase in the amount of money somebody earns","example":"an award presentation/ceremony"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the amount of money that a court decides should be given to somebody who has won a case; the decision to give this money","example":"the Housing Design Award"}]],["board","/bɔ:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “board”.","board [bɔ:d] -K4 n. 董事会；木板；甲板；膳食 vt. 上（飞机、车、船等）；用板盖上；给提供膳宿 vi. 寄宿 n. (Board)人名；(英、西)博德 时态: boarded, boarding, boards (中高研四六托雅 667/611)","欧陆词典释义：board [bɔ:d] -K4 n. 董事会；木板；甲板；膳食 vt. 上（飞机、车、船等）；用板盖上；给提供膳宿 vi. 寄宿 n. (Board)人名；(英、西)博德 时态: boarded, boarding, boards (中高研四六托雅 667/611)","a chopping board .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a long thin piece of strong hard material, especially wood, used, for example, for making floors, building walls and roofs and making boats","example":"He had ripped up the carpet, leaving only the bare boards."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a piece of wood, or other strong material, that is used for a special purpose","example":"a blackboard"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a group of people who have power to make decisions and control a company or other organization","example":"I'll write it up on the board."}]],["bond","/bɒnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bond”.","bond [bɒnd] -4 n. 债券；结合；约定；粘合剂；纽带 vt. 使结合；以…作保 vi. 结合，团结在一起 n. (Bond)人名；(英、德、西、刚(金)、瑞典)邦德 时态: bonded, bonding, bonds (高研四六托雅 1880/2385)","欧陆词典释义：bond [bɒnd] -4 n. 债券；结合；约定；粘合剂；纽带 vt. 使结合；以…作保 vi. 结合，团结在一起 n. (Bond)人名；(英、德、西、刚(金)、瑞典)邦德 时态: bonded, bonding, bonds (高研四六托雅 1880/2385)","The experience created a very special bond between us.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that forms a connection between people or groups, such as a feeling of friendship or shared ideas and experiences","example":"A bond of friendship had been forged between them."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an agreement by a government or a company to pay you interest on the money you have lent; a document containing this agreement","example":"The agreement strengthened the bonds between the two countries."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a sum of money that is paid as bail","example":"the special bond between mother and child"}]],["border","/ˈbɔ:də(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “border”.","border [ˈbɔ:də(r)] -K4 n. 边境；边界；国界 vt. 接近；与…接壤；在…上镶边 vi. 接界；近似 n. (Border)人名；(英)博德 时态: bordered, bordering, borders (高研四托雅 1344/1789)","欧陆词典释义：border [ˈbɔ:də(r)] -K4 n. 边境；边界；国界 vt. 接近；与…接壤；在…上镶边 vi. 接界；近似 n. (Border)人名；(英)博德 时态: bordered, bordering, borders (高研四托雅 1344/1789)","They fled across the border .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the line that divides two countries or areas; the land near this line","example":"a national park on the border between Kenya and Tanzania"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a strip around the edge of something such as a picture or a piece of cloth","example":"Denmark’s border with Germany"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a strip of soil which is planted with flowers, along the edge of the grass","example":"in the US, near the Canadian border"}]],["branch","/brɑ:ntʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “branch”.","branch [brɑ:ntʃ] -K3 n. 树枝，分枝；分部；支流 vt. 分支；出现分歧 vi. 分支；出现分歧 n. (Branch)人名；(英)布兰奇 时态: branched, branching, branches (高研四雅 1807/1178)","欧陆词典释义：branch [brɑ:ntʃ] -K3 n. 树枝，分枝；分部；支流 vt. 分支；出现分歧 vi. 分支；出现分歧 n. (Branch)人名；(英)布兰奇 时态: branched, branching, branches (高研四雅 1807/1178)","The local branch of Bank of America is handling the accounts...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a part of a tree that grows out from the main stem","example":"She climbed the tree and hid in the branches."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a local office or shop/store belonging to a large company or organization","example":"The bank has branches all over the country."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a part of a government or other large organization that deals with one particular aspect of its work","example":"Our New York branch is dealing with the matter."}]],["brand","/brænd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “brand”.","brand [brænd] -K3 n. 商标，牌子；烙印 vt. 铭刻于，铭记；打烙印于；印…商标于 n. (Brand)人名；(英、德、俄、西、意、罗、葡、捷、芬、瑞典、匈)布兰德；(法)布朗 时态: branded, branding, brands (高研四六雅宝 2570/3387)","欧陆词典释义：brand [brænd] -K3 n. 商标，牌子；烙印 vt. 铭刻于，铭记；打烙印于；印…商标于 n. (Brand)人名；(英、德、俄、西、意、罗、葡、捷、芬、瑞典、匈)布兰德；(法)布朗 时态: branded, branding, brands (高研四六雅宝 2570/3387)","Winston is a brand of cigarette...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a type of product made by a particular company","example":"Which brand of toothpaste do you use?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a particular type or kind of something","example":"You pay less for the supermarket's own brand"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a mark made with a piece of hot metal, especially on farm animals to show who owns them","example":"You pay less for the store brand"}]],["breakdown","/ˈbreɪkdaʊn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “breakdown”.","breakdown [ˈbreɪkdaʊn] n. 故障；崩溃；分解；分类；衰弱；跺脚曳步舞 (研六托雅 5147/4096)","欧陆词典释义：breakdown [ˈbreɪkdaʊn] n. 故障；崩溃；分解；分类；衰弱；跺脚曳步舞 (研六托雅 5147/4096)","the breakdown of talks between the US and EU officials.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an occasion when a vehicle or machine stops working","example":"a breakdown on the motorway"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a failure of a relationship, discussion or system","example":"a breakdown recovery service"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"detailed information that you get by studying a set of figures","example":"the breakdown of a marriage"}]],["broadcast","/ˈbrɔ:dkɑ:st/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “broadcast”.","broadcast [ˈbrɔ:dkɑ:st] -K3 n. 广播；播音；广播节目 adj. 广播的 vt. 播送，播放；（无线电或电视）广播；播撒（种子） vi. 广播，播送；播放 时态: broadcast, broadcasting, broadcasts (高研四托 3617/5111)","欧陆词典释义：broadcast [ˈbrɔ:dkɑ:st] -K3 n. 广播；播音；广播节目 adj. 广播的 vt. 播送，播放；（无线电或电视）广播；播撒（种子） vi. 广播，播送；播放 时态: broadcast, broadcasting, broadcasts (高研四托 3617/5111)","In a broadcast on state radio the government also announced that it was willing to resume peace negotiations.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to send out programmes on television or radio","example":"The concert will be broadcast live"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to tell a lot of people about something","example":"Most of the programmes are broadcast in English."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 18th cent.","example":"They began broadcasting in 1922."}]],["career","/kəˈrɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “career”.","career [kəˈrɪə(r)] -K4 n. 生涯；职业；事业；速度，全速 adj. 作为毕生职业的 vi. 全速前进，猛冲 时态: careered, careering, careers (研四托雅 741/1057)","欧陆词典释义：career [kəˈrɪə(r)] -K4 n. 生涯；职业；事业；速度，全速 adj. 作为毕生职业的 vi. 全速前进，猛冲 时态: careered, careering, careers (研四托雅 741/1057)","She is now concentrating on a career as a fashion designer...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the series of jobs that a person has in a particular area of work, usually involving more responsibility as time passes","example":"a career in"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the period of time that you spend in your life working or doing a particular thing","example":"a teaching career"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 16th cent.","example":"What made you decide on a career as"}]],["case","/keɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “case”.","case [keɪs] -K2 n. 情况；实例；箱 vt. 包围；把…装于容器中 n. (Case)人名；(英)凯斯；(西)卡塞；(法)卡斯 时态: cased, casing, cases (高雅 186/139)","欧陆词典释义：case [keɪs] -K2 n. 情况；实例；箱 vt. 包围；把…装于容器中 n. (Case)人名；(英)凯斯；(西)卡塞；(法)卡斯 时态: cased, casing, cases (高雅 186/139)","Surgical training takes at least nine years, or 11 in the case of obstetrics...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular situation or a situation of a particular type","example":"In some cases people have had to wait several weeks for an appointment."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the true situation","example":"The company only dismisses its employees in cases of gross misconduct."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a situation that relates to a particular person or thing","example":"It's a classic case"}]],["cause","/kɔ:z/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cause”.","cause [kɔ:z] -K5 n. 原因；事业；目标 vt. 引起；使遭受 时态: caused, causing, causes (中高研四六托雅 601/476)","欧陆词典释义：cause [kɔ:z] -K5 n. 原因；事业；目标 vt. 引起；使遭受 时态: caused, causing, causes (中高研四六托雅 601/476)","Smoking is the biggest preventable cause of death and disease...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the person or thing that makes something happen","example":"Unemployment is a major cause of poverty."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a reason for having particular feelings or behaving in a particular way","example":"There was discussion about the fire and its likely cause."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an organization or idea that people support or fight for","example":"Drinking and driving is one of the most common causes of traffic accidents."}]],["charge","/tʃɑ:dʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “charge”.","charge [tʃɑ:dʒ] -K5 n. 费用；电荷；掌管；控告；命令；负载 vt. 使充电；使承担；指责；装载；对…索费；向…冲去 vi. 充电；控告；索价；向前冲；记在账上 n. (Charge)人名；(法)沙尔热；(英)查奇 时态: charged, charging, charges (高研四六托雅 923/675)","欧陆词典释义：charge [tʃɑ:dʒ] -K5 n. 费用；电荷；掌管；控告；命令；负载 vt. 使充电；使承担；指责；装载；对…索费；向…冲去 vi. 充电；控告；索价；向前冲；记在账上 n. (Charge)人名；(法)沙尔热；(英)查奇 时态: charged, charging, charges (高研四六托雅 923/675)","Even local nurseries charge £100 a week...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount of money that somebody asks for goods and services","example":"We have to make a small charge for refreshments."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an official claim made by the police that somebody has committed a crime","example":"admission charges"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a statement accusing somebody of doing something wrong or bad","example":"Delivery is free of charge"}]],["charity","/ˈtʃærəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “charity”.","charity [ˈtʃærəti] -K3 n. 慈善；施舍；慈善团体；宽容；施舍物 (研四六托雅宝 3287/2008)","欧陆词典释义：charity [ˈtʃærəti] -K3 n. 慈善；施舍；慈善团体；宽容；施舍物 (研四六托雅宝 3287/2008)","The National Trust is a registered charity .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an organization for helping people in need","example":"Many charities sent money to help the victims of the famine."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the aim of giving money, food, help, etc. to people who are in need","example":"The concert will raise money for local charities."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"kindness and sympathy towards other people, especially when you are judging them","example":"Most of the runners in the London Marathon are raising money for charity"}]],["claim","/kleɪm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “claim”.","claim [kleɪm] -K5 n. 要求；声称；索赔；断言；值得 vt. 要求；声称；需要；认领 vi. 提出要求 时态: claimed, claiming, claims (研四六托雅宝 874/533)","欧陆词典释义：claim [kleɪm] -K5 n. 要求；声称；索赔；断言；值得 vt. 要求；声称；需要；认领 vi. 提出要求 时态: claimed, claiming, claims (研四六托雅宝 874/533)","He claim ed that it was all a conspiracy against him...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to say that something is true although it has not been proved and other people may not believe it","example":"He claims (that) he was not given a fair hearing."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to demand or ask for something because you believe it is your legal right to own or to have it","example":"I don't claim to be an expert."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to ask for money from the government or a company because you have a right to it","example":"Scientists are claiming a major breakthrough in the fight against cancer."}]],["club","/klʌb/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “club”.","club [klʌb] -K5 n. 俱乐部，社团；夜总会；棍棒；（扑克牌中的）梅花 adj. 俱乐部的 vt. 用棍棒打；募集 vi. 集资；组成俱乐部 n. (Club)人名；(英)克拉布 时态: clubbed, clubbing, clubs (中高研四雅 1257/493)","欧陆词典释义：club [klʌb] -K5 n. 俱乐部，社团；夜总会；棍棒；（扑克牌中的）梅花 adj. 俱乐部的 vt. 用棍棒打；募集 vi. 集资；组成俱乐部 n. (Club)人名；(英)克拉布 时态: clubbed, clubbing, clubs (中高研四雅 1257/493)","the Chorlton Conservative Club.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of people who meet together regularly, for a particular activity, sport, etc.","example":"a golf/tennis, etc. club"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the building or rooms that a particular club","example":"a chess/film/movie, etc. club"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a professional sports organization that includes the players, managers, owners and members","example":"to join/belong to"}]],["coefficient","/ˌkəʊɪˈfɪʃnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coefficient”.","coefficient [ˌkəʊɪˈfɪʃnt] n. [数] 系数；率；协同因素 adj. 合作的；共同作用的 (六 5977/7480)","欧陆词典释义：coefficient [ˌkəʊɪˈfɪʃnt] n. [数] 系数；率；协同因素 adj. 合作的；共同作用的 (六 5977/7480)","production coefficient s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a number which is placed before another quantity and which multiplies it, for example 3 in the quantity 3x","example":"the coefficient of friction"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a number that measures a particular property (= characteristic) of a substance","example":"the coefficient of friction"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"the coefficient of friction"}]],["combustion","/kəmˈbʌstʃən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “combustion”.","combustion [kəmˈbʌstʃən] -1 n. 燃烧，氧化；骚动 (六托 9802/12420)","欧陆词典释义：combustion [kəmˈbʌstʃən] -1 n. 燃烧，氧化；骚动 (六托 9802/12420)","The energy is released by combustion on the application of a match...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of burning","example":"Poisonous gases are produced during fossil fuel combustion."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a chemical process in which substances combine with the oxygen","example":"The ratio must be correct in order to achieve complete combustion."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Poisonous gases are produced during fossil fuel combustion."}]],["command","/kəˈmɑ:nd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “command”.","command [kəˈmɑ:nd] -K3 n. 指挥，控制；命令；司令部 vt. 命令，指挥；控制；远望 vi. 命令，指挥；控制 n. (Command)人名；(法)科芒 时态: commanded, commanding, commands (高研四六 2378/2166)","欧陆词典释义：command [kəˈmɑ:nd] -K3 n. 指挥，控制；命令；司令部 vt. 命令，指挥；控制；远望 vi. 命令，指挥；控制 n. (Command)人名；(法)科芒 时态: commanded, commanding, commands (高研四六 2378/2166)","He command ed his troops to attack...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an order given to a person or an animal","example":"Begin when I give the command."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an instruction given to a computer","example":"You must obey the captain's commands."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"control and authority over a situation or a group of people","example":"What is the startup command for the program?"}]],["commerce","/ˈkɒmɜ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “commerce”.","commerce [ˈkɒmɜ:s] -3 n. 贸易；商业；商务 (研四六托 4647/4189)","欧陆词典释义：commerce [ˈkɒmɜ:s] -3 n. 贸易；商业；商务 (研四六托 4647/4189)","They have made their fortunes from industry and commerce .",""],["commitment","/kəˈmɪtmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “commitment”.","commitment [kəˈmɪtmənt] -K2 n. 承诺，保证；委托；承担义务；献身 (高四六托雅 1616/1355)","欧陆词典释义：commitment [kəˈmɪtmənt] -K2 n. 承诺，保证；委托；承担义务；献身 (高四六托雅 1616/1355)"," commitment to the ideals of Bolshevism.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a promise to do something or to behave in a particular way; a promise to support somebody/something; the fact of committing yourself","example":"She doesn't want to make a"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the willingness to work hard and give your energy and time to a job or an activity","example":"the government’s commitment to public services"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that you have promised or agreed to do, or that you have to do","example":"The company's commitment to providing quality at a reasonable price has been vital to its success."}]],["companion","/kəmˈpæniən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “companion”.","companion [kəmˈpæniən] -2 n. 同伴；朋友；指南；手册 vt. 陪伴 n. (Companion)人名；(英)康帕宁 时态: companioned, companioning, companions (高研四六托雅宝 3547/3024)","欧陆词典释义：companion [kəmˈpæniən] -2 n. 同伴；朋友；指南；手册 vt. 陪伴 n. (Companion)人名；(英)康帕宁 时态: companioned, companioning, companions (高研四六托雅宝 3547/3024)","Fred had been her constant companion for the last six years of her life...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person or an animal that travels with you or spends a lot of time with you","example":"travelling companions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who has similar tastes, interests, etc. to your own and whose company you enjoy","example":"Geoff was my companion on the journey."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who shares in your work, pleasures, sadness, etc.","example":"Fear was the hostages' constant companion."}]],["compliance","/kəmˈplaɪəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compliance”.","compliance [kəmˈplaɪəns] -1 n. 顺从，服从；承诺 (研雅宝 4547/4818)","欧陆词典释义：compliance [kəmˈplaɪəns] -1 n. 顺从，服从；承诺 (研雅宝 4547/4818)","Inspectors were sent to visit nuclear sites and verify compliance with the treaty...",""],["comprehensive","/ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “comprehensive”.","comprehensive [ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv] -3 n. 综合学校；专业综合测验 adj. 综合的；广泛的；有理解力的 (研四六托宝 2896/2442)","欧陆词典释义：comprehensive [ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv] -3 n. 综合学校；专业综合测验 adj. 综合的；广泛的；有理解力的 (研四六托宝 2896/2442)","The Rough Guide to Nepal is a comprehensive guide to the region.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"including all, or almost all, the items, details, facts, information, etc., that may be concerned","example":"a comprehensive list of addresses"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"designed for students of all abilities in the same school","example":"a comprehensive study"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"comprehensive insurance ("}]],["compromise","/ˈkɒmprəmaɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compromise”.","compromise [ˈkɒmprəmaɪz] -3 n. 妥协，和解；折衷 vt. 妥协；危害 vi. 妥协；让步 时态: compromised, compromising, compromises (高研四六托雅宝 3751/3685)","欧陆词典释义：compromise [ˈkɒmprəmaɪz] -3 n. 妥协，和解；折衷 vt. 妥协；危害 vi. 妥协；让步 时态: compromised, compromising, compromises (高研四六托雅宝 3751/3685)","Encourage your child to reach a compromise between what he wants and what you want...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an agreement made between two people or groups in which each side gives up some of the things they want so that both sides are happy at the end","example":"After lengthy talks the two sides finally reached a compromise"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a solution to a problem in which two or more things cannot exist together as they are, in which each thing is reduced or changed slightly so that they can exist together","example":"In any relationship, you have to make compromises"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the act of reaching a compromise","example":"a compromise solution/agreement/candidate"}]],["concession","/kənˈseʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “concession”.","concession [kənˈseʃn] -3 n. 让步；特许（权）；承认；退位 (研六托雅宝 5001/3835)","欧陆词典释义：concession [kənˈseʃn] -3 n. 让步；特许（权）；承认；退位 (研六托雅宝 5001/3835)","The King made major concession s to end the confrontation with his people.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that you allow or do, or allow somebody to have, in order to end an argument or to make a situation less difficult","example":"The firm will be forced to make concessions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of giving something or allowing something; the act of conceding","example":"to win a concession from somebody"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a reduction in an amount of money that has to be paid; a ticket that is sold at a reduced price to a particular group of people","example":"a major/an important concession"}]],["concrete","/ˈkɒŋkri:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “concrete”.","concrete [ˈkɒŋkri:t] -K3 n. 具体物；凝结物 adj. 混凝土的；实在的，具体的；有形的 vt. 使凝固；用混凝土修筑 vi. 凝结 时态: concreted, concreting, concretes (高研四六托雅宝 3310/3840)","欧陆词典释义：concrete [ˈkɒŋkri:t] -K3 n. 具体物；凝结物 adj. 混凝土的；实在的，具体的；有形的 vt. 使凝固；用混凝土修筑 vi. 凝结 时态: concreted, concreting, concretes (高研四六托雅宝 3310/3840)","The posts have to be set in concrete ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"made of concrete","example":"a concrete floor"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"based on facts, not on ideas or guesses","example":"concrete evidence/proposals/proof"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a concrete","example":"‘It's only a suspicion,’ she said, ‘nothing concrete.’"}]],["confidence","/ˈkɒnfɪdəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “confidence”.","confidence [ˈkɒnfɪdəns] -K4 n. 信心；信任；秘密 adj. （美）诈骗的；骗得信任的 (研四六托雅宝 1870/1342)","欧陆词典释义：confidence [ˈkɒnfɪdəns] -K4 n. 信心；信任；秘密 adj. （美）诈骗的；骗得信任的 (研四六托雅宝 1870/1342)","I have every confidence in you...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the feeling that you can trust, believe in and be sure about the abilities or good qualities of somebody/something","example":"The players all have confidence in"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a belief in your own ability to do things and be successful","example":"A fall in unemployment will help to restore consumer confidence."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the feeling that you are certain about something","example":"a lack of confidence in the government"}]],["contain","/kənˈteɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contain”.","contain [kənˈteɪn] -K4 vi. 含有；自制 vt. 包含；控制；容纳；牵制（敌军） 时态: contained, containing, contains (高研四六托宝 931/559)","欧陆词典释义：contain [kənˈteɪn] -K4 vi. 含有；自制 vt. 包含；控制；容纳；牵制（敌军） 时态: contained, containing, contains (高研四六托宝 931/559)","The bag contain ed a Christmas card...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"if something contains","example":"This drink doesn't contain any alcohol."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to keep your feelings under control","example":"Her statement contained one or two inaccuracies."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to prevent something harmful from spreading or getting worse","example":"a brown envelope containing dollar bills"}]],["continuity","/ˌkɒntɪˈnju:əti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “continuity”.","continuity [ˌkɒntɪˈnju:əti] -1 n. 连续性；一连串；分镜头剧本 (托雅 6432/4599)","欧陆词典释义：continuity [ˌkɒntɪˈnju:əti] -1 n. 连续性；一连串；分镜头剧本 (托雅 6432/4599)","A historical awareness also imparts a sense of continuity .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of not stopping or not changing","example":"to ensure/provide/maintain continuity"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a logical connection between the parts of something, or between two things","example":"The novel fails to achieve narrative continuity."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the organization of a film/movie or television programme, especially making sure that people’s clothes, objects, etc. are the same from one scene to the next","example":"There are obvious continuities between diet and health."}]],["accounting","/əˈkaʊntɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accounting”.","accounting [əˈkaʊntɪŋ] -2 n. 会计，会计学；账单 v. 解释（account的ing形式）；叙述 原型: accounting 是 account 的现在分词 (托雅 3921/3070)","欧陆词典释义：accounting [əˈkaʊntɪŋ] -2 n. 会计，会计学；账单 v. 解释（account的ing形式）；叙述 原型: accounting 是 account 的现在分词 (托雅 3921/3070)","allegations of theft, forgery and false accounting .",""],["accuracy","/ˈækjərəsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accuracy”.","accuracy [ˈækjərəsi] n. [数] 精确度，准确性 (高研四六托雅宝 4076/3958)","欧陆词典释义：accuracy [ˈækjərəsi] n. [数] 精确度，准确性 (高研四六托雅宝 4076/3958)","We cannot guarantee the accuracy of these figures.",""],["adaptation","/ˌædæpˈteɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adaptation”.","adaptation [ˌædæpˈteɪʃn] -1 n. 适应；改编；改编本，改写本 (高托 5196/5438)","欧陆词典释义：adaptation [ˌædæpˈteɪʃn] -1 n. 适应；改编；改编本，改写本 (高托 5196/5438)","Branagh's screen adaptation of Shakespeare's Henry the Fifth.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a film/movie, book or play that is based on a particular piece of work but that has been changed for a new situation","example":"a screen adaptation of Shakespeare’s ‘Macbeth’"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of changing something, for example your behaviour, to suit a new situation","example":"the adaptation of desert species to the hot conditions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"Adaptations in plants occur over thousands of years."}]],["address","/əˈdres/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “address”.","address [əˈdres] -K4 n. 地址；演讲；致辞；说话的技巧；称呼 vt. 演说；从事；忙于；写姓名地址；向…致辞；与…说话；提出；处理 时态: addressed, addressing, addresses (中高研四六托雅宝 1028/1522)","欧陆词典释义：address [əˈdres] -K4 n. 地址；演讲；致辞；说话的技巧；称呼 vt. 演说；从事；忙于；写姓名地址；向…致辞；与…说话；提出；处理 时态: addressed, addressing, addresses (中高研四六托雅宝 1028/1522)","The address is 2025 M Street, Northwest, Washington, DC, 20036...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"details of where somebody lives or works and where letters, etc. can be sent","example":"What's your name and address"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a series of words and symbols that tells you where you can find something using a computer, for example on the Internet","example":"I'll give you my address and phone number."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a formal speech that is made in front of an audience","example":"Is that your home address"}]],["adoption","/əˈdɒpʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adoption”.","adoption [əˈdɒpʃn] n. 采用；收养；接受 (六托 3674/4220)","欧陆词典释义：adoption [əˈdɒpʃn] n. 采用；收养；接受 (六托 3674/4220)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adoption”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of adopting a child","example":"She put the baby up for adoption."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the decision to start using something such as an idea, a plan or a name","example":"the adoption of new technology"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of choosing somebody as a candidate for an election","example":"his adoption as the Labour candidate"}]],["agenda","/əˈdʒendə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “agenda”.","agenda [əˈdʒendə] -3 n. 议程；日常工作事项；日程表 (高研托雅宝 2130/3026)","欧陆词典释义：agenda [əˈdʒendə] -3 n. 议程；日常工作事项；日程表 (高研托雅宝 2130/3026)","Does television set the agenda on foreign policy?...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a list of items to be discussed at a meeting","example":"The next item on the agenda"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a plan of things to be done, or problems to be addressed","example":"This is an ambitious agenda that will take time to implement."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the intention behind what somebody says or does, that is often secret","example":"Cost-cutting is top of the agenda"}]],["assignment","/əˈsaɪnmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assignment”.","assignment [əˈsaɪnmənt] -2 n. 分配；任务；作业；功课 (研四六托雅 3128/3817)","欧陆词典释义：assignment [əˈsaɪnmənt] -2 n. 分配；任务；作业；功课 (研四六托雅 3128/3817)","The assessment for the course involves written assignment s and practical tests.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a task or piece of work that somebody is given to do, usually as part of their job or studies","example":"You will need to complete three written assignments per semester."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of giving something to somebody; the act of giving somebody a particular task","example":"She is in Greece on an assignment for one of the Sunday newspapers."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"one of our reporters on assignment"}]],["barrier","/ˈbæriə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “barrier”.","barrier [ˈbæriə(r)] -K3 n. 障碍物，屏障；界线 vt. 把…关入栅栏 n. (Barrier)人名；(法)巴里耶 (高研四六托雅宝 2609/2629)","欧陆词典释义：barrier [ˈbæriə(r)] -K3 n. 障碍物，屏障；界线 vt. 把…关入栅栏 n. (Barrier)人名；(法)巴里耶 (高研四六托雅宝 2609/2629)","Duties and taxes are the most obvious barrier to free trade.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an object like a fence that prevents people from moving forward from one place to another","example":"The crowd had to stand behind barriers."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a problem, rule or situation that prevents somebody from doing something, or that makes something impossible","example":"Show your ticket at the barrier."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that exists between one thing or person and another and keeps them separate","example":"The car crashed into the safety barrier and burst into flames."}]],["connection","/kəˈnekʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “connection”.","connection [kəˈnekʃn] -K3 n. 连接；关系；人脉；连接件 (高研四六托 1421/1669)","欧陆词典释义：connection [kəˈnekʃn] -K3 n. 连接；关系；人脉；连接件 (高研四六托 1421/1669)","There was no evidence of a connection between BSE and the brain diseases recently confirmed in cats...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that connects two facts, ideas, etc.","example":"Scientists have established a connection between cholesterol levels and heart disease."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of connecting or the state of being connected","example":"His resignation must have some connection with the recent scandal."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a point, especially in an electrical system, where two parts connect","example":"a direct/close/strong connection"}]],["consultant","/kənˈsʌltənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consultant”.","consultant [kənˈsʌltənt] -3 n. 顾问；咨询者；会诊医生 (高研六托雅 2480/2605)","欧陆词典释义：consultant [kənˈsʌltənt] -3 n. 顾问；咨询者；会诊医生 (高研六托雅 2480/2605)","Shirley's brother is now a consultant heart surgeon in Sweden.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who knows a lot about a particular subject and is employed to give advice about it to other people","example":"a firm of management consultants"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a hospital doctor of the highest rank who is a specialist in a particular area of medicine","example":"the President’s consultant on economic affairs"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 17th cent.","example":"a consultant in obstetrics"}]],["control","/kənˈtrəʊl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “control”.","control [kənˈtrəʊl] -K5 n. 控制；管理；抑制；操纵装置 vt. 控制；管理；抑制 时态: controlled, controlling, controls (中高研四雅宝 432/339)","欧陆词典释义：control [kənˈtrəʊl] -K5 n. 控制；管理；抑制；操纵装置 vt. 控制；管理；抑制 时态: controlled, controlling, controls (中高研四雅宝 432/339)","The restructuring involves Mr Ronson giving up control of the company...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the power to make decisions about how a country, an area, an organization, etc. is run","example":"The party is expecting to gain control of"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the ability to make somebody/something do what you want","example":"The Democrats will probably lose control of"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the act of restricting, limiting or managing something; a method of doing this","example":"A military junta took control of the country"}]],["abroad","/əˈbrɔ:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abroad”.","abroad [əˈbrɔ:d] -K3 n. 海外；异国 adj. 往国外的 adv. 在国外；到海外 (中高托 3363/2243)","欧陆词典释义：abroad [əˈbrɔ:d] -K3 n. 海外；异国 adj. 往国外的 adv. 在国外；到海外 (中高托 3363/2243)","I would love to go abroad this year, perhaps to the South of France.",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"in or to a foreign country","example":"to be/go/travel/live abroad"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"being talked about or felt by many people","example":"She worked abroad for a year."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"outside; outdoors","example":"imports of cheap food from abroad"}]],["accompany","/əˈkʌmpəni/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accompany”.","accompany [əˈkʌmpəni] -K3 vt. 陪伴，伴随；伴奏 vi. 伴奏，伴唱 时态: accompanied, accompanying, accompanies (高研四六托雅宝 2438/1902)","欧陆词典释义：accompany [əˈkʌmpəni] -K3 vt. 陪伴，伴随；伴奏 vi. 伴奏，伴唱 时态: accompanied, accompanying, accompanies (高研四六托雅宝 2438/1902)","Ken agreed to accompany me on a trip to Africa...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to travel or go somewhere with somebody","example":"His wife accompanied him on the trip."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to happen or appear with something else","example":"I must ask you to accompany me to the police station."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to play a musical instrument, especially a piano, while somebody else sings or plays the main tune","example":"Warships will accompany the convoy."}]],["accomplishment","/əˈkʌmplɪʃmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accomplishment”.","accomplishment [əˈkʌmplɪʃmənt] -1 n. 成就；完成；技艺，技能 (六托 4308/13752)","欧陆词典释义：accomplishment [əˈkʌmplɪʃmənt] -1 n. 成就；完成；技艺，技能 (六托 4308/13752)","For a novelist, that's quite an accomplishment ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an impressive thing that is done or achieved after a lot of work","example":"It was one of the President's greatest accomplishments."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a skill or special ability","example":"The series of paintings is quite an accomplishment."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the successful completing of something","example":"Drawing and singing were among her many accomplishments."}]],["advancement","/ədˈvɑ:nsmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “advancement”.","advancement [ədˈvɑ:nsmənt] -1 n. 前进，进步；提升 (托 6629/8724)","欧陆词典释义：advancement [ədˈvɑ:nsmənt] -1 n. 前进，进步；提升 (托 6629/8724)","He cared little for social advancement .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of helping something to make progress or succeed; the progress that is made","example":"the advancement of knowledge/education/science"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"progress in a job, social class, etc.","example":"There are good opportunities for advancement if you have the right skills."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"advancement in the profession"}]],["afford","/əˈfɔ:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “afford”.","afford [əˈfɔ:d] -K3 vt. 给予，提供；买得起 n. (Afford)人名；(英)阿福德 时态: afforded, affording, affords (中高研四六托雅 1846/1722)","欧陆词典释义：afford [əˈfɔ:d] -K3 vt. 给予，提供；买得起 n. (Afford)人名；(英)阿福德 时态: afforded, affording, affords (中高研四六托雅 1846/1722)","My parents can't even afford a new refrigerator...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have enough money or time to be able to buy or to do something","example":"Can we afford a new car?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"if you say that you can’t afford","example":"None of them could afford £50 for a ticket."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to provide somebody with something","example":"She felt she couldn't afford any more time off work."}]],["aircraft","/ˈeəkrɑ:ft/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “aircraft”.","aircraft [ˈeəkrɑ:ft] -K4 n. 飞机，航空器 (高研四托 2803/1538)","欧陆词典释义：aircraft [ˈeəkrɑ:ft] -K4 n. 飞机，航空器 (高研四托 2803/1538)","The return flight of the aircraft was delayed...",""],["allow","/əˈlaʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “allow”.","allow [əˈlaʊ] -K5 vi. 容许；考虑 vt. 允许；给予；认可 时态: allowed, allowing, allows (中高研四 339/257)","欧陆词典释义：allow [əˈlaʊ] -K5 vi. 容许；考虑 vt. 允许；给予；认可 时态: allowed, allowing, allows (中高研四 339/257)","The children are not allow ed to watch violent TV programmes...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to let somebody/something do something; to let something happen or be done","example":"His parents won't allow him to stay out late."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to let somebody have something","example":"He is not allowed to"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to let somebody/something go into, through, out of, etc. a place","example":"They shouldn't be allowed to get away with it."}]],["ambition","/æmˈbɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ambition”.","ambition [æmˈbɪʃn] -K3 n. 野心，雄心；抱负，志向 vt. 追求；有…野心 (高研四六托雅 4283/3185)","欧陆词典释义：ambition [æmˈbɪʃn] -K3 n. 野心，雄心；抱负，志向 vt. 追求；有…野心 (高研四六托雅 4283/3185)","His ambition is to sail round the world...",""],["amuse","/əˈmju:z/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “amuse”.","amuse [əˈmju:z] -K1 vt. 娱乐；消遣；使发笑；使愉快 时态: amused, amusing, amuses (高研四六雅宝 9683/8734)","欧陆词典释义：amuse [əˈmju:z] -K1 vt. 娱乐；消遣；使发笑；使愉快 时态: amused, amusing, amuses (高研四六雅宝 9683/8734)","The thought seemed to amuse him...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody laugh or smile","example":"My funny drawings amused the kids."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make time pass pleasantly for somebody/yourself","example":"This will amuse you."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"It amused him to think that they were probably talking about him at that very moment."}]],["anxiety","/æŋˈzaɪəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “anxiety”.","anxiety [æŋˈzaɪəti] -K3 n. 焦虑；渴望；挂念；令人焦虑的事 (高研四六托雅 2467/2612)","欧陆词典释义：anxiety [æŋˈzaɪəti] -K3 n. 焦虑；渴望；挂念；令人焦虑的事 (高研四六托雅 2467/2612)","Her voice was full of anxiety ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state of feeling nervous or worried that something bad is going to happen","example":"acute/intense/deep anxiety"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a worry or fear about something","example":"Some hospital patients experience high levels of anxiety."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a strong feeling of wanting to do something or of wanting something to happen","example":"Waiting for exam results is a time of great anxiety."}]],["approve","/əˈpru:v/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “approve”.","approve [əˈpru:v] -K4 vi. 批准；赞成；满意 vt. 批准；赞成；为…提供证据 时态: approved, approving, approves (高研四六托 2053/1762)","欧陆词典释义：approve [əˈpru:v] -K4 vi. 批准；赞成；满意 vt. 批准；赞成；为…提供证据 时态: approved, approving, approves (高研四六托 2053/1762)","Not everyone approve s of the festival...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think that somebody/something is good, acceptable or suitable","example":"I told my mother I wanted to leave school but she didn't approve."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to officially agree to a plan, request, etc.","example":"Do you approve of my idea?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to say that something is good enough to be used or is correct","example":"She doesn't approve of me leaving school this year."}]],["approximately","/əˈprɒksɪmətli/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “approximately”.","approximately [əˈprɒksɪmətli] -K adv. 大约，近似地；近于 (高四六托 2365/2850)","欧陆词典释义：approximately [əˈprɒksɪmətli] -K adv. 大约，近似地；近于 (高四六托 2365/2850)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “approximately”.",""],["arise","/əˈraɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “arise”.","arise [əˈraɪz] -K3 vi. 出现；上升；起立 n. (Arise)人名；(西)阿里塞；(日)在濑(姓) 时态: arose, arisen, arising, arises (高研四六托雅 2581/1043)","欧陆词典释义：arise [əˈraɪz] -K3 vi. 出现；上升；起立 n. (Arise)人名；(西)阿里塞；(日)在濑(姓) 时态: arose, arisen, arising, arises (高研四六托雅 2581/1043)","if a problem arise s later in the pregnancy...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to happen; to start to exist","example":"A new crisis has arisen."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to happen as a result of a particular situation","example":"We keep them informed of any changes as they arise."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to begin to exist or develop","example":"Children should be disciplined when the need arises"}]],["artificial","/ˌɑ:tɪˈfɪʃl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “artificial”.","artificial [ˌɑ:tɪˈfɪʃl] -K2 adj. 人造的；仿造的；虚伪的；非原产地的；武断的 (高研四六托雅宝 4003/3499)","欧陆词典释义：artificial [ˌɑ:tɪˈfɪʃl] -K2 adj. 人造的；仿造的；虚伪的；非原产地的；武断的 (高研四六托雅宝 4003/3499)","a wholefood diet free from artificial additives, colours and flavours...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"made or produced to copy something natural; not real","example":"an artificial limb/flower/sweetener/fertilizer"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"created by people; not happening naturally","example":"artificial lighting/light"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not what it appears to be","example":"artificial flowers"}]],["aside","/əˈsaɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “aside”.","aside [əˈsaɪd] -K3 prep. 在…旁边 n. 旁白；私语，悄悄话；离题的话 adv. 离开，撇开；在旁边 (高研四 1878/2376)","欧陆词典释义：aside [əˈsaɪd] -K3 prep. 在…旁边 n. 旁白；私语，悄悄话；离题的话 adv. 离开，撇开；在旁边 (高研四 1878/2376)","Sarah closed the book and laid it aside .",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"to one side; out of the way","example":"She pulled the curtain aside."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be used later","example":"Stand aside"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used after nouns to say that except for one thing, something is true","example":"He took me aside"}]],["assembly","/əˈsembli/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assembly”.","assembly [əˈsembli] -3 n. 装配；集会，集合 (研四托 3965/1596)","欧陆词典释义：assembly [əˈsembli] -3 n. 装配；集会，集合 (研四托 3965/1596)","the campaign for the first free election to the National Assembly.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of people who have been elected to meet together regularly and make decisions or laws for a particular region or country","example":"state/legislative/federal/local assemblies"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the meeting together of a group of people for a particular purpose; a group of people who meet together for a particular purpose","example":"Power has been handed over to provincial and regional assemblies."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a meeting of the teachers and students in a school, usually at the start of the day, to give information, discuss school events or say prayers together","example":"The national assembly has voted to adopt the budget."}]],["assist","/əˈsɪst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assist”.","assist [əˈsɪst] -K3 n. 帮助；助攻 vi. 参加；出席 vt. 帮助；促进 时态: assisted, assisting, assists (高研四六托 2475/2162)","欧陆词典释义：assist [əˈsɪst] -K3 n. 帮助；助攻 vi. 参加；出席 vt. 帮助；促进 时态: assisted, assisting, assists (高研四六托 2475/2162)","Julia was assist ing him to prepare his speech...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to help somebody to do something","example":"Anyone willing to assist can contact this number."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to help something to happen more easily","example":"We are looking for people who would be willing to assist in the group's work."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"We'll do all we can to assist you."}]],["attract","/əˈtrækt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attract”.","attract [əˈtrækt] -K4 vt. 吸引；引起 vi. 吸引；有吸引力 时态: attracted, attracting, attracts (高研四托 1867/1477)","欧陆词典释义：attract [əˈtrækt] -K4 vt. 吸引；引起 vi. 吸引；有吸引力 时态: attracted, attracting, attracts (高研四托 1867/1477)","The Cardiff Bay project is attract ing many visitors...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"if you are attracted","example":"I had always been attracted by the idea of working abroad."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody/something come somewhere or take part in something","example":"What first attracted me to her was her sense of humour."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make people have a particular reaction","example":"That was what first attracted me to the place."}]],["automatic","/ˌɔ:təˈmætɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “automatic”.","automatic [ˌɔ:təˈmætɪk] -K3 n. 自动机械；自动手枪 adj. 自动的；无意识的；必然的 (高研四六托雅 4045/3184)","欧陆词典释义：automatic [ˌɔ:təˈmætɪk] -K3 n. 自动机械；自动手枪 adj. 自动的；无意识的；必然的 (高研四六托雅 4045/3184)","Modern trains have automatic doors.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having controls that work without needing a person to operate them","example":"automatic doors"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"done or happening without thinking","example":"a fully automatic"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"always happening as a result of a particular action or situation","example":"automatic transmission ("}]],["average","/ˈævərɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “average”.","average [ˈævərɪdʒ] -K4 n. 平均；平均数；海损 adj. 平均的；普通的；通常的 vt. 算出…的平均数；将…平均分配；使…平衡 vi. 平均为；呈中间色 时态: averaged, averaging, averages (高研四托雅 1299/1527)","欧陆词典释义：average [ˈævərɪdʒ] -K4 n. 平均；平均数；海损 adj. 平均的；普通的；通常的 vt. 算出…的平均数；将…平均分配；使…平衡 vi. 平均为；呈中间色 时态: averaged, averaging, averages (高研四托雅 1299/1527)","Take the average of those ratios and multiply by a hundred.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"calculated by adding several amounts together, finding a total, and dividing the total by the number of amounts","example":"an average rate/cost/price"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"typical or normal","example":"Average earnings are around £20 000 per annum."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"ordinary; not special","example":"at an average speed of 100 miles per hour"}]],["aware","/əˈweə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “aware”.","aware [əˈweə(r)] -K4 adj. 意识到的；知道的；有…方面知识的；懂世故的 n. (Aware)人名；(阿拉伯、索)阿瓦雷 (高研四托雅 1439/921)","欧陆词典释义：aware [əˈweə(r)] -K4 adj. 意识到的；知道的；有…方面知识的；懂世故的 n. (Aware)人名；(阿拉伯、索)阿瓦雷 (高研四托雅 1439/921)","Smokers are well aware of the dangers to their own health...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"knowing or realizing something","example":"As you're aware, this is not a new problem."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"noticing that something is present, or that something is happening","example":"As far as I'm aware"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"interested in and knowing about something, and thinking it is important","example":"acutely/painfully"}]],["behaviour","/bɪˈheɪvjə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “behaviour”.","behaviour [bɪˈheɪvjə(r)] -K4 n. 行为；习性；运行状况（=behavior） (中高托 10352/787)","欧陆词典释义：behaviour [bɪˈheɪvjə(r)] -K4 n. 行为；习性；运行状况（=behavior） (中高托 10352/787)","Make sure that good behaviour is rewarded.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way that somebody behaves, especially towards other people","example":"good/bad behaviour"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way a person, an animal, a plant, a chemical, etc. behaves or functions in a particular situation","example":"social/sexual/criminal behaviour"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"His behaviour towards her was becoming more and more aggressive."}]],["beyond","/bɪˈjɒnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “beyond”.","beyond [bɪˈjɒnd] -K4 prep. 超过；越过；那一边；在...较远的一边 n. 远处 adv. 在远处；在更远处 (中高研四 746/944)","欧陆词典释义：beyond [bɪˈjɒnd] -K4 prep. 超过；越过；那一边；在...较远的一边 n. 远处 adv. 在远处；在更远处 (中高研四 746/944)","They heard footsteps in the main room, beyond a door...",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"on or to the further side of something","example":"The road continues beyond the village up into the hills."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"later than a particular time","example":"It won't go on beyond midnight."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"more than something","example":"I know what I'll be doing for the next three weeks but I haven't thought beyond that."}]],["blame","/bleɪm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “blame”.","blame [bleɪm] -K4 n. 责备；责任；过失 vt. 责备；归咎于 时态: blamed, blaming, blames (高研四六托雅 1797/2043)","欧陆词典释义：blame [bleɪm] -K4 n. 责备；责任；过失 vt. 责备；归咎于 时态: blamed, blaming, blames (高研四六托雅 1797/2043)","The commission is expected to blame the army for many of the atrocities...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think or say that somebody/something is responsible for something bad","example":"She doesn't blame anyone for her father's death."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"A dropped cigarette is being blamed for the fire."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be responsible for something bad","example":"Police are blaming the accident on dangerous driving."}]],["block","/blɒk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “block”.","block [blɒk] -K4 n. 块；街区；大厦；障碍物 adj. 成批的，大块的；交通堵塞的 vt. 阻止；阻塞；限制；封盖 n. (Block)人名；(英、法、德、西、葡、芬、罗)布洛克 时态: blocked, blocking, blocks (高托雅 1314/1641)","欧陆词典释义：block [blɒk] -K4 n. 块；街区；大厦；障碍物 adj. 成批的，大块的；交通堵塞的 vt. 阻止；阻塞；限制；封盖 n. (Block)人名；(英、法、德、西、葡、芬、罗)布洛克 时态: blocked, blocking, blocks (高托雅 1314/1641)"," block s of council flats.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large piece of a solid material that is square or rectangular","example":"a block of ice/concrete/stone"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a tall building that contains flats or offices; buildings that form part of a school, hospital, etc. which are used for a particular purpose","example":"a chopping block ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a group of buildings with streets on all sides","example":"a tower block"}]],["boil","/bɔɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “boil”.","boil [bɔɪl] -K3 n. 沸腾，煮沸；疖子 vt. 煮沸，烧开；使…激动；使…蒸发 vi. 煮沸，沸腾；激动，激昂 n. (Boil)人名；(俄)博伊尔 时态: boiled, boiling, boils (高研四托雅 4258/4944)","欧陆词典释义：boil [bɔɪl] -K3 n. 沸腾，煮沸；疖子 vt. 煮沸，烧开；使…激动；使…蒸发 vi. 煮沸，沸腾；激动，激昂 n. (Boil)人名；(俄)博伊尔 时态: boiled, boiling, boils (高研四托雅 4258/4944)","I stood in the kitchen, waiting for the water to boil ...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"when a liquid boils","example":"The water was bubbling and boiling away."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"when a kettle","example":"Boil plenty of salted water, then add the spaghetti."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to cook or wash something in boiling water; to be cooked or washed in boiling water","example":"The kettle's boiling."}]],["bomb","/bɒm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bomb”.","bomb [bɒm] -K4 n. 炸弹 vt. 轰炸，投弹于 vi. 轰炸，投弹；失败 时态: bombed, bombing, bombs (高研四六 1992/2266)","欧陆词典释义：bomb [bɒm] -K4 n. 炸弹 vt. 轰炸，投弹于 vi. 轰炸，投弹；失败 时态: bombed, bombing, bombs (高研四六 1992/2266)","Bombs went off at two London train stations...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a weapon designed to explode at a particular time or when it is dropped or thrown","example":"a bomb attack/blast/explosion"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"nuclear weapons ( atomic","example":"a bomb goes off/explodes"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a lot of money","example":"extensive bomb damage"}]],["borrow","/ˈbɒrəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “borrow”.","borrow [ˈbɒrəʊ] -K3 vt. 借；借用 vi. 借；借用；从其他语言中引入 n. (Borrow)人名；(英)博罗 时态: borrowed, borrowing, borrows (中高 3214/2639)","欧陆词典释义：borrow [ˈbɒrəʊ] -K3 vt. 借；借用 vi. 借；借用；从其他语言中引入 n. (Borrow)人名；(英)博罗 时态: borrowed, borrowing, borrows (中高 3214/2639)","Can I borrow a pen please? ...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take and use something that belongs to somebody else, and return it to them at a later time","example":"Can I borrow your umbrella?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take money from a person or bank and agree to pay it back to them at a later time","example":"Members can borrow up to ten books from the library at any one time."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take words, ideas, etc. from another language, person, etc. and use them, as your own","example":"I borrowed the DVD off my brother."}]],["broad","/brɔ:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “broad”.","broad [brɔ:d] -K4 n. 宽阔部分 adj. 宽的，辽阔的；显著的；大概的 adv. 宽阔地 n. (Broad)人名；(英、德)布罗德 级别: broader, broadest (高研四 1404/1462)","欧陆词典释义：broad [brɔ:d] -K4 n. 宽阔部分 adj. 宽的，辽阔的；显著的；大概的 adv. 宽阔地 n. (Broad)人名；(英、德)布罗德 级别: broader, broadest (高研四 1404/1462)","His shoulders were broad and his waist narrow...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"wide","example":"a broad street/avenue/river"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used after a measurement of distance to show how wide something is","example":"broad shoulders"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"including a great variety of people or things","example":"He is tall, broad and muscular."}]],["burst","/bɜ:st/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “burst”.","burst [bɜ:st] -K3 n. 爆发，突发；爆炸 vt. 爆发，突发；爆炸 vi. 爆发，突发；爆炸 n. (Burst)人名；(德、罗)布尔斯特 时态: burst, bursting, bursts (高研四六托 3560/3011)","欧陆词典释义：burst [bɜ:st] -K3 n. 爆发，突发；爆炸 vt. 爆发，突发；爆炸 vi. 爆发，突发；爆炸 n. (Burst)人名；(德、罗)布尔斯特 时态: burst, bursting, bursts (高研四六托 3560/3011)","The driver lost control when a tyre burst ...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to break open or apart, especially because of pressure from inside; to make something break in this way","example":"That balloon will burst if you blow it up any more."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to go or move somewhere suddenly with great force; to come from somewhere suddenly","example":"The dam burst under the weight of water."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be very full of something; to be very full and almost breaking open","example":"Shells were bursting ("}]],["candidate","/ˈkændɪdət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “candidate”.","candidate [ˈkændɪdət] -K4 n. 候选人，候补者；应试者 (高研四六托雅宝 957/1227)","欧陆词典释义：candidate [ˈkændɪdət] -K4 n. 候选人，候补者；应试者 (高研四六托雅宝 957/1227)","The Democratic candidate is still leading in the polls...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who is trying to be elected or is applying for a job","example":"one of the leading candidates for the presidency"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person taking an exam","example":"a presidential candidate"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person or group that is considered suitable for something or that is likely to get something or to be something","example":"He stood as a candidate in the local elections."}]],["capture","/ˈkæptʃə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “capture”.","capture [ˈkæptʃə(r)] -K3 n. 捕获；战利品，俘虏 vt. 俘获；夺得；捕捉，拍摄,录制 时态: captured, capturing, captures (研四六托雅宝 1715/2658)","欧陆词典释义：capture [ˈkæptʃə(r)] -K3 n. 捕获；战利品，俘虏 vt. 俘获；夺得；捕捉，拍摄,录制 时态: captured, capturing, captures (研四六托雅宝 1715/2658)","The guerrillas shot down one aeroplane and capture d the pilot...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to catch a person or an animal and keep them as a prisoner or in a confined space","example":"Allied troops captured over 300 enemy soldiers."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to take control of a place, building, etc. using force","example":"The animals are captured in nets and sold to local zoos."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to succeed in getting control of something that other people are also trying to control","example":"The city was captured in 1941."}]],["celebrate","/ˈselɪbreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “celebrate”.","celebrate [ˈselɪbreɪt] -K3 vt. 庆祝；举行；赞美；祝贺；宣告 vi. 庆祝；过节；举行宗教仪式 时态: celebrated, celebrating, celebrates (中高研四六托 2019/2443)","欧陆词典释义：celebrate [ˈselɪbreɪt] -K3 vt. 庆祝；举行；赞美；祝贺；宣告 vi. 庆祝；过节；举行宗教仪式 时态: celebrated, celebrating, celebrates (中高研四六托 2019/2443)","I was in a mood to celebrate ...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show that a day or an event is important by doing something special on it","example":"Jake's passed his exams. We're going out to celebrate."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to perform a religious ceremony, especially the Christian communion (","example":"We celebrated our 25th wedding anniversary in Florence."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to praise somebody/something","example":"How do people celebrate New Year in your country?"}]],["central","/ˈsentrəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “central”.","central [ˈsentrəl] -K5 n. 电话总机 adj. 中心的；主要的；中枢的 (高研四六雅 743/521)","欧陆词典释义：central [ˈsentrəl] -K5 n. 电话总机 adj. 中心的；主要的；中枢的 (高研四六雅 743/521)","Central America's Caribbean coast...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"most important","example":"The central issue is that of widespread racism."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having power or control over other parts","example":"She has been a central figure in the campaign."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"in the centre of an area or object","example":"Prevention also plays a central role in traditional medicine."}]],["ceremony","/ˈserəməni/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ceremony”.","ceremony [ˈserəməni] -K3 n. 典礼，仪式；礼节，礼仪；客套，虚礼 (高研四六托雅宝 2670/3313)","欧陆词典释义：ceremony [ˈserəməni] -K3 n. 典礼，仪式；礼节，礼仪；客套，虚礼 (高研四六托雅宝 2670/3313)","his grandmother's funeral, a private ceremony attended only by the family...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a public or religious occasion that includes a series of formal or traditional actions","example":"an awards/opening ceremony"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"formal behaviour; traditional actions and words used on particular formal occasions","example":"a wedding/marriage ceremony"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The royal guests were welcomed with pomp and ceremony."}]],["chemical","/ˈkemɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “chemical”.","chemical [ˈkemɪkl] -K4 n. 化学制品，化学药品 adj. 化学的 (高研四六 2617/2548)","欧陆词典释义：chemical [ˈkemɪkl] -K4 n. 化学制品，化学药品 adj. 化学的 (高研四六 2617/2548)"," chemical reactions that cause ozone destruction.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with chemistry","example":"a chemical element"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"produced by or using processes which involve changes to atoms or molecules","example":"the chemical industry"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"using or connected with chemicals","example":"chemical reactions/processes"}]],["classical","/ˈklæsɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “classical”.","classical [ˈklæsɪkl] -3 n. 古典音乐 adj. 古典的；经典的；传统的；第一流的 (高研四六雅 3489/2562)","欧陆词典释义：classical [ˈklæsɪkl] -3 n. 古典音乐 adj. 古典的；经典的；传统的；第一流的 (高研四六雅 3489/2562)","Fokine did not change the steps of classical ballet; instead he found new ways of using them.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"widely accepted and used for a long time; traditional in style or idea","example":"the classical economics of Smith and Ricardo"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with or influenced by the culture of ancient Greece and Rome","example":"the classical theory of unemployment"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"written in a Western musical tradition, usually using an established form (for example a symphony","example":"classical and modern ballet"}]],["collapse","/kəˈlæps/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “collapse”.","collapse [kəˈlæps] -K4 n. 倒塌；失败；衰竭 vt. 使倒塌，使崩溃；使萎陷；折叠 vi. 倒塌；瓦解；暴跌 时态: collapsed, collapsing, collapses (研四六托雅宝 3212/3094)","欧陆词典释义：collapse [kəˈlæps] -K4 n. 倒塌；失败；衰竭 vt. 使倒塌，使崩溃；使萎陷；折叠 vi. 倒塌；瓦解；暴跌 时态: collapsed, collapsing, collapses (研四六托雅宝 3212/3094)","A section of the Bay Bridge had collapse d...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to fall down or fall in suddenly, often after breaking apart","example":"The roof collapsed under the weight of snow."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to fall down (and usually become unconscious), especially because you are very ill/sick","example":"He collapsed in the street and died two hours later."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to sit or lie down and relax, especially after working hard","example":"When I get home I like to collapse on the sofa and listen to music."}]],["commercial","/kəˈmɜ:ʃl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “commercial”.","commercial [kəˈmɜ:ʃl] -K4 n. 商业广告 adj. 商业的；营利的；靠广告收入的 (研四六托雅 1027/1235)","欧陆词典释义：commercial [kəˈmɜ:ʃl] -K4 n. 商业广告 adj. 商业的；营利的；靠广告收入的 (研四六托雅 1027/1235)","Docklands in its heyday was a major centre of industrial and commercial activity...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with the buying and selling of goods and services","example":"the commercial heart of the city"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"making or intended to make a profit","example":"She is developing the commercial side of the organization."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"more concerned with profit and being popular than with quality","example":"a commercial vehicle ("}]],["commit","/kəˈmɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “commit”.","commit [kəˈmɪt] -K4 vt. 犯罪，做错事；把...交托给；指派…作战；使…承担义务 时态: committed, committing, commits (高研四六托雅宝 1394/1393)","欧陆词典释义：commit [kəˈmɪt] -K4 vt. 犯罪，做错事；把...交托给；指派…作战；使…承担义务 时态: committed, committing, commits (高研四六托雅宝 1394/1393)","I have never commit ted any crime...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to do something wrong or illegal","example":"to commit murder/adultery"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to kill yourself deliberately","example":"Most crimes are committed by young men."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to promise sincerely that you will definitely do something, keep to an agreement or arrangement, etc.","example":"appalling crimes committed against innocent children"}]],["common","/ˈkɒmən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “common”.","common [ˈkɒmən] -K1 n. 普通；平民；公有地 adj. 共同的；普通的；一般的；通常的 n. (Common)人名；(法)科蒙；(英)康芒 (中高研四六雅 710/554)","欧陆词典释义：common [ˈkɒmən] -K1 n. 普通；平民；公有地 adj. 共同的；普通的；一般的；通常的 n. (Common)人名；(法)科蒙；(英)康芒 (中高研四六雅 710/554)","His name was Hansen, a common name in Norway...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"happening often; existing in large numbers or in many places","example":"Jackson is a common English name."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"shared by or belonging to two or more people or by the people in a group","example":"Breast cancer is the most common form of cancer among women in this country."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"ordinary; not unusual or special","example":"Some birds which were once a common sight"}]],["compete","/kəmˈpi:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compete”.","compete [kəmˈpi:t] -K3 vi. 竞争；比赛；对抗 时态: competed, competing, competes (高研四六托宝 2065/2583)","欧陆词典释义：compete [kəmˈpi:t] -K3 vi. 竞争；比赛；对抗 时态: competed, competing, competes (高研四六托宝 2065/2583)","The banks have long compete d with American Express's charge cards and various store cards...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to try to be more successful or better than somebody else who is trying to do the same as you","example":"Several companies are competing for the contract."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take part in a contest or game","example":"We can't compete with them on price."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"Young children will usually compete for their mother's attention."}]],["competitive","/kəmˈpetətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “competitive”.","competitive [kəmˈpetətɪv] -K3 adj. 竞争的；比赛的；求胜心切的 (研四六雅 2307/2363)","欧陆词典释义：competitive [kəmˈpetətɪv] -K3 adj. 竞争的；比赛的；求胜心切的 (研四六雅 2307/2363)","Only by keeping down costs will America maintain its competitive advantage over other countries...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used to describe a situation in which people or organizations compete against each other","example":"competitive games/sports"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"as good as or better than others","example":"Graduates have to fight for jobs in a highly competitive"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"trying very hard to be better than others","example":"a shop selling clothes at competitive prices ("}]],["confirm","/kənˈfɜ:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “confirm”.","confirm [kənˈfɜ:m] -K4 vt. 确认；确定；证实；批准；使巩固 时态: confirmed, confirming, confirms (高研四六托雅宝 1851/1156)","欧陆词典释义：confirm [kənˈfɜ:m] -K4 vt. 确认；确定；证实；批准；使巩固 时态: confirmed, confirming, confirms (高研四六托雅宝 1851/1156)","X-rays have confirm ed that he has not broken any bones...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to state or show that something is definitely true or correct, especially by providing evidence","example":"Rumours of job losses were later confirmed"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody feel or believe something even more strongly","example":"His guilty expression confirmed my suspicions."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make a position, an agreement, etc. more definite or official; to establish somebody/something firmly","example":"Please write to confirm your reservation ("}]],["abuse","/əˈbju:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abuse”.","abuse [əˈbju:s] -K4 n. 滥用；虐待；辱骂；弊端；恶习，陋习 vt. 滥用；虐待；辱骂 n. (Abuse)人名；(英)阿比斯 时态: abused, abusing, abuses (高研四六托雅宝 1540/2352)","欧陆词典释义：abuse [əˈbju:s] -K4 n. 滥用；虐待；辱骂；弊端；恶习，陋习 vt. 滥用；虐待；辱骂 n. (Abuse)人名；(英)阿比斯 时态: abused, abusing, abuses (高研四六托雅宝 1540/2352)","investigation of alleged child abuse .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the use of something in a way that is wrong or harmful","example":"alcohol/drug/solvent abuse"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"unfair, cruel or violent treatment of somebody","example":"The system of paying cash bonuses is open to abuse"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"rude and offensive remarks, usually made when somebody is very angry","example":"He was arrested on charges of corruption and abuse of power"}]],["accumulate","/əˈkju:mjəleɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accumulate”.","accumulate [əˈkju:mjəleɪt] -2 vt. 积攒 vi. 累积；积聚 时态: accumulated, accumulating, accumulates (高研四六托雅宝 5083/4997)","欧陆词典释义：accumulate [əˈkju:mjəleɪt] -2 vt. 积攒 vi. 累积；积聚 时态: accumulated, accumulating, accumulates (高研四六托雅宝 5083/4997)","Households accumulate wealth across a broad spectrum of assets...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to gradually get more and more of something over a period of time","example":"I seem to have accumulated a lot of books."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to gradually increase in number or quantity over a period of time","example":"By investing wisely she accumulated a fortune."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"We have accumulated a great amount of evidence."}]],["adjust","/əˈdʒʌst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adjust”.","adjust [əˈdʒʌst] -K3 vt. 调整，使…适合；校准 vi. 调整，校准；适应 时态: adjusted, adjusting, adjusts (高研四六托雅宝 2300/2811)","欧陆词典释义：adjust [əˈdʒʌst] -K3 vt. 调整，使…适合；校准 vi. 调整，校准；适应 时态: adjusted, adjusting, adjusts (高研四六托雅宝 2300/2811)","We have been preparing our fighters to adjust themselves to civil society...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change something slightly to make it more suitable for a new set of conditions or to make it work better","example":"Watch out for sharp bends and adjust your speed accordingly."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to get used to a new situation by changing the way you behave and/or think","example":"This button is for adjusting the volume."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move something slightly so that it looks neater or feels more comfortable","example":"The brakes need to be adjusted."}]],["administrative","/ədˈmɪnɪstrətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “administrative”.","administrative [ədˈmɪnɪstrətɪv] -2 adj. 管理的，行政的 (托 3510/2448)","欧陆词典释义：administrative [ədˈmɪnɪstrətɪv] -2 adj. 管理的，行政的 (托 3510/2448)","Other industries have had to sack managers to reduce administrative costs...",""],["adopt","/əˈdɒpt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adopt”.","adopt [əˈdɒpt] -K4 vi. 采取；过继 vt. 采取；接受；收养；正式通过 时态: adopted, adopting, adopts (高研四六托雅宝 1632/1157)","欧陆词典释义：adopt [əˈdɒpt] -K4 vi. 采取；过继 vt. 采取；接受；收养；正式通过 时态: adopted, adopting, adopts (高研四六托雅宝 1632/1157)","Parliament adopt ed a resolution calling for the complete withdrawal of troops...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take somebody else’s child into your family and become its legal parent(s)","example":"a campaign to encourage childless couples to adopt"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to start to use a particular method or to show a particular attitude towards somebody/something","example":"to adopt a child"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to formally accept a suggestion or policy by voting","example":"She was forced to have her baby adopted."}]],["advocate","/ˈædvəkeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “advocate”.","advocate [ˈædvəkeɪt] -3 n. 提倡者；支持者；律师 vt. 提倡，主张，拥护 时态: advocated, advocating, advocates (高研四六托雅宝 2623/4031)","欧陆词典释义：advocate [ˈædvəkeɪt] -3 n. 提倡者；支持者；律师 vt. 提倡，主张，拥护 时态: advocated, advocating, advocates (高研四六托雅宝 2623/4031)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “advocate”.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to support something publicly","example":"The group does not advocate the use of violence."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"Heart specialists strongly advocate low-cholesterol diets."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who supports or speaks in favour of somebody or of a public plan or action","example":"These policies have been widely advocated."}]],["aggregate","/ˈægrɪgət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “aggregate”.","aggregate [ˈægrɪgət] -2 n. 合计；集合体；总计 adj. 聚合的；集合的；合计的 vt. 集合；聚集；合计 vi. 集合；聚集；合计 时态: aggregated, aggregating, aggregates (托雅宝 12841/5505)","欧陆词典释义：aggregate [ˈægrɪgət] -2 n. 合计；集合体；总计 adj. 聚合的；集合的；合计的 vt. 集合；聚集；合计 vi. 集合；聚集；合计 时态: aggregated, aggregating, aggregates (托雅宝 12841/5505)","The rate of growth of GNP will depend upon the rate of growth of aggregate demand...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a total number or amount made up of smaller amounts that are collected together","example":"a record aggregate of 285 points"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"sand or broken stone that is used to make concrete or for building roads, etc.","example":"The three smaller parties gained an aggregate of 25 per cent of the vote."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Businesses are, in the aggregate, deeper in debt than ever before."}]],["aggressive","/əˈgresɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “aggressive”.","aggressive [əˈgresɪv] -K3 adj. 侵略性的；好斗的；有进取心的；有闯劲的 (高研四六托雅宝 2514/3648)","欧陆词典释义：aggressive [əˈgresɪv] -K3 adj. 侵略性的；好斗的；有进取心的；有闯劲的 (高研四六托雅宝 2514/3648)","Some children are much more aggressive than others...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"angry, and behaving in a threatening way; ready to attack","example":"He gets aggressive when he's drunk."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"acting with force and determination in order to succeed","example":"a dangerous aggressive dog"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"early 19th cent.","example":"an aggressive advertising campaign"}]],["alter","/ˈɔ:ltə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “alter”.","alter [ˈɔ:ltə(r)] -K3 vt. 改变，更改 vi. 改变；修改 n. (Alter)人名；(英)奥尔特；(德、捷、葡、爱沙、立陶、拉脱、俄、西、罗、瑞典)阿尔特 时态: altered, altering, alters (研四六托雅宝 2889/2121)","欧陆词典释义：alter [ˈɔ:ltə(r)] -K3 vt. 改变，更改 vi. 改变；修改 n. (Alter)人名；(英)奥尔特；(德、捷、葡、爱沙、立陶、拉脱、俄、西、罗、瑞典)阿尔特 时态: altered, altering, alters (研四六托雅宝 2889/2121)","Little had alter ed in the village...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become different; to make somebody/something different","example":"Prices did not alter significantly during 2014."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make changes to a piece of clothing so that it will fit you better","example":"He had altered so much I scarcely recognized him."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"It doesn't alter the way I feel."}]],["appoint","/əˈpɔɪnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “appoint”.","appoint [əˈpɔɪnt] -K3 vt. 任命；指定；约定 vi. 任命；委派 时态: appointed, appointing, appoints (高研四六托宝 3172/1272)","欧陆词典释义：appoint [əˈpɔɪnt] -K3 vt. 任命；指定；约定 vi. 任命；委派 时态: appointed, appointing, appoints (高研四六托宝 3172/1272)","It made sense to appoint a banker to this job...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to choose somebody for a job or position of responsibility","example":"They have appointed a new head teacher at my son's school."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to arrange or decide on a time or place for doing something","example":"She has recently been appointed to the committee."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"They appointed him (as) captain of the English team."}]],["approximate","/əˈprɒksɪmət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “approximate”.","approximate [əˈprɒksɪmət] -K2 adj. [数] 近似的；大概的 vt. 近似；使…接近；粗略估计 vi. 接近于；近似于 时态: approximated, approximating, approximates (研四六托雅宝 11835/9895)","欧陆词典释义：approximate [əˈprɒksɪmət] -K2 adj. [数] 近似的；大概的 vt. 近似；使…接近；粗略估计 vi. 接近于；近似于 时态: approximated, approximating, approximates (研四六托雅宝 11835/9895)","The approximate cost varies from around £150 to £250...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"almost correct or accurate, but not completely so","example":"an approximate number/total/cost"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The cost given is only approximate."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be similar or close to something in nature, quality, amount, etc., but not exactly the same","example":"Use these figures as an approximate guide in your calculations."}]],["argue","/ˈɑ:gju:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “argue”.","argue [ˈɑ:gju:] -K4 vi. 争论，辩论；提出理由 vt. 辩论，争论；证明；说服 n. (Argue)人名；(英、法)阿格 时态: argued, arguing, argues (高研四六雅 778/674)","欧陆词典释义：argue [ˈɑ:gju:] -K4 vi. 争论，辩论；提出理由 vt. 辩论，争论；证明；说服 n. (Argue)人名；(英、法)阿格 时态: argued, arguing, argues (高研四六雅 778/674)","The committee is concerned about players' behaviour, especially arguing with referees...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to speak angrily to somebody because you disagree with them","example":"My brothers are always arguing."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give reasons why you think that something is right/wrong, true/not true, etc., especially to persuade people that you are right","example":"He's offering to pay so who am I to argue?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show clearly that something exists or is true","example":"We're always arguing with each other about money."}]],["arrange","/əˈreɪndʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “arrange”.","arrange [əˈreɪndʒ] -K4 vi. 安排；排列；协商 vt. 安排；排列；整理 时态: arranged, arranging, arranges (高研四托 2216/1324)","欧陆词典释义：arrange [əˈreɪndʒ] -K4 vi. 安排；排列；协商 vt. 安排；排列；整理 时态: arranged, arranging, arranges (高研四托 2216/1324)","She arrange d an appointment for Friday afternoon at four-fifteen...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to plan or organize something in advance","example":"The party was arranged quickly."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to put something in a particular order; to make something neat or attractive","example":"She arranged a loan with the bank."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to write or change a piece of music so that it is suitable for a particular instrument or voice","example":"Can I arrange an appointment for Monday?"}]],["assign","/əˈsaɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assign”.","assign [əˈsaɪn] -2 vt. 分配；指派；[计][数] 赋值 vi. 将财产过户（尤指过户给债权人） 时态: assigned, assigning, assigns (研四六托雅 2611/3876)","欧陆词典释义：assign [əˈsaɪn] -2 vt. 分配；指派；[计][数] 赋值 vi. 将财产过户（尤指过户给债权人） 时态: assigned, assigning, assigns (研四六托雅 2611/3876)","When I taught, I would assign a topic to children which they would write about...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give somebody something that they can use, or some work or responsibility","example":"The two large classrooms have been assigned to us."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to provide a person for a particular task or position","example":"The teacher assigned a different task to each of the children."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to send a person to work under the authority of somebody or in a particular group","example":"We have been assigned the two large classrooms."}]],["assure","/əˈʃʊə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assure”.","assure [əˈʃʊə(r)] -K2 vt. 保证；担保；使确信；弄清楚 时态: assured, assuring, assures (研四六托雅宝 2571/2640)","欧陆词典释义：assure [əˈʃʊə(r)] -K2 vt. 保证；担保；使确信；弄清楚 时态: assured, assuring, assures (研四六托雅宝 2571/2640)","He hastened to assure me that there was nothing traumatic to report...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to tell somebody that something is definitely true or is definitely going to happen, especially when they have doubts about it","example":"You think I did it deliberately, but I assure you (that) I did not."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make yourself certain about something","example":"We were assured that everything possible was being done."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something certain to happen","example":"She's perfectly safe, I can assure you"}]],["attend","/əˈtend/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attend”.","attend [əˈtend] -K4 vi. 出席；致力于；照料；照顾 vt. 出席；上（大学等）；照料；招待；陪伴 时态: attended, attending, attends (高研四托雅 1168/1100)","欧陆词典释义：attend [əˈtend] -K4 vi. 出席；致力于；照料；照顾 vt. 出席；上（大学等）；照料；招待；陪伴 时态: attended, attending, attends (高研四托雅 1168/1100)","Thousands of people attend ed the funeral...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be present at an event","example":"We'd like as many people as possible to attend."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to go regularly to a place","example":"The meeting was attended by 90% of shareholders."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to pay attention to what somebody is saying or to what you are doing","example":"to attend a wedding/funeral"}]],["attribute","/əˈtrɪbju:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attribute”.","attribute [əˈtrɪbju:t] -2 n. 属性；特质 vt. 归属；把…归于 时态: attributed, attributing, attributes (研四六托雅宝 3346/3247)","欧陆词典释义：attribute [əˈtrɪbju:t] -2 n. 属性；特质 vt. 归属；把…归于 时态: attributed, attributing, attributes (研四六托雅宝 3346/3247)","Women tend to attribute their success to external causes such as luck.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to say or believe that something is the result of a particular thing","example":"She attributes her success to hard work and a little luck."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to say or believe that somebody is responsible for doing something, especially for saying, writing or painting something","example":"The committee refused to attribute blame"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"This play is usually attributed to Shakespeare."}]],["behave","/bɪˈheɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “behave”.","behave [bɪˈheɪv] -K3 vi. 表现；（机器等）运转；举止端正；（事物）起某种作用 vt. 使守规矩；使表现得… 时态: behaved, behaving, behaves (高研四六托雅 3660/2463)","欧陆词典释义：behave [bɪˈheɪv] -K3 vi. 表现；（机器等）运转；举止端正；（事物）起某种作用 vt. 使守规矩；使表现得… 时态: behaved, behaving, behaves (高研四六托雅 3660/2463)","I couldn't believe these people were behaving in this way...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to do things in a particular way","example":"The doctor behaved very unprofessionally."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to do things in a way that people think is correct or polite","example":"They behaved very badly towards their guests."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"behaving in the way mentioned","example":"He behaved like a true gentleman."}]],["capable","/ˈkeɪpəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “capable”.","capable [ˈkeɪpəbl] -K3 adj. 能干的，能胜任的；有才华的 (研四六托 2392/1848)","欧陆词典释义：capable [ˈkeɪpəbl] -K3 adj. 能干的，能胜任的；有才华的 (研四六托 2392/1848)","He appeared hardly capable of conducting a coherent conversation...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having the ability or qualities necessary for doing something","example":"You are capable of better work than this."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having the ability to do things well","example":"He's quite capable of lying to get out of trouble."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"mid 16th cent.","example":"I'm perfectly capable of doing it myself, thank you."}]],["clarify","/ˈklærəfaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “clarify”.","clarify [ˈklærəfaɪ] -2 vt. 澄清；阐明 vi. 得到澄清；变得明晰；得到净化 时态: clarified, clarifying, clarifies (高研四六托雅宝 5050/4552)","欧陆词典释义：clarify [ˈklærəfaɪ] -2 vt. 澄清；阐明 vi. 得到澄清；变得明晰；得到净化 时态: clarified, clarifying, clarifies (高研四六托雅宝 5050/4552)","Thank you for writing and allowing me to clarify the present position...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something clearer or easier to understand","example":"to clarify a situation/problem/issue"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something, especially butter, pure by heating it","example":"I hope this clarifies my position"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"The law on drugs needs to be clarified."}]],["classify","/ˈklæsɪfaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “classify”.","classify [ˈklæsɪfaɪ] -2 vt. 分类；分等 时态: classified, classifying, classifies (高研四六托雅宝 4515/4168)","欧陆词典释义：classify [ˈklæsɪfaɪ] -2 vt. 分类；分等 时态: classified, classifying, classifies (高研四六托雅宝 4515/4168)","It is necessary initially to classify the headaches into certain types...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to arrange something in groups according to features that they have in common","example":"The books in the library are classified according to"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to decide which type or group somebody/something belongs to","example":"Patients are classified into"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 18th cent.","example":"All rural settlements were classified according to their size."}]],["combine","/kəmˈbaɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “combine”.","combine [kəmˈbaɪn] -K3 n. 联合收割机；联合企业 vt. 使化合；使联合，使结合 vi. 联合，结合；化合 时态: combined, combining, combines (高研四六托雅 1448/1581)","欧陆词典释义：combine [kəmˈbaɪn] -K3 n. 联合收割机；联合企业 vt. 使化合；使联合，使结合 vi. 联合，结合；化合 时态: combined, combining, combines (高研四六托雅 1448/1581)","The Church has something to say on how to combine freedom with responsibility...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to come together to form a single thing or group; to join two or more things or groups together to form a single one","example":"Hydrogen and oxygen combine to form water."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to have two or more different features or characteristics; to put two or more different things, features or qualities together","example":"Hydrogen combines with oxygen to form water."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to do two or more things at the same time","example":"Several factors had combined to ruin our plans."}]],["consist","/kənˈsɪst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consist”.","consist [kənˈsɪst] -3 vi. 由…组成；在于；符合 时态: consisted, consisting, consists (高研四六托雅 2190/1493)","欧陆词典释义：consist [kənˈsɪst] -3 vi. 由…组成；在于；符合 时态: consisted, consisting, consists (高研四六托雅 2190/1493)","Breakfast consist ed of porridge served with butter.",""],["constant","/ˈkɒnstənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “constant”.","constant [ˈkɒnstənt] -K4 n. [数] 常数；恒量 adj. 不变的；恒定的；经常的 n. (Constant)人名；(德)康斯坦特 (高研四六托雅宝 2386/1915)","欧陆词典释义：constant [ˈkɒnstənt] -K4 n. [数] 常数；恒量 adj. 不变的；恒定的；经常的 n. (Constant)人名；(德)康斯坦特 (高研四六托雅宝 2386/1915)","She suggests that women are under constant pressure to be abnormally thin...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"happening all the time or repeatedly","example":"constant interruptions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"that does not change","example":"a constant stream of visitors all day"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Babies need constant attention."}]],["construct","/kənˈstrʌkt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “construct”.","construct [kənˈstrʌkt] -K3 n. 构想，概念 vt. 建造，构造；创立 时态: constructed, constructing, constructs (高研四六托宝 2477/2058)","欧陆词典释义：construct [kənˈstrʌkt] -K3 n. 构想，概念 vt. 建造，构造；创立 时态: constructed, constructing, constructs (高研四六托宝 2477/2058)","The French construct ed a series of fortresses from Dunkirk on the Channel coast to Douai...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to build or make something such as a road, building or machine","example":"When was the bridge constructed?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to form something by putting different things together","example":"They constructed a shelter out of fallen branches."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to draw a line or shape according to the rules of mathematics","example":"a house built of stone"}]],["consult","/kənˈsʌlt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consult”.","consult [kənˈsʌlt] -K3 vi. 请教；商议；当顾问 vt. 查阅；商量；向…请教 时态: consulted, consulting, consults (高研四六托雅 3591/2826)","欧陆词典释义：consult [kənˈsʌlt] -K3 vi. 请教；商议；当顾问 vt. 查阅；商量；向…请教 时态: consulted, consulting, consults (高研四六托雅 3591/2826)","Consult your doctor about how much exercise you should attempt...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to go to somebody for information or advice","example":"If the pain continues, consult your doctor."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to discuss something with somebody to get their permission for something, or to help you make a decision","example":"Have you consulted your lawyer about this?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to look in or at something to get information","example":"a consulting engineer ("}]],["consume","/kənˈsju:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consume”.","consume [kənˈsju:m] -2 vt. 消耗，消费；使…着迷；挥霍 vi. 耗尽，毁灭；耗尽生命 时态: consumed, consuming, consumes (高研四六托 3006/3627)","欧陆词典释义：consume [kənˈsju:m] -2 vt. 消耗，消费；使…着迷；挥霍 vi. 耗尽，毁灭；耗尽生命 时态: consumed, consuming, consumes (高研四六托 3006/3627)","Many people experienced a drop in their cholesterol levels when they consume d oat bran.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to use something, especially fuel, energy or time","example":"The electricity industry consumes large amounts of fossil fuels."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to eat or drink something","example":"25 per cent of the world’s population consumes 80 per cent of the planet’s resources."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to fill somebody with a strong feeling","example":"Before he died he had consumed a large quantity of alcohol."}]],["absolute","/ˈæbsəlu:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “absolute”.","absolute [ˈæbsəlu:t] -K3 n. 绝对；绝对事物 adj. 绝对的；完全的；专制的 (高研四六托宝 3165/2420)","欧陆词典释义：absolute [ˈæbsəlu:t] -K3 n. 绝对；绝对事物 adj. 绝对的；完全的；专制的 (高研四六托宝 3165/2420)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"total and complete","example":"a class for absolute beginners"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used, especially in spoken English, to give emphasis to what you are saying","example":"absolute confidence/trust/silence/truth"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"definite and without any doubt or confusion","example":"‘You're wrong,’ she said with absolute certainty."}]],["absorb","/əbˈsɔ:b/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “absorb”.","absorb [əbˈsɔ:b] -K2 vt. 吸收；吸引；承受；理解；使…全神贯注 时态: absorbed, absorbing, absorbs (高研四六托雅宝 3120/2879)","欧陆词典释义：absorb [əbˈsɔ:b] -K2 vt. 吸收；吸引；承受；理解；使…全神贯注 时态: absorbed, absorbing, absorbs (高研四六托雅宝 3120/2879)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take in a liquid, gas or other substance from the surface or space around","example":"Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the air."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something smaller become part of something larger","example":"Let the rice cook until it has absorbed all the water."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take something into the mind and learn or understand it","example":"The cream is easily absorbed into the skin."}]],["abstract","/ˈæbstrækt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abstract”.","abstract [ˈæbstrækt] -2 n. 摘要；抽象；抽象的概念 adj. 抽象的；深奥的 vt. 摘要；提取；使……抽象化；转移(注意力、兴趣等)；使心不在焉 vi. 做摘要；写梗概 时态: abstracted, abstracting, abstracts (高研四六托雅宝 4007/3729)","欧陆词典释义：abstract [ˈæbstrækt] -2 n. 摘要；抽象；抽象的概念 adj. 抽象的；深奥的 vt. 摘要；提取；使……抽象化；转移(注意力、兴趣等)；使心不在焉 vi. 做摘要；写梗概 时态: abstracted, abstracting, abstracts (高研四六托雅宝 4007/3729)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"based on general ideas and not on any particular real person, thing or situation","example":"abstract knowledge/principles"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"existing in thought or as an idea but not having a physical reality","example":"The research shows that pre-school children are capable of thinking in abstract terms."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"not representing people or things in a realistic way, but expressing the artist’s ideas about them","example":"We may talk of beautiful things but beauty itself is abstract."}]],["abundant","/əˈbʌndənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abundant”.","abundant [əˈbʌndənt] -1 adj. 丰富的；充裕的；盛产 (高研四托宝 6223/7823)","欧陆词典释义：abundant [əˈbʌndənt] -1 adj. 丰富的；充裕的；盛产 (高研四托宝 6223/7823)",null,""],["accomplish","/əˈkʌmplɪʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accomplish”.","accomplish [əˈkʌmplɪʃ] -2 vt. 完成；实现；达到 时态: accomplished, accomplishing, accomplishes (高研四托雅宝 2345/5546)","欧陆词典释义：accomplish [əˈkʌmplɪʃ] -2 vt. 完成；实现；达到 时态: accomplished, accomplishing, accomplishes (高研四托雅宝 2345/5546)",null,""],["accurate","/ˈækjərət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accurate”.","accurate [ˈækjərət] -K3 adj. 精确的 (研四六托雅宝 2728/2738)","欧陆词典释义：accurate [ˈækjərət] -K3 adj. 精确的 (研四六托雅宝 2728/2738)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"correct and true in every detail","example":"an accurate description/account/calculation"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"able to give completely correct information or to do something in an exact way","example":"accurate information/data"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"an accurate","example":"Accurate records must be kept."}]],["acknowledge","/əkˈnɒlɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “acknowledge”.","acknowledge [əkˈnɒlɪdʒ] -K3 vt. 承认；答谢；报偿；告知已收到 时态: acknowledged, acknowledging, acknowledges (高研四六托雅宝 1654/2105)","欧陆词典释义：acknowledge [əkˈnɒlɪdʒ] -K3 vt. 承认；答谢；报偿；告知已收到 时态: acknowledged, acknowledging, acknowledges (高研四六托雅宝 1654/2105)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to accept that something is true","example":"She refuses to acknowledge the need for reform."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to accept that somebody/something has a particular authority or status","example":"Are you prepared to acknowledge your responsibility?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to tell somebody that you have received something that they sent to you","example":"a generally acknowledged fact"}]],["adjacent","/əˈdʒeɪsnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adjacent”.","adjacent [əˈdʒeɪsnt] -1 adj. 邻近的，毗连的 (研六托雅宝 6649/5391)","欧陆词典释义：adjacent [əˈdʒeɪsnt] -1 adj. 邻近的，毗连的 (研六托雅宝 6649/5391)",null,""],["administer","/ədˈmɪnɪstə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “administer”.","administer [ədˈmɪnɪstə(r)] -2 vt. 管理；执行；给予 vi. 给予帮助；执行遗产管理人的职责；担当管理人 时态: administered, administering, administers (研托雅 3661/3700)","欧陆词典释义：administer [ədˈmɪnɪstə(r)] -2 vt. 管理；执行；给予 vi. 给予帮助；执行遗产管理人的职责；担当管理人 时态: administered, administering, administers (研托雅 3661/3700)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to manage and organize the affairs of a company, an organization, a country, etc.","example":"to administer a charity/fund/school"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make sure that something is done fairly and in the correct way","example":"the high cost of administering medical services"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give or to provide something, especially in a formal way","example":"The pension funds are administered by commercial banks."}]],["adverse","/ˈædvɜ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adverse”.","adverse [ˈædvɜ:s] -2 adj. 不利的；相反的；敌对的（名词adverseness，副词adversely） (研六托雅宝 6307/5120)","欧陆词典释义：adverse [ˈædvɜ:s] -2 adj. 不利的；相反的；敌对的（名词adverseness，副词adversely） (研六托雅宝 6307/5120)",null,""],["affordable","/ə'fɔ:dəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “affordable”.","affordable [ə'fɔ:dəbl] -1 adj. 负担得起的 (托宝 5234/10203)","欧陆词典释义：affordable [ə'fɔ:dəbl] -1 adj. 负担得起的 (托宝 5234/10203)",null,""],["agricultural","/ˌæɡrɪ'kʌltʃərəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “agricultural”.","agricultural [ˌæɡrɪ'kʌltʃərəl] -3 adj. 农业的；农艺的 (高 3104/2188)","欧陆词典释义：agricultural [ˌæɡrɪ'kʌltʃərəl] -3 adj. 农业的；农艺的 (高 3104/2188)",null,""],["allocate","/ˈæləkeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “allocate”.","allocate [ˈæləkeɪt] -2 vt. 分配；拨出；使坐落于 vi. 分配；指定 时态: allocated, allocating, allocates (高研六托雅宝 6763/3035)","欧陆词典释义：allocate [ˈæləkeɪt] -2 vt. 分配；拨出；使坐落于 vi. 分配；指定 时态: allocated, allocating, allocates (高研六托雅宝 6763/3035)",null,""],["ambiguous","/æmˈbɪgjuəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ambiguous”.","ambiguous [æmˈbɪgjuəs] -2 adj. 模糊不清的；引起歧义的 (高研六托雅宝 7071/6442)","欧陆词典释义：ambiguous [æmˈbɪgjuəs] -2 adj. 模糊不清的；引起歧义的 (高研六托雅宝 7071/6442)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that can be understood in more than one way; having different meanings","example":"an ambiguous word/term/statement"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not clearly stated or defined","example":"Her account was deliberately ambiguous."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"early 16th cent.","example":"His role has always been ambiguous."}]],["amend","/əˈmend/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “amend”.","amend [əˈmend] -2 vt. 修改；改善，改进 vi. 改正，改善；改过自新 n. (Amend)人名；(德、英)阿门德 时态: amended, amending, amends (研托雅宝 7371/4585)","欧陆词典释义：amend [əˈmend] -2 vt. 修改；改善，改进 vi. 改正，改善；改过自新 n. (Amend)人名；(德、英)阿门德 时态: amended, amending, amends (研托雅宝 7371/4585)",null,""],["analytical","/ˌænəˈlɪtɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “analytical”.","analytical [ˌænəˈlɪtɪkl] -1 adj. 分析的；解析的；善于分析的 原型: analytic (六雅 7338/6653)","欧陆词典释义：analytical [ˌænəˈlɪtɪkl] -1 adj. 分析的；解析的；善于分析的 原型: analytic (六雅 7338/6653)",null,""],["anniversary","/ˌænɪˈvɜ:səri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “anniversary”.","anniversary [ˌænɪˈvɜ:səri] -K3 n. 周年纪念日 (高研六雅 3374/3440)","欧陆词典释义：anniversary [ˌænɪˈvɜ:səri] -K3 n. 周年纪念日 (高研六雅 3374/3440)",null,""],["anticipate","/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “anticipate”.","anticipate [ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt] -K2 vt. 预期，期望；占先，抢先；提前使用 时态: anticipated, anticipating, anticipates (研四六托雅宝 3187/3106)","欧陆词典释义：anticipate [ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt] -K2 vt. 预期，期望；占先，抢先；提前使用 时态: anticipated, anticipating, anticipates (研四六托雅宝 3187/3106)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to expect something","example":"We don't anticipate any major problems."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to see what might happen in the future and take action to prepare for it","example":"Our anticipated arrival time is 8.30."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think with pleasure and excitement about something that is going to happen","example":"The eagerly anticipated movie will be released next month."}]],["anxious","/ˈæŋkʃəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “anxious”.","anxious [ˈæŋkʃəs] -K3 adj. 焦虑的；担忧的；渴望的；急切的 (高研四六托 3827/2630)","欧陆词典释义：anxious [ˈæŋkʃəs] -K3 adj. 焦虑的；担忧的；渴望的；急切的 (高研四六托 3827/2630)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"feeling worried or nervous","example":"He seemed anxious about the meeting."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"causing anxiety; showing anxiety","example":"Parents are naturally anxious for their children."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"wanting something very much","example":"a very nervous girl"}]],["appliance","/əˈplaɪəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “appliance”.","appliance [əˈplaɪəns] -2 n. 器具；器械；装置 (研四六托雅 6043/7150)","欧陆词典释义：appliance [əˈplaɪəns] -2 n. 器具；器械；装置 (研四六托雅 6043/7150)",null,""],["appreciate","/əˈpri:ʃieɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “appreciate”.","appreciate [əˈpri:ʃieɪt] -K3 vi. 增值；涨价 vt. 欣赏；感激；领会；鉴别 时态: appreciated, appreciating, appreciates (高研四六托雅宝 1738/1989)","欧陆词典释义：appreciate [əˈpri:ʃieɪt] -K3 vi. 增值；涨价 vt. 欣赏；感激；领会；鉴别 时态: appreciated, appreciating, appreciates (高研四六托雅宝 1738/1989)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to recognize the good qualities of somebody/something","example":"You can't really appreciate foreign literature in translation."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be grateful for something that somebody has done; to welcome something","example":"His talents are not fully appreciated"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to understand that something is true","example":"Her family doesn't appreciate her."}]],["arbitrary","/ˈɑ:bɪtrəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “arbitrary”.","arbitrary [ˈɑ:bɪtrəri] -1 adj. [数] 任意的；武断的；专制的 (高研四六托雅宝 7545/5353)","欧陆词典释义：arbitrary [ˈɑ:bɪtrəri] -1 adj. [数] 任意的；武断的；专制的 (高研四六托雅宝 7545/5353)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not seeming to be based on a reason, system or plan and sometimes seeming unfair","example":"The choice of players for the team seemed completely arbitrary."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"using power without restriction and without considering other people","example":"He makes unpredictable, arbitrary decisions."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"the arbitrary powers of officials"}]],["architect","/ˈɑ:kɪtekt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “architect”.","architect [ˈɑ:kɪtekt] -2 n. 建筑师 缔造者 (高研四六托雅宝 3365/2891)","欧陆词典释义：architect [ˈɑ:kɪtekt] -2 n. 建筑师 缔造者 (高研四六托雅宝 3365/2891)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person whose job is designing buildings","example":"He was one of the principal architects of the revolution."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who is responsible for planning or creating an idea, an event or a situation","example":"Jones was the architect of the team's first goal."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 16th cent.","example":"The house was designed by architect Louis Kahn."}]],["assert","/əˈsɜ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assert”.","assert [əˈsɜ:t] -2 vt. 维护，坚持；断言；主张；声称 时态: asserted, asserting, asserts (研六托雅宝 3147/3438)","欧陆词典释义：assert [əˈsɜ:t] -2 vt. 维护，坚持；断言；主张；声称 时态: asserted, asserting, asserts (研六托雅宝 3147/3438)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to state clearly and firmly that something is true","example":"She continued to assert that she was innocent."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to behave in a confident and determined way so that other people pay attention to your opinions","example":"She continued to assert her innocence."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make other people recognize your right or authority to do something, by behaving firmly and confidently","example":"The German Chancellor was anxious to assert his government’s commitment to further European unity."}]],["associate","/əˈsəʊʃieɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “associate”.","associate [əˈsəʊʃieɪt] -K3 n. 同事，伙伴；关联的事物 adj. 副的；联合的 vt. 联想；使联合；使发生联系 vi. 交往；结交 时态: associated, associating, associates (高研四六托雅宝 1354/1216)","欧陆词典释义：associate [əˈsəʊʃieɪt] -K3 n. 同事，伙伴；关联的事物 adj. 副的；联合的 vt. 联想；使联合；使发生联系 vi. 交往；结交 时态: associated, associating, associates (高研四六托雅宝 1354/1216)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make a connection between people or things in your mind","example":"I always associate the smell of baking with my childhood."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"to spend time with somebody, especially a person or people that somebody else does not approve of","example":"He is closely associated in the public mind with horror movies."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to show that you support or agree with something","example":"Most people immediately associate addictions with drugs, alcohol and cigarettes."}]],["attain","/əˈteɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attain”.","attain [əˈteɪn] -1 n. 成就 vt. 达到，实现；获得；到达 vi. 达到；获得；到达 时态: attained, attaining, attains (高研四六托雅宝 5323/5042)","欧陆词典释义：attain [əˈteɪn] -1 n. 成就 vt. 达到，实现；获得；到达 vi. 达到；获得；到达 时态: attained, attaining, attains (高研四六托雅宝 5323/5042)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to succeed in getting something, usually after a lot of effort","example":"Most of our students attained five ‘A’ grades in their exams."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to reach a particular age, level or condition","example":"We only consider applicants who have attained a high level of academic achievement."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"attain (a) degree/standard/level/proficiency/mastery"}]],["beneficial","/ˌbenɪˈfɪʃl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “beneficial”.","beneficial [ˌbenɪˈfɪʃl] -2 adj. 有益的，有利的；可享利益的 (高研四托雅 4991/4578)","欧陆词典释义：beneficial [ˌbenɪˈfɪʃl] -2 adj. 有益的，有利的；可享利益的 (高研四托雅 4991/4578)",null,""],["billion","/ˈbɪljən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “billion”.","billion [ˈbɪljən] -5 num. 十亿 n. 十亿；大量 adj. 十亿的 n. (Billion)人名；(法)比利翁 (高研四六托 612/1829)","欧陆词典释义：billion [ˈbɪljən] -5 num. 十亿 n. 十亿；大量 adj. 十亿的 n. (Billion)人名；(法)比利翁 (高研四六托 612/1829)",null,[{"pos":"number","definition":"1 000 000 000; one thousand million","example":"Worldwide sales reached 2.5 billion."},{"pos":"number","definition":"a very large amount","example":"half a billion dollars"},{"pos":"number","definition":"1 000 000 000 000; one million million","example":"They have spent billions on the problem ("}]],["bureaucratic","/ˌbjʊərəˈkrætɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bureaucratic”.","bureaucratic [ˌbjʊərəˈkrætɪk] adj. 官僚的；官僚政治的 (高 6447/6084)","欧陆词典释义：bureaucratic [ˌbjʊərəˈkrætɪk] adj. 官僚的；官僚政治的 (高 6447/6084)",null,""],["capability","/ˌkeɪpəˈbɪləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “capability”.","capability [ˌkeɪpəˈbɪləti] -2 n. 才能，能力；性能，容量 (六托 2958/3838)","欧陆词典释义：capability [ˌkeɪpəˈbɪləti] -2 n. 才能，能力；性能，容量 (六托 2958/3838)",null,""],["cease","/si:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cease”.","cease [si:s] -K3 n. 停止 vi. 停止；终了 vt. 停止；结束 时态: ceased, ceasing, ceases (研四六托雅 4470/2679)","欧陆词典释义：cease [si:s] -K3 n. 停止 vi. 停止；终了 vt. 停止；结束 时态: ceased, ceasing, ceases (研四六托雅 4470/2679)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to stop happening or existing; to stop something from happening or existing","example":"Welfare payments cease as soon as an individual starts a job."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"You never cease to amaze me!"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a phrase used to express surprise and pleasure at something","example":"They voted to cease strike action immediately."}]],["cognitive","/ˈkɒgnətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cognitive”.","cognitive [ˈkɒgnətɪv] -1 adj. 认知的，认识的 (研六托雅 3344/5220)","欧陆词典释义：cognitive [ˈkɒgnətɪv] -1 adj. 认知的，认识的 (研六托雅 3344/5220)",null,""],["commence","/kəˈmens/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “commence”.","commence [kəˈmens] -1 v. 开始；着手；&lt;英&gt;获得学位 时态: commenced, commencing, commences (研六托雅宝 9454/4318)","欧陆词典释义：commence [kəˈmens] -1 v. 开始；着手；&lt;英&gt;获得学位 时态: commenced, commencing, commences (研六托雅宝 9454/4318)",null,""],["commodity","/kəˈmɒdəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “commodity”.","commodity [kəˈmɒdəti] -2 n. 商品，货物；日用品 (研六托雅宝 4581/4365)","欧陆词典释义：commodity [kəˈmɒdəti] -2 n. 商品，货物；日用品 (研六托雅宝 4581/4365)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a product or a raw material that can be bought and sold","example":"rice, flour and other basic commodities"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that is useful or has a useful quality","example":"a drop in commodity prices"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Crude oil is the world's most important commodity."}]],["compel","/kəmˈpel/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compel”.","compel [kəmˈpel] -2 vt. 强迫，迫使；强使发生 n. (Compel)人名；(法)孔佩尔 时态: compelled, compelling, compels (研四六托雅宝 4449/4965)","欧陆词典释义：compel [kəmˈpel] -2 vt. 强迫，迫使；强使发生 n. (Compel)人名；(法)孔佩尔 时态: compelled, compelling, compels (研四六托雅宝 4449/4965)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to force somebody to do something; to make something necessary","example":"The law can compel fathers to make regular payments for their children."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to cause a particular reaction","example":"I feel compelled to"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The court has powers to compel witnesses to attend."}]],["compensation","/ˌkɒmpenˈseɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compensation”.","compensation [ˌkɒmpenˈseɪʃn] -3 n. 补偿；报酬；赔偿金 (研六托雅 3796/2611)","欧陆词典释义：compensation [ˌkɒmpenˈseɪʃn] -3 n. 补偿；报酬；赔偿金 (研六托雅 3796/2611)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something, especially money, that somebody gives you because they have hurt you, or damaged something that you own; the act of giving this to somebody","example":"to claim/award/receive compensation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"things that make a bad situation better","example":"to pay compensation for injuries at work"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"to receive £10 000 in compensation"}]],["complement","/ˈkɒmplɪment/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “complement”.","complement [ˈkɒmplɪment] -2 n. 补语；余角；补足物 vt. 补足，补助 时态: complemented, complementing, complements (研六托雅 6760/5703)","欧陆词典释义：complement [ˈkɒmplɪment] -2 n. 补语；余角；补足物 vt. 补足，补助 时态: complemented, complementing, complements (研六托雅 6760/5703)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to add to something in a way that improves it or makes it more attractive","example":"The excellent menu is complemented by a good wine list."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The team needs players who complement each other"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that adds new qualities to something in a way that improves it or makes it more attractive","example":"The dishes on the menu complement each other perfectly."}]],["comprise","/kəmˈpraɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “comprise”.","comprise [kəmˈpraɪz] -2 vt. 包含；由…组成 时态: comprised, comprising, comprises (研四六托雅 4392/2504)","欧陆词典释义：comprise [kəmˈpraɪz] -2 vt. 包含；由…组成 时态: comprised, comprising, comprises (研四六托雅 4392/2504)",null,[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have somebody/something as parts or members","example":"The collection comprises 327 paintings."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be the parts or members that form something","example":"The committee is comprised of representatives from both the public and private sectors."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Older people comprise a large proportion of those living in poverty."}]]],"pro":[["ambiguous","/æmˈbɪgjuəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ambiguous”.","ambiguous [æmˈbɪgjuəs] -2 adj. 模糊不清的；引起歧义的 (高研六托雅宝 7071/6442)","欧陆词典释义：ambiguous [æmˈbɪgjuəs] -2 adj. 模糊不清的；引起歧义的 (高研六托雅宝 7071/6442)","This agreement is very ambiguous and open to various interpretations...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that can be understood in more than one way; having different meanings","example":"an ambiguous word/term/statement"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not clearly stated or defined","example":"Her account was deliberately ambiguous."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"early 16th cent.","example":"His role has always been ambiguous."}]],["anticipate","/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “anticipate”.","anticipate [ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt] -K2 vt. 预期，期望；占先，抢先；提前使用 时态: anticipated, anticipating, anticipates (研四六托雅宝 3187/3106)","欧陆词典释义：anticipate [ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt] -K2 vt. 预期，期望；占先，抢先；提前使用 时态: anticipated, anticipating, anticipates (研四六托雅宝 3187/3106)","At the time we couldn't have anticipate d the result of our campaigning...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to expect something","example":"We don't anticipate any major problems."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to see what might happen in the future and take action to prepare for it","example":"Our anticipated arrival time is 8.30."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think with pleasure and excitement about something that is going to happen","example":"The eagerly anticipated movie will be released next month."}]],["arbitrary","/ˈɑ:bɪtrəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “arbitrary”.","arbitrary [ˈɑ:bɪtrəri] -1 adj. [数] 任意的；武断的；专制的 (高研四六托雅宝 7545/5353)","欧陆词典释义：arbitrary [ˈɑ:bɪtrəri] -1 adj. [数] 任意的；武断的；专制的 (高研四六托雅宝 7545/5353)","Arbitrary arrests and detention without trial were common.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not seeming to be based on a reason, system or plan and sometimes seeming unfair","example":"The choice of players for the team seemed completely arbitrary."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"using power without restriction and without considering other people","example":"He makes unpredictable, arbitrary decisions."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"the arbitrary powers of officials"}]],["coherent","/kəʊˈhɪərənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coherent”.","coherent [kəʊˈhɪərənt] -1 adj. 连贯的，一致的；明了的；清晰的；凝聚性的；互相耦合的；粘在一起的 (研六托雅宝 7004/5289)","欧陆词典释义：coherent [kəʊˈhɪərənt] -1 adj. 连贯的，一致的；明了的；清晰的；凝聚性的；互相耦合的；粘在一起的 (研六托雅宝 7004/5289)","He has failed to work out a coherent strategy for modernising the service...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"logical and well organized; easy to understand and clear","example":"a coherent narrative/account/explanation"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"able to talk and express yourself clearly","example":"a coherent policy for the transport system"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"mid 16th cent.","example":"She only became coherent again two hours after the attack."}]],["contemporary","/kənˈtemprəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contemporary”.","contemporary [kənˈtemprəri] -K3 n. 同时代的人；同时期的东西 adj. 当代的；同时代的；属于同一时期的 (高研四六托雅 1947/2068)","欧陆词典释义：contemporary [kənˈtemprəri] -K3 n. 同时代的人；同时期的东西 adj. 当代的；同时代的；属于同一时期的 (高研四六托雅 1947/2068)","She writes a lot of contemporary music for people like Whitney Houston...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"belonging to the same time","example":"We have no contemporary account of the battle ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"belonging to the present time","example":"He was contemporary with the dramatist Congreve."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"life in contemporary Britain"}]],["controversial","/ˌkɒntrəˈvɜ:ʃl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “controversial”.","controversial [ˌkɒntrəˈvɜ:ʃl] -3 adj. 有争议的；有争论的 (高研六托雅宝 3090/3444)","欧陆词典释义：controversial [ˌkɒntrəˈvɜ:ʃl] -3 adj. 有争议的；有争论的 (高研六托雅宝 3090/3444)","Immigration is a controversial issue in many countries...",""],["crucial","/ˈkru:ʃl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “crucial”.","crucial [ˈkru:ʃl] -K3 adj. 重要的；决定性的；定局的；决断的 (研四六托雅宝 2397/2013)","欧陆词典释义：crucial [ˈkru:ʃl] -K3 adj. 重要的；决定性的；定局的；决断的 (研四六托雅宝 2397/2013)","He had administrators under him but took the crucial decisions himself...",""],["cumulative","/ˈkju:mjələtɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cumulative”.","cumulative [ˈkju:mjələtɪv] -1 adj. 累积的 (六雅 8447/7270)","欧陆词典释义：cumulative [ˈkju:mjələtɪv] -1 adj. 累积的 (六雅 8447/7270)","It is simple pleasures, such as a walk on a sunny day, which have a cumulative effect on our mood...",""],["derive","/dɪˈraɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “derive”.","derive [dɪˈraɪv] -K2 vt. 源于；得自；获得 vi. 起源 n. (Derive)人名；(法)德里夫 时态: derived, deriving, derives (研四六托雅 3051/1798)","欧陆词典释义：derive [dɪˈraɪv] -K2 vt. 源于；得自；获得 vi. 起源 n. (Derive)人名；(法)德里夫 时态: derived, deriving, derives (研四六托雅 3051/1798)","Mr Ying is one of those happy people who derive pleasure from helping others.",""],["deteriorate","/dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deteriorate”.","deteriorate [dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt] -2 vi. 恶化，变坏 vt. 恶化 时态: deteriorated, deteriorating, deteriorates (研六托雅宝 7587/6333)","欧陆词典释义：deteriorate [dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt] -2 vi. 恶化，变坏 vt. 恶化 时态: deteriorated, deteriorating, deteriorates (研六托雅宝 7587/6333)","There are fears that the situation might deteriorate into full-scale war...",""],["distinct","/dɪˈstɪŋkt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “distinct”.","distinct [dɪˈstɪŋkt] -2 adj. 明显的；独特的；清楚的；有区别的 (研四六托雅宝 3254/2609)","欧陆词典释义：distinct [dɪˈstɪŋkt] -2 adj. 明显的；独特的；清楚的；有区别的 (研四六托雅宝 3254/2609)","Engineering and technology are disciplines distinct from one another and from science...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"easily or clearly heard, seen, felt, etc.","example":"There was a distinct smell of gas."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"clearly different or of a different kind","example":"His voice was quiet but every word was distinct."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used to emphasize that you think an idea or situation definitely exists and is important","example":"The results of the survey fell into two distinct groups."}]],["diverse","/daɪˈvɜ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “diverse”.","diverse [daɪˈvɜ:s] -2 adj. 不同的；多种多样的；变化多的 (高研四六托雅宝 2813/4813)","欧陆词典释义：diverse [daɪˈvɜ:s] -2 adj. 不同的；多种多样的；变化多的 (高研四六托雅宝 2813/4813)","shops selling a diverse range of gifts...",""],["empirical","/ɪmˈpɪrɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “empirical”.","empirical [ɪmˈpɪrɪkl] -1 adj. 经验主义的，完全根据经验的；实证的 (研六雅宝 5285/4444)","欧陆词典释义：empirical [ɪmˈpɪrɪkl] -1 adj. 经验主义的，完全根据经验的；实证的 (研六雅宝 5285/4444)","There is no empirical evidence to support his thesis.",""],["enhance","/ɪnˈhɑ:ns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “enhance”.","enhance [ɪnˈhɑ:ns] -3 vt. 提高；加强；增加 时态: enhanced, enhancing, enhances (研四六托雅宝 2331/2669)","欧陆词典释义：enhance [ɪnˈhɑ:ns] -3 vt. 提高；加强；增加 时态: enhanced, enhancing, enhances (研四六托雅宝 2331/2669)","They'll be keen to enhance their reputation abroad...",""],["equivalent","/ɪˈkwɪvələnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “equivalent”.","equivalent [ɪˈkwɪvələnt] -K3 n. 等价物，相等物 adj. 等价的，相等的；同意义的 (研四六托雅宝 4330/3051)","欧陆词典释义：equivalent [ɪˈkwɪvələnt] -K3 n. 等价物，相等物 adj. 等价的，相等的；同意义的 (研四六托雅宝 4330/3051)","The equivalent of two tablespoons of polyunsaturated oils is ample each day...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"equal in value, amount, meaning, importance, etc.","example":"250 grams or an equivalent amount in ounces"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"the price we would pay elsewhere for a broadly equivalent house"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing, amount, word, etc. that is equivalent to something else","example":"Eight kilometres is roughly equivalent to five miles."}]],["ethical","/ˈeθɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ethical”.","ethical [ˈeθɪkl] -2 n. 处方药 adj. 伦理的；道德的；凭处方出售的 (六 3454/5465)","欧陆词典释义：ethical [ˈeθɪkl] -2 n. 处方药 adj. 伦理的；道德的；凭处方出售的 (六 3454/5465)","the moral and ethical standards in the school.",""],["explicit","/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “explicit”.","explicit [ɪkˈsplɪsɪt] -2 adj. 明确的；清楚的；直率的；详述的 (高研六托雅宝 4826/3722)","欧陆词典释义：explicit [ɪkˈsplɪsɪt] -2 adj. 明确的；清楚的；直率的；详述的 (高研六托雅宝 4826/3722)","sexually explicit scenes in films and books.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"clear and easy to understand","example":"He gave me very explicit directions on how to get there."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"saying something clearly, exactly and openly","example":"She was quite explicit about why she had left."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"said, done or shown in an open or direct way, so that you have no doubt about what is happening","example":"The reasons for the decision should be made explicit."}]],["facilitate","/fəˈsɪlɪteɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “facilitate”.","facilitate [fəˈsɪlɪteɪt] -1 vt. 促进；帮助；使容易 时态: facilitated, facilitating, facilitates (研六托雅宝 3568/4044)","欧陆词典释义：facilitate [fəˈsɪlɪteɪt] -1 vt. 促进；帮助；使容易 时态: facilitated, facilitating, facilitates (研六托雅宝 3568/4044)","The new airport will facilitate the development of tourism...",""],["fundamental","/ˌfʌndəˈmentl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “fundamental”.","fundamental [ˌfʌndəˈmentl] -K3 n. 基本原理；基本原则 adj. 基本的，根本的 (高研四六托雅宝 2328/2031)","欧陆词典释义：fundamental [ˌfʌndəˈmentl] -K3 n. 基本原理；基本原则 adj. 基本的，根本的 (高研四六托雅宝 2328/2031)","Our constitution embodies all the fundamental principles of democracy...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"serious and very important; affecting the most central and important parts of something","example":"There is a fundamental difference"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"central; forming the necessary basis of something","example":"A fundamental change"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"forming the source or base from which everything else is made; not able to be divided any further","example":"a question of fundamental importance"}]],["hypothesis","/haɪˈpɒθəsɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hypothesis”.","hypothesis [haɪˈpɒθəsɪs] -1 n. 假设 (研六托雅宝 3377/3265)","欧陆词典释义：hypothesis [haɪˈpɒθəsɪs] -1 n. 假设 (研六托雅宝 3377/3265)","Work will now begin to test the hypothesis in rats...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an idea or explanation of something that is based on a few known facts but that has not yet been proved to be true or correct","example":"to formulate/confirm a hypothesis"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"guesses and ideas that are not based on certain knowledge","example":"a hypothesis about the function of dreams"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"There is little evidence to support these hypotheses."}]],["inevitable","/ɪnˈevɪtəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “inevitable”.","inevitable [ɪnˈevɪtəbl] -K3 adj. 必然的，不可避免的 (研四六托雅 3561/2837)","欧陆词典释义：inevitable [ɪnˈevɪtəbl] -K3 adj. 必然的，不可避免的 (研四六托雅 3561/2837)","If the case succeeds, it is inevitable that other trials will follow...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that you cannot avoid or prevent","example":"It was an inevitable consequence of the decision."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"so frequent that you always expect it","example":"It was inevitable that"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that is certain to happen","example":"A rise in the interest rates seems inevitable."}]],["inherent","/ɪnˈhɪərənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “inherent”.","inherent [ɪnˈhɪərənt] -2 adj. 固有的；内在的；与生俱来的，遗传的 (研六托雅 4924/4850)","欧陆词典释义：inherent [ɪnˈhɪərənt] -2 adj. 固有的；内在的；与生俱来的，遗传的 (研六托雅 4924/4850)","Stress is an inherent part of dieting.",""],["innovative","/ˈɪnəveɪtɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “innovative”.","innovative [ˈɪnəveɪtɪv] -2 adj. 革新的，创新的；新颖的；有创新精神的 (托宝 4435/5826)","欧陆词典释义：innovative [ˈɪnəveɪtɪv] -2 adj. 革新的，创新的；新颖的；有创新精神的 (托宝 4435/5826)","products which are more innovative than those of their competitors.",""],["integrate","/ˈɪntɪgreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “integrate”.","integrate [ˈɪntɪgreɪt] -3 n. 一体化；集成体 adj. 整合的；完全的 vi. 求积分；取消隔离；成为一体 vt. 使…完整；使…成整体；求…的积分；表示…的总和 时态: integrated, integrating, integrates (研四六托雅宝 3431/3349)","欧陆词典释义：integrate [ˈɪntɪgreɪt] -3 n. 一体化；集成体 adj. 整合的；完全的 vi. 求积分；取消隔离；成为一体 vt. 使…完整；使…成整体；求…的积分；表示…的总和 时态: integrated, integrating, integrates (研四六托雅宝 3431/3349)","He didn't integrate successfully into the Italian way of life...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to combine two or more things so that they work together; to combine with something else in this way","example":"These programs will integrate with your existing software."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become or make somebody become accepted as a member of a social group, especially when they come from a different culture","example":"These programs can be integrated with your existing software."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"They have not made any effort to integrate with the local community."}]],["intervene","/ˌɪntəˈvi:n/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “intervene”.","intervene [ˌɪntəˈvi:n] -2 vi. 干涉；调停；插入 时态: intervened, intervening, intervenes (研六托雅宝 5091/3956)","欧陆词典释义：intervene [ˌɪntəˈvi:n] -2 vi. 干涉；调停；插入 时态: intervened, intervening, intervenes (研六托雅宝 5091/3956)","The situation calmed down when police intervene d...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become involved in a situation in order to improve or help it","example":"She might have been killed if the neighbours hadn't intervened."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to interrupt somebody when they are speaking in order to say something","example":"The President intervened personally in the crisis."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to happen in a way that delays something or prevents it from happening","example":"‘But,’ she intervened, ‘what about the others?’"}]],["justify","/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “justify”.","justify [ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ] -K3 vi. 证明合法；整理版面 vt. 证明…是正当的；替…辩护 时态: justified, justifying, justifies (研四六托雅宝 2834/1959)","欧陆词典释义：justify [ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ] -K3 vi. 证明合法；整理版面 vt. 证明…是正当的；替…辩护 时态: justified, justifying, justifies (研四六托雅宝 2834/1959)","No argument can justify a war...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show that somebody/something is right or reasonable","example":"How can they justify paying such huge salaries?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give an explanation or excuse for something or for doing something","example":"Her success had justified the faith her teachers had put in her."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to arrange lines of printed text so that one or both edges are straight","example":"The Prime Minister has been asked to justify the decision to Parliament."}]],["manipulate","/məˈnɪpjuleɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “manipulate”.","manipulate [məˈnɪpjuleɪt] -2 vt. 操纵；操作；巧妙地处理；篡改 时态: manipulated, manipulating, manipulates (研六托雅宝 4248/4688)","欧陆词典释义：manipulate [məˈnɪpjuleɪt] -2 vt. 操纵；操作；巧妙地处理；篡改 时态: manipulated, manipulating, manipulates (研六托雅宝 4248/4688)","He is a very difficult character. He manipulate s people...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to control or influence somebody/something, often in a dishonest way so that they do not realize it","example":"She uses her charm to manipulate people."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to control or use something in a skilful way","example":"As a politician, he knows how to manipulate public opinion."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move a person’s bones or joints into the correct position","example":"They managed to manipulate us into agreeing to help."}]],["methodology","/ˌmeθəˈdɒlədʒi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “methodology”.","methodology [ˌmeθəˈdɒlədʒi] -1 n. 方法学，方法论 (托 5679/5499)","欧陆词典释义：methodology [ˌmeθəˈdɒlədʒi] -1 n. 方法学，方法论 (托 5679/5499)","Teaching methodologies vary according to the topic...",""],["negligible","/ˈneglɪdʒəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “negligible”.","negligible [ˈneglɪdʒəbl] -1 adj. 微不足道的，可以忽略的 (研六托雅 12050/8612)","欧陆词典释义：negligible [ˈneglɪdʒəbl] -1 adj. 微不足道的，可以忽略的 (研六托雅 12050/8612)","The pay that the soldiers received was negligible ...",""],["notion","/ˈnəʊʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “notion”.","notion [ˈnəʊʃn] -3 n. 概念；见解；打算 (研四六托雅 1714/1969)","欧陆词典释义：notion [ˈnəʊʃn] -3 n. 概念；见解；打算 (研四六托雅 1714/1969)","We each have a notion of just what kind of person we'd like to be...",""],["paradigm","/ˈpærədaɪm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “paradigm”.","paradigm [ˈpærədaɪm] -1 n. 范例；词形变化表 (研宝 5201/7401)","欧陆词典释义：paradigm [ˈpærədaɪm] -1 n. 范例；词形变化表 (研宝 5201/7401)","a new paradigm of production.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a typical example or pattern of something","example":"a paradigm for students to copy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a set of all the different forms of a word","example":"The war was a paradigm of the destructive side of human nature."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"verb paradigms"}]],["perspective","/pəˈspektɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “perspective”.","perspective [pəˈspektɪv] -3 n. 观点；远景；透视图 adj. 透视的 (研四六托雅宝 1412/2305)","欧陆词典释义：perspective [pəˈspektɪv] -3 n. 观点；远景；透视图 adj. 透视的 (研四六托雅宝 1412/2305)","He says the death of his father 18 months ago has given him a new perspective on life...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a particular attitude towards something; a way of thinking about something","example":"a global perspective"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to think about problems and decisions in a reasonable way without exaggerating their importance","example":"Recent events seem less serious when put into an international perspective."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the art of creating an effect of depth and distance in a picture by representing people and things that are far away as being smaller than those that are nearer the front","example":"Try to see the issue from"}]],["phenomenon","/fəˈnɒmɪnən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “phenomenon”.","phenomenon [fəˈnɒmɪnən] -2 n. 现象；奇迹；杰出的人才 (高研四六托雅 2466/2392)","欧陆词典释义：phenomenon [fəˈnɒmɪnən] -2 n. 现象；奇迹；杰出的人才 (高研四六托雅 2466/2392)","scientific explanations of natural phenomena...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a fact or an event in nature or society, especially one that is not fully understood","example":"cultural/natural/social phenomena"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person or thing that is very successful or impressive","example":"Globalization is a phenomenon of the 21st century."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"Early retirement is a relatively new phenomenon in Britain."}]],["preliminary","/prɪˈlɪmɪnəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “preliminary”.","preliminary [prɪˈlɪmɪnəri] -2 n. 准备；预赛；初步措施 adj. 初步的；开始的；预备的 (研四六托雅宝 4404/3851)","欧陆词典释义：preliminary [prɪˈlɪmɪnəri] -2 n. 准备；预赛；初步措施 adj. 初步的；开始的；预备的 (研四六托雅宝 4404/3851)","Preliminary results show the Republican party with 11 percent of the vote...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"happening before a more important action or event","example":"After a few preliminary remarks he announced the winners."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"preliminary results/findings/enquiries"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a preliminary","example":"the preliminary rounds of the contest"}]],["profound","/prəˈfaʊnd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “profound”.","profound [prəˈfaʊnd] -2 adj. 深厚的；意义深远的；渊博的 级别: profounder, profoundest (研六托雅宝 3735/4372)","欧陆词典释义：profound [prəˈfaʊnd] -2 adj. 深厚的；意义深远的；渊博的 级别: profounder, profoundest (研六托雅宝 3735/4372)","discoveries which had a profound effect on many areas of medicine.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"very great; felt or experienced very strongly","example":"profound changes in the earth’s climate"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"showing great knowledge or understanding","example":"My father's death had a profound effect on us all."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"needing a lot of study or thought","example":"The news came as a profound shock."}]],["rational","/ˈræʃnəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “rational”.","rational [ˈræʃnəl] -2 n. 有理数 adj. 合理的；理性的 (研四六托雅宝 4481/3243)","欧陆词典释义：rational [ˈræʃnəl] -2 n. 有理数 adj. 合理的；理性的 (研四六托雅宝 4481/3243)","He's asking you to look at both sides of the case and come to a rational decision...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"based on reason rather than emotions","example":"a rational argument/choice/decision"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"able to think clearly and make decisions based on reason rather than emotions","example":"rational analysis/thought"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"There is no rational explanation for his actions."}]],["reinforce","/ˌri:ɪnˈfɔ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “reinforce”.","reinforce [ˌri:ɪnˈfɔ:s] -2 n. 加强；加固物；加固材料 vt. 加强，加固；强化；补充 vi. 求援；得到增援；给予更多的支持 时态: reinforced, reinforcing, reinforces (研四六托雅宝 3329/2839)","欧陆词典释义：reinforce [ˌri:ɪnˈfɔ:s] -2 n. 加强；加固物；加固材料 vt. 加强，加固；强化；补充 vi. 求援；得到增援；给予更多的支持 时态: reinforced, reinforcing, reinforces (研四六托雅宝 3329/2839)","A stronger European Parliament would, they fear, only reinforce the power of the larger countries...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make a feeling, an idea, etc. stronger","example":"The experience reinforced my sense of loss."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make a structure or material stronger, especially by adding another material to it","example":"Such jokes tend to reinforce racial stereotypes."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to send more people or equipment in order to make an army, etc. stronger","example":"The climate of political confusion has only reinforced the country's economic decline."}]],["resilient","/rɪˈzɪliənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “resilient”.","resilient [rɪˈzɪliənt] -1 adj. 弹回的，有弹力的 adj. 能复原的；有复原力的 (宝 10634/13884)","欧陆词典释义：resilient [rɪˈzɪliənt] -1 adj. 弹回的，有弹力的 adj. 能复原的；有复原力的 (宝 10634/13884)","Cotton is more resistant to being squashed and polyester is more resilient .",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"able to feel better quickly after something unpleasant such as shock, injury, etc.","example":"He'll get over it—young people are amazingly resilient."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"returning to its original shape after being bent, stretched, or pressed","example":"These plants are very resilient to rough handling."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"a pretty resilient plant"}]],["rigorous","/ˈrɪgərəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “rigorous”.","rigorous [ˈrɪgərəs] -2 adj. 严格的，严厉的；严密的；严酷的 (研六托雅 6606/7073)","欧陆词典释义：rigorous [ˈrɪgərəs] -2 adj. 严格的，严厉的；严密的；严酷的 (研六托雅 6606/7073)","The selection process is based on rigorous tests of competence and experience.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"done carefully and with a lot of attention to detail","example":"a rigorous analysis"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"demanding that particular rules, processes, etc. are strictly followed","example":"Few people have gone into the topic in such rigorous detail."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The second team adopted a much more rigorous approach to the problem."}]],["scenario","/səˈnɑ:riəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “scenario”.","scenario [səˈnɑ:riəʊ] -2 n. 方案；情节；剧本；设想 (宝 2756/5562)","欧陆词典释义：scenario [səˈnɑ:riəʊ] -2 n. 方案；情节；剧本；设想 (宝 2756/5562)","the nightmare scenario of a divided and irrelevant Royal Family...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a description of how things might happen in the future","example":"Let me suggest a possible scenario"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a written outline of what happens in a film/movie or play","example":"The worst-case scenario"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 19th cent.","example":"a nightmare scenario"}]],["sophisticated","/səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sophisticated”.","sophisticated [səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd] -3 adj. 复杂的；精致的；久经世故的；富有经验的 v. 使变得世故；使迷惑；篡改（sophisticate的过去分词形式） 原型: sophisticated 是 sophisticate 的过去式和过去分词 (研四六托雅宝 3077/3019)","欧陆词典释义：sophisticated [səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd] -3 adj. 复杂的；精致的；久经世故的；富有经验的 v. 使变得世故；使迷惑；篡改（sophisticate的过去分词形式） 原型: sophisticated 是 sophisticate 的过去式和过去分词 (研四六托雅宝 3077/3019)","Honeybees use one of the most sophisticated communication systems of any insect.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a lot of experience of the world and knowing about fashion, culture and other things that people think are socially important","example":"the sophisticated pleasures of city life"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"clever and complicated in the way that it works or is presented","example":"Mark is a smart and sophisticated young man."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"able to understand difficult or complicated ideas","example":"highly sophisticated computer systems"}]],["specify","/ˈspesɪfaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “specify”.","specify [ˈspesɪfaɪ] -2 vt. 指定；详细说明；列举；把…列入说明书 时态: specified, specifying, specifies (研四六托 4860/2230)","欧陆词典释义：specify [ˈspesɪfaɪ] -2 vt. 指定；详细说明；列举；把…列入说明书 时态: specified, specifying, specifies (研四六托 4860/2230)","They specified a spacious entrance hall...",""],["statistical","/stə'tɪstɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “statistical”.","statistical [stə'tɪstɪkl] -2 adj. 统计的；统计学的 (研四六 4292/3479)","欧陆词典释义：statistical [stə'tɪstɪkl] -2 adj. 统计的；统计学的 (研四六 4292/3479)","The report contains a great deal of statistical information...",""],["strategy","/ˈstrætədʒi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “strategy”.","strategy [ˈstrætədʒi] -K4 n. 战略，策略 (研四六托雅 844/1127)","欧陆词典释义：strategy [ˈstrætədʒi] -K4 n. 战略，策略 (研四六托雅 844/1127)","Next week, health ministers gather in Amsterdam to agree a strategy for controlling malaria...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a plan that is intended to achieve a particular purpose","example":"the government’s economic strategy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of planning something or putting a plan into operation in a skilful way","example":"to develop a strategy for dealing with unemployment"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the skill of planning the movements of armies in a battle or war; an example of doing this","example":"It's all part of an overall strategy to gain promotion."}]],["subjective","/səbˈdʒektɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “subjective”.","subjective [səbˈdʒektɪv] -1 adj. 主观的；个人的；自觉的 (高研六雅宝 5947/5186)","欧陆词典释义：subjective [səbˈdʒektɪv] -1 adj. 主观的；个人的；自觉的 (高研六雅宝 5947/5186)","We know that taste in art is a subjective matter...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"based on your own ideas or opinions rather than facts and therefore sometimes unfair","example":"a highly subjective point of view"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"existing in somebody’s mind rather than in the outside world","example":"Everyone's opinion is bound to be subjective."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the subjective","example":"The criticisms are purely subjective."}]],["subsequent","/ˈsʌbsɪkwənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “subsequent”.","subsequent [ˈsʌbsɪkwənt] -3 adj. 后来的，随后的 (研四六托雅宝 3267/2113)","欧陆词典释义：subsequent [ˈsʌbsɪkwənt] -3 adj. 后来的，随后的 (研四六托雅宝 3267/2113)","the increase of population in subsequent years...",""],["sustainable","/səˈsteɪnəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sustainable”.","sustainable [səˈsteɪnəbl] -1 adj. 可以忍受的；足可支撑的；养得起的；可持续的 (4895/7345)","欧陆词典释义：sustainable [səˈsteɪnəbl] -1 adj. 可以忍受的；足可支撑的；养得起的；可持续的 (4895/7345)","the management, conservation and sustainable development of forests...",""],["tentative","/ˈtentətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “tentative”.","tentative [ˈtentətɪv] -2 n. 假设，试验 adj. 试验性的，暂定的；踌躇的 (高研六托雅宝 7722/7552)","欧陆词典释义：tentative [ˈtentətɪv] -2 n. 假设，试验 adj. 试验性的，暂定的；踌躇的 (高研六托雅宝 7722/7552)","Political leaders have reached a tentative agreement to hold a preparatory conference next month...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not definite or certain because you may want to change it later","example":"We made a tentative arrangement"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not behaving or done with confidence","example":"tentative conclusions"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"a tentative greeting"}]],["theoretical","/ˌθɪəˈretɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “theoretical”.","theoretical [ˌθɪəˈretɪkl] -2 adj. 理论的；理论上的；假设的；推理的 (高研四六托雅宝 3781/2729)","欧陆词典释义：theoretical [ˌθɪəˈretɪkl] -2 adj. 理论的；理论上的；假设的；推理的 (高研四六托雅宝 3781/2729)"," theoretical physics.",""],["transform","/trænsˈfɔ:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “transform”.","transform [trænsˈfɔ:m] -K3 vt. 改变，使…变形；转换 vi. 变换，改变；转化 时态: transformed, transforming, transforms (高研四六托雅 2185/2693)","欧陆词典释义：transform [trænsˈfɔ:m] -K3 vt. 改变，使…变形；转换 vi. 变换，改变；转化 时态: transformed, transforming, transforms (高研四六托雅 2185/2693)","Your metabolic rate is the speed at which your body transform s food into energy...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change the form of something","example":"The photochemical reactions transform the light into electrical impulses."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to completely change the appearance or character of something, especially so that it is better","example":"A new colour scheme will transform your bedroom."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"It was an event that would transform my life."}]],["transparent","/trænsˈpærənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “transparent”.","transparent [trænsˈpærənt] -K1 adj. 透明的；显然的；坦率的；易懂的 (高研四六托雅宝 5884/6902)","欧陆词典释义：transparent [trænsˈpærənt] -K1 adj. 透明的；显然的；坦率的；易懂的 (高研四六托雅宝 5884/6902)","a sheet of transparent coloured plastic...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"allowing you to see through it","example":"The insect's wings are almost transparent."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"allowing you to see the truth easily","example":"a man of transparent honesty"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"easy to understand","example":"a transparent attempt to buy votes"}]],["underlying","/ˌʌndəˈlaɪɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “underlying”.","underlying [ˌʌndəˈlaɪɪŋ] -2 adj. 潜在的；根本的；在下面的；优先的 v. 放在…的下面；为…的基础；优先于（underlie的ing形式） 原型: underlying 是 underlie 的现在分词 (研六托雅宝 4265/3334)","欧陆词典释义：underlying [ˌʌndəˈlaɪɪŋ] -2 adj. 潜在的；根本的；在下面的；优先的 v. 放在…的下面；为…的基础；优先于（underlie的ing形式） 原型: underlying 是 underlie 的现在分词 (研六托雅宝 4265/3334)","To stop a problem you have to understand its underlying causes...",""],["validate","/ˈvælɪdeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “validate”.","validate [ˈvælɪdeɪt] -1 vt. 证实，验证；确认；使生效 时态: validated, validating, validates (托宝 7516/9106)","欧陆词典释义：validate [ˈvælɪdeɪt] -1 vt. 证实，验证；确认；使生效 时态: validated, validating, validates (托宝 7516/9106)","This discovery seems to validate the claims of popular astrology.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to prove that something is true","example":"to validate a theory"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something legally valid","example":"The research findings do not validate the claims made by the manufacturer."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to state officially that something is useful and of an acceptable standard","example":"to validate a contract"}]],["viable","/ˈvaɪəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “viable”.","viable [ˈvaɪəbl] -2 adj. 可行的；能养活的；能生育的 (托雅宝 5049/5700)","欧陆词典释义：viable [ˈvaɪəbl] -2 adj. 可行的；能养活的；能生育的 (托雅宝 5049/5700)","Cash alone will not make Eastern Europe's banks viable ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that can be done; that will be successful","example":"a viable option/proposition"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"capable of developing and surviving independently","example":"There is no viable alternative"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"early 19th cent.","example":"to be commercially/politically/financially/economically viable"}]],["whereby","/weəˈbaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “whereby”.","whereby [weəˈbaɪ] -2 adv. 凭借；通过…；借以；与…一致 (六雅 8497/3568)","欧陆词典释义：whereby [weəˈbaɪ] -2 adv. 凭借；通过…；借以；与…一致 (六雅 8497/3568)","the system whereby Britons choose their family doctors and the government pays those doctors...",""],["withdraw","/wɪðˈdrɔ:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “withdraw”.","withdraw [wɪðˈdrɔ:] -K4 vt. 撤退；收回；撤消；拉开 vi. 撤退；离开 时态: withdrew, withdrawn, withdrawing, withdraws (高研四六托雅宝 2786/1920)","欧陆词典释义：withdraw [wɪðˈdrɔ:] -K4 vt. 撤退；收回；撤消；拉开 vi. 撤退；离开 时态: withdrew, withdrawn, withdrawing, withdraws (高研四六托雅宝 2786/1920)","He reached into his pocket and withdrew a sheet of notepaper...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move back or away from a place or situation; to make somebody/something do this","example":"Government troops were forced to withdraw."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to stop giving or offering something to somebody","example":"Both powers withdrew their forces from the region."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to stop taking part in an activity or being a member of an organization; to stop somebody/something from doing these things","example":"She withdrew her hand from his."}]],["yield","/ji:ld/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “yield”.","yield [ji:ld] -3 n. 产量；收益 vt. 屈服；出产，产生；放弃 vi. 屈服，投降 时态: yielded, yielding, yields (研四六托雅 2652/3333)","欧陆词典释义：yield [ji:ld] -3 n. 产量；收益 vt. 屈服；出产，产生；放弃 vi. 屈服，投降 时态: yielded, yielding, yields (研四六托雅 2652/3333)","Will she yield to growing pressure for her to retire?...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to produce or provide something, for example a profit, result or crop","example":"Higher-rate deposit accounts yield good returns."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to stop resisting something/somebody; to agree to do something that you do not want to do","example":"The research has yielded useful information."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to allow somebody to win, have or take control of something that has been yours until now","example":"trees that no longer yield fruit"}]],["advocate","/ˈædvəkeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “advocate”.","advocate [ˈædvəkeɪt] -3 n. 提倡者；支持者；律师 vt. 提倡，主张，拥护 时态: advocated, advocating, advocates (高研四六托雅宝 2623/4031)","欧陆词典释义：advocate [ˈædvəkeɪt] -3 n. 提倡者；支持者；律师 vt. 提倡，主张，拥护 时态: advocated, advocating, advocates (高研四六托雅宝 2623/4031)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “advocate”.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to support something publicly","example":"The group does not advocate the use of violence."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"Heart specialists strongly advocate low-cholesterol diets."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who supports or speaks in favour of somebody or of a public plan or action","example":"These policies have been widely advocated."}]],["allocate","/ˈæləkeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “allocate”.","allocate [ˈæləkeɪt] -2 vt. 分配；拨出；使坐落于 vi. 分配；指定 时态: allocated, allocating, allocates (高研六托雅宝 6763/3035)","欧陆词典释义：allocate [ˈæləkeɪt] -2 vt. 分配；拨出；使坐落于 vi. 分配；指定 时态: allocated, allocating, allocates (高研六托雅宝 6763/3035)","Tickets are limited and will be allocate d to those who apply first...",""],["autonomous","/ɔ:ˈtɒnəməs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “autonomous”.","autonomous [ɔ:ˈtɒnəməs] -2 adj. 自治的；自主的；自发的 (高托宝 7499/5495)","欧陆词典释义：autonomous [ɔ:ˈtɒnəməs] -2 adj. 自治的；自主的；自发的 (高托宝 7499/5495)","They proudly declared themselves part of a new autonomous province.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"able to govern itself or control its own affairs","example":"an autonomous republic/state/province"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"able to do things and make decisions without help from anyone else","example":"a federation of autonomous groups"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"early 19th cent.","example":"Teachers aim to help children become autonomous learners."}]],["abstract","/ˈæbstrækt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abstract”.","abstract [ˈæbstrækt] -2 n. 摘要；抽象；抽象的概念 adj. 抽象的；深奥的 vt. 摘要；提取；使……抽象化；转移(注意力、兴趣等)；使心不在焉 vi. 做摘要；写梗概 时态: abstracted, abstracting, abstracts (高研四六托雅宝 4007/3729)","欧陆词典释义：abstract [ˈæbstrækt] -2 n. 摘要；抽象；抽象的概念 adj. 抽象的；深奥的 vt. 摘要；提取；使……抽象化；转移(注意力、兴趣等)；使心不在焉 vi. 做摘要；写梗概 时态: abstracted, abstracting, abstracts (高研四六托雅宝 4007/3729)"," abstract principles such as justice...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"based on general ideas and not on any particular real person, thing or situation","example":"abstract knowledge/principles"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"existing in thought or as an idea but not having a physical reality","example":"The research shows that pre-school children are capable of thinking in abstract terms."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"not representing people or things in a realistic way, but expressing the artist’s ideas about them","example":"We may talk of beautiful things but beauty itself is abstract."}]],["accommodate","/əˈkɒmədeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accommodate”.","accommodate [əˈkɒmədeɪt] -2 vi. 适应；调解 vt. 容纳；使适应；供应；调解 时态: accommodated, accommodating, accommodates (研四六托雅宝 3717/3404)","欧陆词典释义：accommodate [əˈkɒmədeɪt] -2 vi. 适应；调解 vt. 容纳；使适应；供应；调解 时态: accommodated, accommodating, accommodates (研四六托雅宝 3717/3404)","The school in Poldown was not big enough to accommodate all the children...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to provide somebody with a room or place to sleep, live or sit","example":"The hotel can accommodate up to 500 guests."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to provide enough space for somebody/something","example":"The aircraft is capable of accommodating 28 passengers."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to consider something, such as somebody’s opinion or a fact, and be influenced by it when you are deciding what to do or explaining something","example":"Over 70 minutes of music can be accommodated on one CD."}]],["acknowledge","/əkˈnɒlɪdʒ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “acknowledge”.","acknowledge [əkˈnɒlɪdʒ] -K3 vt. 承认；答谢；报偿；告知已收到 时态: acknowledged, acknowledging, acknowledges (高研四六托雅宝 1654/2105)","欧陆词典释义：acknowledge [əkˈnɒlɪdʒ] -K3 vt. 承认；答谢；报偿；告知已收到 时态: acknowledged, acknowledging, acknowledges (高研四六托雅宝 1654/2105)","Naylor acknowledge d, in a letter to the judge, that he was a drug addict...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to accept that something is true","example":"She refuses to acknowledge the need for reform."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to accept that somebody/something has a particular authority or status","example":"Are you prepared to acknowledge your responsibility?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to tell somebody that you have received something that they sent to you","example":"a generally acknowledged fact"}]],["administer","/ədˈmɪnɪstə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “administer”.","administer [ədˈmɪnɪstə(r)] -2 vt. 管理；执行；给予 vi. 给予帮助；执行遗产管理人的职责；担当管理人 时态: administered, administering, administers (研托雅 3661/3700)","欧陆词典释义：administer [ədˈmɪnɪstə(r)] -2 vt. 管理；执行；给予 vi. 给予帮助；执行遗产管理人的职责；担当管理人 时态: administered, administering, administers (研托雅 3661/3700)","The plan calls for the UN to administer the country until elections can be held...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to manage and organize the affairs of a company, an organization, a country, etc.","example":"to administer a charity/fund/school"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make sure that something is done fairly and in the correct way","example":"the high cost of administering medical services"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give or to provide something, especially in a formal way","example":"The pension funds are administered by commercial banks."}]],["aggregate","/ˈægrɪgət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “aggregate”.","aggregate [ˈægrɪgət] -2 n. 合计；集合体；总计 adj. 聚合的；集合的；合计的 vt. 集合；聚集；合计 vi. 集合；聚集；合计 时态: aggregated, aggregating, aggregates (托雅宝 12841/5505)","欧陆词典释义：aggregate [ˈægrɪgət] -2 n. 合计；集合体；总计 adj. 聚合的；集合的；合计的 vt. 集合；聚集；合计 vi. 集合；聚集；合计 时态: aggregated, aggregating, aggregates (托雅宝 12841/5505)","The rate of growth of GNP will depend upon the rate of growth of aggregate demand...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a total number or amount made up of smaller amounts that are collected together","example":"a record aggregate of 285 points"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"sand or broken stone that is used to make concrete or for building roads, etc.","example":"The three smaller parties gained an aggregate of 25 per cent of the vote."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Businesses are, in the aggregate, deeper in debt than ever before."}]],["analogous","/əˈnæləgəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “analogous”.","analogous [əˈnæləgəs] adj. 类似的；[昆] 同功的；可比拟的 (六托宝 10202/9154)","欧陆词典释义：analogous [əˈnæləgəs] adj. 类似的；[昆] 同功的；可比拟的 (六托宝 10202/9154)","Marine construction technology like this is very complex, somewhat analogous to trying to build a bridge under water.",""],["anomaly","/əˈnɒməli/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “anomaly”.","anomaly [əˈnɒməli] -1 n. 异常；不规则；反常事物 (托宝 8881/7902)","欧陆词典释义：anomaly [əˈnɒməli] -1 n. 异常；不规则；反常事物 (托宝 8881/7902)","The British public's wariness of opera is an anomaly in Europe.",""],["articulate","/ɑ:ˈtɪkjuleɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “articulate”.","articulate [ɑ:ˈtɪkjuleɪt] -2 adj. 发音清晰的；口才好的；有关节的 vt. 清晰地发（音）；明确有力地表达；用关节连接；使相互连贯 vi. 发音；清楚地讲话；用关节连接起来 n. 【动物学】有节体的动物 时态: articulated, articulating, articulates (研六托雅宝 4865/6482)","欧陆词典释义：articulate [ɑ:ˈtɪkjuleɪt] -2 adj. 发音清晰的；口才好的；有关节的 vt. 清晰地发（音）；明确有力地表达；用关节连接；使相互连贯 vi. 发音；清楚地讲话；用关节连接起来 n. 【动物学】有节体的动物 时态: articulated, articulating, articulates (研六托雅宝 4865/6482)","She is an articulate young woman...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to express or explain your thoughts or feelings clearly in words","example":"She struggled to articulate her thoughts."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"to speak, pronounce or play something in a clear way","example":"It is the school’s duty to articulate its practices to parents."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"to be related to something so that together the two parts form a whole","example":"He was too drunk to articulate properly."}]],["ascertain","/ˌæsəˈteɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ascertain”.","ascertain [ˌæsəˈteɪn] -1 vt. 确定；查明；探知 时态: ascertained, ascertaining, ascertains (研六托雅 9571/5989)","欧陆词典释义：ascertain [ˌæsəˈteɪn] -1 vt. 确定；查明；探知 时态: ascertained, ascertaining, ascertains (研六托雅 9571/5989)","Through doing this, the teacher will be able to ascertain the extent to which the child understands what he is reading...",""],["bias","/ˈbaɪəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bias”.","bias [ˈbaɪəs] -2 n. 偏见；偏爱；斜纹；乖离率 adj. 偏斜的 vt. 使存偏见 adv. 偏斜地 n. (Bias)人名；(法、德、葡、喀)比亚斯；(英)拜厄斯 时态: biased, biassing, biases (研六托雅 3925/4611)","欧陆词典释义：bias [ˈbaɪəs] -2 n. 偏见；偏爱；斜纹；乖离率 adj. 偏斜的 vt. 使存偏见 adv. 偏斜地 n. (Bias)人名；(法、德、葡、喀)比亚斯；(英)拜厄斯 时态: biased, biassing, biases (研六托雅 3925/4611)","Bias against women permeates every level of the judicial system...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a strong feeling in favour of or against one group of people, or one side in an argument, often not based on fair judgement","example":"accusations of political bias in news programmes ("},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an interest in one thing more than others; a special ability","example":"Employers must consider all candidates impartially and without bias."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the fact that the results of research or an experiment are not accurate because a particular factor has not been considered when collecting the information","example":"Some institutions still have a strong bias against women."}]],["catalyst","/ˈkætəlɪst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “catalyst”.","catalyst [ˈkætəlɪst] -1 n. [物化] 催化剂；刺激因素 (六托雅宝 7915/8852)","欧陆词典释义：catalyst [ˈkætəlɪst] -1 n. [物化] 催化剂；刺激因素 (六托雅宝 7915/8852)","I very much hope that this case will prove to be a catalyst for change...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a substance that makes a chemical reaction happen faster without being changed itself","example":"Chlorine will act as a catalyst."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person or thing that causes a change","example":"I see my role as being a catalyst for change."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 20th cent.","example":"The riots were later seen as the catalyst for the new political developments."}]],["collaborate","/kəˈlæbəreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “collaborate”.","collaborate [kəˈlæbəreɪt] -1 vi. 合作；勾结，通敌 时态: collaborated, collaborating, collaborates (研四六托宝 6388/7961)","欧陆词典释义：collaborate [kəˈlæbəreɪt] -1 vi. 合作；勾结，通敌 时态: collaborated, collaborating, collaborates (研四六托宝 6388/7961)","He collaborate d with his son Michael on the English translation of a text on food production...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to work together with somebody in order to produce or achieve something","example":"Researchers around the world are collaborating to develop a new vaccine."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to help the enemy who has taken control of your country during a war","example":"We have collaborated on many projects over the years."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 19th cent.","example":"She agreed to collaborate with him in writing her biography."}]],["commence","/kəˈmens/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “commence”.","commence [kəˈmens] -1 v. 开始；着手；&lt;英&gt;获得学位 时态: commenced, commencing, commences (研六托雅宝 9454/4318)","欧陆词典释义：commence [kəˈmens] -1 v. 开始；着手；&lt;英&gt;获得学位 时态: commenced, commencing, commences (研六托雅宝 9454/4318)","The academic year commence s at the beginning of October...",""],["compelling","/kəmˈpelɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compelling”.","compelling [kəmˈpelɪŋ] -2 adj. 引人注目的；强制的；激发兴趣的 v. 强迫；以强力获得（compel的ing形式） 原型: compelling 是 compel 的现在分词 (研宝 4879/9505)","欧陆词典释义：compelling [kəmˈpelɪŋ] -2 adj. 引人注目的；强制的；激发兴趣的 v. 强迫；以强力获得（compel的ing形式） 原型: compelling 是 compel 的现在分词 (研宝 4879/9505)","Factual and forensic evidence makes a suicide verdict the most compelling answer to the mystery of his death...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that makes you pay attention to it because it is so interesting and exciting","example":"Her latest book makes compelling reading."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"so strong that you must do something about it","example":"That’s an interesting question, Daniel."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that makes you think it is true","example":"The exhibition tells the fascinating story of the steam age."}]],["comprehensive","/ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “comprehensive”.","comprehensive [ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv] -3 n. 综合学校；专业综合测验 adj. 综合的；广泛的；有理解力的 (研四六托宝 2896/2442)","欧陆词典释义：comprehensive [ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv] -3 n. 综合学校；专业综合测验 adj. 综合的；广泛的；有理解力的 (研四六托宝 2896/2442)","The Rough Guide to Nepal is a comprehensive guide to the region.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"including all, or almost all, the items, details, facts, information, etc., that may be concerned","example":"a comprehensive list of addresses"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"designed for students of all abilities in the same school","example":"a comprehensive study"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"comprehensive insurance ("}]],["constrain","/kənˈstreɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “constrain”.","constrain [kənˈstreɪn] -1 vt. 驱使；强迫；束缚 时态: constrained, constraining, constrains (研六托雅宝 7740/5685)","欧陆词典释义：constrain [kənˈstreɪn] -1 vt. 驱使；强迫；束缚 时态: constrained, constraining, constrains (研六托雅宝 7740/5685)","Women are too often constrain ed by family commitments and by low expectations...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to force somebody to do something or behave in a particular way","example":"The evidence was so compelling that he felt constrained to"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to restrict or limit somebody/something","example":"The company said that it was constrained to raise prices."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"Research has been constrained by a lack of funds."}]],["contemplate","/ˈkɒntəmpleɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contemplate”.","contemplate [ˈkɒntəmpleɪt] -2 vt. 沉思；注视；思忖；预期 vi. 冥思苦想；深思熟虑 时态: contemplated, contemplating, contemplates (研六托雅宝 4802/3951)","欧陆词典释义：contemplate [ˈkɒntəmpleɪt] -2 vt. 沉思；注视；思忖；预期 vi. 冥思苦想；深思熟虑 时态: contemplated, contemplating, contemplates (研六托雅宝 4802/3951)","For a time he contemplate d a career as an army medical doctor...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think about whether you should do something, or how you should do something","example":"You're too young to be contemplating retirement."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think carefully about and accept the possibility of something happening","example":"I have never contemplated living abroad."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to think deeply about something for a long time","example":"He continued while she contemplated how to answer."}]],["contradict","/ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contradict”.","contradict [ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt] -1 vt. 反驳；否定；与…矛盾；与…抵触 vi. 反驳；否认；发生矛盾 时态: contradicted, contradicting, contradicts (高研六托雅宝 6863/6870)","欧陆词典释义：contradict [ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt] -1 vt. 反驳；否定；与…矛盾；与…抵触 vi. 反驳；否认；发生矛盾 时态: contradicted, contradicting, contradicts (高研六托雅宝 6863/6870)","She dared not contradict him...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to say that something that somebody else has said is wrong, and that the opposite is true","example":"All evening her husband contradicted everything she said."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be so different from each other that one of them must be wrong","example":"You've just contradicted yourself"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"‘No, it’s not,’ she contradicted (him)."}]],["conversely","/ˈkɒnvɜ:sli/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conversely”.","conversely [ˈkɒnvɜ:sli] adv. 相反地 (研四六雅 8066/6671)","欧陆词典释义：conversely [ˈkɒnvɜ:sli] adv. 相反地 (研四六雅 8066/6671)","In real life, nobody was all bad, nor, conversely , all good.",""],["credible","/ˈkredəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “credible”.","credible [ˈkredəbl] -2 adj. 可靠的，可信的 (雅宝 5991/9699)","欧陆词典释义：credible [ˈkredəbl] -2 adj. 可靠的，可信的 (雅宝 5991/9699)","Baroness Thatcher's claims seem credible to many...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that can be believed or trusted","example":"a credible explanation/witness"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that can be accepted, because it seems possible that it could be successful","example":"It is just not credible that she would cheat."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Community service is seen as the only credible alternative to imprisonment."}]],["denote","/dɪˈnəʊt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “denote”.","denote [dɪˈnəʊt] -1 vt. 表示，指示 时态: denoted, denoting, denotes (研六托雅宝 9748/6148)","欧陆词典释义：denote [dɪˈnəʊt] -1 vt. 表示，指示 时态: denoted, denoting, denotes (研六托雅宝 9748/6148)","Red eyes denote strain and fatigue...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be a sign of something","example":"A very high temperature often denotes a serious illness."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to mean something","example":"In this example ‘X’ denotes the time taken and ‘Y’ denotes the distance covered."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"The red triangle denotes danger."}]],["discriminate","/dɪˈskrɪmɪneɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “discriminate”.","discriminate [dɪˈskrɪmɪneɪt] -1 vi. 区别；辨别 vt. 歧视；区别；辨别 时态: discriminated, discriminating, discriminates (研托雅宝 6782/6572)","欧陆词典释义：discriminate [dɪˈskrɪmɪneɪt] -1 vi. 区别；辨别 vt. 歧视；区别；辨别 时态: discriminated, discriminating, discriminates (研托雅宝 6782/6572)","He is incapable of discriminating between a good idea and a terrible one...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to recognize that there is a difference between people or things; to show a difference between people or things","example":"The computer program was unable to discriminate between letters and numbers."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to treat one person or group worse/better than another in an unfair way","example":"When do babies learn to discriminate voices?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"A number of features discriminate this species from others."}]],["dynamic","/daɪˈnæmɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dynamic”.","dynamic [daɪˈnæmɪk] -2 n. 动态；动力 adj. 动态的；动力的；动力学的；有活力的 (高研四六托雅宝 3978/4218)","欧陆词典释义：dynamic [daɪˈnæmɪk] -2 n. 动态；动力 adj. 动态的；动力的；动力学的；有活力的 (高研四六托雅宝 3978/4218)","He seemed a dynamic and energetic leader...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way in which people or things behave and react to each other in a particular situation","example":"the dynamics of political change"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the science of the forces involved in movement","example":"group dynamics"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a force that produces change, action or effects","example":"Market dynamics are working in the company’s favour."}]],["elaborate","/ɪˈlæbərət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “elaborate”.","elaborate [ɪˈlæbərət] -2 adj. 精心制作的；详尽的；煞费苦心的 vi. 详细描述；变复杂 vt. 精心制作；详细阐述；从简单成分合成（复杂有机物） 时态: elaborated, elaborating, elaborates (研四六托雅宝 4630/4707)","欧陆词典释义：elaborate [ɪˈlæbərət] -2 adj. 精心制作的；详尽的；煞费苦心的 vi. 详细描述；变复杂 vt. 精心制作；详细阐述；从简单成分合成（复杂有机物） 时态: elaborated, elaborating, elaborates (研四六托雅宝 4630/4707)","an elaborate research project.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"very complicated and detailed; carefully prepared and organized","example":"elaborate designs"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"She had prepared a very elaborate meal."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to explain or describe something in a more detailed way","example":"an elaborate computer system"}]],["encompass","/ɪnˈkʌmpəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “encompass”.","encompass [ɪnˈkʌmpəs] -1 vt. 包含；包围，环绕；完成 时态: encompassed, encompassing, encompasses (托宝 5635/6021)","欧陆词典释义：encompass [ɪnˈkʌmpəs] -1 vt. 包含；包围，环绕；完成 时态: encompassed, encompassing, encompasses (托宝 5635/6021)","the extra services, which start next September and encompass a wide range of special interests...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to include a large number or range of things","example":"The job encompasses a wide range of responsibilities."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to surround or cover something completely","example":"The group encompasses all ages."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"The fog soon encompassed the whole valley."}]],["entity","/ˈentəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “entity”.","entity [ˈentəti] -2 n. 实体；存在；本质 (研六托雅宝 3932/3875)","欧陆词典释义：entity [ˈentəti] -2 n. 实体；存在；本质 (研六托雅宝 3932/3875)","the earth as a living entity ...",""],["equip","/ɪˈkwɪp/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “equip”.","equip [ɪˈkwɪp] -2 vt. 装备，配备 时态: equipped, equipping, equips (高研四六托 4145/3643)","欧陆词典释义：equip [ɪˈkwɪp] -2 vt. 装备，配备 时态: equipped, equipping, equips (高研四六托 4145/3643)","They become obsessed with trying to equip their vehicles with gadgets to deal with every possible contingency...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to provide yourself/somebody/something with the things that are needed for a particular purpose or activity","example":"to be fully/poorly equipped"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to prepare somebody for an activity or task, especially by teaching them what they need to know","example":"She got a bank loan to rent and equip a small workshop."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"early 16th cent.","example":"He equipped himself with a street plan."}]],["exacerbate","/ɪgˈzæsəbeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “exacerbate”.","exacerbate [ɪgˈzæsəbeɪt] -1 vt. 使加剧；使恶化；激怒 时态: exacerbated, exacerbating, exacerbates (雅宝 7171/7893)","欧陆词典释义：exacerbate [ɪgˈzæsəbeɪt] -1 vt. 使加剧；使恶化；激怒 时态: exacerbated, exacerbating, exacerbates (雅宝 7171/7893)","Mr Powell-Taylor says that depopulation exacerbate s the problem...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something worse, especially a disease or problem","example":"His aggressive reaction only exacerbated the situation."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"The symptoms may be exacerbated by certain drugs."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"His aggressive reaction only exacerbated the situation."}]],["exploit","/ɪkˈsplɔɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “exploit”.","exploit [ɪkˈsplɔɪt] -3 n. 勋绩；功绩 vt. 开发，开拓；剥削；开采 时态: exploited, exploiting, exploits (高研四六托雅宝 4374/3034)","欧陆词典释义：exploit [ɪkˈsplɔɪt] -3 n. 勋绩；功绩 vt. 开发，开拓；剥削；开采 时态: exploited, exploiting, exploits (高研四六托雅宝 4374/3034)","Critics claim he exploit ed black musicians for personal gain.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to treat a person or situation as an opportunity to gain an advantage for yourself","example":"He exploited his father's name to get himself a job."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to treat somebody unfairly by making them work and not giving them much in return","example":"She realized that her youth and inexperience were being exploited."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to use something well in order to gain as much from it as possible","example":"The opposition parties will always exploit government problems to their own advantage."}]],["fluctuate","/ˈflʌktʃueɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “fluctuate”.","fluctuate [ˈflʌktʃueɪt] -1 vi. 波动；涨落；动摇 vt. 使波动；使动摇 时态: fluctuated, fluctuating, fluctuates (研六托雅宝 12670/11623)","欧陆词典释义：fluctuate [ˈflʌktʃueɪt] -1 vi. 波动；涨落；动摇 vt. 使波动；使动摇 时态: fluctuated, fluctuating, fluctuates (研六托雅宝 12670/11623)","Body temperature can fluctuate if you are ill.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change frequently in size, amount, quality, etc., especially from one extreme to another","example":"fluctuating prices"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"The documentary follows the fluctuating fortunes of one marketing company."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"During the crisis, oil prices fluctuated between $20 and $40 a barrel."}]],["formulate","/ˈfɔ:mjuleɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “formulate”.","formulate [ˈfɔ:mjuleɪt] -2 vt. 规划；用公式表示；明确地表达 时态: formulated, formulating, formulates (研六托雅 5843/4149)","欧陆词典释义：formulate [ˈfɔ:mjuleɪt] -2 vt. 规划；用公式表示；明确地表达 时态: formulated, formulating, formulates (研六托雅 5843/4149)","Little by little, he formulate d his plan for escape.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to create or prepare something carefully, giving particular attention to the details","example":"to formulate a policy/theory/plan/proposal"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to express your ideas in carefully chosen words","example":"The compost is specially formulated for pot plants."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 19th cent.","example":"This new kitchen cleaner is formulated to cut through grease and dirt."}]],["holistic","/həʊˈlɪstɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “holistic”.","holistic [həʊˈlɪstɪk] -1 adj. 整体的；全盘的 (9808/12415)","欧陆词典释义：holistic [həʊˈlɪstɪk] -1 adj. 整体的；全盘的 (9808/12415)","practitioners of holistic medicine.",""],["implicit","/ɪmˈplɪsɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “implicit”.","implicit [ɪmˈplɪsɪt] -2 adj. 含蓄的；暗示的；盲从的 (研六托雅宝 6734/5088)","欧陆词典释义：implicit [ɪmˈplɪsɪt] -2 adj. 含蓄的；暗示的；盲从的 (研六托雅宝 6734/5088)","This is seen as an implicit warning not to continue with military action...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"suggested without being directly expressed","example":"Implicit in his speech was the assumption that they were guilty."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"forming part of something (although perhaps not directly expressed)","example":"implicit criticism"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"complete and not doubted","example":"These assumptions are implicit in his writing."}]],["induce","/ɪnˈdju:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “induce”.","induce [ɪnˈdju:s] -2 vt. 诱导；引起；引诱；感应 时态: induced, inducing, induces (研六托雅宝 5257/3326)","欧陆词典释义：induce [ɪnˈdju:s] -2 vt. 诱导；引起；引诱；感应 时态: induced, inducing, induces (研六托雅宝 5257/3326)","Doctors said surgery could induce a heart attack.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to persuade or influence somebody to do something","example":"Nothing would induce me to take the job."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to cause something","example":"drugs which induce sleep"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make a woman start giving birth to her baby by giving her special drugs","example":"a drug-induced coma"}]],["infrastructure","/ˈɪnfrəstrʌktʃə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “infrastructure”.","infrastructure [ˈɪnfrəstrʌktʃə(r)] -2 n. 基础设施；公共建设；下部构造 (研六 3613/5839)","欧陆词典释义：infrastructure [ˈɪnfrəstrʌktʃə(r)] -2 n. 基础设施；公共建设；下部构造 (研六 3613/5839)","investment in infrastructure ...",""],["inhibit","/ɪnˈhɪbɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “inhibit”.","inhibit [ɪnˈhɪbɪt] -1 vt. 抑制；禁止 时态: inhibited, inhibiting, inhibits (研六托雅宝 7404/5110)","欧陆词典释义：inhibit [ɪnˈhɪbɪt] -1 vt. 抑制；禁止 时态: inhibited, inhibiting, inhibits (研六托雅宝 7404/5110)","Wine or sugary drinks inhibit digestion...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to prevent something from happening or make it happen more slowly or less frequently than normal","example":"A lack of oxygen may inhibit brain development in the unborn child."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody nervous or embarrassed so that they are unable to do something","example":"Financial considerations are inhibiting access to higher education."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Alcohol significantly inhibits the action of the drug."}]],["intrinsic","/ɪnˈtrɪnsɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “intrinsic”.","intrinsic [ɪnˈtrɪnsɪk] -1 adj. 本质的，固有的 (研六托雅 7449/7995)","欧陆词典释义：intrinsic [ɪnˈtrɪnsɪk] -1 adj. 本质的，固有的 (研六托雅 7449/7995)","The paintings have no intrinsic value except as curiosities...",""],["invoke","/ɪnˈvəʊk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “invoke”.","invoke [ɪnˈvəʊk] -1 vt. 调用；祈求；引起；恳求 时态: invoked, invoking, invokes (托宝 5414/5725)","欧陆词典释义：invoke [ɪnˈvəʊk] -1 vt. 调用；祈求；引起；恳求 时态: invoked, invoking, invokes (托宝 5414/5725)","The judge invoke d an international law that protects refugees.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to mention or use a law, rule, etc. as a reason for doing something","example":"It is unlikely that libel laws will be invoked."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to mention a person, a theory, an example, etc. to support your opinions or ideas, or as a reason for something","example":"She invoked several eminent scholars to back up her argument."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to mention somebody’s name to make people feel a particular thing or act in a particular way","example":"His name was invoked as a symbol of the revolution."}]],["mediate","/ˈmi:dieɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mediate”.","mediate [ˈmi:dieɪt] -2 vi. 调解；斡旋；居中 vt. 调停；传达 adj. 间接的；居间的 时态: mediated, mediating, mediates (六托雅宝 7370/6739)","欧陆词典释义：mediate [ˈmi:dieɪt] -2 vi. 调解；斡旋；居中 vt. 调停；传达 adj. 间接的；居间的 时态: mediated, mediating, mediates (六托雅宝 7370/6739)","My mom was the one who mediate d between Zelda and her mom...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to try to end a disagreement between two or more people or groups by talking to them and trying to find things that everyone can agree on","example":"The Secretary-General was asked to mediate in the dispute."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to succeed in finding a solution to a disagreement between people or groups","example":"An independent body was brought in to mediate between staff and management."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to influence something and/or make it possible for it to happen","example":"to mediate differences/disputes/problems"}]],["migrate","/maɪˈgreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “migrate”.","migrate [maɪˈgreɪt] -2 vi. 移动；随季节而移居；移往 vt. 使移居；使移植 时态: migrated, migrating, migrates (研六托雅 6504/7939)","欧陆词典释义：migrate [maɪˈgreɪt] -2 vi. 移动；随季节而移居；移往 vt. 使移居；使移植 时态: migrated, migrating, migrates (研六托雅 6504/7939)","People migrate to cities like Jakarta in search of work...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move from one part of the world to another according to the season","example":"Swallows migrate south in winter."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move from one town, country, etc. to go and live and/or work in another","example":"Thousands were forced to migrate from rural to urban areas in search of work."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to move from one place to another","example":"The infected cells then migrate to other areas of the body."}]],["modify","/ˈmɒdɪfaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “modify”.","modify [ˈmɒdɪfaɪ] -2 vt. 修改，修饰；更改 vi. 修改 时态: modified, modifying, modifies (研四六托雅宝 3685/3239)","欧陆词典释义：modify [ˈmɒdɪfaɪ] -2 vt. 修改，修饰；更改 vi. 修改 时态: modified, modifying, modifies (研四六托雅宝 3685/3239)","The club members did agree to modify their recruitment policy...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change something slightly, especially in order to make it more suitable for a particular purpose","example":"The software we use has been modified for us."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something less extreme","example":"Patients are taught how to modify their diet."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a word, such as an adjective or adverb, that modifies","example":"We found it cheaper to modify existing equipment rather than buy new."}]],["mutual","/ˈmju:tʃuəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mutual”.","mutual [ˈmju:tʃuəl] -3 adj. 共同的；相互的，彼此的 (研四六托雅 2799/3301)","欧陆词典释义：mutual [ˈmju:tʃuəl] -3 adj. 共同的；相互的，彼此的 (研四六托雅 2799/3301)","The East and the West can work together for their mutual benefit and progress...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used to describe feelings that two or more people have for each other equally, or actions that affect two or more people equally","example":"mutual respect/understanding"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"shared by two or more people","example":"mutual support/aid"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"They parted by mutual consent."}]],["notwithstanding","/ˌnɒtwɪθˈstændɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “notwithstanding”.","notwithstanding [ˌnɒtwɪθˈstændɪŋ] -1 adv. 尽管，仍然 prep. 尽管，虽然 conj. 虽然 (研六托 10393/9042)","欧陆词典释义：notwithstanding [ˌnɒtwɪθˈstændɪŋ] -1 adv. 尽管，仍然 prep. 尽管，虽然 conj. 虽然 (研六托 10393/9042)","He despised William Pitt, notwithstanding the similar views they both held.",[{"pos":"preposition","definition":"without being affected by something; despite something","example":"Notwithstanding some major financial problems, the school has had a successful year."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The bad weather notwithstanding, the event was a great success."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"despite this","example":"Notwithstanding, the problem is a significant one."}]],["offset","/ˈɒfset/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “offset”.","offset [ˈɒfset] -2 n. 抵消，补偿；平版印刷；支管 vt. 抵消；弥补；用平版印刷术印刷 vi. 装支管 时态: offset, offsetting, offsets (研六雅宝 6179/5701)","欧陆词典释义：offset [ˈɒfset] -2 n. 抵消，补偿；平版印刷；支管 vt. 抵消；弥补；用平版印刷术印刷 vi. 装支管 时态: offset, offsetting, offsets (研六雅宝 6179/5701)","The increase in pay costs was more than offset by higher productivity...",""],["persist","/pəˈsɪst/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “persist”.","persist [pəˈsɪst] -2 vi. 存留，坚持；持续，固执 vt. 坚持说，反复说 时态: persisted, persisting, persists (研四六托雅 4351/3785)","欧陆词典释义：persist [pəˈsɪst] -2 vi. 存留，坚持；持续，固执 vt. 坚持说，反复说 时态: persisted, persisting, persists (研四六托雅 4351/3785)","Contact your doctor if the cough persist s...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to continue to do something despite difficulties or opposition, in a way that can seem unreasonable","example":"Why do you persist in blaming yourself for what happened?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to continue to exist","example":"She persisted in her search for the truth."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 16th cent.","example":"He persisted with his questioning."}]],["prerequisite","/ˌpri:ˈrekwəzɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “prerequisite”.","prerequisite [ˌpri:ˈrekwəzɪt] -1 n. 先决条件 adj. 首要必备的 (六托宝 11079/10265)","欧陆词典释义：prerequisite [ˌpri:ˈrekwəzɪt] -1 n. 先决条件 adj. 首要必备的 (六托宝 11079/10265)","Good self-esteem is a prerequisite for a happy life...",""],["protocol","/ˈprəʊtəkɒl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “protocol”.","protocol [ˈprəʊtəkɒl] -1 n. 协议；草案；礼仪 vt. 拟定 vi. 拟定 (雅宝 4485/4615)","欧陆词典释义：protocol [ˈprəʊtəkɒl] -1 n. 协议；草案；礼仪 vt. 拟定 vi. 拟定 (雅宝 4485/4615)","He has become something of a stickler for the finer observances of royal protocol .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a system of fixed rules and formal behaviour used at official meetings, usually between governments","example":"a breach of protocol"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the first or original version of an agreement, especially a treaty","example":"the protocol of diplomatic visits"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a set of rules that control the way data is sent between computers","example":"the first Geneva Protocol"}]],["qualitative","/ˈkwɒlɪtətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “qualitative”.","qualitative [ˈkwɒlɪtətɪv] -1 adj. 定性的；质的，性质上的 (研六雅 7101/8234)","欧陆词典释义：qualitative [ˈkwɒlɪtətɪv] -1 adj. 定性的；质的，性质上的 (研六雅 7101/8234)","There are qualitative differences in the way children and adults think...",""],["quantify","/ˈkwɒntɪfaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “quantify”.","quantify [ˈkwɒntɪfaɪ] -1 vt. 量化；为…定量；确定数量 vi. 量化；定量 时态: quantified, quantifying, quantifies (研六 9701/8904)","欧陆词典释义：quantify [ˈkwɒntɪfaɪ] -1 vt. 量化；为…定量；确定数量 vi. 量化；定量 时态: quantified, quantifying, quantifies (研六 9701/8904)","It is difficult to quantify an exact figure as firms are reluctant to declare their losses.",""],["reciprocal","/rɪˈsɪprəkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “reciprocal”.","reciprocal [rɪˈsɪprəkl] -1 n. [数] 倒数；互相起作用的事物 adj. 互惠的；相互的；倒数的，彼此相反的 (研六托雅宝 10639/8842)","欧陆词典释义：reciprocal [rɪˈsɪprəkl] -1 n. [数] 倒数；互相起作用的事物 adj. 互惠的；相互的；倒数的，彼此相反的 (研六托雅宝 10639/8842)","They expected a reciprocal gesture before more hostages could be freed...",""],["refine","/rɪˈfaɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “refine”.","refine [rɪˈfaɪn] -1 vt. 精炼，提纯；改善；使…文雅 时态: refined, refining, refines (研四六托雅 6600/7830)","欧陆词典释义：refine [rɪˈfaɪn] -1 vt. 精炼，提纯；改善；使…文雅 时态: refined, refining, refines (研四六托雅 6600/7830)","Oil is refine d to remove naturally occurring impurities.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make a substance pure by taking other substances out of it","example":"the process of refining oil/sugar"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to improve something by making small changes to it","example":"She has refined her playing technique over the years."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"This theory still needs a little refining."}]],["revise","/rɪˈvaɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “revise”.","revise [rɪˈvaɪz] -K2 n. 修订；校订 vi. 修订；校订；复习功课 vt. 修正；复习；校订 n. (Revise)人名；(法)勒维斯 时态: revised, revising, revises (研四六托雅宝 5829/4941)","欧陆词典释义：revise [rɪˈvaɪz] -K2 n. 修订；校订 vi. 修订；校订；复习功课 vt. 修正；复习；校订 n. (Revise)人名；(法)勒维斯 时态: revised, revising, revises (研四六托雅宝 5829/4941)","He soon came to revise his opinion of the profession.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change your opinions or plans, for example because of something you have learned","example":"I can see I will have to revise my opinions of his abilities now."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change something, such as a book or an estimate, in order to correct or improve it","example":"The government may need to revise its policy in the light of this report."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to prepare for an exam by looking again at work that you have done","example":"a revised edition of a textbook"}]],["simulate","/ˈsɪmjuleɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “simulate”.","simulate [ˈsɪmjuleɪt] -1 adj. 模仿的；假装的 vt. 模仿；假装；冒充 时态: simulated, simulating, simulates (研六托雅宝 7892/9883)","欧陆词典释义：simulate [ˈsɪmjuleɪt] -1 adj. 模仿的；假装的 vt. 模仿；假装；冒充 时态: simulated, simulating, simulates (研六托雅宝 7892/9883)","They rolled about on the Gilligan Road, simulating a bloodthirsty fight...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to pretend that you have a particular feeling","example":"I tried to simulate surprise at the news."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to create particular conditions that exist in real life using computers, models, etc., usually for study or training purposes","example":"Computer software can be used to simulate conditions on the seabed."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be made to look like something else","example":"Role-playing is a useful way of simulating real-life situations."}]],["solely","/ˈsəʊlli/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “solely”.","solely [ˈsəʊlli] adv. 单独地，唯一地 (四六托 4671/3992)","欧陆词典释义：solely [ˈsəʊlli] adv. 单独地，唯一地 (四六托 4671/3992)","Too often we make decisions based solely upon what we see in the magazines...",""],["supplement","/ˈsʌplɪmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “supplement”.","supplement [ˈsʌplɪmənt] -2 vt. 增补，补充 n. 增补，补充；补充物；增刊，副刊 时态: supplemented, supplementing, supplements (研四六托宝 5192/4371)","欧陆词典释义：supplement [ˈsʌplɪmənt] -2 vt. 增补，补充 n. 增补，补充；补充物；增刊，副刊 时态: supplemented, supplementing, supplements (研四六托宝 5192/4371)","people doing extra jobs outside their regular jobs to supplement their incomes...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that is added to something else to improve or complete it","example":"vitamin/dietary supplements"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an extra separate section, often in the form of a magazine, that is sold with a newspaper","example":"Industrial sponsorship is a supplement to government funding."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a book or a section at the end of a book that gives extra information or deals with a special subject","example":"the Sunday colour supplements"}]],["undergo","/ˌʌndəˈgəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “undergo”.","undergo [ˌʌndəˈgəʊ] -2 vt. 经历，经受；忍受 时态: underwent, undergone, undergoing, undergoes (研四六托雅 3141/3059)","欧陆词典释义：undergo [ˌʌndəˈgəʊ] -2 vt. 经历，经受；忍受 时态: underwent, undergone, undergoing, undergoes (研四六托雅 3141/3059)","New recruits have been undergo ing training in recent weeks...",""],["utilize","/ˈju:təlaɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “utilize”.","utilize [ˈju:təlaɪz] -2 vt. 利用 时态: utilized, utilizing, utilizes (研四六托宝 4264/10147)","欧陆词典释义：utilize [ˈju:təlaɪz] -2 vt. 利用 时态: utilized, utilizing, utilizes (研四六托宝 4264/10147)","Sound engineers utilize a range of techniques to enhance the quality of the recordings...",""],["vary","/ˈveəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “vary”.","vary [ˈveəri] -K3 vi. 变化；变异；违反 vt. 改变；使多样化；变奏 n. (Vary)人名；(英、法、罗、柬)瓦里 时态: varied, varying, varies (研四六托雅 2371/1510)","欧陆词典释义：vary [ˈveəri] -K3 vi. 变化；变异；违反 vt. 改变；使多样化；变奏 n. (Vary)人名；(英、法、罗、柬)瓦里 时态: varied, varying, varies (研四六托雅 2371/1510)","As they're handmade, each one varies slightly...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be different from each other in size, shape, etc.","example":"The students' work varies considerably in quality."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change or be different according to the situation","example":"The quality of the students' work varies considerably."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make changes to something to make it slightly different","example":"New techniques were introduced with varying degrees of"}]],["virtually","/ˈvɜ:tʃuəli/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “virtually”.","virtually [ˈvɜ:tʃuəli] -K3 adv. 事实上，几乎；实质上 (研四六托雅 2046/2034)","欧陆词典释义：virtually [ˈvɜ:tʃuəli] -K3 adv. 事实上，几乎；实质上 (研四六托雅 2046/2034)","Virtually all cooking was done over coal-fired ranges...",""],["voluntary","/ˈvɒləntri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “voluntary”.","voluntary [ˈvɒləntri] -3 n. 志愿者；自愿行动 adj. 自愿的；志愿的；自发的；故意的 (高研四六托雅 4701/2263)","欧陆词典释义：voluntary [ˈvɒləntri] -3 n. 志愿者；自愿行动 adj. 自愿的；志愿的；自发的；故意的 (高研四六托雅 4701/2263)","Attention is drawn to a special voluntary course in Commercial French...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"done willingly, not because you are forced","example":"a voluntary agreement"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"done by people who choose to do it without being paid","example":"Attendance on the course is purely voluntary."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"doing a job without wanting to be paid for it","example":"to pay voluntary contributions"}]],["abundant","/əˈbʌndənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abundant”.","abundant [əˈbʌndənt] -1 adj. 丰富的；充裕的；盛产 (高研四托宝 6223/7823)","欧陆词典释义：abundant [əˈbʌndənt] -1 adj. 丰富的；充裕的；盛产 (高研四托宝 6223/7823)","There is an abundant supply of cheap labour...",""],["adverse","/ˈædvɜ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adverse”.","adverse [ˈædvɜ:s] -2 adj. 不利的；相反的；敌对的（名词adverseness，副词adversely） (研六托雅宝 6307/5120)","欧陆词典释义：adverse [ˈædvɜ:s] -2 adj. 不利的；相反的；敌对的（名词adverseness，副词adversely） (研六托雅宝 6307/5120)","The police said Mr Hadfield's decision would have no adverse effect on the progress of the investigation...",""],["albeit","/ˌɔ:lˈbi:ɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “albeit”.","albeit [ˌɔ:lˈbi:ɪt] -2 conj. 虽然；即使 (宝 6086/4587)","欧陆词典释义：albeit [ˌɔ:lˈbi:ɪt] -2 conj. 虽然；即使 (宝 6086/4587)","Charles's letter was indeed published, albeit in a somewhat abbreviated form.",""],["align","/əˈlaɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “align”.","align [əˈlaɪn] -2 vt. 使结盟；使成一行；匹配 vi. 排列；排成一行 时态: aligned, aligning, aligns (宝 5939/7857)","欧陆词典释义：align [əˈlaɪn] -2 vt. 使结盟；使成一行；匹配 vi. 排列；排成一行 时态: aligned, aligning, aligns (宝 5939/7857)","There are signs that the prime minister is align ing himself with the liberals...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to arrange something in the correct position, or to be in the correct position, in relation to something else, especially in a straight line","example":"Make sure the shelf is aligned with the top of the cupboard."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change something slightly so that it is in the correct relationship to something else","example":"The top and bottom line of each column on the page should align."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 17th cent.","example":"Domestic prices have been aligned with those in world markets."}]],["assemble","/əˈsembl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assemble”.","assemble [əˈsembl] -2 vt. 集合，聚集；装配；收集 vi. 集合，聚集 时态: assembled, assembling, assembles (研四六托雅宝 3557/3928)","欧陆词典释义：assemble [əˈsembl] -2 vt. 集合，聚集；装配；收集 vi. 集合，聚集 时态: assembled, assembling, assembles (研四六托雅宝 3557/3928)","There wasn't even a convenient place for students to assemble between classes...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to come together as a group; to bring people or things together as a group","example":"All the students were asked to assemble in the main hall."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to fit together all the separate parts of something, for example a piece of furniture","example":"She then addressed the assembled company"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"to assemble evidence/data"}]],["attain","/əˈteɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attain”.","attain [əˈteɪn] -1 n. 成就 vt. 达到，实现；获得；到达 vi. 达到；获得；到达 时态: attained, attaining, attains (高研四六托雅宝 5323/5042)","欧陆词典释义：attain [əˈteɪn] -1 n. 成就 vt. 达到，实现；获得；到达 vi. 达到；获得；到达 时态: attained, attaining, attains (高研四六托雅宝 5323/5042)","Jim is halfway to attain ing his pilot's licence.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to succeed in getting something, usually after a lot of effort","example":"Most of our students attained five ‘A’ grades in their exams."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to reach a particular age, level or condition","example":"We only consider applicants who have attained a high level of academic achievement."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"attain (a) degree/standard/level/proficiency/mastery"}]],["attribute","/əˈtrɪbju:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attribute”.","attribute [əˈtrɪbju:t] -2 n. 属性；特质 vt. 归属；把…归于 时态: attributed, attributing, attributes (研四六托雅宝 3346/3247)","欧陆词典释义：attribute [əˈtrɪbju:t] -2 n. 属性；特质 vt. 归属；把…归于 时态: attributed, attributing, attributes (研四六托雅宝 3346/3247)","Women tend to attribute their success to external causes such as luck.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to say or believe that something is the result of a particular thing","example":"She attributes her success to hard work and a little luck."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to say or believe that somebody is responsible for doing something, especially for saying, writing or painting something","example":"The committee refused to attribute blame"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"This play is usually attributed to Shakespeare."}]],["clause","/klɔ:z/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “clause”.","clause [klɔ:z] -2 n. 条款；[计] 子句 n. (Clause)人名；(法)克洛斯 (研托雅宝 6415/1871)","欧陆词典释义：clause [klɔ:z] -2 n. 条款；[计] 子句 n. (Clause)人名；(法)克洛斯 (研托雅宝 6415/1871)","He has a clause in his contract which entitles him to a percentage of the profits.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of words that includes a subject and a verb, and forms a sentence or part of a sentence","example":"In the sentence ‘They often go to Italy because they love the food’, ‘They often go to Italy’ is the main clause and ‘because they love the food’ is a subordinate clause."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an item in a legal document that says that a particular thing must or must not be done","example":"There is a clause in the contract forbidding tenants to sublet."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"The contract contains a confidentiality clause."}]],["coincide","/ˌkəʊɪnˈsaɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coincide”.","coincide [ˌkəʊɪnˈsaɪd] -2 vi. 一致，符合；同时发生 vi. (在性格、品质等方面)完全一致，相符 时态: coincided, coinciding, coincides (研六托雅宝 6656/4134)","欧陆词典释义：coincide [ˌkəʊɪnˈsaɪd] -2 vi. 一致，符合；同时发生 vi. (在性格、品质等方面)完全一致，相符 时态: coincided, coinciding, coincides (研六托雅宝 6656/4134)","The exhibition coincide s with the 50th anniversary of his death...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take place at the same time","example":"It's a pity our trips to New York don't coincide."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be the same or very similar","example":"The strike was timed to coincide with the party conference."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to meet; to share the same space","example":"The interests of employers and employees do not always coincide."}]],["compatible","/kəmˈpætəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compatible”.","compatible [kəmˈpætəbl] -2 adj. 兼容的；能共处的；可并立的 (研六托雅宝 7017/5142)","欧陆词典释义：compatible [kəmˈpætəbl] -2 adj. 兼容的；能共处的；可并立的 (研六托雅宝 7017/5142)","Free enterprise, he argued, was compatible with Russian values and traditions...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"able to be used together","example":"The new system will be compatible with existing equipment."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"able to exist or be used together without causing problems","example":"three different, yet entirely compatible programs"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"if two people are compatible","example":"Are measures to protect the environment compatible with economic growth?"}]],["complement","/ˈkɒmplɪment/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “complement”.","complement [ˈkɒmplɪment] -2 n. 补语；余角；补足物 vt. 补足，补助 时态: complemented, complementing, complements (研六托雅 6760/5703)","欧陆词典释义：complement [ˈkɒmplɪment] -2 n. 补语；余角；补足物 vt. 补足，补助 时态: complemented, complementing, complements (研六托雅 6760/5703)","Nutmeg, parsley and cider all complement the flavour of these beans well.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to add to something in a way that improves it or makes it more attractive","example":"The excellent menu is complemented by a good wine list."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The team needs players who complement each other"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that adds new qualities to something in a way that improves it or makes it more attractive","example":"The dishes on the menu complement each other perfectly."}]],["comply","/kəmˈplaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “comply”.","comply [kəmˈplaɪ] -2 vi. 遵守；顺从，遵从；答应 时态: complied, complying, complies (研六托雅宝 4637/3441)","欧陆词典释义：comply [kəmˈplaɪ] -2 vi. 遵守；顺从，遵从；答应 时态: complied, complying, complies (研六托雅宝 4637/3441)","The commander said that the army would comply with the ceasefire...",""],["conceive","/kənˈsi:v/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conceive”.","conceive [kənˈsi:v] -2 vi. 怀孕；设想；考虑 vt. 怀孕；构思；以为；持有 时态: conceived, conceiving, conceives (研六托雅宝 4169/3806)","欧陆词典释义：conceive [kənˈsi:v] -2 vi. 怀孕；设想；考虑 vt. 怀孕；构思；以为；持有 时态: conceived, conceiving, conceives (研六托雅宝 4169/3806)","I just can't even conceive of that quantity of money...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to form an idea, a plan, etc. in your mind; to imagine something","example":"He conceived the idea of transforming the old power station into an arts centre."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"when a woman conceives","example":"God is often conceived of as male."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"I cannot conceive ("}]],["concurrent","/kənˈkʌrənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “concurrent”.","concurrent [kənˈkʌrənt] -1 n. [数] 共点；同时发生的事件 adj. 并发的；一致的；同时发生的 (托 12234/10520)","欧陆词典释义：concurrent [kənˈkʌrənt] -1 n. [数] 共点；同时发生的事件 adj. 并发的；一致的；同时发生的 (托 12234/10520)","Galerie St. Etienne is holding three concurrent exhibitions...",""],["confer","/kənˈfɜ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “confer”.","confer [kənˈfɜ:(r)] -1 vt. 授予；给予 vi. 协商 n. (Confer)人名；(英)康弗 时态: conferred, conferring, confers (研六托雅宝 7144/4769)","欧陆词典释义：confer [kənˈfɜ:(r)] -1 vt. 授予；给予 vi. 协商 n. (Confer)人名；(英)康弗 时态: conferred, conferring, confers (研六托雅宝 7144/4769)","He confer red with Hill and the others in his office...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to discuss something with somebody, in order to exchange opinions or get advice","example":"He wanted to confer with his colleagues before reaching a decision."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give somebody an award, a university degree or a particular honour or right","example":"An honorary degree was conferred on him by Oxford University in 2009."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"He wanted to confer with his colleagues before reaching a decision."}]],["conform","/kənˈfɔ:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conform”.","conform [kənˈfɔ:m] -2 adj. 一致的；顺从的 vi. 符合；遵照；适应环境 vt. 使遵守；使一致；使顺从 时态: conformed, conforming, conforms (研六托雅宝 6957/4792)","欧陆词典释义：conform [kənˈfɔ:m] -2 adj. 一致的；顺从的 vi. 符合；遵照；适应环境 vt. 使遵守；使一致；使顺从 时态: conformed, conforming, conforms (研六托雅宝 6957/4792)","The Night Rider lamp has been designed to conform to new British Standard safety requirements...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to behave and think in the same way as most other people in a group or society","example":"There is considerable pressure on teenagers to conform."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to obey a rule, law, etc.","example":"He refused to conform to the local customs."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to agree with or match something","example":"The building does not conform with safety regulations."}]],["consensus","/kənˈsensəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consensus”.","consensus [kənˈsensəs] -2 n. 一致；舆论；合意 (高研六托雅宝 3317/3897)","欧陆词典释义：consensus [kənˈsensəs] -2 n. 一致；舆论；合意 (高研六托雅宝 3317/3897)","The consensus amongst the world's scientists is that the world is likely to warm up over the next few decades...",""],["consequent","/ˈkɒnsɪkwənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consequent”.","consequent [ˈkɒnsɪkwənt] -1 n. 结果 adj. 随之发生的；作为结果的 (六托雅 14817/6594)","欧陆词典释义：consequent [ˈkɒnsɪkwənt] -1 n. 结果 adj. 随之发生的；作为结果的 (六托雅 14817/6594)","The warming of the Earth and the consequent climatic changes affect us all...",""],["counterpart","/ˈkaʊntəpɑ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “counterpart”.","counterpart [ˈkaʊntəpɑ:t] -3 n. 副本；配对物；极相似的人或物 (研六托雅宝 3816/4029)","欧陆词典释义：counterpart [ˈkaʊntəpɑ:t] -3 n. 副本；配对物；极相似的人或物 (研六托雅宝 3816/4029)","The Foreign Secretary telephoned his Italian counterpart to protest.",""],["deduce","/dɪˈdju:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deduce”.","deduce [dɪˈdju:s] -1 vt. 推论，推断；演绎出 时态: deduced, deducing, deduces (研四六雅宝 13290/7733)","欧陆词典释义：deduce [dɪˈdju:s] -1 vt. 推论，推断；演绎出 时态: deduced, deducing, deduces (研四六雅宝 13290/7733)","Alison had cleverly deduce d that I was the author of the letter.",""],["deviate","/ˈdi:vieɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deviate”.","deviate [ˈdi:vieɪt] -1 vi. 脱离；越轨 vt. 使偏离 时态: deviated, deviating, deviates (研六托雅宝 13796/11974)","欧陆词典释义：deviate [ˈdi:vieɪt] -1 vi. 脱离；越轨 vt. 使偏离 时态: deviated, deviating, deviates (研六托雅宝 13796/11974)","They stopped you as soon as you deviate d from the script...",""],["discrete","/dɪˈskri:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “discrete”.","discrete [dɪˈskri:t] n. 分立元件；独立部件 adj. 离散的，不连续的 (六托雅宝 9847/9082)","欧陆词典释义：discrete [dɪˈskri:t] n. 分立元件；独立部件 adj. 离散的，不连续的 (六托雅宝 9847/9082)","instruction manuals that break down jobs into scores of discrete steps.",""],["dispose","/dɪˈspəʊz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dispose”.","dispose [dɪˈspəʊz] -2 n. 处置；性情 vi. 处理；安排；（能够）决定 vt. 处理；处置；安排 时态: disposed, disposing, disposes (研四六托雅宝 6900/4101)","欧陆词典释义：dispose [dɪˈspəʊz] -2 n. 处置；性情 vi. 处理；安排；（能够）决定 vt. 处理；处置；安排 时态: disposed, disposing, disposes (研四六托雅宝 6900/4101)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dispose”.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to arrange things or people in a particular way or position","example":"The visitors disposed themselves in a circle round the statue."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody behave in a particular way","example":"a drug that disposes the patient towards sleep"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The visitors disposed themselves in a circle round the statue."}]],["elicit","/iˈlɪsɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “elicit”.","elicit [iˈlɪsɪt] -1 vt. 抽出，引出；引起 时态: elicited, eliciting, elicits (六托雅宝 6680/7717)","欧陆词典释义：elicit [iˈlɪsɪt] -1 vt. 抽出，引出；引起 时态: elicited, eliciting, elicits (六托雅宝 6680/7717)","Mr Norris said he was hopeful that his request would elicit a positive response...",""],["finite","/ˈfaɪnaɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “finite”.","finite [ˈfaɪnaɪt] -1 n. 有限之物 adj. 有限的；限定的 (研六雅宝 9670/8060)","欧陆词典释义：finite [ˈfaɪnaɪt] -1 n. 有限之物 adj. 有限的；限定的 (研六雅宝 9670/8060)","a finite set of elements...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having a definite limit or fixed size","example":"a finite number of possibilities"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a finite","example":"The world's resources are finite."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"‘Am’, ‘is’, ‘are’, ‘was’ and ‘were’ are the finite forms of ‘be’; ‘being’ and ‘been’ are the non-finite forms."}]],["forthcoming","/ˌfɔ:θˈkʌmɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “forthcoming”.","forthcoming [ˌfɔ:θˈkʌmɪŋ] -2 n. 来临 adj. 即将来临的 (研六雅 6748/4117)","欧陆词典释义：forthcoming [ˌfɔ:θˈkʌmɪŋ] -2 n. 来临 adj. 即将来临的 (研六雅 6748/4117)","his opponents in the forthcoming elections.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"going to happen, be published, etc. very soon","example":"the forthcoming elections"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"ready or made available when needed","example":"a list of forthcoming books"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"willing to give information about something","example":"the band’s forthcoming UK tour"}]],["furthermore","/ˌfɜ:ðəˈmɔ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “furthermore”.","furthermore [ˌfɜ:ðəˈmɔ:(r)] -2 adv. 此外；而且 (研四六 3213/2799)","欧陆词典释义：furthermore [ˌfɜ:ðəˈmɔ:(r)] -2 adv. 此外；而且 (研四六 3213/2799)","Furthermore, they claim that any such interference is completely ineffective.",""],["hence","/hens/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hence”.","hence [hens] -K2 adv. 因此；今后 (研四六托雅 3639/1904)","欧陆词典释义：hence [hens] -K2 adv. 因此；今后 (研四六托雅 3639/1904)","The trade imbalance is likely to rise again in 1990. Hence a new set of policy actions will be required soon...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"for this reason","example":"We suspect they are trying to hide something, hence the need for an independent inquiry."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"Middle English","example":"Today’s children eat more junk food and get less exercise than previous generations of children. It is not surprising, therefore"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"Old English","example":"Children who grow up on a diet of junk food find it difficult to change this habit later in life. It is essential, therefore"}]],["incidence","/ˈɪnsɪdəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “incidence”.","incidence [ˈɪnsɪdəns] -1 n. 发生率；影响；[光] 入射；影响范围 (研六托雅宝 5847/3906)","欧陆词典释义：incidence [ˈɪnsɪdəns] -1 n. 发生率；影响；[光] 入射；影响范围 (研六托雅宝 5847/3906)","The incidence of breast cancer increases with age.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the extent to which something happens or has an effect","example":"an area with a high incidence"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way in which light meets a surface","example":"the angle of incidence"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The country had the lowest incidence of AIDS cases proportional to its population."}]],["infer","/ɪnˈfɜ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “infer”.","infer [ɪnˈfɜ:(r)] -1 vi. 推断；作出推论 vt. 推断；推论 时态: inferred, inferring, infers (研四六托宝 9219/7194)","欧陆词典释义：infer [ɪnˈfɜ:(r)] -1 vi. 推断；作出推论 vt. 推断；推论 时态: inferred, inferring, infers (研四六托宝 9219/7194)","I infer red from what she said that you have not been well...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to reach an opinion or decide that something is true on the basis of information that is available","example":"Much of the meaning must be inferred from the context."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to suggest indirectly that something is true","example":"Readers are left to infer the killer’s motives."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"It is reasonable to infer that the government knew about these deals."}]],["innovate","/ˈɪnəveɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “innovate”.","innovate [ˈɪnəveɪt] vi. 创新；改革；革新 vt. 改变；创立；创始；引人 时态: innovated, innovating, innovates (研 18968/20988)","欧陆词典释义：innovate [ˈɪnəveɪt] vi. 创新；改革；革新 vt. 改变；创立；创始；引人 时态: innovated, innovating, innovates (研 18968/20988)","his constant desire to innovate and experiment.",""],["intermediate","/ˌɪntəˈmi:diət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “intermediate”.","intermediate [ˌɪntəˈmi:diət] -2 n. [化学] 中间物；媒介 adj. 中间的，中级的 vi. 起媒介作用 (研四六托雅 6876/4864)","欧陆词典释义：intermediate [ˌɪntəˈmi:diət] -2 n. [化学] 中间物；媒介 adj. 中间的，中级的 vi. 起媒介作用 (研四六托雅 6876/4864)","You should consider breaking the journey with intermediate stopovers at airport hotels.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"located between two places, things, states, etc.","example":"an intermediate stage/step"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"having more than a basic knowledge of something but not yet advanced; suitable for somebody who is at this level","example":"Liquid crystals are considered to be intermediate between liquid and solid."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"an intermediate skier/student, etc."}]],["likewise","/ˈlaɪkwaɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “likewise”.","likewise [ˈlaɪkwaɪz] -2 adv. 同样地；也 (研四六托雅 4530/5011)","欧陆词典释义：likewise [ˈlaɪkwaɪz] -2 adv. 同样地；也 (研四六托雅 4530/5011)","These requests are ignored. His requests for rent are likewise sometimes ignored...",[{"pos":"adverb","definition":"the same; in a similar way","example":"He voted for the change and he expected his colleagues to do likewise"},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"also","example":"Her second marriage was likewise unhappy."},{"pos":"adverb","definition":"used to show that you feel the same towards somebody or about something","example":"‘Let me know if you ever need any help.’ ‘Likewise.’"}]],["mature","/məˈtʃʊə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mature”.","mature [məˈtʃʊə(r)] -2 adj. 成熟的；充分考虑的；到期的；成年人的 vi. 成熟；到期 vt. 使…成熟；使…长成；慎重作出 时态: matured, maturing, matures 级别: maturer, maturest (高研四六托雅宝 5133/4122)","欧陆词典释义：mature [məˈtʃʊə(r)] -2 adj. 成熟的；充分考虑的；到期的；成年人的 vi. 成熟；到期 vt. 使…成熟；使…长成；慎重作出 时态: matured, maturing, matures 级别: maturer, maturest (高研四六托雅宝 5133/4122)","You will learn what to expect as your child mature s physically...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"behaving in a sensible way, like an adult","example":"Jane is very mature for her age."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"fully grown and developed","example":"a mature and sensible attitude"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"developed over a period of time to produce a strong, rich flavour","example":"sexually mature"}]],["nevertheless","/ˌnevəðəˈles/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “nevertheless”.","nevertheless [ˌnevəðəˈles] -K3 adv. 然而，不过；虽然如此 conj. 然而，不过 (研四六雅 2582/1337)","欧陆词典释义：nevertheless [ˌnevəðəˈles] -K3 adv. 然而，不过；虽然如此 conj. 然而，不过 (研四六雅 2582/1337)","Most marriages fail after between five and nine years. Nevertheless, people continue to get married.",""],["pursue","/pəˈsju:/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “pursue”.","pursue [pəˈsju:] -K3 vi. 追赶；继续进行 vt. 继续；从事；追赶；纠缠 时态: pursued, pursuing, pursues (研四六托宝 1785/1976)","欧陆词典释义：pursue [pəˈsju:] -K3 vi. 追赶；继续进行 vt. 继续；从事；追赶；纠缠 时态: pursued, pursuing, pursues (研四六托宝 1785/1976)","It became harder for women married to diplomats to pursue their own interests...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to do something or try to achieve something over a period of time","example":"to pursue a goal/an aim/an objective"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to continue to discuss, find out about or be involved in something","example":"We intend to pursue this policy with determination."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to follow or chase somebody/something, especially in order to catch them","example":"She wishes to pursue a medical career."}]],["retain","/rɪˈteɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “retain”.","retain [rɪˈteɪn] -K3 vt. 保持；雇；记住 时态: retained, retaining, retains (研四六托雅宝 2724/1460)","欧陆词典释义：retain [rɪˈteɪn] -K3 vt. 保持；雇；记住 时态: retained, retaining, retains (研四六托雅宝 2724/1460)","The interior of the shop still retain s a nineteenth-century atmosphere...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to keep something; to continue to have something","example":"to retain your independence"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to continue to hold or contain something","example":"He struggled to retain control of the situation."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"if a member of the public retains","example":"The house retains much of its original charm."}]],["subordinate","/səˈbɔ:dɪnət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “subordinate”.","subordinate [səˈbɔ:dɪnət] -2 n. 下属，下级；部属，属下 adj. 从属的；次要的 vt. 使……居下位；使……服从 时态: subordinated, subordinating, subordinates (研六托雅 9779/6201)","欧陆词典释义：subordinate [səˈbɔ:dɪnət] -2 n. 下属，下级；部属，属下 adj. 从属的；次要的 vt. 使……居下位；使……服从 时态: subordinated, subordinating, subordinates (研六托雅 9779/6201)","Haig tended not to seek guidance from subordinate s...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having less power or authority than somebody else in a group or an organization","example":"In many societies women are subordinate to men."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"less important than something else","example":"She was directly subordinate to the president."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The monarch is formally subordinate to Parliament."}]],["succession","/səkˈseʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “succession”.","succession [səkˈseʃn] -2 n. 连续；继位；继承权；[生态] 演替 (研四六雅 6389/3702)","欧陆词典释义：succession [səkˈseʃn] -2 n. 连续；继位；继承权；[生态] 演替 (研四六雅 6389/3702)","Adams took a succession of jobs which have stood him in good stead...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a number of people or things that follow each other in time or order","example":"a succession of visitors"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the regular pattern of one thing following another thing","example":"He's been hit by a succession of injuries since he joined the team."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of taking over an official position or title; the right to take over an official position or title, especially to become the king or queen of a country","example":"She has won the award for the third year in succession"}]],["thereby","/ˌðeəˈbaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “thereby”.","thereby [ˌðeəˈbaɪ] -2 adv. 从而，因此；在那附近；在那方面 (研四六托雅 3891/2910)","欧陆词典释义：thereby [ˌðeəˈbaɪ] -2 adv. 从而，因此；在那附近；在那方面 (研四六托雅 3891/2910)","Our bodies can sweat, thereby losing heat by evaporation...",""],["ultimate","/ˈʌltɪmət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ultimate”.","ultimate [ˈʌltɪmət] -K3 n. 终极；根本；基本原则 adj. 最终的；极限的；根本的 (研四六托宝 2601/3002)","欧陆词典释义：ultimate [ˈʌltɪmət] -K3 n. 终极；根本；基本原则 adj. 最终的；极限的；根本的 (研四六托宝 2601/3002)","He said it is still not possible to predict the ultimate outcome...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"happening at the end of a long process","example":"our ultimate goal/aim/objective/target"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"most extreme; best, worst, greatest, most important, etc.","example":"We will accept ultimate responsibility for whatever happens."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"from which something originally comes","example":"The ultimate decision lies with the parents."}]],["uniform","/ˈju:nɪfɔ:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “uniform”.","uniform [ˈju:nɪfɔ:m] -K3 n. 制服 adj. 统一的；一致的；相同的；均衡的；始终如一的 vt. 使穿制服；使成一样 时态: uniformed, uniforming, uniforms (高研四六托雅宝 3043/3504)","欧陆词典释义：uniform [ˈju:nɪfɔ:m] -K3 n. 制服 adj. 统一的；一致的；相同的；均衡的；始终如一的 vt. 使穿制服；使成一样 时态: uniformed, uniforming, uniforms (高研四六托雅宝 3043/3504)","The town police wear dark blue uniform s and flat caps...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the special set of clothes worn by all members of an organization or a group at work, or by children at school","example":"a military/police/nurse’s uniform"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the clothes worn by the members of a sports team when they are playing","example":"soldiers in uniform"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"the type of clothes that a person or group usually wears","example":"The hat is part of the school uniform"}]],["whereas","/ˌweərˈæz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “whereas”.","whereas [ˌweərˈæz] -K3 conj. 然而；鉴于；反之 (研四六托雅 2731/1524)","欧陆词典释义：whereas [ˌweərˈæz] -K3 conj. 然而；鉴于；反之 (研四六托雅 2731/1524)","Pensions are linked to inflation, whereas they should be linked to the cost of living...",""],["widespread","/ˈwaɪdspred/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “widespread”.","widespread [ˈwaɪdspred] -3 adj. 普遍的，广泛的；分布广的 (高研四六托 3282/2621)","欧陆词典释义：widespread [ˈwaɪdspred] -3 adj. 普遍的，广泛的；分布广的 (高研四六托 3282/2621)","There is widespread support for the new proposals...",""],["worthwhile","/ˌwɜ:θˈwaɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “worthwhile”.","worthwhile [ˌwɜ:θˈwaɪl] -2 adj. 值得做的，值得花时间的 (高研四六雅 6958/4264)","欧陆词典释义：worthwhile [ˌwɜ:θˈwaɪl] -2 adj. 值得做的，值得花时间的 (高研四六雅 6958/4264)","The President's trip to Washington this week seems to have been worthwhile ...",""],["coincidence","/kəʊˈɪnsɪdəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coincidence”.","coincidence [kəʊˈɪnsɪdəns] -2 n. 巧合；一致；同时发生 (高研六托雅 5812/5527)","欧陆词典释义：coincidence [kəʊˈɪnsɪdəns] -2 n. 巧合；一致；同时发生 (高研六托雅 5812/5527)","Mr. Berry said the timing was a coincidence and that his decision was unrelated to Mr. Roman's departure...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of two things happening at the same time by chance, in a surprising way","example":"a strange/an extraordinary/a remarkable coincidence"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of things being present at the same time","example":"What a coincidence!"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of two or more opinions, etc. being the same","example":"It's not a coincidence that"}]],["consecutive","/kənˈsekjətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consecutive”.","consecutive [kənˈsekjətɪv] -2 adj. 连贯的；连续不断的 (研六托雅 4845/7149)","欧陆词典释义：consecutive [kənˈsekjətɪv] -2 adj. 连贯的；连续不断的 (研六托雅 4845/7149)","The Cup was won for the third consecutive year by the Toronto Maple Leafs...",""],["criterion","/kraɪˈtɪəriən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “criterion”.","criterion [kraɪˈtɪəriən] -K2 n. （批评判断的）标准；准则；规范；准据 (高研六雅宝 -/1799)","欧陆词典释义：criterion [kraɪˈtɪəriən] -K2 n. （批评判断的）标准；准则；规范；准据 (高研六雅宝 -/1799)","The most important criterion for entry is that applicants must design and make their own work...",""],["diminish","/dɪˈmɪnɪʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “diminish”.","diminish [dɪˈmɪnɪʃ] -2 vt. 使减少；使变小 vi. 减少，缩小；变小 时态: diminished, diminishing, diminishes (研六托雅 3958/4526)","欧陆词典释义：diminish [dɪˈmɪnɪʃ] -2 vt. 使减少；使变小 vi. 减少，缩小；变小 时态: diminished, diminishing, diminishes (研六托雅 3958/4526)","The threat of nuclear war has diminish ed...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become or to make something become smaller, weaker, etc.","example":"The world's resources are rapidly diminishing."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody/something seem less important than they really are","example":"His influence has diminished with time."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Our efforts were producing diminishing returns"}]],["divert","/daɪˈvɜ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “divert”.","divert [daɪˈvɜ:t] -2 vt. 转移；使…欢娱；使…转向 vi. 转移 n. (Divert)人名；(法)迪韦尔 时态: diverted, diverting, diverts (研六托雅宝 5673/4924)","欧陆词典释义：divert [daɪˈvɜ:t] -2 vt. 转移；使…欢娱；使…转向 vi. 转移 n. (Divert)人名；(法)迪韦尔 时态: diverted, diverting, diverts (研六托雅宝 5673/4924)","Rainham Marshes, east London, where a new bypass will divert traffic from the A13...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody/something change direction","example":"Northbound traffic will have to be diverted onto minor roads."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to use money, materials, etc. for a different purpose from their original purpose","example":"The course of the stream has now been diverted."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take somebody’s thoughts or attention away from something","example":"The war diverted people's attention away from the economic situation."}]],["enrich","/ɪnˈrɪtʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “enrich”.","enrich [ɪnˈrɪtʃ] -1 vt. 使充实；使肥沃；使富足 n. (Enrich)人名；(西)恩里奇 时态: enriched, enriching, enriches (研六托雅 6879/8880)","欧陆词典释义：enrich [ɪnˈrɪtʃ] -1 vt. 使充实；使肥沃；使富足 n. (Enrich)人名；(西)恩里奇 时态: enriched, enriching, enriches (研六托雅 6879/8880)","An extended family enrich es life in many ways...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to improve the quality of something, often by adding something to it","example":"The study of science has enriched all our lives."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody/something rich or richer","example":"Most breakfast cereals are enriched with vitamins."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"a nation enriched by oil revenues"}]],["framework","/ˈfreɪmwɜ:k/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “framework”.","framework [ˈfreɪmwɜ:k] -2 n. 框架，骨架；结构，构架 (高研四六托雅 2968/2177)","欧陆词典释义：framework [ˈfreɪmwɜ:k] -2 n. 框架，骨架；结构，构架 (高研四六托雅 2968/2177)"," within the framework of federal regulations.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the parts of a building or an object that support its weight and give it shape","example":"built on a wooden/metal framework"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a set of beliefs, ideas or rules that is used as the basis for making judgements, decisions, etc.","example":"the structure of the building/​human body"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the structure of a particular system","example":"the social structure of society"}]],["hierarchy","/ˈhaɪərɑ:ki/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hierarchy”.","hierarchy [ˈhaɪərɑ:ki] -2 n. 层级；等级制度 (研六托雅宝 5206/3591)","欧陆词典释义：hierarchy [ˈhaɪərɑ:ki] -2 n. 层级；等级制度 (研六托雅宝 5206/3591)","Like most other American companies with a rigid hierarchy , workers and managers had strictly defined duties...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a system, especially in a society or an organization, in which people are organized into different levels of importance from highest to lowest","example":"the social/political hierarchy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the group of people in control of a large organization or institution","example":"She's quite high up in the management hierarchy."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a system that ideas or beliefs can be arranged into","example":"a hierarchy of needs"}]],["incline","/ɪnˈklaɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “incline”.","incline [ɪnˈklaɪn] -1 n. 倾斜；斜面；斜坡 vt. 使倾斜；使倾向于 vi. 倾斜；倾向；易于 时态: inclined, inclining, inclines (研四六雅 12701/12104)","欧陆词典释义：incline [ɪnˈklaɪn] -1 n. 倾斜；斜面；斜坡 vt. 使倾斜；使倾向于 vi. 倾斜；倾向；易于 时态: inclined, inclining, inclines (研四六雅 12701/12104)","I incline to the view that he is right.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to tend to think or behave in a particular way; to make somebody do this","example":"I incline to the view that we should take no action at this stage."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to bend your head forward, especially as a sign of agreement, welcome, etc.","example":"Young people incline towards individualistic behaviour."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to lean or slope in a particular direction; to make something lean or slope","example":"The government is more effective than we incline to think."}]],["incorporate","/ɪnˈkɔ:pəreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “incorporate”.","incorporate [ɪnˈkɔ:pəreɪt] -2 vt. 包含，吸收；体现；把……合并 adj. 合并的；一体化的；组成公司的 vi. 合并；混合；组成公司 时态: incorporated, incorporating, incorporates (研六托雅宝 2600/2095)","欧陆词典释义：incorporate [ɪnˈkɔ:pəreɪt] -2 vt. 包含，吸收；体现；把……合并 adj. 合并的；一体化的；组成公司的 vi. 合并；混合；组成公司 时态: incorporated, incorporating, incorporates (研六托雅宝 2600/2095)","The new cars will incorporate a number of major improvements.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to include something so that it forms a part of something","example":"The new car design incorporates all the latest safety features."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to create a legally recognized company","example":"We have incorporated all the latest safety features into the design."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Many of your suggestions have been incorporated in the plan."}]],["initial","/ɪˈnɪʃl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “initial”.","initial [ɪˈnɪʃl] -K3 n. 词首大写字母 adj. 最初的；字首的 vt. 用姓名的首字母签名 时态: initialled, initialling, initials (高研四六托雅宝 1943/1525)","欧陆词典释义：initial [ɪˈnɪʃl] -K3 n. 词首大写字母 adj. 最初的；字首的 vt. 用姓名的首字母签名 时态: initialled, initialling, initials (高研四六托雅宝 1943/1525)","The initial reaction has been excellent...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"happening at the beginning; first","example":"an initial payment of £60 and ten instalments of £25"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 16th cent.","example":"in the initial stages"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the first letter of a person’s first name","example":"My initial reaction"}]],["minimize","/ˈmɪnɪmaɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “minimize”.","minimize [ˈmɪnɪmaɪz] -2 vt. 使减到最少；小看，极度轻视 vi. 最小化 时态: minimized, minimizing, minimizes (研六托宝 3941/8977)","欧陆词典释义：minimize [ˈmɪnɪmaɪz] -2 vt. 使减到最少；小看，极度轻视 vi. 最小化 时态: minimized, minimizing, minimizes (研六托宝 3941/8977)","Concerned people want to minimize the risk of developing cancer...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to reduce something, especially something bad, to the lowest possible level","example":"Good hygiene helps to minimize the risk of infection."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to try to make something seem less important than it really is","example":"Costs were minimized by using plastic instead of leather."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something small, especially on a computer screen","example":"He always tried to minimize his own faults, while exaggerating those of others."}]],["norm","/nɔ:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “norm”.","norm [nɔ:m] -2 n. 标准，规范 (研六托雅宝 3387/3718)","欧陆词典释义：norm [nɔ:m] -2 n. 标准，规范 (研六托雅宝 3387/3718)","the commonly accepted norm s of democracy.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a situation or a pattern of behaviour that is usual or expected","example":"a departure from the norm"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"standards of behaviour that are typical of or accepted within a particular group or society","example":"Older parents seem to be the norm rather than the exception nowadays."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a required or agreed standard, amount, etc.","example":"social/cultural norms"}]],["precise","/prɪˈsaɪs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “precise”.","precise [prɪˈsaɪs] -K2 adj. 精确的；明确的；严格的 (高研四六托雅宝 3826/2761)","欧陆词典释义：precise [prɪˈsaɪs] -K2 adj. 精确的；明确的；严格的 (高研四六托雅宝 3826/2761)","I can remember the precise moment when my daughter came to see me and her new baby brother in hospital...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"clear and accurate","example":"precise details/instructions/measurements"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used to emphasize that something happens at a particular time or in a particular way","example":"Can you give a more precise definition of the word?"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"taking care to be exact and accurate, especially about small details","example":"I can be reasonably precise about the time of the incident."}]],["abolish","/əˈbɒlɪʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abolish”.","abolish [əˈbɒlɪʃ] -2 vt. 废除，废止；取消，革除 时态: abolished, abolishing, abolishes (高研六托雅宝 7490/3736)","欧陆词典释义：abolish [əˈbɒlɪʃ] -2 vt. 废除，废止；取消，革除 时态: abolished, abolishing, abolishes (高研六托雅宝 7490/3736)","The following year Parliament voted to abolish the death penalty for murder...",""],["absorption","/əbˈsɔ:pʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “absorption”.","absorption [əbˈsɔ:pʃn] n. 吸收；全神贯注，专心致志 (六托 8596/5819)","欧陆词典释义：absorption [əbˈsɔ:pʃn] n. 吸收；全神贯注，专心致志 (六托 8596/5819)","This controls the absorption of liquids...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of a liquid, gas or other substance being taken in","example":"Vitamin D is necessary to aid the absorption of calcium from food."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of a smaller group, country, etc. becoming part of a larger group or country","example":"the absorption of immigrants into the host country"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of somebody being very interested in something so that it takes all their attention","example":"His work suffered because of his total absorption in sport."}]],["accelerate","/əkˈseləreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accelerate”.","accelerate [əkˈseləreɪt] -2 vt. 使……加快；使……增速 vi. 加速；促进；增加 时态: accelerated, accelerating, accelerates (高研四六托雅宝 4925/5328)","欧陆词典释义：accelerate [əkˈseləreɪt] -2 vt. 使……加快；使……增速 vi. 加速；促进；增加 时态: accelerated, accelerating, accelerates (高研四六托雅宝 4925/5328)","Growth will accelerate to 2.9 per cent next year...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to happen or to make something happen faster or earlier than expected","example":"Inflation continues to accelerate."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to start to go faster","example":"Exposure to the sun can accelerate the ageing process."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"early 16th cent.","example":"The runners accelerated smoothly around the bend."}]],["accessible","/əkˈsesəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accessible”.","accessible [əkˈsesəbl] -2 adj. 易接近的；可进入的；可理解的 (高六托雅宝 4377/4162)","欧陆词典释义：accessible [əkˈsesəbl] -2 adj. 易接近的；可进入的；可理解的 (高六托雅宝 4377/4162)","The Centre is easily accessible to the general public...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that can be reached, entered, used, seen, etc.","example":"The remote desert area is accessible only by helicopter."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that can be reached, entered, used, etc. by somebody who has problems walking","example":"These documents are not accessible to the public."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"easy to understand","example":"accessible toilets for wheelchair users"}]],["accountable","/əˈkaʊntəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accountable”.","accountable [əˈkaʊntəbl] -2 adj. 有责任的；有解释义务的；可解释的 (5713/7192)","欧陆词典释义：accountable [əˈkaʊntəbl] -2 adj. 有责任的；有解释义务的；可解释的 (5713/7192)","Public officials can finally be held accountable for their actions...",""],["accumulate","/əˈkju:mjəleɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accumulate”.","accumulate [əˈkju:mjəleɪt] -2 vt. 积攒 vi. 累积；积聚 时态: accumulated, accumulating, accumulates (高研四六托雅宝 5083/4997)","欧陆词典释义：accumulate [əˈkju:mjəleɪt] -2 vt. 积攒 vi. 累积；积聚 时态: accumulated, accumulating, accumulates (高研四六托雅宝 5083/4997)","Households accumulate wealth across a broad spectrum of assets...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to gradually get more and more of something over a period of time","example":"I seem to have accumulated a lot of books."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to gradually increase in number or quantity over a period of time","example":"By investing wisely she accumulated a fortune."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"We have accumulated a great amount of evidence."}]],["accurate","/ˈækjərət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accurate”.","accurate [ˈækjərət] -K3 adj. 精确的 (研四六托雅宝 2728/2738)","欧陆词典释义：accurate [ˈækjərət] -K3 adj. 精确的 (研四六托雅宝 2728/2738)","Police have stressed that this is the most accurate description of the killer to date...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"correct and true in every detail","example":"an accurate description/account/calculation"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"able to give completely correct information or to do something in an exact way","example":"accurate information/data"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"an accurate","example":"Accurate records must be kept."}]],["adjacent","/əˈdʒeɪsnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adjacent”.","adjacent [əˈdʒeɪsnt] -1 adj. 邻近的，毗连的 (研六托雅宝 6649/5391)","欧陆词典释义：adjacent [əˈdʒeɪsnt] -1 adj. 邻近的，毗连的 (研六托雅宝 6649/5391)","He sat in an adjacent room and waited...",""],["alter","/ˈɔ:ltə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “alter”.","alter [ˈɔ:ltə(r)] -K3 vt. 改变，更改 vi. 改变；修改 n. (Alter)人名；(英)奥尔特；(德、捷、葡、爱沙、立陶、拉脱、俄、西、罗、瑞典)阿尔特 时态: altered, altering, alters (研四六托雅宝 2889/2121)","欧陆词典释义：alter [ˈɔ:ltə(r)] -K3 vt. 改变，更改 vi. 改变；修改 n. (Alter)人名；(英)奥尔特；(德、捷、葡、爱沙、立陶、拉脱、俄、西、罗、瑞典)阿尔特 时态: altered, altering, alters (研四六托雅宝 2889/2121)","Little had alter ed in the village...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become different; to make somebody/something different","example":"Prices did not alter significantly during 2014."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make changes to a piece of clothing so that it will fit you better","example":"He had altered so much I scarcely recognized him."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"It doesn't alter the way I feel."}]],["amend","/əˈmend/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “amend”.","amend [əˈmend] -2 vt. 修改；改善，改进 vi. 改正，改善；改过自新 n. (Amend)人名；(德、英)阿门德 时态: amended, amending, amends (研托雅宝 7371/4585)","欧陆词典释义：amend [əˈmend] -2 vt. 修改；改善，改进 vi. 改正，改善；改过自新 n. (Amend)人名；(德、英)阿门德 时态: amended, amending, amends (研托雅宝 7371/4585)","The president agreed to amend the constitution and allow multi-party elections...",""],["assurance","/əˈʃʊərəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assurance”.","assurance [əˈʃʊərəns] -2 n. 保证，担保；（人寿）保险；确信；断言；厚脸皮，无耻 (研六雅 5702/3133)","欧陆词典释义：assurance [əˈʃʊərəns] -2 n. 保证，担保；（人寿）保险；确信；断言；厚脸皮，无耻 (研六雅 5702/3133)","He would like an assurance that other forces will not move into the territory that his forces vacate...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a statement that something will certainly be true or will certainly happen, particularly when there has been doubt about it","example":"They called for assurances that the government is committed to its education policy."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"belief in your own abilities or strengths","example":"Unemployment seems to be rising, despite repeated assurances to the contrary"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a type of insurance in which money is paid out when somebody dies or after an agreed period of time","example":"There was an air of easy assurance and calm about him."}]],["bilateral","/ˌbaɪˈlætərəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bilateral”.","bilateral [ˌbaɪˈlætərəl] -2 adj. 双边的；有两边的 (托雅 6869/6801)","欧陆词典释义：bilateral [ˌbaɪˈlætərəl] -2 adj. 双边的；有两边的 (托雅 6869/6801)"," bilateral talks between Britain and America.",""],["cease","/si:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cease”.","cease [si:s] -K3 n. 停止 vi. 停止；终了 vt. 停止；结束 时态: ceased, ceasing, ceases (研四六托雅 4470/2679)","欧陆词典释义：cease [si:s] -K3 n. 停止 vi. 停止；终了 vt. 停止；结束 时态: ceased, ceasing, ceases (研四六托雅 4470/2679)","At one o'clock the rain had cease d.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to stop happening or existing; to stop something from happening or existing","example":"Welfare payments cease as soon as an individual starts a job."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"You never cease to amaze me!"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a phrase used to express surprise and pleasure at something","example":"They voted to cease strike action immediately."}]],["compel","/kəmˈpel/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compel”.","compel [kəmˈpel] -2 vt. 强迫，迫使；强使发生 n. (Compel)人名；(法)孔佩尔 时态: compelled, compelling, compels (研四六托雅宝 4449/4965)","欧陆词典释义：compel [kəmˈpel] -2 vt. 强迫，迫使；强使发生 n. (Compel)人名；(法)孔佩尔 时态: compelled, compelling, compels (研四六托雅宝 4449/4965)","the introduction of legislation to compel cyclists to wear a helmet...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to force somebody to do something; to make something necessary","example":"The law can compel fathers to make regular payments for their children."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to cause a particular reaction","example":"I feel compelled to"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The court has powers to compel witnesses to attend."}]],["competence","/ˈkɒmpɪtəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “competence”.","competence [ˈkɒmpɪtəns] -1 n. 能力，胜任；权限；作证能力；足以过舒适生活的收入 (高六托雅宝 5191/4201)","欧陆词典释义：competence [ˈkɒmpɪtəns] -1 n. 能力，胜任；权限；作证能力；足以过舒适生活的收入 (高六托雅宝 5191/4201)","His competence as an economist had been reinforced by his successful fight against inflation...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to do something well","example":"to gain a high level of competence in English"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the power that a court, an organization or a person has to deal with something","example":"professional/technical competence"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a skill that you need in a particular job or for a particular task","example":"The judge has to act within the competence of the court."}]],["comprise","/kəmˈpraɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “comprise”.","comprise [kəmˈpraɪz] -2 vt. 包含；由…组成 时态: comprised, comprising, comprises (研四六托雅 4392/2504)","欧陆词典释义：comprise [kəmˈpraɪz] -2 vt. 包含；由…组成 时态: comprised, comprising, comprises (研四六托雅 4392/2504)","The special cabinet committee comprise s Mr Brown, Mr Mandelson, and Mr Straw...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have somebody/something as parts or members","example":"The collection comprises 327 paintings."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be the parts or members that form something","example":"The committee is comprised of representatives from both the public and private sectors."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Older people comprise a large proportion of those living in poverty."}]],["convert","/kənˈvɜ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “convert”.","convert [kənˈvɜ:t] -K3 n. 皈依者；改变宗教信仰者 vt. 使转变；转换…；使…改变信仰 vi. 转变，变换；皈依；改变信仰 n. (Convert)人名；(法)孔韦尔 时态: converted, converting, converts (研四六托雅宝 2895/2245)","欧陆词典释义：convert [kənˈvɜ:t] -K3 n. 皈依者；改变宗教信仰者 vt. 使转变；转换…；使…改变信仰 vi. 转变，变换；皈依；改变信仰 n. (Convert)人名；(法)孔韦尔 时态: converted, converting, converts (研四六托雅宝 2895/2245)","The signal will be convert ed into digital code.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change or make something change from one form, purpose, system, etc. to another","example":"The hotel is going to be converted into a nursing home."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be able to be changed from one form, purpose, or system to another","example":"The pub is a converted warehouse."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to change or make somebody change their religion or beliefs","example":"What rate will I get if I convert my dollars into euros?"}]],["coordinate","/kəʊ'ɔ:dɪneɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coordinate”.","coordinate [kəʊ'ɔ:dɪneɪt] -2 n. 坐标；同等的人或物 vt. 调整；整合 adj. 并列的；同等的 vi. 协调 时态: coordinated, coordinating, coordinates (研四六托雅宝 4847/7991)","欧陆词典释义：coordinate [kəʊ'ɔ:dɪneɪt] -2 n. 坐标；同等的人或物 vt. 调整；整合 adj. 并列的；同等的 vi. 协调 时态: coordinated, coordinating, coordinates (研四六托雅宝 4847/7991)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coordinate”.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to organize the different parts of an activity and the people involved in it so that it works well","example":"They appointed a new manager to coordinate the work of the team."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to make the different parts of your body work well together","example":"We need to develop a coordinated approach to the problem."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"if you coordinate","example":"This shade coordinates with a wide range of other colours."}]],["controversy","/ˈkɒntrəvɜ:si/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “controversy”.","controversy [ˈkɒntrəvɜ:si] -3 n. 争论；论战；辩论 (研六托雅 2876/3460)","欧陆词典释义：controversy [ˈkɒntrəvɜ:si] -3 n. 争论；论战；辩论 (研六托雅 2876/3460)","The proposed cuts have caused considerable controversy .",""],["deduct","/dɪˈdʌkt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deduct”.","deduct [dɪˈdʌkt] -2 vt. 扣除，减去；演绎 时态: deducted, deducting, deducts (研六雅宝 11281/7941)","欧陆词典释义：deduct [dɪˈdʌkt] -2 vt. 扣除，减去；演绎 时态: deducted, deducting, deducts (研六雅宝 11281/7941)","The company deduct ed this payment from his compensation...",""],["detect","/dɪˈtekt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “detect”.","detect [dɪˈtekt] -2 vt. 察觉；发现；探测 时态: detected, detecting, detects (研四六托雅 2763/2502)","欧陆词典释义：detect [dɪˈtekt] -2 vt. 察觉；发现；探测 时态: detected, detecting, detects (研四六托雅 2763/2502)","a sensitive piece of equipment used to detect radiation...",""],["differentiate","/ˌdɪfəˈrenʃieɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “differentiate”.","differentiate [ˌdɪfəˈrenʃieɪt] -2 vt. 区分，区别 vi. 区分，区别 时态: differentiated, differentiating, differentiates (研托雅宝 6387/5138)","欧陆词典释义：differentiate [ˌdɪfəˈrenʃieɪt] -2 vt. 区分，区别 vi. 区分，区别 时态: differentiated, differentiating, differentiates (研托雅宝 6387/5138)","A child may not differentiate between his imagination and the real world...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to recognize or show that two things are not the same","example":"It's difficult to differentiate between the two varieties."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be the particular thing that shows that things or people are not the same","example":"I can't differentiate one variety from another."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to treat people or things in a different way, especially in an unfair way","example":"The male's yellow beak differentiates it from the female."}]],["encounter","/ɪnˈkaʊntə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “encounter”.","encounter [ɪnˈkaʊntə(r)] -K3 n. 遭遇，偶然碰见 vi. 遭遇；偶然相遇 vt. 遭遇，邂逅；遇到 时态: encountered, encountering, encounters (研四六托雅宝 2712/2892)","欧陆词典释义：encounter [ɪnˈkaʊntə(r)] -K3 n. 遭遇，偶然碰见 vi. 遭遇；偶然相遇 vt. 遭遇，邂逅；遇到 时态: encountered, encountering, encounters (研四六托雅宝 2712/2892)","Every day of our lives we encounter stresses of one kind or another...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to experience something, especially something unpleasant or difficult, while you are trying to do something else","example":"We encountered a number of difficulties in the first week."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to meet somebody, or discover or experience something, especially somebody/something new, unusual or unexpected","example":"I had never encountered such resistance before."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"She was the most remarkable woman he had ever encountered."}]],["entail","/ɪnˈteɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “entail”.","entail [ɪnˈteɪl] -1 vt. 使需要，必需；承担；遗传给；蕴含 n. 引起；需要；继承 时态: entailed, entailing, entails (研六托雅宝 6162/4558)","欧陆词典释义：entail [ɪnˈteɪl] -1 vt. 使需要，必需；承担；遗传给；蕴含 n. 引起；需要；继承 时态: entailed, entailing, entails (研六托雅宝 6162/4558)","Such a decision would entail a huge political risk...",""],["evident","/ˈevɪdənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “evident”.","evident [ˈevɪdənt] -2 adj. 明显的；明白的 (高研四六托 3466/2975)","欧陆词典释义：evident [ˈevɪdənt] -2 adj. 明显的；明白的 (高研四六托 3466/2975)","His footprints were clearly evident in the heavy dust...",""],["feasible","/ˈfi:zəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “feasible”.","feasible [ˈfi:zəbl] -1 adj. 可行的；可能的；可实行的 (研四六托雅宝 7591/6420)","欧陆词典释义：feasible [ˈfi:zəbl] -1 adj. 可行的；可能的；可实行的 (研四六托雅宝 7591/6420)","She questioned whether it was feasible to stimulate investment in these regions...",""],["incentive","/ɪnˈsentɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “incentive”.","incentive [ɪnˈsentɪv] -2 n. 动机；刺激 adj. 激励的；刺激的 (研六托雅宝 2726/3252)","欧陆词典释义：incentive [ɪnˈsentɪv] -2 n. 动机；刺激 adj. 激励的；刺激的 (研六托雅宝 2726/3252)","There is little or no incentive to adopt such measures...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that encourages you to do something","example":"There is no incentive for people to save fuel."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a payment or concession","example":"There is an added incentive for you to buy from our catalogue—a free gift with every purchase."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"tax incentives to encourage savings"}]],["initiate","/ɪˈnɪʃieɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “initiate”.","initiate [ɪˈnɪʃieɪt] -2 n. 开始；新加入者，接受初步知识者 vt. 开始，创始；发起；使初步了解 adj. 新加入的；接受初步知识的 时态: initiated, initiating, initiates (研六托雅宝 3524/3422)","欧陆词典释义：initiate [ɪˈnɪʃieɪt] -2 n. 开始；新加入者，接受初步知识者 vt. 开始，创始；发起；使初步了解 adj. 新加入的；接受初步知识的 时态: initiated, initiating, initiates (研六托雅宝 3524/3422)","They wanted to initiate a discussion on economics...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something begin","example":"to initiate legal proceedings against somebody"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to explain something to somebody and/or make them experience it for the first time","example":"The government has initiated a programme of economic reform."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to make somebody a member of a particular group, especially as part of a secret ceremony","example":"Many of them had been initiated into drug use at an early age."}]],["isolate","/ˈaɪsəleɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “isolate”.","isolate [ˈaɪsəleɪt] -1 n. [生物] 隔离种群 vt. 使隔离；使孤立；使绝缘 adj. 隔离的；孤立的 vi. 隔离；孤立 时态: isolated, isolating, isolates (研四六托雅宝 3963/3830)","欧陆词典释义：isolate [ˈaɪsəleɪt] -1 n. [生物] 隔离种群 vt. 使隔离；使孤立；使绝缘 adj. 隔离的；孤立的 vi. 隔离；孤立 时态: isolated, isolating, isolates (研四六托雅宝 3963/3830)","This policy could isolate the country from the other permanent members of the United Nations Security Council...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to separate somebody/something physically or socially from other people or things","example":"Patients with the disease should be isolated."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to separate a part of a situation, problem, idea, etc. so that you can see what it is and deal with it separately","example":"He was immediately isolated from the other prisoners."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to separate a single substance, cell, etc. from others so that you can study it","example":"This decision will isolate the country from the rest of Europe."}]],["levy","/ˈlevi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “levy”.","levy [ˈlevi] -2 n. 征收；征兵，征税 vt. 征收（税等）；征集（兵等） vi. 征税；征兵 n. (Levy)人名；(西、意、葡、芬、法、瑞典)莱维；(英、以)利维 时态: levied, levying, levies (研托雅宝 13303/7232)","欧陆词典释义：levy [ˈlevi] -2 n. 征收；征兵，征税 vt. 征收（税等）；征集（兵等） vi. 征税；征兵 n. (Levy)人名；(西、意、葡、芬、法、瑞典)莱维；(英、以)利维 时态: levied, levying, levies (研托雅宝 13303/7232)","an annual motorway levy on all drivers.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an extra amount of money that has to be paid, especially as a tax to the government","example":"to put/impose a levy"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"the trade-union political levy"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to use official authority to demand and collect a payment, tax, etc.","example":"a tax levied by the government on excess company profits"}]],["maximise","/'mæksɪmaɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “maximise”.","maximise ['mæksɪmaɪz] vt. 把…增加到最大限度；尽量增大（等于maximize） 时态: maximised, maximising, maximises (-/7248)","欧陆词典释义：maximise ['mæksɪmaɪz] vt. 把…增加到最大限度；尽量增大（等于maximize） 时态: maximised, maximising, maximises (-/7248)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “maximise”.",""],["monitor","/ˈmɒnɪtə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “monitor”.","monitor [ˈmɒnɪtə(r)] -K3 n. 监视器；监听器；监控器；显示屏；班长 vt. 监控 时态: monitored, monitoring, monitors (中高研四六托雅 2349/2431)","欧陆词典释义：monitor [ˈmɒnɪtə(r)] -K3 n. 监视器；监听器；监控器；显示屏；班长 vt. 监控 时态: monitored, monitoring, monitors (中高研四六托雅 2349/2431)","Officials had not been allowed to monitor the voting...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a television screen used to show particular kinds of information; a screen that shows information from a computer","example":"The details of today's flights are displayed on the monitor."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a piece of equipment used to check or record something","example":"a PC with a 17-inch colour monitor"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a student in a school who performs special duties, such as helping the teacher","example":"a heart monitor"}]],["neutral","/ˈnju:trəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “neutral”.","neutral [ˈnju:trəl] -2 adj. 中立的，中性的；中立国的；非彩色的 n. 中立国；中立者；非彩色；齿轮的空档 (研四六托 4223/4121)","欧陆词典释义：neutral [ˈnju:trəl] -2 adj. 中立的，中性的；中立国的；非彩色的 n. 中立国；中立者；非彩色；齿轮的空档 (研四六托 4223/4121)","Let's meet on neutral territory...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not supporting or helping either side in a disagreement, competition, etc.","example":"Journalists are supposed to be politically neutral."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"not belonging to any of the countries that are involved in a war; not supporting any of the countries involved in a war","example":"I didn't take my father's or my mother's side; I tried to remain neutral"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"deliberately not expressing any strong feeling","example":"neutral territory/waters"}]],["nonetheless","/ˌnʌnðəˈles/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “nonetheless”.","nonetheless [ˌnʌnðəˈles] -2 adv. 尽管如此，但是 (研六托 3298/4823)","欧陆词典释义：nonetheless [ˌnʌnðəˈles] -2 adv. 尽管如此，但是 (研六托 3298/4823)","There was still a long way to go. Nonetheless, some progress had been made...",""],["overseas","/ˌəʊvəˈsi:z/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “overseas”.","overseas [ˌəʊvəˈsi:z] -3 adv. 在海外，海外 adj. 海外的，国外的 原型: overseas 是 oversea 的复数 (研四六雅 4955/2990)","欧陆词典释义：overseas [ˌəʊvəˈsi:z] -3 adv. 在海外，海外 adj. 海外的，国外的 原型: overseas 是 oversea 的复数 (研四六雅 4955/2990)","He has returned to South Africa from his long overseas trip.",""],["pose","/pəʊz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “pose”.","pose [pəʊz] -K3 vi. 摆姿势；佯装；矫揉造作 vt. 造成，形成；摆姿势；装模作样；提出…讨论 n. 姿势，姿态；装模作样 时态: posed, posing, poses (研四六托雅宝 2230/2739)","欧陆词典释义：pose [pəʊz] -K3 vi. 摆姿势；佯装；矫揉造作 vt. 造成，形成；摆姿势；装模作样；提出…讨论 n. 姿势，姿态；装模作样 时态: posed, posing, poses (研四六托雅宝 2230/2739)","This could pose a threat to jobs in the coal industry...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to create a threat, problem, etc. that has to be dealt with","example":"to pose a threat/challenge/danger/risk"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to ask a question, especially one that needs serious thought","example":"The task poses no special problems"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to sit or stand in a particular position in order to be painted, drawn or photographed","example":"The delegates posed for a group photograph."}]],["presume","/prɪˈzju:m/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “presume”.","presume [prɪˈzju:m] -2 vi. 相信；擅自行为 vt. 假定；推测；擅自；意味着 时态: presumed, presuming, presumes (研六托宝 5740/4921)","欧陆词典释义：presume [prɪˈzju:m] -2 vi. 相信；擅自行为 vt. 假定；推测；擅自；意味着 时态: presumed, presuming, presumes (研六托宝 5740/4921)","I presume you're here on business...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to suppose that something is true, although you do not have actual proof","example":"They are very expensive, I presume?"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to accept that something is true until it is shown not to be true, especially in court","example":"‘Is he still abroad?’ ‘ I presume so"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to accept something as true or existing and to act on that basis","example":"I presumed (that) he understood the rules."}]],["priority","/praɪˈɒrəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “priority”.","priority [praɪˈɒrəti] -K3 n. 优先；优先权；[数] 优先次序；优先考虑的事 (研四六托雅宝 2112/1729)","欧陆词典释义：priority [praɪˈɒrəti] -K3 n. 优先；优先权；[数] 优先次序；优先考虑的事 (研四六托雅宝 2112/1729)","Being a parent is her first priority ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that you think is more important than other things and should be dealt with first","example":"a high/low priority"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the most important place among various things that have to be done or among a group of people","example":"Education is a top priority"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the right of a vehicle to go before other traffic at a particular place on a road","example":"Our first priority"}]],["prohibit","/prəˈhɪbɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “prohibit”.","prohibit [prəˈhɪbɪt] -2 vt. 阻止，禁止 时态: prohibited, prohibiting, prohibits (高研四六托雅 3990/5809)","欧陆词典释义：prohibit [prəˈhɪbɪt] -2 vt. 阻止，禁止 时态: prohibited, prohibiting, prohibits (高研四六托雅 3990/5809)","a law that prohibit s tobacco advertising in newspapers and magazines...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to stop something from being done or used especially by law","example":"a law prohibiting the sale of alcohol"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something impossible to do","example":"Soviet citizens were prohibited from travelling abroad."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The policy prohibits smoking on school grounds."}]],["prospect","/ˈprɒspekt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “prospect”.","prospect [ˈprɒspekt] -K4 n. 前途；预期；景色 vt. 勘探，勘察 vi. 勘探，找矿 时态: prospected, prospecting, prospects (研四六托雅宝 2323/1724)","欧陆词典释义：prospect [ˈprɒspekt] -K4 n. 前途；预期；景色 vt. 勘探，勘察 vi. 勘探，找矿 时态: prospected, prospecting, prospects (研四六托雅宝 2323/1724)","Unfortunately, there is little prospect of seeing these big questions answered...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the possibility that something will happen","example":"There is no immediate prospect of peace."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an idea of what might or will happen in the future","example":"A place in the semi-finals is in prospect"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the chances of being successful","example":"There's a reasonable prospect that his debts will be paid."}]],["radical","/ˈrædɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “radical”.","radical [ˈrædɪkl] -4 n. 基础；激进分子；[物化] 原子团；[数] 根数 adj. 激进的；根本的；彻底的 (研四六托雅 2929/2361)","欧陆词典释义：radical [ˈrædɪkl] -4 n. 基础；激进分子；[物化] 原子团；[数] 根数 adj. 激进的；根本的；彻底的 (研四六托雅 2929/2361)","The country needs a period of calm without more surges of radical change...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"concerning the most basic and important parts of something; thorough and complete","example":"the need for radical changes"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"new, different and likely to have a great effect","example":"demands for radical reform of the law"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"in favour of thorough and complete political or social change","example":"radical differences between the sexes"}]],["random","/ˈrændəm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “random”.","random [ˈrændəm] -2 n. 随意 adj. [数] 随机的；任意的；胡乱的 adv. 胡乱地 (高研六托雅宝 3619/3811)","欧陆词典释义：random [ˈrændəm] -2 n. 随意 adj. [数] 随机的；任意的；胡乱的 adv. 胡乱地 (高研六托雅宝 3619/3811)","The survey used a random sample of two thousand people across England and Wales...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"done, chosen, etc. without somebody deciding in advance what is going to happen, or without any regular pattern","example":"the random killing of innocent people"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"not known or not identified","example":"a random sample/selection"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing or person that is random","example":"The information is processed in a random order."}]],["reluctant","/rɪˈlʌktənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “reluctant”.","reluctant [rɪˈlʌktənt] -3 adj. 不情愿的；勉强的；顽抗的 (研四六托雅 3900/3511)","欧陆词典释义：reluctant [rɪˈlʌktənt] -3 adj. 不情愿的；勉强的；顽抗的 (研四六托雅 3900/3511)","Mr Spero was reluctant to ask for help...",""],["restore","/rɪˈstɔ:(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “restore”.","restore [rɪˈstɔ:(r)] -K3 vi. 恢复；还原 vt. 恢复；修复；归还 时态: restored, restoring, restores (研四六托雅宝 2543/2217)","欧陆词典释义：restore [rɪˈstɔ:(r)] -K3 vi. 恢复；还原 vt. 恢复；修复；归还 时态: restored, restoring, restores (研四六托雅宝 2543/2217)","The army has recently been brought in to restore order...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to bring back a situation or feeling that existed before","example":"The measures are intended to restore public confidence in the economy."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to bring somebody/something back to a former condition, place or position","example":"Order was"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to repair a building, work of art, piece of furniture, etc. so that it looks as good as it did originally","example":"Such kindness restores your faith in human nature ("}]],["restrict","/rɪˈstrɪkt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “restrict”.","restrict [rɪˈstrɪkt] -K2 vt. 限制；约束；限定 时态: restricted, restricting, restricts (高研四六托 3539/2207)","欧陆词典释义：restrict [rɪˈstrɪkt] -K2 vt. 限制；约束；限定 时态: restricted, restricting, restricts (高研四六托 3539/2207)","There is talk of raising the admission requirements to restrict the number of students on campus...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to limit the size, amount or range of something","example":"Speed is restricted to 30 mph in towns."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to stop somebody/something from moving or acting freely","example":"We restrict the number of students per class to 10."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to control something with rules or laws","example":"Fog severely restricted visibility."}]],["sector","/ˈsektə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sector”.","sector [ˈsektə(r)] -K4 n. 部门；扇形，扇区；象限仪；函数尺 vt. 把…分成扇形 (研六托雅 1974/909)","欧陆词典释义：sector [ˈsektə(r)] -K4 n. 部门；扇形，扇区；象限仪；函数尺 vt. 把…分成扇形 (研六托雅 1974/909)","the nation's manufacturing sector .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a part of an area of activity, especially of a country’s economy","example":"the manufacturing sector"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a part of a particular area, especially an area under military control","example":"service-sector jobs ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a part of a circle lying between two straight lines drawn from the centre to the edge","example":"each sector of the war zone"}]],["sufficient","/səˈfɪʃnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “sufficient”.","sufficient [səˈfɪʃnt] -K3 adj. 足够的；充分的 (研四六托雅宝 3099/1582)","欧陆词典释义：sufficient [səˈfɪʃnt] -K3 adj. 足够的；充分的 (研四六托雅宝 3099/1582)","One metre of fabric is sufficient to cover the exterior of an 18-in-diameter hatbox...",""],["terminate","/ˈtɜ:mɪneɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “terminate”.","terminate [ˈtɜ:mɪneɪt] -2 vt. 使终止；使结束；解雇 adj. 结束的 vi. 结束，终止；结果 时态: terminated, terminating, terminates (研六托雅宝 7189/5291)","欧陆词典释义：terminate [ˈtɜ:mɪneɪt] -2 vt. 使终止；使结束；解雇 adj. 结束的 vi. 结束，终止；结果 时态: terminated, terminating, terminates (研六托雅宝 7189/5291)","Her next remark abruptly terminate d the conversation...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to end; to make something end","example":"Your contract of employment terminates in December."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to end a journey/trip","example":"The agreement was terminated immediately."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"to terminate a pregnancy ("}]],["trend","/trend/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “trend”.","trend [trend] -K3 n. 趋势，倾向；走向 vt. 使…趋向 vi. 趋向，伸向 n. (Trend)人名；(英)特伦德 时态: trended, trending, trends (高研四六托雅宝 1697/1949)","欧陆词典释义：trend [trend] -K3 n. 趋势，倾向；走向 vt. 使…趋向 vi. 趋向，伸向 n. (Trend)人名；(英)特伦德 时态: trended, trending, trends (高研四六托雅宝 1697/1949)","This is a growing trend .",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change or develop in a general direction","example":"Prices have been trending upwards."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to be discussed a lot on a social media","example":"See what's trending on Twitter in your local area right now."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a general direction in which a situation is changing or developing","example":"economic/social/political trends"}]],["trigger","/ˈtrɪgə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “trigger”.","trigger [ˈtrɪgə(r)] -3 n. 扳机；[电子] 触发器；制滑机 vt. 引发，引起；触发 vi. 松开扳柄 n. (Trigger)人名；(英)特里杰 时态: triggered, triggering, triggers (研六托雅宝 3666/4962)","欧陆词典释义：trigger [ˈtrɪgə(r)] -3 n. 扳机；[电子] 触发器；制滑机 vt. 引发，引起；触发 vi. 松开扳柄 n. (Trigger)人名；(英)特里杰 时态: triggered, triggering, triggers (研六托雅宝 3666/4962)","A man pointed a gun at them and pulled the trigger .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the part of a gun that you press in order to fire it","example":"to pull/squeeze the trigger"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"something that is the cause of a particular reaction or development, especially a bad one","example":"He kept his finger on the trigger."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the part of a bomb that causes it to explode","example":"The trigger for the strike was the closure of yet another factory."}]],["welfare","/ˈwelfeə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “welfare”.","welfare [ˈwelfeə(r)] -3 n. 福利；幸福；福利事业；安宁 adj. 福利的；接受社会救济的 (高研四六托雅 1933/1883)","欧陆词典释义：welfare [ˈwelfeə(r)] -3 n. 福利；幸福；福利事业；安宁 adj. 福利的；接受社会救济的 (高研四六托雅 1933/1883)","I do not think he is considering Emma's welfare ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the general health, happiness and safety of a person, an animal or a group","example":"We are concerned about the child's welfare."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"practical or financial help that is provided, often by the government, for people or animals that need it","example":"The state is still the main provider of welfare."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"money that the government pays regularly to people who are poor, unemployed, sick, etc.","example":"child welfare"}]],["whereupon","/ˌweərəˈpɒn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “whereupon”.","whereupon [ˌweərəˈpɒn] -1 conj. 于是 adv. 因此 (17007/11840)","欧陆词典释义：whereupon [ˌweərəˈpɒn] -1 conj. 于是 adv. 因此 (17007/11840)","Mr Muite refused to talk to them except in the company of his legal colleagues, whereupon the police officers departed...",""],["withdrawal","/wɪðˈdrɔ:əl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “withdrawal”.","withdrawal [wɪðˈdrɔ:əl] -3 n. 撤退，收回；提款；取消；退股 (托 4130/3213)","欧陆词典释义：withdrawal [wɪðˈdrɔ:əl] -3 n. 撤退，收回；提款；取消；退股 (托 4130/3213)"," withdrawal of friendship...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of moving or taking something away or back","example":"the withdrawal of support"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of no longer taking part in something or being a member of an organization","example":"the withdrawal of the UN troops from the region"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of taking an amount of money out of your bank account","example":"the withdrawal of a product from the market"}]],["volatility","/ˌvɒlə'tɪlətɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “volatility”.","volatility [ˌvɒlə'tɪlətɪ] n. [化学] 挥发性；易变；活泼 (11720/10769)","欧陆词典释义：volatility [ˌvɒlə'tɪlətɪ] n. [化学] 挥发性；易变；活泼 (11720/10769)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “volatility”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality in a person of changing easily from one mood to another","example":"There was concern about the father's volatility."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality in a situation of being likely to change suddenly","example":"Diverse investments can protect against market volatility."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality in a substance of changing easily into a gas","example":"The cold reduces the volatility of the substance."}]],["tendency","/ˈtendənsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “tendency”.","tendency [ˈtendənsi] -K3 n. 倾向，趋势；癖好 (高研四六托雅 3040/2377)","欧陆词典释义：tendency [ˈtendənsi] -K3 n. 倾向，趋势；癖好 (高研四六托雅 3040/2377)","The army has become increasingly restless over the mounting separatist tendencies of the northern republics.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"if somebody/something has a particular tendency","example":"to display"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a new custom that is starting to develop","example":"I have a tendency"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group within a larger political group, whose views are more extreme than those of the rest of the group","example":"There is a tendency for this disease to run in families."}]],["substantial","/səbˈstænʃl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “substantial”.","substantial [səbˈstænʃl] -K3 n. 本质；重要材料 adj. 大量的；实质的；内容充实的 (研四六托雅宝 2544/1536)","欧陆词典释义：substantial [səbˈstænʃl] -K3 n. 本质；重要材料 adj. 大量的；实质的；内容充实的 (研四六托雅宝 2544/1536)","The party has just lost office and with it a substantial number of seats...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"large in amount, value or importance","example":"substantial sums of money"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"large and solid; strongly built","example":"a substantial change"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"Middle English","example":"Substantial numbers of people support the reforms."}]],["relevant","/ˈreləvənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “relevant”.","relevant [ˈreləvənt] -K3 adj. 相关的；切题的；中肯的；有重大关系的；有意义的，目的明确的 (高研四六托雅 2814/1241)","欧陆词典释义：relevant [ˈreləvənt] -K3 adj. 相关的；切题的；中肯的；有重大关系的；有意义的，目的明确的 (高研四六托雅 2814/1241)","We are trying to make politics more relevant to younger people.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"closely connected with the subject you are discussing or the situation you are thinking about","example":"a relevant suggestion/question/point"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having ideas that are valuable and useful to people in their lives and work","example":"Do you have the relevant experience?"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"early 16th cent.","example":"Send me all the relevant information."}]],["substitute","/ˈsʌbstɪtju:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “substitute”.","substitute [ˈsʌbstɪtju:t] -K3 n. 代用品；代替者 vi. 替代 vt. 代替 时态: substituted, substituting, substitutes (高研四六托雅宝 5613/4548)","欧陆词典释义：substitute [ˈsʌbstɪtju:t] -K3 n. 代用品；代替者 vi. 替代 vt. 代替 时态: substituted, substituting, substitutes (高研四六托雅宝 5613/4548)","They were substituting violence for dialogue...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person or thing that you use or have instead of the one you normally use or have","example":"a meat substitute"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a player who replaces another player in a sports game","example":"a substitute family"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Paul's father only saw him as a substitute for his dead brother."}]],["subsidy","/ˈsʌbsədi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “subsidy”.","subsidy [ˈsʌbsədi] -3 n. 补贴；津贴；补助金 (研四六托雅宝 4252/3907)","欧陆词典释义：subsidy [ˈsʌbsədi] -3 n. 补贴；津贴；补助金 (研四六托雅宝 4252/3907)","European farmers are planning a massive demonstration against farm subsidy cuts...",""],["acquisition","/ˌækwɪˈzɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “acquisition”.","acquisition [ˌækwɪˈzɪʃn] -3 n. 获得物，获得；收购 (高研四六托雅 3856/2567)","欧陆词典释义：acquisition [ˌækwɪˈzɪʃn] -3 n. 获得物，获得；收购 (高研四六托雅 3856/2567)","the acquisition of a profitable paper recycling company.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of getting something, especially knowledge, a skill, etc.","example":"theories of child language acquisition"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that somebody buys to add to what they already own, usually something valuable","example":"His latest acquisition is a racehorse."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a company, piece of land, etc. bought by somebody, especially another company; the act of buying it","example":"The money will be spent on acquisitions for the university library."}]],["adaptation","/ˌædæpˈteɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adaptation”.","adaptation [ˌædæpˈteɪʃn] -1 n. 适应；改编；改编本，改写本 (高托 5196/5438)","欧陆词典释义：adaptation [ˌædæpˈteɪʃn] -1 n. 适应；改编；改编本，改写本 (高托 5196/5438)","Branagh's screen adaptation of Shakespeare's Henry the Fifth.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a film/movie, book or play that is based on a particular piece of work but that has been changed for a new situation","example":"a screen adaptation of Shakespeare’s ‘Macbeth’"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of changing something, for example your behaviour, to suit a new situation","example":"the adaptation of desert species to the hot conditions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"Adaptations in plants occur over thousands of years."}]],["adherence","/ədˈhɪərəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adherence”.","adherence [ədˈhɪərəns] n. 坚持；依附；忠诚 (托 9972/9968)","欧陆词典释义：adherence [ədˈhɪərəns] n. 坚持；依附；忠诚 (托 9972/9968)","strict adherence to the constitution.",""],["alleviate","/əˈli:vieɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “alleviate”.","alleviate [əˈli:vieɪt] -1 vt. 减轻，缓和 时态: alleviated, alleviating, alleviates (研六托雅宝 7531/7706)","欧陆词典释义：alleviate [əˈli:vieɪt] -1 vt. 减轻，缓和 时态: alleviated, alleviating, alleviates (研六托雅宝 7531/7706)","Nowadays, a great deal can be done to alleviate back pain.",""],["amplify","/ˈæmplɪfaɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “amplify”.","amplify [ˈæmplɪfaɪ] -1 vt. 放大，扩大；增强；详述 vi. 详述 时态: amplified, amplifying, amplifies (研四六托雅宝 9595/9902)","欧陆词典释义：amplify [ˈæmplɪfaɪ] -1 vt. 放大，扩大；增强；详述 vi. 详述 时态: amplified, amplifying, amplifies (研四六托雅宝 9595/9902)","This landscape seemed to trap and amplify sounds...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to increase something in strength, especially sound","example":"to amplify a guitar/an electric current/a signal"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to add details to a story, statement, etc.","example":"She refused to amplify further."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"You may need to amplify this point."}]],["anticipation","/ænˌtɪsɪˈpeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “anticipation”.","anticipation [ænˌtɪsɪˈpeɪʃn] -1 n. 希望；预感；先发制人；预支 (托雅 6188/6360)","欧陆词典释义：anticipation [ænˌtɪsɪˈpeɪʃn] -1 n. 希望；预感；先发制人；预支 (托雅 6188/6360)","There's been an atmosphere of anticipation around here for a few days now...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of seeing that something might happen in the future and perhaps doing something about it now","example":"He bought extra food in anticipation of"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a feeling of excitement about something (usually something good) that is going to happen","example":"happy/eager/excited anticipation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The courtroom was filled with anticipation."}]],["approximate","/əˈprɒksɪmət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “approximate”.","approximate [əˈprɒksɪmət] -K2 adj. [数] 近似的；大概的 vt. 近似；使…接近；粗略估计 vi. 接近于；近似于 时态: approximated, approximating, approximates (研四六托雅宝 11835/9895)","欧陆词典释义：approximate [əˈprɒksɪmət] -K2 adj. [数] 近似的；大概的 vt. 近似；使…接近；粗略估计 vi. 接近于；近似于 时态: approximated, approximating, approximates (研四六托雅宝 11835/9895)","The approximate cost varies from around £150 to £250...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"almost correct or accurate, but not completely so","example":"an approximate number/total/cost"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The cost given is only approximate."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be similar or close to something in nature, quality, amount, etc., but not exactly the same","example":"Use these figures as an approximate guide in your calculations."}]],["arise","/əˈraɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “arise”.","arise [əˈraɪz] -K3 vi. 出现；上升；起立 n. (Arise)人名；(西)阿里塞；(日)在濑(姓) 时态: arose, arisen, arising, arises (高研四六托雅 2581/1043)","欧陆词典释义：arise [əˈraɪz] -K3 vi. 出现；上升；起立 n. (Arise)人名；(西)阿里塞；(日)在濑(姓) 时态: arose, arisen, arising, arises (高研四六托雅 2581/1043)","if a problem arise s later in the pregnancy...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to happen; to start to exist","example":"A new crisis has arisen."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to happen as a result of a particular situation","example":"We keep them informed of any changes as they arise."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to begin to exist or develop","example":"Children should be disciplined when the need arises"}]],["assert","/əˈsɜ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assert”.","assert [əˈsɜ:t] -2 vt. 维护，坚持；断言；主张；声称 时态: asserted, asserting, asserts (研六托雅宝 3147/3438)","欧陆词典释义：assert [əˈsɜ:t] -2 vt. 维护，坚持；断言；主张；声称 时态: asserted, asserting, asserts (研六托雅宝 3147/3438)","Mr. Helm plans to assert that the bill violates the First Amendment...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to state clearly and firmly that something is true","example":"She continued to assert that she was innocent."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to behave in a confident and determined way so that other people pay attention to your opinions","example":"She continued to assert her innocence."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make other people recognize your right or authority to do something, by behaving firmly and confidently","example":"The German Chancellor was anxious to assert his government’s commitment to further European unity."}]],["assimilate","/əˈsɪməleɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assimilate”.","assimilate [əˈsɪməleɪt] -1 vt. 吸收；使同化；把…比作；使相似 vi. 吸收；同化 时态: assimilated, assimilating, assimilates (研六托雅宝 9426/8860)","欧陆词典释义：assimilate [əˈsɪməleɪt] -1 vt. 吸收；使同化；把…比作；使相似 vi. 吸收；同化 时态: assimilated, assimilating, assimilates (研六托雅宝 9426/8860)","There is every sign that new Asian-Americans are just as willing to assimilate ...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to fully understand an idea or some information so that you are able to use it yourself","example":"The committee will need time to assimilate this report."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to become, or allow somebody to become, a part of a country or community rather than remaining in a separate group","example":"Some people can only assimilate change gradually."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make an idea, a person’s attitude, etc. fit into something or be acceptable","example":"New arrivals find it hard to assimilate."}]],["attitude","/ˈætɪtju:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attitude”.","attitude [ˈætɪtju:d] -K4 n. 态度；看法；意见；姿势 (高研四 1155/920)","欧陆词典释义：attitude [ˈætɪtju:d] -K4 n. 态度；看法；意见；姿势 (高研四 1155/920)","the general change in attitude towards handicapped people...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way that you think and feel about somebody/something; the way that you behave towards somebody/something that shows how you think and feel","example":"changes in public attitudes to/about marriage"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"confident, sometimes aggressive behaviour that shows you do not care about other people’s opinions and that you want to do things in an individual way","example":"social attitudes to/towards/about/on education"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a position of the body","example":"the government’s attitude towards single parents"}]],["beneficial","/ˌbenɪˈfɪʃl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “beneficial”.","beneficial [ˌbenɪˈfɪʃl] -2 adj. 有益的，有利的；可享利益的 (高研四托雅 4991/4578)","欧陆词典释义：beneficial [ˌbenɪˈfɪʃl] -2 adj. 有益的，有利的；可享利益的 (高研四托雅 4991/4578)","vitamins which are beneficial to our health...",""],["capability","/ˌkeɪpəˈbɪləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “capability”.","capability [ˌkeɪpəˈbɪləti] -2 n. 才能，能力；性能，容量 (六托 2958/3838)","欧陆词典释义：capability [ˌkeɪpəˈbɪləti] -2 n. 才能，能力；性能，容量 (六托 2958/3838)","People experience differences in physical and mental capability depending on the time of day...",""],["cognitive","/ˈkɒgnətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cognitive”.","cognitive [ˈkɒgnətɪv] -1 adj. 认知的，认识的 (研六托雅 3344/5220)","欧陆词典释义：cognitive [ˈkɒgnətɪv] -1 adj. 认知的，认识的 (研六托雅 3344/5220)","As children grow older, their cognitive processes become sharper.",""],["cohesion","/kəʊˈhi:ʒn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cohesion”.","cohesion [kəʊˈhi:ʒn] -1 n. 凝聚；结合；[力] 内聚力 (托宝 10791/9083)","欧陆词典释义：cohesion [kəʊˈhi:ʒn] -1 n. 凝聚；结合；[力] 内聚力 (托宝 10791/9083)","By 1990, it was clear that the cohesion of the armed forces was rapidly breaking down...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act or state of keeping together","example":"the cohesion of the nuclear family"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the force causing molecules","example":"social/political/economic cohesion"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"the cohesion of the nuclear family"}]],["collateral","/kəˈlætərəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “collateral”.","collateral [kəˈlætərəl] -1 n. 抵押品；[法] 担保品；旁系亲属 adj. 并行的；旁系的；附属的 (托宝 10379/15524)","欧陆词典释义：collateral [kəˈlætərəl] -1 n. 抵押品；[法] 担保品；旁系亲属 adj. 并行的；旁系的；附属的 (托宝 10379/15524)","Many people use personal assets as collateral for small business loans...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"property or something valuable that you promise to give to somebody if you cannot pay back money that you borrow","example":"We had put our house up as collateral for our bank loan."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"collateral benefits"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with something else, but in addition to it and less important","example":"an independent contract collateral to the main contract"}]],["comparable","/ˈkɒmpərəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “comparable”.","comparable [ˈkɒmpərəbl] -2 adj. 可比较的；比得上的 (研四六托雅 4639/3741)","欧陆词典释义：comparable [ˈkɒmpərəbl] -2 adj. 可比较的；比得上的 (研四六托雅 4639/3741)","paying the same wages to men and women for work of comparable value...",""],["compensate","/ˈkɒmpenseɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compensate”.","compensate [ˈkɒmpenseɪt] -2 vt. 补偿，赔偿；付报酬 vi. 补偿，赔偿；抵消 时态: compensated, compensating, compensates (高研六托雅宝 5037/4464)","欧陆词典释义：compensate [ˈkɒmpenseɪt] -2 vt. 补偿，赔偿；付报酬 vi. 补偿，赔偿；抵消 时态: compensated, compensating, compensates (高研六托雅宝 5037/4464)","The official promise to compensate people for the price rise clearly hadn't been worked out properly...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to provide something good to balance or reduce the bad effects of damage, loss, etc.","example":"Nothing can compensate for the loss of a loved one."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to pay somebody money because they have suffered some damage, loss, injury, etc.","example":"Her lawyers say she should be compensated for the suffering she had been caused."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"His voice doesn’t have much range but he compensates with clever lyrics."}]],["compile","/kəmˈpaɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compile”.","compile [kəmˈpaɪl] -2 vt. 编译；编制；编辑；[图情] 汇编 时态: compiled, compiling, compiles (研四六托雅宝 5289/4566)","欧陆词典释义：compile [kəmˈpaɪl] -2 vt. 编译；编制；编辑；[图情] 汇编 时态: compiled, compiling, compiles (研四六托雅宝 5289/4566)","Councils were required to compile a register of all adults living in their areas...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to produce a book, list, report, etc. by bringing together different items, articles, songs, etc.","example":"We are trying to compile a list of suitable people for the job."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to translate instructions from one computer language into another so that a particular computer can understand them","example":"The album was compiled from live recordings from last year's tour."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"We are trying to compile a list of suitable people for the job."}]],["concession","/kənˈseʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “concession”.","concession [kənˈseʃn] -3 n. 让步；特许（权）；承认；退位 (研六托雅宝 5001/3835)","欧陆词典释义：concession [kənˈseʃn] -3 n. 让步；特许（权）；承认；退位 (研六托雅宝 5001/3835)","The King made major concession s to end the confrontation with his people.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that you allow or do, or allow somebody to have, in order to end an argument or to make a situation less difficult","example":"The firm will be forced to make concessions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of giving something or allowing something; the act of conceding","example":"to win a concession from somebody"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a reduction in an amount of money that has to be paid; a ticket that is sold at a reduced price to a particular group of people","example":"a major/an important concession"}]],["confine","/kənˈfaɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “confine”.","confine [kənˈfaɪn] -K2 n. 界限，边界;约束；限制 vt. 限制；禁闭 时态: confined, confining, confines (研四六托雅宝 5337/2898)","欧陆词典释义：confine [kənˈfaɪn] -K2 n. 界限，边界;约束；限制 vt. 限制；禁闭 时态: confined, confining, confines (研四六托雅宝 5337/2898)","Health officials have successfully confine d the epidemic to the Tabatinga area...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to keep somebody/something inside the limits of a particular activity, subject, area, etc.","example":"The work will not be confined to the Glasgow area."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to keep a person or an animal in a small or closed space","example":"I will confine myself"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have to stay in bed, in a wheelchair","example":"Keep the dog confined in a suitable travelling cage."}]],["consequently","/ˈkɒnsɪkwəntli/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consequently”.","consequently [ˈkɒnsɪkwəntli] -2 adv. 因此；结果；所以 (研四六托 4363/3023)","欧陆词典释义：consequently [ˈkɒnsɪkwəntli] -2 adv. 因此；结果；所以 (研四六托 4363/3023)","Grandfather Dingsdale had sustained a broken back while working in the mines. Consequently, he spent the rest of his life in a wheelchair...",""],["consolidate","/kənˈsɒlɪdeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consolidate”.","consolidate [kənˈsɒlɪdeɪt] -2 vt. 巩固，使固定；联合 vi. 巩固，加强 时态: consolidated, consolidating, consolidates (研六托雅宝 7157/6138)","欧陆词典释义：consolidate [kənˈsɒlɪdeɪt] -2 vt. 巩固，使固定；联合 vi. 巩固，加强 时态: consolidated, consolidating, consolidates (研六托雅宝 7157/6138)","The question is: will the junta consolidate its power by force?...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make a position of power or success stronger so that it is more likely to continue","example":"With this new movie he has consolidated"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to join things together into one; to be joined into one","example":"Italy consolidated their lead with a second goal."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"early 16th cent.","example":"All the debts have been consolidated."}]],["constitute","/ˈkɒnstɪtju:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “constitute”.","constitute [ˈkɒnstɪtju:t] -2 vt. 组成，构成；建立；任命 时态: constituted, constituting, constitutes (研六托雅宝 2887/2270)","欧陆词典释义：constitute [ˈkɒnstɪtju:t] -2 vt. 组成，构成；建立；任命 时态: constituted, constituting, constitutes (研六托雅宝 2887/2270)","Testing patients without their consent would constitute a professional and legal offence...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be considered to be something","example":"Does such an activity constitute a criminal offence?"},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to be the parts that together form something","example":"The increase in racial tension constitutes a threat to our society."},{"pos":"linking verb","definition":"to form a group legally or officially","example":"His action was interpreted as constituting a threat to the community."}]],["contingent","/kənˈtɪndʒənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contingent”.","contingent [kənˈtɪndʒənt] -2 n. 分遣队；偶然事件；分得部分；代表团 adj. 因情况而异的；不一定的；偶然发生的；可能的；依情况而定的；偶然的；[逻]有条件的 (托宝 9268/8532)","欧陆词典释义：contingent [kənˈtɪndʒənt] -2 n. 分遣队；偶然事件；分得部分；代表团 adj. 因情况而异的；不一定的；偶然发生的；可能的；依情况而定的；偶然的；[逻]有条件的 (托宝 9268/8532)","Nigeria provided a large contingent of troops to the West African Peacekeeping Force...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a group of people at a meeting or an event who have something in common, especially the place they come from, that is not shared by other people at the event","example":"The largest contingent was from the United States."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a group of soldiers that are part of a larger force","example":"A strong contingent of local residents were there to block the proposal."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"the French contingent in the UN peacekeeping force"}]],["contrary","/ˈkɒntrəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contrary”.","contrary [ˈkɒntrəri] -2 n. 相反；反面 adj. 相反的；对立的 adv. 相反地 (高研四六托 5495/4761)","欧陆词典释义：contrary [ˈkɒntrəri] -2 n. 相反；反面 adj. 相反的；对立的 adv. 相反地 (高研四六托 5495/4761)","This view is contrary to the aims of critical social research for a number of reasons...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"different from something; against something","example":"Contrary to popular belief"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"completely different in nature or direction","example":"The government has decided that the publication of the report would be ‘contrary to the public interest’."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"Contrary to expectations and the weather forecast, we had a fine day for the experiment."}]],["convention","/kənˈvenʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “convention”.","convention [kənˈvenʃn] -K3 n. 大会；[法] 惯例；[计] 约定；[法] 协定；习俗 (研四六托雅 2472/1947)","欧陆词典释义：convention [kənˈvenʃn] -K3 n. 大会；[法] 惯例；[计] 约定；[法] 协定；习俗 (研四六托雅 2472/1947)","It's just a social convention that men don't wear skirts...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way in which something is done that most people in a society expect and consider to be polite or the right way to do it","example":"social conventions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large meeting of the members of a profession, a political party, etc.","example":"By convention"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official agreement between countries or leaders","example":"She is a young woman who enjoys flouting conventions."}]],["correlation","/ˌkɒrəˈleɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “correlation”.","correlation [ˌkɒrəˈleɪʃn] -1 n. [数] 相关，关联；相互关系 (六 3502/3912)","欧陆词典释义：correlation [ˌkɒrəˈleɪʃn] -1 n. [数] 相关，关联；相互关系 (六 3502/3912)","the correlation between smoking and disease.",""],["discourse","/ˈdɪskɔ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “discourse”.","discourse [ˈdɪskɔ:s] -1 n. 论述；谈话；演讲 vt. 说出；演奏出 vi. 演说；谈论；讲述 时态: discoursed, discoursing, discourses (研六托宝 3253/2919)","欧陆词典释义：discourse [ˈdɪskɔ:s] -1 n. 论述；谈话；演讲 vt. 说出；演奏出 vi. 演说；谈论；讲述 时态: discoursed, discoursing, discourses (研六托宝 3253/2919)","a tradition of political discourse .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a long and serious treatment or discussion of a subject in speech or writing","example":"a discourse on issues of gender and sexuality"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the use of language in speech and writing in order to produce meaning; language that is studied, usually in order to see how the different parts of a text are connected","example":"He was hoping for some lively political discourse at the meeting."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"spoken/written discourse"}]],["distort","/dɪˈstɔ:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “distort”.","distort [dɪˈstɔ:t] -2 vt. 扭曲；使失真；曲解 vi. 扭曲；变形 时态: distorted, distorting, distorts (研六托雅宝 6622/5932)","欧陆词典释义：distort [dɪˈstɔ:t] -2 vt. 扭曲；使失真；曲解 vi. 扭曲；变形 时态: distorted, distorting, distorts (研六托雅宝 6622/5932)","The media distort s reality; categorises people as all good or all bad...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to change the shape, appearance or sound of something so that it is strange or not clear","example":"a fairground mirror that distorts your shape"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to twist or change facts, ideas, etc. so that they are no longer correct or true","example":"The loudspeaker seemed to distort his voice."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"Newspapers are often guilty of distorting the truth."}]],["diversity","/daɪˈvɜ:səti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “diversity”.","diversity [daɪˈvɜ:səti] -2 n. 多样性；差异 (托宝 2531/4642)","欧陆词典释义：diversity [daɪˈvɜ:səti] -2 n. 多样性；差异 (托宝 2531/4642)","the cultural diversity of British society.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a range of many people or things that are very different from each other","example":"the biological diversity of the rainforests"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality or fact of including a range of many people or things","example":"a great/wide/rich diversity"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"There is a need for greater diversity and choice in education."}]],["duration","/djuˈreɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “duration”.","duration [djuˈreɪʃn] -2 n. 持续，持续的时间，期间 [语音学]音长，音延 (研四六托雅宝 5426/3698)","欧陆词典释义：duration [djuˈreɪʃn] -2 n. 持续，持续的时间，期间 [语音学]音长，音延 (研四六托雅宝 5426/3698)","He was given the task of protecting her for the duration of the trial...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the length of time that something lasts or continues","example":"The school was used as a hospital for the duration of the war."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"a contract of three years’ duration"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"until the end of a particular situation","example":"She stayed there for the duration of the journey."}]],["enact","/ɪˈnækt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “enact”.","enact [ɪˈnækt] -2 vt. 颁布；制定法律；扮演；发生 时态: enacted, enacting, enacts (托宝 4710/6524)","欧陆词典释义：enact [ɪˈnækt] -2 vt. 颁布；制定法律；扮演；发生 时态: enacted, enacting, enacts (托宝 4710/6524)","The authorities have failed so far to enact a law allowing unrestricted emigration...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to pass a law","example":"legislation enacted by parliament"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to perform a play or act a part in a play","example":"scenes from history enacted by local residents"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take place","example":"They seemed unaware of the drama being enacted a few feet away from them."}]],["enhancement","/ɪn'hɑ:nsmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “enhancement”.","enhancement [ɪn'hɑ:nsmənt] n. 增加；放大 (7849/8152)","欧陆词典释义：enhancement [ɪn'hɑ:nsmənt] n. 增加；放大 (7849/8152)","Music is merely an enhancement to the power of her words...",""],["equilibrium","/ˌi:kwɪˈlɪbriəm/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “equilibrium”.","equilibrium [ˌi:kwɪˈlɪbriəm] -1 n. 均衡；平静；保持平衡的能力 (六托雅宝 9063/4064)","欧陆词典释义：equilibrium [ˌi:kwɪˈlɪbriəm] -1 n. 均衡；平静；保持平衡的能力 (六托雅宝 9063/4064)","Stocks seesawed ever lower until prices found some new level of equilibrium ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a state of balance, especially between opposing forces or influences","example":"The point at which the solid and the liquid are in equilibrium"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a calm state of mind and a balance of emotions","example":"Any disturbance to the body's state of equilibrium can produce stress."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"We have achieved an equilibrium in the economy."}]],["expose","/ɪk'spəʊz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “expose”.","expose [ɪk'spəʊz] -K3 vt. 揭露，揭发；使曝光；显示 时态: exposed, exposing, exposes (高研四六托雅 2005/2577)","欧陆词典释义：expose [ɪk'spəʊz] -K3 vt. 揭露，揭发；使曝光；显示 时态: exposed, exposing, exposes (高研四六托雅 2005/2577)","Lowered sea levels expose d the shallow continental shelf beneath the Bering Sea...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show something that is usually hidden","example":"He smiled suddenly, exposing a set of amazingly white teeth."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to tell the true facts about a person or a situation, and show them/it to be immoral, illegal, etc.","example":"Miles of sand are exposed at low tide."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to put somebody/something in a place or situation where they are not protected from something harmful or unpleasant","example":"My job as a journalist is to expose the truth."}]],["henceforth","/ˌhensˈfɔ:θ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “henceforth”.","henceforth [ˌhensˈfɔ:θ] -1 adv. 今后；自此以后 (研六雅 17401/11925)","欧陆词典释义：henceforth [ˌhensˈfɔ:θ] -1 adv. 今后；自此以后 (研六雅 17401/11925)","Henceforth, parties which fail to get 5% of the vote will not be represented in parliament...",""],["impose","/ɪmˈpəʊz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “impose”.","impose [ɪmˈpəʊz] -K4 vt. 强加；征税；以…欺骗 vi. 利用；欺骗；施加影响 时态: imposed, imposing, imposes (研四六托雅宝 2334/1517)","欧陆词典释义：impose [ɪmˈpəʊz] -K4 vt. 强加；征税；以…欺骗 vi. 利用；欺骗；施加影响 时态: imposed, imposing, imposes (研四六托雅宝 2334/1517)","Britain impose d fines on airlines which bring in passengers without proper papers...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to introduce a new law, rule, tax, etc.; to order that a rule, punishment, etc. be used","example":"A new tax was imposed on fuel."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to force somebody/something to have to deal with something that is difficult or unpleasant","example":"to impose limitations/restrictions/constraints"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody accept the same opinions, wishes, etc. as your own","example":"This system imposes additional financial burdens on many people."}]],["inference","/ˈɪnfərəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “inference”.","inference [ˈɪnfərəns] -1 n. 推理；推论；推断 (研六雅 9554/6696)","欧陆词典释义：inference [ˈɪnfərəns] -1 n. 推理；推论；推断 (研六雅 9554/6696)","There were two inference s to be drawn from her letter.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that you can find out indirectly from what you already know","example":"to draw/make inferences"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act or process of forming an opinion, based on what you already know","example":"The clear inference is that the universe is expanding."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"If he is guilty then, by inference"}]],["input","/ˈɪnpʊt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “input”.","input [ˈɪnpʊt] -2 n. 投入；输入电路 vt. [自][电子] 输入；将…输入电脑 时态: input, inputting, inputs (研四六 4120/2275)","欧陆词典释义：input [ˈɪnpʊt] -2 n. 投入；输入电路 vt. [自][电子] 输入；将…输入电脑 时态: input, inputting, inputs (研四六 4120/2275)","We listen to our employees and value their input ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"time, knowledge, ideas, etc. that you put into work, a project, etc. in order to make it succeed; the act of putting something in","example":"Her specialist input to the discussions has been very useful."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the act of putting information into a computer; the information that you put in","example":"Barley is one of the main inputs to the process of distillation."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a place or means for electricity, data, etc. to enter a machine or system","example":"I'd appreciate your input on this."}]],["intact","/ɪnˈtækt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “intact”.","intact [ɪnˈtækt] -2 adj. 完整的；原封不动的；未受损伤的 (研六托雅宝 4626/4953)","欧陆词典释义：intact [ɪnˈtækt] -2 adj. 完整的；原封不动的；未受损伤的 (研六托雅宝 4626/4953)","Most of the cargo was left intact after the explosion...",""],["intensive","/ɪnˈtensɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “intensive”.","intensive [ɪnˈtensɪv] -2 n. 加强器 adj. 加强的；集中的；透彻的；加强语气的 (研四六托雅 4973/3826)","欧陆词典释义：intensive [ɪnˈtensɪv] -2 n. 加强器 adj. 加强的；集中的；透彻的；加强语气的 (研四六托雅 4973/3826)","several days and nights of intensive negotiations...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"involving a lot of work or activity done in a short time","example":"an intensive language course"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"extremely thorough; done with a lot of care","example":"two weeks of intensive training"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"aimed at producing as much food as possible using as little land or as little money as possible","example":"intensive diplomatic negotiations"}]],["interpretation","/ɪnˌtɜ:prɪˈteɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “interpretation”.","interpretation [ɪnˌtɜ:prɪˈteɪʃn] -K2 n. 解释；翻译；演出 (四六托 2380/1744)","欧陆词典释义：interpretation [ɪnˌtɜ:prɪˈteɪʃn] -K2 n. 解释；翻译；演出 (四六托 2380/1744)","The opposition Conservative Party put a different interpretation on the figures...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the particular way in which something is understood or explained","example":"Her evidence suggests a different interpretation of the events."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the particular way in which somebody chooses to perform a piece of music, a role in a play, etc.","example":"It is not possible for everyone to put their own interpretation on the law."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Dreams are open to interpretation"}]],["acquaintance","/əˈkweɪntəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “acquaintance”.","acquaintance [əˈkweɪntəns] -2 n. 熟人；相识；了解；知道 (高研四六托宝 6274/5967)","欧陆词典释义：acquaintance [əˈkweɪntəns] -2 n. 熟人；相识；了解；知道 (高研四六托宝 6274/5967)","The proprietor was an old acquaintance of his...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person that you know but who is not a close friend","example":"Claire has a wide circle of friends and acquaintances"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"slight friendship","example":"He's just a business acquaintance."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"knowledge of something","example":"I bumped into an old acquaintance on the train."}]],["acute","/əˈkju:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “acute”.","acute [əˈkju:t] -2 adj. 严重的，[医] 急性的；敏锐的；激烈的；尖声的 级别: acuter, acutest (高研四六托雅宝 5255/3249)","欧陆词典释义：acute [əˈkju:t] -2 adj. 严重的，[医] 急性的；敏锐的；激烈的；尖声的 级别: acuter, acutest (高研四六托雅宝 5255/3249)","The war has aggravated an acute economic crisis...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"very serious or severe","example":"There is an acute shortage of water."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"an acute","example":"acute pain"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"very sensitive and well developed","example":"the world’s acute environmental problems"}]],["ambiguity","/ˌæmbɪˈgju:əti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ambiguity”.","ambiguity [ˌæmbɪˈgju:əti] n. 含糊；不明确；暧昧；模棱两可的话 (六雅 7034/5407)","欧陆词典释义：ambiguity [ˌæmbɪˈgju:əti] n. 含糊；不明确；暧昧；模棱两可的话 (六雅 7034/5407)","There is considerable ambiguity about what this part of the agreement actually means.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state of having more than one possible meaning","example":"Write clear definitions in order to avoid ambiguity."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a word or statement that can be understood in more than one way","example":"A lot of humour depends on ambiguity."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state of being difficult to understand or explain because of involving many different aspects","example":"There were several inconsistencies and ambiguities in her speech."}]],["apprehend","/ˌæprɪˈhend/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “apprehend”.","apprehend [ˌæprɪˈhend] -1 vt. 理解；逮捕；忧虑 vi. 理解；担心 时态: apprehended, apprehending, apprehends (研托宝 11622/13950)","欧陆词典释义：apprehend [ˌæprɪˈhend] -1 vt. 理解；逮捕；忧虑 vi. 理解；担心 时态: apprehended, apprehending, apprehends (研托宝 11622/13950)","Police have not apprehend ed her killer.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to catch somebody and arrest them","example":"The police apprehended an armed suspect near the scene of the crime."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to understand or recognize something","example":"The thief was apprehended in the act of stealing a car."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"He was slow to apprehend danger."}]],["assimilation","/əˌsɪməˈleɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assimilation”.","assimilation [əˌsɪməˈleɪʃn] n. 同化；吸收；[生化] 同化作用 (六 9369/12513)","欧陆词典释义：assimilation [əˌsɪməˈleɪʃn] n. 同化；吸收；[生化] 同化作用 (六 9369/12513)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assimilation”.",""],["authenticity","/ˌɔ:θenˈtɪsəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “authenticity”.","authenticity [ˌɔ:θenˈtɪsəti] n. 真实性，确实性；可靠性 (宝 8177/10267)","欧陆词典释义：authenticity [ˌɔ:θenˈtɪsəti] n. 真实性，确实性；可靠性 (宝 8177/10267)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “authenticity”.",""],["bureaucratic","/ˌbjʊərəˈkrætɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bureaucratic”.","bureaucratic [ˌbjʊərəˈkrætɪk] adj. 官僚的；官僚政治的 (高 6447/6084)","欧陆词典释义：bureaucratic [ˌbjʊərəˈkrætɪk] adj. 官僚的；官僚政治的 (高 6447/6084)","Diplomats believe that bureaucratic delays are inevitable...",""],["chronology","/krəˈnɒlədʒi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “chronology”.","chronology [krəˈnɒlədʒi] n. 年表；年代学 (托 12696/12865)","欧陆词典释义：chronology [krəˈnɒlədʒi] n. 年表；年代学 (托 12696/12865)","She gave him a factual account of the chronology of her brief liaison.",""],["commitment","/kəˈmɪtmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “commitment”.","commitment [kəˈmɪtmənt] -K2 n. 承诺，保证；委托；承担义务；献身 (高四六托雅 1616/1355)","欧陆词典释义：commitment [kəˈmɪtmənt] -K2 n. 承诺，保证；委托；承担义务；献身 (高四六托雅 1616/1355)"," commitment to the ideals of Bolshevism.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a promise to do something or to behave in a particular way; a promise to support somebody/something; the fact of committing yourself","example":"She doesn't want to make a"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the willingness to work hard and give your energy and time to a job or an activity","example":"the government’s commitment to public services"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that you have promised or agreed to do, or that you have to do","example":"The company's commitment to providing quality at a reasonable price has been vital to its success."}]],["compulsory","/kəmˈpʌlsəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compulsory”.","compulsory [kəmˈpʌlsəri] -2 n. （花样滑冰、竞技体操等的）规定动作 adj. 义务的；必修的；被强制的 (高研六托雅宝 12735/3997)","欧陆词典释义：compulsory [kəmˈpʌlsəri] -2 n. （花样滑冰、竞技体操等的）规定动作 adj. 义务的；必修的；被强制的 (高研六托雅宝 12735/3997)","In East Germany learning Russian was compulsory ...",""],["credibility","/ˌkredəˈbɪləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “credibility”.","credibility [ˌkredəˈbɪləti] n. 可信性；确实性 (4048/5675)","欧陆词典释义：credibility [ˌkredəˈbɪləti] n. 可信性；确实性 (4048/5675)","The police have lost their credibility ...",""],["detrimental","/ˌdetrɪˈmentl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “detrimental”.","detrimental [ˌdetrɪˈmentl] -1 n. 有害的人（或物）；不受欢迎的求婚者 adj. 不利的；有害的 (托雅宝 10826/9873)","欧陆词典释义：detrimental [ˌdetrɪˈmentl] -1 n. 有害的人（或物）；不受欢迎的求婚者 adj. 不利的；有害的 (托雅宝 10826/9873)","foods suspected of being detrimental to health...",""],["dissemination","/dɪˌsemɪ'neɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dissemination”.","dissemination [dɪˌsemɪ'neɪʃn] n. 宣传；散播；传染（病毒） (13011/12237)","欧陆词典释义：dissemination [dɪˌsemɪ'neɪʃn] n. 宣传；散播；传染（病毒） (13011/12237)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dissemination”.",""],["feasibility","/ˌfi:zə'bɪlətɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “feasibility”.","feasibility [ˌfi:zə'bɪlətɪ] n. 可行性；可能性 (11824/8983)","欧陆词典释义：feasibility [ˌfi:zə'bɪlətɪ] n. 可行性；可能性 (11824/8983)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “feasibility”.",""],["integrity","/ɪnˈtegrəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “integrity”.","integrity [ɪnˈtegrəti] -2 n. 完整；正直；诚实；廉正 (研六托雅宝 3464/4364)","欧陆词典释义：integrity [ɪnˈtegrəti] -2 n. 完整；正直；诚实；廉正 (研六托雅宝 3464/4364)","I have always regarded him as a man of integrity ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality of being honest and having strong moral principles","example":"personal/professional/artistic integrity"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state of being whole and not divided","example":"to behave with integrity"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"a man of great integrity"}]],["legislation","/ˌledʒɪsˈleɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “legislation”.","legislation [ˌledʒɪsˈleɪʃn] -3 n. 立法；法律 (研四六托雅宝 2017/1365)","欧陆词典释义：legislation [ˌledʒɪsˈleɪʃn] -3 n. 立法；法律 (研四六托雅宝 2017/1365)","a letter calling for legislation to protect women's rights.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a law or a set of laws passed by a parliament","example":"an important piece of legislation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of making and passing laws","example":"New legislation on the sale of drugs will be introduced next year."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"a call for legislation to ban smoking in public places"}]],["magnitude","/ˈmægnɪtju:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “magnitude”.","magnitude [ˈmægnɪtju:d] -1 n. 大小；量级；[地震] 震级；重要；光度 (研六托雅宝 3971/5792)","欧陆词典释义：magnitude [ˈmægnɪtju:d] -1 n. 大小；量级；[地震] 震级；重要；光度 (研六托雅宝 3971/5792)","An operation of this magnitude is going to be difficult...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the great size or importance of something; the degree to which something is large or important","example":"We did not realize the magnitude of the problem."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the degree to which a star is bright","example":"a discovery of the first magnitude"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the size of an earthquake","example":"The star varies in brightness by about three magnitudes."}]],["mandatory","/ˈmændətəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mandatory”.","mandatory [ˈmændətəri] -1 adj. 强制的；托管的；命令的 n. 受托者（等于mandatary） (托雅宝 5119/5806)","欧陆词典释义：mandatory [ˈmændətəri] -1 adj. 强制的；托管的；命令的 n. 受托者（等于mandatary） (托雅宝 5119/5806)","the mandatory retirement age of 65...",""],["perception","/pəˈsepʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “perception”.","perception [pəˈsepʃn] -2 n. 知觉；[生理] 感觉；看法；洞察力；获取 (研六托雅宝 1866/2545)","欧陆词典释义：perception [pəˈsepʃn] -2 n. 知觉；[生理] 感觉；看法；洞察力；获取 (研六托雅宝 1866/2545)","He is interested in how our perception s of death affect the way we live.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the way you notice things, especially with the senses","example":"our perception of reality"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to understand the true nature of something","example":"visual perception"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an idea, a belief or an image you have as a result of how you see or understand something","example":"She showed great perception in her assessment of the family situation."}]],["ratio","/ˈreɪʃiəʊ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ratio”.","ratio [ˈreɪʃiəʊ] -2 n. 比率，比例 (研四六托雅 3088/2365)","欧陆词典释义：ratio [ˈreɪʃiəʊ] -2 n. 比率，比例 (研四六托雅 3088/2365)","In 1978 there were 884 students at a lecturer/student ratio of 1:15...",""],["rationale","/ˌræʃəˈnɑ:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “rationale”.","rationale [ˌræʃəˈnɑ:l] -1 n. 基本原理；原理的阐述 (6049/8003)","欧陆词典释义：rationale [ˌræʃəˈnɑ:l] -1 n. 基本原理；原理的阐述 (6049/8003)","However, the rationale for such initiatives is not, of course, solely economic...",""],["redundancy","/rɪˈdʌndənsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “redundancy”.","redundancy [rɪˈdʌndənsi] -2 n. [计][数] 冗余（等于redundance）；裁员；人浮于事 (研宝 16763/3877)","欧陆词典释义：redundancy [rɪˈdʌndənsi] -2 n. [计][数] 冗余（等于redundance）；裁员；人浮于事 (研宝 16763/3877)","The ministry has said it hopes to avoid compulsory redundancies.",""],["restraint","/rɪˈstreɪnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “restraint”.","restraint [rɪˈstreɪnt] -2 n. 抑制，克制；约束 (研四六托宝 5419/4343)","欧陆词典释义：restraint [rɪˈstreɪnt] -2 n. 抑制，克制；约束 (研四六托宝 5419/4343)","The Prime Minister is calling for new restraint s on trade unions...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a rule, a fact, an idea, etc. that limits or controls what people can do","example":"The government has imposed export restraints on some products."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of controlling or limiting something because it is necessary or sensible to do so","example":"social restraints on drinking alcohol"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality of behaving calmly and with control","example":"The EU has set strict limits on pollution levels."}]],["validity","/vəˈlɪdəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “validity”.","validity [vəˈlɪdəti] n. [计] 有效性；正确；正确性 (六托雅 4542/4628)","欧陆词典释义：validity [vəˈlɪdəti] n. [计] 有效性；正确；正确性 (六托雅 4542/4628)","Shocked by the results of the elections, they now want to challenge the validity of the vote...",""],["vulnerability","/ˌvʌlnərə'bɪlətɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “vulnerability”.","vulnerability [ˌvʌlnərə'bɪlətɪ] n. 易损性；弱点 (5951/7848)","欧陆词典释义：vulnerability [ˌvʌlnərə'bɪlətɪ] n. 易损性；弱点 (5951/7848)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “vulnerability”.",""],["adhesion","/ədˈhi:ʒn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adhesion”.","adhesion [ədˈhi:ʒn] n. 粘附；支持；固定 (19916/10938)","欧陆词典释义：adhesion [ədˈhi:ʒn] n. 粘附；支持；固定 (19916/10938)","Better driving equipment will improve track adhesion in slippery conditions.",""],["allocation","/ˌæləˈkeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “allocation”.","allocation [ˌæləˈkeɪʃn] n. 分配，配置；安置 (7082/3262)","欧陆词典释义：allocation [ˌæləˈkeɪʃn] n. 分配，配置；安置 (7082/3262)","The aid allocation for Pakistan was still under review...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an amount of money, space, etc. that is given to somebody for a particular purpose","example":"We have spent our entire allocation for the year."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of giving something to somebody for a particular purpose","example":"the allocation of food to those who need it most"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The allocation must be made according to a strict set of criteria."}]],["assumption","/əˈsʌmpʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assumption”.","assumption [əˈsʌmpʃn] -3 n. 假定；设想；担任；采取 (高研四六托雅宝 2606/1693)","欧陆词典释义：assumption [əˈsʌmpʃn] -3 n. 假定；设想；担任；采取 (高研四六托雅宝 2606/1693)","They have taken a wrong turning in their assumption that all men and women think alike...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a belief or feeling that something is true or that something will happen, although there is no proof","example":"an underlying/implicit assumption"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of taking or beginning to have power or responsibility","example":"We need to challenge some of the basic assumptions of Western philosophy."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"We are working on the assumption that"}]],["authentic","/ɔ:ˈθentɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “authentic”.","authentic [ɔ:ˈθentɪk] -2 adj. 真正的，真实的；可信的 (高研六托雅宝 5000/6476)","欧陆词典释义：authentic [ɔ:ˈθentɪk] -2 adj. 真正的，真实的；可信的 (高研六托雅宝 5000/6476)"," authentic Italian food...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"known to be real and genuine and not a copy","example":"I don't know if the painting is authentic."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"true and accurate","example":"an authentic account of life in the desert"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"made to be exactly the same as the original","example":"the authentic voice of young black Americans"}]],["commodity","/kəˈmɒdəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “commodity”.","commodity [kəˈmɒdəti] -2 n. 商品，货物；日用品 (研六托雅宝 4581/4365)","欧陆词典释义：commodity [kəˈmɒdəti] -2 n. 商品，货物；日用品 (研六托雅宝 4581/4365)","The government increased prices on several basic commodities like bread and meat.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a product or a raw material that can be bought and sold","example":"rice, flour and other basic commodities"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that is useful or has a useful quality","example":"a drop in commodity prices"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Crude oil is the world's most important commodity."}]],["complementary","/ˌkɒmplɪˈmentri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “complementary”.","complementary [ˌkɒmplɪˈmentri] -1 adj. 补足的，补充的 (托宝 8490/6673)","欧陆词典释义：complementary [ˌkɒmplɪˈmentri] -1 adj. 补足的，补充的 (托宝 8490/6673)","To improve the quality of life through work, two complementary strategies are necessary...",""],["compromise","/ˈkɒmprəmaɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compromise”.","compromise [ˈkɒmprəmaɪz] -3 n. 妥协，和解；折衷 vt. 妥协；危害 vi. 妥协；让步 时态: compromised, compromising, compromises (高研四六托雅宝 3751/3685)","欧陆词典释义：compromise [ˈkɒmprəmaɪz] -3 n. 妥协，和解；折衷 vt. 妥协；危害 vi. 妥协；让步 时态: compromised, compromising, compromises (高研四六托雅宝 3751/3685)","Encourage your child to reach a compromise between what he wants and what you want...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an agreement made between two people or groups in which each side gives up some of the things they want so that both sides are happy at the end","example":"After lengthy talks the two sides finally reached a compromise"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a solution to a problem in which two or more things cannot exist together as they are, in which each thing is reduced or changed slightly so that they can exist together","example":"In any relationship, you have to make compromises"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"the act of reaching a compromise","example":"a compromise solution/agreement/candidate"}]],["constituent","/kənˈstɪtjuənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “constituent”.","constituent [kənˈstɪtjuənt] -2 n. 成分；选民；委托人 adj. 构成的；选举的 (研六托雅宝 5746/4050)","欧陆词典释义：constituent [kənˈstɪtjuənt] -2 n. 成分；选民；委托人 adj. 构成的；选举的 (研六托雅宝 5746/4050)","Caffeine is the active constituent of drinks such as tea and coffee.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who lives, and can vote in a constituency","example":"She has the full support of her constituents."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"one of the parts of something that combine to form the whole","example":"Silicon and oxygen are the fundamental constituents of rocks in the earth’s crust."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late 15th cent.","example":"Tar is a harmful constituent of tobacco smoke."}]],["definitive","/dɪˈfɪnətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “definitive”.","definitive [dɪˈfɪnətɪv] -2 n. 限定词 adj. 决定性的；最后的；限定的 (托雅宝 6616/7809)","欧陆词典释义：definitive [dɪˈfɪnətɪv] -2 n. 限定词 adj. 决定性的；最后的；限定的 (托雅宝 6616/7809)","No one has come up with a definitive answer as to why this should be so...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"final; not able to be changed","example":"a definitive agreement/answer/statement"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"considered to be the best of its kind and almost impossible to improve","example":"The definitive version"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"the definitive biography of Einstein"}]],["discrepancy","/dɪsˈkrepənsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “discrepancy”.","discrepancy [dɪsˈkrepənsi] -1 n. 不符；矛盾；相差 (研六雅宝 6872/7003)","欧陆词典释义：discrepancy [dɪsˈkrepənsi] -1 n. 不符；矛盾；相差 (研六雅宝 6872/7003)","the discrepancy between press and radio reports.",""],["dispense","/dɪˈspens/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dispense”.","dispense [dɪˈspens] -1 vi. 免除，豁免 vt. 分配，分发；免除；执行 时态: dispensed, dispensing, dispenses (六托宝 8334/6379)","欧陆词典释义：dispense [dɪˈspens] -1 vi. 免除，豁免 vt. 分配，分发；免除；执行 时态: dispensed, dispensing, dispenses (六托宝 8334/6379)","The Union had already dispense d £40,000 in grants...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give out something to people","example":"The machine dispenses a range of drinks and snacks."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to provide something, especially a service, for people","example":"The organization dispenses free health care to the poor."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to prepare medicine and give it to people, as a job","example":"to dispense justice/advice"}]],["distortion","/dɪ'stɔ:ʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “distortion”.","distortion [dɪ'stɔ:ʃn] n. 变形；[物] 失真；扭曲；曲解 (六托 7511/6168)","欧陆词典释义：distortion [dɪ'stɔ:ʃn] n. 变形；[物] 失真；扭曲；曲解 (六托 7511/6168)","I think it would be a gross distortion of reality to say that they were motivated by self-interest...",""],["eradicate","/ɪˈrædɪkeɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “eradicate”.","eradicate [ɪˈrædɪkeɪt] -1 vt. 根除，根绝；消灭 时态: eradicated, eradicating, eradicates (六托雅宝 9110/8573)","欧陆词典释义：eradicate [ɪˈrædɪkeɪt] -1 vt. 根除，根绝；消灭 时态: eradicated, eradicating, eradicates (六托雅宝 9110/8573)","They are already battling to eradicate illnesses such as malaria and tetanus...",""],["hypothetical","/ˌhaɪpəˈθetɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “hypothetical”.","hypothetical [ˌhaɪpəˈθetɪkl] -1 adj. 假设的；爱猜想的 (宝 8049/8688)","欧陆词典释义：hypothetical [ˌhaɪpəˈθetɪkl] -1 adj. 假设的；爱猜想的 (宝 8049/8688)","Let's look at a hypothetical situation in which Carol, a recovering cocaine addict, gets invited to a party.",""],["illuminate","/ɪˈlu:mɪneɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “illuminate”.","illuminate [ɪˈlu:mɪneɪt] -1 vt. 阐明，说明；照亮；使灿烂；用灯装饰 vi. 照亮 时态: illuminated, illuminating, illuminates (研六托雅宝 5388/6519)","欧陆词典释义：illuminate [ɪˈlu:mɪneɪt] -1 vt. 阐明，说明；照亮；使灿烂；用灯装饰 vi. 照亮 时态: illuminated, illuminating, illuminates (研六托雅宝 5388/6519)","No streetlights illuminate d the street...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to shine light on something","example":"Floodlights illuminated the stadium."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something clearer or easier to understand","example":"The earth is illuminated by the sun."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to decorate a street, building, etc. with bright lights for a special occasion","example":"This text illuminates the philosopher's early thinking."}]],["legitimate","/lɪˈdʒɪtɪmət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “legitimate”.","legitimate [lɪˈdʒɪtɪmət] -2 adj. 合法的；正当的；合理的；正统的 vt. 使合法；认为正当（等于legitimize） 时态: legitimated, legitimating, legitimates (研六雅宝 3195/4329)","欧陆词典释义：legitimate [lɪˈdʒɪtɪmət] -2 adj. 合法的；正当的；合理的；正统的 vt. 使合法；认为正当（等于legitimize） 时态: legitimated, legitimating, legitimates (研六雅宝 3195/4329)","The French government has condemned the coup in Haiti and has demanded the restoration of the legitimate government...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"for which there is a fair and acceptable reason","example":"a legitimate grievance"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"allowed and acceptable according to the law","example":"It seemed a perfectly legitimate"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"born when its parents are legally married to each other","example":"Politicians are legitimate targets for satire."}]],["marginal","/ˈmɑ:dʒɪnl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “marginal”.","marginal [ˈmɑ:dʒɪnl] -2 adj. 边缘的；临界的；末端的 (研六雅宝 6094/3361)","欧陆词典释义：marginal [ˈmɑ:dʒɪnl] -2 adj. 边缘的；临界的；末端的 (研六雅宝 6094/3361)","This is a marginal improvement on October...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"small and not important","example":"a marginal improvement in weather conditions"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"not part of a main or important group or situation","example":"The story will only be of marginal interest to our readers."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"won or lost by a very small number of votes and therefore very important or interesting as an indication of public opinion","example":"The difference between the two estimates is marginal."}]],["obsolete","/ˈɒbsəli:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “obsolete”.","obsolete [ˈɒbsəli:t] -1 adj. 废弃的；老式的 n. 废词；陈腐的人 vt. 淘汰；废弃 (研托雅宝 8876/11255)","欧陆词典释义：obsolete [ˈɒbsəli:t] -1 adj. 废弃的；老式的 n. 废词；陈腐的人 vt. 淘汰；废弃 (研托雅宝 8876/11255)","So much equipment becomes obsolete almost as soon as it's made.",""],["pervasive","/pəˈveɪsɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “pervasive”.","pervasive [pəˈveɪsɪv] -1 adj. 普遍的；到处渗透的；流行的 (托 6779/10013)","欧陆词典释义：pervasive [pəˈveɪsɪv] -1 adj. 普遍的；到处渗透的；流行的 (托 6779/10013)","the pervasive influence of the army in national life...",""],["plausible","/ˈplɔ:zəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “plausible”.","plausible [ˈplɔ:zəbl] -1 adj. 貌似可信的，花言巧语的；貌似真实的，貌似有理的 (研六托雅宝 7125/6473)","欧陆词典释义：plausible [ˈplɔ:zəbl] -1 adj. 貌似可信的，花言巧语的；貌似真实的，貌似有理的 (研六托雅宝 7125/6473)","A more plausible explanation would seem to be that people are fed up with the Conservative government...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"reasonable and likely to be true","example":"Her story sounded perfectly plausible."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"good at sounding honest and sincere, especially when trying to trick people","example":"The only plausible explanation is that he forgot."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"mid 16th cent.","example":"She was a plausible liar."}]],["precede","/prɪˈsi:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “precede”.","precede [prɪˈsi:d] -2 vt. 领先，在…之前；优于，高于 vi. 领先，在前面 时态: preceded, preceding, precedes (研六托宝 5604/4328)","欧陆词典释义：precede [prɪˈsi:d] -2 vt. 领先，在…之前；优于，高于 vi. 领先，在前面 时态: preceded, preceding, precedes (研六托宝 5604/4328)","Intensive negotiations between the main parties precede d the vote...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to happen before something or come before something/somebody in order","example":"the years preceding the war"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to go in front of somebody","example":"His resignation was preceded by weeks of speculation."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"She preceded me in the job."}]],["preclude","/prɪˈklu:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “preclude”.","preclude [prɪˈklu:d] -1 vt. 排除；妨碍；阻止 时态: precluded, precluding, precludes (研六托宝 8092/7006)","欧陆词典释义：preclude [prɪˈklu:d] -1 vt. 排除；妨碍；阻止 时态: precluded, precluding, precludes (研六托宝 8092/7006)","At 84, John feels his age preclude s too much travel...",""],["prevalent","/ˈprevələnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “prevalent”.","prevalent [ˈprevələnt] -1 adj. 流行的；普遍的，广传的 (研六托雅 6987/8828)","欧陆词典释义：prevalent [ˈprevələnt] -1 adj. 流行的；普遍的，广传的 (研六托雅 6987/8828)","This condition is more prevalent in women than in men...",""],["prospective","/prəˈspektɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “prospective”.","prospective [prəˈspektɪv] -2 n. 预期；展望 adj. 未来的；预期的 (研六托雅 5420/4764)","欧陆词典释义：prospective [prəˈspektɪv] -2 n. 预期；展望 adj. 未来的；预期的 (研六托雅 5420/4764)","The story should act as a warning to other prospective buyers...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"expected to do something or to become something","example":"a prospective buyer"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"expected to happen soon","example":"They are worried about prospective changes in the law."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"I had a phone call from a prospective client today."}]],["reconcile","/ˈrekənsaɪl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “reconcile”.","reconcile [ˈrekənsaɪl] -2 vt. 使一致；使和解；调停，调解；使顺从 时态: reconciled, reconciling, reconciles (研六托雅宝 6560/5586)","欧陆词典释义：reconcile [ˈrekənsaɪl] -2 vt. 使一致；使和解；调停，调解；使顺从 时态: reconciled, reconciling, reconciles (研六托雅宝 6560/5586)","It's difficult to reconcile the demands of my job and the desire to be a good father...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to find an acceptable way of dealing with two or more ideas, needs, etc. that seem to be opposed to each other","example":"an attempt to reconcile the need for industrial development with concern for the environment"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make people become friends again after an argument or a disagreement","example":"It was hard to reconcile his career ambitions with the needs of his children."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make somebody/yourself accept an unpleasant situation because it is not possible to change it","example":"The pair were reconciled after Jackson made a public apology."}]],["redundant","/rɪˈdʌndənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “redundant”.","redundant [rɪˈdʌndənt] -2 adj. 多余的，过剩的；被解雇的，失业的；冗长的，累赘的 (研六托雅宝 12969/4968)","欧陆词典释义：redundant [rɪˈdʌndənt] -2 adj. 多余的，过剩的；被解雇的，失业的；冗长的，累赘的 (研六托雅宝 12969/4968)","My husband was made redundant late last year.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"without a job because there is no more work available for you in a company","example":"to be made redundant"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not needed or useful","example":"redundant employees"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"The picture has too much redundant detail."}]],["retrospective","/ˌretrəˈspektɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “retrospective”.","retrospective [ˌretrəˈspektɪv] -1 n. 回顾展 adj. 回顾的；怀旧的；可追溯的 (研托 9036/8807)","欧陆词典释义：retrospective [ˌretrəˈspektɪv] -1 n. 回顾展 adj. 回顾的；怀旧的；可追溯的 (研托 9036/8807)","a retrospective of the films of Judy Garland...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"thinking about or connected with something that happened in the past","example":"She felt a pang of retrospective sympathy for Mel."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"intended to take effect from a particular date in the past rather than from the present date","example":"retrospective legislation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a public exhibition of the work that an artist has done in the past, showing how his or her work has developed","example":"retrospective pay awards"}]],["abstraction","/æbˈstrækʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abstraction”.","abstraction [æbˈstrækʃn] -1 n. 抽象；提取；抽象概念；空想；心不在焉 (托 8413/7880)","欧陆词典释义：abstraction [æbˈstrækʃn] -1 n. 抽象；提取；抽象概念；空想；心不在焉 (托 8413/7880)","Is it worth fighting a big war, in the name of an abstraction like sovereignty?",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a general idea not based on any particular real person, thing or situation; the quality of being abstract","example":"She was gazing in abstraction at the far corner of the room."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the state of thinking deeply about something and not paying attention to what is around you","example":"water abstraction from rivers"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the action of removing something from something else; the process of being removed from something else","example":"Ideological abstractions are never going to attract many voters."}]],["accessibility","/əkˌsesə'bɪlətɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accessibility”.","accessibility [əkˌsesə'bɪlətɪ] n. 易接近；可亲；可以得到 (托 10407/12242)","欧陆词典释义：accessibility [əkˌsesə'bɪlətɪ] n. 易接近；可亲；可以得到 (托 10407/12242)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accessibility”.",""],["accountability","/əˌkaʊntə'bɪlətɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accountability”.","accountability [əˌkaʊntə'bɪlətɪ] n. 有义务；有责任；可说明性 (宝 4799/5194)","欧陆词典释义：accountability [əˌkaʊntə'bɪlətɪ] n. 有义务；有责任；可说明性 (宝 4799/5194)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accountability”.",""],["accumulation","/əˌkju:mjə'leɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accumulation”.","accumulation [əˌkju:mjə'leɪʃn] -1 n. 积聚，累积；堆积物 (托 8460/5822)","欧陆词典释义：accumulation [əˌkju:mjə'leɪʃn] -1 n. 积聚，累积；堆积物 (托 8460/5822)","an accumulation of experience and knowledge.",""],["analogy","/əˈnælədʒi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “analogy”.","analogy [əˈnælədʒi] -1 n. 类比；类推；类似 (研六托雅宝 5913/5394)","欧陆词典释义：analogy [əˈnælədʒi] -1 n. 类比；类推；类似 (研六托雅宝 5913/5394)","It is probably easier to make an analogy between the courses of the planets, and two trains travelling in the same direction.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a comparison of one thing with another thing that has similar features; a feature that is similar","example":"The teacher drew an analogy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of comparing one thing with another thing that has similar features in order to explain it","example":"There are no analogies with any previous legal cases."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"learning by analogy"}]],["assure","/əˈʃʊə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assure”.","assure [əˈʃʊə(r)] -K2 vt. 保证；担保；使确信；弄清楚 时态: assured, assuring, assures (研四六托雅宝 2571/2640)","欧陆词典释义：assure [əˈʃʊə(r)] -K2 vt. 保证；担保；使确信；弄清楚 时态: assured, assuring, assures (研四六托雅宝 2571/2640)","He hastened to assure me that there was nothing traumatic to report...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to tell somebody that something is definitely true or is definitely going to happen, especially when they have doubts about it","example":"You think I did it deliberately, but I assure you (that) I did not."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make yourself certain about something","example":"We were assured that everything possible was being done."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something certain to happen","example":"She's perfectly safe, I can assure you"}]],["beneficiary","/ˌbenɪˈfɪʃəri/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “beneficiary”.","beneficiary [ˌbenɪˈfɪʃəri] -1 n. [金融] 受益人，受惠者；封臣 adj. 拥有封地的；受圣俸的 (六托 6549/6087)","欧陆词典释义：beneficiary [ˌbenɪˈfɪʃəri] -1 n. [金融] 受益人，受惠者；封臣 adj. 拥有封地的；受圣俸的 (六托 6549/6087)","The main beneficiaries of pension equality so far have been men.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who gains as a result of something","example":"Who will be the main beneficiary of the cuts in income tax?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person who receives money or property when somebody dies","example":"She was the sole beneficiary of her father’s will."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"Who will be the main beneficiary of the cuts in income tax?"}]],["cognition","/kɒgˈnɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “cognition”.","cognition [kɒgˈnɪʃn] n. 认识；知识；认识能力 (10977/22519)","欧陆词典释义：cognition [kɒgˈnɪʃn] n. 认识；知识；认识能力 (10977/22519)","processes of perception and cognition .",""],["compliance","/kəmˈplaɪəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compliance”.","compliance [kəmˈplaɪəns] -1 n. 顺从，服从；承诺 (研雅宝 4547/4818)","欧陆词典释义：compliance [kəmˈplaɪəns] -1 n. 顺从，服从；承诺 (研雅宝 4547/4818)","Inspectors were sent to visit nuclear sites and verify compliance with the treaty...",""],["complication","/ˌkɒmplɪˈkeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “complication”.","complication [ˌkɒmplɪˈkeɪʃn] -2 n. 并发症；复杂；复杂化；混乱 (研六托雅 4995/4982)","欧陆词典释义：complication [ˌkɒmplɪˈkeɪʃn] -2 n. 并发症；复杂；复杂化；混乱 (研六托雅 4995/4982)","The age difference was a complication to the relationship...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that makes a situation more complicated or difficult","example":"The bad weather added a further complication to our journey."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a new problem or illness that makes treatment of a previous one more complicated or difficult","example":"She developed complications after the surgery."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Infertility is one of the complications of this type of radiotherapy."}]],["compute","/kəmˈpju:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compute”.","compute [kəmˈpju:t] -1 n. 计算；估计；推断 vt. 计算；估算；用计算机计算 vi. 计算；估算；推断 时态: computed, computing, computes (研四六托雅 7824/10477)","欧陆词典释义：compute [kəmˈpju:t] -1 n. 计算；估计；推断 vt. 计算；估算；用计算机计算 vi. 计算；估算；推断 时态: computed, computing, computes (研四六托雅 7824/10477)","I tried to compute the cash value of the ponies and horse boxes.",""],["concede","/kənˈsi:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “concede”.","concede [kənˈsi:d] -3 vi. 让步 vt. 承认；退让；给予，容许 时态: conceded, conceding, concedes (研六托雅宝 4192/3862)","欧陆词典释义：concede [kənˈsi:d] -3 vi. 让步 vt. 承认；退让；给予，容许 时态: conceded, conceding, concedes (研六托雅宝 4192/3862)","Bess finally concede d that Nancy was right...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to admit that something is true, logical, etc.","example":"‘Not bad,’ she conceded grudgingly."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give something away, especially unwillingly; to allow somebody to have something","example":"He was forced to concede (that) there might be difficulties."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to admit that you have lost a game, an election, etc.","example":"I had to concede the logic of this."}]],["contingency","/kənˈtɪndʒənsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contingency”.","contingency [kənˈtɪndʒənsi] -1 n. 偶然性；[安全] 意外事故；可能性；[审计] 意外开支；[离散数学或逻辑学]偶然式 (雅 8027/7087)","欧陆词典释义：contingency [kənˈtɪndʒənsi] -1 n. 偶然性；[安全] 意外事故；可能性；[审计] 意外开支；[离散数学或逻辑学]偶然式 (雅 8027/7087)","I need to examine all possible contingencies.",""],["deduction","/dɪˈdʌkʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deduction”.","deduction [dɪˈdʌkʃn] -2 n. 扣除，减除；推论；减除额 (7020/7701)","欧陆词典释义：deduction [dɪˈdʌkʃn] -2 n. 扣除，减除；推论；减除额 (7020/7701)","It was a pretty astute deduction ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of using information you have in order to understand a particular situation or to find the answer to a problem","example":"He arrived at the solution by a simple process of deduction."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of taking an amount of something, especially money, away from a total; the amount that is taken away","example":"If my deductions are correct, I can tell you who the killer was."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"We can examine the bones of dinosaurs and make deductions about how they lived."}]],["deficiency","/dɪˈfɪʃnsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deficiency”.","deficiency [dɪˈfɪʃnsi] -2 n. 缺陷，缺点；缺乏；不足的数额 (研六托雅宝 6360/5386)","欧陆词典释义：deficiency [dɪˈfɪʃnsi] -2 n. 缺陷，缺点；缺乏；不足的数额 (研六托雅宝 6360/5386)","They did blood tests on him for signs of vitamin deficiency ...",""],["deployment","/dɪ'plɔɪmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deployment”.","deployment [dɪ'plɔɪmənt] n. 调度，部署 (6428/8183)","欧陆词典释义：deployment [dɪ'plɔɪmənt] n. 调度，部署 (6428/8183)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deployment”.",""],["determinant","/dɪˈtɜ:mɪnənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “determinant”.","determinant [dɪˈtɜ:mɪnənt] -1 n. 决定因素；[数] 行列式 adj. 决定性的 (托宝 11034/8235)","欧陆词典释义：determinant [dɪˈtɜ:mɪnənt] -1 n. 决定因素；[数] 行列式 adj. 决定性的 (托宝 11034/8235)","The windows and the views beyond them are major determinant s of a room's character.",""],["deviation","/ˌdi:viˈeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deviation”.","deviation [ˌdi:viˈeɪʃn] n. 偏差；误差；背离 (六宝 6460/6723)","欧陆词典释义：deviation [ˌdi:viˈeɪʃn] n. 偏差；误差；背离 (六宝 6460/6723)","Deviation from the norm is not tolerated.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of moving away from what is normal or acceptable; a difference from what is expected or acceptable","example":"deviation from the previously accepted norms"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount by which a single measurement is different from the average","example":"sexual deviation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"a deviation from the plan"}]],["distinction","/dɪˈstɪŋkʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “distinction”.","distinction [dɪˈstɪŋkʃn] -2 n. 区别；差别；特性；荣誉、勋章 (高研四六托雅宝 2921/1865)","欧陆词典释义：distinction [dɪˈstɪŋkʃn] -2 n. 区别；差别；特性；荣誉、勋章 (高研四六托雅宝 2921/1865)","There are obvious distinction s between the two wine-making areas...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a clear difference or contrast especially between people or things that are similar or related","example":"distinctions between traditional and modern societies"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality of being excellent or important","example":"Philosophers did not use to make a distinction"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality of being something that is special","example":"We need to draw a distinction"}]],["domain","/dəˈmeɪn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “domain”.","domain [dəˈmeɪn] -1 n. 领域；域名；产业；地产 n. (Domain)人名；(英、法)多曼 (研六托雅宝 3627/3345)","欧陆词典释义：domain [dəˈmeɪn] -1 n. 领域；域名；产业；地产 n. (Domain)人名；(英、法)多曼 (研六托雅宝 3627/3345)","the great experimenters in the domain of art...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area of knowledge or activity; especially one that somebody is responsible for","example":"Financial matters are her domain."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"lands owned or ruled by a particular person, government, etc., especially in the past","example":"Physics used to be very much a male domain."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a set of websites on the Internet which end with the same group of letters, for example ‘","example":"The Spice Islands were within the Spanish domains."}]],["efficacy","/ˈefɪkəsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “efficacy”.","efficacy [ˈefɪkəsi] -1 n. 功效，效力 (托宝 6281/9115)","欧陆词典释义：efficacy [ˈefɪkəsi] -1 n. 功效，效力 (托宝 6281/9115)","Recent medical studies confirm the efficacy of a healthier lifestyle.",""],["elimination","/ɪˌlɪmɪ'neɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “elimination”.","elimination [ɪˌlɪmɪ'neɪʃn] n. 消除；淘汰；除去 (四六托 7330/7987)","欧陆词典释义：elimination [ɪˌlɪmɪ'neɪʃn] n. 消除；淘汰；除去 (四六托 7330/7987)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “elimination”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of removing or getting rid of something/somebody completely","example":"the elimination of disease/poverty/crime"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act or process of defeating a person or a team so that they no longer take part in a competition, etc.","example":"the elimination of toxins from the body"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of killing somebody, especially an enemy or opponent","example":"There were three eliminations in the first round of the competition."}]],["enrichment","/ɪn'rɪtʃmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “enrichment”.","enrichment [ɪn'rɪtʃmənt] n. 丰富；改进；肥沃；发财致富 (10003/12512)","欧陆词典释义：enrichment [ɪn'rɪtʃmənt] n. 丰富；改进；肥沃；发财致富 (10003/12512)","the enrichment of society.",""],["equivalence","/ɪ'kwɪvələns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “equivalence”.","equivalence [ɪ'kwɪvələns] n. 等值；相等 (17793/13194)","欧陆词典释义：equivalence [ɪ'kwɪvələns] n. 等值；相等 (17793/13194)","the equivalence of science and rationality.",""],["escalate","/ˈeskəleɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “escalate”.","escalate [ˈeskəleɪt] -2 vt. 使逐步上升 vi. 逐步增强；逐步升高 时态: escalated, escalating, escalates (研托雅宝 7542/11155)","欧陆词典释义：escalate [ˈeskəleɪt] -2 vt. 使逐步上升 vi. 逐步增强；逐步升高 时态: escalated, escalating, escalates (研托雅宝 7542/11155)","Both unions and management fear the dispute could escalate ...",""],["exploitation","/ˌeksplɔɪˈteɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “exploitation”.","exploitation [ˌeksplɔɪˈteɪʃn] n. 开发，开采；利用；广告推销；剥削 (研六托 6888/4853)","欧陆词典释义：exploitation [ˌeksplɔɪˈteɪʃn] n. 开发，开采；利用；广告推销；剥削 (研六托 6888/4853)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “exploitation”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a situation in which somebody treats somebody else in an unfair way, especially in order to make money from their work","example":"the exploitation of children"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the use of land, oil, minerals, etc.","example":"Starvation and poverty are the result of global economic exploitation, not lack of resources."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of using a situation in order to get an advantage for yourself","example":"commercial exploitation of the mineral resources in Antarctica"}]],["inclusion","/ɪnˈklu:ʒn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “inclusion”.","inclusion [ɪnˈklu:ʒn] n. 包含；内含物 (5409/5156)","欧陆词典释义：inclusion [ɪnˈklu:ʒn] n. 包含；内含物 (5409/5156)","a confident performance which justified his inclusion in the team.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the fact of including somebody/something; the fact of being included","example":"His inclusion in the team is in doubt."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person or thing that is included","example":"There were some surprising inclusions in the list."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"Legal issues precluded the interview’s inclusion on the DVD."}]],["induction","/ɪnˈdʌkʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “induction”.","induction [ɪnˈdʌkʃn] -1 n. [电磁] 感应；归纳法；感应现象；入门培训，入职仪式，就职；诱导 (六宝 10709/7240)","欧陆词典释义：induction [ɪnˈdʌkʃn] -1 n. [电磁] 感应；归纳法；感应现象；入门培训，入职仪式，就职；诱导 (六宝 10709/7240)","the induction of the girls into the sport.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of introducing somebody to a new job, skill, organization, etc.; a ceremony at which this takes place","example":"induction into the local business community"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of making a pregnant woman start to give birth, using artificial means such as a special drug","example":"The induction of new students will take place in the main hall."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a method of discovering general rules and principles from particular facts and examples","example":"the induction of labour"}]],["inequality","/ˌɪnɪˈkwɒləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “inequality”.","inequality [ˌɪnɪˈkwɒləti] -1 n. 不平等；不同；不平均 (6991/4436)","欧陆词典释义：inequality [ˌɪnɪˈkwɒləti] -1 n. 不平等；不同；不平均 (6991/4436)","People are concerned about social inequality ...",""],["inherit","/ɪnˈherɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “inherit”.","inherit [ɪnˈherɪt] -2 vt. 继承；遗传而得 vi. 成为继承人 时态: inherited, inheriting, inherits (研四六托雅宝 4471/3786)","欧陆词典释义：inherit [ɪnˈherɪt] -2 vt. 继承；遗传而得 vi. 成为继承人 时态: inherited, inheriting, inherits (研四六托雅宝 4471/3786)","He has no son to inherit his land.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to receive money, property, etc. from somebody when they die","example":"She inherited a fortune from her father."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to have qualities, physical features, etc. that are similar to those of your parents, grandparents, etc.","example":"He will inherit the title on the death of his uncle."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"if you inherit","example":"He has inherited his mother's patience."}]],["insight","/ˈɪnsaɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “insight”.","insight [ˈɪnsaɪt] -2 n. 洞察力；洞悉 n. (Insight)人名；(英)因赛特 (研四六托雅 2840/3302)","欧陆词典释义：insight [ˈɪnsaɪt] -2 n. 洞察力；洞悉 n. (Insight)人名；(英)因赛特 (研四六托雅 2840/3302)","The project would give scientists new insight s into what is happening to the earth's atmosphere...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to see and understand the truth about people or situations","example":"a writer of great insight"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an understanding of what something is like","example":"With a flash of insight I realized what the dream meant."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"The book gives us fascinating insights into life in Mexico."}]],["instability","/ˌɪnstəˈbɪləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “instability”.","instability [ˌɪnstəˈbɪləti] -2 n. 不稳定（性）；基础薄弱；不安定 (六 6926/7796)","欧陆词典释义：instability [ˌɪnstəˈbɪləti] -2 n. 不稳定（性）；基础薄弱；不安定 (六 6926/7796)","unpopular policies, which resulted in social discontent and political instability .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality of a situation in which things are likely to change or fail suddenly","example":"political and economic instability"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a mental condition in which somebody’s behaviour is likely to change suddenly","example":"mental/emotional instability"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"He showed increasing signs of mental instability."}]],["integration","/ˌɪntɪˈgreɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “integration”.","integration [ˌɪntɪˈgreɪʃn] n. 集成；综合 (3575/3170)","欧陆词典释义：integration [ˌɪntɪˈgreɪʃn] n. 集成；综合 (3575/3170)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “integration”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act or process of combining two or more things so that they work together","example":"The aim is to promote closer economic integration."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act or process of mixing people who have previously been separated, usually because of colour, race, religion, etc.","example":"His music is an integration of tradition and new technology."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"racial integration in schools"}]],["intensity","/ɪnˈtensəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “intensity”.","intensity [ɪnˈtensəti] n. 强度；强烈；[电子] 亮度；紧张 (研四六 3300/4017)","欧陆词典释义：intensity [ɪnˈtensəti] n. 强度；强烈；[电子] 亮度；紧张 (研四六 3300/4017)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “intensity”.",""],["interdependency","/ɪn'tədɪpendənsɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “interdependency”.","interdependency [ɪn'tədɪpendənsɪ] n. 互相依赖；相关性 (26359/38401)","欧陆词典释义：interdependency [ɪn'tədɪpendənsɪ] n. 互相依赖；相关性 (26359/38401)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “interdependency”.",""],["interval","/ˈɪntəvl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “interval”.","interval [ˈɪntəvl] -K2 n. 间隔；间距；幕间休息 (高研四六托雅 4646/2689)","欧陆词典释义：interval [ˈɪntəvl] -K2 n. 间隔；间距；幕间休息 (高研四六托雅 4646/2689)","The ferry service has restarted after an interval of 12 years...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a period of time between two events","example":"The interval between major earthquakes might be 200 years."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a short period of time separating parts of a play, film/movie or concert","example":"He knocked on the door and after a brief interval it was opened."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a short period during which something different happens from what is happening the rest of the time","example":"There will be an interval of 20 minutes after the second act."}]],["jurisdiction","/ˌdʒʊərɪsˈdɪkʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “jurisdiction”.","jurisdiction [ˌdʒʊərɪsˈdɪkʃn] -1 n. 司法权，审判权，管辖权；权限，权力 (托宝 4651/3477)","欧陆词典释义：jurisdiction [ˌdʒʊərɪsˈdɪkʃn] -1 n. 司法权，审判权，管辖权；权限，权力 (托宝 4651/3477)","The British police have no jurisdiction over foreign bank accounts.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the authority that an official organization has to make legal decisions about somebody/something","example":"The Court of Appeal exercised its jurisdiction to order a review of the case."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area or a country in which a particular system of laws has authority","example":"These matters do not fall within our jurisdiction."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"Practice varies between different European jurisdictions."}]],["justification","/ˌdʒʌstɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “justification”.","justification [ˌdʒʌstɪfɪˈkeɪʃn] -2 n. 理由；辩护；认为有理，认为正当；释罪 (六雅宝 5816/3708)","欧陆词典释义：justification [ˌdʒʌstɪfɪˈkeɪʃn] -2 n. 理由；辩护；认为有理，认为正当；释罪 (六雅宝 5816/3708)","To me the only justification for a zoo is educational...",""],["lateral","/ˈlætərəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “lateral”.","lateral [ˈlætərəl] -1 adj. 侧面的，横向的 n. 侧部；[语] 边音 vt. 横向传球 (研托雅宝 8322/7342)","欧陆词典释义：lateral [ˈlætərəl] -1 adj. 侧面的，横向的 n. 侧部；[语] 边音 vt. 横向传球 (研托雅宝 8322/7342)","McKinnon estimated the lateral movement of the bridge to be between four and six inches.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with the side of something or with movement to the side","example":"the lateral branches of a tree"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"lateral eye movements"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a consonant sound which is produced by placing a part of the tongue against the palate","example":"the lateral branches of a tree"}]],["likelihood","/ˈlaɪklihʊd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “likelihood”.","likelihood [ˈlaɪklihʊd] -2 n. 可能性，可能 (研四六雅 4596/4994)","欧陆词典释义：likelihood [ˈlaɪklihʊd] -2 n. 可能性，可能 (研四六雅 4596/4994)","The likelihood of infection is minimal...",""],["literal","/ˈlɪtərəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “literal”.","literal [ˈlɪtərəl] -1 adj. 文字的；逐字的；无夸张的 (六宝 7706/8711)","欧陆词典释义：literal [ˈlɪtərəl] -1 adj. 文字的；逐字的；无夸张的 (六宝 7706/8711)","In many cases, the people there are fighting, in a literal sense, for their homes.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"being the most basic meaning of a word or phrase, rather than an extended or poetic","example":"I am not referring to ‘small’ people in the literal sense of the word."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that follows the original words exactly","example":"The literal meaning of ‘petrify’ is ‘turn to stone’."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"lacking imagination","example":"a literal translation"}]],["longitudinal","/ˌlɒŋgɪˈtju:dɪnl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “longitudinal”.","longitudinal [ˌlɒŋgɪˈtju:dɪnl] adj. 长度的，纵向的；经线的 (9814/13011)","欧陆词典释义：longitudinal [ˌlɒŋgɪˈtju:dɪnl] adj. 长度的，纵向的；经线的 (9814/13011)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “longitudinal”.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"going downwards rather than across","example":"The plant's stem is marked with thin green longitudinal stripes."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"concerning the development of something over a period of time","example":"a longitudinal study of ageing"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with longitude","example":"the town’s longitudinal position"}]],["manifest","/ˈmænɪfest/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “manifest”.","manifest [ˈmænɪfest] -2 vt. 证明，表明；显示 vi. 显示，出现 n. 载货单，货单；旅客名单 adj. 显然的，明显的；明白的 时态: manifested, manifesting, manifests (研六雅宝 5931/6436)","欧陆词典释义：manifest [ˈmænɪfest] -2 vt. 证明，表明；显示 vi. 显示，出现 n. 载货单，货单；旅客名单 adj. 显然的，明显的；明白的 时态: manifested, manifesting, manifests (研六雅宝 5931/6436)","the manifest failure of the policies...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show something clearly, especially a feeling, an attitude or a quality","example":"Social tensions were manifested in the recent political crisis."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"to appear or become noticeable","example":"The symptoms of the disease manifested themselves ten days later."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"His nervousness was manifest to all those present."}]],["methodological","/ˌmeθədə'lɒdʒɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “methodological”.","methodological [ˌmeθədə'lɒdʒɪkl] adj. 方法的，方法论的 (10971/9331)","欧陆词典释义：methodological [ˌmeθədə'lɒdʒɪkl] adj. 方法的，方法论的 (10971/9331)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “methodological”.",""],["mobility","/məʊˈbɪləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mobility”.","mobility [məʊˈbɪləti] n. 移动性；机动性；[电子] 迁移率 (六托宝 5701/4407)","欧陆词典释义：mobility [məʊˈbɪləti] n. 移动性；机动性；[电子] 迁移率 (六托宝 5701/4407)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “mobility”.",""],["modification","/ˌmɒdɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “modification”.","modification [ˌmɒdɪfɪˈkeɪʃn] n. 修改，修正；改变 (六 5523/3751)","欧陆词典释义：modification [ˌmɒdɪfɪˈkeɪʃn] n. 修改，修正；改变 (六 5523/3751)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “modification”.",""],["motive","/ˈməʊtɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “motive”.","motive [ˈməʊtɪv] -2 n. 动机，目的；主题 adj. 发动的；成为动机的 vt. 使产生动机，激起 (研四六托 3578/3406)","欧陆词典释义：motive [ˈməʊtɪv] -2 n. 动机，目的；主题 adj. 发动的；成为动机的 vt. 使产生动机，激起 (研四六托 3578/3406)","Police have ruled out robbery as a motive for the killing.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a reason for doing something","example":"There seemed to be no motive for the murder."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"I'm suspicious of his motives."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"causing movement or action","example":"the profit motive ("}]],["narrative","/ˈnærətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “narrative”.","narrative [ˈnærətɪv] -2 n. 叙述；故事；讲述 adj. 叙事的，叙述的；叙事体的 (研六雅宝 3097/5167)","欧陆词典释义：narrative [ˈnærətɪv] -2 n. 叙述；故事；讲述 adj. 叙事的，叙述的；叙事体的 (研六雅宝 3097/5167)","a fast-moving narrative ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"describing events or telling a story","example":"narrative fiction"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a description of events, especially in a novel","example":"a narrative poem"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act, process or skill of telling a story","example":"a gripping narrative of their journey up the Amazon"}]],["normative","/ˈnɔ:mətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “normative”.","normative [ˈnɔ:mətɪv] -1 adj. 规范的，标准的 (8619/13073)","欧陆词典释义：normative [ˈnɔ:mətɪv] -1 adj. 规范的，标准的 (8619/13073)","Normative sexual behaviour in our society remains heterosexual.",""],["notable","/ˈnəʊtəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “notable”.","notable [ˈnəʊtəbl] -2 adj. 值得注意的，显著的；著名的 n. 名人，显要人物 (研六托雅宝 5293/4196)","欧陆词典释义：notable [ˈnəʊtəbl] -2 adj. 值得注意的，显著的；著名的 n. 名人，显要人物 (研六托雅宝 5293/4196)","The proposed new structure is notable not only for its height, but for its shape...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"deserving to be noticed or to receive attention; important","example":"a notable success/achievement/example"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"His eyes are his most notable feature"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a famous or important person","example":"The town is notable for its ancient harbour."}]],["numerical","/nju:ˈmerɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “numerical”.","numerical [nju:ˈmerɪkl] -1 adj. 数值的；数字的；用数字表示的（等于numeric） (研六托雅 10114/7312)","欧陆词典释义：numerical [nju:ˈmerɪkl] -1 adj. 数值的；数字的；用数字表示的（等于numeric） (研六托雅 10114/7312)","Your job is to group them by letter and put them in numerical order.",""],["abnormal","/æbˈnɔ:ml/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abnormal”.","abnormal [æbˈnɔ:ml] -1 adj. 反常的，不规则的；变态的 (高研四六托雅 8241/6548)","欧陆词典释义：abnormal [æbˈnɔ:ml] -1 adj. 反常的，不规则的；变态的 (高研四六托雅 8241/6548)"," abnormal heart rhythms and high anxiety levels.",""],["absolute","/ˈæbsəlu:t/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “absolute”.","absolute [ˈæbsəlu:t] -K3 n. 绝对；绝对事物 adj. 绝对的；完全的；专制的 (高研四六托宝 3165/2420)","欧陆词典释义：absolute [ˈæbsəlu:t] -K3 n. 绝对；绝对事物 adj. 绝对的；完全的；专制的 (高研四六托宝 3165/2420)","It's not really suited to absolute beginners...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"total and complete","example":"a class for absolute beginners"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used, especially in spoken English, to give emphasis to what you are saying","example":"absolute confidence/trust/silence/truth"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"definite and without any doubt or confusion","example":"‘You're wrong,’ she said with absolute certainty."}]],["absorb","/əbˈsɔ:b/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “absorb”.","absorb [əbˈsɔ:b] -K2 vt. 吸收；吸引；承受；理解；使…全神贯注 时态: absorbed, absorbing, absorbs (高研四六托雅宝 3120/2879)","欧陆词典释义：absorb [əbˈsɔ:b] -K2 vt. 吸收；吸引；承受；理解；使…全神贯注 时态: absorbed, absorbing, absorbs (高研四六托雅宝 3120/2879)","Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the air and moisture from the soil...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take in a liquid, gas or other substance from the surface or space around","example":"Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the air."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something smaller become part of something larger","example":"Let the rice cook until it has absorbed all the water."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take something into the mind and learn or understand it","example":"The cream is easily absorbed into the skin."}]],["accomplish","/əˈkʌmplɪʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accomplish”.","accomplish [əˈkʌmplɪʃ] -2 vt. 完成；实现；达到 时态: accomplished, accomplishing, accomplishes (高研四托雅宝 2345/5546)","欧陆词典释义：accomplish [əˈkʌmplɪʃ] -2 vt. 完成；实现；达到 时态: accomplished, accomplishing, accomplishes (高研四托雅宝 2345/5546)","If we'd all work together, I think we could accomplish our goal...",""],["accordance","/əˈkɔ:dns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accordance”.","accordance [əˈkɔ:dns] -1 n. 一致；和谐 (研四六 8086/32964)","欧陆词典释义：accordance [əˈkɔ:dns] -1 n. 一致；和谐 (研四六 8086/32964)","Entries which are not in accordance with the rules will be disqualified.",""],["activate","/ˈæktɪveɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “activate”.","activate [ˈæktɪveɪt] -1 vt. 刺激；使活动；使活泼；使产生放射性 vi. 激活；有活力 时态: activated, activating, activates (研托雅 6113/4543)","欧陆词典释义：activate [ˈæktɪveɪt] -1 vt. 刺激；使活动；使活泼；使产生放射性 vi. 激活；有活力 时态: activated, activating, activates (研托雅 6113/4543)","Video cameras with night vision can be activate d by movement.",""],["apparatus","/ˌæpəˈreɪtəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “apparatus”.","apparatus [ˌæpəˈreɪtəs] -1 n. 装置，设备；仪器；器官 (研四六雅宝 6978/5318)","欧陆词典释义：apparatus [ˌæpəˈreɪtəs] -1 n. 装置，设备；仪器；器官 (研四六雅宝 6978/5318)","For many years, the country had been buried under the apparatus of the regime.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the tools or other pieces of equipment that are needed for a particular activity or task","example":"a piece of laboratory apparatus"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the structure of a system or an organization, particularly that of a political party or a government","example":"Firefighters needed breathing apparatus to enter the burning house."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a system of organs in the body","example":"camping equipment"}]],["apprehension","/ˌæprɪˈhenʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “apprehension”.","apprehension [ˌæprɪˈhenʃn] n. 理解；恐惧；逮捕；忧惧 (托雅 9457/7714)","欧陆词典释义：apprehension [ˌæprɪˈhenʃn] n. 理解；恐惧；逮捕；忧惧 (托雅 9457/7714)","It reflects real anger and apprehension about the future...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"worry or fear that something unpleasant may happen","example":"There is growing apprehension that fighting will begin again."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of capturing or arresting somebody, usually by the police","example":"He watched the election results with some apprehension"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"There is apprehension about the safety of the missing children."}]],["audit","/ˈɔ:dɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “audit”.","audit [ˈɔ:dɪt] -2 n. 审计；[审计] 查账 vt. （美）旁听 vi. 审计；[审计] 查账 时态: audited, auditing, audits (研托雅宝 5503/3172)","欧陆词典释义：audit [ˈɔ:dɪt] -2 n. 审计；[审计] 查账 vt. （美）旁听 vi. 审计；[审计] 查账 时态: audited, auditing, audits (研托雅宝 5503/3172)","Each year they audit our accounts and certify them as being true and fair.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an official examination of business and financial records to see that they are true and correct","example":"an annual audit"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an official examination of the quality or standard of something","example":"a tax audit"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"preparing the accounts for audit"}]],["bankruptcy","/ˈbæŋkrʌptsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bankruptcy”.","bankruptcy [ˈbæŋkrʌptsi] -2 n. 破产 (六托 4171/5401)","欧陆词典释义：bankruptcy [ˈbæŋkrʌptsi] -2 n. 破产 (六托 4171/5401)","It is the second airline in two months to file for bankruptcy ...",""],["barrier","/ˈbæriə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “barrier”.","barrier [ˈbæriə(r)] -K3 n. 障碍物，屏障；界线 vt. 把…关入栅栏 n. (Barrier)人名；(法)巴里耶 (高研四六托雅宝 2609/2629)","欧陆词典释义：barrier [ˈbæriə(r)] -K3 n. 障碍物，屏障；界线 vt. 把…关入栅栏 n. (Barrier)人名；(法)巴里耶 (高研四六托雅宝 2609/2629)","Duties and taxes are the most obvious barrier to free trade.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an object like a fence that prevents people from moving forward from one place to another","example":"The crowd had to stand behind barriers."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a problem, rule or situation that prevents somebody from doing something, or that makes something impossible","example":"Show your ticket at the barrier."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"something that exists between one thing or person and another and keeps them separate","example":"The car crashed into the safety barrier and burst into flames."}]],["breach","/bri:tʃ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “breach”.","breach [bri:tʃ] -2 n. 违背，违反；缺口 vt. 违反，破坏；打破 时态: breached, breaching, breaches (研托雅宝 7862/2451)","欧陆词典释义：breach [bri:tʃ] -2 n. 违背，违反；缺口 vt. 违反，破坏；打破 时态: breached, breaching, breaches (研托雅宝 7862/2451)","The newspaper breach ed the code of conduct on privacy...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a failure to do something that must be done by law","example":"a breach of contract/copyright/warranty"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"an action that breaks an agreement to behave in a particular way","example":"They are in breach of"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"a break in a relationship between people or countries","example":"(a) breach of the peace"}]],["clarity","/ˈklærəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “clarity”.","clarity [ˈklærəti] -1 n. 清楚，明晰；透明 n. (Clarity)人名；(英)克拉里蒂 (研雅宝 5443/5359)","欧陆词典释义：clarity [ˈklærəti] -1 n. 清楚，明晰；透明 n. (Clarity)人名；(英)克拉里蒂 (研雅宝 5443/5359)","the ease and clarity with which the author explains difficult technical and scientific subjects.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality of being expressed clearly","example":"a lack of clarity in the law"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to think about or understand something clearly","example":"The brilliant clarity of his argument could not be faulted."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"if a picture, substance or sound has clarity","example":"clarity of thought/purpose/vision"}]],["collapse","/kəˈlæps/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “collapse”.","collapse [kəˈlæps] -K4 n. 倒塌；失败；衰竭 vt. 使倒塌，使崩溃；使萎陷；折叠 vi. 倒塌；瓦解；暴跌 时态: collapsed, collapsing, collapses (研四六托雅宝 3212/3094)","欧陆词典释义：collapse [kəˈlæps] -K4 n. 倒塌；失败；衰竭 vt. 使倒塌，使崩溃；使萎陷；折叠 vi. 倒塌；瓦解；暴跌 时态: collapsed, collapsing, collapses (研四六托雅宝 3212/3094)","A section of the Bay Bridge had collapse d...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to fall down or fall in suddenly, often after breaking apart","example":"The roof collapsed under the weight of snow."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to fall down (and usually become unconscious), especially because you are very ill/sick","example":"He collapsed in the street and died two hours later."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"to sit or lie down and relax, especially after working hard","example":"When I get home I like to collapse on the sofa and listen to music."}]],["communal","/kəˈmju:nl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “communal”.","communal [kəˈmju:nl] -2 adj. 公共的；公社的 n. (Communal)人名；(法)科米纳尔 (托宝 6398/6943)","欧陆词典释义：communal [kəˈmju:nl] -2 adj. 公共的；公社的 n. (Communal)人名；(法)科米纳尔 (托宝 6398/6943)","Communal violence broke out in different parts of the country.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"shared by, or for the use of, a number of people, especially people who live together","example":"a communal kitchen/garden, etc."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"involving different groups of people in a community","example":"As a student he tried communal living for a few years."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"early 19th cent.","example":"communal violence between religious groups"}]],["compassion","/kəmˈpæʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compassion”.","compassion [kəmˈpæʃn] -2 n. 同情；怜悯 (研托宝 4986/7736)","欧陆词典释义：compassion [kəmˈpæʃn] -2 n. 同情；怜悯 (研托宝 4986/7736)","Elderly people need time and compassion from their physicians.",""],["competent","/ˈkɒmpɪtənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “competent”.","competent [ˈkɒmpɪtənt] -2 adj. 胜任的；有能力的；能干的；足够的 (研四六托 5797/4995)","欧陆词典释义：competent [ˈkɒmpɪtənt] -2 adj. 胜任的；有能力的；能干的；足够的 (研四六托 5797/4995)","He was a loyal, distinguished and very competent civil servant.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having enough skill or knowledge to do something well or to the necessary standard","example":"Make sure the firm is competent to carry out the work."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"of a good standard but not very good","example":"He's very competent in his work."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"having the power to decide something","example":"I don’t feel competent to comment."}]],["complementarity","/ˌkɒmplɪmen'tærɪtɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “complementarity”.","complementarity [ˌkɒmplɪmen'tærɪtɪ] n. 互补性；补充；补足 (22346/36753)","欧陆词典释义：complementarity [ˌkɒmplɪmen'tærɪtɪ] n. 互补性；补充；补足 (22346/36753)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “complementarity”.",""],["complexity","/kəmˈpleksəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “complexity”.","complexity [kəmˈpleksəti] -2 n. 复杂，复杂性；复杂错综的事物 (六托 3757/3335)","欧陆词典释义：complexity [kəmˈpleksəti] -2 n. 复杂，复杂性；复杂错综的事物 (六托 3757/3335)","a diplomatic tangle of great complexity .",""],["conceal","/kənˈsi:l/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conceal”.","conceal [kənˈsi:l] -2 vt. 隐藏；隐瞒 时态: concealed, concealing, conceals (研四六托雅宝 5148/3994)","欧陆词典释义：conceal [kənˈsi:l] -2 vt. 隐藏；隐瞒 时态: concealed, concealing, conceals (研四六托雅宝 5148/3994)","Frances decided to conceal the machine behind a hinged panel...",""],["conception","/kənˈsepʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conception”.","conception [kənˈsepʃn] -2 n. 怀孕；概念；设想；开始 (六托雅宝 4636/3245)","欧陆词典释义：conception [kənˈsepʃn] -2 n. 怀孕；概念；设想；开始 (六托雅宝 4636/3245)","My conception of a garden was based on gardens I had visited in England...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of forming an idea or a plan","example":"The plan was brilliant in its conception but failed because of lack of money."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an understanding or a belief of what something is or what something should be","example":"Marx’s conception of social justice"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the process of an egg being fertilized","example":"He has no conception of"}]],["conclusive","/kənˈklu:sɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conclusive”.","conclusive [kənˈklu:sɪv] -1 adj. 决定性的；最后的；确实的；确定性的 (研托宝 12501/9670)","欧陆词典释义：conclusive [kənˈklu:sɪv] -1 adj. 决定性的；最后的；确实的；确定性的 (研托宝 12501/9670)","Her attorneys claim there is no conclusive evidence that any murders took place...",""],["confidential","/ˌkɒnfɪˈdenʃl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “confidential”.","confidential [ˌkɒnfɪˈdenʃl] -2 adj. 机密的；表示信任的；获信任的 (高研六托雅宝 7010/5254)","欧陆词典释义：confidential [ˌkɒnfɪˈdenʃl] -2 adj. 机密的；表示信任的；获信任的 (高研六托雅宝 7010/5254)","She accused them of leaking confidential information about her private life...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"meant to be kept secret and not told to or shared with other people","example":"confidential information/documents"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"showing that what you are saying is private or secret","example":"Your medical records are strictly confidential"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"trusted with private or secret information","example":"He spoke in a confidential tone, his voice low."}]],["confront","/kənˈfrʌnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “confront”.","confront [kənˈfrʌnt] -K3 vt. 面对；遭遇；比较 时态: confronted, confronting, confronts (研六托雅宝 2415/3105)","欧陆词典释义：confront [kənˈfrʌnt] -K3 vt. 面对；遭遇；比较 时态: confronted, confronting, confronts (研六托雅宝 2415/3105)","She was confront ed with severe money problems...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to appear and need to be dealt with by somebody","example":"the economic problems confronting the country"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to deal with a problem or difficult situation","example":"The government found itself confronted by massive opposition."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to face somebody so that they cannot avoid seeing and hearing you, especially in an unfriendly or dangerous situation","example":"She knew that she had to confront her fears."}]],["conformity","/kənˈfɔ:məti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conformity”.","conformity [kənˈfɔ:məti] -1 n. 一致，适合；符合；相似 (研六托宝 11474/8985)","欧陆词典释义：conformity [kənˈfɔ:məti] -1 n. 一致，适合；符合；相似 (研六托宝 11474/8985)","The prime minister is, in conformity with the constitution, chosen by the president.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"behaviour or actions that follow the accepted rules of society","example":"Governments often invoke patriotism to enforce conformity."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The procedure is in strict conformity with standard international practices."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"following the rules of something; conforming","example":"They act in unthinking conformity to customs."}]],["conquest","/ˈkɒŋkwest/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conquest”.","conquest [ˈkɒŋkwest] -1 n. 征服，战胜；战利品 n. (Conquest)人名；(英)康奎斯特 (研四六雅宝 7652/6507)","欧陆词典释义：conquest [ˈkɒŋkwest] -1 n. 征服，战胜；战利品 n. (Conquest)人名；(英)康奎斯特 (研四六雅宝 7652/6507)","He had led the conquest of southern Poland in 1939...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of taking control of a country, city, etc. by force","example":"the Norman Conquest ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an area of land taken by force","example":"the Spanish conquests in South America"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person that somebody has persuaded to love them or to have sex with them","example":"I'm just one of his many conquests."}]],["consolidation","/kənˌsɒlɪ'deɪʃən/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consolidation”.","consolidation [kənˌsɒlɪ'deɪʃən] n. 巩固；合并；团结 (宝 8504/9011)","欧陆词典释义：consolidation [kənˌsɒlɪ'deɪʃən] n. 巩固；合并；团结 (宝 8504/9011)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consolidation”.",""],["consistency","/kənˈsɪstənsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consistency”.","consistency [kənˈsɪstənsi] -1 n. [计] 一致性；稠度；相容性 (托宝 4975/5721)","欧陆词典释义：consistency [kənˈsɪstənsi] -1 n. [计] 一致性；稠度；相容性 (托宝 4975/5721)","He scores goals with remarkable consistency ...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the quality of always behaving in the same way or of having the same opinions, standard, etc.; the quality of being consistent","example":"She has played with great consistency all season."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the consistency","example":"We need to ensure the consistency of service to our customers."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"Beat the ingredients together to a creamy consistency."}]],["constraint","/kənˈstreɪnt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “constraint”.","constraint [kənˈstreɪnt] -2 n. [数] 约束；局促，态度不自然；强制 (六托宝 4643/2988)","欧陆词典释义：constraint [kənˈstreɪnt] -2 n. [数] 约束；局促，态度不自然；强制 (六托宝 4643/2988)","Their decision to abandon the trip was made because of financial constraint s...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a thing that limits or restricts something, or your freedom to do something","example":"constraints of time/money/space"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"strict control over the way that you behave or are allowed to behave","example":"financial/economic/legal/political constraints"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"This decision will impose serious constraints on all schools."}]],["contribution","/ˌkɒntrɪˈbju:ʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contribution”.","contribution [ˌkɒntrɪˈbju:ʃn] -K n. 贡献；捐献；投稿 (高研四雅 1776/1201)","欧陆词典释义：contribution [ˌkɒntrɪˈbju:ʃn] -K n. 贡献；捐献；投稿 (高研四雅 1776/1201)","American economists have made important contribution s to the field of financial and corporate economics...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a sum of money that is given to a person or an organization in order to help pay for something","example":"to make a contribution"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a sum of money that you pay regularly to your employer or the government in order to pay for benefits such as health insurance, a pension, etc.","example":"a substantial contribution"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an action or a service that helps to cause or increase something","example":"All contributions will be gratefully received."}]],["convenient","/kənˈvi:niənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “convenient”.","convenient [kənˈvi:niənt] -K2 adj. 方便的；[废语]适当的；[口语]近便的；实用的 (高研四六托雅 5368/3494)","欧陆词典释义：convenient [kənˈvi:niənt] -K2 adj. 方便的；[废语]适当的；[口语]近便的；实用的 (高研四六托雅 5368/3494)","a flexible and convenient way of paying for business expenses...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"useful, easy or quick to do; not causing problems","example":"It is very convenient to pay by credit card."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"near to a particular place; easy to get to","example":"You'll find these meals quick and convenient to prepare."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"Fruit is a convenient source of vitamins and energy."}]],["convey","/kənˈveɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “convey”.","convey [kənˈveɪ] -2 vt. 传达；运输；让与 时态: conveyed, conveying, conveys (高研四六托雅宝 3756/3682)","欧陆词典释义：convey [kənˈveɪ] -2 vt. 传达；运输；让与 时态: conveyed, conveying, conveys (高研四六托雅宝 3756/3682)","When I returned home, I tried to convey the wonder of this machine to my husband...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make ideas, feelings, etc. known to somebody","example":"Colours like red convey a sense of energy and strength."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to take, carry or transport somebody/something from one place to another","example":"Please convey my apologies to your wife."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"He tried desperately to convey how urgent the situation was."}]],["conviction","/kənˈvɪkʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conviction”.","conviction [kənˈvɪkʃn] -3 n. 定罪；确信；证明有罪；确信，坚定的信仰 (研六托雅宝 3066/2840)","欧陆词典释义：conviction [kənˈvɪkʃn] -3 n. 定罪；确信；证明有罪；确信，坚定的信仰 (研六托雅宝 3066/2840)","It is our firm conviction that a step forward has been taken...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of finding somebody guilty of a crime in court; the fact of having been found guilty","example":"She has six previous convictions for theft."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a strong opinion or belief","example":"He plans to appeal against his conviction."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the feeling or appearance of believing something strongly and of being sure about it","example":"an offence which carries, on conviction, a sentence of not more than five years’ imprisonment"}]],["coordination","/kəʊˌɔ:dɪˈneɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coordination”.","coordination [kəʊˌɔ:dɪˈneɪʃn] n. 协调，调和；对等，同等 (托 6072/9109)","欧陆词典释义：coordination [kəʊˌɔ:dɪˈneɪʃn] n. 协调，调和；对等，同等 (托 6072/9109)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coordination”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of making parts of something, groups of people, etc. work together in an efficient and organized way","example":"a need for greater coordination between departments"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to control your movements well","example":"a lack of coordination in conservation policy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"a pamphlet produced by the government in coordination with"}]],["correspondence","/ˌkɒrəˈspɒndəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “correspondence”.","correspondence [ˌkɒrəˈspɒndəns] -2 n. 通信；一致；相当 (研六托雅 5961/4152)","欧陆词典释义：correspondence [ˌkɒrəˈspɒndəns] -2 n. 通信；一致；相当 (研六托雅 5961/4152)","The judges' decision is final and no correspondence will be entered into...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the letters a person sends and receives","example":"personal/private correspondence"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the activity of writing letters","example":"The editor welcomes correspondence from readers on any subject."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a connection between two things; the fact of two things being similar","example":"the correspondence column/page"}]],["crude","/kru:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “crude”.","crude [kru:d] -2 n. 原油；天然的物质 adj. 粗糙的；天然的，未加工的；粗鲁的 级别: cruder, crudest (研四六托雅 5015/4502)","欧陆词典释义：crude [kru:d] -2 n. 原油；天然的物质 adj. 粗糙的；天然的，未加工的；粗鲁的 级别: cruder, crudest (研四六托雅 5015/4502)","Standard measurements of blood pressure are an important but crude way of assessing the risk of heart disease or strokes...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"simple and not very accurate but giving a general idea of something","example":"In crude terms"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"simply made, not showing much skill or attention to detail","example":"a crude drawing of a face"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"offensive or rude, especially about sex","example":"crude jokes/language"}]],["currency","/ˈkʌrənsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “currency”.","currency [ˈkʌrənsi] -4 n. 货币；通货 (高研六托雅 3738/2114)","欧陆词典释义：currency [ˈkʌrənsi] -4 n. 货币；通货 (高研六托雅 3738/2114)","Tourism is the country's top earner of foreign currency ...",""],["dedication","/ˌdedɪˈkeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dedication”.","dedication [ˌdedɪˈkeɪʃn] n. 奉献；献身；赠言 (雅宝 6990/6951)","欧陆词典释义：dedication [ˌdedɪˈkeɪʃn] n. 奉献；献身；赠言 (雅宝 6990/6951)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dedication”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the hard work and effort that somebody puts into an activity or a purpose because they think it is important","example":"hard work and dedication"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a ceremony that is held to show that a building or an object has a special purpose or is special to the memory of a particular person","example":"I really admire Gina for her dedication to her family."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the words that are used at the beginning of a book, piece of music, a performance, etc. to offer it to somebody as a sign of thanks or respect","example":"It takes dedication to be successful in a sport."}]],["deficit","/ˈdefɪsɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deficit”.","deficit [ˈdefɪsɪt] -4 n. 赤字；不足额 (研六托雅宝 2403/2918)","欧陆词典释义：deficit [ˈdefɪsɪt] -4 n. 赤字；不足额 (研六托雅宝 2403/2918)","They're ready to cut the federal budget deficit for the next fiscal year.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount by which money spent or owed is greater than money earned in a particular period of time","example":"a budget/trade deficit"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the amount by which something, especially an amount of money, is too small or smaller than something else","example":"The trade balance has been in deficit"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 18th cent.","example":"There's a deficit of $3 million in the total needed to complete the project."}]],["deliberate","/dɪˈlɪbərət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deliberate”.","deliberate [dɪˈlɪbərət] -K3 adj. 故意的；深思熟虑的；从容的 vt. 仔细考虑；商议 时态: deliberated, deliberating, deliberates (研四六托雅宝 6343/4700)","欧陆词典释义：deliberate [dɪˈlɪbərət] -K3 adj. 故意的；深思熟虑的；从容的 vt. 仔细考虑；商议 时态: deliberated, deliberating, deliberates (研四六托雅宝 6343/4700)","It has a deliberate policy to introduce world art to Britain...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"done on purpose rather than by accident","example":"a deliberate act of vandalism"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"done slowly and carefully","example":"The speech was a deliberate attempt to embarrass the government."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"She spoke in a slow and deliberate way."}]],["denial","/dɪˈnaɪəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “denial”.","denial [dɪˈnaɪəl] -2 n. 否认；拒绝；节制；背弃 (研六雅 4743/6046)","欧陆词典释义：denial [dɪˈnaɪəl] -2 n. 否认；拒绝；节制；背弃 (研六雅 4743/6046)","Despite official denial s, the rumours still persist...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a statement that says something is not true or does not exist","example":"the prisoner’s repeated denials of the charges against him"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a refusal to allow somebody to have something they have a right to expect","example":"The terrorists issued a denial of responsibility for the attack."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a refusal to accept that something unpleasant or painful is true","example":"an official denial that there would be an election before the end of the year"}]],["dependency","/dɪˈpendənsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dependency”.","dependency [dɪˈpendənsi] -1 n. 属国；从属；从属物 (7839/6214)","欧陆词典释义：dependency [dɪˈpendənsi] -1 n. 属国；从属；从属物 (7839/6214)","the tiny British dependency of Montserrat in the eastern Caribbean.",""],["deprive","/dɪˈpraɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “deprive”.","deprive [dɪˈpraɪv] -2 vt. 使丧失，剥夺 时态: deprived, depriving, deprives (研六托雅 6202/4489)","欧陆词典释义：deprive [dɪˈpraɪv] -2 vt. 使丧失，剥夺 时态: deprived, depriving, deprives (研六托雅 6202/4489)","The disintegration of the Soviet Union deprive d western intelligence agencies of their main enemies...",""],["desirable","/dɪˈzaɪərəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “desirable”.","desirable [dɪˈzaɪərəbl] -2 n. 合意的人或事物 adj. 令人满意的；值得要的 (研四六托雅宝 5313/3408)","欧陆词典释义：desirable [dɪˈzaɪərəbl] -2 n. 合意的人或事物 adj. 令人满意的；值得要的 (研四六托雅宝 5313/3408)","Prolonged negotiation was not desirable ...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that you would like to have or do; worth having or doing","example":"She chatted for a few minutes about the qualities she considered desirable in"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"causing other people to feel sexual desire","example":"Such measures are desirable, if not essential."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The house has many desirable features."}]],["destructive","/dɪˈstrʌktɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “destructive”.","destructive [dɪˈstrʌktɪv] -2 adj. 破坏的；毁灭性的；有害的，消极的 (研四六托雅 5818/6370)","欧陆词典释义：destructive [dɪˈstrʌktɪv] -2 adj. 破坏的；毁灭性的；有害的，消极的 (研四六托雅 5818/6370)","the awesome destructive power of nuclear weapons...",""],["detectable","/diˈtektəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “detectable”.","detectable [diˈtektəbl] adj. 可检测的；可发觉的 (托 15404/12671)","欧陆词典释义：detectable [diˈtektəbl] adj. 可检测的；可发觉的 (托 15404/12671)","Doctors say the disease is probably inherited but not detectable at birth.",""],["abolition","/ˌæbəˈlɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abolition”.","abolition [ˌæbəˈlɪʃn] n. 废除；废止 (托宝 13737/5158)","欧陆词典释义：abolition [ˌæbəˈlɪʃn] n. 废除；废止 (托宝 13737/5158)","the abolition of slavery in Brazil and the Caribbean.",""],["abrupt","/əˈbrʌpt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abrupt”.","abrupt [əˈbrʌpt] -2 adj. 生硬的；突然的；唐突的；陡峭的 (高研六托雅宝 8703/8560)","欧陆词典释义：abrupt [əˈbrʌpt] -2 adj. 生硬的；突然的；唐突的；陡峭的 (高研六托雅宝 8703/8560)","Rosie's idyllic world came to an abrupt end when her parents' marriage broke up...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"sudden and unexpected, often in an unpleasant way","example":"an abrupt change/halt/departure"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"speaking or acting in a way that seems unfriendly and rude; not taking time to say more than is necessary","example":"The accident brought his career to an abrupt end."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late 16th cent.","example":"an abrupt manner"}]],["accommodation","/əˌkɒməˈdeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accommodation”.","accommodation [əˌkɒməˈdeɪʃn] -K2 n. 住处，膳宿；调节；和解；预订铺位 (高研四六雅 5369/2048)","欧陆词典释义：accommodation [əˌkɒməˈdeɪʃn] -K2 n. 住处，膳宿；调节；和解；预订铺位 (高研四六雅 5369/2048)","The government will provide temporary accommodation for up to three thousand people...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a place to live, work or stay in","example":"rented/temporary/furnished accommodation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"somewhere to live or stay, often also providing food or other services","example":"Hotel accommodation is included in the price of your holiday."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"an agreement or arrangement between people or groups with different opinions which is acceptable to everyone; the process of reaching this agreement","example":"The building plans include much needed new office accommodation."}]],["accounting","/əˈkaʊntɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accounting”.","accounting [əˈkaʊntɪŋ] -2 n. 会计，会计学；账单 v. 解释（account的ing形式）；叙述 原型: accounting 是 account 的现在分词 (托雅 3921/3070)","欧陆词典释义：accounting [əˈkaʊntɪŋ] -2 n. 会计，会计学；账单 v. 解释（account的ing形式）；叙述 原型: accounting 是 account 的现在分词 (托雅 3921/3070)","allegations of theft, forgery and false accounting .",""],["accordingly","/əˈkɔ:dɪŋli/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accordingly”.","accordingly [əˈkɔ:dɪŋli] -2 adv. 因此，于是；相应地；照著 (研四六 5589/3199)","欧陆词典释义：accordingly [əˈkɔ:dɪŋli] -2 adv. 因此，于是；相应地；照著 (研四六 5589/3199)","We have a different background, a different history. Accordingly, we have the right to different futures...",""],["accuracy","/ˈækjərəsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accuracy”.","accuracy [ˈækjərəsi] n. [数] 精确度，准确性 (高研四六托雅宝 4076/3958)","欧陆词典释义：accuracy [ˈækjərəsi] n. [数] 精确度，准确性 (高研四六托雅宝 4076/3958)","We cannot guarantee the accuracy of these figures.",""],["adaptable","/əˈdæptəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adaptable”.","adaptable [əˈdæptəbl] -1 adj. 适合的；能适应的；可修改的 (托宝 14811/13973)","欧陆词典释义：adaptable [əˈdæptəbl] -1 adj. 适合的；能适应的；可修改的 (托宝 14811/13973)","a more adaptable and skilled workforce...",""],["adequate","/ˈædɪkwət/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adequate”.","adequate [ˈædɪkwət] -K3 adj. 充足的；适当的；胜任的 (高研四六托雅宝 3297/2398)","欧陆词典释义：adequate [ˈædɪkwət] -K3 adj. 充足的；适当的；胜任的 (高研四六托雅宝 3297/2398)","One in four people worldwide are without adequate homes...",""],["adoption","/əˈdɒpʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adoption”.","adoption [əˈdɒpʃn] n. 采用；收养；接受 (六托 3674/4220)","欧陆词典释义：adoption [əˈdɒpʃn] n. 采用；收养；接受 (六托 3674/4220)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adoption”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of adopting a child","example":"She put the baby up for adoption."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the decision to start using something such as an idea, a plan or a name","example":"the adoption of new technology"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of choosing somebody as a candidate for an election","example":"his adoption as the Labour candidate"}]],["adversity","/ədˈvɜ:səti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adversity”.","adversity [ədˈvɜ:səti] -1 n. 逆境；不幸；灾难；灾祸 (托 11343/14307)","欧陆词典释义：adversity [ədˈvɜ:səti] -1 n. 逆境；不幸；灾难；灾祸 (托 11343/14307)","He showed courage in adversity .",""],["advocacy","/ˈædvəkəsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “advocacy”.","advocacy [ˈædvəkəsi] -1 n. 主张；拥护；辩护 (宝 5074/10533)","欧陆词典释义：advocacy [ˈædvəkəsi] -1 n. 主张；拥护；辩护 (宝 5074/10533)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “advocacy”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the giving of public support to an idea, a course of action or a belief","example":"He won the Peace Prize for his advocacy of non-violent protest."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the work of lawyers who speak about cases in court","example":"He won the Peace Prize for his advocacy of non-violent protest."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"He won the Peace Prize for his advocacy of non-violent protest."}]],["alleviation","/əˌli:vɪ'eɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “alleviation”.","alleviation [əˌli:vɪ'eɪʃn] n. 缓和；镇痛物 (23947/22740)","欧陆词典释义：alleviation [əˌli:vɪ'eɪʃn] n. 缓和；镇痛物 (23947/22740)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “alleviation”.",""],["analytical","/ˌænəˈlɪtɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “analytical”.","analytical [ˌænəˈlɪtɪkl] -1 adj. 分析的；解析的；善于分析的 原型: analytic (六雅 7338/6653)","欧陆词典释义：analytical [ˌænəˈlɪtɪkl] -1 adj. 分析的；解析的；善于分析的 原型: analytic (六雅 7338/6653)","I have an analytical approach to every survey.",""],["apparent","/əˈpærənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “apparent”.","apparent [əˈpærənt] -K3 adj. 显然的；表面上的 (高研四六雅 2502/1770)","欧陆词典释义：apparent [əˈpærənt] -K3 adj. 显然的；表面上的 (高研四六雅 2502/1770)","I was a bit depressed by our apparent lack of progress...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"easy to see or understand","example":"Their devotion was apparent."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"that seems to be real or true but may not be","example":"Then, for no apparent reason"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"It was apparent from her face that she was really upset."}]],["applicable","/əˈplɪkəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “applicable”.","applicable [əˈplɪkəbl] -1 adj. 可适用的；可应用的；合适的 (研四六宝 7582/4629)","欧陆词典释义：applicable [əˈplɪkəbl] -1 adj. 可适用的；可应用的；合适的 (研四六宝 7582/4629)","What is a reasonable standard for one family is not applicable for another...",""],["architecture","/ˈɑ:kɪtektʃə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “architecture”.","architecture [ˈɑ:kɪtektʃə(r)] -2 n. 建筑学；建筑风格；建筑式样；架构 (高研四六托雅 3509/2712)","欧陆词典释义：architecture [ˈɑ:kɪtektʃə(r)] -2 n. 建筑学；建筑风格；建筑式样；架构 (高研四六托雅 3509/2712)","He studied classical architecture and design in Rome.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the art and study of designing buildings","example":"to study architecture"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the design or style of a building or buildings","example":"the architecture of the eighteenth century"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the design and structure of a computer system","example":"modern architecture"}]],["attainable","/əˈteɪnəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attainable”.","attainable [əˈteɪnəbl] adj. 可得到的；可达到的；可到达的 (17650/18781)","欧陆词典释义：attainable [əˈteɪnəbl] adj. 可得到的；可达到的；可到达的 (17650/18781)","It is unrealistic to believe perfection is an attainable goal.",""],["autonomy","/ɔ:ˈtɒnəmi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “autonomy”.","autonomy [ɔ:ˈtɒnəmi] n. 自治，自治权 (研托雅宝 4712/3908)","欧陆词典释义：autonomy [ɔ:ˈtɒnəmi] n. 自治，自治权 (研托雅宝 4712/3908)","Activists stepped up their demands for local autonomy last month.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the freedom for a country, a region or an organization to govern itself independently","example":"a campaign in Wales for greater autonomy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the ability to act and make decisions without being controlled by anyone else","example":"giving individuals greater autonomy in their own lives"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 17th cent.","example":"Head office is giving the regional offices more autonomy."}]],["coherence","/kəʊˈhɪərəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “coherence”.","coherence [kəʊˈhɪərəns] n. 一致；连贯性；凝聚 (托 11502/10272)","欧陆词典释义：coherence [kəʊˈhɪərəns] n. 一致；连贯性；凝聚 (托 11502/10272)","The anthology has a surprising sense of coherence .",""],["collaboration","/kəˌlæbəˈreɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “collaboration”.","collaboration [kəˌlæbəˈreɪʃn] -2 n. 合作；勾结；通敌 (六托雅 4176/4618)","欧陆词典释义：collaboration [kəˌlæbəˈreɪʃn] -2 n. 合作；勾结；通敌 (六托雅 4176/4618)","There is substantial collaboration with neighbouring departments...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of working with another person or group of people to create or produce something","example":"It was a collaboration that produced extremely useful results."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a piece of work produced by two or more people or groups of people working together","example":"The new plane was a triumph of European industrial and technical collaboration."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of helping the enemy during a war when they have taken control of your country","example":"She wrote the book in collaboration"}]],["collective","/kəˈlektɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “collective”.","collective [kəˈlektɪv] -3 n. 集团；集合体；集合名词 adj. 集体的；共同的；集合的；集体主义的 (研四六托 3342/3132)","欧陆词典释义：collective [kəˈlektɪv] -3 n. 集团；集合体；集合名词 adj. 集体的；共同的；集合的；集体主义的 (研四六托 3342/3132)","It was a collective decision...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"done or shared by all members of a group of people; involving a whole group or society","example":"collective leadership/decision-making/responsibility"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"used to refer to all members of a group","example":"collective memory ("},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"The collective name for mast, boom and sails on a boat is the ‘rig’."}]],["compatibility","/kəmˌpætəˈbɪləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compatibility”.","compatibility [kəmˌpætəˈbɪləti] n. [计] 兼容性 (六 12951/9133)","欧陆词典释义：compatibility [kəmˌpætəˈbɪləti] n. [计] 兼容性 (六 12951/9133)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compatibility”.",""],["compensation","/ˌkɒmpenˈseɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “compensation”.","compensation [ˌkɒmpenˈseɪʃn] -3 n. 补偿；报酬；赔偿金 (研六托雅 3796/2611)","欧陆词典释义：compensation [ˌkɒmpenˈseɪʃn] -3 n. 补偿；报酬；赔偿金 (研六托雅 3796/2611)","He received one year's salary as compensation for loss of office...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"something, especially money, that somebody gives you because they have hurt you, or damaged something that you own; the act of giving this to somebody","example":"to claim/award/receive compensation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"things that make a bad situation better","example":"to pay compensation for injuries at work"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"to receive £10 000 in compensation"}]],["component","/kəmˈpəʊnənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “component”.","component [kəmˈpəʊnənt] -3 n. 成分；组件；[电子] 元件 adj. 组成的，构成的 (高研四六托雅宝 1760/1631)","欧陆词典释义：component [kəmˈpəʊnənt] -3 n. 成分；组件；[电子] 元件 adj. 组成的，构成的 (高研四六托雅宝 1760/1631)","Enriched uranium is a key component of a nuclear weapon...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"used to describe one of several parts of which something is made","example":"Break the problem down into its component parts"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"one of several parts of which something is made","example":"the components of a machine"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 17th cent.","example":"the car component industry"}]],["consequence","/ˈkɒnsɪkwəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consequence”.","consequence [ˈkɒnsɪkwəns] -K3 n. 结果；重要性；推论 (高研四六托雅宝 1626/1234)","欧陆词典释义：consequence [ˈkɒnsɪkwəns] -K3 n. 结果；重要性；推论 (高研四六托雅宝 1626/1234)","Her lawyer said she understood the consequence s of her actions and was prepared to go to jail...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a result of something that has happened","example":"This decision could have serious consequences"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"importance","example":"Two hundred people lost their jobs as a"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a game in which each player writes the first line of a story on a piece of paper and then passes it to the next player who writes the second line, and so on. Each player folds the paper so that the next player cannot see what is already written. The result is a number of crazy and often funny stories. The stories follow a pattern that always begins with the names of two people and ends with the sentence 'And the consequence was…’","example":"He drove too fast with tragic consequences."}]],["considerable","/kənˈsɪdərəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “considerable”.","considerable [kənˈsɪdərəbl] -K4 adj. 相当大的；重要的，值得考虑的 (研四六托雅宝 2855/1042)","欧陆词典释义：considerable [kənˈsɪdərəbl] -K4 adj. 相当大的；重要的，值得考虑的 (研四六托雅宝 2855/1042)","To be without Pearce would be a considerable blow...",""],["abide","/əˈbaɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abide”.","abide [əˈbaɪd] -1 vi. 持续；忍受；停留 vt. 忍受，容忍；停留；遵守 时态: abided, abiding, abides (研六托宝 8457/9496)","欧陆词典释义：abide [əˈbaɪd] -1 vi. 持续；忍受；停留 vt. 忍受，容忍；停留；遵守 时态: abided, abiding, abides (研六托宝 8457/9496)","I can't abide people who can't make up their minds...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to dislike somebody/something so much that you hate having to be with or deal with them","example":"I can't abide people with no sense of humour."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to stay or live in a place","example":"He couldn't abide the thought of being cooped up in an office."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"I can’t abide people who look down on others."}]],["abnormality","/ˌæbnɔ:ˈmæləti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abnormality”.","abnormality [ˌæbnɔ:ˈmæləti] -1 n. 异常；畸形，变态 (11416/7380)","欧陆词典释义：abnormality [ˌæbnɔ:ˈmæləti] -1 n. 异常；畸形，变态 (11416/7380)","Further scans are required to confirm the diagnosis of an abnormality ...",""],["abundance","/əˈbʌndəns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “abundance”.","abundance [əˈbʌndəns] -1 n. 充裕，丰富 (研六托雅宝 5425/7038)","欧陆词典释义：abundance [əˈbʌndəns] -1 n. 充裕，丰富 (研六托雅宝 5425/7038)","The area has an abundance of wildlife...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a large quantity that is more than enough","example":"Exotic plants grew there in great abundance."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"The brochure promised beautiful walks with an abundance of wildlife."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"in large quantities","example":"The country has an abundance of natural resources."}]],["accelerated","/æk'seləreɪtɪd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accelerated”.","accelerated [æk'seləreɪtɪd] v. 加速；促进（accelerate的变形） adj. 加速的；加快的 原型: accelerated 是 accelerate 的过去式和过去分词 (托 10808/14045)","欧陆词典释义：accelerated [æk'seləreɪtɪd] v. 加速；促进（accelerate的变形） adj. 加速的；加快的 原型: accelerated 是 accelerate 的过去式和过去分词 (托 10808/14045)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accelerated”.",""],["adhere","/ədˈhɪə(r)/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adhere”.","adhere [ədˈhɪə(r)] -2 vi. 坚持；依附；粘着；追随 vt. 使粘附 时态: adhered, adhering, adheres (研四六托雅宝 6516/6380)","欧陆词典释义：adhere [ədˈhɪə(r)] -2 vi. 坚持；依附；粘着；追随 vt. 使粘附 时态: adhered, adhering, adheres (研四六托雅宝 6516/6380)","All members of the association adhere to a strict code of practice...",""],["adversarial","/ˌædvəˈseəriəl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adversarial”.","adversarial [ˌædvəˈseəriəl] adj. 对抗的；对手的，敌手的 (15137/20802)","欧陆词典释义：adversarial [ˌædvəˈseəriəl] adj. 对抗的；对手的，敌手的 (15137/20802)","In our country there is an adversarial relationship between government and business.",""],["affinity","/əˈfɪnəti/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “affinity”.","affinity [əˈfɪnəti] -1 n. 密切关系；吸引力；姻亲关系；类同 (托宝 9246/6169)","欧陆词典释义：affinity [əˈfɪnəti] -1 n. 密切关系；吸引力；姻亲关系；类同 (托宝 9246/6169)","He has a close affinity with the landscape he knew when he was growing up...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a strong feeling that you understand somebody/something and like them or it","example":"Sam was born in the country and had a deep affinity with nature."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a close relationship between two people or things that have similar qualities, structures or features","example":"Humans have a special affinity for dolphins."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"Middle English","example":"There is a close affinity between Italian and Spanish."}]],["aggravate","/ˈægrəveɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “aggravate”.","aggravate [ˈægrəveɪt] -1 vt. 加重；使恶化；激怒 时态: aggravated, aggravating, aggravates (研六托雅宝 9820/9460)","欧陆词典释义：aggravate [ˈægrəveɪt] -1 vt. 加重；使恶化；激怒 时态: aggravated, aggravating, aggravates (研六托雅宝 9820/9460)","Stress and lack of sleep can aggravate the situation...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make an illness or a bad or unpleasant situation worse","example":"Pollution can aggravate asthma."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to annoy somebody, especially deliberately","example":"Military intervention will only aggravate the conflict even further."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"mid 16th cent.","example":"The government’s actions will only aggravate the problem."}]],["allegation","/ˌæləˈgeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “allegation”.","allegation [ˌæləˈgeɪʃn] -3 n. 指控; 陈述，主张; 宣称; 陈词，陈述; (六托 3516/3459)","欧陆词典释义：allegation [ˌæləˈgeɪʃn] -3 n. 指控; 陈述，主张; 宣称; 陈词，陈述; (六托 3516/3459)","The company has denied the allegation s...",""],["ambivalence","/æm'bɪvələns/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ambivalence”.","ambivalence [æm'bɪvələns] n. [心理] 矛盾情绪；正反感情并存 (托宝 9873/12403)","欧陆词典释义：ambivalence [æm'bɪvələns] n. [心理] 矛盾情绪；正反感情并存 (托宝 9873/12403)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “ambivalence”.",""],["amendment","/əˈmendmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “amendment”.","amendment [əˈmendmənt] -3 n. 修正案；改善；改正 (托宝 3667/2864)","欧陆词典释义：amendment [əˈmendmənt] -3 n. 修正案；改善；改正 (托宝 3667/2864)","an amendment to the defense bill.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a small change or improvement that is made to a law or a document; the process of changing a law or a document","example":"to introduce/propose/table an amendment"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a statement of a change to the Constitution","example":"Parliament passed the bill without further amendment."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"In the US the first ten amendments to the Constitution are called the Bill of Rights","example":"She made several minor amendments to her essay."}]],["appreciation","/əˌpri:ʃiˈeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “appreciation”.","appreciation [əˌpri:ʃiˈeɪʃn] n. 欣赏，鉴别；增值；感谢 (高六托 4322/4701)","欧陆词典释义：appreciation [əˌpri:ʃiˈeɪʃn] n. 欣赏，鉴别；增值；感谢 (高六托 4322/4701)","an investigation into children's understanding and appreciation of art...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"pleasure that you have when you recognize and enjoy the good qualities of somebody/something","example":"She shows little appreciation of good music."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a full or sympathetic understanding of something, such as a situation or a problem, and of what it involves","example":"The crowd murmured in appreciation"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the feeling of being grateful for something","example":"I had no appreciation of the problems they faced."}]],["assertion","/əˈsɜ:ʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assertion”.","assertion [əˈsɜ:ʃn] n. 断言，声明；主张，要求；坚持；认定 (5339/5380)","欧陆词典释义：assertion [əˈsɜ:ʃn] n. 断言，声明；主张，要求；坚持；认定 (5339/5380)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assertion”.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a statement saying that you strongly believe something to be true","example":"He was correct in his assertion that the minister had been lying."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of stating, using or claiming something strongly","example":"Do you have any evidence to support your assertions?"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"the assertion of his authority"}]],["attainment","/əˈteɪnmənt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attainment”.","attainment [əˈteɪnmənt] -1 n. 达到；成就；学识 (托宝 10837/5891)","欧陆词典释义：attainment [əˈteɪnmənt] -1 n. 达到；成就；学识 (托宝 10837/5891)","the attainment of independence.",""],["benchmark","/ˈbentʃmɑ:k/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “benchmark”.","benchmark [ˈbentʃmɑ:k] -1 n. 基准；标准检查程序 vt. 用基准问题测试（计算机系统等） (8070/12631)","欧陆词典释义：benchmark [ˈbentʃmɑ:k] -1 n. 基准；标准检查程序 vt. 用基准问题测试（计算机系统等） (8070/12631)","The truck industry is a benchmark for the economy.",""],["bureaucracy","/bjʊəˈrɒkrəsi/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “bureaucracy”.","bureaucracy [bjʊəˈrɒkrəsi] -2 n. 官僚主义；官僚机构；官僚政治 (研六雅宝 4976/4420)","欧陆词典释义：bureaucracy [bjʊəˈrɒkrəsi] -2 n. 官僚主义；官僚机构；官僚政治 (研六雅宝 4976/4420)","State bureaucracies can tend to stifle enterprise and initiative.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the system of official rules and ways of doing things that a government or an organization has, especially when these seem to be too complicated","example":"unnecessary/excessive bureaucracy"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a system of government in which there are a large number of state officials who are not elected; a country with such a system","example":"We need to reduce paperwork and bureaucracy in the company."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 19th cent.","example":"the power of the state bureaucracy"}]],["causal","/ˈkɔ:zl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “causal”.","causal [ˈkɔ:zl] n. 表示原因的连词 adj. 因果关系的；有原因的 (六宝 8904/5218)","欧陆词典释义：causal [ˈkɔ:zl] n. 表示原因的连词 adj. 因果关系的；有原因的 (六宝 8904/5218)","Rawlins stresses that it is impossible to prove a causal link between the drug and the deaths...",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"connected with the relationship between two things, where one causes the other to happen","example":"the causal relationship between poverty and disease"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"a word such as because","example":"the causal relationship between poverty and disease"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"late Middle English","example":"the causal relationship between poverty and disease"}]],["chronological","/ˌkrɒnəˈlɒdʒɪkl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “chronological”.","chronological [ˌkrɒnəˈlɒdʒɪkl] -1 adj. 按年代顺序排列的；依时间前后排列而记载的 (托雅 13403/12001)","欧陆词典释义：chronological [ˌkrɒnəˈlɒdʒɪkl] -1 adj. 按年代顺序排列的；依时间前后排列而记载的 (托雅 13403/12001)","I have arranged these stories in chronological order.",""],["circumvent","/ˌsɜ:kəmˈvent/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “circumvent”.","circumvent [ˌsɜ:kəmˈvent] -1 v. 包围；智取；绕行，规避 时态: circumvented, circumventing, circumvents (托宝 11924/14169)","欧陆词典释义：circumvent [ˌsɜ:kəmˈvent] -1 v. 包围；智取；绕行，规避 时态: circumvented, circumventing, circumvents (托宝 11924/14169)","Military planners tried to circumvent the treaty.",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to find a way of avoiding a difficulty or a rule","example":"They found a way of circumventing the law."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to go or travel around something that is blocking your way","example":"They found a way of circumventing the law."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"They found a way of circumventing the law."}]],["clarification","/ˌklærəfɪ'keɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “clarification”.","clarification [ˌklærəfɪ'keɪʃn] n. 澄清，说明；净化 (托 11316/8909)","欧陆词典释义：clarification [ˌklærəfɪ'keɪʃn] n. 澄清，说明；净化 (托 11316/8909)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “clarification”.",""],["collaborative","/kəˈlæbərətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “collaborative”.","collaborative [kəˈlæbərətɪv] -1 adj. 合作的，协作的 (6418/9253)","欧陆词典释义：collaborative [kəˈlæbərətɪv] -1 adj. 合作的，协作的 (6418/9253)","a collaborative research project...",""],["commercialization","/kəˌmɜ:ʃəlaɪ'zeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “commercialization”.","commercialization [kəˌmɜ:ʃəlaɪ'zeɪʃn] n. 商品化，商业化 (15905/35213)","欧陆词典释义：commercialization [kəˌmɜ:ʃəlaɪ'zeɪʃn] n. 商品化，商业化 (15905/35213)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “commercialization”.",""],["conducive","/kənˈdju:sɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conducive”.","conducive [kənˈdju:sɪv] -1 adj. 有益的；有助于…的 (雅宝 11002/11125)","欧陆词典释义：conducive [kənˈdju:sɪv] -1 adj. 有益的；有助于…的 (雅宝 11002/11125)","Make your bedroom as conducive to sleep as possible...",""],["configuration","/kənˌfɪgəˈreɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “configuration”.","configuration [kənˌfɪgəˈreɪʃn] -1 n. 配置；结构；外形 (六托雅宝 6153/4862)","欧陆词典释义：configuration [kənˌfɪgəˈreɪʃn] -1 n. 配置；结构；外形 (六托雅宝 6153/4862)","Stonehenge, in south-western England, an ancient configuration of giant stones.",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"an arrangement of the parts of something or a group of things; the form or shape that this arrangement produces","example":"The design is based on four configurations of squares."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the equipment and programs that form a computer system and the way that these are set up to run","example":"The stars seemed to appear in a different configuration."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"mid 16th cent.","example":"There was a changing configuration of lights coming from the stadium."}]],["contradiction","/ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “contradiction”.","contradiction [ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkʃn] -2 n. 矛盾；否认；反驳 (研四六雅 5451/4353)","欧陆词典释义：contradiction [ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkʃn] -2 n. 矛盾；否认；反驳 (研四六雅 5451/4353)","the contradiction s between her private life and the public persona...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a lack of agreement between facts, opinions, actions, etc.","example":"There is a contradiction between the two sets of figures."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of saying that something that somebody else has said is wrong or not true; an example of this","example":"His public speeches are in direct contradiction to"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late Middle English","example":"How can we resolve this apparent contradiction?"}]],["accompany","/əˈkʌmpəni/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accompany”.","accompany [əˈkʌmpəni] -K3 vt. 陪伴，伴随；伴奏 vi. 伴奏，伴唱 时态: accompanied, accompanying, accompanies (高研四六托雅宝 2438/1902)","欧陆词典释义：accompany [əˈkʌmpəni] -K3 vt. 陪伴，伴随；伴奏 vi. 伴奏，伴唱 时态: accompanied, accompanying, accompanies (高研四六托雅宝 2438/1902)","Ken agreed to accompany me on a trip to Africa...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to travel or go somewhere with somebody","example":"His wife accompanied him on the trip."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to happen or appear with something else","example":"I must ask you to accompany me to the police station."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to play a musical instrument, especially a piano, while somebody else sings or plays the main tune","example":"Warships will accompany the convoy."}]],["accord","/əˈkɔ:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accord”.","accord [əˈkɔ:d] -5 n. 符合；一致；协议；自愿 vt. 使一致；给予 vi. 符合；一致 时态: accorded, according, accords (研四六托雅宝 6075/5594)","欧陆词典释义：accord [əˈkɔ:d] -5 n. 符合；一致；协议；自愿 vt. 使一致；给予 vi. 符合；一致 时态: accorded, according, accords (研四六托雅宝 6075/5594)","a fitting way to celebrate the peace accord .",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a formal agreement between two organizations, countries, etc.","example":"The two sides signed a peace accord"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Old English","example":"A peace accord was reached on 26 March."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"in agreement with","example":"They signed a trade accord with the Americans."}]],["assessable","/ə'sesəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assessable”.","assessable [ə'sesəbl] adj. 可估价的；可评价的；可征收的；可征税的 (45357/27871)","欧陆词典释义：assessable [ə'sesəbl] adj. 可估价的；可评价的；可征收的；可征税的 (45357/27871)","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “assessable”.",""],["consultative","/kənˈsʌltətɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “consultative”.","consultative [kənˈsʌltətɪv] -1 adj. 咨询的 (18897/6770)","欧陆词典释义：consultative [kənˈsʌltətɪv] -1 adj. 咨询的 (18897/6770)","the consultative committee on local government finance.",""],["conventional","/kənˈvenʃənl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “conventional”.","conventional [kənˈvenʃənl] -K3 adj. 符合习俗的，传统的；常见的；惯例的 (高研四六托宝 2554/2253)","欧陆词典释义：conventional [kənˈvenʃənl] -K3 adj. 符合习俗的，传统的；常见的；惯例的 (高研四六托宝 2554/2253)","a respectable married woman with conventional opinions.",[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"tending to follow what is done or considered acceptable by society in general; normal and ordinary, and perhaps not very interesting","example":"conventional behaviour/morality"},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"following what is traditional or the way something has been done for a long time","example":"She's very conventional in her views."},{"pos":"adjective","definition":"not nuclear","example":"conventional methods/approaches"}]],["correlate","/ˈkɒrəleɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “correlate”.","correlate [ˈkɒrəleɪt] -1 n. 相关物；相关联的人 vt. 使有相互关系；互相有关系 adj. 关联的 vi. 关联 时态: correlated, correlating, correlates (研六托雅 5266/6763)","欧陆词典释义：correlate [ˈkɒrəleɪt] -1 n. 相关物；相关联的人 vt. 使有相互关系；互相有关系 adj. 关联的 vi. 关联 时态: correlated, correlating, correlates (研六托雅 5266/6763)","Obesity correlate s with increased risk for hypertension and stroke...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"one of two or more facts, figures, etc. that are closely connected and affect or depend on each other","example":"Drug use is a significant correlate of property crime."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"if two or more facts, figures, etc. correlate","example":"The figures do not seem to correlate."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show that there is a close connection between two or more facts, figures, etc.","example":"A high-fat diet correlates with a greater risk of heart disease."}]],["demonstrate","/ˈdemənstreɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “demonstrate”.","demonstrate [ˈdemənstreɪt] -K3 vt. 证明；展示；论证 vi. 示威 时态: demonstrated, demonstrating, demonstrates (研四六托雅宝 1379/1392)","欧陆词典释义：demonstrate [ˈdemənstreɪt] -K3 vt. 证明；展示；论证 vi. 示威 时态: demonstrated, demonstrating, demonstrates (研四六托雅宝 1379/1392)","The study also demonstrate d a direct link between obesity and mortality...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show something clearly by giving proof or evidence","example":"These results demonstrate convincingly that our campaign is working."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show by your actions that you have a particular quality, feeling or opinion","example":"Let me demonstrate to you some of the difficulties we are facing."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to show and explain how something works or how to do something","example":"His sudden departure had demonstrated how unreliable he was."}]],["dilemma","/dɪˈlemə/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dilemma”.","dilemma [dɪˈlemə] -2 n. 困境；进退两难；两刀论法 (高研六托雅宝 4118/4551)","欧陆词典释义：dilemma [dɪˈlemə] -2 n. 困境；进退两难；两刀论法 (高研六托雅宝 4118/4551)","He was faced with the dilemma of whether or not to return to his country...",[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a situation which makes problems, often one in which you have to make a very difficult choice between things of equal importance","example":"to face a dilemma"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"early 16th cent.","example":"to be in a dilemma"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"in a situation in which you have to make a choice between things that are equally unpleasant","example":"I could see no way of resolving this moral dilemma."}]],["dominate","/ˈdɒmɪneɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “dominate”.","dominate [ˈdɒmɪneɪt] -K4 vt. 控制；支配；占优势；在…中占主要地位 vi. 占优势；处于支配地位 时态: dominated, dominating, dominates (研四六托雅宝 2312/2041)","欧陆词典释义：dominate [ˈdɒmɪneɪt] -K4 vt. 控制；支配；占优势；在…中占主要地位 vi. 占优势；处于支配地位 时态: dominated, dominating, dominates (研四六托雅宝 2312/2041)","The book is expected to dominate the best-seller lists...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to control or have a lot of influence over somebody/something, especially in an unpleasant way","example":"As a child he was dominated by his father."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be the most important or noticeable feature of something","example":"He tended to dominate the conversation."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be the largest, highest or most obvious thing in a place","example":"She always says a lot in meetings, but she doesn't dominate."}]],["emphasize","/ˈemfəsaɪz/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “emphasize”.","emphasize [ˈemfəsaɪz] -K3 vt. 强调，着重 时态: emphasized, emphasizing, emphasizes (研四六托雅 1975/3599)","欧陆词典释义：emphasize [ˈemfəsaɪz] -K3 vt. 强调，着重 时态: emphasized, emphasizing, emphasizes (研四六托雅 1975/3599)","But it's also been emphasize d that no major policy changes can be expected to come out of the meeting...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give special importance to something","example":"His speech emphasized the importance of attracting industry to the town."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something more noticeable","example":"She emphasized that their plan would mean sacrifices and hard work."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to give extra force to a word or phrase when you are speaking, especially to show that it is important","example":"He emphasized how little was known about the disease."}]],["enforce","/ɪnˈfɔ:s/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “enforce”.","enforce [ɪnˈfɔ:s] -2 vt. 实施，执行；强迫，强制 时态: enforced, enforcing, enforces (研四六雅 3545/3577)","欧陆词典释义：enforce [ɪnˈfɔ:s] -2 vt. 实施，执行；强迫，强制 时态: enforced, enforcing, enforces (研四六雅 3545/3577)","Until now, the government has only enforce d the ban with regard to American ships...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make sure that people obey a particular law or rule","example":"It's the job of the police to enforce the law."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to make something happen or force somebody to do something","example":"The legislation will be difficult to enforce."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"Middle English","example":"United Nations troops enforced a ceasefire in the area."}]],["exceed","/ɪkˈsi:d/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “exceed”.","exceed [ɪkˈsi:d] -2 vt. 超过；胜过 vi. 超过其他 时态: exceeded, exceeding, exceeds (研四六托雅宝 3281/2718)","欧陆词典释义：exceed [ɪkˈsi:d] -2 vt. 超过；胜过 vi. 超过其他 时态: exceeded, exceeding, exceeds (研四六托雅宝 3281/2718)","Its research budget exceed s $700 million a year...",[{"pos":"verb","definition":"to be greater than a particular number or amount","example":"The price will not exceed £100."},{"pos":"verb","definition":"to do more than the law or an order, etc. allows you to do","example":"His achievements have exceeded expectations"},{"pos":"verb","definition":"late Middle English","example":"She was exceeding the speed limit ("}]],["accentuate","/əkˈsentʃueɪt/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accentuate”.","accentuate [əkˈsentʃueɪt] -1 vt. 强调；重读 时态: accentuated, accentuating, accentuates (托宝 10880/9738)","欧陆词典释义：accentuate [əkˈsentʃueɪt] -1 vt. 强调；重读 时态: accentuated, accentuating, accentuates (托宝 10880/9738)",null,""],["accommodating","/əˈkɒmədeɪtɪŋ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “accommodating”.","accommodating [əˈkɒmədeɪtɪŋ] v. 使适应；调节（accommodate的ing形式）；调解 adj. 随和的；乐于助人的；肯通融的 原型: accommodating 是 accommodate 的现在分词 (托宝 21838/32981)","欧陆词典释义：accommodating [əˈkɒmədeɪtɪŋ] v. 使适应；调节（accommodate的ing形式）；调解 adj. 随和的；乐于助人的；肯通融的 原型: accommodating 是 accommodate 的现在分词 (托宝 21838/32981)",null,""],["adequacy","/'ædɪkwəsɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adequacy”.","adequacy ['ædɪkwəsɪ] n. 足够；适当；妥善性 (14558/12492)","欧陆词典释义：adequacy ['ædɪkwəsɪ] n. 足够；适当；妥善性 (14558/12492)",null,""],["adjacency","/ə'dʒeɪsnsɪ/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adjacency”.","adjacency [ə'dʒeɪsnsɪ] n. 毗邻；四周；邻接物 (46097/49557)","欧陆词典释义：adjacency [ə'dʒeɪsnsɪ] n. 毗邻；四周；邻接物 (46097/49557)",null,""],["admissible","/ədˈmɪsəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “admissible”.","admissible [ədˈmɪsəbl] adj. 可容许的；可采纳的；可接受的 (21026/16289)","欧陆词典释义：admissible [ədˈmɪsəbl] adj. 可容许的；可采纳的；可接受的 (21026/16289)",null,""],["adoptive","/əˈdɒptɪv/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “adoptive”.","adoptive [əˈdɒptɪv] adj. 采用的；有收养关系的 (10779/21113)","欧陆词典释义：adoptive [əˈdɒptɪv] adj. 采用的；有收养关系的 (10779/21113)",null,""],["aesthetic","/i:sˈθetɪk/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “aesthetic”.","aesthetic [i:sˈθetɪk] -2 adj. 美的；美学的；审美的，具有审美趣味的 (研六托雅宝 4296/5161)","欧陆词典释义：aesthetic [i:sˈθetɪk] -2 adj. 美的；美学的；审美的，具有审美趣味的 (研六托雅宝 4296/5161)",null,[{"pos":"adjective","definition":"concerned with beauty and art and the understanding of beautiful things","example":"an aesthetic appreciation of the landscape"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"made in an artistic way and beautiful to look at","example":"The works of art are judged on purely aesthetic grounds"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 18th cent.","example":"The benefits of conservation are both financial and aesthetic."}]],["affiliation","/əˌfɪliˈeɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “affiliation”.","affiliation [əˌfɪliˈeɪʃn] n. 友好关系；加入；联盟；从属关系 (研宝 6180/9080)","欧陆词典释义：affiliation [əˌfɪliˈeɪʃn] n. 友好关系；加入；联盟；从属关系 (研宝 6180/9080)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"a person’s connection with a political party, religion, etc.","example":"He was arrested because of his political affiliation."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"one group or organization’s official connection with another","example":"Trade unions have a long history of affiliation to the Labour Party."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"late 18th cent.","example":"the institute’s affiliation with the university"}]],["alleged","/ə'ledʒd/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “alleged”.","alleged [ə'ledʒd] v. 宣称（allege的过去式和过去分词）；断言 adj. 所谓的；声称的；被断言的 原型: alleged 是 allege 的过去式和过去分词 (4091/3878)","欧陆词典释义：alleged [ə'ledʒd] v. 宣称（allege的过去式和过去分词）；断言 adj. 所谓的；声称的；被断言的 原型: alleged 是 allege 的过去式和过去分词 (4091/3878)",null,""],["articulation","/ɑ:ˌtɪkjuˈleɪʃn/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “articulation”.","articulation [ɑ:ˌtɪkjuˈleɪʃn] n. 关节；接合；清晰发音 (11023/10313)","欧陆词典释义：articulation [ɑ:ˌtɪkjuˈleɪʃn] n. 关节；接合；清晰发音 (11023/10313)",null,[{"pos":"noun","definition":"the expression of an idea or a feeling in words","example":"the articulation of his theory"},{"pos":"noun","definition":"the act of making sounds in speech or music","example":"The singer worked hard on the clear articulation of every note."},{"pos":"noun","definition":"a joint or connection that allows movement","example":"The tongue and teeth are both organs of articulation."}]],["attributable","/əˈtrɪbjətəbl/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “attributable”.","attributable [əˈtrɪbjətəbl] -1 adj. 可归于…的；可归属的 (10740/8052)","欧陆词典释义：attributable [əˈtrɪbjətəbl] -1 adj. 可归于…的；可归属的 (10740/8052)",null,""],["census","/ˈsensəs/","Try to recall the Chinese meaning of “census”.","census [ˈsensəs] -2 n. 人口普查，人口调查 vt. 实施统计调查 (研托雅宝 6047/5187)","欧陆词典释义：census [ˈsensəs] -2 n. 人口普查，人口调查 vt. 实施统计调查 (研托雅宝 6047/5187)",null,""]]};
